-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[14] = {
[7000]={"Nimithil is standing in the rear of the Hall of Ost Anglebed.\
\
Nimithil is concerned that the arguing in the hall will soon turn to violence and asks for your support in calming the crowd.","Instancia: Legado de Conflicto","Talk to Nimithil","'I have never seen my people like this... it is tremendously worrying, and I feel I must say something before the hour is too late.\
\
'Will you follow me along with my guards, ${PLAYER}? I do not know what will come of my words.'","Observe the meeting between Nimithil and Malthellim","Defeat Yamanim, Hosdam, and Khutâ","Subdue Steward Malthellim","Nimithil can be found somewhere in the Hall of Ost Anglebed.\
\
You have travelled to the hall with Nimithil, but became separated amid a large crowd of belligerent people. You should reunite with Nimithil.","'I cannot believe that the Steward felt this the best way to keep his people safe from the Enemy!\
\
'It is true that many of the people in Lebennin come from families that once supported Castamir, but his legacy was a tainted one, and he fell from favour with all but his most devoted. It is no folly that he came to be known only as the Usurper!\
\
'Malthellim must be locked away, lest he allow more of the Enemy inside these walls.'","Listen to Nimithil speak to the crowd of Gondorians","Nimithil and Malthellim are speaking near the fire-pit in the centre of the Hall of Ost Anglebed.\
\
Nimithil is sharing what you have learned in Lornost and Ost Anglebed with Malthellim. You should listen as they speak.","Nimithil is standing in the rear of the Hall of Ost Anglebed.\
\
You have found Nimithil, but the Steward has not yet returned to the Hall. You should ask Nimithil what is to be done.","'Let us leave the hall while my guards escort Malthellim and his men away. I cannot stand to look upon him any longer.'","Search for Nimithil among the crowd","Nimithil can be found in the rear of the Hall of Ost Anglebed.\
\
You have subdued Steward Malthellim with the aid of Nimithil's guards, and should now speak to Nimithil.","Steward Malthellim can be found in the Hall of Ost Anglebed.\
\
Malthellim has drawn his weapon in desperation, and must now be subdued if the people of Ost Anglebed are to remain safe.","Concerned by the growing influence of the Heirs of Castamir in Lebennin, Nimithil hopes to warn Steward Malthellim of treachery within Ost Anglebed and prevent her people from splintering.","Malthellim looks appalled and swiftly draws his weapon!","Yamanim, Hosdam, and Khutâ are moving against the dissenters within the Hall of Ost Anglebed.\
\
Malthellim has aligned himself with the Heirs of Castamir and has now allowed the Corsair and Haradrim men in Ost Anglebed to execute dissenting folk.","The doors to the hall are thrust open and rattle loudly against the walls"},
[7001]={"Try to survive!","This way is not safe!","You must try to escape!\
\
Run south, towards Helm's Deep.","Try to escape towards the north-west","'Let me at 'em! What do you say, you brute? Let's charge!\
\
'Wait. What's...what's that?'","Something has unnerved the other Orcs....","You must try to escape!\
\
Run north...into the strange trees.","Talk to your neighbour again","Watch and wait","The boss wants you to get back in line","This way has been taken by the cursed Men!","'The night is almost over, but we'll take 'em. These horsemen have no friends to save them.\
\
'We'll get over the walls and eat the hearts of every last one of them. Today we feast.\
\
'Now get back in line, worm!'","Now you must flee! These strange trees will provide cover.","Try to escape south","'What do you think you're getting out of line for? It's not our turn yet. It'll never be our turn.\
\
'The boys in front will do all the killing, and our swords don't even have a drop of blood.\
\
'This ain't what I came for!'","Escape through the forest!","But where did these trees come from? This forest was not here before...was it?","Find a spot to rest, and rest briefly at the edge of the trees","You must seize the Hornburg and drive out the Men!","You must try to escape!\
\
Run north-west, towards the Fords of Isen.","¡Cuidado!","The Uruk-commander stands near the ugly gate up ahead.\
\
You should ask the boss when the battle will be over, for you grow bored without a drop of blood to stain your sword.","Get back in line and talk to your neighbour","You must try to escape!\
\
Run east, along the dike.","Ask the boss when the battle will be done","Your place in line is back a ways, near some other Orcs.\
\
You should speak with your neighbour.","Your place in line is back a ways, near some other Orcs.\
\
You should watch and wait.","Try to escape towards the east","Your place in line is back a ways, near some other Orcs.\
\
You should get back in line.","Instancia: ¡Tomemos el Hornburg!","Run north!","A blasted Elf has blocked the way","Find a resting spot at the edge of the trees."},
[7002]={"The muddy depths of Lhaid Ogo are home to many decaying horrors, and a Dunlending messenger may be lost within.","Talk to Anirin in Lhaid Ogo","Somewhere inside Lhaid Ogo, a messenger from Dunland may be in trouble.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo, you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>","You have found Anirin in the depths of Lhaid Ogo and should speak with him.","Search Lhaid Ogo for the lost Dunlending messenger","'Look out! It still lives!'","'We should leave at once! My leg is still hurt, but if I lean on you I can make it.'","Instance: Lhaid Ogo","'Who...who are you? I need to...to see the Brenin...at Lhanuch....'\
\
You assure him that you will bring him to Glynn Brenin at once.\
\
'This great beast attacked me as I was passing the entrance to this cave, and I could not get away. Thank you for saving me! It is fortunate you were passing by...and so far from habitation!\
\
'I bring a message from Lheu Brenin of Tûr Morva, in the south: he urges Glynn Brenin not to believe the lies of the Wizard Saruman! The Wizard has sent agents to the Brenin to try and buy his loyalty, and he is worried that other clans may have accepted these offers. The Uch-luth have not done so? Oh, good fortune! You must bring me to Lhanuch at once!'"},
[7003]={"Instancia: Liberando Woodhurst","Now that Thurferth has left, Gifemund and Calin have engaged in a quieter discussion.","Speak to Calin before joining the confrontation. \
\
It appears Gifemund and Thurferth are in an argument that could get violent near the empty throne.","'I think we got here just in time. The argument between Gifemund and Thurferth is beginning to heat up, but I am not sure what can be done besides letting them work it out.'","Observe Calin and Gifemund's discussion","There is a heated discussion between Gifemund and Thurferth in front of the empty throne in the mead hall.","Gifemund has made his move, and demanded Guard Captain Thurferth step down due to his failing to keep the city safe. They now try to settle their differences in front of the empty throne they have both sought.","'Herubrand needs to hear of what occurred here today. Thurferth's suggestion to side with Saruman is disturbing, and I wonder how many feel that way. Gifemund and I will meet with Herubrand immediately.\
\
'Make your way there when you are ready.'","Speak with Calin","'I believe the time has come to include Gifemund in our secrets, and share our plans with him. He can prove to be a powerful ally. I will bring him to Herubrand shortly.'","Speak to Calin near the throne at the back of the mead hall.","Observa la discusión"},
[7004]={"'You have acquitted yourself well, ${PLAYER}, and have most definitely earned this reward. May our arms remain strong!'","'I will rain arrows upon our enemies!'","Talk to Céola","'We shall speak again later, ${PLAYER}.'","The Khundolar prepare to lay siege to Etheburg, and you have chosen to defend the way-post.","'${PLAYER}, I am glad that you have chosen to stand with us! Twiga will lead the forces in the upper tier of Etheburg, while you, our men, and I defend the lower tiers.\
\
'If you so desire, you may enter the watch-towers and speak with the archers on duty. If you do, they will rain arrows down upon our foes.\
\
'Now, to arms!'","Defeat all of the attacking Khundolar.","Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.\
\
You should speak with Céola regarding the battle at Etheburg.","<rgb=#FF0000>Céola must not be defeated</rgb>","Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.\
\
You should speak at once with Céola to learn his plan.","Instancia: Luces en la Tierra","Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands","Defeated all of the attacking Khundolar","<rgb=#FF0000>Céola was defeated</rgb>","Defeat all of the attacking Khundolar"},
[7005]={"'We will speak to the chieftain and learn what he knows of the raiding-party. For there to be no sign of it, given the dying words of Thrúgord, seems most peculiar to me.'","'I take it you have seen no sign of this raiding-party? How surprising.'","Return to Glóin in the village square and protect him from the Orcs","Meet with Runerik, the village chieftain of Limlók","Talk to Venko at Limlók","'Farewell to the worms who raided my town, and to the vermin who led them. None shall mourn.\
\
'I thank you for your aid and that of your companions, ${PLAYER}. It was well-given.'","Find Imák and protect him from the Orcs","Venko wishes to speak with the village chieftain of Limlók to learn what befell the raiding-party from Gundabad.","The posts of the encircling wall are lower here","'Our companions are safe? That is good to hear, my friend! Let us finish off the Orcs here and the village will follow suit!'","'These Orcs are canny, ${PLAYER}! They set fires along the outskirts of the village at the same time, in order to thin out the defenders.\
\
'But they did not account for us!'","The wooden palisade appears sturdy enough at this location","Examine the eastern fence of Limlók","Shorter posts were used for the encircling wall behind the barn","Find Venko and protect him from the Orcs","The raiding-party has attacked the village of Limlók from multiple directions at the same time!","Runerik Knotbeard stands outside his home in Limlók.","Follow Runerik Knotbeard","Examine the north-western fence of Limlók","'Enjoy... the days you have left... for they are few!'\
\
Natsatúg coughs weakly and blood spreads from his wounds, soaking his armour.\
\
'The time of the dwarves... is nearly ended! The Lord of Gundabad... the Lord of Gundabad...'\
\
Natsatúg closes his eyes, and with his last exhalation he breathes a name.","The cliffs beyond the palisade here should serve as adequate defence","Examine the south-eastern fence of Limlók","Instancia: Limlók bajo ataque","The raiding-party that threatened the safety of Limlók has been defeated, thanks to your efforts and those of your companions, as well as those of the people who dwell there. One Orc remains alive, but he will soon die of his wounds.","The raiding-party from Gundabad had designs upon the peaceful Beorning village of Limlók... but where has it gone?","Listen to Glóin's words","Examine the north-eastern fence of Limlók","Venko is ready to speak with the Beorning chieftain at the village of Limlók and learn if he has seen the missing raiding-party from Gundabad.","You hear a waterfall beyond the wall here: a natural defence?","Talk to Natsatúg before he dies of his wounds","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his house in Limlók","Runerik believes his town has nothing to fear from the missing raiding-party, but your companions want to check Limlók's exterior fences just to make sure.","Examine the south-western fence of Limlók","'This attack is better-planned than I expected from the Orcs! They set fires on opposite sides of the village at the same time, forcing us to split the defences!\
\
'I hate to say it, but these Orcs may work better together than we do!'","Limlók is under attack!","Runerik does not believe his village is any more susceptible to danger than is usual for his people."},
[7006]={"Instancia: Recuerdos lejanos","Sigue a Prestadír por el agujero del muro","Habla con Prestadír","Prestadír te ha pedido que lo sigas afuera.","Prestadír se encuentra sobre las turbulentas aguas del Fontegrís, justo fuera de los muros de Eitheldir.","'No soy tan versado en la historia de esta tierra como algunos de los míos, pero sé lo suficiente para compartir parte de ella contigo, ${PLAYER}. Siete siglos después del inicio de la Segunda Edad, el gran herrero elfo Celebrimbor viajó desde Lindon para morar en los bosques de acebos al pie de las Montañas Nubladas. Ese reino llegó a ser conocido como Eregion, y fue la cuna de muchos tesoros y grandes obras de artesanía.\
\
'El corazón del reino de Celebrimbor se extendía al sur del Sonorona, pero los elfos expulsaron a los trolls y a los Amonedain hostiles de la zona, construyendo puestos de avanzada en las colinas boscosas de las fronteras. El principal de ellos era esta fortaleza, Eitheldir, construida para vigilar los vados del Fontegrís y mantener abierto el camino a Lindon.\
\
'El gobierno del torreón se le otorgó a Oranoril, una compañera noldor de Celebrimbor. Había servido como capitana en las guerras contra Morgoth, y era famosa tanto por su lealtad como por su ferocidad.'","Habla con Prestadír a las afueras de Eitheldir","Prestadír se encuentra a las afueras de las ruinas de Eitheldir.","Prestadír se encuentra en las ruinas de Eitheldir.","'No les habría negado el refugio si hubieran venido honradamente y no se hubieran dado al robo. Pero, por desgracia, no ha sido así.'\
\
Prestadír alza la vista al cielo, escudriñando las alturas.\
\
'Parece que va a llover', dice, y luego devuelve la mirada a la tierra.\
\
'¿Habéis oído hablar de la Guerra entre los Elfos y Sauron, ${PLAYER}, en la que el Señor Oscuro ansiaba dominar las obras de Eregion? Celebrimbor percibió los designios de Sauron, pero hubo poco tiempo para prepararse para la destrucción que aguardaba a los elfos.'","'Oranoril se hizo cargo de los soldados restantes tras la muerte de Celebrimbor; solo su gran dote de mando evitó que la derrota se convirtiera en un ineludible baño de sangre, y ordenó a su pueblo que se retirara. En la Cordillera de Acebeda contempló con horror cómo las fuerzas de Sauron marchaban tras el espantoso estandarte que habían hecho del otrora orgulloso herrero elfo.\
\
'Sabiendo que le aguardaba un destino similar si la atrapaban, Oranoril ideó un plan para salvar a los que pudiera de su pueblo. Eligió a un pequeño grupo de su propia casa y engañó al ejército de Sauron para que los persiguiera. En una persecución implacable, los condujo al otro lado del Bruinen hasta el Ángulo, mientras el grueso de sus congéneres escapaba por senderos secretos hacia las montañas y luego al joven refugio de Elrond. Ravaedron era uno de ellos, y nunca olvidó la imagen de la compañía de Oranoril desapareciendo por la cresta, perseguida por los soldados de Sauron.'","'La compañía de Oranoril eludió a los ejércitos del Señor Oscuro hasta llegar a Eitheldir, pero cuando llegaron a los pies de la fortaleza descubrieron que el cruce del Fontegrís ya había sido tomado por el enemigo. Siguió un breve asedio, pero los orcos superaban con creces a los pocos elfos que quedaban; las puertas fueron destrozadas y el torreón arrasado. Uno a uno perecieron los compañeros de Oranoril, hasta que solo quedaron ella y tres más.\
\
'Juntos llevaron a cabo un último desafío, abriéndose paso entre la multitud hasta el cuerpo de Celebrimbor y arrancándolo de las garras de los orcos. Reuniendo sus últimas fuerzas, Oranoril, la última elfa con vida en Eitheldir, tomó el cadáver del herrero y saltó desde el precipicio a las espumosas aguas del Fontegrís. Y así, incluso en su victoria, Sauron fue despojado de sus trofeos, y su ira no tuvo igual.\
\
'Furioso de que muchos de los Noldor lo hubieran eludido, e incapaz de encontrar a dónde habían huido, Sauron invadió Eriador desde el Ángulo, con la intención de aplastar el reino de Lindon. En su lugar, se encontró con que los Hombres de Númenor lo esperaban, pues habían respondido a la llamada de Gil-galad, y las fuerzas combinadas de elfos y hombres doblegaron el poder de Sauron. ¿De dónde vino el golpe de gracia? Pues de Elrond y la gente de Imladris, ya que, cuando recuperaron las fuerzas, regresaron con un fuego renovado en sus corazones, y Sauron no pudo hacerles frente. Derrotado, ahora fue su turno de huir: escapó a Mordor.'","Habla con Prestadír fuera de los muros de Eitheldir","'Después de la guerra, los elfos buscaron los restos de Oranoril y Celebrimbor tanto en el Fontegrís como en el Aguagrís, pero no hallaron rastro de sus cuerpos. Este precipicio se convirtió en un lugar de peregrinación para muchos de los Noldor, sobre todo para quienes habían llegado a Rivendel gracias al sacrificio de Oranoril.\
\
'Ravaedron era uno de ellos, ${PLAYER}, y sé que no le resulta fácil caminar hoy por el Ángulo, con recuerdos como estos aún tan vivos en su memoria. Eregion quedó desolada tras la Guerra entre los Elfos y Sauron, y sus salas destrozadas se desmoronaron con el paso de los años, cubriéndose de hierba y enredaderas, pero las piedras recuerdan lo que ocurrió, al igual que los que estuvieron allí.\
\
'Por eso no me opongo a la decisión de Ravaedron de abandonar la Tierra Media. Si esa es la paz que desea, quiero que la tenga.'","Has venido con Prestadír para patrullar por las ruinas de Eitheldir y saber qué quiere decirte."},
[7007]={"'To destroy darkness, must wear shadow. You have seen maw of darkness and live to tell story. We leave now?'","Defeated Dheghûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The shadowy beast's power fades as it sinks back to whence it came!","Destroy the source of the Dheghûn","Destroy the source of the Dheghûn.","Instancia: Sombras perdidas","You should speak with Rhûd-pulo-Drât.","Find the source of the Dheghûn","At the end of the cavern, a large organic bulb pulses","Your tampering has only released an unknown horror upon Gondor!","Defeat Gúthrakh the Ravenous","Rhûd-pulo-Drât is in need of a warrior to brave the depths of Nardol's ancient mine and destroy the source of the Dheghûn beneath the mountain.","'I saw with my eyes, all you have done. You are very very good, ${RACE}. Let us return to  Drû Bhûta and speak to Ghân-buri-Ghân of the good story we share.'","Defeat the Dheghûn and find out where they are coming from within the Nardol mines.","Defeat Dheghûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Rhûd-pulo-Drât"},
[7009]={"Listen to Halbarad determine what must be done","'Nothing.'","Golodir has found his way to the large chamber, and his anger is evident.","You see no recognition in Lothrandir's eyes. He shakes and convulses before you, a pitiable figure that bears little resemblance to the strong-willed man you remember. Of all Saruman's crimes, this may be the one that strikes nearest to your heart.\
\
He seems to be trying to speak, but his words are muffled and his voice weak.","The woman named Mercy has told you where you might find Lothrandir: in the southernmost passage of the building in which you find yourself. You must search the building for him, and quickly!","Talk to Lothrandir in his cell","Gun Ain has given voice to something remarkable. Can it be true? Does Lothrandir still live?","Halbarad has found a large room, its floor covered with dirty water, and has called for you to join him.","Instancia: Lothrandir","Halbarad has determined what should be done.","Far below, in a large room, Halbarad beckons you onward","Halbarad has reunited with his lost kinsman.","The Grey Company has separated into groups in order to search more of Isengard for their captive kinsman.","Search the flooded pits for some sign of the captive Lothrandir","'I came to this room from another passage, ${PLAYER}. It seems that the wall of Isengard is a warren of rooms and tunnels, but we will search them all for my kinsman. Saruman cannot hide him from us forever.'\
\
Halbarad stops speaking and listens for a moment to the steady dripping of water in a distant corner.","For the first time, Gun Ain's eyes are alight with a fierce and sudden joy. She exults in her words, and radiates a restless energy.\
\
'You spoke of the strength of Lothrandir's will, and you were not wrong. Saruman tried to exert control over his mind, tried with every ounce of his power, but still your friend resisted. The Wizard wove convincing illusions and portraits of despair, but still Lothrandir fought. Many and powerful were the tricks he employed to break your friend's mind, but each one failed. Lothrandir remained strong, and the Wizard could find no means of bending him to his will.\
\
'In the end, Saruman had to abandon the effort. He took another prisoner from his cell, a Falcon Clan warrior named Kenned who had proved unable to work in the Pits, and dressed him in Lothrandir's garb. That is the poor creature you see before you; he has at last earned his freedom.'","Talk to Lothrandir in the large chamber","Talk to Halbarad in the large chamber","'What sorcery have they worked on my kinsman? Lothrandir is a shell of himself, ${PLAYER}, and I will make those responsible for his sad state reap the reward of their crime!'","The Rangers have lost a kinsman and a friend, and are sharing a moment of grief before they must return to Aragorn with the sad news.","'Let us leave this sunken pit, ${PLAYER}. I will be glad to see daylight again, and I know Lothrandir must feel the same!'","Allow the Rangers time to mourn","You have agreed to search for Lothrandir in some more of the buildings in the wall of Isengard.","Talk to Halbarad outside Lothrandir's cell","'Is that you, ${PLAYER}? I did not think I would see you again.'\
\
Lothrandir smiles weakly.\
\
'The Wizard was not pleased when you escaped. I almost felt sorry for Saruman. I think his Orcs are endlessly disappointing him.'","Squinting in the half-light, a pile of rags reveals itself to be a weary prisoner","Talk to Golodir in the large chamber","Lothrandir stands before you, a shadow of his former self.","Lothrandir is in a cell unlocked by Gun Ain's key, off the southernmost passage.","Talk to Gun Ain in the large chamber","You have seen anger in Gun Ain's eyes before today, and fear, but never have you seen the look she gives you now. Her expression is pained.\
\
'All I wanted was a name, ${PLAYER}. I wanted to be someone again. I wanted a family to replace the one I had lost, friends to take the place of my emptiness... but there is no one.\
\
'Look at them! That is what I wanted, ${PLAYER}, but no one will miss me! No one will cry when I have gone. No one will mourn.'","'Lothrandir is safe and we have accomplished our aim, ${PLAYER}. I will be glad to leave this place behind us.'","Find Lothrandir in a cell off the southernmost passage of the building"},
[7010]={"A young girl crouches by a ragged camp-site. Can this be the screaming shadow?","Talk to the mysterious girl","'Let us leave this place, ${PLAYER}. Gun Ain will have to find somewhere to make an honest living, somewhere she will not hinder the Lossoth. She will find a more forgiving place to live, or she will die in this harsh place. Others who served Angmar would not have even that chance.'","'I do not want your mercy! A pox on all ${CLASS}s and Rangers!'","Find the screaming shadow within the massive cavern","Lothrandir must not be defeated","Lothrandir has been defeated","'Keep searching the depths of Kolo-hampât for the mysterious shadow that steals away the prey of the Lossoth hunters.'","'Look at this, ${PLAYER}! I had no idea such an expansive cavern existed beneath the frozen tundra of Forochel.\
\
'We must be on guard as we make our way through this cavern in search of the screaming shadow that has harried the Lossoth hunters. It has carried away much of their slain prey, and what few tracks I was able to find came to the entrance of this cave before being lost in the shifting snows of this land.\
\
'Do not be dazzled by the reflections in the ice! We must remain alert to all threats while we search the cavern!'","Lothrandir has chosen to spare the life of Gun Ain and is waiting to speak to you.","You have found a mysterious girl crouched by a ragged camp-fire in the depths of Kolo-hampât and must now defend yourself from her.","'We need to cover more ground, ${PLAYER}. If we search different areas of this cavern, we will have a better chance of finding what we seek.'","You have found a mysterious girl crouched by a ragged camp-fire in the depths of Kolo-hampât.","Instancia: Lothrandir de los Yermos Helados","Defend yourself from Gun Ain","Gun Ain falls to the icy ground, exhausted and defeated","The girl stares at you fiercely, her eyes wild with anger and fear. She shivers in the cold, and her face is thin and drawn. There is a feral air about her, and she seems tense, poised to strike.","Learn the history of this mysterious girl","Lothrandir has gone his own way to search the depths of Kolo-hampât, and now you must seek out the mysterious 'screaming shadow' yourself.","'Stay your hand, ${PLAYER}, and I will put away my weapon as well.\
\
'Listen to me, Gun Ain! You served Angmar, this we know, and it has gone badly for you since you were cast from your clan. You cannot steal from the Lossoth as you have done; you must find a new home, or you will die here among the ice and the snow. None would mourn you, No-name, if you perished as you are.\
\
'We will do you no more harm. Swear to me that you will leave the lands of the Lossoth and seek an honest living elsewhere. This mercy is yours today. Do not throw it away. If you continue to trouble the people of Forochel, you will find that my heart has exhausted its pity.'","Talk to Lothrandir","Lothrandir is in Kolo-hampât, seeking the 'screaming shadow' that has interfered with the Lossoth hunters.","Lothrandir is in Kolo-hampât, waiting to speak with you.","You have entered the massive cavern of Kolo-hampât with the Ranger Lothrandir in search of the 'screaming shadow' that has interfered with the Lossoth hunters."},
[7011]={"Khâshap is cornered!","Khâshap has left his champion Utho to deal with you.","Defeat Khâshap","The pursuit of Khâshap has led you to a dead end. He has no choice but to take a stand.","'This is it. It's now or never. He has nowhere left to hide.\
\
'But this is also his home turf. We face some tough odds. But I am sure you have faced far worse.\
\
'If he manages to deliver the phial, there's no telling what the consequences may be. Do not stop for anything. Bring him to justice!'","'I swear that man had nine lives. Every step of the way he used his minions as shields and would slip off into the night.\
\
'Today was a good day. Not only did we solve the case, but we stopped an even larger plot from manifesting.\
\
'Thank you. I could not have done this without you.'","Khâshap has fled into the bustling Streets of Râhal Bakh where he has the protection of his cohorts.","A gate blocks your way!","Khâshap continues his escape to another gate. But it seems he is out of options.","Continue the pursuit","Talk to Hadorion","Instance: Maladies for Remedies","Defeat Utho the Grasper","Khâshap has fled deeper into the Streets of Râhal Bakh. Catch up to him before it is too late.","Khâshap at long last has been stopped. The engine of the apothecaries will no longer reach his masters, and the crisis averted.\
\
You should speak to Hadorion.","The way is open! Continue your pursuit!","Pursue Khâshap"},
[7013]={"Regresa con el Uruk cautivo y mantente alerta","Habla con el Uruk cautivo","Drusi Begwyl vigila a su cautivo y quiere preguntarte algo.","<rgb=#FF0000>Tanto Meneldir como Flam Helur deben sobrevivir</rgb>","'¿Saruman? ¿Por qué mencionaría el nombre del Mago Blanco?\
\
'¿Qué quiso decir con eso?'","Habla con Drusi Begwyl","Flam Helur ha aceptado llevarte a ti y a Meneldir hasta el Uruk que él y su compañera capturaron.","Escucha las últimas palabras de Ushdul","'¿Viste esos jabalíes? Pasaron corriendo justo por aquí, y habría disparado algunas flechas, pero no quería apartar mi atención del cautivo.\
\
'¡Eran grandes, eso sí! Podría haber carne suficiente en esos huesos para preparar bastantes filetes de jabalí para la gente de Clegur. ¡Dime que los viste, y que Flam fue lo bastante rápido con su arco o su cuchillo para conseguirlos!'\
\
Aseguras a Drusi que la carne de jabalí puede llevarse al poblado cuando terminen aquí... pero ¿quizá haya asuntos más urgentes?\
\
'¿Más urgentes?' pregunta. 'Supongo... pero aun así: esos jabalíes eran realmente algo, y sería una pena dejar escapar tantas posibles cenas sin siquiera intentarlo.'","Habla con el moribundo Ushdul","Instancia: Marca de la Mano Blanca","Has impedido que los Uruks rescaten a Ushdul.","'Cuando me libre de estas ratas, ¡haré que paguéis! ¡Desearéis no haberos cruzado con Ushdul!\
\
'¡No tenéis idea de lo que os espera, a ninguno de vosotros!'","Habla con Flam Helur","Permanece alerta y descubre qué trajo a Ushdul y a los Uruks a la Ciénaga de los Cisnes","'No falta mucho ahora... solo una carrera corta cuesta arriba.\
\
'¡Perdonad el frío en el aire, amigos! ¡Pero ya casi llegamos!'","El cautivo de Drusi te mira con desprecio.","'Esto no cambia... nada. Moriréis... aún más dolorosamente que yo.'\
\
Ushdul reúne visiblemente sus fuerzas, el odio brillando en sus ojos.\
\
'¡Escuchadme, todos vosotros! ¡Escuchad las palabras de Ushdul!'","Meneldir está listo para luchar contra cualquier nuevo peligro que se acerque.","¡Flam Helur ha caído, y has fallado!","¡Meneldir ha caído, y has fallado!","Ushdul está muriendo, atravesado por flechas disparadas por quienes se suponía que venían a rescatarlo.","El Uruk herido se mueve","Ushdul yace moribundo. Ha exigido que escuches sus últimas palabras.","'Creo que estos recién llegados deben de haber venido a rescatar a nuestro cautivo, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'¡Demostrémosles que han cometido un gran error! ¡No lo dejaremos ir sin luchar!'","Meneldir y los Fuertes buscan descubrir qué ha traído a Ushdul y a los otros Uruks a la Ciénaga de los Cisnes.","Flam Helur, uno de los cazadores Fuertes de Clegur, ha aceptado llevarte al Uruk que él y su compañera Drusi capturaron.","Habla con Meneldir"},
[7014]={"Golpea la puerta de la fortaleza","La puerta de la fortaleza de Zabadgathol se encuentra justo delante de ti.\
\
Bori quiere que golpees la puerta de la fortaleza para invocar a Mazog.","Bori espera una respuesta a su desafío.\
\
Ve a hablar con él y defiéndelo si es necesario.","'¿Por qué no responde? Por todo lo que se ha dicho de él, no habría pensado que Mazog fuera tan cobarde como parece ahora.\
\
'¡Quizás la vista de Zigilburk brillando a la luz de este lugar le haya cortado las piernas y el valor!'","Habla con Sweina","Bori se encuentra cerca de una de las entradas de Zabadgathol.\
\
Bori te espera para que lo acompañes a Zabadgathol.","Bori ha sido congelado por alguna maldad, y se te libera para llevar las malas noticias a los enanos.","Habla con Bori","Sweina ha llegado a las afueras.\
\
Deberías hablar con Sweina sobre el giro de los acontecimientos.","'Aunque me duela decirlo, deberíamos irnos. Si este hechicero tiene el poder que dices, no podremos sobrevivir lo suficiente para liberar a Bori o recuperar Zigilburk de su mano encantada.\
\
'¡Rápido, ${CLASS}! Antes de que los Orcos decidan que nuestras cabezas son un mensaje suficiente!'","Instancia: Mazog","Bori está seguro de que con el poder del hacha de mithril Zigilburk, junto con tu ayuda, puede derrotar a Mazog y evitar la guerra.","'¡Golpea la puerta, ${PLAYER}, y dile a Mazog que hemos venido a poner fin a su patética vida y reinado!'","'¿Recuerdas nuestra victoria en Stazgnâkh? Esta será aún más gloriosa, porque ahora tengo el poder de Zigilburk en mis manos.\
\
'Con un solo golpe eliminaremos a Mazog y los Orcos quedarán sin líder y confundidos.\
\
'¡Adelante, amigos! Hay muchos cuellos de orco por delante, ¡y Zigilburk está sedienta de batalla!'","Tu golpe resuena en toda la caverna, pero no hay respuesta.","Sobrevive a tu encuentro con Gorothúl y haz lo que te diga","'${PLAYER}, ¿qué ha pasado? ¿Dónde está Bori?'\
\
Sweina escucha tu relato en silencio, apretando los puños de rabia.\
\
'¡Malditos orcos! Siempre buscan un aliado fuerte, una fuerza poderosa que les diga qué hacer, un maestro menor bajo su gran maestro, quizás, pero aún así terrible.\
\
'Tenemos que salir de aquí, ${PLAYER}. No hay nada que podamos hacer por Bori ahora.'"},
[7015]={"Instancia: Mazog en la telaraña","'Issuriel fue a inspeccionar el otro camino, al noreste. Espero que no haya encontrado tanto peligro como yo, ¡por su bien y por el nuestro! Deberás destruir las telarañas situadas a lo largo del camino, porque las arañas las han tejido detrás de ella, y será necesario que el camino esté despejado si queremos llevar a Mazog por allí.'","Usa el estandarte de los Malledhrim para dar órdenes de apoyo a Achardor","La Guardia Oculta ha comenzado el peligroso viaje a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas a lo largo de Râd Iorist.","Issuriel ha sido gravemente herida y se está desmayando justo al borde de la conciencia. Sus párpados tiemblan débilmente, pero no parece reconocerte.","Achardor está vigilando a lo largo de Râd Iorist, el peligroso camino hacia Dol Guldur que ha sido elegido por la Guardia Oculta.","'¡Lo has logrado, ${PLAYER}! Estamos libres de las telarañas y ahora podemos seguir a Issuriel y Mazog antes de que les ocurra algún daño!'","'Issuriel y Cúcheron fueron adelante para explorar por dónde podemos llevar al prisionero. Ves el resultado de la misión de Cúcheron; debemos esperar que Issuriel haya tenido más éxito en la suya.\
\
'Viaja hacia el noreste, rompiendo las telarañas en el camino, hasta que llegues a Issuriel. Necesitaremos que el camino esté despejado si queremos llevar a Mazog allí.'","'¡Estoy tan contenta de verte, ${PLAYER}! Pensé que estar aquí en una misión de tanta importancia me daría suficiente valentía... pero aquí entre las telarañas mi coraje se desvanece, y solo deseo estar en casa.\
\
'Fue sabio venir por este camino, porque necesitábamos secreto, pero aquí en la oscuridad es difícil para mí saberlo realmente. Confiaré en ti para que me des órdenes usando esta bandera de los Malledhrim. Te apoyaré como lo hice en el Bosque Ahogado: con poder, con moral o con un poco de ambos. Juntos, mi coraje será mayor contra las arañas de este lugar.\
\
'¡No estamos solos! ¡Regresan!'","'Cúcheron y Sigileth se han quedado atrás, por el momento. Se asegurarán de que ninguna araña pueda sorprendernos por detrás.\
\
'El resto de nosotros avanzará como un grupo. Este camino está lleno de peligro, ¡y ahora estamos demasiado lejos para dar marcha atrás! ¡Debemos seguir adelante!'","Ha llegado el momento de llevar a Mazog más lejos por Râd Iorist, aunque los bosques estén infestados de arañas.","'¡Vamos, ${PLAYER}! Ahora cojearemos en derrota hacia Ost Galadh, donde la Hueste Dorada ha establecido un puesto avanzado. ¡No puedo creer que hayamos llegado a este final desastroso!'","Habla con Sigileth","Issuriel tiene un mal presentimiento sobre algo y quiere hablar contigo mientras su nerviosismo aumenta.","'Has luchado bien, y las criaturas han sido repelidas. Quizás este camino no sea tan peligroso como temía después de todo.\
\
'Cúcheron e Issuriel fueron por delante, cada uno en una dirección diferente, para explorar qué camino deberíamos seguir.\
\
'No han regresado.'","La Guardia Oculta lucha por su supervivencia contra las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas incluso mientras uno de sus miembros y su prisionero sucumben al veneno del maestro de las arañas.","Habla con Achardor","El camino de la Guardia Oculta a lo largo de Râd Iorist ha terminado en desastre: Issuriel y Mazog han sido envenenados, y ahora el éxito de la misión está en peligro.","Asegura las cadenas de Mazog","Defiende a Issuriel","Revisa a Issuriel herida","Issuriel se encuentra en algún lugar a lo largo de Râd Iorist, al noreste de Achardor y Cúcheron. Las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas han tejido telarañas detrás de ella, y deben ser cortadas si los Elfos quieren unirse a ella con el prisionero.","La posición de Achardor a lo largo de Râd Iorist ha sido atacada por las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas. ¡Debes defender a Mazog de su ataque!","Habla con Issuriel","Achardor ha llegado a la posición de Issuriel a lo largo de Râd Iorist, con Mazog a su lado.","Habla con Issuriel más allá de las telarañas, al noreste","El camino que Cúcheron exploró no es seguro, y ahora el Elfo debe ser defendido de las arañas que lo persiguen. Asegúrate de que Mazog no sea asesinado.","'Puede que no tengamos mucho tiempo. Asegúrate de que las cadenas de Mazog estén seguras y llévalo por delante hasta donde Achardor y Cúcheron esperan. Cuanto antes salgamos de este laberinto infestado de telarañas, mejor para todos nosotros.'","Has resistido otro ataque de las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas y ahora deberías hablar con Achardor","Defiende a Mazog","Achardor necesita tu ayuda para liberarse de las telarañas y seguir a Issuriel y Mazog en lo profundo del bosque de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.","Retiras las telarañas pegajosas y adherentes de los eslabones de las cadenas de Mazog, y el orco te mira impasible.","'¡Algo está mal. ¿Lo sientes? ¡Este lugar no es seguro!'","Defiende a Achardor y a la Guardia Oculta","Cúcheron ha sido salvado, gracias a tus esfuerzos y a los de Achardor, y Mazog sigue siendo prisionero de la Guardia Oculta.","Ayuda a Achardor a liberarse de las telarañas que lo atan","Habla con Cúcheron","'¡Pensamiento rápido y acción aún más rápida, ${PLAYER}! He llegado a esperar ambas de ti, y es afortunado para mi salud continua que así sea.\
\
'No podemos llevar a Mazog por ese camino. Las arañas se vuelven cada vez más densas en esa dirección, y vi una gran masa moviéndose detrás de las arañas. Hay una terrible amenaza en ese camino.\
\
'Achardor y yo permaneceremos en guardia aquí con Mazog; las arañas han tejido grandes telarañas detrás de Issuriel mientras pasaba hacia el noreste. Despeja el camino de telarañas y encuentra a Issuriel, y nosotros la seguiremos después.'","'Para bien o para mal, debemos caminar por este camino peligroso, ${PLAYER}; nuestro camino pasa por las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.\
\
'El resto de nuestra compañía ha ido por delante y mantendrá el camino para que lleves al prisionero a cada uno de ellos. Las arañas y los perros negros están por todas partes, así que mantente alerta.\
\
'Ya conoces el apoyo que puedo brindarte: puedo hacer que nuestros enemigos sangren hasta morir, o puedo apoyarte con poder o moral. Hazme saber lo que deseas gritando tus órdenes para mí con este estandarte.'","Achardor te espera para que le des una orden de apoyo utilizando su estandarte de los Malledhrim.","La posición de Sigileth en Râd Iorist está siendo atacada por las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas. Debes defender a Sigileth y a Mazog.","Has resistido un primer ataque de las arañas a lo largo de Râd Iorist y ahora deberías hablar con Sigileth.","'Esto no es como se suponía que esto iba a terminar, ${PLAYER}. No solo nuestro prisionero ha sido envenenado por el veneno de Saebereth, sino también Issuriel. Puede que no haya esperanza de supervivencia para ninguno de los dos.\
\
'No podemos continuar así. Debemos ir al puesto más cercano de los Malledhrim, para recuperarnos de este triste desarrollo.\
\
'Si podemos recuperarnos, ${PLAYER}. Si podemos.'","'No me gusta este lugar, ${PLAYER}; hubiera sido mejor tomar el camino recto hacia el este a Dol Guldur que avanzar penosamente por estos bosques infestados de arañas. Ya he matado a muchas de estas criaturas, y escuché el canto del arco de Cúcheron hacia el noroeste después de que se fue por ese camino.\
\
'Pero ese debate ha terminado, y ahora que estamos obligados a caminar por este camino, haré mi deber para el Señor y la Dama de Lórien y para esta Guardia Oculta.\
\
'¡Lucharemos juntos! Usa esta bandera de los Malledhrim para darme tus órdenes: ya sea para apoyarte completamente con ataque o defensivamente, o con una mezcla agradable de ambos.'","Sigileth te espera para hablar contigo a lo largo de Râd Iorist, en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.","La posición de Issuriel en Râd Iorist ha sido atacada por las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas. Debe ser defendida.","Issuriel ha sido gravemente herida por las arañas de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas y yace desmayada bajo la luz de la luna llena. Mazog también ha sufrido una herida y parece estar en el mismo estado."},
[7016]={"Harding and Captain Agelmund are meeting on the Officers balcony of the Meadhall.","Harding and Captain Agelmund are discussing the recent attacks by the Easterlings, and what else has set in motion around Harwick.","'I'll take you to Feldburg right away.'","Listen to Harding","'We should leave before Harding changes his mind and decides to put you in jail for questioning. Let me know when you're ready to go.'","Speak with Agelmund, Captain of the Wold","Observe the meeting of Harding and his Captain","In the meadhall of Harwick, a meeting is taking place between Harding and his Captain, Agelmund. The Easterlings are advancing into the Wold, and the Rohirrim are hard pressed to keep their defences secure.","Harding and Captain Agelmund are meeting on the Officers' balcony of the Mead Hall.","Instancia: Conoce a Harding","'Who are you, stranger, to interrupt my council? I told the guard I was not to be disturbed, save for critically important matters.\
\
'Speak up! What dire news have you?'"},
[7017]={"Shúkurz is trying to feign a believable fight.\
\
You should play along, but stay close to Brukshar while fighting.","'It's time you folks let me go -- I've had enough of Gundabad.'","You should continue following Shúkurz.","Shúkurz might have seen what you saw. It wouldn't hurt to ask him.","You tell Shúkurz of the shadows you saw.\
\
'But -- but if anyone had been in that tunnel, we would've seen them.\
\
'...now I'LL be jumping at shadows! All right, just keep your head down -- we'll be in and out fast.'","The Orcs are eager for a fight.\
\
You should try to communicate with Shúkurz... somehow.","Shúkurz waits for you a little ways into the tunnel.","Shúkurz has brought you deep into Vatug-ronk, with the hope of learning Dhúrstrok's location.","You and Shúkurz have managed to obtain Dhúrstrok's location, all while escaping with your lives. But you've been noticing strange things....\
\
You should talk to Shúkurz.","'Well, that went better than I expected! I was sure we were dead meat, but you put up a believable fight. And look -- we got a map to Dhúrstrok! Wow, it's all the way up in the catwalks. Bet the old lifts could take us there.'\
\
You tell Shúkurz about the footsteps you heard on your way here. He quickly inspects your surroundings.\
\
'Can't say I saw or heard anything strange. And you didn't see anyone? I think we should be all right.'","Talk to Shúkurz","Fight Shúkurz","Instancia: Conociendo al intendente","You should follow Shúkurz deeper into the tunnel.","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not stray too far from Brukshar</rgb>","Follow Shúkurz","Shúkurz adopts a shaky fighting stance. His eyes dart towards your weapons, but he gives a subtle nod.","You have strayed too far from Brukshar","Brukshar has called off the fight.\
\
You should continue following Shúkurz.","'Just follow my lead.'"},
[7018]={"'¡Así que este es el camino secreto que Mithrandir usó para entrar en la fortaleza del Nigromante! Raddir no habló de ello con mucho detalle, incluso con sus amigos. La experiencia lo dejó muy cambiado, y era más lento para reír y cantar de lo que había sido antes.\
\
'¡Raddir también será vengado cuando lancemos el asalto final sobre la fortaleza! Se encuentra directamente sobre nosotros aquí, y nuestros enemigos no conocen su peligro.'","Habla con Bróin","Instancia: Recuerdos de Mithrandir","Has encontrado una caverna bajo Dol Guldur y debes despejarla de enemigos si va a ser utilizada por la Hueste Dorada.","Limpia Thurimen, la caverna bajo los cimientos de Dol Guldur, de enemigos","Has encontrado una caverna excavada profundamente bajo la fortaleza de Dol Guldur. ¿Podría ser este el mismo pasaje que Gandalf utilizó para infiltrarse en la fortaleza del Nigromante hace mucho tiempo?","Avanza más en Thurimen, despejándola de enemigos","'¡No puedo creerlo, pero este pasaje es exactamente lo que necesitamos para lanzar nuestro asalto final sobre Dol Guldur! ¡Los atacaremos por sorpresa desde abajo y estaremos dentro de las murallas de la fortaleza antes de que nuestros enemigos sepan que están siendo atacados!\
\
'¡Volveremos aquí con una compañía considerable y lanzaremos nuestro asalto final!'","Bróin y Sigileth han llegado a Thurimen y están asombrados de ver lo bien que se adapta a sus propósitos.","'¿Estás listo para irnos? Volveremos a Thangúlhad y nos prepararemos para la batalla final. Este camino secreto hacia la fortaleza me da esperanza... ¡nuestra victoria está casi asegurada!'","Has despejado gran parte de Thurimen de amenazas y deberías continuar hacia adelante y hacia arriba."},
[7020]={"Listen to Elladan's tale of the Battle of Dagorlad","Listen as Elrohir concludes the tale of the Battle of Dagorlad","'In an age long-ended, a great battle was fought upon Dagorlad between the numberless armies of the Dark Lord and the Last Alliance of Elves and Men. For years, they clashed upon the battle plain, and each momentary victory and defeat dimmed the hope of the war ever coming to an end.\
\
'After many trying battles, the Last Alliance pressed southward and approached the Black Gate of Mordor. Yet, the nearer they drew to the Black Land, the more foes the Dark Lord sent forth.\
\
'But lo, Elendil the Tall and High King Gil-galad of the Noldor possessed much wisdom and valour, and soon the plans were drawn for a final assault against the Black Gate.\
\
'The Last Alliance assembled at a great bulwark and it was there they made their stand against Sauron and his armies.","Elrohir is describing the courage of Gil-galad and Elendil in the face of the Ringwraiths.","Instancia: Recuerdos de la Última Alianza","Elrohir is nearing the end of his tale. You should continue to follow along.","Elrohir and Elladan are telling you the tale of the Last Alliance's victory at the Battle of Dagorlad. You should follow along and listen as Elrohir begins the tale.","'Victories over the Dark Lord's servants would not come easily for long...\
\
'Although Orcs and evil Men fell in scores upon the battle plain, Sauron soon loosed his nine greatest servants upon the Last Alliance. Once they were Men, but twisted by the Rings given to them by the Dark Lord, they grew stretched and withered into unseen forms. As the corruption of the Rings consumed them, these Men grew beyond death itself! For in truth, the Dark Lord held their Rings and thus tethered them to service and life unending. Even if they were struck down, they were not slain -- merely banished for a time!\
\
'Many names have been bestowed upon them by those who have beheld their terrible shapes: Dwimmerlaik, Dúrchir, Gwetherain, and Nazgûl. In the tongue of Westron, their name is perhaps the most precise -- Ringwraiths!'","Listen to Elrohir's tale of the Last Alliance","As the Second Age approached its end, Elrond stood with the Last Alliance against the forces of Sauron and won a decisive victory that led to the Dark Lord's defeat.","'¡Los Nueve blandieron el miedo mismo contra la Última Alianza y todos, excepto los más audaces, temblaron ante ellos!'","The Last Alliance gathered at a great bulwark in Dagorlad and prepared to strike against the armies of Mordor.","Elrohir is describing a great battle between the Ringwraiths and the commanders of the Last Alliance.","Elrohir and Elladan are telling you the tale of the Last Alliance's victory at the Battle of Dagorlad. You should follow along and listen as Elladan continues the tale.","Listen to Elrohir's tale of the Battle of Dagorlad","Follow the Last Alliance across the flaming trench toward Mordor","'¡Ni siquiera los Nueve pudieron resistir a Aiglos y Narsil, y fueron derribados y desterrados de vuelta a Mordor!'","Elladan is describing the trials of the Last Alliance as they drew closer to the Black Gate.","'Although many of their kin fled before the Ringwraiths, Gil-galad and Elendil did not falter. Gil-galad held close the mighty spear, Aiglos, and Elendil bore the blade, Narsil -- the very sword that was broken, reforged, and wielded anew by King Elessar! They fought as one and cut through the Dark Lord's forces with a fury unlike any the Elves or Men had ever witnessed.\
\
'They soon stood before the Black Gate itself, but the battle would not be won so easily!\
\
'Alas, the Ringwraiths and a vast army of Orcs had gathered beneath the dark ramparts of the Black Gate, and they sought to stand between the Last Alliance and their Master!","'Quite the tale, my friend, was it not?'","'And so, the Battle of Dagorlad drew to a close...\
\
'The Last Alliance won a decisive victory over the Dark Lord and banished his mightiest servants back to the Black Land. The might of Men and Elves proved the greater that day, and let us hope it shall prove true once more!\
\
'Although the fighting within Mordor lasted over seven more years before Sauron himself was finally defeated, this battle turned the tide in a war that many thought unwinnable.\
\
'Yet many victories and defeats still laid ahead...'","Elrohir has finished his tale of the Battle of Dagorlad.","Follow Gil-galad and Elendil into battle against the Ringwraiths","Listen to Elrohir's final remarks","Follow the Last Alliance into battle against the armies of Mordor","'Orcos, Orientales, Sureños y bestias malvadas se alzaron en desafío a la Última Alianza de Elfos y Hombres.'"},
[7021]={"Master Elrond is waiting to speak with you in the Library of his house.","'Go now to the library upstairs, ${PLAYER}. I will meet you there, and we will discuss how the Rangers can be assembled as quickly as can be managed.'","Arwen is outside the library in the House of Elrond and wishes to speak with you.","Instancia: Mensajes de Lórien","Pethelen is in the main hall of the House of Elrond.\
\
You have entered the House of Elrond with Pethelen, and he is waiting to speak with you.","'Halros, Halbarad, and Calenglad will speak with others of the Dúnedain near the borders of the Shire and throughout the North Downs and Evendim, but there are two more Rangers you will need to find personally. The distances are simply too great for anyone but you to cover in time.'","Talk to Pethelen","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I will send for you when this item is ready.'","'I am pleased you received my summons, ${PLAYER}. I apologize for being so close as to the reason for its urgency, but there are dangers on the road, and I did not wish any information that might do us harm to fall into the hands of evil Men.\
\
'Two days ago, courier-hawks arrived in Rivendell bearing messages from Lórien. The messages were short, but even in their brevity they caused me pause.\
\
'The messages are from the Lady Galadriel. I understand some of their meaning, but I can only guess at the full import of her words.'","'It will not be easy to gather the Dúnedain as quickly as it must be done, ${PLAYER}. It would be best for you to bring the message to certain of Aragorn's kin, that they may then speak to the rest of their people, while you travel to those of more distant lands.\
\
'I have prepared the names of those to whom you must speak. Walk with me, and I will tell you where they can be found.'","Enter the Hall of Fire","'And so it shall be, ${PLAYER}. You will walk the paths of Eriador one more time, in search of these Dúnedain. They will gather others of their kin, and when all is made ready, the Grey Company will set forth.\
\
'It will be done as Galadriel of Lórien has asked. We respond to her messages with the haste we must, and with the messenger those messages deserve: a ${CLASS} of proven loyalty, to gather the Grey Company in time!'","'Very good, ${PLAYER}. Many hopes rest on your journey through Eriador to gather the Dúnedain for their journey!'","'I know of the messages from my grandmother, ${PLAYER}, and I know too that my father has asked you to gather the Dúnedain that they may ride south to the aid of Aragorn.\
\
'We knew this day would come, he and I, and have both long prepared for its arrival. It has been my part to craft an item of beauty and of use, an item Aragorn will have need of before all is done. He knows of its making, and it will be a sign to him that the hour has indeed arrived when he must seize that which is his. I hope it will be a comfort to him, too, in distant lands.\
\
'When the Dúnedain are all assembled, I will send for you. I must be sure someone can bear this item to him. I will call you before the Rangers depart.'","Habla con Elrohir","Lord Elrond has asked to meet you in the library of his house to further discuss the charge: to gather the Dúnedain that they may ride to the aid of Aragorn in Rohan.","'Unless it is forbidden, be sure to tell me what is going on, ${PLAYER}! Now, hurry into the Hall of Fire to speak with Master Elrond!'","Talk to Master Elrond","'Golodir was a strong man and true of heart, but my father is right. He has suffered much. I did not know.\
\
'I know very little of Corunir, beyond that he be loyal to a fault. Did he not remain in Aughaire for years, awaiting Golodir's return from beyond the Rammas Deluon?'","Master Elrond is waiting inside the library of his house to speak with you.","The Lady Arwen catches your eye and smiles a greeting","Enter the Library in the House of Elrond","Talk to Lord Elrond","'Once you have met Radanir in the Trollshaws and told him that the Rangers must assemble, you should travel west into the Lone-lands. At the base of Weathertop, you will find Candaith. He is sure to join the Grey Company.\
\
'After you have spoken to Candaith, you will travel into Bree-land to speak with Saeradan at his cabin. He is not as prone to wandering as others of his kin, but he must be told of Aragorn's need.\
\
'But there are other Rangers you must find.'","Elrohir is in the library of his father's house.","Master Elrond is in the Hall of Fire inside his house in Rivendell, waiting to speak with you.","Lord Elrond is waiting to speak with you in the library of his house.","'What you say fills me with foreboding, ${PLAYER}. I do not know all the details of the journey on which Aragorn set forth last December, but if Lady Galadriel says he has need of his kin, well... that can mean nothing good, can it?\
\
'Lord Elrond said he would meet you in the library for further discussion of how to gather the Dúnedain? You should go there at once! It is just upstairs.'","Walk to the Library in the House of Elrond","Talk to Lady Arwen","Master Elrond is waiting for you in the Hall of Fire, inside the Last Homely House.","You have come to Imladris in response to an urgent summons from Master Elrond.","'Very good, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps now we will have an answer for why this haste is necessary.\
\
'Is that Elladan? It is! Perhaps he will have some answers for us.'","Master Elrond is in the library of his house."},
[7022]={"Debes debilitar la respuesta del campamento a tu ataque emboscando y eliminando a varios de sus guardias veteranos antes de que comience la fase principal del asalto.","'¿Estás listo para volver a Echad Dúnann entonces?'","Guardias veteranos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tiendas quemadas (${VALUE}/40)","Toma una tea de la hoguera","Usa la antigua forja para potenciar tu adamantita infundida.","Coge antorchas de la hoguera en el centro del campamento dunlendino y prende fuego a tantas tiendas como sea posible para crear pánico y desorden.","Instancia: Incursión de medianoche","Derrota a los guardias veteranos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Vaya espectáculo habéis montado aquí, amigos míos. Los dunlendinos no os perdonarán pronto vuestras hazañas de esta noche.'","Habla con Perimbant","Usa el yunque antiguo","<rgb=#FF0000>Hoguera apagada (${VALUE}/6)</rgb>","Has creado una adamantita potenciada","Capitán dunlendino derrotado","Debes encontrar y derrotar al capitán dunlendino antes de que pueda reunir a sus tropas para repeler tu asalto.","¡Un soldado desesperado ha apagado la hoguera!","Derrota al capitán dunlendino","Habla con Perimbant para volver a Echad Dúnann.","Sin que lo sepan los dunlendinos de Eregion, su campamento más grande se ha construido sobre una antigua forja de elfos donde una vez se forjaron algunas de las mejores armas de principios de la Tercera Edad. Para poder acceder a esta forja, Perimbant ha ideado un audaz plan para asaltar el campamento a través del río a la luz de la luna, entrando a hurtadillas para vencer a los guardias y prender fuego a gran parte del campamento, dispersando a los desprevenidos defensores en el caos de la batalla y las llamas."},
[7023]={"'¡Puedo apuntar a miembros específicos de nuestros enemigos para ralentizar su velocidad de ataque o de movimiento, o hacer llover sobre ellos una furia tan grande con mi arco Cumaeth que sus defensas se rompan! Dime cuál de estas tácticas quieres que use usando esta bandera de los Malledhrim!'","Has advertido a Achardor del intento de escape de Mazog, y ahora el Orco puede ser recapturado.","Habla con Bróin","Con el corazón encogido, notas el cuerpo de un Elfo junto al estanque estancado","Bróin está en la Bodega Desolada, esperando para hablar contigo.","'Según Raddir, este es el punto medio de Râd Cened, el camino que ha elegido para que tomemos a través del Bosque Ahogado. ¡Eres afortunado, Mazog, de que necesitemos que estés vivo! Si fuera mi decisión, o la de Achardor, ya estarías muerto y dejado para pudrirte dentro de una de las fétidas piscinas de este pantano.'\
\
Mazog no dice nada, y Sigileth continúa.\
\
'Este estandarte de la Hueste Dorada te permitirá seleccionar un rol de apoyo para que yo lo use durante la batalla, ${PLAYER}. Puedo extraer la sangre vital de nuestros enemigos con Lanchigil y Egnassigil o proporcionarte apoyo de moral o poder. Depende de ti.'","Examinar el cuerpo","Issuriel te espera para hablar contigo a lo largo del camino de Râd Cened.","Cúcheron ha explorado la siguiente etapa de tu viaje a través del Bosque Ahogado con Mazog.","Cúcheron te ha pedido que despejes el túnel al noreste de su posición de peligro mientras él vigila a Mazog y luego regreses con él.","La posición de Cúcheron a lo largo del camino de la Guardia Oculta a través del Bosque Ahogado ha sido atacada. Debes defender a Mazog de estos enemigos.","¡Mazog está intentando escapar! Debes llegar a Achardor antes que él","Usa el estandarte de la Hueste Dorada para dar órdenes de apoyo a Sigileth","'Este viaje ya nos ha costado mucho, ${PLAYER}, y con cada pérdida, se vuelve más difícil mantener a este desgraciado con vida.\
\
'No soporto mirarlo. Contar el dolor que ya nos ha costado llevaría mucho tiempo, y me preocupa que no haya terminado de agregar a eso.\
\
'Dejemos esta bodega por ahora. Achardor lo vigilará... y Sigileth y los demás vigilarán a Achardor.'","'¡Grita tus órdenes para mi rol de apoyo junto a este estandarte de los Malledhrim, ${PLAYER}! Soy experta en extraer la sangre de mis enemigos con mis cuchillos gemelos, Lanchigil y Egnassigil, pero también soy experta en restaurar el moral y el poder agotados.'","Issuriel te ha pedido que asegures las cadenas de Mazog y que lo escoltes a través de los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado hasta Cúcheron, que espera un poco más adelante.","Habla con Achardor en la bodega de la Posada Embrujada","¡Los Râd Cened Creepers se han reunido para atacar a los intrusos en el Bosque Ahogado! ¡Debes defender a Mazog de esta amenaza!","Tras la muerte de Raddir, la Guardia Oculta ha avanzado cojeando hasta la bodega de una posada entre los Troncosombríos, allí para decidir qué se puede hacer.","Habla con Sigileth","Cúcheron está esperando para preguntarte algo, ahora que los ataques han cesado por el momento.","No has logrado llegar a Achardor antes que Mazog","'El recuerdo de nuestro desesperado viaje por tierra para salir del Bosque Ahogado es borroso, ${PLAYER}, pero hemos llegado a Audaghaim. Es un lugar para lamer nuestras heridas, aunque no todas nuestras heridas pueden ser curadas, aquí o en cualquier otro lugar.\
\
'¡No puedo creer que Raddir se haya ido! ¿Puede nuestra misión haber fracasado incluso antes de comenzar?\
\
'Afilaré mi espada. Puede que pronto beba la sangre de nuestro prisionero, una vez que veamos la sabiduría y abandonemos esta imprudente misión.'","Habla con Achardor","Asegura las cadenas de Mazog","'¿El túnel está despejado? Bien. Luché contra algunos lagartos de pantano más, pero no fue nada que no pudiera manejar con Cúmaeth.\
\
'Asegúrate de que las cadenas de Mazog estén seguras y tráelo a través del túnel. No deberías tener más problemas.'","Sigileth ha explorado la siguiente etapa de tu viaje a través del Bosque Ahogado con Mazog.","Despeja el túnel de peligros para que Mazog pueda ser escoltado de manera segura a través de él","Issuriel te espera para hablar contigo en el camino de Râd Cened.\
\
Has recorrido parte del camino elegido por Raddir a través del Bosque Ahogado y ahora debes seguir el camino de Râd Cened con Mazog.","Lo impensable ha ocurrido: Raddir ha sido asesinado en el Bosque Ahogado.","Cúcheron te ha pedido que uses su estandarte de la Hueste Dorada para dar órdenes que le permitan apoyarte en la batalla.","Instancia: Medianoche en el Bosque Ahogado","La posición de Sigileth a lo largo del camino de la Guardia Oculta a través del Bosque Ahogado ha sido atacada. Debes defender a Mazog de estos enemigos.","Habla con Issuriel","Revisas las cadenas de Mazog y siguen seguras. Te mira evaluándote, lo cual es de alguna manera más desconcertante que su habitual mueca.","Sigileth te ha pedido que uses su estandarte de la Hueste Dorada para dar órdenes que ella pueda apoyarte en la batalla.","'Hemos hecho bien en repeler a los trepadores del Bosque Ahogado, ${PLAYER}, pero estoy seguro de que habrá más. Debemos proteger a Mazog de sus espinas y zarcillos, aunque nuestros corazones no estén completamente en ello.\
\
'Asegúrate de que sus cadenas estén seguras y avanza con él a través del pantano. Cúcheron debería estar justo adelante.'","Usa el estandarte de la Hueste Dorada para dar órdenes de apoyo a Issuriel","Defiende a Mazog","Mazog tiene una mirada siniestra en sus ojos. Asegúrate de que sus cadenas permanezcan seguras.","'El túnel está justo al noreste, ${PLAYER}. Despeja los peligros y luego regresa a mí. Me quedaré aquí y vigilaré a Mazog hasta tu regreso.'","Habla con Cúcheron","'Usa este estandarte de la Hueste Dorada para darme órdenes, ${PLAYER}. Haré todo lo posible para apoyarte en la batalla restaurando el moral y el poder.'","Cúcheron está fuera del túnel, vigilando a Mazog y esperando tu regreso.","Le explicas a Cúcheron que deseas despejar el túnel de peligros antes de llevar a Mazog a través de él, y Raddir asiente.\
\
'Es una buena idea; las enredaderas aquí permanecieron dormidas para que Sigileth y yo pudiéramos pasar, pero por supuesto Mazog habría intentado despertarlas en el peor momento posible. ¡Cúcheron es quizás más astuto de lo que le di crédito!'\
\
Raddir parece pensar por un momento, y luego comienza vacilante.\
\
'Volví aquí porque pensé que vi... pensé que vi a alguien que conocía, ${PLAYER}... un amigo. Pero no podía ser, porque este amigo... este amigo no ha caminado por este camino durante muchos años y desde entonces ha ido a donde nadie puede seguirlo.\
\
'Si no supiera mejor, habría jurado que era él. Pero aquí no hay nada más que enredaderas. Fue un truco de la luz, mi error en la penumbra.'","'El paso hasta ahora ha sido tranquilo, pero nuestra suerte en este miserable pantano puede cambiar en un momento, si bajamos la guardia; ¡así que no debemos hacerlo!\
\
'Si te colocas junto a este estandarte y me gritas tus órdenes, puedo proporcionar apoyo en la batalla. Las flechas que dejo volar desde Cúmaeth pueden ralentizar la velocidad de ataque de nuestros enemigos o dificultar su movimiento; además, puedo bombardear a nuestros enemigos con tal lluvia de flechas que sus defensas generales se rompen.\
\
'¡Usa este estandarte de los Malledhrim durante la batalla para indicarme cuál de estas tácticas deseas!'","'No podemos hablar aquí, ${PLAYER}. Hemos impedido la fuga del Orco pero ahora, debemos reunir a la Guardia Oculta para preparar un nuevo plan. Sin Raddir...'\
\
El rostro de Achardor es una tormenta de emociones. Se controla a sí mismo, pero claramente es un esfuerzo.\
\
'Debemos reunirnos con los Malledhrim. Hay una aldea llamada Audaghaim entre los Troncosombríos. El plan era que el cuerpo principal de los Malledhrim la usara como punto de abastecimiento antes de avanzar más en el Bosque Negro. Debemos ir allí y discutir qué se debe hacer.'","Es hora de llevar a Mazog más lejos por Râd Cened, la ruta que Raddir ha seleccionado para llevar a la Guardia Oculta a través del peligroso Bosque Ahogado.","Has logrado ponerte delante de Mazog y puedes impedir su escape","La Guardia Oculta comienza el peligroso cruce del Bosque Ahogado con Mazog.","Te aseguras de que las cadenas de Mazog permanezcan seguras. Una vez más, el Orco te recompensa solo con una mirada evaluadora.","Te aseguras de que las cadenas de Mazog estén seguras. El Orco te mira con desprecio, y sus ojos brillan de odio.","'Hemos recorrido parte del camino, ${PLAYER}, pero aún queda un largo camino por recorrer; el Bosque Ahogado es peligroso, y aunque Raddir ha elegido nuestro camino con cuidado, aún debemos tener precaución. El resto de la Guardia Oculta se ha adelantado, porque no podemos avanzar como grupo si queremos mantener nuestro secreto. Llevarás a Mazog a los miembros de nuestra compañía, más adelante en el pantano.\
\
'¿Escuchaste eso? ¡Algo se acerca! Dejaré la coordinación de nuestro ataque en tus manos; grita tus órdenes para mí junto a este estandarte, y repelaremos cualquier mal que se acerque. Mis talentos son para la restauración del moral y el poder, aunque no serán de utilidad para nuestro prisionero. ¡No dejes que Mazog sufra heridas!'","Llamas su nombre e intentas obtener una respuesta del Elfo, pero ya es demasiado tarde: Raddir está muerto.\
\
No hay señales de lucha ni marcas de heridas que puedas ver, pero a pesar de ese enigma, una cosa está clara: la Guardia Oculta ha perdido a uno de los suyos.","Sigileth te está esperando para hablar contigo, ahora que los ataques han cesado por el momento.","Sigileth te ha pedido que asegures las cadenas de Mazog y lo escoltes a través de los pantanos del Bosque Ahogado hasta Raddir, que espera más adelante.","'Hemos hecho bien en repeler estos ataques, ${PLAYER}. Asegúrate de que las cadenas de Mazog permanezcan seguras y llévalo más adentro del Bosque Ahogado.\
\
'Te encontrarás con Raddir a continuación a lo largo de Râd Cened. Dale mis gracias por planificar esta ruta. Hemos hecho bien en superar sus peligros, y la presencia de Mazog sigue siendo un secreto para los Orcos del Bosque Negro.'","'Necesito un poco de aire fresco, ${PLAYER}. Vamos a salir al porche de la posada. La vista de nuestro prisionero me hace sentir mal.'","Issuriel te ha pedido que uses su estandarte de la Hueste Dorada para dar órdenes que le permitan apoyarte en la batalla contra cualquier amenaza.","¡Mazog está intentando escapar! Debes llegar a Achardor, más adelante en el camino elegido por Raddir a través del Bosque Ahogado, antes de que lo haga Mazog.","'No he visto criaturas de ese tipo a una legua de Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}. Me llenan de asco. Aún así, triunfamos sobre ellas, y Cúmaeth tiene muchas flechas en reserva.\
\
'Hay un túnel justo adelante; se encuentra en la ruta que Raddir seleccionó para nosotros. No quiero llevar a Mazog por allí hasta que sepamos que está despejado.\
\
'Me quedaré aquí y vigilaré a Mazog. Entra en el túnel y límpialo de cualquier peligro y luego regresa aquí a mí. Entonces podrás llevar al Orco de forma segura a través del túnel.'","Llega a Achardor antes que Mazog","'¡Qué alegría! Miren cómo caen los Elfos que buscan encarcelarme, uno por uno. ¡Quizás tú seas el siguiente, ${PLAYER}, ${RACE} que lo merece tanto!\
\
'¡Acaben con todos los enemigos de Mazog, Señor de las Cuevas! Ninguna cadena puede atarme para siempre, y si mis manos están atadas, que mis piernas me lleven a los aliados que deben haber hecho esto, los aliados que incluso ahora buscan liberarme de esta esclavitud.\
\
'¡Ho, Orcos de mi lejano linaje! ¡Buscan liberar a Mazog, y él será libre con las recompensas de la generosidad!'","Usa el estandarte de la Hueste Dorada para dar órdenes de apoyo a Cúcheron","Regresa a Cúcheron"},
[7027]={"La lluvia y el viento se han vuelto muy intensos, y Bingo quiere encontrar un lugar resguardado donde quedarse.","El Nazgûl ha huido.","'¡Busquemos a Bingo antes de que la tormenta empeore!'","Un Nazgûl ha descendido sobre las llanuras de Rohan, ¡y Bingo está en peligro!","Egwylf cree que podrías ahuyentar al Nazgûl si logras prender fuego a la hierba.","Recoge la antorcha del suelo donde ha caído","Habla con Egwylf","¡Necesitas tomar la antorcha para poder prender fuego a la hierba!","Mientras viajas por las llanuras de Rohan con Bingo, Egwylf y Willem Bigote, una fuerte tormenta ha estorbado vuestro avance.","Busca un lugar donde refugiarte de la tormenta","El Nazgûl sisea con furia. ¡No quiere acercarse a las llamas!","Protege a Egwylf y Willem del Nazgûl","Protege a Bingo del Nazgûl","'¡Esta tormenta surgió muy de repente, ${PLAYER}! ¡Deberíamos buscar un lugar donde refugiarnos de la lluvia y el viento!\
\
'¡También estoy bastante nervioso por los rayos!'","Te has visto ${PLAYERNAME:atrapado[m]|atrapada[f]} en la tormenta junto a Bingo, Egwylf y Willem.","¡La llama prende!","'Tenemos que encontrar a Bingo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Esa criatura podría volver!'","Habla con Bingo antes de que la tormenta empeore","Instancia: Identidad equivocada"},
[7028]={"Talk to Horn in Stangard","Nona is standing on a small rise amidst rocks in the Rushgore.\
\
Some terrible presence has come near to you in the Rushgore.","Horn is waiting to speak to you about the price for healing Nona.","Galadriel has come to speak with you about Nona.","The Nazgûl stands atop the hill. You need to find a means of driving it off!","Travel to Lothlórien to seek the aid of Galadriel","Survive your encounter with great evil in the Rushgore","Talk to Nona atop the rocky rise in the Rushgore","Find Nona! She is in grave danger!","Horn is standing uncomfortably in Lothlórien, waiting to speak with you.","Bring Nona to Stangard for the healing she needs","An evil presence has come to the Rushgore, and you are in great danger!","'Do not... let them...'\
\
Nona struggles to speak, but the effort is too great for her to make out the words. She beseeches you with wide eyes, but you cannot meet her stare. Your gaze keeps returning to the blood soaking the floor beneath her.\
\
She tries again.\
\
'Wadu's... it was...'\
\
You cannot give the Rohirrim what they demand. There has to be another way to save her life.","An Easterling has attempted to escape, and you need to defeat him before he alerts his fellows.","You are returning with Nona to Stangard, in order to regroup and plan your next move.","Suddenly, a woman's scream pierces the stillness! Nona is in trouble!","Horn is waiting for your answer in Stangard.","You hastily grab the fallen torch, burning your hand!","'${PLAYER}... is everything... all right?'\
\
Nona's breathing is ragged and shallow, and the gash in her side still bleeds around the cloths with which you tried to staunch it.\
\
When you brought her to Stangard she was barely conscious. You found Horn near the entrance and begged for his people to tend to Nona's hurts. He sought out the leader of Stangard to see what could be done, and has not yet returned.","'I will never call my people distrustful again, ${PLAYER}. The blindfold felt somewhat unnecessary to me. Only the most urgent of need has driven me here, and I would not want to return!'\
\
Horn's face softens, and his brow creases with worry.\
\
'Do you think the girl will recover? I saw the way those Elves looked at her wound. Whatever they saw there, they did not like it. If it was not an Easterling blade... what does that mean for her? What is wrong? ${PLAYER}?'","'There has to be some other way, ${PLAYER}. You spoke of the Elf-witch in the woods to the north along Anduin. My people shun that place as a den of evil glamour, but... if there was a power that could heal this girl...'\
\
Horn glowers at you, his eyebrows knitted together angrily.\
\
'A pox on her! I will not have her blood on my hands, or on her own. Lead us to this Elf-witch, ${PLAYER}! I have heard the tales. Perhaps she will be unable to bewitch me if I am expecting it! Why did you ever bring this girl to Stangard, ${PLAYER}? This is not her place.'\
\
Horn gazes into the middle distance, and in a quiet voice he continues.\
\
'In Stangard, is a sword valued more highly than the life of a girl? What sort of man would willingly serve in such a place?'\
\
He shakes his head, and the urgency returns to his voice.\
\
'Well? For what are you waiting? Let us go at once!'","'I will not run from you. I am your better. My people have powerful friends. I will show them how strong a man of the Khundolar can be!'","Nona is somewhere in the Rushgore, and it sounds like she's in trouble!","Talk to Horn in Lothlórien","'The danger has passed, ${PLAYER}. The wound was deep, but it did not fester. And yet, I did not wish to leave this girl to the care of my healers. The risk that her wound was caused by a morgul blade, and that she could become a wraith like the creature you encountered that night, compelled me to heal her hurts personally. If that had proven the case, I would have ended her suffering. It would have been a mercy, and necessary to safe-guard Lothlórien and indeed all lands.\
\
'Do you think me cruel? I am glad it did not come to that. I do not believe her wound was caused by a morgul blade, and it is my hope and belief she will live. I am... surprised. We will speak more of it later, away from watchful ears.\
\
'The girl Nona is sleeping. When she is awake you will be brought to her. For now you should rest, ${PLAYER}. Dream no troubling dreams! In Lothlórien your rest will be peaceful. I am certain of it.'","Nona is struggling to speak.","Survive the Easterling ambush and prevent any of them from alerting their fellows","Nona lies crumpled on the ground before you, soaking in the blood from a sword-wound in her side. She struggles weakly to speak.\
\
'${PLAYER}... are you...?'\
\
The effort is too great for her; she needs the aid of a healer if she is to survive this wound. In the back of your mind, one worrying question refuses to go away. From what blade did she take this wound? Did an Easterling blade cause this injury, or was it the blade of the Nazgûl?\
\
You prepare yourself for the long journey back to Stangard with Nona.","There are Easterlings in the mists of the Rushgore, and something worse beside!","You are making your way through the Rushgore with Nona.","Instancia: Nieblas del Anduin","'Something is near, ${PLAYER}! It must be the wraith we have sought... it makes my blood run cold!'\
\
Nona looks at you with wide eyes, and you are suddenly reminded that she has not had much experience with creatures of such evil. She puts her hand on the hilt of Wadu's sword, her sword, and her former fright is replaced with grim determination.\
\
'We found it. Now what do we do with it?'","'There is clearly some glamour on this land. I feel as if I could take on any foe and achieve victory, or cross any landscape, no matter the obstacles!\
\
'Your Elf-witch works wonders! Only song could do justice to her powers of healing! The relief I feel is... it is overwhelming, ${PLAYER}. The girl will live!\
\
'Unless it is rude to ask it, I would like to return to the forest floor now. I will return to Stangard by myself, but I would like to see you again! Once the girl is recovered, bring her as well. If I am to compose a song of your adventure, I will need both of your accounts, after all.'","'We have a long way to go, ${PLAYER}. As much as I wish we did not need to refuge at the town of the horse-lords, it seems we must. We have lost the trail of this creature, this wraith of which you speak, and until we can learn where it has gone we are only wasting time.\
\
'It is frustrating to know our purpose and be unable to accomplish it!'","Talk to Nona in the Rushgore","You have brought Nona to Stangard, but do not know if the Rohirrim will be able to save her life.","Talk to Nona where she lies in Stangard","Talk to the Khundolar Captain","'I did my best for you, ${PLAYER}, but you are not going to be pleased. He did not understand why we should heal the hurts of this Dunlending girl.\
\
'Eventually he relented somewhat, and he has agreed that our healers will do what they can for the girl.'","You have come to seek the aid of Galadriel. Will she give it?","Talk to Galadriel in Lothlórien","You are walking through the Rushgore with Nona when she stops and wants to talk to you about something.","Walk with Nona through the Rushgore"},
[7029]={"'No deberíamos demorarnos más aquí. ¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para marcharte? Te mostraré los caminos secretos para salir de Carn Dûm y regresar a Gath Forthnír.'","Instancia: La Caída de Mordirith","Con la luz de Dúnachar, Golodir ha derrotado a Mordirith, aunque el villano escapó antes de poder ser vencido por completo. Deberías hablar con Golodir para ver qué desea que hagas.","'Qué final tan inquietante para nuestra batalla. Temo que haya mucho más en esa anciana de lo que vemos en la superficie.\
\
'Sin embargo, no podemos ocuparnos de ese asunto ahora. ¡Debemos irnos de aquí antes de que nos veamos superados por los angmarim o sus servidores!'","Ayuda a Golodir mientras te adentras más en el Castillo del Rey Brujo.","Has viajado muy adentro de Carn Dûm junto a Golodir, hasta la propia fortaleza del Rey Brujo. Aquí Golodir espera enfrentarse a Mordirith y destruir la Corona de Hierro para siempre.","Deberías hablar con Golodir de inmediato.","'Mordirith el cobarde ha escapado... pero ¿notaste que la hoja de Dúnachar seguía incrustada en su pecho? Apuesto a que el dolor de la luz de esa hoja será un recordatorio constante del mal que ha cometido.\
\
'Mientras mi venganza aún no se ha completado, apostaría a que habrá otros que culminen esta tarea. Por ahora, puedo hallar consuelo en este hecho...\
\
'¡Un momento, alguien se acerca!'","'Parece que mi largo cautiverio en Carn Dûm nos ha sido útil. Hemos llegado muy adentro de la fortaleza del Rey Brujo sin ser detectados. Sería una locura pensar, no obstante, que nuestra fortuna se mantendrá. Ya Mordirith podría ser consciente de nuestra presencia.\
\
'Prepárate para la batalla que se avecina. Tengo pocos consejos que ofrecerte, salvo advertirte que Mordirith es un maestro del engaño y la ilusión. Intentará quebrar tu determinación con sus palabras. ¡No lo permitas! Aférrate a tu esperanza y confía en tus compañeros.\
\
'¿Partimos ahora?'","Habla con Golodir"},
[7030]={"Talk to Golasgil between the slag hills","'I will stay here and guard Calenglad's body from our foes, ${PLAYER}. You are needed to the west, between the slag hills, for the soldiers there are hard-pressed! Go, quickly!'","Find Pippin atop the western slag hill","Golasgil has been thrown to the ground by a great Olog, and now the beast seeks to finish what it began.","You have heard Pippin's voice from above the din of battle. He needs your help!","Golasgil has been mortally wounded.","Talk to Beregond atop the western slag hill","Beregond is atop the western slag hill, calling for help.","Talk to Golasgil where he lies","Pippin does not move","The armies of Mordor converge on the slag hills as Aragorn and the Host of the West prepare for the final assault.","Aragorn is atop the eastern slag hill, ready to engage once more with the enemies that approach.","Stand your ground and defend Aragorn","'My kinsmen and these others have cast back all of the enemy's advances to this point, ${PLAYER}. We must not fail now!'","Talk to Aragorn atop the eastern slag hill","Help soldiers caught between the slag hills","Instancia: Mordor Triunfante","The battle rages all around you, and Beregond intends to rally the forces to keep fighting until the end.","Pippin lies beneath a great Olog atop the western slag hill.","Golasgil of Anfalas has been caught between the slag hills and needs your help.","You have found Beregond, but Pippin does not stand with him","Defeat the Olog that crushed Golasgil","You hear a scream from above. That was Pippin's voice!","Check on Pippin where he lies","Aragorn has asked you to make your way to the western slag hill and to help soldiers caught in the middle of the fighting.","'The halfling... he saved my life! I was stunned and fell beneath the press of battle, but even as the great troll reached out to end my life, Peregrin stabbed it with his blade!\
\
'He slew the beast, but it fell upon him and I fear he is dead!'","Find Calenglad where he fell on the battlefield","'I cannot see you, friend... everything is... darkness...\
\
'I know I do not... do not have long. Fight on... fight on...\
\
'If there is a day to come... after this... look to the people... of Anfalas. Tell them... tell them their lord...'","'There is no end to this onslaught, ${PLAYER}! As long as we remain divided, we are weak. We must move as a group if we are to stand long.\
\
'We must fight back to King Elessar before it is too late!'","'Do not... give up... ${PLAYER}. Remember...'\
\
Calenglad coughs weakly, but he smiles despite the pain.\
\
'From above... I saw light. It cannot... be quenched...\
\
'The new age...'","The eastern slag hill has come under heavy attack, and Aragorn calls his kinsmen to him for the final defence.","Great shouting and clamour rises from the west","Aragorn has asked you to find Calenglad where he fell, if you can, and ease his pain.","'We have to do something about those flying beasts, or there will be no one left to carry on the fight!\
\
'Follow me, ${PLAYER}! We must find some archers!'","'Oh no! Help me!'"},
[7031]={"'Encontrémonos con Mordrambor, ${PLAYER}. Tenemos mucho que decirle... y mucho que oír, me temo.\
\
'Debemos estar en guardia. Aprendamos de la locura de Laerdan, y de la nuestra: incluso en cautiverio, un Númenóreano Negro puede causar grandes males.'","Calenglad está dentro de la fortaleza de Tinnudir.\
\
Mordrambor ha escapado, dejando tras de sí muertos y moribundos.","Encuentra a Tadan","Calenglad está dentro de la fortaleza de Tinnudir.\
\
Tú y Calenglad habéis entrado en la fortaleza de Tinnudir para enfrentar a Mordrambor, el Númenóreano Negro encarcelado.","'${PLAYER}... era Tann Morgul. Intenté traerlo... a Calenglad... pero...\
\
'Mordrambor... sus hechicerías...'","Calenglad está dentro de la fortaleza de Tinnudir.\
\
Has entrado en la fortaleza de Tinnudir para enfrentar a Mordrambor, el Númenóreano Negro encarcelado.","Tadan está en la habitación en lo alto de las escaleras, donde Mordrambor estaba encerrado.\
\
El Númenóreano Negro ha escapado de su prisión, y no hay rastro de su carcelero.","Enfrenta a Mordrambor con Calenglad","'Debemos reparar los daños causados a la fortaleza, pero algunas heridas no tendrán cura.'","Instancia: Mordrambor","Calenglad ha decidido enfrentar a Mordrambor y averiguar si sabe algo sobre Narchuil.","'Mordrambor se ha ido, ${PLAYER}, y deja a muchos de mi gente muertos o muriendo. Parece que urdió crueles hechicerías en la mente de su carcelero: ¿cuántas veces resolvió Tadan traerme Tann Morgul, solo para que el asunto se desvaneciera de su memoria? Está claro que esta reliquia de maldad otorgó a nuestro prisionero parte del poder que buscaba.\
\
'¡No! ¡No culpes a Tadan por esto! Cualquiera de nosotros podría haber caído igual. Le fue encomendada una tarea peligrosa, y ahora ha llegado al final de su servicio. Llora por él, pero no le atribuyas culpa alguna: esta recae solo en Angmar y en sus crueles siervos.'"},
[7032]={"Espera a que Skardí Doblafilos deje tu equipo sobre el mostrador y luego tómalo.","'Espero que no te importe que te observe. No vemos muchos aventureros por aquí. Lo más cercano suele ser ese Meneldir. Dice que es un Montaraz, pero yo diría que es solo una excusa para tener tierra en la ropa y desaparecer en lo salvaje a todas horas...\
\
'Pero en fin, Musgovilla es una aldea tranquila. ¡Siempre lo ha sido! No causes problemas y podrás quedarte cuanto quieras. Pero antes debes visitar a nuestro herrero, Skardí Doblafilos. Él limpiará y arreglará tu equipo. Su tienda está subida por esos escalones. Busca el cartel con el yunque.'","'¡Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un aventurero[m]|una aventurera[f]}, puedo verlo! ¿Qué te trae a Musgovilla?'\
\
Antes de que puedas responder, el enano sigue hablando.\
\
'Este es un pueblo tranquilo, y su gente lo prefiere así. ¿Bevan te advirtió que no perturbes la paz? Claro que sí. Me lo dice a mí casi cada quincena, como si yo fuera a convocar a un grupo de enanos alborotadores de mi tierra natal en cualquier momento. ¡Bwahahaha! ¡Ojalá pudiera!\
\
'¿Cómo dijiste que te llamabas?'","El guardia en la puerta de Musgovilla te saluda con una sonrisa amistosa, haciéndote señas para que te acerques.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Avanza presionando W, y haz clic derecho sobre Bevan para hablar con él)</rgb>","¡Madthrug ha sido derrotado!","Musgovilla está bajo ataque, y Meneldir necesita tu ayuda para salvar la aldea.","Habla con Meneldir y completa la misión 'Un Mundo Más Grande'","Has encontrado a uno de los villanos responsables del ataque a la aldea de Musgovilla. ¿Qué ha traído a trasgos como este a la Ciénaga de los Cisnes?","Has derrotado al trasgo, pero no pudo haber provocado todos estos incendios él solo. Sin duda tiene aliados cerca.","El repique de las campanas indica que el peligro ha llegado a Musgovilla","Bevan en la puerta te recomendó que te presentaras a Geralt, uno de los habitantes de Musgovilla.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Avanza con W, gira izquierda y derecha con A y D, retrocede con S)</rgb>","'¡Debes seguir a Meneldir afuera, ${PLAYER}! ¡Yo iré detrás de ti!'","Habla con Geralt junto a la fuente en la plaza del pueblo\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Puedes avanzar presionando W y girar hacia la izquierda o derecha con A y D)</rgb>","Meneldir ha salido apresurado de la herrería, y debes seguirlo\
\
El repique de las campanas indica que algún problema ha llegado a Musgovilla","'¡Muchas gracias por salvar a nuestro hijo de esas horribles criaturas! ¿Qué eran? ¿Alguna raza de orco? ¿Por qué vendrían a Musgovilla?\
\
'¡Somos muy afortunados de que estuvieras aquí!'","Skardí Doblafilos te ha pedido que dejes tu equipo sobre el mostrador, y él lo arreglará gratis... esta vez.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho en el punto brillante para dejar tu equipo sobre el mostrador)</rgb>","'Pero como iba diciendo, ¡Musgovilla es una aldea tranquila! ¡Siempre lo ha sido! No causes problemas y podrás quedarte cuanto quieras. Pero antes que nada: deberías visitar a nuestro herrero, Skardí Doblafilos. Él limpiará y arreglará tu equipo. Su tienda está justo subiendo esos escalones. Busca el cartel con el yunque.'","Toma tu equipo del mostrador y habla con Skardí Doblafilos\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho en el saco para abrirlo y ver su contenido. Haz clic derecho en los objetos dentro para recogerlos y ponerlos en tu inventario. Pulsa “I” para ver tu Inventario)</rgb>","'Mi amigo Skardí dice la verdad: no quieres entrar en batalla sin tus armas equipadas, pues no te servirán de nada en el fondo de tus bolsas. También tiene razón en esto: Musgovilla es un pueblo tranquilo, y pocos aventureros pasan por aquí, y menos aún alguien que se porta como tú. ¿Qué camino te ha traído a Musgovilla, en la frontera de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes, ${PLAYER:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}?'\
\
Consideras qué deberías decir de tu pasado a este curioso desconocido. ¿Hablarías de una crianza que te dio el deseo de ver maravillas lejanas, o de los peligros que incluso ahora amenazan a los Pueblos Libres, obligándote a luchar por aquellos que no pueden? Antes de que puedas elegir palabras, Meneldir alza la palma.","Derrota a Madthrug","¡Madthrug se lanza a atacarte!","Quédate junto a Meneldir y permanece alerta","Espera a que Skardí Doblafilos deje tu equipo sobre el mostrador y entonces recógelo.","Habla con Eleri","Equipa tus armas y habla con Meneldir dentro de la herrería\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Cuando consigas nuevas armas y armaduras, presiona 'I' para ver tu Inventario. Desde ahí, puedes equiparlos haciendo clic con el botón derecho en sus Íconos o arrastrándolos al panel de personajes, al que puedes acceder presionando 'C')</rgb>","Habla con Meneldir en la plaza de Musgovilla","Skardí Doblafilos está dentro de la herrería de Musgovilla, al sureste de la fuente.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Entra en la herrería haciendo clic derecho en la puerta para abrirla, luego presiona W para entrar)</rgb>","Habla con Skardí Doblafilos dentro de la herrería de Musgovilla","El hombre dentro de la herrería de Musgovilla, Meneldir, te ha llamado para hablarle\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Cuando consigas nuevas armas y armaduras, presiona 'I' para ver tu Inventario. Desde ahí, puedes equiparlos haciendo clic con el botón derecho en sus Íconos o arrastrándolos al panel de personajes, al que puedes acceder presionando 'C')</rgb>","'Creo que encontrarás a la gente de aquí amistosa y acogedora, si los tratas con amabilidad. Habla con Geralt junto a la fuente y verás si me equivoco.'","Espera a que Skardí Doblafilos repare tu equipo y lo deje en el mostrador","Eleri ha llamado a todos en Musgovilla para ayudar a defender la aldea del ataque del grupo trasgo","'Me alegro por toda ayuda que puedas darme. ¡Mantente cerca!'","Habla con Bevan en la puerta de Musgovilla\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Avanza presionando W y haz clic derecho en Bevan para hablar con él)</rgb>","Espera a que Skardí Doblafilos repare tu equipo y lo coloque sobre el mostrador","Habla con Wenna","Meneldir tiene una petición para ti.","Prepárate para defender a los aldeanos de Madthrug, líder de la partida de asalto","Has ayudado a salvar Musgovilla de los estragos de los Uruks... pero ¿por qué vinieron al pueblo en primer lugar?","'Puedo ver por el polvo del camino en tu ropa que has viajado una gran distancia para llegar aquí, y mientras no causes problemas a mi gente, tienes derecho a quedarte. Hace falta alguien resistente para ganarse la vida aquí, en el borde de lo salvaje, y la gente de Musgovilla estará encantada de darte trabajo, si quieres hacerlo.\
\
'Creo que encontrarás que la gente de aquí es amable y acogedora, si los tratas con amabilidad.'","Has encontrado al aparente líder de la partida de asalto, y no es un trasgo... es uno de los Uruk-hai de combate.\
\
Madthrug lidera la partida de asalto contra Musgovilla, amenazando a los pacíficos habitantes del pueblo.","Instancia: Musgovilla, la Aldea Fronteriza","La madre de Tegwyn, Wenna, está agradecida por tu ayuda salvando a su hijo de los Uruks.","Trasgo asaltante derrotado","Escucha a Meneldir y a Skardí discutir los acontecimientos","Skardí Doblafilos está dentro de la herrería de Musgovilla, al sur de la puerta.","Asegúrate de que Tegwyn esté a salvo","Derrota al trasgo asaltante\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho en el trasgo asaltante para entrar en combate)</rgb>","Deja tu equipo sobre el mostrador\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho en el punto brillante para dejar tu equipo sobre el mostrador)</rgb>","Skardí Doblafilos está muy interesado en ver a alguien como tú en la pacífica aldea de Musgovilla.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Mantén presionado el botón derecho del ratón para girar tu cámara y mantener a la gente importante a la vista)</rgb>","'Estos Uruks han decorado su equipo con un símbolo que no he visto antes: la marca de una mano blanca. Quizá sea el símbolo de esta partida de saqueo, pero aunque han causado mucho daño a Musgovilla, eran pocos y desorganizados. ¿Qué necesidad tendrían de tal sigilo? Ninguna ahora, gracias a nuestros esfuerzos... pero aún me pregunto. Lo pensaré, ${PLAYER}.'","Skardí Doblafilos ha reparado tu equipo y te invita a recogerlo del mostrador. Espera con entusiasmo tu opinión sobre su trabajo.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho en el zurrón brillante para abrirlo y ver su contenido. Haz clic derecho en los objetos que hay dentro del saco para ponerlos en tu inventario. Pulsa 'I' para ver tu Inventario)</rgb>","¡Debes derrotar a Madthrug para asegurar la seguridad de Musgovilla!","'Llevar encima un montón de equipo no te servirá de mucho en combate, como bien sabes. ¡Debes asegurarte de equipar tus armas antes de luchar!'","Entra en la herrería de Musgovilla al sureste de la fuente.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho en la puerta para abrirla y luego avanza con W para entrar)</rgb>","Sigue a Meneldir afuera para descubrir qué peligro ha llegado a Musgovilla","Espera a que Skardí Doblafilos vaya detrás del mostrador\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Mantener presionado el botón derecho del ratón te permite girar la cámara y mantener a la vista a la gente de interés)</rgb>","'¿Bajo ataque? ¿Por quién?\
\
'Esto huele a orcos para mí, ${PLAYER}, pero no lo entiendo. ¡Los orcos no han causado problemas en estas tierras por muchos años!\
\
'Ven conmigo, y mantente cerca. ¡Llegaremos al fondo de esto y salvaremos la aldea si es necesario!'","Habla con Meneldir","La promesa de aventura y una inclinación por viajar te han traído a Musgovilla, un pequeño asentamiento en la frontera de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes y el Antiguo Cardolan. ¿Qué te espera ahora?","Meneldir está junto a la puerta de Musgovilla, reflexionando sobre los sucesos de los últimos minutos.","El hombre apoyado en la pared de la tienda llama tu atención"},
[7033]={"'This is never easy, ${PLAYER}, but it is important. If we are to go on, we must take some time to remember those we have lost. These men died for Gondor, for Rohan, for every land in which dwell the good-hearted. We have constructed a great pyre, and by its light we will remember our fallen.\
\
'Will you accept the task, and the honour, of lighting the pyre? Once it is burning we will begin.'","Enter the Tower of Ecthelion with Éomer","Light the pyre","There is little time to mourn those lost at Pelennor, but Aragorn knows that some time must be spared to remember the fallen.","'I am ready to depart. We should find what rest we can before our next tasks begin.'","Pick up the stone for Snowmane's cairn.","'Morning has come. Let us return to the city and climb to the Citadel. I would visit my uncle where he lies in state, and pay my respects to him.'","Place the stone on the cairn that marks Snowmane's grave.","Speak with Éomer on the Pelennor.","<rgb=#FF0000>Mourn</rgb> for Théoden King","Habla con Éomer","Speak with Éomer inside the Tower of Ecthelion.","Use the torch to light the pyre.","Éomer motions that he wishes to speak to you","Pick up the torch for lighting the pyre.","Enter the Tower of Ecthelion.","Pay your respects to Théoden King.","Listen to Éomer speak.","Walk with Éomer to Théoden's bedside","Place the stone on the cairn for Snowmane","The night is lit by the fire of the burning pyre","'We have arrived, ${PLAYER}. My heart is full of sorrow, but I would look upon my uncle's visage and think upon his life and deeds even so.'","Listen to Éomer as he speaks the names of the fallen.","The torch burns brightly in the night","Remain alert while Éomer speaks","'I have said all I can, and now the rule of Rohan will be mine alone. It is a heavy burden. I hope to live up to my uncle's example, but it will not be easy. Still, I will do my best for the people of Rohan!\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I am ready now to depart.'","Listen to the record of the fallen","Recoge la antorcha","Walk with Éomer to pay respects to Théoden.","Speak with Éomer at the Tower of Ecthelion.","You are overcome by the loss of many great warriors.","Instancia: De luto por los muertos","Pick up the stone for Snowmane's cairn","'The pyre will burn until morning, and the heat of the burning will carry our grief into the night sky.\
\
'There is another creature of nobility we should remember: Snowmane, the steed of the king. Come, let us mark the spot where he died and we have buried him.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Mourn</rgb> the loss of your fellow warriors"},
[7034]={"Yadêphal is in Barad-dûr, where Sauron reigned.","Talk to Yadêphal in Barad-dûr","Dulgabêth is in Barad-dûr, and demands to know why you have come to treat with him instead of Aragorn.","You know that Aragorn will never accept this offer","'I care not for thy name or thy titles. Thou art not the King of Gondor. Has Yadêphal failed in this simple duty? Or has the king proven craven?'\
\
Dulgabêth sneers.\
\
'So thou art the Mouth of Gondor. The king fears to approach me, and sends his servant instead. Thou claimest to speak with his voice? Pah! I hear the cowardice in it!'","'I have given thee my offer, Mouth of Gondor. Now it is thy duty to present it to thy king.\
\
'May he accept it with haste. He would be a fool to do otherwise.'","Aragorn will never accept this offer, but you should tell Dulgabêth of your intention to bring it before the king.","Aragorn bestowed upon you the authority to speak on his behalf, and you have gone with Yadêphal to hear what his master, once the Mouth of Sauron, has to say to Gondor.","Aragorn has given you authority to treat with Dulgabêth on his behalf.","Tell Dulgabêth your name and your title","Aragorn has given you authority to hear what Dulgabêth has to say.","Tell Dulgabêth you will bring his offer before the king","Listen to Dulgabêth's offer in Barad-dûr","Instancia: Boca de Gondor","'You will return with me to the Black Gate, and you will relay my master's offer to the King of Gondor. I will then return with his acceptance.\
\
'This could have been resolved more easily were your king not so craven!'","Follow Yadêphal to Dulgabêth in Barad-dûr","'Follow me, emissary of Gondor. You have a messenger's protection, for now, but if you stray too far it will go badly for you.'"},
[7035]={"Defeat Madin Brenin and his guards.","Instancia: La advertencia de Munfaeril","Munfaeril has asked you to take a warning to Madin, Brenin of Barnavon.","Defeated Madin Brenin and his guards","Deliver Munfaeril's warning to Madin Brenin","'Murderer! Begone from this place and never return, else you will be killed.'","'Ha! You dare threaten the Brenin of Barnavon? I have the protection of Saruman the Wise... you have no authority here.\
\
'Oh-ho! You present me with the Sigil of the Uch-gwirod and expect me to believe the spirit herself sent you? How do I know you did not steal it from the shrine? For that alone you should die.\
\
'Indeed, your interference and blasphemy will not be brooked, duvodiad. Prepare to join the spirits. Guards!'","Defeat Madin Brenin and his guards","Deliver Munfaeril's warning to Madin Brenin in Barnavon."},
[7036]={"Approach Lúkhag","'The Angmarim had my father in their clutches from the start.... I should have known that he would believe them to the bitter end. May the earth reclaim his bones and find some use for him.\
\
'I will not apologize for coming here on my own, as it was my burden to bear. Still, I appreciate your help; I did not think you would trust me after learning of my past.\
\
'Let me know when you are ready to depart. Rékkur ought to know the truth behind Gáfin's death.'","Aighrig seems intent on confronting the Angmarim at the tower's entrance.\
\
She has asked you not to attack them unless it's in self-defence.","Lúkhag has led you to Dûn Traikh, presumably where she last saw Aighrig.","Instance: Mysteries To Unravel","Defend Lúkhag","Lúkhag appears to know where she's going, but will need you to defend her.","Defend Aighrig","Talk to Aighrig","The conversation between Latharn and Aighrig has not ended peacefully.","Latharn has been defeated.\
\
You should check on Aighrig.","Lúkhag is waiting for you on the road leading to Dûn Traikh.","'Have you seen that island in the middle of the lake, ${PLAYER}? Grytholm, it is called, home to the bats of this region. I once considered it peaceful, but the Angmarim have taken over the cave on the island since, twisting bats to do their bidding. Gáfin must have discovered this before he died.\
\
'I came here in search of Latharn, the one who wrote the report we found in Zarkul-sulûn. Join me if you wish, but I will continue with or without you.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Aighrig has been defeated!</rgb>","'Stay your hand. Please, do not attack them unless they attack first. I hope it does not come to that, but....'","Aighrig has stopped in front of the tower and has something to say.","<rgb=#FF0000>Lúkhag has been defeated!</rgb>","Aighrig is determined to find Latharn.","'Back to Annâk-khurfu, then. I have had enough of this place.'","Observe the confrontation","Lúkhag has led you to Aighrig, who has come to Dûn Traikh alone.","Seeing that you've caught up, Lúkhag continues flying towards Dûn Traikh."},
[7037]={"Remain alert for any Heirsworn treachery","'Always have I been loyal to the Heirs of Castamir, ${PLAYER}! I gave them whatever tidings I could of Elessar's plans, and the woman Ioreth proved a font of information! Indeed... it was most challenging to determine what news could be of use amidst all of her ramblings!\
\
'I lost contact with Maethon shortly before the King departed for Outer Gondor, and received no further word from the other supporters of the Heirs; I had to decide what actions to take on my own. That stayed my hand for a time, but always I sought for some means of separating the King from his defenders while we ventured in Anfalas and Pinnath Gelin.\
\
'But now that Balakhâd has assumed his rightful mantle, I can die knowing I have done what I could to support his rise! If I must die, then I will die for him! Praise the memory of Castamir, and all his heirs!'","Confront Aphadaer and Balakhâd","Together, you and Tatháta the Beast have determined to defeat the leadership of the Song of Waves and Wind and prevent the fleet from being used further against Gondor or anywhere else.","Defeat Nakási Wave-reaper","Prepare for battle and talk to Nakási Wave-reaper","Remain on your guard against those who command the Song of Waves and Wind.","Aphadaer claims he has taken the life of King Elessar. Tell him <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, for the King will survive his wound.","Nakási Wave-reaper has accomplished her mission, and she stares at you with contentment.","Remain on your guard as you confront the leadership of the Song","Prepare for battle and speak to Aphadaer","The battle is over.","Talk to Tatháta on the dock","Tatháta is beside the Heirsworn ship Phazanêg.","Remain alert for any treachery on the part of the Heirsworn.","Tell them <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, the King will live","'The Heirsworn ship moored alongside the dock here is called Phazanêg, \\qThe Last Heir.\\q\
\
'You must see that this name comes true, and put an end to he who rallies the Heirsworn! My business is with Nakási.'","Aphadaer has sought the protection of Balakhâd for the death of King Elessar.","Instancia: Nakási Segadora de Olas y los herederos de Castamir","Aphadaer has decided to prove his loyalty to Balakhâd and the Heirs of Castamir by facing you in battle.","'You cannot defeat me, ${PLAYER}, not even with Rothog and Tatháta by your side. My victory is already complete, for I have avenged Tumúldo and satisfied my quest. Gondor burns, as I knew it must. My enemies, all of my enemies, have suffered for the hurts they caused me. Now I am beyond all hurt.\
\
'You have already lost, no matter the outcome of this battle.'"},
[7038]={"'Swiftly now!'","You are suddenly ensnared in thick webbing!","Talk to Legolas at Torech Ungol","Captain Róglarg yells out to you and beckons you over!","Captain Róglarg is standing before the sealed entrance to Torech Ungol.\
\
You have cleared the debris as Captain Róglarg ordered. Aside from the tremors of shifting rocks in the depths of Torech Ungol, seemingly no progress has been made in unsealing Torch Ungol.","Instancia: Sacrificios necesarios","Captain Róglarg can be found at Torech Ungol.\
\
You and Captain Róglarg have led a company of Orcs to Torech Ungol to be sacrificed to Shelob.","'They're begging for another rest, are they? Silent One can't protest, eh? Clever....\
\
'If they're scared now, they're a foolish lot. They haven't even seen her! I have...and she looks even worse than you! Ha! Probably got more of a tongue than you do, too!\
\
'Well, there'll be no more resting. They'll have plenty of time for that once she comes around!\
\
'Keep an eye on them. I don't want ANY getting away!'","Signal '<rgb=#FF00FF>no</rgb>' to Captain Róglarg","Debris can be found outside the mouth of Torech Ungol.\
\
Captain Róglarg has ordered you to clear debris from the main tunnel of Torech Ungol in an attempt to appease Shelob.","You have come to Torech Ungol with Captain Róglarg and should now lead the sacrifices to the mouth of Torech Ungol.","Signal Captain Róglarg","Captain Róglarg grumbles to himself.\
\
'I've been over here keeping eyes on the lot of them, and now I count only six! Where did two of them get off to?\
\
'Maybe they jumped into the tunnels. A lot of good that'll do them... she'll get them either way!\
\
'Have you seen anything, Silent One? Your neck still works, doesn't it?'","Clear debris from the sealed entrance to Torech Ungol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I guess Her Ladyship isn't playing by the rules anymore...\
\
'Shelob's got topsides on us, and I ain't putting this one right! If Lugbúrz wants the Tower so badly, the Big Bosses can sort it out themselves!'\
\
'Nar, I'm not trusting them to understand this one. Old Shagrat did as he was told, and he still got the Pits! Ah, yes, I know just the place!\
\
'Well, I guess it's just you and me now, \\qSilent One\\q....'","Legolas can be found near the entrance of Torech Ungol.\
\
Legolas has freed you from the webs that ensnared you. You should speak to Legolas and flee Torech Ungol!","Legolas swiftly cuts you loose, but the webbing pulls the Silent One's armour from you!","Desperate to be rid of the relentless attacks by creatures of Her Ladyship's lesser broods, Captain Róglarg of Cirith Ungol prepares to sacrifice a company of Orcs to Shelob at her lair, Torech Ungol.","Signal Captain Róglarg at Torech Ungol","Webs have shot forth from the hidden caves and tunnels of Torech Ungol, dragging many Orcs in your company to their dooms. You should flee Torech Ungol with Captain Róglarg.","Flee Torech Ungol with Captain Róglarg!","Escape with Captain Róglarg","Captain Róglarg is standing before the sealed entrance to Torech Ungol.\
\
You have brought the sacrifices to the mouth of Torech Ungol, but it is blocked by stone and debris. You should get Captain Róglarg's attention and see if he knows what to do.","Keep watch on the Orcs and await Her Ladyship's arrival","'Well now, I didn't like the sound of that....\
\
'Nar, you've probably gone and made it worse! Not a single way through that mess...and Her Ladyship's bound to be hungry if She's trapped down there!'\
\
Captain Róglarg looks at the sacrifices.\
\
'We'll wait a few minutes and see if anything comes of it.'","Return to Captain Róglarg","Captain Róglarg is keeping watch at Torech Ungol.\
\
Captain Róglarg has asked you if you know where the two missing Orcs in the company have gone. You should tell him no, even if you know better.","You are trapped in the thick webs of Her Ladyship! You must struggle free!","Captain Róglarg is keeping watch at Torech Ungol.\
\
Captain Róglarg has called you over. You should see what he wants.","\\qEscort\\q the sacrifices to Torech Ungol with Captain Róglarg","You break stone after stone, but Torech Ungol remains sealed!","'What is this? A cave-in?!\
\
'Must have been all that business with the mountain and Lugbúrz that brought it down! Her Ladyship must be trapped down there, and if that Elf-warrior actually stuck a pin into her, she might have trouble breaking free. Nar, she'll be none too happy about this....\
\
'I'd be glad to be rid of Her Ladyship, but it's her children that are mucking about in Lhingris, and only she can bring them in line. We've got to get this sorted and fast, or we'll all have it much worse. Don't have the High Up to look out for us when it comes to her!\
\
'You're the Silent One, right? Clear that debris there, and see if the tunnel opens up a bit. Maybe Her Ladyship won't notice you!\
\
'Garn! Try to break through!'","'There is no time to speak, ${PLAYER}. Swiftly now, we must go!'","You should await Her Ladyship's arrival at Torech Ungol until Captain Róglarg signals otherwise.","Try to free yourself from the webs!","Captain Róglarg has fled to the entrance of Torech Ungol.\
\
You have escaped the webs of Shelob and her children with Captain Róglarg. You should escape and return to Cirith Ungol."},
[7039]={"Negotiate with Jajax","Hebil has come to ask for Jajax's help.","You have asked Jajax to pull his men out of Lothgobel","Jajax is in the tavern of Lothgobel.\
\
You should speak with Jajax.","Instancia: Negociaciones","Speak with Jajax to tell him you agree","Jajax has agreed to speak with you about the fate of Lothgobel.","'Normally an outsider would not be granted an audience with a captain of the Corsairs, but you have earned this right twofold. You bested the challenge laid before you, and you bested many of my men in battle already.\
\
'Tell me what it is you want.'\
\
You tell Jajax that you want his men to leave Lothgobel.","You tell Jajax that his offer is more than fair.\
\
'Aye, that it is. And we do not play fair. See how the men grumble and stir already? It seems that some of them do not like my speech....'","'You had best get out of here straight away, ${PLAYER}. There is about to be a brawl of mighty proportions. I promise you I'll keep to my end of the bargain, eh? Now you keep to yours.\
\
'Let the Corsairs handle their differences as they see fit.'","You hear the tavern door slam open...","Watch the confrontation between Jajax and Hebil","This seems like one of those situations you should get out of... quickly."},
[7040]={"Orcs are attacking Thinglad!\
\
You should defeat many Orcs.","'Those who did this are surely still nearby. I can smell their foul breath upon the air. Be alert, ${PLAYER}!'","'${PLAYER}, I look to you to ensure that Wynmar keeps his word. Please help the Rohirrim with anything they need before they depart these woods.\
\
'Will you see our friends back to their camp?'","Defeat attackers","You should speak with Noriel at once.","Wynmar appears to be rather smitten with Noriel","Noriel has asked Wynmar to lead his people from Thinglad, and he has given his word","Listen to Noriel and Wynmar","'I greet you, ${PLAYER}. I apologize for following you, but we did...and it is a good thing, too. It looks like we were just in time to save you and your fair friend.\
\
'Pray...introduce me to this brave lady. I rarely see a warrior fight so well, man or woman.'","You should talk to Noriel.","Observe the dialogue between Noriel and Wynmar.","Instancia: Los vecinos se encuentran","The Elves of Thinglad are unveiled to their Stangard neighbours at last.","Talk to Noriel","Thank Wynmar for his intervention","You should talk to Wynmar.","'Are you ready to bring Wynmar back to his camp?'"},
[7041]={"Leafshade has agreed to tell you the story of how he met Nestinanessornë, and what happened afterward.","Talk to Nestinanessornë","Nakási Wave-reaper and her Corsairs have come to Leafshade's grove.","'You are one of the long-lived ones, like my friend Ferien, hoom. But even poison can bring the Elves low, if it is of a bad sort. The poison used by these burárum, these Orcs, is of a very bad sort indeed. Any others struck by their arrows would have died at once, and never known there was poison to survive. An Elf might last a little longer, but without my Entish medicine you would have perished too. You are, hoom, lucky? Ents do not believe in such a thing, but Ferien used to speak of it to me, hoom, toom. Oh, she did!\
\
'If I had not seen you on my return journey, you would surely be dead now. You have Ferien's luck, little Nestinanessornë. You slept for a long time, and will need to sleep longer if you are to be fully healed. What did Ferien used to say to me? \\qYou are not... out of the woods yet...?\\q Hoom, boom, toom! Imagine that, Nestinanessornë, hm, hm, hm.'","Nestinanessornë lies upon the stone table in Leafshade's grove.","Leafshade and Nestinanessornë discuss the Elf's need to leave the Ent's grove.","'Why should we not burn this grove as a message to the folk of Gondor who live in Anfalas? We have set fire to their ships, but the ships come from elsewhere and are manned by crews selected by the Prince of Dol Amroth and by the King, far away in the White City.\
\
'I say we burn this grove to show they are not safe in their homes. The waves bring us even to their shores, and they are not safe from us.'","'Where... where am I? What happened to me?\
\
'I remember the marching ranks of the Orcs! My friends... I have to warn my friends... and the defenders of Helm's Deep...\
\
'But... but how did I come to be here? Pain... I remember a pain in my side...'","Listen to the conversation of Leafshade and Nestinanessornë","'You have to... have to let me go, Leafshade.\
\
'My friends need me! Horn... Nona... ${PLAYER}... Gléowine...\
\
'I tried to stand, and walk, but my body... still too weak...'","Nestinanessornë has collapsed in Leafshade's grove, seeking to go to the aid of his friends.","Talk to Nakási Wave-reaper","'Nestinanessornë left with them, and sailed away on one of their ships. I did not want to fight, and I am glad, hoom, glad that I did not have to.\
\
'But I hope my friend... is safe. He was not yet fully recovered from his wound, and could not hope to oppose the people of the ships... if it came to fighting.'\
\
Leafshade stares at you with half-lidded eyes. He seems nearly ready to fall asleep once again.","Observe the confrontation between Nakási Wave-reaper and Leafshade","Leafshade and Nestinanessornë discuss what befell the Elf, and how he came to be in the Ent's care.","Talk to Leafshade","Instancia: Nestinanessornë","Leafshade remembers his conversations with Nestinanessornë.","Nakási Wave-reaper poses a threat to Leafshade and to Nestinanessornë.","Leafshade is ready to conclude his tale."},
[7042]={"Magor te ha ayudado a despejar el camino hacia un oscuro y profundo antro. Sintiéndose en peligro, se ha ido a buscar ayuda, dejándote a ti la tarea de descubrir la nueva amenaza. Busca el mal que se encuentra delante de ti y destrúyelo.","Al entrar en Azanarukâr, te encuentras con los batallones de las tropas de élite de Mazog. Los Elfos te han pedido que elimines la amenaza que representa Mazog en Azanarukâr derrotando a sus líderes.","'¡Vámonos de aquí, ${PLAYER}! Hemos estado demasiado tiempo en presencia de este ser malvado, y anhelo el alivio de mi temor.'","'¡Atrás! ¡Nunca me contaminaréis con vuestro veneno! Bien, se han ido; estoy aliviado. Pensé que me convertiría en algo como ellos: una monstruosidad. Me atacaron por sorpresa, me rodearon y me capturaron. Se oyen rumores de destinos tan retorcidos, pero ahora he visto el malvado charco de suciedad que corrompe las profundidades de este lugar -- lo he visto con mis propios ojos.\
\
'Os daré un momento para que os recuperéis, y luego debéis seguirme. Aplastaremos a estos monstruos antes de que puedan corromper algo más allá de este lugar malvado. Será una gran tarea. Solo puedo imaginar las horribles cosas a las que nos enfrentaremos al penetrar en esta zona.\
\
'¡Date prisa; recobra el juicio y prepárate!'","Derrota a los berserkers orcos de Moria (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has matado a dos grandes Rogmul que afirmaban guardar Azanarukâr desde hace mucho tiempo. Escuchas horribles rugidos delante de ti y solo puedes imaginar el peligro que se esconde detrás de la siguiente curva.","Instancia: Nueva Diablura","Los Elfos de Lothlórien te han enviado al corazón de Azanarukâr para descubrir qué le ha pasado a Magor y qué es lo que realmente sucede en estas profundidades inexploradas.","Has derrotado a los líderes de los Orcos de Moria que Mazog envió a Azanarukâr y has encontrado a Magor, el Elfo perdido. Ahora, Magor quiere que le ayudes a derrotar a las criaturas sin nombre que habitan en las profundidades de Azanarukâr. Necesitará ayuda para acabar con esta plaga.","Berserkers orcos de Moria derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Magor, el Elfo prisionero"},
[7043]={"Habla con Halbarad y escucha su relato","Halbarad teje un relato de temor.","Halbarad ha accedido a contarte la noche en que el Vado de Sarn fue atacado.","'Mi propio corazón fue presa de un terrible presentimiento, pero tenía el deber del mando y no lo abandonaría. Quiero que sepas esto, ${PLAYER}, antes de contarte los hechos que siguieron: estos hombres y mujeres que se mantuvieron conmigo aquella noche... no había en ellos ni una gota de cobardía.\
\
'Pero no teníamos idea de lo que enfrentaríamos esa noche.'","Instancia: La Noche Cae sobre el Vado de Sarn","Escucha el relato de Halbarad"},
[7044]={"Talk to Éomer in Edoras","Gríma stares at you with those piercing eyes.\
\
'You were fortunate, ${PLAYER},' he says, the shadow of a half-smile creasing his lips.\
\
'That will not happen again.'","Listen as Éomer speaks with Théoden","'If you will leave your weapons outside the hall, I will bring you inside to see Théoden King.'","Éomer is ready to confront Théoden and his advisor Gríma Wormtongue.","Talk to Háma inside Meduseld","Talk to Corudan in front of Meduseld","Gríma studies you with piercing eyes, and you feel distinctly uncomfortable. How much knowledge of your imprisonment in Isengard did Saruman share with his nefarious agent?\
\
You learned in the caverns below Isengard that Gríma is a pawn of Saruman... but does Gríma know that you know it?","Talk to Háma","Talk to Éomer in front of Meduseld","You have come with Éomer to Edoras to speak with his uncle Théoden, the King of Rohan.","Háma is before the gates of Meduseld, waiting to take your weapons.","'Look there, ${PLAYER}. Behold the Golden Hall of Meduseld, seat of my uncle Théoden, the King of Rohan. We will speak with him and obtain a decree the Reeves will be unable to ignore. They must move their people across the Entwash where we can better protect them! A decree by Théoden King will be more difficult for them to ignore, I deem.'\
\
Éomer looks momentarily discomfited.\
\
'I rode north with my Éored to hunt the Orcs against my uncle's wishes. He may still be displeased, but we must hope that he will forgive the disobedience for its happy result: the death of the Orcs.'","'I do not understand why I must leave my bow with this man, ${PLAYER}. Do they not trust my word as an Elf? If I say I will do no harm to their King, no harm will come to him from my hand.\
\
'It is not that I am offended. It is just that we went to some trouble to recover this bow the last time it left my possession, and I do not believe you could win a similar wager to get it back again!'\
\
Corudan laughs.\
\
'Ah, I will leave it here with this man Háma. The Rohirrim seem so afraid of Elves I believe I could make a frightful face at one of them and cow him into returning my bow, if it came to that.'","Éomer is standing on the approach to Meduseld, the Golden Hall, and wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Horn in front of Meduseld","Talk to Gríma","It is not yet time for your audience with Théoden. You will be called before him when he is ready for you.","Háma, el portero de Théoden, está ante las puertas de Meduseld y debe aprobar tu entrada antes de que puedas ver al Rey.","'I am Háma, the Doorward of Théoden. You have come to the Golden Hall of Meduseld in the presence of Éomer, nephew of the King, and you are as welcome here as he himself be, if he speaks well of you.'","Wait for your audience with Théoden","'I will leave Nona's sword with Háma, for I trust the Doorward of Théoden and know him to be an honourable man. He will see to it that the blade is returned to me after our audience.\
\
'I do not like to be without it for even a moment, but I will do as Théoden King requires.'","'I am sorry you must be inconvenienced in this way, ${PLAYER}. Do not blame Háma for it. He is simply doing his duty. The safety of the King must come before all, and keeping the weapons of strangers outside the hall can help ensure it.\
\
'It was never like this in days of old, however. I sense the influence of Gríma in this.'","Witness the will of Théoden","'Come with me. I will bring you before Théoden King.'","Talk to Háma in front of Meduseld","You stand before the seat of Théoden, King of Rohan, but it is his advisor Gríma that will decide your fate.","Instancia: La noche cae sobre Meduseld","You have come into Meduseld with Háma, seeking an audience with Théoden.","'I have seen enough, ${PLAYER}! It is as I feared when my uncle forbade me to pursue the Orcs. His will is not his own! It is Gríma's doing!'","Gríma has called you forth to speak to him.","You have come before the seat of Théoden, King of Rohan.","Talk to Éomer in Meduseld","Your companions are outside Meduseld and have been asked to leave their weapons with Háma."},
[7045]={"'¡La Ira Furtiva ha sido derrotada, ${PLAYER}! ¡No volverá a molestarnos, si sabe lo que le conviene! Ahora que se ha ido, espero que los hobbits de Wistmead dejen de sentir los efectos de su presencia. No es demasiado pronto, si me preguntas, ¡pero más vale tarde que nunca!\
\
'Ojalá hubiéramos podido hacer más para ayudar a Halson Cleary. La suya es una historia triste, y aunque me alegra haber puesto fin a la maldad de la Ira Furtiva, llegamos demasiado tarde para ayudar al pobre difunto señor Cleary. ¿Más vale tarde que nunca, dije? Es difícil llegar más tarde que esto, doscientos años después, pero aún así espero que encuentre algo de descanso en ello.\
\
'Me gustaría hacer los arreglos para darle sepultura. Hablaré con el Alcalde, y quizás el Servicio Postal Rápido pueda correr con los gastos; ¡si hubieran entregado las cartas de Ivy Redsmith, algo de dolor podría haberse evitado! No, no juzgaré a jefes de correos que murieron hace tiempo. La Ira Furtiva tuvo parte en el abandono de sus deberes.\
\
'Creo que a Halson Cleary le gustaría ser enterrado en su jardín. Colocaremos las cartas de Ivy junto a él, y que encuentre paz al fin con su recuerdo.'","'¡Esta fue una mala idea y ya me arrepiento! Demos la vuelta y digámosle a Bingo que no encontramos nada. ¿Qué dices, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Sé que cuenta con nosotros, pero no tiene toda la información, ¿verdad? Cree que yo no creo en los fantasmas, y además de eso, cree que eso será una ventaja para nosotros en esta empresa. ¡Pero se equivoca! ¿No sería mi creencia en aparecidos, espectros y apariciones fantasmales incluso una desventaja aún mayor?\
\
'Oh, ¡bueno, está bien! Podemos seguir. ¡Pero no estoy nada contento con esto, nada contento!'","'¡Por fin! He de decir, ${PLAYER}, que no entiendo cómo caben todas estas escaleras dentro de la granja. Parecía bastante más pequeña por fuera, ¿no?\
\
'¡Malditos fantasmas y espectros! ¿Por qué las cosas no pueden ser como aparentan?\
\
'Supongo que tenemos que seguir adelante. ¿Quizás el próximo truco sea que este espeluznante edificio no es tan aterrador ni tan embrujado como parece? ¡Eso espero!'","El bosque invade la parte trasera de la granja","Has llegado con Dinodas Boffin a los bosques brumosos que bordean Wistmead en busca del espíritu que perturba la Comarca.","'Bueno, la puerta del sótano está cerrada, así que supongo que mejor damos la vuelta y volvemos a casa...\
\
'¿Qué dices? ¿La puerta está abierta? Ay, ay, ay... ¡Puede haber cualquier cosa al acecho ahí abajo, ${PLAYER}! ¿De verdad tenemos que bajar?'","Dinodas se encuentra dentro de la vieja granja de los Cleary.","Tú y Dinodas habéis encontrado una granja en ruinas en medio del bosque brumoso. ¿Serán estos los Acres siniestros de los que habló el espectro?","Dirígete a la sala principal de la granja","Dinodas está mirando la puerta del sótano en el lado oeste de la granja.","'He reflexionado, ${PLAYER}, y he decidido que no podía dejaros a ti y al joven Dinodas afrontar este peligro solos. ¡Así que dejé mis reparos a un lado y me preparé para seguiros a los dos, y resulta que mis otros primos habían pensado lo mismo!\
\
'Algo en la historia de este espíritu me parece bastante sospechoso. ¡Creo que debemos llegar al fondo del asunto, y de inmediato!'","La puerta del sótano parece no estar cerrada con llave","¡Bingo y sus primos han llegado a la sala principal de la vieja granja de los Cleary, dispuestos a mantenerse a tu lado contra la Ira Furtiva!","Inspecciona la fachada de la granja","Inspecciona la parte trasera de la granja","Nadie descansa ahora en este porche lateral, si es que alguien lo hizo alguna vez","La Ira Furtiva se desata dentro de la vieja granja de los Cleary.","Instancia: Ninguno salvo uno","¡Han llegado refuerzos: toda una caterva de Boffins!","La puerta del lado oeste de la granja no está cerrada con llave y te llevará a ti y a Dinodas al sótano bajo la granja.","Hay algo muy peculiar en estas escaleras...","Habla con Dinodas junto a la puerta del sótano","Inspecciona el lado oeste de la granja","Has llegado con Dinodas a la granja embrujada de los Acres siniestros, y los dos debéis abriros camino por el sótano para descubrir sus secretos.","Abre la puerta del lado oeste de la granja y entra al sótano","Hay algo peculiar en estas escaleras","Bingo y sus primos han llegado a la sala principal de la vieja granja de los Cleary, dispuestos a mantenerse a tu lado contra el espíritu misterioso... ¿pero será suficiente para oponerse a la malicia de ese ser maléfico?","Habla con Dinodas entre los árboles brumosos","Bingo se encuentra dentro de la vieja granja de los Cleary.","Si el fantasma de Halson Cleary es realmente el responsable de las apariciones de Wistmead y la Maldición de los Acres siniestros, Bingo está seguro de que tú y su primo Dinodas podréis llegar al fondo del asunto.","Abre paso por la granja embrujada junto a Dinodas","Por fin has llegado a la sala principal de la granja embrujada.","Por fin: entrega el correo (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Bingo te ha dado las únicas armas que podrían dañar a la Ira Furtiva: las cartas que Ivy Redsmith escribió a Halson Cleary hace tanto tiempo.","Ayuda a Dinodas a resistir el miedo que amenaza con abrumarlo","Permanece junto a Bingo mientras confronta al espíritu misterioso","'Let's go, ${PLAYER}.'","Has llegado a la sala principal de la vieja granja de los Cleary con Dinodas Boffin, y no debes ceder al miedo que amenaza con abrumar al joven hobbit.","La puerta está cerrada con llave y atrancada, y no puede abrirse desde este lado","Habla con Dinodas dentro de la vieja granja de los Cleary","¡Bingo te lanza una bolsa de sobres y la atrapas al vuelo!","Habla con Bingo en la granja embrujada","Inspecciona el lado este de la granja","Habla con Bingo dentro de la vieja granja de los Cleary","'¿Has visto eso, ${PLAYER}? ¡Le llamé Mentiroso Furtivo! ¡Oh, si Celandine hubiera estado aquí para ver mi increíble valentía y coraje! Se lo contarás, ¿verdad?\
\
'Es curioso. Tenía miedo cuando llegamos al bosque, y después cuando llegamos a la espeluznante granja escondida en su interior. Estaba fuera de mí de terror cuando me dijiste que la puerta del sótano no estaba cerrada con llave. ¡Y cada nueva visión que contemplamos mientras avancábamos por la granja de los Cleary multiplicaba por diez mi horror!\
\
'Pero cuando llegó el momento, cuando nos enfrentamos al espectro y tantos de mis hermanos y hermanas estaban a mi lado... bueno, las cosas ya no parecían tan aterradoras. ¡Qué extraño! Aún así, ahora miro a mi alrededor y el escalofrío empieza a volver, y te digo que estoy listo para irme. ¡Sí, vámonos mientras tengamos la oportunidad, ${PLAYER}! ¡Brrrr! ¿A qué esperas?'","Enfrenta a la Ira Furtiva junto a Bingo y los demás Boffins"},
[7046]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Do not be seen!</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>You were seen by Dolguzigir!</rgb>","Lhaereth has entered and is speaking to one who can only be the keeper of the Halls of Black Lore.\
\
You should listen to their conversation.","You have entered the Halls of Black Lore to uncover what Lhaereth seeks, but danger is near.","You have safely made it outside","You have entered the Halls of Black Lore.\
\
You should speak to Faeron.","Someone, or something, has created a diversion for you!\
\
You should escape the Halls of Black Lore!","Escape the Halls","You should follow Faeron and keep to the shadows.","'Stay together, stay quiet. Remember: if Lhaereth is already here, do not engage.'","Listen to the conversation","Instancia: Nada por nada","Talk to Faeron","Lhaereth bursts into the Halls!","You hear a sudden crash and a yelp!","<rgb=#FF0000>You were seen by Lhaereth!</rgb>","Follow Faeron","'I do not think we were seen. We should return to the tower.'"},
[7047]={"'Upon Thrór's brow, carved in crude dwarf-runes, was the name: AZOG'","Hersegg can be found at Azanulbizar.\
\
You should talk to Hersegg.","'Hidden beneath the eaves of trees and stones at the foot of Zirakzigil, Nár built a fire and prepared what meagre meal he could that might befit a king and one road-weary traveller.\
\
'When the supper was ended, Thrór stood at once. As if in answer, Nár knelt before the old king and helped him to fasten a shield to his arm.'","Hersegg can be found at Azanulbizar.\
\
You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.","Hersegg has asked you to learn the fate of Thrór.\
\
You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.","Follow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale","'Although both Thrór and Nár saw many signs of Orcs in the dale, they were old and overtrodden. Outside Khazad-dûm, all was still and silent. Before them, the East-gate yawned open, as if to beckon the two of them forth.\
\
'But the journey had been long, and Nár thought better of seeking shelter within Moria.'","Instancia: El cuento de Nár","'And waited... until he thought he could bear it no longer.\
\
'Despite every doubt, though, his resolve did not falter. Even if he were fated to live the rest of his days huddled beside a fire at Azanulbizar, Nár would not disobey his king — it was his duty to await Thrór's return.'","Hoping to aid King Thorin in guiding the Prince to victory, Hersegg, grand-daughter of Hermáth Stormhammer, has offered to tell you the tragic tale of Nár.","'And that is all there is to tell of the doom of Thrór, ${PLAYER}.'","'Nár had known the truth at once, but wished not to believe it. It was Thrór.\
\
'As Nár crept closer, there came a chittering laughter from beyond the darkness of the East-gate.'","'At first, Nár again made for the Redhorn Pass, but Orcs beyond counting had gathered there and watched him with their red eyes. And so, Nár fled back the way he had come. As he passed by the gates of Khazad-dûm again, more great Orcs, including some larger than any he had heard of before, had surrounded Thrór’s corpse and were hacking it to pieces. Into that hateful frenzy, a great mass of crows descended, and to them, the Orcs began to fling the scraps of the Dwarf-king. Nár dared not look again.\
\
'Tear-blind, Nár ran on along the banks of Kheled-zâram, fleeing the Orcs and wolves that now hunted him in cruel sport. When at last he came to the ruins of Amdân, he found them barred, and black arrows hounded his every step. Desperate to escape his own doom, however, Nár thought of Kibil-nâla and leapt down the paths alongside the stream. By some stroke of fortune, Nár had won his escape, but behind him the laughter of Azog and the Orcs rang in his ears.\
\
'For many months, Nár wandered in the wilderness, wracked with sorrow, the sight of his King’s defilement branded in his heart. At long last, he found his way north to the High Pass across the Misty Mountains, then made his way back to Thrór’s Coomb. By the time he entered Zudrugund the guards scarcely recognized him, so haggard and wild he had grown.\
\
'Nár was never well in his mind again.'","'Thrór had bidden Nár to stay and await his return, but it was not merely the word of his king that kept him from daring to enter Moria. In truth, and to his shame, Nár was afraid.\
\
'For many days Nár hid among the trees outside the gates, lonely and troubled. When he dared to draw nearer to the gate and peer into the gloom, neither sound nor the faintest flicker of light emerged from within.\
\
'More troublingly still, neither had Thrór.'","'When Nár awoke, his clothing was cold and heavy with rain. Nár's rest had ended abruptly, and in a daze, he tried to regain his bearings.\
\
'Above him the sky loomed dark, its hue a sickly purple, and he could not tell if it was day or night. Aside from the sound of trickling rainfall, all was still and silent.\
\
'Alas, Nár would have little time to ponder his situation.'","Talk to Hersegg","'...but whatever the case he summoned Thráin and gave to him what heirlooms of their house remained – chief among them his Ring, last of the Seven that had been given to the Dwarf-kings.\
\
'He said to Thráin, \\qRiches may yet spring anew from this bauble, my son. Or perhaps not. Yet one cannot breed gold without gold.\\q When Thráin asked if his intent was to return to Erebor, Thrór remained silent. After a long moment, he said, \\qThese bones are too old. I will not be avenged on Smaug - that fate, perchance, shall be yours, or your sons’. I have known too much of loss and of Men’s derision. I go to seek better fortunes, if they may yet be found.\\q\
\
'He did not say where he meant to go, and Thráin did not ask, but merely wished him fortune in his quest.'","'Long after the realm of Grárik had fallen to the cold-drake Vethúg, and twenty years after the Lonely Mountain fell to Smaug, King Thrór and his folk came to dwell in a coomb near the wilds of Dunland. From the old stronghold of Zudrugund, Thrór ruled what remained of the two kingdoms he had fled in his life. His son was Thráin, a formidable warrior; his grandsons Thorin and Frerin, and granddaughter Dís, were yet young. His people were few, poor, and hungry, and they knew little joy since the loss of their homes in the North.\
\
'Dotage and gloom took their toll on King Thrór, and he thought long of regaining the splendour of his fathers’ halls. But it was not in the halls of Erebor where Smaug now slumbered upon the heirlooms of his people, nor the frozen wastes in the north that called to him: it was Khazad-dûm itself! It had been more than eight hundred years since doom befell it - since the Elves named it Moria, but it mattered not. Thrór determined that he would reclaim it, and in so doing, restore the glory of his kingdom and of Durin's Folk. What true reason had he, none know for certain. \
\
'Perhaps he had gone mad, or perhaps not....'","Learn the fate of Thrór and the name of his murderer"},
[7048]={"'We made it! Now we need to come up with some way to attract Núrzum's attention before he sees Nona...'","'It is one thing to hear of Núrzum's great size and strength, but it is entirely different to see it for yourself! How can we hope to fight such a creature?\
\
'Woe be to Aldstan, if Núrzum finds him!'","Talk to Horn in Byre Tor","Stay close to Horn and survive your encounter with Núrzum","You have come with Horn to the eastern gate of Byre Tor, and the cold winds begin to rise.","You have escaped the centre of Byre Tor, but Nona is still in danger! Horn is at a loss, and does not know what he can do to help her.","Nona is in danger, but you can do nothing without putting the rest of you at risk! You must stay close to Horn and Corudan!","Corudan became separated from Nona when Orcs attacked, and now she is by herself somewhere in Byre Tor, with Núrzum stalking through the streets.","'Nona and I were driven apart by attacking Orcs, and I have not seen her since. She must still be in the city. We will find her again!\
\
'That great shaking can only be Núrzum! We must not let him see us. If we do not dispose of these Orcs quickly he is sure to find us!'","Núrzum has returned to Byre Tor! Stay close to Horn, and out of the sight of the giant!","'We cannot keep like this for long, ${PLAYER}. Núrzum may not be looking for us, but if he happens upon the two of us while searching for Aldstan, he will not show mercy. That much I know for certain!\
\
'And what if he happens upon Nona and Corudan? We cannot stay here. We have to find them and leave the city!'","Horn has retreated to the stables of Byre Tor, while Núrzum continues his destructive march through the city.","'I do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}! We cannot leave her! I refuse to leave Byre Tor without Nona!'","Nona has given Núrzum the slip, much to your relief and that of your companions... especially Horn.","'Byre Tor looks much as it did when last we were here. We have been fortunate to run into fewer Orcs than before, but remain alert, for they still hold this city.\
\
'I have seen nothing yet that might reveal Núrzum's interest in Byre Tor.'","'It was not difficult to escape the giant, ${PLAYER}. He is big and I am small. He is slow and I am fast. He is an unnatural thing, given to evil, and I am the sister of Wadu, the daughter of Suvulch. He is alone and I have friends who care for me.\
\
'This Núrzum was o'ermatched before he even came to Byre Tor today. I was never frightened of him.\
\
'Still, I am glad we are safe. We should leave this place before he realizes we have gone. And ${PLAYER}, thank you for watching out for Horn, today and for the last several days. It eased the worry of my heart to know you were by his side.'","Horn is by the side of a building in Byre Tor. He is desperate to think of some way to keep Núrzum from finding Nona.","Horn is hiding behind a barricade in Byre Tor, as Núrzum encroaches upon his position.","Horn is by the stables in Byre Tor, trying to come up with a way to keep Núrzum from finding Nona.","You and Horn have found Corudan in Byre Tor, but the Elf and the Dunlending were separated by attacking Orcs and now Nona is missing.","You have been spotted by Núrzum!","Talk to Corudan in Byre Tor","You have come with Horn, Corudan, and Nona to the city of Byre Tor.","'What a relief it is to see Nona safe again! Núrzum will answer to me for threatening her!\
\
'Another day, perhaps. Now we should return to Nona's cave and puzzle over the meaning of why Núrzum seeks this man Aldstan.'","'The wind is picking up, ${PLAYER}. Do you feel it?'\
\
Horn looks about with concern.\
\
'I think we may have found what we sought, my friend! Stay by me, and get ready to run if we must!'","Reassure Horn that all will be well","Stay close to Horn! Núrzum is moving through the streets of Byre Tor and you must not lose track of your companion!","You have come to Byre Tor with your companions to see what you can learn of Núrzum's seeming interest in the city.","Instancia: Núrzum","Talk to Nona in Byre Tor","'We cannot do anything from here, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps if we could get to the other side of the courtyard...'\
\
Horn's eyes are alight with the desperation of fear.\
\
'We might be able to run behind Núrzum while his back is turned! From the far side of the courtyard we can get his attention, and draw him away from Nona!'"},
[7049]={"'What purpose could you have for such destruction, giant? Hoom. Do you even understand what agony you have brought upon the creatures here? You tear the trees from the ground, you freeze the Huorns where they take root, and even the foul wood-trolls are not spared your ire.\
\
'My friends either lay sleeping in this winter you have buried us in, or they lack the courage to stand against you.\
\
'Hooom... but I do not. I shall not allow you any further in these woods, monster!'","Instancia: La ira de Núrzum","The Ents of the Balewood wish to impart their knowledge of Núrzum's assault into Wildermore upon you.","Leave Drû Vádokan and travel to the forest's edge","Talk to the strange tree, Duskleaf","The destruction that followed Duskleaf's defeat is known well to Ents and Men alike","The lands of Men lay to the east beyond the forest's edge.\
\
You have defeated the Ent, Duskleaf. You should now continue eastward and fulfil the bargain that you made with Saruman.","The forest's edge can be found outside the eastern gate of Drû Vádokan in north-western Balewood.\
\
You are standing inside Drû Vádokan, the White Hand's base in the Balewood. You must travel to the forest's edge and wreak havoc upon the Men of Wildermore.","You hear the familiar creaking of branches as more trees rise against you in the distance","Journey into Wildermore and defeat any that stand in your way","The forest's edge lies to the south-east in Whitshaws.\
\
The trees of the Balewood are enraged at your presence in the woods. You must defeat them if you are to seek your revenge on the Men of Wildermore.","Journey deeper into the forest","You have found your path blocked by a strange tree that looks as if it wishes to speak with you","You discover your path blocked by what appear to be angry trees. Clear them and continue your journey to the east!","Duskleaf is standing in northern Balewood.\
\
You have found your path blocked by a strange tree that is looking at you with a mix of anger and confusion. You should speak with this tree before continuing eastward.","The forest's edge lies to the south-east in Whitshaws.\
\
You have found yourself beset on all sides by denizens of the forest. You should continue travelling to the east, but be sure to defeat any that stand in your way."},
[7050]={"Instancia: El poder de Roblecorazón","'Gracias por ayudarme esta última vez. No creo que pudiera hacerlo por mi cuenta, siendo la frágil anciana que soy. Has hecho mucho por mí, más de lo que quizá jamás llegues a saber. No puedo empezar a agradecerte por tus servicios.\
\
'Ven, veamos qué se puede encontrar aquí. No creo que nadie vaya a molestarnos.'","Habla con Sara Roblecorazón","Sigue a Sara Roblecorazón más adentro de Barad Gúlaran.","Sigue a Sara Roblecorazón hasta el corazón de Barad Gúlaran.","Sara Roblecorazón te ha pedido que hables con ella y quiere que la sigas mientras te cuenta su historia."},
[7053]={"Tárasánë is in the Pristine Glade.\
\
You and Tárasánë appear to be in the Pristine Glade. You should speak to her and learn how this has come to be.","Instancia: De sueños y deseos","You have beheld a vision of Vethúg Wintermind, the cold-drake of the Ered Mithrin!","Behold Tárasánë's visions (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Do not fear, little one. You have fallen into a deep slumber, and here you dream of distant lands. \
\
'Curious. Of all the lands you have beheld, your mind has wandered hither. You have come to this place before, have you not? \
\
'You have seen it in waking, but through my power, it has been shaped anew by your thoughts and desires.\
\
'Look around you, and see now these visions of what is to come....'","'Wake now, ${PLAYER}....'","Visions of the Green Lady can be found within your dream of the Pristine Glade.\
\
The Green Lady has asked you to seek out the visions that have crept into your dream of the Pristine Glade.","You have beheld a vision of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior!","You have beheld a vision of the Herald of Winter, Hrímil Frost-heart!","The Green Lady once dwelled in the heights of the Emyn-nu-Fuin, but that was long before the darkening of Mirkwood.","Talk to Tárasánë, the Green Lady","Tárasánë is in the Pristine Glade.\
\
Tárasánë stands before the Great Tree of the Pristine Glade. You have witnessed the three visions she bestowed upon you, and you should now speak to her once more.","'What I have shown you may not come to pass, but it will be the future that awaits you if you abandon this quest. There are things that remain beyond my sight in the frozen wastes of Morgoth, and so, you must remain vigilant.\
\
'Remember well what you have seen, ${PLAYER}. It is time you awoke....'"},
[7054]={"Gandalf is in Galadriel's garden, waiting to speak with you.","Haldir is in the woods of Lothlórien.","Talk to Galadriel and describe to her your dream","'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. It is good to see you. There is just so much that needs to be done! The Eagles have proven able companions to me in these dark days. Gwaihir has agreed to bear me where next I need go, and his brother Landroval has been keeping his sharp eyes on the Anduin. Would that I could be everywhere!\
\
'I fought against fire and shadow in the depths of Moria and on the peak, and when returned to this world I faced another foe from afar. These deeds have left me tired, and I will not speak of them now.\
\
'We will speak again, ${PLAYER}, if our deeds prove fruitful. If they do not, well...'\
\
Gandalf trails away. Suddenly, with a blaze in his eye and a tone of mirthful anger, he continues.\
\
'Perhaps they would have proven enough had we not stood around talking about them for so long, my sentimental ${RACE}! We have our own tasks now... let us get to them!'","'I will send for Alfrohir to bring you down the river to Thinglad, ${PLAYER}. Gandalf believes a great evil harries our absent friends. Perhaps your presence on the banks of the Anduin can prevent it from discovering or endangering them.'","Talk to Haldir within Lothlórien","Galadriel is in her garden, waiting to speak with you.","Against all your hopes, Gandalf has returned!","'All right, I think this is far enough. You may remove the blindfold now, and I will bring you to the Lady Galadriel.'","'I do not know what to think of this Galadriel, ${PLAYER}. Her words are fair, but beneath the surface she wields strength to match even the fiercest warrior of my people. I am... surprised.\
\
'Let us do as she says, and perhaps the answer to the riddle of your dream will be revealed along the Great River.'","'Guide your friend well, for I will not be responsible for any injuries she suffers while blindfolded. This is the law of the Golden Wood. No outsiders must see the secret trails of Lothlórien. It is out of respect for you, ${PLAYER}, that I permit even this.\
\
'Follow me with care.'","'We have both been through a great deal since last we met, ${PLAYER}, and neither of us is the same person we then were. I do not have the time to tell you what befell me since we parted, but know this: the Quest remains. Your dream tells Galadriel more than she lets on, and it tells me more yet. Our friends face a grave danger along the Anduin. I hope it is not too late for them to avoid it.'\
\
Gandalf's eyes seem to pierce you, and you shiver uncomfortably; there is something unfamiliar in the Wizard's bearing. He reminds you of Saruman.","Galadriel is waiting to speak with you in her gardens.","You have come to Lothlórien with Nona to learn the meaning behind your curious dreams.","Nona is in the gardens of Galadriel, and wants to speak with you.","Instancia: Viejos amigos y nuevas noticias","'I did not expect you in Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}. What need has driven you hither, when so many need your help elsewhere?'\
\
You relate to Galadriel the troubling images you beheld while dreaming in Grimbold's camp, but your spirits fall when she betrays no sign of understanding.\
\
'Your dreams are your own, ${PLAYER}. I had nothing to do with these images you saw.'","'This land is a pretty one, as these Elves seem fond of saying, but this is what the daughter of Suvulch has to say: the hills of Nan Laeglin at sunset are more beautiful by far.\
\
'I submitted to the binding of my eyes for your sake, ${PLAYER}, and to learn the secret behind your dream, but do not expect it again. I will leave this land with my sight unhindered, or these Elves will learn a sharp lesson at the point of Wadu's blade.\
\
'Where is this Elf-queen?'","Talk to Nona in Galadriel's garden","Talk once more to Gandalf","Haldir is in the woods of Lothlórien, waiting to speak with you."},
[7055]={"'Ah, it is good to see you....\
\
'My men and I were ambushed as we approached Snowbourn, and I fear I am the last standing among us.\
\
'I'd come to aid when Gísling warned me of the impending attack on Walstow. I hope that girl brought the might of my people down on those monsters.\
\
'Fastred is somewhere among all of this chaos, but I have seen him not.\
\
'He must be found - the man may be brash, but I fear for his family, and more importantly, the Sutcrofts. Let us search near the Mead Hall, perhaps he has set up his defences there.'","Gísling has fallen!","'We have made it, ${PLAYER}, but I fear we have come too late....\
\
'I must find Fastred at once... would you be willing to fend off the Orcs as I push through the front line?\
\
'I'll meet up with you deeper in Snowbourn once I find him.\
\
'On your mark, I will start my charge!'","Crúmgam stands outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. Fastred's vigour is renewed after the safety of his son was assured. Crúmgam must be defeated to return peace to Snowbourn.","'What madness is this?!\
\
'These fiends think us so weak that they strike at us in Snowbourn? I have slain many Orcs this day, and many more will fall before it ends.\
\
'My own home was invaded by that scum, and I sent Elflád to safety in the barracks once I slew the Orcs to their last.\
\
'I will slay as many as I must to see my son returned to my care. If I should find his abductor, I will split them from head to toe.'","Gísil has fallen!","Fastred is standing outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
Fastred has emerged from the Mead Hall. You should speak to him at once.","Defend Gísling","Gísil is in northern Snowbourn, and has asked you to follow him to the Mead Hall in hopes of meeting with Fastred.","Talk to Fastred","Gísling can be found in south-eastern Snowbourn.\
\
Winsig asks that you find and aid Gísling and the people of Snowbourn while she seeks out Fastred.","Talk to Winsig","'That wretch will not threaten the lives of those for whom I care most dearly ever again.\
\
'His foul sorcery was no match for the might of Rohan and the valour of my people. The Sutcrofts will stand strong, as we always have.\
\
'I wish to spend time with my son, now that I know he is safe. Such fear can never consume me again - he will be kept safe from harm.'","Gísling asks that you seek his father, Gísil as soon as you are able","As the last Orc is felled, Gísling implores you to seek his father near the north gate","Winsig has gone to find Fastred. You should aid the people of Snowbourn in repelling the Orc assault.","Gísil is said to be near the north gate of Snowbourn.\
\
Gísling has moved to aid the people of Snowbourn and asks that you seek the aid of his father and Fastred.","Confront Crúmgam","Gísil is standing at the north gate of Snowbourn.\
\
Gísil and his men were struck by a vicious assult of Orcs. Gísil is wounded, but seeks to locate Fastred.","Winsig has fallen!","Gísil sets off towards the Mead Hall","Fastred now seeks to exact his revenge on his son's abductor.","Fight your way to the north gate of Snowbourn","Find and talk to Gísling","Defeat Crúmgam","Fastred is standing in central Snowbourn.\
\
Crúmgam has been defeated and the Orc force is broken. Fastred, his Thanes, and his people are safe for the moment.","Fastred has fallen!","Defend Winsig as she enters Snowbourn","'What luck! I expected not to see you again, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'The Orcs are relentless, and I fear they shall soon overwhelm us.\
\
'When you departed for Walstow, I sent word to my father in Garsfeld. I can only hope my message was received.\
\
'If he has made it here, he would be near the north gate. I must hold this location, but please, seek out my father!'","Gísling can be found in eastern Snowbourn. He is overwhelmed defending the city from the siege and requires your aid.","Fight your way to the Mead Hall of Snowbourn","Instancia: Sobre estas piedras","Having defeated the Orcs and providing Winsig safe passage, you should seek out Gísling","As Fastred speaks the sky darkens, and a wave of dread passes over you","Crúmgam produces a shredded piece of Folcred's clothing and Fastred is overcome","Winsig is standing outside the east gate of Snowbourn.\
\
Winsig has ridden with you to Snowbourn in hopes of fending off an Orc assault on the town. It seems you are already too late!","The Orcs defeated, Gísil stands wounded among his fallen men","Talk to Gísil","Winsig seeks your aid in fighting to repel the vicious assault of Crúmgam on Snowbourn.","As you approach the Mead Hall, Fastred emerges, his face contorted in rage","<rgb=#FF0000>Fastred, Gísil, Gísling, and Winsig must survive</rgb>","Defeat Crúmgam's forces","As the sky darkens, a familiar figure appears in Snowbourn. You should confront this man, and put and end to his villainy.","'Come, let us rest from such an ordeal. Once you are ready, I believe Gísil wishes to speak with you, but for now, we shall take our leave.'"},
[7056]={"Stand against the forces of evil","'There is no time to mourn, ${PLAYER}! We have to find Aragorn, for I fear he has gotten too far ahead and may become surrounded by his foes if we do not aid him!'","Defeat Crúmgam and his allies","Habla con Calenglad","Talk to Horn and fight alongside him","'This young Ranger, this Halros, is able to do his duty without questioning it? Did I ever have that strength? I know that is what is expected of me, and I came here to prove it, but...\
\
'If I was more like him, would I be able to fight on this field without regret? It weighs me down, even as I know why I must fight. But so many have died, and still the hosts of Mordor pour onto the plain! I thought I could protect Nona and our child from harm, but I see now that there is no hope of that. There are too many evils arrayed against us!'","Habla con Aragorn","'I could not move, ${PLAYER}... it was fell sorcery, and... I was powerless...'\
\
Horn's breath comes raggedly, and there are tears in his eyes.\
\
'Halros sprang to my defence, and took the blows that were meant for me. He died in my place... there was nothing I could do...'","'${PLAYER}, I have not seen you since the morning, and I feared the worst! We have a brief reprieve for now, but it will not last long. I have seen such horrors... so many good men lost...'","Crúmgam has been defeated!","Crúmgam has been defeated, but not without sacrifice.","Stand with Aragorn as he confronts Gothmog","'There is too much sorrow on this field, ${PLAYER}. Gothmog flees, and my anger will follow him, but this is not the day he will pay for the hurts he has caused us.'","You break free of Crúmgam's evil!","'Let us make for the city, ${PLAYER}. I have lost too many friends today.'","Instancia: En un campo de rojo","Gothmog has fled the battlefield, leaving Aragorn and the Grey Company to mourn the slain he leaves behind.","The forces of Mordor prepare for a final attack on the fields of the Pelennor.","You have found Aragorn and the Grey Company on the battlefield as they prepare to confront Gothmog.","You have become held by a powerful and evil force, unable to move!","Talk to Horn on the battlefield","You have fought alongside Horn, but the horrors of battle are taxing his courage.","Crúmgam must pay for his crimes against the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.","'The enemies that pour forth from Mordor will not stop until they have slain every last one of us, ${PLAYER}. They will not stop even then, for there is no mercy in their hearts. They will kill even women and children, the old and the infirm.\
\
'I do not regret my decision! I will fight to make Nona and our child safe, and if I never see them again I will go to my grave knowing that I did what I could. I do not fight for glory or for honour. I fight for time, not for myself but for those I love!'","You have found Horn in the midst of battle, but the bloodshed is taking its toll on him."},
[7057]={"Habla con Narmeleth cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}","'¿Puedes continuar, ${PLAYER}?'","'Debemos apresurarnos, con Narchuil reforjado no pasará mucho tiempo antes de que todo Eriador sea invadido.'","'Vamos a acabar con esto, ${PLAYER}.'","Viaja con Narmeleth para derrotar a Mordirith.","Habla con Narmeleth.\
\
Con las últimas fuerzas, Narmeleth clavó la espada rota en el pecho de Mordirith. Su cuerpo deformado yace cerca del cuerpo colapsado de Narmeleth.","Instancia: Queda una esperanza","'Se ha hecho... el espíritu de Mordirith se ha ido, arrojado al vacío... nunca volverá... Sin embargo, temo que me ha costado la poca gracia que me quedaba y mi tiempo aquí en esta Tierra Media está llegando a su fin....\
\
'No... ¡no llores! Con gusto pagaría este precio de nuevo. Ahora puedo abandonar estas costas sabiendo que he ayudado, aunque sea un poco, a repeler... la oscuridad a la que serví durante tanto tiempo. Pronto, veré a mi madre... a mi padre...'","'Debemos apresurarnos para tomar a Mordirith por sorpresa.'","Protege a Narmeleth","Has fallado en proteger a Narmeleth","Viaja con Narmeleth para derrotar a Mordirith y Mordrambor.","Sigue a Narmeleth","Su vida se ha gastado derrotando a Mordirith, el cuerpo sin vida de Narmeleth yace ante ti. Su rostro, una vez marcado por la culpa y la tristeza, ahora está en paz.\
\
Deberías regresar a Gath Forthnír para contarles todo lo que ha sucedido.'","Habla con Narmeleth","Derrota a Mordrambor","La última esperanza para derrotar a Mordirith, el Falso Rey de Angmar, es un asalto final contra él en su fortaleza de Gador Gularan."},
[7058]={"You have earned the trust of Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden, and she has brought you into Kidzul-kâlah with the hope that you will be a comfort to her friend.","Instancia: Solo medio recordado","Visitors unlooked-for have come to Kidzul-kâlah!","Gultháva has released the enchantment that sealed the chamber in which her friend resides, deep within Kidzul-kâlah.","Talk to Gultháva in her secret grotto","A sensation of peaceful slumber fills the grotto","Gultháva's friend has been revealed to be the shade of Isildur, long kept imprisoned in a secret grotto behind Kidzul-kâlah.","Lead Gandalf and the Elves to Gultháva's friend","Gandalf, Elrond, and Glorfindel have entered Kidzul-kâlah and wants you to lead them to Gultháva's friend.","Talk to Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden","'I have not allowed anyone to see my friend for many a span of years. Perhaps your visit will be a comfort to him.'","Smooth paths of crushed stones climb to a rocky platform in the centre of the odd chamber.","'You have done me a cruelty! In return I demand this of you: harm him not! If you can bring him peace, I charge you with the accomplishment of it!\
\
'There are those who seek to do him ill: forces of evil, servants of a powerful darkness. I brought him here to give him safety from them, and I sang my slumbering song so he might find rest. I knew it could not last, and I wept, but I wanted only to keep him safe. That is all I ever wanted.\
\
'Beware his foes, cruel stranger. A shade stalks among the foetid pools, and dread follows in his train; he seeks my friend, and I have long kept him away. Now that you have broken my protections, you must take up the mantle in his defence. If you should fail, my wrath shall be as the deluge, and will wash you away in the torrent!'","Talk to Elrond in the torrential passage","A piercing scream shattered the stillness! Has something happened to Gultháva?","The shade is reminiscent of Vágari, but possesses none of the Wanderer's dread","Gandalf the Wizard and the Elf-lords Elrond and Glorfindel have come to the flooded passages of Kidzul-kâlah.","'Who... are you? Have you come to let me out? I have been here... for a long time.'\
\
The shade looks around the grotto with evident confusion.\
\
'I think I meant to leave, but whenever I set my mind to it I am overcome by such drowsiness. I should ask Gultháva about it....'","The Maiden of the Gladden is inside Kidzul-kâlah.","'I have spent some time in discussion with Gandalf, and he persuaded me to join him as he unravels this mystery. I do not believe we will find that for which he hopes, but I have brought the sceptre of Annúminas with me at his request.\
\
'The keeper of this place sought to bar our passage. I grieve to cause her such pain, but we must know what she has sealed within Kidzul-kâlah.'","Climb one of the paths up to the centre of the grotto","Make your way through the torrential passage to the chamber where Gultháva keeps her friend","Hurry back down the torrential passage and find Gultháva","Talk to Gultháva's friend","Remain alert in the secret grotto","'Gandalf's suspicion proved correct, ${PLAYER}. I did not think it could be so, but when I beheld him with my own eyes I could not deny it. The shade of Isildur remained after his death, and Gultháva kept him hidden from friend and foe alike. But what can have bound him here beyond the span of his life? There is more to learn of this matter.\
\
'He spoke of an island in the river. He must have returned to Tol Send. Go there and speak with him, and then return to the Beorninghús with what you have learned.'","In appearance, Gultháva's friend puts you in mind of Vágari the Wanderer, but whereas that shade filled you with a sense of dread, this one does not.","Talk to the shade of Isildur in Gultháva's secret grotto","'I see the faces of those I knew... but that was so long ago. There was war, and it seemed it would never end. And yet it did... at last there was an ending, but...\
\
'Peace? No... it did not last. I remember... I remember...\
\
'I remember death! Treachery and death! I swam... there was an island in the river... an island....'","Gultháva mourns the disappearance of her friend, the shade she held captive for so long."},
[7059]={"Habla con el señor de los túmulos","'¿Valió la pena el esfuerzo? ¿Aprendiste tu lección? ¡Deja que los Muertos duerman su sueño sin sueños y camina tú mismo sobre la hierba verde bajo el sol!'","La entrada a Othrongroth está cerca, al oeste.\
\
Tom Bombadil te llevó a salvo a la entrada de Othrongroth, el Gran Túmulo, en las Quebradas de los Túmulos. Tu búsqueda del Rey Brujo te llevará al interior del túmulo.","'Instancia: Othrongroth","El Rey Brujo y el enano Skorgrím han entrado en Othrongroth. Deberías seguirlos al interior del túmulo y buscarlos allí.","Ve a la entrada del Gran Túmulo, Othrongroth","Tom Bombadil te ha traído al túmulo llamado Othrongroth. Un sirviente del Nazgûl, Andraste, dijo que el Señor de los Nazgûl se encontraría aquí.","'¡Aquí estamos, mis valientes! ¡No tengo tiempo que perder, salvando viajeros tontos! ¡Mi Baya de Oro volverá a casa, y debo preparar sus cuencos de lirios!\
\
'La entrada de Othrongroth está al oeste. Ten cuidado. ¡No prestes atención a voces mortales!'","'¡Qué gusto! Mi Maestro te envía saludos. Te concedo el favor de una audiencia antes de matarte. Pareces deseoso de cierto conocimiento, así que te lo daré. ¡Porque los Muertos no hablan!' El tumulario se ríe.\
\
'¡Mi Maestro busca un gran Poder para el Señor Oscuro, pero el Señor Oscuro tiene más planes que este. ¡El Enano Pálido irá al norte y reunirá un ejército en nombre de Angmar y el Rey Brujo!\
\
'El demacrado, alberga un gran poder en él y a quien debo esta forma, va hacia el este. Allí, en Agamaur, despertará un Poder que yace dormido en las aguas. ¡Con ella bajo su mando, los cielos se tornarán en sangre y todos desesperarán!\
\
'Ahora tu audiencia llega a su fin. Tu muerte te espera.'","Gracias a la llegada de Tom Bombadil, el señor de los túmulos ha sido derrotado. Tom espera para hablar contigo.","Sigue al Rey Brujo","Tu camino a través del Gran Túmulo te llevó al Jinete Negro, quien notó tu presencia y llamó a los Muertos para atacarte. ¡Derrota a estas criaturas y continúa a través de Othrongroth!","Tu persecución del Rey Brujo te ha conducido a una habitación con un tumulario sentado en un gran trono. La criatura te dio la bienvenida y dijo que si querías una audiencia, podías acercarte.","Persigue al Rey Brujo"},
[7060]={"Much depends upon your haste! You must reach Umbar Baharbêl!","Race westward along the road to Umbar Baharbêl","Khashig has called for you to stop and explain your haste.","'Stop! What drives you toward Umbar Baharbêl with such reckless speed?\
\
'${PLAYER}? Is that you?'","Race to Umbar Baharbêl before it is too late!","The cannons fall silent behind you as you outpace your enemies... but Umbar remains far distant","Khashig leaps from his guard-post and calls for you to stop","Instancia: Supera al viento, supera a las olas","Warn Khashig of the approaching danger"},
[7061]={"Move through the twisting passage and Gandalf will tell you what he knows of Magoldir","Gandalf stands within the Halls of Memory woven by the words of Vóin the Zhélruka, long ago.","Instancia: Pintando el cuadro","Gandalf's study of the Black Book of Mordor has raised as many questions as it has answered.","Gandalf informed you, regretfully, that this branch of his study has come to naught. Instead, the Wizard desires for you to return to the entrance of the Halls of Memory, there to follow a different avenue of inquiry.","'Spare me this look of disappointment, ${PLAYER}! I have not been idle, and while that course of study has come to an early end, there is another avenue upon which I have had some success.\
\
'I told you that Vóin filled the Black Book with much talk of Thafar-gathol; indeed, it seems to have been an obsession of his. The reading was slow, and for a time I paid it little mind, for I could not see how it might relate to the rest of his writings. But I am a Wizard! I am Gandalf! I was seized with sudden inspiration and knew there must be some element I missed, a kernel of useful information buried within his constant talk of Thafar-gathol. And so there was!'","Gandalf has found the place he sought in the Black Book, and is ready to speak to you of Vóin's journey in Mordor.","Listen to Gandalf's thoughts concerning Vóin's encounter with Magoldir","Vóin adventured in the Grey Mountains in search of lost Thafar-gathol","Gandalf has found the place he sought in the Black Book, and is ready to speak to you of Vóin's journey in the Grey Mountains.","'That is all I have learned so far. It will take some days to learn more, but I am confident Vóin and Magoldir will not keep their secrets from me for long.'","'Vóin writes of Mordor in many different pages of his tome, but I cannot tell if he speaks of one journey or several. The writing on these pages is confused, and many of the details are obscured; I cannot say when he adventured there or for what purpose. I believe when he reached the end of the book, he continued to write on the overleaf pages, seemingly at random. This makes a true accounting of the chronology difficult.\
\
'And yet, there are some conclusions to be made. This black-bound tome bears the mark of Sauron, and that is not a symbol commonly found beyond the borders of his land.'","Vóin wrote of a journey he took in search of Thafar-gathol in the company of King Thráin I, who led the Longbeards prior to the founding of Erebor beneath the Lonely Mountain. Further information about this journey lies ahead, beyond the unformed passage that joins the several Halls of Memory.","Gandalf desires to speak to you concerning what he has learned from his study of the Black Book of Mordor.","The fog dissipates, revealing further avenues of knowledge","Gandalf has told you that the name Magoldir does not appear only within the pages of the Black Book of Mordor, and he desires to tell you what else he knows of the Elf.","Listen to Gandalf's description of Vóin's account","'Almost two thousand years before this encounter with Vóin in the Ered Mithrin, an Elf named Magoldir served beneath High King Gil-galad during the Siege of Barad-dûr. His name appears in a list of Elves who maintained the fortifications of an encampment in Mordor called Echad-in-Edhil, but that is all. If he performed any heroic deeds on behalf of the Last Alliance, they are not recorded.\
\
'Indeed, if it were not for the frequent mentions of his name in the Black Book, I should think he perished during the Siege.'","Many questions remain","Talk to Gandalf in the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Gandalf has told you that despite failing to find Thafar-gathol, Vóin found something of interest in the Grey Mountains, and he has asked you to consider what it might have been.","Gandalf speaks to you of the Halls of Memory, a representation of the contents of the Black Book of Mordor given shape by his words and those of the dwarf Vóin.","Listen to the musings of Gandalf","Consider the obscured figures in Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Consider the obscured figures in the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Something befell Vóin among the rocky crags of Mordor, but his account remains vague, the details obscured.\
\
Gandalf has asked you to consider the cryptic figures he has found in Vóin's account of his journey in Mordor.","Move through the twisting passage until you reach another of the Halls of Memory","Return to the entrance of the Halls of Memory, there to pursue a different avenue of inquiry","Gandalf waits at the entrance to the Halls of Memory, prepared to follow a different avenue of inquiry.","While adventuring in the Grey Mountains, Vóin encountered an Elf named Magoldir, who claimed to oppose evil in all of its forms. According to the Wizard, the name \\qMagoldir\\q occurs frequently among the pages of the Black Book of Mordor.","Talk to Gandalf in Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Talk to Gandalf in the Halls of Memory","'Why did King Thráin agree to lead an expedition in search of Thafar-gathol? His father Náin had been slain in Moria, along with many of his people, and the survivors gathered in the Grey Mountains. They dwelled for a time in the Steel Keep and reopened several of their mines, but it was not enough. If he could make use of the Zhélruka to find a more suitable home, with wealth to rival lost Khazad-dûm, he would do so.'","Vóin wrote of a journey he took to a \\qcold, hard land,\\q where great evil dwelt. Further information about this journey lies ahead, beyond the unformed passage that joins the several Halls of Memory.","It was to Mordor that Vóin ventured... but when did he go, and why?","Gandalf is speaking to you of Vóin's journey in Mordor, where he apparently obtained the Black Book, but the Wizard remains confused about a number of obscured events in the Zhélruka's account.","'Much of the writing within the Black Book of Mordor remains a mystery to me, ${PLAYER}, but I know enough of ancient dwarvish to make a beginning. The tome was written by a dwarf named Vóin, the thrice-great grandfather of Khîl Tale-spinner. Like Khîl himself, Vóin was one of the Zhélruka. He kept a home in Járnfast more than a thousand years ago, but the Black Book you found within the hidden chamber there is all that remains of his life. Vóin himself appears in no other record that I have found.\
\
'The writing of dwarves, or at least that of the Longbeards I have known, is generally straightforward and to the point. Not so that of the Zhélruka! Indeed, while I have not had occasion to study many works of the dwarves of the East, Vóin's writing in the Black Book seems more convoluted than others of his kind. He writes in multiple languages, using many different runic alphabets. Furthermore, some of these scrawlings are clearly written using a cipher, or I am not a Wizard! There are curious gaps between some of these lines and on some of these pages. Khîl's cryptic ancestor may have written some of his account with hidden letters, ${PLAYER}, but unless we learn their trick they will remain invisible to us. That is a pity, but I warrant the visible writing will keep us busy enough!\
\
'He writes often of the lost city of Thafar-gathol. It seems to have been a preoccupation of his.'"},
[7063]={"Frodo has slowed his pace. The Dead Marshes are taking their toll on him.","Continue the passage of the marshes","Gollum has bounded back to you. Your master is right: the creature has not guided you wrong... yet.\
\
You still do not trust him.","Talk to Gollum, if he can bring himself to speak","Frodo looks very tired. The journey through the swamp is taking its toll.","Gollum is terrified, and is in no shape to go on. The frightening encounter with the terrible shadow has shaken him tremendously.","This will be a good place to sit next to Frodo and keep watch","Remain awake and alert, Sam!","'Come, come, hobbitses! Good Sméagol knows the way through the swamp. Step only where he steps, or you will find yourself at the bottom, and no one will help you then, oh no!\
\
'If you must go to His black country, only Sméagol can bring you there unseen. Only Sméagol! That is a bad place, yes, a bad place indeed. It would be wiser to turn back, yes it would, but you said you needed to go, and go you will, yes!'","A terrible shadow approaches from high above the Dead Marshes!","You do not like what you overheard Gollum muttering to himself, if you did not imagine it.","How has Frodo fared?","'That was a Black Rider! I hoped we had seen the last of them, but I suppose that was an idle daydream. They are still searching for us.\
\
'The Ring is so heavy, Sam. I know we need to keep going, but perhaps we can rest for a moment? Sméagol is beside himself... I do not think he will want to move for a while. Look at him! The poor creature. Not just him: all three of us! I will be glad to leave these Dead Marshes, but... just a rest... a short one.\
\
'Then we will keep moving. Is that all right, Sam?'","A cold chill runs down your spine!","'Did it see us? Aaaaach! Did it see us? Winged wraiths, terrible, terrible! They see everything, precious, everything! And they tell Him all that they see, they do! Did it see us?'\
\
Gollum is shaking, his eyes wide with the terror of the experience. He will not move for some time.","Make your way, carefully, through the swamp <rgb=#00FF00>(press 'Insert' to toggle your more careful walk)</rgb>","Instance: Passage of the Marshes","Hide!","You and Frodo inch closer and closer to Mordor, but you do not trust the guide that has brought you into the Dead Marshes: the creature Gollum.","Comfort Frodo and decide what to do","'How are you holding up, Sam? This is a hard land... it seems so many of the places we must journey through are hard lands! I miss my own comfortable bed, and Bag End!\
\
'There's nothing for it, is there? We have to keep going, one foot in front of the other. Sméagol will show us the way, if we are kind to him. He was treated very cruelly in Mordor, Sam. He has been through a lot.\
\
'I suppose that is true for all of us, now. Just keep going, that is all we can do.'","You have to go on, even if the Dead Marshes seem to go on forever.","Talk to Gollum, and let him know how things stand","Try and stay awake, Sam!","Talk to Mister Frodo in the Dead Marshes","'Nice hobbit, nice Sam, nothing to worry about, no, precious! Gollum, gollum! Did you get the sleepies you needed, did you, gollum? We needs to be moving again, yes, yes we do! No time for delays now!\
\
'Master says we must go, so go we must, yes! Time to go, precious! Time to move!'","Frodo blinks at you for a moment and slowly rouses from his slumber.\
\
'I suppose it is time to set out again? I am ready to be out of this wretched swamp, and the only way for it is to get moving again, I suppose. I am very tired, Sam.'","Sit next to Frodo and stay alert for any dangers while he rests","Talk to Gollum and keep a watchful eye on the wretch","Talk to Frodo and make sure he is feeling all right","The journey through the swamp has proven to be very difficult, with no end in sight.","'Step with care, hobbitses... the ground underfoot is not to be trusted, oh no it is not. Sméagol will show you where to go.'","Gollum has bounded ahead through the swamps, showing you and Frodo the way.","Frodo has wandered off by himself! You have to find him!","Talk to Mister Frodo","Stay close to Gollum, and make sure he does not try anything","'What... what is it, Sam? Were you... were you calling for me? I felt as if I heard you from a long way off, but there was something....'\
\
Frodo shakes his head, trying to remember something.\
\
'There were faces in the water. I could see them by the light of the candles, I think. But how could that be? There were so many: good faces and proud faces, stern faces and evil faces too. But why?'","You hate to do it, but it is time to wake Frodo and set out once again.","Talk to Frodo and make sure he is all right","Find out what Gollum is up to, the villain!","Frodo has decided to catch some sleep, and wants you to sit next to him.","'This swamp is even worse than I thought it would be, Sam. I have found my feet sinking into the mud even on terrain that seems solid, and would have become quite stuck if I hadn't noticed immediately!\
\
'I know you do not trust Sméagol, but he is the only guide we have. Without his help, could we hope to come to Mordor? I do not think it likely, Sam.'","You sit next to Frodo and resolve to stay awake and alert","You are sure Gollum will try something at some point during the passage of the marshes. Stay close to him and make sure the wretch has no opportunity to cause trouble!"},
[7064]={"Talk to Durin by the overlook in the ruins atop High Sundergrót","Wait with your companions while they discuss your find and the history of High Sundergrót","Hill-beasts and bats haunt the upper reaches of the ruins perched atop High Sundergrót.\
\
You should clear the path of these dangers to make the way safe for Durin and your companions.","Instancia: Peregrinación a Sundergrót","Your companions have rested from their climb and now look around the snowy heights of High Sundergrót.","Prince Durin has come to High Sundergrót and waits to speak with you.","'You and your travelling companions have done well, ${PLAYER}! I received Glóin's message at Skarháld not long after it was sent, for his messenger-ravens are renowned for their speed, and the bird he selected was no exception. His tidings of a new Lord of Gundabad fill me not with fear but with anticipation, for no Orc will stand between me and my chosen path, no matter his lineage. I had the message copied and sent on to the Lonely Mountain, the Iron Hills, and other dwarf-holdings in lands both near and far. My armies gather to march on Gundabad, and all will be forewarned with the tidings uncovered on your scouting expedition.\
\
'I am eager to turn my gaze upon the Mountain-home, and sought no delay, but I wanted to first make the journey here to Sundergrót. It was here that the very first Durin to bear that name put an end to the usurper Mótsog, solidifying his power and his claim to lead the dwarves with that victory. By making this journey I hoped to become closer to my ancient forebear, that I may draw strength for the battles to come from the memory of he whose name I bear.\
\
'I confess that I did not expect so much climbing.'","The forlorn wind whistles among the crags, but nothing else moves","Examine the broken dwarf-blade lying near the overlook on the upper level","Talk to Durin at High Sundergrót","Search the drift of snow to the north, where a glint of metal has caught your eye","Continue north-east and climb the fallen pillar lying over the stairs to reach the upper level of the ruins in High Sundergrót","Listen to the words of Durin by the overlook in High Sundergrót","'The climb to this high place has quite exhausted me, and we are not yet at the top. I must rest for a moment. You go on ahead, and keep your eyes open.'","Durin and your companions have safely arrived on the upper level of the ruins perched atop High Sundergrót.","You hear growling sounds and fluttering wings in the upper reaches of the ruins","'The path continues to the north-east. I ask you to keep climbing, my friend, and to clear the way for the rest of us.'","Accompany Durin on the northward road to war","'Just a... just a moment, my friend. The climb to this high place has quite exhausted me, and we are not yet at the top. I must rest for a moment.'","The climb to High Sundergrót has left Glóin quite exhausted, and he wishes to speak with you before you proceed.","'This is a matter of some delicacy, my friend, and I urge you to exercise discretion. I will not belabour the point, for I trust you will use such prudence as this subject requires.\
\
'I tasked you with finding and defeating the raiding-party from Gundabad that endangered the folk living among the Wells of Langflood, and from Glóin's message-raven I know that you did so successfully. But there is one matter of concern that was not made clear to me in the message.\
\
'I ask you this, then: were Imák and Venko effective on this errand? Did you have any reason to question their loyalties? Did they strike you as good-hearted allies of the Longbeards, or did you detect veins of disloyalty or deception running beneath their surface appearances?\
\
'I do not know if you are familiar with the Greymaul Rebellion, but all my people know the lesson of High Sundergrót: even our closest friends can be tempted into treachery, as was Mótsog the Traitor. He was once the dearest friend of Durin, Father of the Dwarves, and still he raised the Greymaul army in rebellion, claiming a lordship that was not his. Durin the First repaid that treachery with death, though Mótsog was once his closest friend. I would not say this Zhélruka or this Stout-axe are as dear to us as that, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
You assure Durin that you have few complaints about the trustworthiness or effectiveness of your companions.\
\
'Then I do not either. Still, I advise you to keep an eye upon the Zhélruka especially, for his people believe they have a claim upon Gundabad, and I do not want to win it back from the Orcs only to lose it to these dwarves from the east!'","Continue climbing northward among the crags of High Sundergrót","Long ago and high above Sundergrót, the Greymaul Rebellion came to an end. It is now a place of great import for Durin's Folk, and Longbeards have been known to visit the high crags for contemplation and reflection.","Durin has asked you to continue your climb to the upper levels of High Sundergrót, among the ruins to the north-east. A sloping pillar lies across the broken stairs that will help you gain access to the upper levels.","A broken dwarf-blade catches your eye by the overlook on the upper level of the ruins perched atop High Sundergrót.","Clear beasts and bats from the ruins in the upper reaches of High Sundergrót","Glóin suggested that you continue your northward climb among the crags of High Sundergrót.","Durin is ready to turn once more for the north, and to war.","The drift covers an ancient helmet of dwarf-make, shattered long ago","This blade is of such ancient make that it must have been broken long ago","'To Elderslade, then! May the journey be quick, and the road uneventful. Victory lies at the end of it, at the very gates of Gundabad!'","Talk to Glóin among the crags of High Sundergrót"},
[7065]={"Defeat the third opponent","Enter the combat area","Defeat the first opponent.","Enter the combat area.","You forfeit the challenge!","Defeat the second opponent","A new pit-fighting tournament has begun and you have been asked to participate.","Defeat the first opponent","'Good work, ${RACE}. Párgrub finally winning supplies! Soon this poor snaga will be the best merchant, yes.'","Defeat the third opponent.","Instancia: Luchador de foso","Opponent defeated!","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the combat area!</rgb>","Defeat the second opponent."},
[7066]={"'Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. No esperaba verte aquí, pero me alegra que hayas venido.\
\
'La Hueste Dorada parte hacia el Bosque Negro para llevar la guerra al Enemigo más allá de las fronteras de Lothlórien, y me senté junto al árbol de Faengris para verlos partir. El hermano de Faengris, Achardor, va con ellos, buscando venganza por la muerte de mi esposo. Le dije lo mismo que te dije a ti, que quiero honrar la memoria de Faengris en lugar de buscar venganza, pero no me escuchó.\
\
'Por favor, protégelo, ${PLAYER}. Demasiadas muertes han llegado ya a mi familia.'","Habla con Raddir","Habla con Bróin","Braiglinn te ha traído para conocer a algunos de los Elfos con los que lucharás durante el viaje de la Hueste Dorada a través del Bosque Negro: Raddir, Sigileth y Achardor.","'¡Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}! Es bueno verte de nuevo, y te doy la bienvenida a las filas de la Guardia Oculta. Los cuchillos de Sigileth, el arco de Cúcheron, el conocimiento del camino de Raddir y la fuerte voluntad de Achardor llevarán a cabo esta misión, y la amistad entre Moria y Lothlórien se fortalecerá por ello.\
\
'¡Que el Enemigo tiemble al enterarse de la llegada de la Hueste Dorada, y no pensará en la Guardia Oculta hasta que estemos en las puertas de Dol Guldur y exijamos a los prisioneros allí retenidos a cambio de la vida de Mazog!'","La Guardia Oculta, el grupo de Elfos encargado de llevar a Mazog en secreto a Dol Guldur, se está preparando para cruzar el Anduin, después de lo cual se encontrarán con los enanos que transportan al líder de los Orcos.","Habla con Sigileth","Los Elfos y los enanos están discutiendo los planes relacionados con Mazog.","Habla con Achardor","Braiglinn te espera para hablar contigo en Imlad Lalaith.","'Es un placer conocerte, ${PLAYER}, y sé que serás de gran ayuda para nosotros en esta misión. Si vamos a llevar al líder de los Orcos a Dol Guldur con la esperanza de que podamos intercambiar su libertad por la de los prisioneros enanos, debemos hacerlo en secreto. Nuestros números no son tan grandes como para resistir un esfuerzo decidido para quitarnos al prisionero antes de llegar a la fortaleza.'","'Hemos cruzado, ${PLAYER}. Los enanos deberían estar justo adelante con su cautivo; vamos a saludarlos y discutir los planes para nuestro viaje.'","'¡Por fin estamos en marcha, ${PLAYER}! Si tienes fe en estos Elfos, esta \\qGuardia Oculta,\\q entonces yo también.\
\
'¡Que nuestro viaje a través del Bosque Negro sea rápido y nuestro regreso aún más, con Bori y los otros prisioneros sanos y salvos!'","Escucha la discusión sobre el plan relacionado con Mazog","Bróin ha pedido hablar contigo.","'El Señor Celeborn y la Dama Galadriel han determinado que los Elfos de Lothlórien deben estar aliados con los enanos de Moria, como lo estuvieron hace mucho tiempo. Han seleccionado a varios Elfos para supervisar el paso de Mazog a través del Bosque Negro hasta Dol Guldur, donde el Orco será intercambiado por los prisioneros retenidos por el Enemigo en esa fortaleza.\
\
'Te llevaré a estos Elfos, esta Guardia Oculta, mientras hacen sus preparativos.'","'Me llamo Sigileth, , y ya estoy al tanto de tus hazañas. Eres ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} para acompañarnos en esta misión, aunque tengo mis dudas sobre su sabiduría. Es una pena que los enanos hayan perdido a algunos de los suyos en las cárceles del enemigo, pero así es la guerra. Devolver a Mazog a sus aliados me parece indefendible.\
\
'Si el Señor Celeborn y la Dama Galadriel ven valor en ello, no es lugar de Sigileth cuestionarlo.'","Habla con Issuriel","Has cruzado el río con la compañía de Elfos encargados de llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur, y Raddir ahora te espera para hablar contigo.","Cairches te espera para transportarte a través del Anduin con la compañía de Elfos encargados de llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur.","Habla con Cúcheron","'¡Te damos la bienvenida, ${PLAYER}! Somos la Guardia Oculta, formada por orden del Señor y la Dama, y nuestra misión es llevar a Mazog a las puertas de Dol Guldur, para intercambiar su vida por la de los prisioneros que se encuentran en esa fortaleza. ¡El secreto es nuestra consigna y la sorpresa nuestro aliado!\
\
'Issuriel ya me ha hablado de tus grandes hazañas. Sé que serás un miembro vital de la Guardia Oculta en este viaje.'","Habla con Braiglinn","'Veamos el campamento que estos Elfos han hecho. Habrá pocas comodidades enanas aquí en estos oscuros bosques, pero haré lo mejor que pueda para no quejarme. ¡Nos espera un gran viaje!'","'Será un placer para mí guiar a la Guardia Oculta a través del río en este, el primer paso de su viaje.\
\
'Que termine en victoria.'","Braiglinn te espera para llevarte a conocer a más de los Elfos que componen la Guardia Oculta.","Braiglinn te ha traído para conocer a dos Elfos más con los que lucharás durante el viaje a Dol Guldur: Cúcheron e Issuriel.","'Los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta fueron elegidos por su experiencia variada en varios ámbitos: Sigileth por su habilidad en el combate cuerpo a cuerpo y Raddir por su capacidad experta en rastreo.\
\
'Si fuera mi decisión, podría haber dejado que Achardor se uniera a la fuerza principal de los Malledhrim en lugar de la Guardia Oculta, dada la reciente tragedia de la muerte de su hermano. Pero estoy seguro de que la Dama Galadriel tenía sus propias razones para hablar en su favor y cree que será una parte importante de la Guardia Oculta.\
\
'Te llevaré al resto de la compañía, ${PLAYER}.'","Instancia: Planes de la Hueste Dorada","'Mi hermano Faengris fue asesinado por Orcos que bajaron de las montañas siguiendo a la compañía que buscó refugio en el Bosque de Oro recientemente, y deseo acabar con la vida de Mazog yo mismo! Me duele saber que debemos entregarlo a sus aliados, y ya he argumentado mucho en contra de eso.\
\
'Le pedí al Señor Celeborn que me dejara acompañar al grupo que transporta al prisionero, pero negó mi solicitud. Solo una vez que la Dama Galadriel habló con él cambió de opinión; no sé lo que dijo, pero estoy agradecido por ello. Ahora mantendré un ojo atento sobre Mazog durante el viaje, y si me da la más mínima razón, me vengaré de él.'","Habla con Cairches"},
[7067]={"Algunos Angmarim han regresado a los alrededores de Delossad para registrar las ruinas.\
\
Muildir te ha informado de los Angmarim que merodean afuera y quiere que los derrotes antes de entrar.","'Muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Ahora tu exploración de las ruinas no debería verse interrumpida. Pero antes de que pruebes la puerta nuevamente: Delossad es un lugar antiguo, y algún recuerdo de un gran mal pesa sobre sus piedras. Temo que algo terrible surgiera de allí, y te pido que mantengas la calma cuando estés dentro.\
\
'Examina todo lo que te parezca extraño, pues creo que la memoria del dolor que habita este lugar se revelará ante ti. Aprende cuanto puedas, pero mantente alerta: criaturas de la oscuridad son atraídas por estos lugares, y puede que tengas que defenderte.\
\
'Yo montaré guardia aquí fuera y me aseguraré de que ningún enemigo entre en Delossad mientras estés dentro.'","'Abandonemos este lugar. El recuerdo se aferra a estas piedras como un sudario y me llena de inquietud.'","'Escucha, ${PLAYER}: muchos de los Angmarim que vinieron a Tâl Bruinen están buscando en otros lugares, pero algunos han regresado para registrar las ruinas.\
\
'Derrota a los que encuentres aquí y vuelve conmigo antes de buscar en el interior. No quiero que te vean abrir la puerta.'","Derrota Angmarim en Delossad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Examina los objetos inusuales dentro de Delossad","'Ve ahora a las profundidades de Delossad y descubre los secretos que puedas, ${PLAYER}. Yo montaré guardia aquí para asegurar que tu búsqueda no sea interrumpida.'","Muildir se oculta cerca de la entrada de Delossad.\
\
Has derrotado a los Angmarim que volvieron a Delossad y ahora deberías regresar con él.","Te has encontrado con Mordrambor en las profundidades de Delossad, y te ha encerrado en una de las celdas donde Amarthiel fue prisionera.\
\
Muildir ha venido en tu ayuda y te liberará de la celda.","Muildir se oculta cerca de la entrada de Delossad.\
\
Está esperando hablar contigo antes de que investigues las ruinas de Delossad.","Angmarim derrotados en Delossad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'La mayoría de los Angmarim han ido a registrar otras zonas de Tâl Bruinen, pero algunos han regresado. Derrótalos con cautela y vuelve conmigo; no quiero que te vean abrir la puerta.'","'¿Estás bien, ${PLAYER}? El Númenóreano Negro apareció frente a Delossad, y apenas tuve un momento para ocultarme. Si hubiera sido cualquier otro oponente, habría entrado en combate, pero no podía esperar derrotarlo sin otros de mi linaje. Fue hacia la puerta y entró, y yo lo seguí en secreto, con la tenue esperanza de poder oponerme a él si llegaba el momento.\
\
'Tiemblo al pensar lo que habría hecho si hubiera sabido que yo estaba allí.\
\
'Abandonemos este lugar, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Me dirás lo que aprendiste mientras salimos de las sombras de estas ruinas tristes.'","Habla con Muildir","Instancia: Prisionera de los Pueblos Libres","El interior de Delossad, conocido como Sithad en días olvidados, es oscuro y lúgubre. Sus muros han visto gran dolor, y un aire pesado lo envuelve todo.\
\
Estás buscando en la penumbra de Delossad pistas sobre el misterio del anillo de Amarthiel, Narchuil.","Has viajado con Muildir a las ruinas de Delossad para buscar respuestas sobre el pasado de Narchuil."},
[7070]={"Speak with Mizâdi once more inside the tent.","Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro.","Place the bowl of food in front of Khónyo Bóro.","Speak with Mizâdi once more inside the tent","Speak with Mizâdi inside Mizâdi's tent","'Question the Bóro, please.'","Speak with Numûru inside Mizâdi's tent.","Speak with Mizâdi inside the tent","Place the bowl of food in front of Khónyo Bóro","Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro","Speak with Khónyo Bóro inside Mizâdi's tent in Ingar-garâsh","Shâra Mizâdi has requested your presence in the interrogation of Khónyo Bóro in her tent in Ingar-garâsh.","Speak with Numûru inside Mizâdi's tent","Pick up the bowl of food from the table inside Mizâdi's tent","'I do not think he speaks the truth. He is close to breaking, I can feel it. He is scared, but still feels duty bound.'","Speak with Mizâdi inside the tent.","Speak with Mizâdi inside Mizâdi's tent.","'I knew he would crack! No one can resist a good stew... or even my stew.'","Instancia: Persiguiendo a Bârshud, Parte 2","'I will not tell you what you want to know, northern swine.'","Speak with Khónyo Bóro inside Mizâdi's tent in Ingar-garâsh.","'Now that we know Bârshud headed to Zajâna, we can make our own way there as well.'","Grab the bowl of food from the table inside Mizâdi's tent."},
[7072]={"Roamingstar is at the Crossings of the Erui.\
\
You have defeated the armoured wights and Roamingstar has arrived, filling you with hope. You should listen as she confronts her Sister.","Defeat the summoned armoured wights","Listen to the Lone Lady","More armoured wights rise from the shallows of the Erui!","The Sisters of Lebennin seek to calm their Sister's fury before it consumes both the Enemy and the people of Gondor alike.","The Armour of the Usurper falls broken into the shallows of the Erui!","'You have done me a great favour, ${PLAYER}. I shall not trouble you again.'","The Five Sisters are gathered at the Crossings of Erui.\
\
You have defeated the Lone Lady and broken her madness. You should watch as her Sisters speak to her.","'Why do you persist, ${RACE}? You claim that my Sisters fear for me? That I should speak to them before it is too late?\
\
'I have no Sisters!\
\
'I cast you from my waters once, and I shall do so again!'","Instancia: Furia del Erui","As the armoured wights sink back into the Erui, Roamingstar appears!","The Lone Lady is at the Crossings of Erui.\
\
You have defeated many of the Lone Lady's armoured wights and should now listen as she speaks.","The Lone Lady can be found at the Crossings of Erui.\
\
You have arrived at the Crossings of Erui and should now try to speak to the Lone Lady.","Defeat the Lone Lady's risen armoured wights","The Lone Lady's armoured wights can be found at the Crossings of Erui.\
\
The Lone Lady has withdrawn in her anger and has summoned more armoured wights to drive you from the Erui. You must stand fast!","Observe the meeting of the Five Sisters","Defeat the Armour of the Usurper","The Armour of the Usurper is at the Crossings of Erui.\
\
The Lone Lady has taken control of Castamir's long-lost armour and now wields it in her final assault against your and her Sisters. You must defeat the Lone Lady.","The Lone Lady's armoured wights can be found at the Crossings of Erui.\
\
The Lone Lady has summoned wights of the Kin-strife to push you from her waters. You must defeat them!","Talk to the Lone Lady","'I am glad you urged my Sisters to seek me, ${PLAYER}, and thankful that they could pull me from the depths of my sorrow.\
\
'There is naught I can say to atone for the evils I visited upon you, but know that you are always welcome in my waters. Although some of the armoured wights may still roam the Erui, I shall work to quiet them.\
\
'Take the armour I bore against you, and bring it to the Men of these lands. Let this dark chapter of our shared history be done at last....'","Castamir's armour comes to life!","The last of the risen armoured wights sinks back into the Erui...","Listen as Roamingstar confronts the Lone Lady","The Lone Lady is at the Crossings of Erui.\
\
You have calmed the anger of the Lone Lady and should now speak to her."},
[7073]={"King Elessar has brought his soldiers to bear against the Corsair raiders that threaten Iáphel.","A young boy emerges from the hiding-place: Orgolas of Anfalas!","Find and defeat Corsairs hiding behind the northern buildings of Iáphel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I stayed behind, ${PLAYER}, and I was right to do so: some of the Corsair raiders hid themselves around the square and thought to attack Elessar from the rear. But there may be more! We should follow after him and see if any other villains had the same idea.'","Talk to Orgolas","A Corsair leaps from his hiding-place and attacks!","Talk to Rossaran among the northern buildings of Iáphel","Talk to King Elessar by the shore","Talk to King Elessar outside Iáphel","'Would that I had a company of mounted swan-knights with which to sweep the Corsairs from this place! You and I will have to do, ${PLAYER}, and we must be up to the task. That is the command of the King!'","Talk to Gimli in the main square of Iáphel","Gimli remained in the main square of Iáphel to root Corsair raiders from out of hiding.","'This attack is a personal affront to me, ${PLAYER}, for this land is not just under the protection of Lady Nauriel and the Knights of the Green Hills, but it falls also within my purview as the King of Gondor! The people of Iáphel will not be endangered while I still live to prevent it!'","Search for Corsairs hiding behind the northern buildings of Iáphel.","'I do not fully understand it, ${PLAYER}. The main Corsair ships must be anchored further down the river, for most of the raiders rowed here in secret, piloting small boats. Why then would they set fire to the hillside as they approached Iáphel, giving away their presence before they reached the village that was their destination?'\
\
You suggest to Elessar that perhaps the Corsairs wanted to inspire fear in the hearts of the villagers, and he nods.\
\
'Perhaps that is the answer. Still, it is good to hear that most of the villagers remain unharmed. We drove the Corsairs back to the river and most of them fled in their small ships. They may seek to return once they have licked their wounds, but I think it more likely they will not attack Iáphel again for some time.\
\
'We should search along the shoreline and ensure that no Corsairs remain here in hiding. It is possible we overlooked some of the fleeing pillagers in our charge down the hill.'","Instancia: Incursores en Tûm Rost","'One of the Corsairs, a huge lout with muscles like I have never seen, lifted Thorongil up by one arm and dangled him over the river. \\qIs this one of those halflings I have heard about?\\q he asked, and Thorongil spat curses at him and said he was named Thorongil and would have all the Corsairs put to death if they didn't unhand him. They laughed at that, oh, did they ever! I can still hear the laughter, it's terrible!\
\
'But there was something about that name they didn't like. \\qThorongil, you say?\\q the big fellow asked, drawing his sword. I think he would have killed Thorongil then and there, but an Elf among the Corsairs said something to him and his face became like a storm cloud. I couldn't really hear it from where I was hiding, but I think the Elf was saying the captain would want to keep Thorongil onboard her ship.\
\
'The big lout put his sword away and hauled Thorongil onto their boat and they rowed out into the river and then they were gone. I know it was wrong and we shouldn't have come here! But I didn't know how to get out of it, and then it was all over and it was too late! The way they spoke about their captain... it fills me with terror even now!'","'The Reaper of the Waves? I think we know this captain, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Nakási has reason to hate Gondor, and she told you herself that she planned to wreak vengeance upon my kingdom. It would not surprise me to learn she planned to raid every village along the river's edge in Pinnath Gelin, but the abduction of Thorongil caused her to change this plan. He may prove a useful hostage for the Kindred of the Coins.\
\
'But I am getting ahead of myself. Right now we must bring this unwelcome news to Thorongil's mother Nauriel, and then perhaps we can do something to prevent Nakási from escaping Outer Gondor with Thorongil in her custody.'","You defeated another of the hiding Corsairs","Search along the shoreline for any sign of hidden Corsairs","You should listen to Orgolas's story.","Rossaran is waiting to hear your report among the northern buildings of Iáphel.","What has brought Orgolas to this place? He was supposed to remain in Ost Arndír!","Gwindir, the vintner of Iáphel, sits in a widening red pool and stares at you with glassy eyes, his clothes red-stained. You ask if he is injured, and he shakes his head.\
\
'This is not blood,' he says. 'It is worse! My finest bottles were smashed beyond repair and their contents drained! I pray the King still has the bottles we gifted to him. They are irreplaceable now.'\
\
Gwindir falls silent.","'We are fortunate, my friend. Most of the villagers are unharmed, for the Corsairs set the hillside aflame as they climbed up to the village, and the folk of Iáphel did not delay; they took shelter among these buildings at the first sign of the Corsair approach. Once we have put out the fires, most of the danger should be over.\
\
'Just before you returned, I heard the dwarf Gimli shouting back in the main square. You should ensure he has all in hand; it could be more of the Corsairs hid themselves and thought to do some mischief when our backs were turned.'","King Elessar has asked you to search along the shoreline for sign of Corsairs that did not take to their boats.","Talk to the Swan-knight Rossaran in Iáphel","Corsairs have raided the grassy hills and fields of Tûm Rost, threatening the village and vineyards of Iáphel with destruction.","Found and defeated Corsairs hiding in Iáphel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","This potential hiding-place is free of hidden Corsairs","King Elessar wears a thoughtful expression as he waits for you to speak to him.","Listen to Orgolas explain what befell Thorongil","'I'm sorry! I'm sorry!' Orgolas stammers nervously, overcome with fright. 'I told Thorongil it was wrong, and we should not follow the warriors, but he said if we didn't that my father Golasgil would know his heir to be a coward! And I am no coward, ${PLAYER}, but...'","King Elessar has asked you to go with the Swan-knight Rossaran to drive the Corsairs from northern Iáphel.","You and Gimli have caught up with King Elessar by the shore, down the hill from Iáphel.","Talk to Orgolas outside his hiding-place"},
[7076]={"Help construct a barricade.","The spiders have left to regroup","Help construct the final barricades.","Defend the workers from the spiders.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, is it not? It is good you have come. Quickly now - we need assistance with these barricades. We must finish constructing them before Iphantemel learns of our plans.'","Talk to Oroniel","All is still quiet below","Thranduil has a plan to besiege Iphantemel's den in Torech Emel.","Defend the workers from the attacking spiders.","'The watch is built and safe. Come, let us return to Felegoth. I place the path to Torech Emel under the watch of my guards.'","The movement in the gorge below has quieted","The barricade is constructed","Help construct another barricade.","Help construct the final barricades (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'The spiders retreat! Has Iphantemel called them to her? I know not. The Old Mother does not wish to fight us any longer, at least for the present, it would seem.'","Help construct a barricade","Talk to Thranduil","Instancia: Reino de la Vieja Madre","Defend the workers from the spiders","Defeat the attacking spiders","Spiders approach!","You should talk to Oroniel.","Talk to Thranduil.","Help construct another barricade","More spiders approach!"},
[7077]={"Sigue a Radagast más adentro de Agamaur","Dannasen se encuentra en el campamento de los Eglain, al sur del trono de Neven, el comandante de las sombras.\
\
Antes de ser convocado por Ivar para contener a las sombras, Neven era un tumulario. Ahora que lo has derrotado, Dannasen puede que esté dispuesto a ayudarte.","Instancia: El Paso Rojo","Has viajado con Radagast hasta el pantano corrupto de Agamaur. Ayúdalo a llegar al campamento de los Eglain, al oeste.","'Neven me ordena que mantenga mi puesto y debo obedecer. Él es nuestro comandante. Estoy bajo sus órdenes, al igual que mis hombres. El honor nos une, incluso más que la maldición de Iarwain Ben-adar.\
\
'No abandonaré a mi comandante, aunque él haya cambiado mucho. No puedo desobedecer sus órdenes mientras él esté aquí. Si deseas que luchemos, debes hablar con Neven. Él se encuentra al norte.'","'Perdimos a muchos. Los tumularios, eran demasiados. El Señor Demacrado... el Señor Demacrado no puede ser derrotado.\
\
'Debemos huir... Lo siento. Habla con Elsa, mi voluntad está tan afectada que no puedo hablar más.'","'¡Apresúrate, el Señor Demacrado Ivar no está lejos, cerca de las puertas de Garth Agarwen al norte. Puede que no se muestre de inmediato, así que puede que tengamos que obligarlo a salir.\
\
'El camino por delante será difícil, pero no pierdas la esperanza. ¡Triunfaremos hoy si no perdemos el ánimo!'","'Elsa y yo luchamos lo mejor que pudimos, pero había demasiados tumularios. Habla con Elsa. Ella puede saber cómo debemos proceder contra el mal de Agamaur.'","Habla con Elsa para saber más sobre sus batallas en Agamaur.\
\
Gracias a Dannasen y sus hombres, el camino hacia el oeste en dirección a Agamaur se ha abierto, y has podido alcanzar a Elsa y Eriac.","'Debemos ir al oeste, hacia el campamento de los Eglain. Elsa y Eriac nos estarán esperando y podré atender mejor la corrupción desde allí.\
\
'El poder que continúa corrompiendo este pantano es terrible, pero puede que no tengamos que enfrentarlo solos. Las bestias me dicen que hay sombras de la especie de Emelin que habitan aquí y podrían aceptar ayudar a los Eglain. No sé por qué no permanecen con su propia especie, pero al menos no han causado daño a los Eglain.\
\
'Ahora debemos apresurarnos... los mismos árboles gritan de dolor. Debo ver qué puedo hacer para ayudarlos lo más rápido posible. Sígueme, aunque no puedo prometer ayuda, porque temo que necesitaré todas mis fuerzas para enfrentarme a Ivar Manosangrienta.'","Sigue a Radagast mientras se adentra en Agamaur.\
\
Dannasen, como animado por un nuevo aliento, ha llamado a sus hombres a luchar para abrir el camino hacia el oeste. Quizás ahora puedas alcanzar a Elsa y Eriac.","Habla con Dannasen","Habla con Radagast","'Nos han vencido. No hay forma de ocultarlo. Este Ivar controla el agua, a los tumularios y al bosque mismo. No puede ser derrotado por mi escueta fuerza, y temo que haya algo mucho más terrible en las ruinas al norte.\
\
'Sé que queda muy poco tiempo antes de que un gran mal se desate desde Garth Agarwen. Nuestra única esperanza es Radagast, solo él podrá detener a este Ivar. Por favor, ve al norte hacia la puerta de Garth Agarwen con él. Detén al Señor Demacrado Ivar.'","'¿Volvemos al campamento de los Eglain ahora?'","'Esta criatura es realmente muy poderosa, pero contra un corazón lleno de esperanza y confianza en sus aliados, tal poder no significa nada. Gracias por tu ayuda aquí, amigo mío. Hemos hecho un buen trabajo hoy. La corrupción creciente de Ivar se ha detenido, al menos por el momento.\
\
'Debo regresar ahora al campamento de los Eglain y ayudar a acabar con este mal para siempre. Hay más que deberías hacer aquí, si estás dispuesto. Pero no hablaremos de tales asuntos ahora.'","El trono de Neven se encuentra más al norte, en las ruinas.\
\
Neven tiene cierta influencia sobre el capitán de las sombras, Dannasen. Quizás si hablas con él encuentres una forma de cambiar las órdenes de Dannasen.","Las ruinas del antiguo reino de Rhudaur, deformadas por el tiempo y el contacto con un mal oscuro, se extienden ante ti. Junto a Radagast el Pardo, debes encontrar a Elsa y Eriac y ayudarlos contra el Señor Demacrado, Ivar Manosangrienta, y sus sirvientes no muertos.","'No abandonaré a mi comandante, aunque ha cambiado mucho. No puedo desobedecer sus órdenes mientras él esté aquí. Si quieres que luchemos, debes hablar con Neven. Su trono está al norte.'","El líder de las sombras reside en el campamento aparentemente abandonado de los Eglain.\
\
La derrota de Raizamarga ha abierto el camino a las ruinas del oeste, donde viven las sombras de las que Radagast te habló. Deberías hablar con Dannasen, su líder, para obtener su ayuda.","La puerta de Garth Agarwen se encuentra al norte.\
\
Elsa te ha enviado a buscar a Ivar en Garth Agarwen para poner fin a su existencia.","Habla con Radagast para ver si quiere que hagas algo más.\
\
Radagast ha expulsado al Señor Demacrado Ivar de Agamaur y ha detenido sus horribles planes... por ahora.","'Un tumulario, una criatura maligna de Angmar... ¿cómo no lo vi antes? He permanecido tanto tiempo en este pantano, maldecido por Iarwain Ben-adar para traer la salvación -- o la destrucción -- de la Doncella Roja, que habita en Garth Agarwen, bajo la influencia de los hombres demacrados.\
\
'Estuve ciego a lo que Neven se había convertido. Ahora debo redimir mi error y debemos luchar para intentar romper la maldición.'"},
[7078]={"Repe el asalto final","Speak with Edsig","Instancia: Recordando a Thrymm","The enemy attack has been broken, and Forlaw remains unscathed. However, that this many Orcs are marching on the roads of Wildermore is troubling.","The Orc army is approaching, and are coming up the road!","<rgb=#FF0000>Edsig was Defeated!</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Gárferth is defeated!</rgb>","Edsig and Gárferth are prepared to defend the city of Forlaw, or die trying. They are encouraged by Thrymm's arrival, knowing that he could probably single-handedly defeat the attacking Orcs.","The Orcs marching on Forlaw are almost defeated, but the worst is yet to come. They are spurred on by two lumbering and brutal war-trolls.","The Orcs have arrived with a rather large raiding party. This attacking force is quite possibly the largest to ever march on the city of Forlaw.","'We will go to our father right away to let him know what happened here.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Edsig and Gárferth must stay alive</rgb>","Defeat the Orcs assaulting Forlaw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cyneberg tells you of the first attack on Forlaw by the White Hand. Not long ago, while Cyneberg was in Scylfig and before Thrymm left to join her, Thrymm and the twin sons of Gárwig courageously defended Forlaw from a large Orc attack.","Return to Edsig","'That appears to be all of them! Well done, Thrymm and Gárferth. You both fought well.\
\
'Thrymm, this many Orcs marching down the roads is alarming. I can see it on your face. You look worried. \
\
'I share your concern for Cyneberg in Scylfig, and whether Scylfig is prepared. You should send word as soon as you can. Gárferth and I will see to the defence of Forlaw while you are away.'","'Thrymm! We are glad you could make it. We sent word through town calling for those who could aid in our defence, but it is early and not many heard it. \
\
'A scout came to Lornsettle, frantic to report to Gárwig and the rest of us of a good sized formation of Orcs that were marching down the road toward Forlaw. They should be here any moment now!\
\
'Gárferth and I will stay here to guard the gate. We will make sure none pass.'"},
[7079]={"Coloca la piedra superior en el túmulo de Carchammadel","Coloca la piedra superior en el túmulo de Tadan","Has venido con Calenglad a Barad Rath para recordar a los Montaraces caídos durante la fuga de Mordrambor de Tinnudir.","Los Dúnedain esperan que coloques la piedra superior en el túmulo de Tadan.","Los Dúnedain esperan que coloques la piedra superior en el túmulo de Carchammadel.","Los Dúnedain han venido a Barad Rath para llorar la pérdida de algunos de sus miembros.","'El aire es frío, y mi corazón está cargado de pena. Toda batalla trae consigo su caudal de dolor, pero más allá del velo de tristeza se alza la esperanza de la victoria.'","'Torogethir ha cumplido lo que dijo que haría, pues este es su cuervo, Ala-Veloz. Las tropas de Amarthiel están abandonando estas tierras por la Puerta de Evendim.\
\
'Debemos marcharnos de aquí, ${PLAYER}. Te agradezco por acompañar a mi gente y por tu parte en el homenaje a nuestros deudos.'","Instancia: Recuerdo","Coloca la piedra superior en el túmulo de Colhamnir","Calenglad está en la ladera cerca de Barad Rath.\
\
Los Dúnedain han venido a Barad Rath para recordar a sus caídos, y Calenglad espera caminar contigo hasta el lugar.","Los Dúnedain esperan que coloques la piedra superior en el túmulo de Colhamnir.","Escucha a Calenglad","Habla con Calenglad","Observa la construcción del túmulo","'Dejemos Barad Rath, ${PLAYER}. Espero algún día volver aquí, a los túmulos de Tadan, Carchammadel y Colhamnir, y compartir con ellos la noticia de nuestra victoria sobre Angmar y su regente traicionera.'","Toma tu lugar junto a Cuguminuial","Ala-Veloz trae un mensaje temido, aunque esperado: las tropas de Amarthiel han comenzado a cruzar la Puerta de Evendim en busca de Narchuil."},
[7080]={"'¿Has venido a liberarme? Skorgrím Duramano ha reunido un ejército de trasgos en el desfiladero de Rath Teraig, y si no lo detenemos, arrasará todas las tierras libres.\
\
No hay tiempo que perder, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Debemos derrotar al Capitán y a su tripulación si queremos escapar de Kheledûl con vida y advertir del peligro que crece en Rath Teraig.\
\
¡El capitán regresará pronto! ¡Rápido, desata mis manos! ¡Debemos escapar de aquí!'","Hablar con Avorthal","'Debemos darnos prisa, ${PLAYER}. Skorgrím ha reunido un ejército de trasgos en Rath Teraig, y aunque mi rescate debería poner fin a la amenaza de guerra entre enanos y elfos, temo que el ejército trasgo no permanecerá mucho tiempo en ese estrecho paso.\
\
'Llevemos esta advertencia fuera de Kheledûl a la luz de la mañana, ¡y que nuestras oportunidades de paz también brillen intensamente!'","Instance: Rescate a la luz de la luna","Svanr, el ex-maestro del puerto de Kheledûl, te ha traído por un camino oculto hasta las puertas de la ciudad. Ahora depende de ti <rgb=#FF0000>colarte en Kheledûl y liberar a Avorthal</rgb>.","Has defendido a Avorthal con éxito","Avorthal está en la cubierta de la \\qPiedra de Ira,\\q todavía atracada en Kheledûl.\
\
El Capitán de la \\qPiedra de Ira\\q ha sido derrotado. Deberías hablar con Avorthal y hacer tu escape.","Encontrar a Avorthal","'Debemos regresar ahora.'","Avorthal está retenido en la \\qPiedra de Ira,\\q el barco atracado en la ciudad portuaria de Kheledûl.\
\
Si no lo liberas esta noche, la \\qPiedra de Ira\\q llevará a Avorthal lejos del rescate y condenará a Ered Luin a la guerra entre enanos y elfos."},
[7082]={"Has derrotado a Muz, el cuidador de huargos","Habla con Candaith","'Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}, mejor que yo, al parecer. Los Uruk-hai y los orcos casi me vencen y mis heridas son profundas.\
\
'Pero no debes preocuparte por mí ahora. Más allá de esa puerta está el Uruk que dirige esta fuerza. Pasa por la puerta y derótalo. No podemos permitir que estos orcos se establezcan en el norte.'","En algún lugar por encima de ti, Candaith te espera para hablar contigo de nuevo.\
\
Has vencido a dos de los líderes de la tropa de guerra orca.","La expedición de los Uruk-haï yace en ruinas. Has ganado la batalla. Deberías hablar con Candaith.","Habla con Candaith en la cumbre de la Cima de los Vientos","Derrota a los sirvientes de Rigûl","Busca a los enemigos Bûb-hosh y Muz","Candaith desea hablar contigo","'Mis heridas son graves, pero me recuperaré. Vamos, volvamos a mi campamento.'","El Montaraz Candaith ha solicitado tu ayuda para eliminar la amenaza de los orcos de las Colinas de los Vientos. Candaith cree que la presencia de orcos del Sur en la cumbre de la Cima de los Vientos es un presagio de una invasión de Eriador.","Encuentra y derrota al líder Uruk-hai","Una pequeña tropa de Trasgos te ha recibido al pie de la Cima de los Vientos. Candaith te ha enviado por el camino de la izquierda, mientras él despeja el camino de la derecha, reuniéndose una vez más en la cima de la Cima de los Vientos.","Candaith te envió por una de las ramas del camino que sube a la Cima de los Vientos, mientras él tomaba la otra, en busca de los líderes de la tropa de guerra orca.","Instance: Recupera la Cima de los Vientos","Has derrotado a Olog-snaga","Derrota a Rigûl","Has encontrado al líder de la expedición de Saruman, el Uruk Rigûl. Debes vencer a Rigûl y a sus sirvientes para romper su voluntad y expulsarlos de las Colinas de los Vientos.","Has derrotado a Bûb-hosh","Has llegado al pie de la Cima de los Vientos y has descubierto que orcos del Sur han llegado a la cima. Candaith espera tu ayuda para expulsar a la tropa de guerra de las ruinas de Amon Sûl.","You have defeated Rigûl","'El camino se divide más adelante. Yo seguiré el de la derecha, tú toma el de la izquierda. Si todo va bien, nos volveremos a encontrar en la Cima de los Vientos. Espera a que me haya ido antes de continuar.\
\
'Recuerda que debemos derrotar a los líderes de esta partida de guerra si queremos desalentarlos. Usa las antorchas que encuentres para encender las hogueras que verás en el camino. Quizás atraigan la atención de los orcos cercanos.'","'Debemos darnos prisa, ${PLAYER}. Tenemos a los líderes de estos Uruk-hai acorralados como ratas en las laderas de la Cima de los Vientos. Si podemos derrotarlos, quizás logremos romper la voluntad de esta partida de guerra y hacer que huyan a sus amos del Sur. Prepárate para cualquier cosa.'","'Es hora de que te vayas.'"},
[7083]={"Habla con Candaith","Habla con Candaith en la cima de la Cima de los Vientos","En algún lugar por encima de ti, Candaith te espera para hablar contigo de nuevo.\
\
Has vencido a dos de los líderes de la tropa de guerra orca.","La expedición de los Uruk-haï yace en ruinas. Has ganado la batalla. Deberías hablar con Candaith.","Busca a los enemigos Bûb-hosh y Muz","Derrota a los sirvientes de Rigûl","Candaith desea hablar contigo","Muz, el Guardián de Huargos, derrotado","Bûb-hosh derrotado","'Debemos darnos prisa, ${PLAYER}. Tenemos a los líderes de estos Uruk-hai acorralados como ratas en las laderas de la Cima de los Vientos. Si logramos derrotarlos, aún podríamos quebrar la voluntad de esta hueste y hacer que regresen gimoteando junto a sus amos en el Sur. Prepárate para cualquier cosa.'","Rigûl derrotado","'Mis heridas son graves, pero me recuperaré. Vamos, volvamos a mi campamento.'","Derrota a Bûb-hosh","El Montaraz Candaith ha solicitado tu ayuda para eliminar la amenaza de los orcos de las Colinas de los Vientos. Candaith cree que la presencia de orcos del Sur en la cumbre de la Cima de los Vientos es un presagio de una invasión de Eriador.","Encuentra y derrota al líder Uruk-hai","'Ha llegado el momento de dejar este lugar, ${PLAYER}.'","'Lo has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}, mejor de lo que yo mismo he logrado, al parecer. Los Uruk-hai y los orcos casi me vencieron y mis heridas son graves.\
\
'Pero no debes preocuparte por mí ahora. Más allá de esa puerta se encuentra el Uruk que lidera esta fuerza. Atraviesa la puerta y derrótalo. No podemos permitir que estos orcos tengan una posición en el norte.'","Una pequeña tropa de Trasgos te ha recibido al pie de la Cima de los Vientos. Candaith te ha enviado por el camino de la izquierda, mientras él despeja el camino de la derecha, reuniéndose una vez más en la cima de la Cima de los Vientos.","Candaith te envió por una de las ramas del camino que sube a la Cima de los Vientos, mientras él tomaba la otra, en busca de los líderes de la tropa de guerra orca.","Instance: Recupera la Cima de los Vientos","Derrota a Rigûl","Has encontrado al líder de la expedición de Saruman, el Uruk Rigûl. Debes vencer a Rigûl y a sus sirvientes para romper su voluntad y expulsarlos de las Colinas de los Vientos.","Olog-snaga derrotado","Has llegado al pie de la Cima de los Vientos y has descubierto que orcos del Sur han llegado a la cima. Candaith espera tu ayuda para expulsar a la tropa de guerra de las ruinas de Amon Sûl.","'El camino se divide más adelante. Yo seguiré el de la derecha, tú toma el de la izquierda. Si todo va bien, nos volveremos a encontrar en la Cima de los Vientos. Espera a que me haya ido antes de continuar.\
\
'Recuerda que debemos derrotar a los líderes de esta partida de guerra si queremos desalentarlos. Usa las antorchas que encuentres para encender las hogueras que verás en el camino. Quizás atraigan la atención de los orcos cercanos.'","Derrota a Muz, el Guardián de Huargos"},
[7084]={"Corudan needs your help if he is to reach the chamber deep within Ashâgir where the last stockpile of Hungry Fire was hidden.","'I know of this Narghâk, this Hungry Fire, only by its evil reputation. I will carry as many of the crates as I can safely hold, ${PLAYER}, but if they should come alight I will ensure neither you nor Corudan the Elf escape the burning.\
\
'If I am to perish in a conflagration of Narghâk, so too will you. See that I do not.'","Rothog has fallen, and you have failed!","Talk to Corudan inside Ashâgir","Talk to Rothog inside Ashâgir","Corudan has devised a desperate plan, and he needs your help and the assistance of Rothog the Storm to carry it out.","Instancia: Volver a Ashâgir","'Azagath and his Thardúth masters may not know why we have returned to Ashâgir, but if they marked our passage here they will try to stop us.\
\
'We must be prepared for anything as we return to that sealed chamber, ${PLAYER}!'","Deep within Ashâgir, Rothog is ready to do his part."},
[7085]={"Una ola de temor te recorre mientras la reliquia es destruida, luego desaparece.","Has venido a Azanarukâr con Magor en busca de un artefacto dejado por Gorothúl en las profundidades.","Gwathnor derrotado","'¿Podemos irnos? No hay nada que nos retenga aquí; deberíamos regresar a los niveles superiores, donde el aire es limpio.'","'Hemos puesto fin a la creciente fuerza de Gwathnor y dispersado las formas de Grawulun que fueron atraídas por Azanarukâr, ${PLAYER}. Hemos ganado una pequeña victoria, un pequeño respiro -- sin la baliza de Gorothúl, pasará un tiempo antes de que Gwathnor y sus sirvientes puedan volver a encontrar el mundo del exterior.\
\
'Pero no durará para siempre. No poseemos los medios para destruir a estas criaturas, aunque sean espíritus menores -- están más allá de nuestra capacidad. Podemos obstaculizarlos por un tiempo, y esperar que la paz que compramos valga los peligros.\
\
'Siento que lo es.'","<rgb=#FF0000> No permitas que Gwathnor o sus aliados se acerquen a la salida </rgb>","Has encontrado la reliquia dentro de Azanarukâr, y deberías destruirla para evitar que se desarrollen más de los planes de Gorothúl.","Magor ha sido derrotado","'Aquí estamos, ${PLAYER}, donde una vez estuvimos antes: las profundidades más recónditas de Azanarukâr. He venido aquí a menudo desde que nos conocimos por primera vez, aunque mejor equipado que en esa aventura. La Dama del Bosque me ha dado una gran Piedra Élfica y muchas cosas han huido ante su luz.\
\
'Debemos ser cautelosos, ya que había Regmyl aquí antes, y los vi llevar un artefacto de gran maldad. No los veo ahora, pero seguramente no están lejos.\
\
'Procedamos, amigos, y veamos lo que nos espera en Azanarukâr.'","Habla con Magor","Defiende a Magor","Derrota a Gwathnor","Instancia: Volver a Azanarukâr","<rgb=#FF0000> Una fuerza oscura ha escapado de la caverna </rgb>","Gwathnor ha despertado y debe ser derrotado para evitar que su poder crezca. \
\
<rgb=#FF0000>No permitas que Gwathnor ni ninguno de sus esbirros se acerquen a la puerta.</rgb>","Destruye la baliza de Gorothúl","Magor espera hablar contigo en las profundidades de Azanarukâr después de tu derrota de Gwathnor y las formas de Grawulun.","En las profundidades de Azanarukâr, Magor desea luchar a tu lado en busca del artefacto que cree que Gorothúl dejó allí."},
[7086]={"'That is as many tomes as we can carry without weighing us down. There is one more place I would like to look before we leave: the Sai's bed-chamber. I believe it is in the rear of the area. Anything of higher value will likely be found there.'","You have collected as many tomes as you can carry.\
\
You should talk to Sorkamâl.","You see the bottom section of a broken statue near the royal bed","Defeat Dúrkhamos the Far-reaching","The statue you assembled exudes a fell aura.\
\
You should destroy the assembled Thardúth statue.","The stone is unnaturally cold to the touch","Defeated Dúrkhamos the Far-reaching","Destroy the Thardúth statue","You have collected the pieces of the artifact.\
\
You should assemble the artifact by placing the pieces on the bottom section.","Sorkamâl is curious to learn more about the broken artifact.\
\
You should collect the remaining artifact pieces.","You have found a strange broken statue near the Sai's bed.\
\
You should investigate the artifact piece.","'We have saved what we can. Let us be gone from this place, before some other foul sorcerer ambushes us or any other statues come to life.'","Sorkamâl would like to check one more location before you leave.\
\
You should investigate the Sai's bed-chamber.","Collected artifact pieces (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Collect artifact pieces (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You have arrived in the royal living quarters.\
\
You should talk to Sorkamâl.","Sorkamâl fears valuable tomes may be destroyed in the fighting in Emax Dûl.\
\
You should collect historical tomes in the royal living quarters.","Talk to Sorkamâl","Destroyed the Thardúth statue","Collect historical tomes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The completed artifact unleashes dark magic all around it!","Collected historical tomes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What a beautiful palace this is! It is unfortunate that such ugly cruelty has been allowed to reside inside it....\
\
'Come, we should scour this place and retrieve as many tomes as we can carry. The guards and servants are already acting strangely, perhaps because of this 'Thothril the Entangler' I keep hearing so much about. We should gather what we can and leave, and quickly.'","Instancia: Volver al Barrio Real","The palace of Emax Dûl has fallen under the control of one of the Thardúth of Damudûr, Thothril the Entangler. Many important records and tomes are still stored in this historic Nêshakari fortress. We must recover them, before they are destroyed in the fighting!","Assemble the artifact","Investigate the artifact piece","An Ordâkhai sorcerer has appeared and threatens you!\
\
You should defeat Dúrkhamos the Far-reaching.","Investigate the Sai's bed-chamber"},
[7087]={"Talk to Skalla","The Great Goblin's forces are approaching, and will soon clash with those of the hobgoblin warlord.","'What a battle! Those goblin fools did not expect a visit from a Great Eagle! Haha!\
\
'Let us return to Vegbár. I could use a hot meal and a stiff drink!'","Battle has been joined!","The battle has been won!\
\
You should talk to Langhár.","The Great Goblin's forces are approaching.\
\
You should talk to Skalla.","Witness the battle","Instancia: La venganza del Gran Trasgo","'Coming, ${PLAYER}?'","'We received word that the Great Goblin and his host are on the move and will arrive soon! Ready yourself; this may be messy.'","The Great Goblin's forces are approaching. The Warlord's host lies in wait. Battle will soon erupt. All we can do now is watch, and hope they fall upon each other's spears.","Habla con Langhár"},
[7089]={"'The foe is fallen, but at what cost? Alas for poor Baldmund!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Fríthild must survive</rgb>","Defeated the Warg-riders","<rgb=#FF0000>Fríthild was defeated</rgb>","Reeve Fríthild has chosen to take to the field against the Warg-riders at Baldmund's recommendation.","You should speak with Reeve Fríthild.","Defeat the Warg-riders","Defeat the Warg-riders terrorizing the eastern fields of the Broadacres.","Talk to Reeve Fríthild","'Come, ${PLAYER}. Let us depart from this bloody field.'","Instance: Ride Against the Goblins","DNT -- Players will not see","'Let us to arms, friends! These goblin-vermin shall feel the wrath of the Riders!'"},
[7090]={"Guto has stormed off, and he and the Elder are at odds... but the Elder has seen the threat behind the words of Saruman","Talk to Elder Riagán","Follow Guto","The Elder looks like he wishes to speak with you.\
\
You should talk to Elder Riagán.","Instancia: Reparando los males de Trum Dreng","Guto is at his encampment.\
\
You should speak with Guto.","Notify Elder Riagán that Guto brings a guest","Make sure that the servant of Isengard keeps to his peaceful intentions","Guto and the servant of Isengard are just behind you.\
\
You should observe the meeting with the Elder and make sure that nothing goes awry.","Hear Guto's proposition","'${PLAYER}, I am troubled. I understand Guto's vision... to see the Stag-clan glorious and strong once again, living in our lands of old, but I will not compromise the integrity of my people for a dream that cannot be.\
\
'That meeting with the servant of Isengard was disconcerting; I did not like the look of that man. I may have been lulled by his words, had you not expressed your immediate distrust of Isengard.\
\
'I thank you for keeping me alert during that strange discourse.'","'These are troubling times indeed....'","The Elder is in Lhan Tarren.\
\
You should notify Elder Riagán that Guto is arriving soon with the half-orc guest from Isengard.","'If I am not mistaken, it appears that these White Hand half-orcs are behind all of the Dragon-clan's attacks on Trum Dreng, and the villainous plan to uproot the Stags once and for all.\
\
'My grandfather might stand in the way of an open attack on these fiends, but it must be done. Will you stand with me, ${PLAYER}?'","Someone approaches...","You and Guto have discovered that the White Hand is behind the recent aggression by the Dragon-clan.","'Ah, you have returned! Elain was just telling me of your many victories in our lands.'\
\
The Elder listens with concern as you tell him quickly of what transpired between Guto and the half-orc emissary of Isengard.\
\
'You do not trust this man, ${PLAYER}. You have had dealings with this White Hand before now, have you? And this emissary comes here to treat with me... how interesting.'","The Elder notes your mistrust of the soldiers of Isengard"},
[7091]={"Clear the path of wights","Leave Lhan Gogledh as the Huntsman commanded.","Clear a path through the wights for Lhucu.","'It appears that my father has fallen completely under the sway of Mostun and has driven all of our people from the village. Look! He is protected by the abominations that walk the cairns!\
\
'Go, ${PLAYER}, and clear a path so that I might confront my father.'","The path is now clear","You have accompanied Lhucu to the village of Lhan Gogledh to confront her father, Trehéarn Brenin.","Talk to Lhucu","Defeat Mostun","Talk to Lhucu.","Let Lhucu know that the path has been cleared below.","Banish the fell spirit Mostun from the mortal world.","'It is time, then, that I confront my father and make him atone for his deeds. Thank you for all of your help, ${PLAYER}.'","Speak with Lhucu.","Defeated Trehéarn Brenin","Confront and defeat Trehéarn Brenin.","Instance: Rise and Fall","'The Wild Huntsman is revered by all of the clans, for he rules over the gwirod. His judgement is final and exacting.\
\
'We should leave this place immediately.'","Withdraw through the main gate","Defeat Trehéarn Brenin","Defeated Mostun"},
[7092]={"Cadelhin's tale has finished","Seek out the tomb of Cadelhin within the barrow and place the amulet thereon.","Talk to Cadelhin","Place the amulet on Cadelhin's tomb","'Following my father's betrayal, I led a group of friends away from my home, as none of my followers could believe what my father and his men had done.\
\
'We saw no other way to avenge this foul deed but to stand against them. Unfortunately, after some time we were defeated, and I was laid in this barrow and held here, never to be free. I will need to gather strength before I can assist you further.\
\
'What? Wait... to arms! The shades of my father's men seek to destroy me and recover the amulet. Please, defend me as I muster my strength.'","You have defended Cadelhin","Protect Cadelhin from the shades that seek to do him harm.","Listen to Cadelhin's tale.","'I am grateful to you for your assistance. Weakened am I and weary of this curse. My people suffer from this curse because of my father, but I am not wholly without blame.\
\
'I was a very capable hunter, and sought out the Rhi Helvarch, a powerful spirit near here, to bless my betrothal. Upon completing an arduous challenge, the Rhi Helvarch blessed the amulet that you recently recovered. The marriage was not to last, however, for my father murdered my wife and sundered the amulet. My belief is that when my father slew my wife and broke the amulet that I had given to her, the curse unfolded upon us. Such an act of betrayal is what brought this down upon us.\
\
'Please go, so that I might regain my strength and summon those that would aid me. I will send word to the man that led you to this place when it is time to return.'","Instance:  Rise of the Fallen Son","Lhudd has asked you to explore the ancient barrow in an attempt to discover more about the shades that dwell still in the Lich Bluffs. He believes that the shade of Cadelhin may know how to break the curse that binds them.","Listen to Cadelhin's tale"},
[7093]={"Defend the herald of the Rohirrim from his ambushers.","Hold out until reinforcements arrive.","'You are correct... I hear the baying of the Dunlending hounds approaching even now.\
\
'It seems we were fools to trust these wild men to parley fairly, but so be it... let us show them the quality of our valour!'","The herald has fallen silent, his breath coming in a few last ragged gasps as his life fades.","Blow the Horn of the Rohirrim","Defeat the Dunlending attackers","Instance: Rohirrim Herald","Talk to the Rohirrim herald","'You are a fine ${RACE} to stand by me in my final hour.\
\
'Take my horn to the Ford and let Grimbold know that I have fallen. Tell him I am sorry....'\
\
The herald's voice trails off into laboured breathing as he closes his eyes in pain and exhaustion.\
\
He does not speak again.","The Rohirrim have come to your aid","With the battle over, the herald you strove to protect lies dying. You speak to him, hoping to bring his final words to his allies at the Ford of Isen.","Overwhelming numbers of wild men are approaching. Summon the Rohirrim to your aid.","Having quickly moved to rescue a herald of the Rohirrim from a Dunlending ambush, you have arrived only in time to desperately fend off the attackers.","You blow the Horn of the Rohirrim"},
[7094]={"Marigold ha sugerido espiar a las criaturas arboréas.\
\
Si una de ellas se marcha, quizá sea posible detener juntas a las otras dos.","'Parece que están hablando de algo importante. No podemos luchar contra los tres a la vez, pero si solo uno se marcha, seguro que podemos detener a los otros dos.\
\
'Por ahora, deberíamos escuchar su conversación. Quizá nos ayude a entender qué está ocurriendo.'","En busca de las extrañas criaturas arboréas que vio, Marigold te ha llevado a lo más profundo del Bosque Viejo.","Marigold ha desafiado a las criaturas arboréas.","Debes proteger a Marigold mientras te guía a través del bosque.","'No pensé que tendríamos tanta suerte al llegar hasta aquí sin ser atacados por los animales del bosque.\
\
'El lugar donde vi a esas criaturas arboréas no está lejos de aquí. No te preocupes: conozco el Bosque Viejo como la palma de mi mano.'","'¡Vámonos antes de que aparezca otro fantasma!'","Espía a las criaturas arboréas","Habla con Marigold","Las criaturas arboréas han sido derrotadas.","'¡Vaya, este día no deja de volverse más extraño! Si los fantasmas están siendo atraídos al bosque por una espada, tenemos que encontrarla. Los Guardianes ya están preocupados por los animales del bosque; ¡no necesitamos añadir a eso los espíritus de las Quebradas de los Túmulos!\
\
'Al menos conozco a alguien que podría ayudarnos. ¡Te llevaré a verlo enseguida!'","Defiende a Marigold","Instancia: Raíz y podredumbre","Marigold ha encontrado a las criaturas arboréas.\
\
Deberías hablar con ella y elaborar un plan.","Marigold está esperando a que la alcances antes de internarse más en el Bosque Viejo.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Marigold ha sido derrotada!</rgb>"},
[7095]={"Rothog has summoned you to his chambers as he confronts Zarzíra Dawn-star about her misdeeds.","Talk to Rothog the Storm","Instancia: La furia de Rothog","Speak to Rothog","'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER}. With Zarzíra defeated and Shaidal well on his way to freedom, things seem to have worked out. Now please go, my people have some cleaning up to do.'","'Now you will see a matter of justice. While I am very confident about how this will go, do be wary, as this serpent seems to be willing to strike.'","Defeat Zarzíra and her men","Rothog has summoned you to his chambers to confront Zarzíra Dawn-star about her misdeeds.","Defeat Zarzíra and her men as they attack you in the audience chamber.","Speak to Rothog the Storm about Zarzíra's treachery.","With Zarzíra vanquished, Rothog beckons to you","'Zarzíra made a grave mistake so openly attacking you in my presence. I am overjoyed by your victory. You see, Zarzíra and her men were not worth me bloodying my blades, as they are so below me. But I commend you for your quick action.\
\
'Rest assured, if Shaidal is successful in the task that I laid out before him, he will go free.\
\
'Thank you again for helping solve what could have been a rather complicated situation!'"},
[7097]={"Talk to Gori on the bridge","Talk to Gori","Talk to Gori by the plaque","'My ancestor was close with Fundin’s widow, Vigdis. She wrote that the queen’s beard turned white when news of the king’s death reached her. Perhaps it was from grief, perhaps it was from having to take over the duties of ruling until their son, Kalin VI the Young, came of age in 501.'","'Creo que podría pasar décadas maravillándome con los detalles de este lugar. Pero vamos, volvamos a Amdân antes de que vengan más enemigos a buscar a sus amigos.'","Gori has paused to speak with you before the next set of stairs.","Gori Stonesetter needs protection so that he might see for himself the ruins of the ancient buildings and bridges his ancestors helped build.","'Fundin's Steps. My ancestor spent much time working on this staircase. She wrote that she worked under the great stoneworker, King Fundin II. Landslides left the already ancient paths to Atrad-zarakh too perilous to safely traverse. They carved the stairs from the very bedrock itself!'","Gori continues his way through the ruins, too distracted to notice any imminent danger.","Gori is catching his breath after the battle and motions you over to talk with him.","'See those pillars there? An ancestor of mine built them ages past! She left detailed journals of her time here. Sadly, the pages of the journal are as crumbled as the ruins, but I hope to learn more here. The stone of this valley has stood for many thousands of years.'","Instancia: Ruinas de los Ancestros","'Khur Azan - the Dim-crossing. Built over two thousand years ago, and now here we are! A testament to our mastery over the valley. Look at these arches, and the detailing. Our ancestors were comfortable enough and had time enough to build grandly. This is no simple bridge over the Kibil-nâla, but a grand testament to the power and abilities of the builders.'","Gori waits for you by the side of the River Kibil-nâla."},
[7098]={"Attempt to stand against Voskor and his force","'I... I think there's no rescue for me, stranger....\
\
'The Uruk... he is too strong. Leave me....'","'Come, let us flee into the cave and leave such violence to the likes of them! Are you ready to follow us?'","The Orc roadway can be found to the west of the cave Húna discovered.\
\
Húna has reunited with Bebbe, but during their conversation the frantic screams of one of their fellows nearby has filled them with grave concern.","The Orc roadway stretches through much of Balewood.\
\
Sensing that the refugees may be nearby, you decide to search the barren roadway for any sign of Byre Tor refugees before more Orcs return.","Leodwald can be found laying on the roadway in Balewood.\
\
You should speak to Leodwald about his condition before confronting the Uruk captain a second time.","Húna has been slain!","A frantic yell coming from the Orc roadway pierces the air","A surly Uruk captain standing over a wounded refugee sees you approach","The cave can be found to the east of the Orc roadway.\
\
The Uruk captain has been brutally defeated by a raging Huorn. You should flee for safety while the Huorn pursues the wounded Uruk into the woods.","Search the roadway for sign of Byre Tor refugees","Húna is on the roadway in Balewood.\
\
The snarls of Orcs in the distance have cut short Húna's heroics, and you should speak to him to discern what action is to be taken.","'Thank you for your aid, friend....'\
\
Húna struggles to catch his breath.\
\
'My fellows and I became separated when the wood-trolls attacked us... I feel a coward for abandoning them so, but we are defenceless... I know not what fates have befallen them by now.\
\
'You look like a hearty ${CLASS}. Will you aid me in my search for them?'","'If these are truly the forces we are to contend with in this forest, I hold not much hope for our escape....\
\
'Nevertheless... thank you for your aid, friend. We would have succumbed to the cold, even if those monsters had not found us.\
\
'I mean you no ill-will, but such terrors are likely even beyond your skill, friend. You are welcome to stay with us until it is again safe to leave the cave.\
\
'Come, let us warm ourselves and rest inside.'","You summon the courage to stand as the vicious Huorn beats back the Uruk captain","You are frozen in fear as the ground trembles - you must wait to see what unfolds.","The snarls of Orcs can be heard faintly in the distance...","The man's attackers can be found on the roadway.\
\
You have discovered a man of Byre Tor fleeing from vicious wood-trolls of Balewood.","Húna can be found outside the cave to the east of the roadway in Balewood.\
\
You have escaped certain defeat from a powerful Uruk captain and a vicious Huorn, and should now seek shelter with the other refugees in the nearby cave.","Húna can be found along the Orc roadway in Balewood.\
\
Having saved the man from certain doom, you should now speak to him to learn of his plight and the fates of the other refugees.","Talk to Húna","Húna is travelling along the Orc roadway in Balewood.\
\
You should aid Húna in seeking out his fellows in Balewood.","'Let us away, ${PLAYER}... I fear no good will come of us staying on this road. We should take refuge among the trees here, and perhaps then we shall find my fellows....'","Léodwald has been slain!","The ground trembles as Voskor begins to speak","In the dark of Balewood, you have discovered a snow-covered pack, a sign that the refugees of Byre Tor may yet live.","Instancia: Corriendo hacia la nada","Follow Húna and Bebbe to the Orc roadway","Follow Húna deeper into Balewood","Approach the Uruk captain, Voskor","You have escaped Rottenheart and the Orcs!","The Orc attackers can be found on the roadway in Balewood.\
\
In response to your defiance, the Uruk captain has set his Orcs upon you. They must be defeated if the refugees are to escape the forest alive.","A muffled yell pierces the snowfall as a refugee runs into view","<rgb=#FF0000>The refugees of Byre Tor must survive</rgb>","Talk to Leodwald and confront Voskor","Húna is running north-east of the roadway in Balewood.\
\
Húna believes that his fellows might be found off the side of the road in Balewood. You should continue to follow and protect him.","Defeated the refugee's attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bébba has been slain!","The Uruk smirks before gesturing to you, Bébba, and Húna","The Uruk captain can be found along the roadway in Balewood.\
\
Húna's fellow, Leodwald, has been wounded and captured by a vile Uruk captain of Isengard. You should confront the Uruk before any more harm can come to the Rohirrim.","Talk to Húna and flee into the cave","Defeat the refugee's attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat the attacking Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Flee to the cave with the Byre Tor refugees","Defeated the attacking Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7099]={"Your joyous bellow echoes through the valley!","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso.","'I have heard from Skarding of your deeds in Misthallow. You have my thanks.\
\
'Now, let us celebrate!'","Talk to Runerik.","Approach the gathering in the woods.","<rgb=#FF0000>Roar</rgb> to the wilds!","Instancia: Corriendo salvajemente","Run wild!","Approach the gathering in the woods","A celebration is in order after the fall of Lumrog and Gúrbarash's cowardly flight.","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso","Talk to Runerik"},
[7100]={"Move further into Kûr Anzar","Move to meet Numûru and Razâl outside the Angar Aragín, the tower of Kûr Anzar at the top of the city.","Speak with Numûru","Instancia: Saboteando a Kûr Anzar","Move closer to speak with Numûru and Razâl.","Sacos de grano recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Barricades set on fire (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Listen to Numûru","Listen to Numûru and Razâl's conversation","Destroyed weapon racks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Move further into Kûr Anzar.","Set fire to the barricades near the tower","Speak with Razâl outside Kûr Anzar.","Meet Numûru and Razâl outside the tower of Kûr Anzar","Sabotage the Barkhûshim forces in Kûr Anzar by taking grain sacks, destroying weapon stands and defeating Barkhûshim sentries.","Assist Razâl and Numûru on a mission into Kûr Anzar to weaken the Barkhûshim.","Recoge sacos de grano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Barkhûshim sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroy racks of weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Numûru outside Kûr Anzar.","Listen to Numûru near Angar Aragín.","Listen to Numûru and Razâl's conversation.","'I almost feel bad for the Barkhûshim, now that I've got Numûru a bit stirred up.\
\
'I will also soften your resistance. My sword arm may be slow but it helps when the enemy doesn't see it coming. You should move through the city, taking back their ill-gotten grain stores and destroying their weapons as the opportunity arises. Make sure to defeat their sentries, lest they call out our presence here. \
\
'We will meet again at the top of Kur Anzar, near the Angar Aragín.'","Defeat Barkhûshim sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Move closer to speak with Numûru and Razâl","'No! They've taken him!'","Speak with Razâl","'I will move ahead and clear our path.'","Set fire to the barricades near the tower.","Speak with Razâl near Angar Aragín, the tower of Kûr Anzar."},
[7101]={"The second stone is yours!","'The time has come to prove yourself worthy. Speak the words in the King's chosen language.'","Unlock the door","The time has come to speak the password to the Emissary.","The Emissary roars with delight!","The door is open!\
\
You should retrieve the second stone!","'You are a worthy servant of the Master. Go, and complete your mission.'","Speak the Words","The Emissary has asked you to speak the pass code in \\qthe King's chosen language\\q.\
\
You should speak the words to the Emissary.","Take the second stone","Talk to the Emissary","You have the key!\
\
You should unlock the door and retrieve the second stone!","'You are worthy! Take this. By your own hands the door may be unlocked. Reunite the stones. All will serve the Master!'\
\
He reaches into the gaping maw that comprises most of his body, produces an ancient key, and hands it to you.","Instance: Say the Words","You should talk to the Emissary in the Mountains of Shadow Chamber."},
[7102]={"'${PLAYER}!\
\
'Dori, Glóin, and Bofur have travelled deeper into the rift on foot. It grows narrower and more treacherous ahead, and so, I offered to tend to the goats.\
\
'Of course, that was not the only reason Dréri and I have remained behind! We Stout-axes are hardy dwarves, but we are not accustomed to such cold weather. Ah, but I think these Longbeards would not feel so at home on the plains of Dor Amarth!\
\
'In truth, I feel a sense of dread in the shadows of the Grey Mountains. It is nothing more than a feeling, I think, but there is something about this place that has left me uneasy.\
\
'It has been some time. You should go ahead and see what is keeping the others.'","'Listen to me, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Dori's voice drops to a whisper.\
\
'Do not think I chose my words to make a fool of myself. This Prince seems wiser than his kinsfolk, but I do not trust these Zhélruka.\
\
'If they make for Dómekh then they make for Thikil-gundu, and the Zhélruka do not share the spoils of delving and war. If Ingór was to learn that our path also leads to the Steel Keep, I do not think we would find him so friendly much longer.\
\
'I believe the only way this can be settled without the spilling of dwarf-blood is to accept Ingór's offer of passage to Skarháld.'","Shards of ice litter the ground, betraying a final, futile struggle by Vethúg Wintermind...","Talk to Dori in the Bitter Scar","Dori can be found in the Bitter Scar.\
\
You have discovered concerning evidence that Karazgar may have slain or taken Vethúg Wintermind from the Bitter Scar. You should leave at once with Dori and Company.","After learning that Vethúg Wintermind fell upon the foothills of Winterstith, Dori and Company have decided to seek the fallen cold-drake and discover some final proof of his demise.","'I do not like the look of this....\
\
'Either we have been deceived by the Zhélruka or Vethúg was not as wounded as he appeared to be! There is no mistaking that Vethúg tore this rift in the foothills of Winterstith, but it is where he has gone that concerns me!\
\
'Do you see these marks in the earth? I first thought nothing of them, but there are signs of battle here among the fallen stones of Winterstith! Unless the great cold-drake battled only against rocks and ice as they fell, some other foe must have come to this place. I know few who could withstand the might of Vethúg Wintermind, and so, I fear this is the work of Karazgar!\
\
'Perhaps you can uncover the truth of what has happened here, ${PLAYER}.'","Examine the signs of battle in the Bitter Scar","Dori, Glóin, and Bofur stand huddled near the end of the Bitter Scar...","Dori can be found in the Bitter Scar.\
\
You have travelled to the end of the Bitter Scar and rejoined Dori and Company, but there is no sign of the remains of Vethúg Wintermind.","Signs of battle can be found at the end of the Bitter Scar.\
\
You have come upon the aftermath of a struggle between Vethúg Wintermind and an unknown foe. You should examine the signs of battle to determine what has happened.","Ingór crosses his arms and waits for Dori's response...","'Rust... and rime. It is as I feared, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Was Vethúg slain by Karazgar's hand or did the Weeping Warrior find some crueler purpose for the great cold-drake?'\
\
Dori glances at the damaged remains of the bloodied, black arrow.\
\
'If Vethúg Wintermind lives still, he will not have forgotten the hurts done to him by the Longbeards and Bardings....\
\
'We must go.'","Dori can be found in the Bitter Scar.\
\
You have discovered that a great struggle occurred between Karazgar and Vethúg Wintermind, and it seems Karazgar was the victor. You should speak to Dori at once.","Witness the meeting of the companies of Dori and Ingór","Dori can be found in the Bitter Scar.\
\
Ingór has revealed himself to be a Prince of the Zhélruka, and he has offered Dori and Company safe passage to Skarháld. You should speak to Dori and see if he wishes to accept.","Only Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, could have left this behind...","Instancia: Cicatrices de batalla","Ingór, son of Vékun, has come to the Bitter Scar with a company of his own and appears eager to speak to Dori and Company.\
\
You should remain on guard and defend Dori and Company if the need arises.","Náth can be found at the Bitter Scar.\
\
You have travelled to the end of the Bitter Scar with Dori and Company, you now prepare to search for the remains of Vethúg Wintermind. You should speak to Náth.","A company of Zhélruka blocks the way!","Dori, Bofur, and Glóin have ventured into the Bitter Scar.\
\
You should follow Dori, Bofur, and Glóin into the Bitter Scar.","You are able to free a bloodied, black arrow from the frozen earth...","Talk to Dori","Deliver the black arrow to Dori","'Let us follow these Zhélruka to Skarháld, ${PLAYER}, but speak not of our true purpose.'","Find Dori, Glóin, and Bofur in the Bitter Scar","Talk to Náth","Leave the Bitter Scar with Dori and Company"},
[7104]={"Talk to Fróthi.","The lore-master Fróthi wishes to examine what remains of the dragon-tooth necklace.","The vision fades and you realize your finger has come away from the dragon tooth","'A vision you say? Well, what did you see?'\
\
You tell the dwarf what you saw, as best you can.\
\
'Poisoned? Unending pain? One could almost pity the creature... almost. He must hate dragons with nearly as much passion as Durin's Folk!'","Experience the vision","Instancia: El Legado de Scatha","Talk to Fróthi","A vision comes over you, unbidden","Experience the vision.","Examine Scatha's tooth","Examine Scatha's tooth with Fróthi.","'Now, let us return this tooth to Górsim. We dwarves do not take kindly to stolen or lost treasures! If Górsim lost this last tooth... well, let us not ponder on that!'"},
[7105]={"The hobbits are upon Treebeard's Hill.","Gandalf is at Treebeard's Hill in Fangorn.","The hobbits appear to have made a new friend","'I trust you with this great deed, ${PLAYER}. I do not know for certain if your efforts will end in change, but I have hope.\
\
'Just talk to the Ents you find. Learn of their memories and help them piece together the riddles that occupy their slow minds.'","Observe the fate of the two hobbits","Gandalf believes you have the power to stir the sleeping shepherds of Fangorn","Gandalf wishes to speak with you atop Treebeard's Hill.","'I think I have told you enough, without telling you too much. Let us return to the present.'","Habla con Gandalf","Listen to Gandalf","'Let me share some of my knowledge with you, ${PLAYER}, for I believe that you came to this place tracking two old friends. They are friends to me also, and I know what became of them.\
\
'Believe it or not, this has a great deal to do with you.'","Instancia: Amigos dispersos","'The hobbits are safe with Treebeard, but do you see what I see? The Ents have never seen hobbits before. Even the sleeping Ent you passed was interested in them.'","Gandalf is on Treebeard's Hill.","Gandalf wishes to speak with you."},
[7107]={"Defend Erebor from Vethúg Wintermind and his brood","King Thorin III Stonehelm can be found before the gates of Erebor.\
\
Vethúg Wintermind makes for Erebor, and King Thorin III Stonehelm has readied an army of dwarves and Elves to oppose him. You should speak to King Thorin when you are prepared to defend Erebor.","Struggle against the cold!","Defeat Vethúg Wintermind","Vethúg Wintermind has descended from the sky.\
\
Vethúg Wintermind is attacking Erebor. You should attempt to defeat him.","'We have prevailed... and that... is enough.'","<rgb=#FF0000>King Thorin III Stonehelm must not be defeated</rgb>","'${PLAYER}...\
\
'When first we tried to reclaim Thikil-gundu, we were overproud and greedy -- even by the measures of Durin's Folk! It mattered not to us if the Dragons had been sealed within the Anvil of Winterstith or if they had merely returned to the Withered Heath. Vethúg had long lain in wait within Thikil-gundu for the return of the Longbeards, and my folk did not know that when they closed the gates behind them, they wrought their own tombs. \
\
'King Dáin I was taken by surprise, and before he could raise his axe, Vethúg breathed a fell frost upon him. The ice encased him, and a swift gust of Vethúg's wings toppled and shattered our proud King.  Frór sacrificed himself to save the few of us who remained, that we might flee the gates of Thikil-gundu, but Vethúg had won his victory before the battle had even begun. We entered the Steel Keep in celebration... and we left it a broken people.\
\
'This time, Vethúg will not take us by surprise. Let us join the defenders of Erebor below!'","Talk to King Thorin III Stonehelm","After spending countless years within Thikil-gundu, Vethúg Wintermind comes to wreak vengeance upon Durin's Folk.","Vethúg breathes frost upon you, and ice begins to encase you!","With a crash, Vethúg Wintermind lands before the gates of Erebor!","Follow King Thorin III Stonehelm","You should follow King Thorin III Stonehelm and remain alert at the gates of Erebor.","The cold has taken you.","'We of Durin's Folk are honoured to have you at our side, ${PLAYER}. Many a dwarf-axe has been sharpened, the Elves have nocked their arrows, and our barricades have been assembled. There will be no rousing speeches or well-intentioned pleasantries before this battle, my friend. Vethúg is a great cold-drake, and it shall take our combined might, mettle, and a fair share of good fortune to overcome him.\
\
'Despite my misgivings, one of my scouts insisted upon remaining in the field. He is a brave dwarf, for he knows that he may be the first to be espied from above by Vethúg.\
\
'Remain alert, ${PLAYER}. My scout shall soon return....'","King Thorin III Stonehelm can be found before the gates of Erebor.\
\
You were incapacitated during the battle against Vethúg Wintermind, but have awoken to find King Thorin III Stonehelm standing triumphantly above you.","King Thorin III pauses and beckons for you to come closer","<rgb=#FF0000>The King under the Mountain has been defeated!</rgb>","'You fought well... my friend. We feared we had lost you in the fighting, but you have... survived.\
\
'The fighting continued for some time, and many more were lost in the battle. When all hope was thought lost, a company arrived from Dale and the young King loosed one of the remaining Black Arrows of old at Vethúg Wintermind. It did not end him, but it pierced his wing and unsteadied him. Before a final blow could be struck, he took flight once more and fled Erebor in fear.\
\
'Our foe is beaten... the day is won. There will be time enough to rest, recover, and grieve soon....'","King Thorin III Stonehelm is making ready to defend Erebor.\
\
King Thorin III Stonehelm has spoken to the forces arrayed in defence of Erebor. You should now speak to King Thorin III Stonehelm.","Instancia: Vástago del Invierno","By some miracle you have survived, but what has happened?","Vethúg Wintermind's brood has descended upon Erebor.\
\
Vethúg Wintermind has come to Erebor. You should aid the dwarves of Erebor in defending against the attacks of Vethúg's brood."},
[7108]={"Talk to Girhâzi","Instance: Searching for Hope","Khûldim Umûn has led you into a salt mine where he claims the Dubarâkh is hidden. You should follow Girhâzi and Khûldim.","'Well this is it, ${PLAYER}. Hopefully, this pashâg is telling the truth, though I doubt it. We have no other clues to go on, so we must hold on to hope.\
\
'I do not like the idea of being trapped here with no escape. I will leave the Dumûri here to secure our exit. We can handle the Usan-kûni we will likely encounter in these caves.'","Accompany Girhâzi and Khûldim","Listen to the conversation","Attackers defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'That was unexpected, to say the least! Have you been hurt?\
\
'We should leave here before more arrive. I do not know how many members this cult may have, and we are only two. Perhaps we can return later with more warriors to oust these cultists. For now, let us return to Iridír.'","Khûldim Umûn has informed Girhâzi that the Dubarâkh is inside an abandoned salt mine. You have been invited to join them as they search the caves for the lost library of Ambarûli culture and history.","Defeated attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Girhâzi must survive","Defend yourself from the attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Khûldim Umûn has led you into a salt mine where he claims the Dubarâkh is hidden. You should talk to Girhâzi."},
[7109]={"Belondor places his hand on the ground where his crew fell, silent tears falling onto the stone floor.\
\
'I blamed myself, ${PLAYER}, for being a fool. They trusted me with their lives and I failed them. I still hold myself responsible for my poor decisions, but I am not the one who killed them, and my hatred should be directed at Azagath and not myself.\
\
'I knew him for many years. I thought him to be my friend. Men of a common purpose and a similar mind. What evil lurks inside him, I wonder, to give him the power to rip souls from bodies and command spirits like his puppets? And how did I not see it before?'","Defeated Ghâbekhid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Within Mâkhda Khorbo, Belondor has noticed that the gate previously blocking access to the stairs is now open. You should go up the stairs.","You have searched Mâkhda Khorbo and found the remains of a map, torn in half. You should talk to Belondor.","Talk to Belondor","'Prepare yourself for a fight ${PLAYER}. There are enemies ahead. They will not stay our search.'","You have failed to protect Belondor","At the end of a hallway in Mâkhda Khorbo you and Belondor have found a tapestry on the wall that is a map. You should examine the map.","This large map is an old and tattered tapestry. The right half of it has been cut and torn from what remains; and recently, by the looks of it. The lettering on it is written in a language with which you are unfamiliar.","You have arrived at the Iron Stairwell in Mâkhda Khorbo, where you and Belondor faced each other as enemies, and where his crew was slain by Azagath's dark magic. You should talk to Belondor.","'I cannot read the script on this map, but I recognize it all the same. This is a map showing the Shield Isles and Cape of Umbar. The eastern half of the map has been taken. Surely if they are travelling overland, their journey is to the east.\
\
'Maps themselves are not rare. Something must have been marked on that side of the map that they are trying to find. Considering the previous owners of the map, this indeed bodes ill.'","Examine the map","Defeat Ghâbekhid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You are in an area of Mâkhda Khorbo that Belondor says he saw Azagath and Nakási enter. You should search the area for signs of why they may have come here.","Belondor must survive","Belondor stops for a moment and looks around. He mutters something to himself, and you can see on his face that something just occurred to him.","'I think we have found what we came for. Let us leave this hateful place.'","Ascend the Iron Stairwell","You have followed Belondor into an upstairs area. You should talk to Belondor.","'When last we were in this room together, we faced each other as enemies. How is it that it feels like an eternity ago, but also like it was just yesterday? I have been trying to push all of this from my mind, ${PLAYER}. It seemed like the only way I would be able to go on.\
\
'But I see now that closing off my heart does them an injustice. They were family to me, ${PLAYER}, and I miss them with all of my heart. But is that not the danger any time you choose to love? I don't think I care much for the alternative.'","Instancia: Buscando en las profundidades","Belondor has asked you to accompany him as he returns to Mâkhda Khorbo in search of clues that may explain why Azagath and Nakási went there, as well as where they are going.","You spot something at the end of this hall","You have found a map","Examine the item","As you enter this upstairs area, you discover that it is infested with bats. You should defeat bats.","You and Belondor have spotted something at the end of this hallway. You should investigate what it is.","Continue searching the area","You have arrived at the Iron Stairway in Mâkhda Khorbo, where you and Belondor faced each other as enemies, and where his crew was slain by Azagath's dark magic. You should talk to Belondor."},
[7110]={"Gimli is not sure what to make of Lheu Brenin.","Gimli must not be defeated","The child of the Westfold has tried to get your attention.","Lheu Brenin has been defeated, and the people who shelter in the Glittering Caves are now safe from the Falcon Clan.","Survive the assault of the Falcon Clan warriors","Defeat Lheu Brenin","Lheu Brenin is ready to fight, and has no fear of you or Gimli.","Talk to the Rohirrim child","Lheu Brenin, leader of the Falcon Clan, has finally paid for his crimes","Learn what evil has entered the Glittering Caves","'The natural beauty of this place takes my breath away, ${PLAYER}, but we have an important errand here and cannot stop with our mouths agape. Let us proceed and ensure that nothing lurks here to threaten the folk that shelter in the caves.'","Lheu Brenin has vast reserves of strength, and wishes to see you dead. You have to weaken him through battle!","'No one threatens my land, my king, or my family, ${RACE}! Any villains who do had better run back to their Wizard masters!'","Instancia: Caminos Secretos","Talk to Lheu Brenin","'Who is this blustery man, ${PLAYER}? He is no friend of yours, and that makes him no friend of mine. I do not like his words or his tone. Let us teach him not to ally with Wizards who cannot tell the difference between evil and good!'","Lheu Brenin has come to the end of his strength, and has paid for his crimes.","Some villainy has come to the Glittering Caves of Aglarond.","Lheu Brenin and other members of the Falcon Clan have come to the Glittering Caves.","'We come once more face to face, ${PLAYER}, and once more you find yourself overmatched. Before you stand the finest of my warriors, and I the strongest of them all. None know the high mountainous paths and deep tunnels as well as the Hebog-lûth, and we have put that knowledge to good use.\
\
'I have been promised a king's reward by my ally Saruman for the death of Rohan's people, and you will not stop me. I know its women and children shelter in the caves behind you, and my force of loyal Falcons will kill any they find. You think to stop me with such allies as I see before me? A single dwarf and one child?'","Gimli has fallen!","You have encountered a small child in the Glittering Caves.","'This man is less than a worm, ${PLAYER}! He is no man at all, but a thrall of Saruman's, thinking only of his reward and caring nothing for anyone: not for the people of his tribe with whom he should have a bond, nor for my people, who have done him no wrong.\
\
'I will not let him threaten my family or my king!'","Talk to Gimli in the Glittering Caves","The small girl waves off your inquiry, dismissing your questions with a toss of her hair.\
\
'There is no time to talk! My mother is with the other folk of Westfold, hiding in the cave, but I heard something back here and came to see what it was. Do you know what I found?'\
\
She looks around quickly, and then says in a hushed whisper, 'Villains! Villains from Dunland!'","Weaken Lheu Brenin","Lheu Brenin has commanded his warriors to kill everyone in the Glittering Caves.","Gimli is in the Glittering Caves, ready to proceed further into Aglarond.","'You can do it, ${PLAYER}! I know that you can defeat this villain! Stand strong for Rohan, and for Théoden King!'\
\
The girl knows nothing of Lheu Brenin's treachery in Dunland, but her belief in you, combined with the Falcon Clan's crimes, results in the restoration of your morale.","'Let us return to the folk who shelter in the Glittering Caves, ${PLAYER}. We will make sure this child reaches them safely... or perhaps she will ensure we make it safely!'","The child of the Westfold has excitedly asked for you to speak to her.","You have come with Gimli deeper into the Glittering Caves to make certain the folk who shelter here will be safe.","Talk to the child of the Westfold","'I should never have let you leave Tâl Methedras alive. Now I will remedy that mistake!'","Lheu Brenin's breath is coming now in fits and gasps, but still he remains strong and defiant.\
\
'How many of your friends have I slain, ${PLAYER}? I will not stop now. I will continue until none remain, and Saruman will pay me a sum worthy of a dragon's hoard for the favour!'","Habla con Gimli","'Even the children of Rohan fight against their enemies, when pressed! It fills my heart with pride to see it, for a child under the Mountain would do the same. I am impressed!\
\
'Already I engage in competition with Legolas. Need I now wager with this child, as well? Ha!'"},
[7112]={"Talk to Rahâzi","You have come with Rahâzi, Corudan, and Sigileth to the fortress above Jirush with the hope that you will be able to find Balakhâd and free him from Ordâkhai captivity.","You escape from the fortress and look for your companions","'I have spent weeks hunting agents of the Heirsworn who seek to claim the bounties placed upon the Kindred of the Coins by the widow Saklaphêl. Agents such as you, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
You deny that you are in Saklaphêl's employ. Tatháta eyes you closely.","Leave the fortress by the main gate before you are discovered by the Ordâkhai","Listen to what Tatháta has to say","Tatháta watches you carefully","Your part of the plan requires you to sneak inside the fortress turn to the right to search for the prisoner.","'You have had ample time to act upon the widow's orders, if you sought her bounty upon us. Have I not espied you from afar in the company of Kinsman Belondor, his back turned to you at length and without fear? And when I decided on that moonlit night mere days ago to put an end to both these questions and your life, was it not the arrival of Khôltekh and Rothog that stayed my attack? I am not often surprised, ${PLAYER}, but on that night your friendship with my allies was a startlement to me. No servant of Saklaphêl could deceive such as they for long.\
\
'Why do you ally with the Kindred? Are we not enemies?'\
\
You briefly describe your shared fear that Azagath and Nakási are using a map they took from the Mâkhda Khorbo to search for a buried evil of Sauron's somewhere east of Umbar. Tatháta nods slowly.","'The sands have run from the hourglass, ${PLAYER}, and our conversation is ended. I am pleased I did not slay you. Your answers were most informative.\
\
'Good-bye.'","Sneak into the fortress and search the right side of the Ordâkhai camp","Remain on your guard and listen to the newcomer","A number of Ordâkhai soldiers have already been slain. What transpired here?","'Listen closely to the plan.\
\
'I will make for the buildings opposite the entrance, and move from shadow to shadow. Corudan and Sigileth will pass through the main gate and search for their quarry on the left side of the fortress. And you will look search for him on the right side, ${PLAYER}. I will give you some minutes before engaging the enemy... but you will not have very long!\
\
'In days to come, may the Ordâkhai speak in hushed tones of our work tonight! Fortune smile upon us!'","Tatháta has offered to answer a single question of yours.","Tatháta has answered your question, and the sound of distant shouting has brought your conversation with her to a close.","'I will answer a single question. Choose your inquiry with care.'","Ask Tatháta a single question","The time has come for you to leave the fortress before you are discovered by the Ordâkhai.","Instancia: Sombras en Jirush","Tatháta has agreed to answer a single question of yours.","Tatháta has come to the fortress above Jirush.","Talk to Tatháta","Rahâzi wants to go over the plan before you infiltrate the fortress above Jirush.","Distant shouting disturbs the fortress. Rahâzi's task is accomplished"},
[7113]={"Escucha a Cebadilla Mantecona","'¿A eso llamas cantares marineros?\
\
'¿Oh, te crees algún tipo de ${PLAYERNAME:Marinero[m]|Marinerqa[f]}, eh? ¿Has estado siquiera en el Mar alguna vez?'\
\
Bill Helechal suelta una miserable risotada.\
\
'Debería mandarte a la cárcel por torturar a esta buena gente con esa voz espantosa tuya, . ¿No es así, Harry?'\
\
Harry Goatleaf asiente, aunque notas cierta renuencia en ello.\
\
'¡O quizá debería ahorrarles la molestia!'","¡Has sido groseramente ${PLAYERNAME:interrumpido[m]|interrumpida[f]}!","Rojo de vergüenza, ¡Bill Helechal abandona el Poney Pisador!","Habla con Cebadilla Mantecona","Interpreta cantares marineros en el escenario del Poney Pisador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Qué dices, ${PLAYER}? ¿Unos cuantos más?'","Cebadilla Mantecona te ha pedido que interpretes cantares marineros por todo el Poney Pisador.","Bill Helechal está en el Poney Pisador.","Interpreta cantares marineros en el centro del Poney Pisador (${NUMBER}/3)","Instancia: Cantares en la Tormenta","Cebadilla Mantecona se encuentra en el Poney Pisador.","Interpreta cantares marineros en la entrada del Poney Pisador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Oh, hola, ! ¿Te apetece un trago?\
\
'Ah, ¿qué digo? Tienes actuaciones que atender, así que dejaré que sigas con ellas. Tengo muchos clientes esta noche, así que ¿por qué no actúas por todo el salón? ¿Por qué no empiezas por la entrada? Después, seguro que hay gente dispuesta a escuchar junto a la silla del barbero, en mi escenario del fondo, y cerca de la chimenea trasera. ¡Y si la gente parece animarse, incluso podrías dirigir unos cantares en el centro del salón!\
\
'Estas son solo sugerencias, por supuesto. Eres ${PLAYERNAME:el Marinero[m]|la Marinera[f]}, después de todo, así que dejo los cantares a tu elección.'","Enfrenta a Bill Helechal","Interpreta cantares marineros en la chimenea trasera del Poney Pisador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has sido groseramente ${PLAYERNAME:interrumpido[m]|interrumpida[f]} por dos hombres, Bill Helechal y Harry Goatleaf, que han irrumpido ruidosamente en el Poney Pisador.","Interpreta cantares marineros en la silla del barbero del Poney Pisador (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","<rgb=#FF0000>No pierdas la compostura</rgb>","'¿Estás bien, ?'\
\
'Perdona que haya intervenido, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}, pero no puedo permitir ese comportamiento en el Poney. Estoy seguro de que te habrías defendido admirablemente, pero este es un establecimiento respetable. Bill debería saber comportarse, aunque supongo que eso nunca lo ha detenido. Después de ese numerito, ¡tendrá suerte si consigue sus bebidas al triple del precio!\
\
'Y no te tomes a pecho lo que dijo el viejo Bill. Mucha gente aquí, incluyéndome, disfrutó de tus cantares. No siempre tengo buen oído para la canción, ¡pero hasta yo me descubrí moviendo el pie detrás del mostrador!'\
\
Barliman Butterbur sonríe amablemente.\
\
'De hecho, ¿cantarías unos cuantos más para nosotros? Solo hasta que pare la lluvia, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}.'","Cebadilla Mantecona necesita un Marinero experimentado para mantener los ánimos altos —y a los clientes sentados— en el Poney Pisador mientras una tormenta azota Bree.","Cebadilla Mantecona confronta a Bill Helechal y Harry Goatleaf."},
[7114]={"Talk to Sharkey","Talk to Tautila","Confront Sharkey","Sharkey is in the warrens of Tûn Melen.\
\
Sharkey has revealed himself. You should confront Sharkey.","Sharkey is in the warrens of Tûn Melen.\
\
After you defeated his guards, Sharkey has surrendered to you and Tautila. You should talk to Sharkey.","'I did not... expect you to come, ${PLAYER}. \
\
'My wounds... are not deep. I just need... a moment to catch my breath.'\
\
Tautila's eyes widen as he looks past you.","Tautila can be found deep within the warrens of Tûn Melen.\
\
You have found and freed Tautila, but he is unable to walk. You should talk to Tautila and try to help him to his feet.","Instancia: La noche de Zarquino","Contrary to Radagast's belief, Sharkey seems to be a pale half-orc. His hair is matted with some sort of white clay, but darker patches are still visible around it. You would never describe a half-orc as handsome, but it seems that Sharkey has taken a great deal of care in crafting his appearance. His brow is furrowed in frustration as he looks you up and down.\
\
'Not one of them could stop you?'\
\
Sharkey glares at you. Behind his stern gaze, you detect a hint of shock.","Tautila can be found somewhere in the warrens of Tûn Melen.\
\
Sharkey has taken Tautila and plans to hang him as punishment. You should try to rescue Tautila from Sharkey.","Tautila is alive, but bound and badly beaten","Tautila is not in his cage, but Vulfila appears to have been waiting for you","Seemingly unable to stand on his own, Tautila collapses","Free Tautila","'Surprised to see me, eh?\
\
'So was Sharkey... but I told him all about what you and Tautila got up to down here in the warrens.\
\
'Sharkey says whoever captures you gets to keep half the spoils of the next dig. Don't get any ideas about turning back, though, or Sharkey's going to string that little sneak up before the night's out!\
\
'What do you say, ${PLAYER}? Care to make me a richer man?'","'Let's... get out of here, ${PLAYER}.'","Tautila can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen.\
\
You have returned after nightfall as Tautila asked. You should speak to Tautila.","Tautila can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen.\
\
You have defeated Garmog. After he surrendered and bartered the true identity of Sharkey for his life, Garmog fled the warrens of Tûn Melen. You should talk to Tautila.","Talk to Vulfila","Tautila can be found deep within the warrens of Tûn Melen.\
\
You have found Tautila. You should loosen his restraints and free him.","'What need would a wizard have to lead a band of ruffians for petty thievery? Could a wizard not do such things himself if he so desired?\
\
'How can we trust that Garmog was not... deceiving us?'\
\
You tell Tautila that you can't be certain, but the name Sharkey has long been known to you. From the fields of Bree-land to Andrath, his outlaws have long troubled the Free Peoples. Your mind turns to the pipe-weed discovered in the ruins of Isengard. Could Garmog have spoken true? Is Sharkey the 'old man' truly Saruman?\
\
'Whatever plans Garmog had are undone, and I do not think the Wilderfolk shall need to fear the return of his ruffians.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}... and thank you for saving my life.'","Find and rescue Tautila from Sharkey","'Wait... please! I can explain! I'm not Sharkey!'\
\
The half-orc lowers his sword.\
\
'My name is Garmog, and I once served Saruman....'","Sharkey, the vicious leader of a band of half-orcs and ruffians, has big plans for the Gladden Fields.","Vulfila can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen.\
\
Tautila has been taken from his cage and Vulfila appears to have been waiting for you to return. You should confront Vulfila."},
[7115]={"'Come, let us leave this memory and return to the others. Are you ready, little one?'","'Hoom. I have told you but half of what there is to tell... for far grimmer tales remain.\
\
'Let us leave this place and return to Barallas and the others.'","Brúndoron lays slain as the Orcs serving Lomor prepare to return his hewn trunk to Isengard","Mossbeard is standing outside the future location of the White Hand encampment in the Balewood.\
\
Mossbeard is prepared to tell you a portion of what the trees have told him of Núrzum's origins before returning to Barallas and the others.","Listen as Mossbeard tells the tale of Brúndoron's fall","Talk to Mossbeard","Instancia: Raíces destrozadas","'Viler truths I have seldom known, ${PLAYER}. The others must know of these happenings soon, but you must understand as well if you are to continue to aid us.\
\
'Hoom, where the Orc-camp now lies once stood a bold Huorn... one of the very greatest in this forest.  My memories of those days are as clear as ever they have been... but they are tainted by the knowledge I have gained from the trees.\
\
'Come, let me tell you of the Huorn's fate....'","Mossbeard has chosen to tell you of Brúndoron, an elder Huorn of the Balewood slain before Núrzum came into power.","Mossbeard is standing in the future location of the White Hand encampment in the Balewood.\
\
Mossbeard's story has come to a close. You should speak to him before continuing your journey to Barallas and the others.","Mossbeard's story is still unfolding.\
\
Mossbeard is sharing his memories as learned from the trees of the Balewood. You should listen as he tells you more of this story."},
[7116]={"Talk to Felgúr","You are trapped in webs!","Enter Torech Ungol","Felgúr smells someone coming.\
\
You should talk to Felgúr.","Listen to the conversation","Felgúr ran into Torech Ungol, followed by Rûkhor and the Ungoledain.\
\
You should enter Torech Ungol.","Find Felgúr","Run!","The Pale Herald is coming.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","Instancia: La que camina en la oscuridad","Escape Torech Ungol","The time has come to enter Torech Ungol and discover if Ungwetári yet lives.","'They are near; I can smell them. And someone else… the Pale Herald. Be ready.'","Break free of the webs!","'You saw her. You saw Ungwetári. I can see the dread in your eyes, but fear not. We are safe in the presence of Lord Celeborn.'","'Tell me what happened.'","Felgúr ran into Torech Ungol, followed by Rûkhor and the Ungoledain.\
\
You should find Felgúr.","You have escaped Shelob.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","Felgúr was just devoured by Shelob. She is coming for you.\
\
Run!","Shelob is coming!\
\
You need to escape from the webs!","You have escaped Shelob","Habla con Legolas."},
[7117]={"This man has the rank of Rinc.\
\
His mood is one of eagerness.\
\
He was born in Faldham and his loyalty has always been to Elfhelm and his heirs.","Elfmar's men are in the field outside the Mead Hall of Faldham.\
\
Elfmar has asked you to train with his men so they will have some additional battle experience.","Talk to Elfmar to begin training with him","'Oh my. Nona and Horn will likely be sparring like that for awhile. I have been wondering how much longer it might take. Each of their interest in the other has been quite obvious to me, though perhaps not to themselves.'\
\
Corudan smiles.\
\
'Would you like to spar with me? They are not likely to end anytime soon.'","This man has the rank of Guma.\
\
His mood is one of understated confidence.\
\
He was born in Minas Tirith but is of Rohirric descent, and came to Faldham many years ago. He has already distinguished himself in battle with the Orcs.","This man has the rank of Ceorl.\
\
His mood is one of trepidation.\
\
He was born in Garsfeld, but now lives in Faldham and his loyalty is to Elfmar while Elfhelm is away.","Train with Elfmar's men in the field outside the Faldham Mead Hall","Trained a man of Rinc rank","'Are you ready to return to the Mead Hall? Nothing follows up a sweat quite like a great mug of ale!'","Elfmar is in the field outside the Mead Hall of Faldham.","Elfmar wants to have another bout with you.","Nona and Horn are in the field outside the Faldham Mead Hall.","This man has the rank of Rinc.\
\
His mood is one of confidence.\
\
He was born in Harwick and came to Faldham with his family very recently. He practices daily so he may better protect them.","This man has the rank of Ceorl.\
\
His mood is one of extreme confidence, but you can tell it is misplaced. He is certain to yield at the first chance of injury.\
\
He lives in Snowbourn and came to Faldham to serve Elfhelm, but he arrived after Elfhelm rode to the Fords and now seeks to impress Elfmar.","'I will try not to hurt these horse-lords too badly, ${PLAYER}, for your sake.'","Elfmar has asked for your aid in training his men, and also for a chance to discuss the situation in Rohan.","Trained a man of Guma rank","Talk to Elfmar","This man has the rank of Rinc.\
\
His mood is one of weariness.\
\
He was born in Langhold and has seen much of war. He came to Faldham because this is where his steed finally succumbed to exhaustion. He offered his sword to Elfmar as a means of regaining his honour.","'Well-fought, both of you. I will find someone with whom to test my own mettle!'","Instancia: Hermanos de escudo","This man has the rank of Ceorl.\
\
His mood is one of slight trepidation.\
\
He was born in Faldham, and he works daily on his combat skill but to little result. He hopes his training with you will help.","'Things go ill in Rohan, ${PLAYER}. I fear that the King's men are fewer than in days past, and less resolute. I have heard whispers from villagers and lords alike that put little faith in Théoden King.\
\
'I stand with Éomer, the King's nephew and Third Marshal of the Riddermark. He is my shield-brother, and we have sparred in peace and fought side by side during war. If he were here, he would be the first to volunteer to train with my men. Alas, Éomer is carried hither and yon by the tides of danger, and he goes where he is most needed. For today, that is elsewhere.\
\
'It will not always be so, and that is why I want you to train with my men. They will have need of the experience when the Orcs come to Faldham, as surely they must.'","'I do not quite know what to make of this, ${PLAYER}. If I did not know better, I would say that those two were a-courting. But... that would be unwise to say aloud. Perhaps I am mistaken.'\
\
Elfmar shakes his head.\
\
'Thank you for your help! I know that my men are better prepared to face what must surely await them now. I hope you found the training useful as well.'","Talk to Corudan","This man has the rank of Guma.\
\
His mood is one of eagerness.\
\
He was born in Faldham and is a frequent companion of Elfmar and Éomer.","Talk to Nona","'It has been the custom in Faldham for the leader to take the first battle for himself, and I see no reason it should be different today. Let us have a good battle, ${PLAYER}, and by our example inspire the men!'","'Is it true that your friend and boon companion Horn is from Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale? If he is the son of Reeve Ingbert, then his sister is the girl Ingyth.'\
\
Elfmar looks troubled.\
\
'I wonder how she has taken the death of Prince Théodred? The two were betrothed, and now, alas, never will they marry. This war has already taken the happiness of many, and it is only just begun!\
\
'I am ready to spar with you again, ${PLAYER}! And this time I will not let you have the victory so easily!'","Trained a man of Ceorl rank","Nona looks for someone with whom to spar","Horn goes off to find someone with whom to spar","This man has the rank of Ceorl.\
\
His mood is one of quiet confidence, and you cannot tell his level of skill from his countenance.\
\
He was born in Edoras and came to Faldham at a young age.","Corudan wishes to train with you as well.","Elfmar wishes to train with you.","Talk to Horn","Elfmar is standing outside his Mead Hall, and he wishes to speak with you about the possibility of training his men."},
[7118]={"Watch the funeral proceedings","Fríthild lies upon the table before the fireplace.\
\
Thane Ordlac asked you to retrieve Fríthild's sword and place it upon her in state.","'My thanks to you for bringing honour to Fríthild. It means much to her children. However, before we adjourn, I must make one pronouncement, and you should be a witness to it....'","Watch the funeral proceedings.","Thane Ordlac stands before the table where Reeve Fríthild lies.\
\
Thane Ordlac wishes for you to speak with him again.","Fríthild's shield is on the table near the door.\
\
Thane Ordlac asked you to retrieve Fríthild's shield and place it upon her in state.","'${PLAYER}, will you bring Fríthild's sword and place it, as well, upon her in honour?'","Collected Reeve Fríthild's sword","Placed Reeve Fríthild's sword upon her in state","Fríthild lies upon the table before the fireplace.\
\
Thane Ordlac asked you to retrieve Fríthild's shield and place it upon her in state.","Talk to Fríthbert","Fríthild's sword is on the table near the door.\
\
Thane Ordlac asked you to retrieve Fríthild's sword and place it upon her in state.","Talk to Dudsig","Collected Reeve Fríthild's shield","'Thane Ordlac has instructed me to keep the children in seclusion. I am sure you understand that with their mother dead and Fríthbert not yet old enough to assume his title, they are in danger...you never found the traitor in Oserley, you know.\
\
'As much as I dislike you, you have proven a trusted friend to the Broadacres; however, even you will not be allowed to speak with the children again without Thane Ordlac's leave.\
\
'Good day to you.'","Place Reeve Fríthild's sword upon her in state","'Good ${CLASS}, did our mother truly proclaim Thane Ordlac as our regent? This is most horrible.\
\
'I cannot say why, but Ordlac makes me uneasy. He always seems friendly and cheerful, but he makes light even of sad things....'","Place Fríthild's shield upon her in state","Dudsig is near the door to Reeve Fríthild's house.\
\
Dudsig wishes to speak with you.","'I am glad that you are able to join us, my friend. I am sure that Fríthild would have wished it. Let us begin....'","Thane Ordlac stands before the table where Reeve Fríthild lies.\
\
You should speak with Thane Ordlac before the funeral begins.","Placed Fríthild's shield upon her in state","'I am frightened, ${PLAYER}. Thane Ordlac smiles very much, but I do not like his eyes. There is no kindness in his eyes. He looks at us strangely, and it frightens me.'","'I believe you were dismissed....'","Talk to Thane Ordlac","Collect Reeve Fríthild's shield","Talk to Edhild","Instance: Shield-maiden of Rohan","You have come to Reeve Fríthild's house to honour her before her children.","Collect Reeve Fríthild's sword","Young Reeve Fríthbert and his sister Edhild appear distraught at Thane Ordlac's pronouncement. You should speak with them."},
[7119]={"Talk to Maedal outside the Uruk camp","Drafli Broadshield has recovered his confidence and needs to speak to you.","Maedal is outside the Uruk camp on Amon Hen, waiting to speak with you for your part of the plan to rescue Drafli Broadshield from captivity.","Listen to the situation within the Uruk camp","Instancia: Corto de estatura, grande en hazañas","'That was a fortunate gambit, ${PLAYER}! We survived, but I do not dare to call that a triumph. We must leave the East Wall as soon as we can, for the wraith may return when it recovers from the disappointment of which it spoke.\
\
'We cannot stay here.'","Talk to Isteron atop Amon Hen","Enter the camp and defeat the Uruk guarding Drafli's cage","Talk to Hestil outside the Uruk camp","You have been spotted, and the rescue mission has ended in failure!","'Let us hurry back to Parth Galen, ${PLAYER}. We do not want to be here when our foe returns.'","Ramdir is near the summit of Amon Hen, and you should speak to him.","Talk to Ramdir atop Amon Hen","'Our part of the plan to free Drafli should be easy, ${PLAYER}. We are to sneak up to the gate and listen to the conversation of the Uruks. Listen for anything that would make us need to change our plans.\
\
'I may not be much of a Captain, but I will be the best Burglar I can for my friends. Follow me, and do not let yourself be seen!'","'The glowers worked tremendously, ${PLAYER}! I cannot believe I took glistershade so much for granted! All they do is glow? Sometimes that is enough!\
\
'But they can't help us now, can they? Look at that thing!'","Talk to Drafli Broadshield","'There is the encampment, ${PLAYER}. Do you remember the plan? You and Maedal will creep up to the entrance so you can spy on the activities of the Uruks within the walls. Once you have determined that things are as we expect them to be, Rodwen and I will drop into the camp from above while Cúfaron sows confusion among the Uruks with his arrows.\
\
'I have tasked Ramdir with keeping an eye on Isteron. Our lore-master has decided that he wants to study the effect of some plant he found on the Uruks, and I... well, I am sure Ramdir can keep him from interfering with the plan.\
\
'It is time, ${PLAYER}. May good fortune shine on all of us, and we will have Drafli Broadshield back with us before the moon is any higher in the night sky!'","'It is no use, ${PLAYER}. My friends are better off without me. I am no use as a guardian. Look at me! Stuck in this cage, depending on someone else to free me. That is not the way of a dwarf!'\
\
You tell Drafli that his friends are endangered and need his help.\
\
'But what can I do? I am stuck here in this cage!'","The Uruk camp has mostly emptied in pursuit of Isteron! You need to go and rescue Drafli Broadshield while the others see to Isteron's well-being.","Avoid being seen!","Isteron is in trouble near the top of Amon Hen.","'Ha ha! I am ready to fight once more, ${PLAYER}! I am a dwarf, I am a guardian, and I am free! Now let us go save my friends!'","You need to observe what's going on inside the Uruk camp on Amon Hen. Be careful not to be seen!","Survive your encounter with the Grim Southron","Defeated Drafli's guard","Drafli Broadshield is inside his cage in the Uruk camp on Amon Hen. You need to speak to him to get him out of his depression.","Hestil's group of adventurers-for-hire is in danger near the summit of Amon Hen.","It is time for Hestil's group of adventurers-for-hire to rescue their guardian from his captivity, and you have agreed to help with the task.","Hestil is outside the Uruk encampment on Amon Hen, waiting to speak with you before setting the plan into motion."},
[7122]={"'They would surely have overrun our defences had you not been here. Some men were lost, but not so many that we can not recover.'","The enemy will assault both of the barricaded entrances into Brockbridge. Herefara has asked you to use your war-steed and help the defenders that are more overwhelmed.","The city of Brockbridge faces its greatest challenge yet as an army marches on the stalemate siege in an attempt to punch through their stalwart defences.","Instancia: Asedio intensificado","Defend Brockbridge","<rgb=#FF0000>Herefara has been defeated</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow guards to be defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Herefara cannot be defeated</rgb>","'${PLAYER}, we thank you for your assistance defeating everything the enemy threw at us today.'","Herefara would like to thank you for your assistance in keeping the enemy at bay and ensuring not too many men were lost in the battle.","The enemy is preparing to assault Brockbridge with renewed vigour, and the few defenders remaining will be hard-pressed to keep the city secure.","<rgb=#FF0000>Guards defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>","'Drums announced their approach, as they were not afraid to let us know they are coming. Their confidence is unsettling. Our defenders will soon be pressed to keep up. We must keep both gates defended, and I ask that you help any of the men who become overwhelmed!\
\
'We cannot lose too many men, or we will be overrun. I will guard this gate, but I ask that you mount your war-steed to more easily assist either gate.'","Talk to Herefara"},
[7123]={"Hármelak waits for tidings of the army that approaches the city, and your brother Jajax is not about to give her this news. It falls to you to do this, Daxamat.","Talk to your brother Jajax in Dâr Laja and tell him what you saw","Your quick action has unearthed Sigileth from the rubble that might have proved her tomb!","Talk to Sigileth among the rubble beside the collapsed entrance to Utug-bûr","'Hurry, ${PLAYER}! We have little time to waste!'","You have only moments before the entrance to Utug-bûr collapses. If you are to escape with Sigileth, you will have to act quickly.","Heed the words of Corudan","Corudan knows the need for haste if you are to rescue Sigileth.","Days later, anxious eyes turn to the east and consider the army of soldiers approaching Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Hármelak inside Dâr Laja and tell her what you saw","'I cannot believe it!'","'What is it? I can see from your face you have tidings to share, but you fear they will be unwelcome. Speak them, and I will decide if it is so.'\
\
You tell Hármelak that an army approaches the city, but you were unable to see who leads it, or what their intentions may be. Hármelak purses her lips, deep in thought.\
\
'When Belondor asked to bring soldiers to battle in the lands to the east, I told him I needed time to think upon it; he waited not for my answer, but took the soldiers and marched within the hour. Such disrespect cannot be allowed... but it is said that when commanders of men taste victory in battle, they can at times desire more and more. If Belondor leads this returning army, will he think to use it to take control of this city?\
\
'Or perhaps this is an army of Heirsworn. If Balakhâd escaped capture by the party sent to retrieve him, his survival could prove a beacon to his folk. Thinks he to overthrow the Kindred of the Coins? But from where could this army have come?'\
\
You suggest to Hármelak that there may be a third possibility. She considers you carefully.\
\
'What is this third possibility, tidings-bearer Daxamat?'\
\
You suggest that the army may be tired from battle in the east, and the soldiers may simply want to return home. In this you see the guidance of ${PLAYER}, a hero who knows when to fight, and when not to fight. Hármelak weighs your suggestion.\
\
'We will see if you are right, Daxamat. We will see. Send word to the scouts that whoever leads this army is to be brought before me at once!'","'What did you see, Dax? An army approaches Umbar Baharbêl?'\
\
You tell Jajax that a great force of soldiers emerged from Ambarûl, drawing even with Telperiën's Wall, but they raised no banner and you could not discern their loyalties.\
\
'Did you see ${PLAYER} among them? Or perhaps Belondor leads these men? Is this army the same that he took with him in haste... or is it an army of Heirsworn, come to take the city?\
\
'I am not bringing Hármelak these tidings, Dax. I leave that to you!'","Several days ago, in the aftermath of the Dagor Carlanthir.","You can go no further without risking entombment with the Thardúth... but perhaps Sigileth will hear your voice if you call for her down the hallway!","<rgb=#FF0000>You have to reach the exit before the entrance collapses!</rgb>","Break the rubble beside the collapsed entrance to Utug-bûr","Break more of the rubble beside the collapsed entrance to Utug-bûr","Choose your words with care and call for Sigileth to return to you","Instancia: Sigileth en la oscuridad","You are out of time! You must escape from Utug-bûr!","'${PLAYER}...\
\
'Has anyone... ever told you...\
\
'You are such... a bother...'\
\
Sigileth smiles up at you weakly.\
\
'Thank you... my dear friend...' she murmurs quietly.","Days earlier, in the aftermath of the Dagor Carlanthir","Days pass, and a ruler in Umbar Baharbêl anxiously awaits news","Escape from Utug-bûr!","Talk to Corudan inside Utug-bûr","You cannot have imagined it! You know someone lives beneath the rubble!","You can go no further inside Utug-bûr or you will be trapped forever with the Thardúth.","She lives! Can it be possible?","Jajax waits in Dâr Laja to hear news of what his brother Daxamat learned of the approaching army."},
[7124]={"Habla con Bingo en las orillas del Brandivino","Nada al otro lado del río","Habla con Bingo, pero que no te gotee encima","Dar ejemplo quizás pueda ayudar. Si cruzas el río nadando, puede que Bingo encuentre la manera de hacer lo mismo.","Bingo está listo para aprender a nadar, y necesita tu consejo.","Deberías regresar con Bingo y ver si tu demostración le ha ayudado a ganar algo de confianza.","'¡Eso ha sido incréible, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! ¡Creo que yo puedo hacerlo también!'","Te duelen los músculos, pero has hecho una buena demostración","'¡Lo he hecho, ${PLAYER}! ¿Me has visto? Tu hazaña fue bastante buena, pero me temo que la mía te ha dejado un poco en evidencia.\
\
'Ha sido una verdadera muestra de destreza en natación, ¿no crees?'","'Estoy empapado pero feliz, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. ¡Volvamos a la Perca Dorada y sequémonos!'","'Bueno, aquí estamos, ${PLAYER}. ¡Es hora de que este hobbit aprenda algo nuevo!'","'Estoy algo más templado, ¡pero el agua todavía parece fría y ahora me siento cansado!\
\
'¿Crees que este podría ser un mal sitio? ¿Puede que deba probar otro lugar de la orilla? ¡Buena idea!'","Instancia: Nada o húndete","Como preparación para su viaje, has acompañado a Bingo a la orilla del Brandivino para ayudarle mientras aprende a nadar.","Bingo ha chapoteado un poco en el agua. Es posible que haya nadado un poco, pero es difícil decirlo a ciencia cierta.","'Se me ocurre que quizá haya cometido un pequeño error de juicio, ${PLAYER}, y quizá no me haya vestido del todo apropiadamente para las... frías... heladas... aguas.'\
\
Bingo se estremece.\
\
'¿Qué opinas? ¿Crees que necesitaría calentar primero, para que la sangre fluya? ¡Es una idea fantástica, mi inteligente ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!'","Vuelve con Bingo y comprueba si tu demostración ha sido de ayuda","Habla con Bingo en la orilla del Brandivino"},
[7125]={"'You have done well this day, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The people of my lands have far less to fear now, and I speak not only of the defeat of the Dead.\
\
'Your presence has changed the fate of the war here in Gondor, and I shall ever watch over your deeds in the East.\
\
'Come now, let us return to my glade.'","The Ruthless Dead appear once more, angered by your presence!","The river Gilrain flows south to the mere from Roamingstar's glade.\
\
You have defeated the Ruthless Dead once more and should now meet Roamingstar at the edge of the mere.","DNT -- will not be seen","Instancia: Hermana del Gilrain","As the last of the Dead vanish, you continue your pursuit of Roamingstar","Confront Nerzus and the Ruthless Dead","Follow the river south towards the mere","Defeat the Ruthless Dead before they can cross the Gilrain","The river Gilrain flows south from Roamingstar's glade.\
\
You have defeated the Ruthless Dead you encountered along the river's edge and should now continue south.","Nerzus of the Ruthless Dead suddenly appears before you!","The Ruthless Dead are attacking from the western banks of the Gilrain.\
\
You have encountered the Ruthless Dead along the Gilrain and should prevent them from crossing.","As thanks for your aid and to protect the lands of Gondor, Roamingstar seeks to prevent the Ruthless Dead from crossing into Lebennin.","The Ruthless Dead are attacking from the western banks of the Gilrain.\
\
The Ruthless Dead have renewed their attack, and must be defeated before they can cross the Gilrain unhindered.","'Let us leave the Dead to contemplate their doom, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Roamingstar","Granted a respite, you must now reach Roamingstar","The river Gilrain flows south from Roamingstar's glade.\
\
Roamingstar has asked you to follow the Gilrain south to the mere and prevent the Dead from crossing it.","Roamingstar's power has banished Nerzus and sent the Ruthless Dead fleeing back to their dark home","'I feel a chill at the water's edge, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'The Dead move to cross the river, and they must not be allowed to pass into Lebennin! You are known to them, but I am not... if you can drive them back from the river's edge and lure them to the mere, I shall ensure that they will only find peace far from these lands. Should they dare to cross the Gilrain then... even I do not know what will become of them, but they shall never reach the far banks.\
\
'I can grant you safety in my waters, but if you stray from the Gilrain, I cannot protect you from the Dead!\
\
'Go now, ${CLASS}!'","A watery image of Roamingstar dashes through the shallows of the Gilrain...","Nerzus and the Ruthless Host can be found on the western banks of the mere.\
\
You have encountered Nerzus and his grim host as they ready to cross into Lebennin.","Roamingstar can be found at the edge of the mere along the Gilrain in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have defeated the Ruthless Dead and driven them far from Dor-en-Ernil. You should now speak to Roamingstar.","Follow the Gilrain further south","Defeat the Ruthless Dead trying to cross the Gilrain","Roamingstar is standing on a small shoal along the Gilrain.\
\
You have agreed to aid Roamingstar in banishing the Ruthless Dead and should now speak to her.","Follow the Gilrain to the edge of the mere"},
[7127]={"'Temo lo que ha hecho Gormr. Puede que ya sea demasiado tarde, pero Ivar es demasiado poderoso para que entremos directamente en la tumba. Nos detendrá si lo intentamos. Tendremos que encontrar otro camino.\
\
'Elladan y Elrohir irán a ver si pueden encontrar un camino alternativo. Nosotros subiremos estas escaleras y veremos si podemos rodear por el costado. ¡Apurémonos!'","Tras huir de los salones, habla con Dwalin una vez más.","Los enanos Duramano esperan devolver la vida a su líder muerto hace mucho tiempo, Skorgrím. Junto a Dwalin, has viajado a la tumba excavada por los Duramano para Skorgrím con el fin de poner fin a sus planes.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para dejar estos salones, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}? Por mi parte, estaré feliz de dejarlos atrás.'","'¿Lo sientes, ? ¡Hay maldad en el aire! La última vez que sentí algo así fue cuando cruzaba el Bosque Negro hace muchos años. ¡Tendremos que estar muy atentos aquí!\
\
'Elrohir y los demás están aquí para ayudar, pero no debemos demorarnos demasiado, o podríamos perder la oportunidad de detener el mal que ocurre aquí. ¡Debemos irnos ya! ¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}?'","'Ah, aunque no logramos detener los planes de los Duramano, hemos hecho bien en este día, ${PLAYER}. Al final del día, la Mansión de Thorin estará libre de los Duramano, y todos sabrán que son enanos sin importancia.\
\
'Me pregunto, sin embargo, ¿cuándo veremos los efectos de este día y el regreso de Skorgrím? Me alegrará tenerte en la Mansión de Thorin como uno de mis buenos y firmes enanos.\
\
'Ahora, ¡dejemos atrás estas salas!'","Has fallado en defender a Dwalin","'¡Tenemos que salir de aquí! Hemos asestado un golpe importante a los Duramano, aunque no pudimos evitar que el ritual se llevara a cabo. A Skorgrím habrá que enfrentarlo otro día.\
\
'¡Rápido, debemos huir! ¡Sea lo que sea que haya hecho Ivar, el lugar se está derrumbando a nuestro alrededor!'","Continúa defendiendo a Dwalin mientras te acercas a tu objetivo: el lugar donde se realiza el ritual para restaurar a Skorgrím.","Instancia: Tumba de Skorgrím","Acompaña y defiende a Dwalin mientras avanzas hacia la tumba de Skorgrím.","Sigue a Dwalin para ver si puedes detener la resurrección.","Habla con Dwalin"},
[7128]={"Enter Plas-maru and seek out the main chamber","Instance: Something Foul","Drive back the fell spirit from Lhucu.","'Untie me, Duvodiad, and I shall lead you out of this place.'","Entered Plas-maru","Use levers to open the gate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Lhucu","Defeat Mostun","Naeglanc has sent you to uncover what is happening in the depths of Plas-maru.","Travel deep into Plas-maru and locate the levers that control the gate to the main chamber.","Speak with Lhucu and escape Plas-maru.","Defeat the chieftain and his fell spirit companion","Seek out the main chamber of Plas-maru.","Enter the main chamber of Plas-maru and uncover the secret of the cairn.","Used levers to open the gate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Discover what is causing the wights to stir within the Bonevales","You have defeated Mostun, now free Lhucu"},
[7129]={"Examine Sigileth","The Orcs remaining in Maurûsh seemingly abandoned much of their equipment at one of their camp-fires.","Silirtas also stands frozen in place. What has happened to them... or to you?","A feeling of exhaustion overwhelms you","Sigileth and Silirtas stand unmoving in Maurûsh. What has happened to them... or to you?","Sigileth stares at you with concern.","Mithrandir has come to Maurûsh... but for what purpose has the Wizard travelled so far south?","Instancia: Algo ha despertado","Wait for answers","Examine the imposing creature worshipped by the Orcs","Something stirs within the old keep of Maurûsh, but it is not the presence of the Ordâkhai that threatens Urash Dâr from behind its walls.","Silirtas and Sigileth have come with you to investigate Maurûsh.","'A terrible evil sleeps in this place, ${PLAYER}, and it is more dangerous than you can face alone! We cannot stay here!\
\
'Quickly, now!'","Search deeper within Maurûsh for some way to free your friends","'${PLAYER}! Are you all right? You appeared to swoon for a moment, and you responded to nothing!'\
\
You ask Sigileth if she or Silirtas heard the terrible voice that spoke to you, or saw the large and fearsome Orcs, and both Elves shake their heads.\
\
'You were dazed for only moments, ${PLAYER}. How could you...?'\
\
Sigileth's voice trails away to nothing, and she suddenly looks past you to the south.\
\
'Someone approaches!'","Sigileth stands unmoving, as if she were frozen in place","Examine the abandoned possessions at the camp-fire","Talk to Sigileth within Maurûsh","A great weight lifts from your eyelids","Some great evil pursues you! You have to escape from Maurûsh!","Flee down the slope to the south to escape from Maurûsh!","An unusual creature, larger than the other Orcs you have seen, stands deep within Maurûsh. Or is this creature a product of the enchantment in which you have been snared?","Examine Silirtas","Sigileth has fallen, and you have failed!","A great weight lifts from your eyelids.","Talk to Silirtas outside Maurûsh","Some evil located deeper within Maurûsh may hold the key to freeing Sigileth and Silirtas from the ensnaring enchantment.","Talk to Mithrandir in Maurûsh","'Something drove the Ordâkhai from this place. Was it the Orcs... or was it something else? We should be careful, but we must learn these answers if we can.'"},
[7130]={"You have made your way through the wilds of Ithilien in search of Mûmakil, and now the brothers Duilin and Derufin have once more crossed paths in their respective hunts.","Instancia: Hijos de Raíz Negra","Survive the encounter, and ensure that Duilin and Derufin live to tell the tale","You have encountered two Mûmakil in the wilds of Ithilien, but Duilin and Derufin have lost the element of surprise and now the three of you must escape from the trumpeting beasts.","'We should not all tramp through the wild together, ${PLAYER}. The two of us would be silent enough, I expect, but my brother makes more noise in the brush than even the largest Mûmak!\
\
'This sword of mine has proven the better of every creature upon which I set my mark, and today will be no different. If you choose to hunt with me, we will travel up the slope to the north for a better view, the better to surprise our prey.'","'I am ready to take to the wild in search of Mûmakil! Waste no time, and we might find one of the great beasts before my brother. There will be glory enough for all, but it brings me no shame to confess I want to be the first!'","'I encountered a number of Orcs ranging through the forested hills of this land, but I caught no sign of any Mûmakil. How can such large beasts evade us?\
\
'And yet, I feel the earth tremble. Do you feel that? Can it be?'","'I have slain a number of Haradrim warriors on the road through this land already, but I have not seen a single Mûmak at which to let fly my arrows.\
\
'But there is a trembling in the earth. Do you feel that? Is it possible our prey approaches?'","Choose to accompany Derufin","'I will be pleased to have you join me, ${PLAYER}! Let us waste no more time! I want to be the first to find a Mûmak, and if we are to bring one down before my brother finds one we will need to hurry!'","Duilin and Derufin are waiting for you to choose which of the brothers you wish to accompany on the hunt for a Mûmak.","You have left Bâr Húrin with Duilin and Derufin to hunt one of the mighty Mûmakil.","Choose to accompany one of the brothers and follow him in search of prey\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you are in a Fellowship, every character must choose the same brother to follow, or the instance will fail.</rgb>","Duilin and Derufin have agreed to help you with your own mission if you will help them with theirs: hunting the mighty Mûmakil the Haradrim have brought to Gondor.","Talk to Derufin on the path","'My brother and I rarely hunt together, ${PLAYER}. We find that we have much more success when tracking a foe if we travel alone. That way, if one of us frightens the beast, the other may be able to take advantage of the confusion of our prey.\
\
'My chosen weapon is this longbow, and my accuracy with it is legendary among the folk of the Blackroot Vale. If you come with me, I suggest that we travel eastward by way of the road, and the long sight-lines will give us the advantage over any raiding parties we encounter while we search for a Mûmak.'","Talk to Duilin on the path","Meet up with the other hunter","Choose to accompany Duilin"},
[7131]={"Habla con el guardián Galadhrim.","Los Galadhrim están esperando a escuchar qué tienes que decir sobre la solicitud de Bósi.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, ? Es posible que no haya más orcos que hayan cruzado las fronteras, pero si los hay, debemos estar preparados para luchar.\
\
¡Vamos entonces! ¡Te mostraré el camino!'","Habla con el arquero Galadhrim.","Has decidido caminar por los bosques de Lothlórien con Legolas y Gimli en busca de patrullas de orcos.","Bósi está en la frontera de Lothlórien, intentando conseguir una audiencia con Celeborn.","Bósi está teniendo una audiencia con Celeborn de Lórien sobre el envío de Elfos para asistir a los enanos en Khazad-dûm.","'Habla con estos Elfos, ${PLAYER}. Parecen confiar en ti, y quizás tu palabra me consiga la audiencia con Celeborn que he solicitado.'","Legolas y Gimli están de pie en uno de los caminos que atraviesan los bosques de Lothlórien.\
\
Legolas espera viajar contigo a través de los bosques de Lothlórien.","'Por respeto a ti, ${PLAYER}, y como cortesía por el bien que nos has hecho, me han dicho que te encuentre y te envíe a la orilla del bosque.\
\
Ha llegado un extraño a las fronteras. En estos tiempos inusuales, un visitante así en Lothlórien solo ha sido visto una vez.\
\
Este extraño es un enano, y está preguntando por ti, ${PLAYER}.'","'Las cosas no van bien para la Guarnición de Hierro en Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Mazog aún gobierna gran parte de las profundidades y muchos niveles desde su fortaleza de Zabadgathol, y muchos buenos enanos han caído ante sus fuerzas. Algunos, como mi propio hijo Bori, siguen siendo prisioneros, ¡o peor! No puedo soportar pensar en los tormentos que pueden haber sufrido tras los muros de Zabadgathol.\
\
Aun así, los enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro luchan por recuperar las cavernas ocultas, pero por cada belleza que se descubre, dos males parecen surgir de las profundidades.\
\
He venido a pedir ayuda al gobernante de estos bosques élficos. Si Celeborn de Lothlórien desea beneficiarse de la amistad con los enanos, debe corresponder de igual manera. Eres de confianza para estos elfos, ${PLAYER}. Habla con este guardián, este centinela, sobre nuestra situación. Quizá te escuchen.'","Instancia: Hijos de la Hoja y la Piedra","Vigila la audiencia de Bósi con Celeborn.","¡No has logrado proteger a Gimli!","'Por el bien de la Guarnición de Hierro he soportado la indignidad de ser vendado durante el trayecto aquí, ${PLAYER}, pero mi gente podría enseñar algo de cortesía a los elfos de este lugar si visitaran Khazad-dûm.\
\
Veamos ahora si las malas maneras de los elfos provienen de su Señor.'","'Llevaremos a este enano a hablar con Celeborn, ${PLAYER}, pero tú serás responsable de él. Serás responsable de cualquier acción que él tome mientras permanezca dentro del Bosque de Oro.\
\
Ven con nosotros.'","Sigue a Legolas y Gimli hasta la orilla del bosque.","Se te ha dicho que sigas a Legolas y Gimli hasta la orilla del bosque para encontrarte con un enano que ha preguntado por ti.","'El Señor de los Galadhrim posee gran sabiduría, y desea que los enanos no enfrenten la oscuridad de Khazad-dûm solos.\
\
Así será, y tú también te enfrentarás a los males que ahora se ocultan bajo las montañas, ${PLAYER}, si ese es tu deseo.'","Galadriel espera para hablar contigo tras la audiencia con Bósi.","Mientras estaba vendado, Bósi ha sido llevado a Caras Galadhon dentro de Lothlórien para su audiencia con Celeborn.","'Es hora de que te vayas, joven. Hay mucho por hacer.'","Habla con Legolas.","Habla con Bósi.","Has venido con Legolas y Gimli cerca de la frontera del bosque, y has sido saludado por uno de los Galadhrim."},
[7132]={"'Ah-ha! There you are, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'You may have noticed that a great deal of Azgarzôr's men have gone. That may be because I set some of their ships on fire, but I do not know their thinking for certain!'\
\
Jajax lets out a small chuckle.\
\
'Do not fear, I did not burn the finest of them, for I do not think my heart could have taken it. But yes, we have much to attend to here while those fools are distracted...\
\
'I can see in your friends' eyes a burning anger... I feel much the same way for what has been done to my people. Let us be through with this, my friend. Azgarzôr must be slain this day!'","As you approach the tent, a wave of dread passes over you...","'It is done then...\
\
'I miss my brother greatly, ${PLAYER}, but I can rest easier knowing his murder has been avenged.\
\
'Azgarzôr shall be forgotten, but the deeds of my brother shall be remembered in Dor-en-Ernil for ages to come.\
\
'Ready yourself to depart, ${PLAYER}. I have but a few more words to say here....'","DNT -- will not be seen","Erchar and Herion can be found within Hata Kebir.\
\
Garvir's brothers are battling their way deeper into Hata Kebir. You should aid them.","Erchar and Herion can be found within Hata Kebir.\
\
You have begun to assault Hata Kebir with Garvir's brothers and should follow them into battle.","Fight your way into Hata Kebir with Erchar and Herion","Instancia: Hijos del Usurpador","Talk to Jajax in Hata Kebir","Azgarzôr's tent is in the heart of Hata Kebir.\
\
Jajax has joined with you and Garvir's brothers to confront Azgarzôr. You should battle your way to his tent.","Horses can be found just inside the western entrance to Hata Kebir.\
\
Erchar has asked you to free the horses and spook them, so that they might cause further commotion within Hata Kebir.","Fight your way to Azgarzôr's tent","Erchar is standing outside Hata Kebir.\
\
You have arrived at Hata Kebir and should now speak to Erchar before beginning your assault.","After defeating the Haradrim and stable-hands, the horses stand undefended","Erchar is standing in Hata Kebir.\
\
You have defeated Azgarzôr and avenged Garvir. You should speak to Erchar before leaving the camp.","Seeking to put an end to the reign of the Heirs of Castamir, Jajax prepares himself for an uneasy and hopefully brief alliance with Garvir's brothers.","Fight your way further into Hata Kebir","'We must leave this place before more of Azgarzôr's men return!'","Azgarzôr is in Hata Kebir.\
\
You have found Azgarzôr, and must now defeat him.","Jajax is standing outside the inner camp-sites of Hata Kebir.\
\
You have battled your way deep into Hata Kebir and have discovered Jajax amid the largely-emptied tents nearby. You should speak to him.","Free and spook horses in Hata Kebir (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You notice a familiar face in the distance...","Freed and spooked horses in Hata Kebir (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Confront and defeat Azgarzôr","'Are you prepared, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'I hope so, for I can wait no longer! Garvir must be avenged!'","Azgarzôr is slain!","Talk to Erchar"},
[7133]={"Talk to Harnion about sparring with the soldiers.","Talk to Harnion","Go to the centre of the sparring area.","Spar with the soldiers","Spar with the soldiers until you've faced them all.","Go to the centre of the sparring area","'Well done, ${PLAYER}. I think the soldiers deserve a bit of a rest now.'","Return to Harnion","'Well, that's sure to humble them a bit! Well done. They'll certainly redouble their training after that showing of skill, with or without my orders!'","Harnion, the Master-at-Arms of the Training Ground, has asked for your aid in helping the soldiers with their sparring skills.","'${PLAYER}, the threat of battle has been lingering for quite some time now, and the soldiers have grown restless from anticipation. A sparring session will do them some good. It will help them practice, but it may also relieve some of their nerves!\
\
'If you think you can take them, head on down to the centre of the room.'","<rgb=#FF0000>You must not be defeated by the soldiers</rgb>","Instancia: Entrenamiento en Minas Tirith","Talk to Harnion about the sparring match.","You have been bested by the soldiers!"},
[7134]={"Instancia: Espectro del Miedo Gris","'La criatura ha huido, ${PLAYER}, y no podemos perseguirla desde aquí. Pero veremos desbaratados sus designios y derribadas las intrigas de su amo. Lo juro.\
\
'Por ahora sacaremos a Meneldir de este lugar. No lo dejaremos aquí.'","Busca a Meneldir y Gorwen en las catacumbas bajo Dol Ernil","Habla con Halbarad en Dol Ernil","Sobrevive a tu encuentro con el Miedo Gris","Habla con Gorwen en las catacumbas bajo Dol Ernil","'¿Una trampilla que conduce a catacumbas bajo la fortaleza? No creo que Gorwen siguiera a Meneldir hasta un lugar así, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Seguiremos buscando aquí arriba, pero si crees que existe la posibilidad de que ambos hayan descendido a las catacumbas...\
\
'Si eso es lo que crees, no te impediré continuar tu búsqueda allí. Nos reuniremos contigo abajo cuando hayamos terminado de buscarlos aquí arriba... y con suerte te traeremos noticias de que han sido encontrados y de que tu búsqueda en las catacumbas fue innecesaria.'","Halbarad se encuentra en la sala del trono de Dol Ernil, buscando alguna pista sobre el paradero de Gorwen y Meneldir.","'Debe de haber alguna pista aquí en la sala del trono de Dol Ernil, ${PLAYER}, si tan solo podemos encontrarla.'","Escucha las últimas palabras de Meneldir","Busca pistas en la sala del trono de Dol Ernil","'Algo no está bien, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Mientras estabas fuera, Meneldir y yo pasamos el tiempo en tranquila conversación. ¡Nada parecía fuera de lugar durante horas! Pero entonces, de pronto, se puso de pie de un salto, volcó su copa y dejó caer su mendrugo de pan en la tierra. \\q¡No está lo bastante oscuro para tales criaturas!\\q, gritó, desenvainando su espada. \\q¿Qué ves?\\q, le pregunté, pero no me respondió; creo que no oyó mis palabras, y salió corriendo del campamento y se internó entre las ruinas.\
\
'Recojí mi propio equipo y lo seguí, pero por temor a ser alcanzado por uno de sus golpes a ciegas no me atreví a acercarme demasiado. Es un milagro que no se topara con los tumularios que merodean por las ruinas de arriba, o tal vez no lo sea. Puede que no entendieran las palabras que pronunciaba y creyeran que sus golpes iban dirigidos contra ellos.\
\
'Pero yo oí esas palabras. Él no sabe dónde está, ${PLAYER}. Creyó que la sala del trono de arriba era una granja en el bosque, y que la trampilla era la entrada a un sótano de raíces. No sé qué enemigo ilusorio cree estar enfrentando, pero sea cual sea la forma que adopta, sé esto: debe de ser obra del Miedo Gris.'","Halbarad busca alguna pista sobre la desaparición de Meneldir y Gorwen.","Llega a las catacumbas bajo Dol Ernil","'Las huellas conducen a Dol Ernil, pero el mensaje que leo en ellas es confuso. No puedo determinar si Gorwen y Meneldir llegaron hasta aquí en paz, o si su avance fue entorpecido por una embestida de enemigos. Al menos estaban juntos. De eso estoy seguro.\
\
'Debemos seguirlos. Prepárense para la batalla, amigos.'","Habla con Halbarad en la sala del trono de Dol Ernil","Un mal terrible acecha en las catacumbas bajo Dol Ernil.","Meneldir se escabulle. Ya no está.","Usa la trampilla en la esquina de la sala del trono para descender a las catacumbas","Debes buscar a Meneldir y Gorwen en las catacumbas... solo.","La trampilla en un rincón de la sala del trono conduce a unas catacumbas bajo la fortaleza.","La trampilla conduce a catacumbas bajo la fortaleza.","Meneldir ha sufrido una herida grave. Le queda poco tiempo.","¿Descendieron Meneldir y Gorwen a las catacumbas bajo Dol Ernil?","Meneldir y Gorwen han desaparecido del campamento exterior de Dol Ernil. ¿Se toparon con el Miedo Gris?","Algo anda mal en las catacumbas bajo Dol Ernil, y más de una vida está en peligro.","La respiración de Meneldir es superficial y su pulso lento. No le queda mucho tiempo.\
\
'Había trolls, ${PLAYER}... como los de antes. Mi guardia... mi vigilia... no abandonaría a esa gente. No... no esta vez.\
\
'No por mi... no por mi juramento. Por mí.'","Las huellas se han vuelto aún más confusas en la sala del trono de Dol Ernil.","Has encontrado a Gorwen. ¡Está viva!"},
[7135]={"¡La red está colocada!","'Después de todo, parece que hoy no conseguiré una nueva montura. Aunque... ¡podría intentar hacerme amiga de uno de sus cachorros!\
\
'Bueno, esa es una aventura para otro día.'","Espera a que el lince sea capturado.","Habla con Diamante","'He estado rastreando a un lince durante días, y siempre viene por este sendero a esta hora. Vamos a buscar un buen sitio para colgar la red. Toma, cógela tú. Encuentra un sitio para el pastel y luego cuelga la red sobre él.'","Coloca el pastel","Habla con Adamanda","Espera que la trampa se despliegue","Tras descubrir que el lince era una madre reciente, Adamanda ha liberado a la criatura.\
\\Debes hablar con Adamanda.","'Ven, dejemos que se termine el pastel en paz.'","Coloca la trampa","Arrodíllate detrás del arbusto con Diamante","¡Con red y pastel en mano, Diamante está lista para llevar a cabo su Gran Plan y colocar una trampa para su presa!","'¡No hay manera de que el lince pueda resistir ese pastel! ¡Ahora a esconderse y esperar!'","Instancia: Ejecutando el Gran Plan","El pastel está en un lugar irresistible","El sendero está en la Comarca Allende.\
\
Adamanda Nortuk te ha pedido que coloques una trampa a lo largo del sendero que usa frecuentemente el lince.","Adamanda te espera fuera de Nobotella.\
\
Habla con Adamanda Nortuk."},
[7136]={"'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}, bien hecho! A Amarthiel no le agradará en absoluto este giro.\
\
'Házmelo saber cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir, y regresaremos a Tinnudir con nuestro cautivo.'","El Montaraz Tadan y sus compañeros Dúnedain se ocultan en el extremo de la calzada hacia Haudh Elendil, aguardando en emboscada a que Mordrambor aparezca.\
\
Tadan necesita que atraigas a Mordrambor hacia la emboscada de los Dúnedain al final de la calzada.","Instancia: Hacer saltar la trampa","Se te ha pedido que lleves a Mordrambor de regreso al extremo de la calzada con los Montaraces.","'Calenglad habla muy bien de ti, ${PLAYER}. ¡Si esta noche tenemos éxito, hablará aún mejor!\
\
'Mordrambor ha entrado en la tumba de Elendil y sin duda saldrá en breve con sus sirvientes. Si logramos conservar el elemento sorpresa, mis hermanos y yo seremos más que suficientes para enfrentarlo. Preséntate ante este lugarteniente de Amarthiel y atráelo hasta este extremo de la calzada. Caeremos sobre él y lo haremos prisionero, y entonces veremos qué puede contarnos este servidor de confianza de Amarthiel.\
\
'Este enemigo no es en absoluto débil, ${PLAYER}. Estarás en peligro mientras conduces a Mordrambor hasta nuestra posición, y no podremos ayudarte; si nos revelamos demasiado pronto, todo estará perdido. Dile algo que despierte su curiosidad y lo haga seguirte... quizá que has encontrado un arma capaz de destruirlo. Dudará de que tal arma exista y te seguirá de buen grado para refutarlo. Que la fortuna te acompañe en esto, ${PLAYER}.'","'¿Por qué no habría de derribarte, ${RACE}?'\
\
La sonrisa burlona de Mordrambor vacila ligeramente cuando le dices que has llevado un poderoso artefacto al otro extremo de la calzada, uno que sellará su perdición. Casi de inmediato regresa.\
\
'Admiro tu valentía, aunque sea extremadamente insensata. Iré contigo a ver ese artefacto y te daré la muerte que parece que ansías.'","Tadan y sus compañeros Montaraces han ideado un plan para capturar a Mordrambor, uno de los lugartenientes Númenóreanos Negros de Amarthiel, mientras viaja desde Haudh Elendil con una escolta inusualmente reducida.","Habla con Tadan","El Montaraz Tadan está al final de la calzada, frente a Haudh Elendil.\
\
Tadan te espera para hablar contigo tras la captura de Mordrambor.","'Volvamos entonces a Tinnudir con nuestro prisionero. ¡Quizá por fin nuestra suerte esté empezando a cambiar!'","Enfréntate a Mordrambor en el extremo más alejado de la calzada"},
[7137]={"'Come, let us retire for now. Talking and thinking are more exhausting than a day's labour, when such heavy topics are underway.'","Sithric is enraged at Stanric's new defiance, but Stanric is determined to be strong","Gadda is outside of the Mead Hall at Stangard.","Talk to Stanric.","Talk to Stanric inside his house","Gadda points you to Stanric's house for a discussion away from unfriendly eyes and ears","'Sithric does not seem happy with my newfound zeal, eh? No matter; I endeavour to do all that you did and more to get Stangard back on its feet, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Sithric can go rot for all I care. You are welcome in Stangard any time, but I will venture to say that your work here is done!'","Gadda, Stanric, and Sithric are outside of the Mead Hall.","Stanric is in his household near the Mead Hall.","Talk to Gadda","Sithric has at last caught wind of your deeds on behalf of Stangard, and for some reason he is displeased....","'Come with me, ${PLAYER}. It is high time for change.'","'Sithric has his eye on us already. He grows suspicious whenever anyone he deems dangerous to his cause leaves his sight for long.'","Observe the confrontation between Sithric and Stanric","You tell Stanric about the good you were able to do with little effort, free of the restrictions of politics","Stanric seems determined to make a change","'My men have been coming to thank me for various good deeds you have done for them, traveller.\
\
'Please, tell me how you were able to do so much for us, for I wish to continue this trend after you leave.'","Tell Stanric of your methods and hear his thoughts","'Stanric wishes to speak with you in private, ${PLAYER}. He is inside of his house now.\
\
'Go on, there is little time. Unfriendly eyes are all around us.'","Stanric is inside of his house in Stangard, near the Mead Hall.","Follow Stanric outside","Talk to Stanric","Instance: Stanric's Stand","Gadda is outside of Stanric's house.","Stanric has gone outside.\
\
You should follow him."},
[7139]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Éowyn must not be defeated</rgb>","Nâdar can be found at the western edge of Entwade.\
\
You have encountered the leader of the White Hand forces in Entwade. You should defeat him.","'${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again!'\
\
'These wretched Orcs will trouble us no longer, but what of the others?'\
\
You speak of the forces you encountered in the south and east of Entwade.\
\
'Aye, that is heartening! We have slain all they mustered here, but we must secure the western flank.\
\
'Let us move swiftly, lest the White Hand gain the advantage!'","Ordgar has been defeated!","The gate of Entwade remains strong as the Orc force dwindles","Síric is in northern Entwade.\
\
You have discovered Síric and his men amidst slain White Hand forces. You should speak to Síric.","Inguc has been defeated!","Talk to Síric","Follow Éowyn to the western flank","DNT -- Players will not see","'The White Hand shall not trouble the Wade again, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'While Edric may never have those he lost back, I know he felt what he did was right and I trust his dedication to his duty. I hope this can bring some sense of closure to him.'","'It is as I feared! The White Hand have already begun their strike against Entwade.\
\
'We must move swiftly to aid Thane Edric's men in holding against the Enemy's forces.\
\
'Follow me, ${PLAYER}!'","<rgb=#FF0000>The Men of Entwade must not be defeated</rgb>","Magenred has been defeated!","Síric can be found in northern Entwade with Womar and Gifel.\
\
You should seek out Síric and aid him.","Talk to Anrad","Éowyn and the others can be found to the west.\
\
Éowyn is running toward the western flank of Entwade. You should follow her.","Agelman has been defeated!","Thane Edric's men can be found to the east of the Mead Hall of Entwade.\
\
You should aid Agelman and Éowyn in combat.","Éowyn has been defeated!","Aid Agelman and Éowyn in defending Entwade","Anrad has been defeated!","Anrad can be found at the gate of Entwade near the Sutcrofts.\
\
You have defended the southern flank of Entwade and should now secure the gate.","'You have come just in time, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'The Orcs are upon us, and we cannot allow them to raze the palisades!\
\
'We will slay any that make for the gate, but you must defeat those that attack the fence! Swiftly now!'","Follow Éowyn","Defeat Nâdar","Defeat Orcs attacking the palisades of Entwade","Éowyn is standing outside the Mead Hall of Entwade.\
\
You should speak to Lady Éowyn and drive the White Hand from Entwade.","Talk to Éowyn","Mordor Orcs can be found outside the gates of Entwade, hacking at the nearby fences.\
\
Anrad has asked that you slip past the Orcs at the gate and engage Orcs attacking the walls of Entwade.","Find Síric","Síric has been defeated!","Instancia: Pacificando el Vado","Éowyn can be found inside Entwade in eastern Kingstead.\
\
You have repelled the White Hand and brought some measure of peace to the Wade. You should now speak to Éowyn.","Éowyn can be found near the Mead Hall of Entwade.\
\
You should follow Éowyn.","Kenbert has been defeated!","'Come, let us return to Edoras.'","Gifel has been defeated!","Slain Orcs and Uruks litter the ground at Síric's feet","Hoping to cut down the White Hand invaders once and for all, Éowyn rides to Entwade with vengeance in her heart."},
[7141]={"Captain Garmund can be found just ahead of you, at the northern edge of the farmland.\
\
Garmund has asked you to help him repel many of the White Hand trespassers across the farmland.","You have helped drive the White Hand forces away","'Let us return to the outpost at the watch-tower. We cannot hope to regain the fields in such short time.'","Instancia: Juramentos prestados","Captain Garmund has organized an unexpected counter-attack against the Orcs who have sacked the farmlands outside of Cliving in the hopes of driving back some of the White Hand forces.","Talk to Garmund","'I am glad to have you with me, ${PLAYER}. Stay close and be ready to strike our foe.\
\
'Come. Let us see what these trespassers are made of!'"},
[7142]={"'There she stands, ${PLAYER}. Come, let us be done with this errand.'","Angbor can be found inside the Great Hall of Tumladen.\
\
You have arrived in the Great Hall and should now speak to Angbor.","Lady Terenis and Angbor can be found in the Great Hall of Tumladen.\
\
Lord Angbor is now speaking with Lady Terenis about the battle at Pelargir. You should listen to their conversation.","Talk to Angbor","'I know we have had disagreements, but you will honour Angbor's charge, won't you? I hope I did not make you wish to leave so soon!\
\
'I fear for the people of Lebennin, and your aid could prove invaluable!'","At the request of Aragorn, Lord Angbor has come to Tumladen to privately deliver a message of victory to Lady Terenis.","Follow Lord Angbor and Lady Terenis to the fireplace","Instancia: Juramento de Secreto","Lady Terenis and Angbor can be found in the Great Hall of Tumladen.\
\
You have arrived in the Great Hall with Angbor, and should now approach Lady Terenis.","'You will remain in Tumladen for a time, will you not?'","Listen as Lord Angbor and Lady Terenis speak","Lady Terenis can be found in the rear of the Great Hall of Tumladen.\
\
Lord Angbor has returned to the fields of Lebennin with his host, and has left you to aid Lady Terenis.","Approach Lady Terenis with Angbor","Talk to Lady Terenis","Lady Terenis and Angbor can be found in the Great Hall of Tumladen.\
\
You should follow Lady Terenis and Angbor to the fireplace in the rear of the Great Hall."},
[7143]={"Help Khagâmi","Investigate the sound you heard to the east","'${PLAYER}! When I spied the camp-fire, I did not expect to find you there, nor did I expect you to be under attack! It seems all is quiet now, though. Your friend looks quite shaken. I hope she is uninjured. Maybe you should see how she fares.\
\
'You are both welcome to join Rhadrog and I at our camp atop the hill. It is better hidden from foes and is also more defensible.'","'My apologies, when that man came out of nowhere, I just froze! I thought I would die just from the fright alone. Thank you for saving my life! And especially that archer.\
\
'Who is that? Do you know him? You spoke like old friends.'\
\
You tell her that you are indeed friends with him and you did not expect to see him in An Shêru.\
\
'I, for one, am quite glad you are both here! It seems I chose my travelling companion well.'","'${PLAYER}, I should tell you of my task and destination. I am on a quest to find an ancient dwarf city called Jiret-menêsh. Tales claim that it has been in An Shêru longer than the sun has been in the sky. It is well documented in the libraries of Zajâna that the Temámir were avid trading partners with Zajâna and others for centuries.\
\
'When Urash-zâl, the Din of Stone, shook the ground and dried the Usâl, the people of Zajâna had their own difficulties. It went unnoticed for some time that all contact with Jiret-menêsh had been lost. Most believe that the Temámir were either all killed or they abandoned this forsaken land, which is quite plausible.\
\
'However, there have recently been whispers that the hearty Dwarves of Jiret-menêsh have emerged from the ground, where they have been hiding in isolation for one hundred years. Doorward Azagâya sent me to investigate the rumours and see if this is true. Should it be so, I am to establish friendly relations with them, and if possible, negotiate terms of establishing trade between our cities.\
\
'Surely you can imagine being the first to... what was that?'\
\
You heard the unmistakable sound of a boot crunching gravel coming from east of the camp.","Bandits defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Khagâmi is tired from her travels west through An Shêru, and is ready to settle in for the night. Together, you have set up a camp-fire and made yourselves as comfortable as you are able to while on the road.","Instancia: Tomando un descanso","While you and Khagâmi were talking at the camp-fire, you both heard a suspicious sound from the east. You should investigate what it was.","While you and Khagâmi were talking at the camp-fire, you both fell under attack! You should help Khagâmi.","You received some unexpected help while defending your camp. You should talk to Faeron.","Khagâmi is tired from her travels west through An Shêru, and is ready to settle in for the night. By joining her at her camp-fire, you may learn something of her journey.","Defeat the remaining bandits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Faeron","Talk to Khagâmi","While you and Khagâmi were talking at the camp-fire, you both fell under attack! You should defeat the bandits.","Khagâmi is being attacked!"},
[7145]={"'Hold a moment, Isildur,' Gandalf interrupts. 'Cease thy story-telling!'","'I am not surprised you do not know of the Vandassari, for they were treasures brought from Númenor to Middle-earth by my father and brother, long ago. Seven only survived the realm's fall, but seven was enough, and indeed would prove to be too many. They were the Oath-stones, and they were set upon the borders of the kingdoms we founded, three in Arnor and four in Gondor, to make peace with the tribes that lived nearby.\
\
'These were the Oath-stones of Arnor: Helcessar of Forochel, pale blue. Tauressar of Rhudaur, pale green. Ambossar of Cardolan, red-brown.\
\
'These were the Oath-stones of Gondor: Landassar of Rhovanion, golden brown. Orossar of Erech, deep black. Airessar of Harad, clear crystal. Naldassar of Rhûn, white-silver.\
\
'There was a power in them, but it was Sauron's malice that turned vows sworn upon an Oath-stone into bonds of enslavement. He searched for the Vandassari, attempting to weaken our alliances and subvert them for his own ends. He found Airessar, the crystal Oath-stone my brother Anárion set atop the lighthouse of Calatirion at the harbour of Vëalondë, and with his dark arts he used it to compel the service of the Haradrim.\
\
'While we worked to assemble the Great Alliance, it was the Bright Company that journeyed to Umbar and broke Sauron's control over Airessar and the enslaved Haradrim. This ensured the Great Alliance need not contend with an army from the south when it reached Dagorlad, which might have proven insurmountable.'","'Was this the last of the interruptions I must endure? I will continue my tale, if all agree to still their tongues!'","Habla con Glorfindel","Lendelen is at Echad-in-Edhil.","The High Elves of the Bright Company undertake the most dangerous missions required by the Great Alliance.","Habla con Gandalf","Talk to Lendelen","Listen to the concerns of Gandalf","Glorfindel is at Echad-in-Edhil.","Talk to the shade of Isildur","'What brought they from the foundered land,' Gandalf murmurs quietly, 'over the flowing sea? Seven stars and seven stones and one white tree.'\
\
The Wizard shakes his head, and fixes you with his stern eyes.\
\
'I always believed the seven stones referred to by this Rhyme of Lore were the palantíri, the seeing-stones that Elendil brought from Númenor to these shores. Can it be that the palantíri were the stars of the rhyme, and the Vandassari were the stones? How can I not have known this, ${PLAYER}? What strange fog has clouded my knowledge on their account? And yet these Oath-stones have no place in my memory.'","'This way, my friend. Glorfindel will be glad to meet you, and he will hear my report. Whether this strange inaction of Sauron's servants will be as pleasing, I cannot say. I myself am troubled by it, but I do not lead the Bright Company. Glorfindel will know more than either of us, I expect!'","The shade of Isildur has been interrupted by Gandalf, and he is not happy about it.","Gandalf has interrupted the shade of Isildur's story-telling, bringing you back to the present situation on Tol Send.","Listen to the tale told by the shade of Isildur","Talk to Magoldir","Gandalf has interrupted the telling of Isildur's tale with a number of questions.","The shade of Isildur is on Tol Send.","Gandalf is on Tol Send.","'Why has the old man interrupted the telling of my tale? Does he desire to hear no more of it? It was only at your behest and his that I began to speak of this sorrowful time, and if he did not intend to let me finish it he should never have had me start!'","'Glorfindel speaks glowingly of my wisdom, but he boasts overmuch. I seek only the destruction of evil, and take no praise for myself. If there is glory to be had, divide it among every member of the Bright Company and give no greater a portion to one Elf or another. Yes, at the light-house of Calatirion I spoke the words that shattered Sauron's control over the Vandassar perched atop the tower, but I could not have reached it without the others of the company.\
\
'Give the praise to all or to none, dear Glorfindel. I think you seek to avoid your own share and give too much of it to others.'","'It is good to meet you, friend ${CLASS}, for in war all friendships must be prized. I am the captain of the Glánnothrim, the Bright Company, and we are tasked by High King Gil-galad to undertake some of the most dangerous missions on behalf of Elvenkind. You have not heard of us, I imagine? That is good, for none of us expect or desire glory. All we seek is the defeat of evil, wherever it lies. It lies now in Mordor.\
\
'We are few in number, but that does not cause us to shrink from danger. Rather does it cause us to rely upon our fellows, and draw courage from their strength. Meet you now Lendelen, closest and wisest of my counsellors. Watch him closely, for he shares our purpose but possesses more wisdom than any Elf I have known! He is my trusted confidant, and a dear friend.'","Magoldir is at Echad-in-Edhil.","Instancia: Cuentos de la Compañía Brillante"},
[7147]={"Jajax has returned to you at great speed. You are not the only sibling to have gotten into trouble!","Khôltekh has asked you for your name.","Wait for Jajax to return... and cause no trouble","Jajax has agreed to recount to you what happened to him and his brother Daxamat when the two of them sailed from Gondor to Umbar after the conclusion of the war.","Itûr has asked you to discreetly escape from Khôltekh through the northern exit of the courtyard.","'You have to go, Dax, before Khôltekh remembers you are here. Quietly, through the northern exit!'","Jajax has decided to look for information about what has happened in Umbar.","Jajax has arrived at a run!","Talk to Khôltekh in the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern","'Dax! This place is no longer safe for us! This Kindred of the Coins intends to imprison or put to death any freebooter and pirate that does not sail in support of them!\
\
'There's no time... we have to leave this city! Quickly, back to the ship!'","Escape through the northern exit of the courtyard","Talk to Itûr... quietly","You have returned to Umbar with your brother Jajax.","'What is your name? Daxamat?'\
\
Khôltekh nods idly, but behind his eyes you sense that he is paying very close attention to your face, and filing away your name for later consideration.\
\
'Some there are who lead, and some there are who follow. Even the Kindred of the Coins is subject to this rule, my new friend. Azagath the Sea-shadow prides himself on leading; he does so with aplomb. Rothog the Storm carries out the wishes of those who give the commands, and they are made stronger with every swing of his mighty fists, and every bite of his sharp teeth. Ask the Heirs of Castamir who attended the half-troll's last bout before the Sea-stone Mutiny about those teeth...'\
\
Khôltekh grins.\
\
'A private joke, Daxamat. But heed these words, for they are also true: the wisest of all is he who knows when to lead and when to follow. The wisest is he who knows when to speak, and when to listen. Which are you, my new friend? And who do you follow? The Heirs of Castamir? Or perhaps the Church of the All Seeing? This city has many foes, and sometimes they require some... rooting out. The uprising in Umbar was thorough... but Azagath has mused aloud that he sometimes wonders if it was thorough enough.'","Talk to Jajax in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl","Your friend Itûr has recognized you and called you over to him.","Jajax stands in the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern.","'Ah, it is good to be home! The sea-breeze welcomes us back to Umbar! My name may be spoken of all across the world already, but it will mean a little more to hear it spoken in the streets of our city. No doubt my exploits will earn us a tankard or two of ale in the Crab and Cutlass, or in the Teeming Net Tavern. You were always partial to the Hungry Deep, weren't you, Dax?\
\
'But we have work to do! The drinking will have to wait. But just a little while!'","Follow Jajax","Talk to Itûr in the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern","'Dax! I haven't seen you in an age! I thought you perished in the war... but you must have escaped that fate, somehow! I take it some portion of your brother's good fortune must have transferred to you? We could have used some of that here!\
\
'Were you in the battle? I heard the Corsairs who followed Balakhôr were slain by an army of Dead Men... and that they were led by the hated warrior Thorongil, who despised the Umbari so much he returned to life that he may slay even more! But that cannot be so. Still, there have been strange occurrences here in recent days, ever since the great earthquake that collapsed the Temple of the All Seeing. People say he is dead... if such a thing is possible. But the Empire of Ordâkh did not stand long against the uprising, and when the fighting ended the Kindred of the Coins announced that neither Sauron nor Ordâkh would rule again in Umbar.\
\
'The Kindred claim they have ushered in a new age, but for people like you and me, Dax, and like your brother... I do not know if they mean it. The gaols are full of thieves and Corsairs alike; no opponent of the Kindred lives long after voicing it. If they learn that you sailed with any Heir of Castamir...'","Talk to Jajax outside the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern","Jajax told you the city is not safe for the two of you, and you have to hurry back to your ship and escape!","Remain in the courtyard as your brother Jajax requested, and cause as little trouble as possible.","Instancia: Las aventuras de Jajax y Daxamat","Follow Jajax back to the ship... and quickly!","Your brother Jajax has asked you to follow him through the city.","Talk to Jajax in the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern","'Something about the city is different, Dax. Do you feel it too?\
\
'There are too many guards here. The Haradrim of Ordâkh seem to be gone, but in their place the guardsmen appear... more vigilant. What has happened to my City of Sails? I do not like this. Someone must answer for it... and they will answer to Jajax!'","Itûr has quietly caught your attention.","Wait in the courtyard for Jajax to return"},
[7148]={"Instancia: La emboscada","Talk to Dagoras north of Cirith Negen","Gimli is standing off the road north of Cirith Negen, waiting to attack the enemy ambushers.","You and the Rangers have turned the tables on the ambushers at Cirith Negen.","'The Rangers are in position, ${PLAYER}, and so too are the Elves. Now we just need someone to give the signal to attack.\
\
'Why don't you walk down the road behind Cirith Negen and let our enemies know they have been outmaneuvered? The time for stealth is over, now that we are ready to launch the attack!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not get too close to Cirith Negen before the Rangers are in position</rgb>","You have been spotted by the ambushers, and ruined the plan!","Survive combat until the Rangers can attack!","You have met up with Dagoras in the woods north of Cirith Negen.","Talk to Gimli north of Cirith Negen","Attack the Orc leader at Cirith Negen to signal the other Rangers","Your attack on the Orc leader at Cirith Negen will be the signal for Dagoras and the other Rangers to begin the full assault.","You need to survive until the Rangers can finish their attack!","'Let us return to Aragorn and report of our success.'","You have come with Legolas, Gimli, and a number of Rangers to the northern side of Cirith Negen in order to disrupt the Orc and Easterling ambush.","The tables have been turned!","'We have come the long way 'round Cirith Negen, ${PLAYER}, and now we are in position to surprise the Orcs and Easterlings before they can attack Aragorn's host.\
\
'We will descend upon them in full-throated fury, and send them screaming back to their own lands, or to death!'","'We have victory! The enemy has been dispersed, and will no longer pose a threat to the Host of the West!\
\
'Thank you for your heroism, ${PLAYER}! I must thank your friend Gimli as well, both for the swing of his axe and the stillness of his tongue during our approach. I know that dwarves enjoy to bellow, and keeping his quiet must not have been easy!\
\
'We have all done a service for Aragorn this day. I am glad to have made the road safe for the host.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Gimli must not be defeated!</rgb>","The Rangers have launched their attack!"},
[7149]={"Kyrstig has pointed out the first tomb on the left in Akhaldarâg as yours.\
\
You should enter the tomb.","Clear the tomb of Angmarim","Enter the dwarf-tomb","Talk to Kyrstig","'I have a bad feeling about this. We should get back to camp, and quickly!'","'I need your help over here! I found Loknashra! I can't defeat her by myself, but perhaps the two of us have a chance! Follow me!'","'Our first real mission without Ausma! Finally, a chance to show our mettle! When you're ready, we'll split up and hit all of these tombs at once, clearing out the Angmarim we find inside. This will only work if we clear them at the same time, or else some of the cultists might get away and warn the others. Once each of our tombs is cleared, we are to return to camp straight away! Everyone ready?'","The dwarf-tomb contains Angmarim possessed of evil intent.","The tomb has been cleared!","Confront Loknashra","Instancia: El ataque de los aprendices","Kyrstig waits to speak with you.","<rgb=#FF0000>The Scout Trio must survive!</rgb>","Scout-master Ausma has charged you and her three apprentices with dismantling the Angmarim forces in the Pit of Stonejaws.","It is time to confront Loknashra!","Kyrstig needs your help.","You should defeat the dwarf-wights in the tomb.","Defeat the Dwarf-wights"},
[7150]={"Estás de pie fuera de la brecha en la muralla este de Archet, al oeste del Refugio del Cazador.\
\
Debes evitar que los Montebruno capturen Archet.","Derrota a los Montebruno y a su líder","Habla con Jon Helecharroyo","Ned Pruner está gravemente herido y requiere asistencia.","'¡La plaza del mercado está a salvo por ahora, pero debemos seguir adelante! Si tardamos demasiado, ¡perderemos todo Archet!  \
\
'¡Debemos encontrar otra forma de entrar al centro del pueblo!'","'Amdir... Amdir está cerca. Escapó de la masacre en el Tejón. Tienes que ayudarlo... a defender el Tejón...\
\
'¡Esos Montebruno quieren al hobbit... y al Capitán. Yo... vi algo en las llamas... ¡ve tras ellos! ¡Debes salvarlos...!'","Archet está bajo ataque. Jon Helecharroyo y los otros cazadores han decidido entrar al pueblo por la Puerta Este. Debes avanzar y conocer el destino de Mundo, Celandine, Amdir y el Capitán Helecharroyo.","<rgb=#FF0000>Jon Helecharroyo ha caído</rgb>","<rgb=#00FF00>Has llegado a tiempo al Capitán Helecharroyo</rgb>","'¡Qué tragedia nos ha ocurrido esta noche! Pero derrotamos la amenaza de los Montebruno. Creo que pasará mucho tiempo antes de que se atrevan a ser tan audaces de nuevo, con o sin la ayuda de los malvados maestros de Angmar.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Has limpiado el área de los artesanos de enemigos</rgb>","Encuentra una manera de llegar al centro de Archet y encontrar a Amdir.\
\
Después de que derrotaste a los prisioneros, Ned Pruner te dijo que los bandidos Montebruno habían intentado invadir Archet por fin, y que Amdir ayudó a defender la posada. Amdir se puede encontrar en algún lugar adelante; deberías ayudarlo en la defensa de la Posada del Tejón Loco.\
\
Después de que Ned murió, su pobre esposa Peg vino a atender su cuerpo.","<rgb=#00FF00>Has derrotado a Calder Cob</rgb>","'No hay mucho tiempo que perder. ¡Ya el pueblo arde! Solo tenemos un corto tiempo para descansar aquí antes de que vean que hemos roto a través de la Muralla Este. Temo que estemos menos seguros por momentos....'","<rgb=#00FF00>Has limpiado la plaza del mercado de enemigos</rgb>","Con Archet a salvo, deberías hablar con Jon Helecharroyo.","<rgb=#00FF00>Has limpiado el patio de la cárcel de enemigos</rgb>","'Este es un día muy triste. Archet está quemado, mi padre está muerto y el Montaraz fue llevado por hombres malvados, si es que se les puede llamar hombres.  \
\
Ahora, todo lo que podemos hacer es esperar a que las llamas se apaguen. Entonces... con suerte, podremos comenzar a reconstruir nuestro pobre pueblo.'","'Tú has salido bien ${PLAYERNAME:parado[m]|parada[f]}, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, pero todo podría estar perdido de todos modos. Hemos protegido la plaza del mercado y el área de los artesanos. Ya The Mad Badger arde. Quizás mi padre aún esté vivo, pero... no tengo muchas esperanzas.\
\
'Síguenos a Atli y a mí. Defenderemos lo que queda de este pueblo hasta la muerte, si es necesario.'","Protege a Jon Helecharroyo","La plaza del mercado de Archet está bloqueada, y Jon Helecharroyo teme que llegues demasiado tarde. Quiere seguir adelante.","'Tienes que encontrar una manera de llegar al Badger. Los Montebruno están atacando cada rincón del pueblo. Rápido, ve a encontrar a Amdir y termina con estos Montebruno. Déjame con mi pobre Ned....'","Habla con Ned Pruner","Protege Archet derrotando la invasión de los Montebruno.\
\
Amdir fue incapacitado por la herida morgul que sufrió del Nazgûl, y ahora depende de ti salvar Archet de los Montebruno.","Instancia: El Asalto a Archet","'La traición de Calder Cob y Otto fue solo el comienzo de esta batalla, temo. Debemos encontrar una manera de llegar a la Posada del Tejón Loco. Peg nos ha dejado un camino hacia la plaza del mercado. ¡Quizás haya una forma de entrar por allí! ¡Sígueme!'","Llegaste demasiado tarde para salvar el área de los artesanos, pero puede que no sea demasiado tarde para salvar todo Archet."},
[7151]={"'I see that you are all here... and, I assume, ready to begin. Andras even brought his boy with him. I hope his wares fetch a price that is not embarrassing.\
\
'Shall we begin then?'","Talk to Bedwur","'It is commendable that you wish to aid the boy, but I must finish the other lots before we can discuss an arrangement.'","'The boy will pay his father's debt. Whether through the war-camps or the mines, I will get what is owed to me.'","Merchants of the Ox-clan gather frequently for auctions, where large amounts of goods -- and money -- trade hands.","Observe the auction","Many merchants have gathered here tonight.","Instancia: La Subasta"},
[7152]={"Defeat the goblins","Take part in the Finder's Gathering with Bergil and the other children.","Join the children at the table for the Finder's Gathering.","Join the Finder's Gathering","'Yes, I think we should leave. Let us ALL go back to the Old Guest-house now, and decide what to do after that.'","'I think Glatham is right in this, ${PLAYER}. Come, let us go - before any more goblins come in through that breach!'","Search for Glatham","'Glatham and I... we were coming back through the cisterns when suddenly there were goblins everywhere. And I thought… I could swear that there was a strange woman there. I saw no more. I ran.\
\
'I was certain Glatham was right behind me. But he wasn't. He is still in there with all those goblins.\
\
'You must come at once, ${PLAYER}. Please!'","The children's Gathering takes place in a back room of the Old Guest-house. Gifts, brought by all, are piled high on the table for all to enjoy.","By dispatching  the goblins near Glatham and the strange woman, you have caught the attention of the goblin captain.","You have come with Gelwen and Bergil to the cisterns. See if Gelwen can retrace her steps and to find her brother Glatham.","Talk to Gelwen","Gelwen has stumbled into the room, troubled and out of breath. Talk to her to find out what has happened.","Gelwen stands with Bergil, Glatham, and the mysterious woman near where the goblins came in.\
\
You have defeated the goblins who made a breach into this part of the cisterns and for the moment, it is safe. You should see what Gelwen has to say.","Take part in the Gathering","Defeat the goblin captain","'Now which way did I come? Yes, of course.'","You have found Glatham, surrounded by goblins! More goblins come in through a breach in the wall.","You have come with Gelwen and Bergil to the cisterns. Go with them and find Glatham.","Instancia: El banquete y la brecha"},
[7153]={"Instancia: La Batalla ante el Rammas Deluon","Derrota rápidamente a las hechiceras","Faelbenn ha sido derrotado","Recibe tus órdenes de Faelbenn.","Habla con Faelbenn","Previene que los baluartes caigan","'No hay nada más que hacer aquí... vámonos.'","'¡Este fue quizás el mayor golpe que hemos dado a Angmar! Esto muestra que se han debilitado, y pronto podría ser el momento de darles un golpe final.'","Hechiceras de Angmar derrotadas (${VALUE}/5)","Un baluarte ha caído","Tiempo expirado","Derrota a las hechiceras de Angmar (${VALUE}/5)","El Montaraz Faelbenn te ha pedido que le ayudes a derrotar a los refuerzos de Angmar que están cruzando el Rammas Deluon.","Derrota a las hechiceras de Angmar y evita que los refuerzos crucen el Rammas Deluon.","¡La victoria es tuya... deberías hablar de nuevo con Faelbenn de inmediato!","'¡Debemos apresurarnos, ${PLAYER}! Los refuerzos de Angmar están intentando cruzar el Rammas Deluon y se están reuniendo cerca de las diversas piedras. Desafortunadamente, no nos atrevemos a cruzar la línea de las piedras, ya que hay malvadas hechiceras suplicando a las piedras, haciéndolas más mortales de lo que hemos visto jamás.\
\
'Sin embargo, no todo es oscuro. Las hechiceras no pueden mantener su estado por mucho tiempo y su determinación flaqueará. En esos momentos, ¡debes atacar y derrotar a esas hechiceras!\
\
'No olvides sin embargo, si queremos mantener nuestro bloqueo del Rammas Deluon, nuestros baluartes deben mantenerse en pie, así que también debes ayudar en su defensa.'","Defiende a Faelbenn"},
[7154]={"You are a Lothlórien sentry, keeping watch over the Golden Wood. You should join your fellow sentry up ahead.","Follow the archers to the north-east, up the hill","Orc invaders have appeared in Lothlórien! Help defend the Golden Wood.","King Thranduil asked you to follow the archers to the north-east, up the hill.","Join your fellow archer to the east, and keep watch over Lothlórien","Instance: The Battle Under the Trees","Galadriel has used her powers to defeat the last of this Orc assault. Now she wishes to talk to you.","You have arrived in Mirkwood. You have crossed paths with Lord Thranduil himself, and should talk with him.","You have come to a hilltop in Mirkwood held by Elves and embattled on all sides.","You have arrived in Mirkwood and come to the edge of the fighting.","Talk to Thranduil on the hilltop","Defend Lothlórien from Orcs and trolls","'From Lothlórien you come? Then hope yet glimmers. Your aid is most welcome here.\
\
'I will move on with my retinue, but you are needed ahead, up the hill! Follow the archers to battle! Perhaps we will meet again, when the fighting is done!'","To the east, you see King Thranduil ride up on his mighty steed","Push onward to the east and defeat the Orc-invaders","Defeat Orc-invaders in Mirkwood by the lamp-posts in the wood","Defeat every attacking enemy on the hilltop. This is the last stand!","Habla con Galadriel","You have crossed paths with Lord Thranduil once again in Mirkwood.","<rgb=#FF0000>Thranduil has been defeated</rgb>","'You, however, have done your part, and I thank you. Return to your Lord and Lady and have them know that I would share in their council regarding Dol Guldur, as soon as it is safe to do so.'","'You are needed in Mirkwood. I fear they will need all the aid that we can spare. Go now.'","Orc invaders have appeared in Lothlórien! Push onward to where the fighting appears worst.","Orc invaders have appeared in Lothlórien and now Lady Galadriel has taken to the field. Fight by her side and guard her at all costs.","'We have driven them back! You fought bravely, soldier.\
\
'Nay, do not pursue them. Too many of our kin have fallen this day, and we must restore our strength in case they strike at us yet again.'","Head east and protect Galadriel while she readies her defences","Thranduil relata las pruebas que el Bosque Negro y Lothlórien soportaron mientras Gondor marchaba y luchaba a las puertas de Mordor.","Head east and talk to King Thranduil"},
[7155]={"Defiende Aughaire de los asaltos de Angmar.","Firingal ha sido derrotado","Instancia: La Batalla por Aughaire","Evita las derrotas de los Trév Gállorg (${VALUE}/8)","Defiende a Firingal","Defiende todos los baluartes de Aughaire","Aughaire ha sido defendida","'¡Debemos apresurarnos, ${PLAYER}! El ejército de Angmar está cerca.\
\
'Debemos proteger todos los baluartes de Aughaire o no podremos defender la ciudad. Cuando suene la alarma, ve a ayudar a defender ese baluarte. Yo vigilaré la Puerta de Aughaire por si alguien se cuela entre nuestras defensas.\
\
'¡Ve ahora y defiende al buen pueblo de Aughaire!'","Has acompañado al montaraz Firingal a Aughaire para defender el pueblo contra los asaltos de la horda de Mordirith.","Uno de los baluartes de Aughaire ha caído","Habla con Firingal","Los Trév Gállorg han caído (${VALUE}/8)","'¡Rápido, volvamos a Gath Forthnír a ver si nos necesitan en otro lugar!'","Deberías informar a Firingal.","'¡Has luchado gloriosamente, ${PLAYER}! Hemos defendido Aughaire y derrotado a las fuerzas de Angmar. ¡Siento que la marea está cambiando contra Mordirith!'","Defiende Aughaire","Habla con Firingal sobre la defensa de Aughaire."},
[7157]={"Belvagor ha sido derrotado","'Hemos llegado, ${PLAYER}, y parece que los orcos aún no han iniciado su ataque. ¡Bien! Tenemos un momento para planear. Más arriba en la colina están los tres pasos que dan acceso al Bosque de Oro: el Paso Norte, el Paso Oeste y el Paso Este; algunos de mi gente ya han ido a defenderlos.\
\
Viaja a cada paso y observa las habilidades de los elfos en cada lugar: combate cuerpo a cuerpo, combate a distancia o sanación. Después regresa y dinos a mí y a mis compañeros dónde posicionarnos.\
\
Cuando los tres tengamos órdenes, podréis llevar las Banderas de Lórien a los cuatro campamentos orcos. Solo cuando una bandera esté cerca de un campamento podrás destruir el ídolo del Enemigo.'","Un paso ha sido sobrepasado","Belvagor y sus dos amigos esperan órdenes en la ladera que asciende hacia Fanuidhol.\
\
Belvagor y sus dos amigos esperan que les indiques qué pasos deben defender. Para ello, primero debes viajar al Paso Norte, Paso Oeste y Paso Este y observar la composición de los defensores en cada uno; entonces podrás tomar una decisión informada.","Ídolos del Enemigo destruidos (${VALUE}/4)","Ordena a los elfos a los pasos que consideres necesarios (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","¡El ataque de los orcos está en marcha! Debes trabajar junto a tus aliados para llevar una Bandera de Lórien a los cuatro campamentos orcos para que el ídolo del Enemigo en cada uno pueda ser destruido, y debes hacerlo antes de que cualquiera de los tres pasos sea sobrepasado.","Defiende todos los pasos de los orcos","Has destruido cuatro ídolos del Enemigo y ahora deberías regresar para hablar con Belvagor en el paso que le indicaste que defendiera.","Defiende a Belvagor","Belvagor se encuentra en la base de la ladera que asciende hacia Fanuidhol.\
\
El elfo Belvagor está esperando hablar contigo sobre su plan para repeler el ataque de los orcos.","No repeliste a los orcos a tiempo","Instancia: La Batalla de Lórien","Los orcos de Moria han comenzado su asalto a Lothlórien, y depende de ti, tus aliados y un pequeño grupo de elfos repelerlos.","Habla con Belvagor","Destruye los ídolos del Enemigo (${VALUE}/4)","'¿Estás listo para abandonar este campo de batalla, ${PLAYER}?'","'¡Los orcos se retiran! El Bosque de Oro está a salvo, por ahora. No podemos descansar mucho tiempo, ¡pero hoy nos has ayudado a alcanzar la victoria!'","El tiempo es esencial"},
[7158]={"Defiende los baluartes de los Pueblos Libres","Habla con Tordoron","Deberías hablar con Tordoron sobre tu victoria.","'¡Somos victoriosos, ${PLAYER}! La plaga de Angmar se está derrumbando... no pasará mucho tiempo, creo, antes de que la Corona de Hierro sea derrotada...'","¡Tiempo agotado!","Reclama todos los campamentos de Angmar (${VALUE}/4)","Defiende a Tordoron","'¿Estás ${PLAYER:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}, ${PLAYER}? ¡Bien! Entonces, ¡vámonos!\
\
'Debemos reclamar todos los campamentos de Angmar o seremos obligados a retirarnos.'","'Partamos ahora, ${PLAYER}.'","¡Tordoron ha sido derrotado!","Reclama rápidamente todos los campamentos","¡Un baluarte ha caído!","Instancia: La Batalla de Rhunendin","El montaraz Tordoron ha pedido tu ayuda para asaltar las fuerzas de Angmar en Rhunendin.","Hable con Tordoron para recibir sus órdenes de marcha."},
[7159]={"Una barricada ha sido superada","Evita que una barricada sea superada","Evita que Brogur sea derrotado","'Las barricadas están preparadas y mis enanos están listos. Todo lo que queda por hacer ahora es esperar a que lleguen los orcos.\
\
'Te pediría que sigas el flujo de la batalla y ayudes donde más se te necesite. Además, no olvides desplegar los estandartes de Khazad-dûm. Pueden ayudar a inspirar a todos los Pueblos Libres a grandes hazañas e incluso pueden ayudar a cambiar el rumbo de la batalla. Sin embargo, no las uses a la ligera, ya que una vez desplegada, la fuerza de una bandera se gasta.\
\
'Prepárate, porque me temo que no pasará mucho tiempo ahora...'","El líder del asalto contra el Camino Profundo ha entrado en batalla. Elimina a este Orco para reclamar la victoria.","Deberías hablar con Brogur para ver de qué ayuda podrías ser en la próxima batalla.","Has viajado al Camino Profundo para ayudar a defenderlo. Sigue las órdenes de Brogur para ayudar a los Enanos de Moria a resistir.","'No hay nada más que hacer aquí, así que deberíamos irnos. ¿Tienes todo preparado para marcharte?'","Derrotados Horngoth y sus secuaces","Brogur ha sido derrotado","Derrota a Horngoth y sus secuaces","'Ha sido una batalla gloriosa, ${PLAYER}. ¡Una que será recordada durante mucho tiempo! Los orcos pensaron que podrían recurrir a artimañas para ganar ventaja, pero no han sido capaces de resistir ante nuestro poder combinado.\
\
'¡Ahora, terminemos nuestros asuntos aquí y veamos qué más podemos hacer para repeler a estos inmundos orcos!'","Ayuda a defender el Camino Profundo contra el asalto de Mazog.","Habla con Brogur","Defiende el Camino Profundo","Instancia: La batalla del Camino Profundo","Con Horngoth derrotado, la batalla del Camino Profundo ha sido ganada. Habla con Brogur para ver qué más quiere que hagas."},
[7160]={"The men are disorganized and in chaos, and Grimbold wants to gather them together for one last stand.","Instance: The Battle of the Ford, Afternoon","'We are doing well, ${PLAYER}! Every second we give to Prince Théodred is a second unwasted! So long as we stand, Rohan stands with us!'","You have come down the road in retreat with Grimbold, and he has put up his hand to stop you.","'A thousand curses upon Saruman! He sent a second force of uruks to the Ford on the other side of the river! We have to get back to the Prince at once! Without Cadda at the Ford, Prince Théodred cannot drive them off with the few men he has in his party!'","Fight off the attacking forces in order to buy Théodred precious time to retreat","'This is far enough, ${PLAYER}! Let us turn and face our pursuers! We must give Prince Théodred some time to move further south!'","Théodred's host has been driven back from the gates of Isengard in disarray, and pockets of Rohirrim are fighting for their lives as they retreat.","You have retreated further down the road and are once more embroiled in the fighting. You must buy Théodred as much time as you can!","A rider has brought disturbing news: a second force of uruks has left Isengard in secret and has driven the defending force at the Ford of Isen back into Rohan.","Grimbold has fought off his opponent and wants to speak with you while he catches his breath.","'We cannot die here! We have to get back to the Ford at once to save Prince Théodred! He will be caught between the hammer and the anvil of Saruman!'","'They will be on us in moments, ${PLAYER}. Let me gather the men about us and ready them for this last assault.'","Talk to Grimbold"},
[7161]={"You have returned with as much haste as you can to the Ford of Isen and must now try to save Prince Théodred from the forces of Saruman.","'${PLAYER}! I thought we would not meet again. The old man was not pleased to lose you as his guest, and he was very cross with Morflak. But in his wisdom he sent me forth to gain his forgiveness, and with a simple mission!'","Confront Morflak","'Death to the forces of Saruman! Death to them all! Quickly, ${PLAYER}, we must get to the water's edge and see what has happened to the Prince!'","Morflak's attention is drawn to the eastern bank of the Ford, but before you can take advantage of his inattention, you are yourself rooted to the spot with wonder.\
\
A line of riders has come from Rohan, and the courage of the uruks melts away as the Rohirrim prepare to charge.","In the eastern distance, you hear a horn blowing from far away","Talk to Morflak","Grimbold needs you to fight alongside him to where Théodred is suffering the fierce attacks of Saruman's forces.","Instance: The Battle of the Ford, Sunset","You have come to the eyot in the middle of the river Isen and have found the uruk Morflak gloating over Théodred's fallen form.","Talk to Grimbold","Prince Théodred is in trouble on the eyot in the middle of the Isen! You need to fight alongside Grimbold to come to the aid of the Prince!","'There is no time, ${PLAYER}! Prince Théodred is beset on all sides! We have to cross the river and break through the ring that surrounds him!'","Talk to Grimbold on the bank of the Isen"},
[7162]={"Una barricada ha sido superada","Ayuda a mantener la Sala Vigesimoprimera contra el asalto de Mazog.","Repliégate y defiende la Cámara de Mazarbul","Repliégate y defiende las barricadas de la sala","Una vez más, los zapadores trasgos han destruido las barreras en las barricadas. Wíli ha ordenado una retirada a la Cámara de Mazarbul.","Defiende la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Cámara de Mazarbul defendida","Habla con Wíli","Defiende a Wíli","Has viajado hasta la Vigésimo Primera Sala para participar en su defensa.¡Sigue las instrucciones de Wíli y ayuda a los enanos de Moria!","'¡Los orcos de Mazog casi nos tienen, ${PLAYER}! Sus trucos viles casi nos llevan a la perdición. Afortunadamente, con tu fuerza, pudimos hacer nuestra defensa aquí, en la Cámara de Mazarbul.\
\
'Quizás después de nuestra victoria Mazarbul ahora sea conocido por algo más que ser el lugar donde Ori y muchos otros valientes enanos encontraron su fin. Quizás sea conocido como el lugar donde la recuperación de Moria realmente comenzó.'","Los zapadores trasgos han destruido las barreras en las barricadas de la Sala Vigesimoprimera. Wíli ha ordenado una retirada a la sala que da a la Cámara de Mazarbul.","Instancia: La Batalla de la Sala Vigesimoprimera","'No creo que haya nada más que podamos hacer aquí, ${PLAYER}. ¿Vamos?'","'Nuestras defensas están en orden. Ahora debo decirte el papel que vas a jugar en la próxima batalla.\
\
'Te pediría que ayudes a las barricadas cuando estén bajo asalto y asegures que se mantengan. Si incluso una barricada es superada, todo estará perdido. Afortunadamente, hay muchas banderas de enanos para nosotros. Estas banderas pueden sacar el coraje y la fuerza que se encuentra en los corazones de todos e inspirarlos. Despliega estos estandartes, ${PLAYER}, cuando las cosas parezcan más desesperadas. Podrían cambiar el rumbo de la batalla.\
\
'Esas son mis órdenes, camarada. Ahora debemos esperar y esperar que podamos respirar otro día.'","Evita que una barricada sea superada","Habla con Wíli para ver qué ayuda puedes prestar en su defensa.","Con los orcos expulsados, habla con Wíli para ver si hay algo más que quiera que hagas.","Wíli ha sido derrotado"},
[7163]={"Defiende a Stóthkell","La Vía de los Herreros ha sido defendida","Enanos derrotados (${VALUE}/8)","Stóthkell ha sido derrotado","Habla con Stóthkell","Evita que los enanos sean derrotados (${VALUE}/8)","'Estoy mortificado, ${PLAYER}. ¡Mi orgullo casi nos cuesta la pérdida de Zigilburk! Si no fuera por ti y tus compañeros, no habríamos resistido este día.\
\
Te doy las gracias de todo corazón. Eres ${PLAYER:un verdadero amigo[m]|una verdadera amiga[f]} de los enanos.'","Habla con Stóthkell para ver qué ayuda puedes prestar en la defensa.","Sigue a Stóthkell para descubrir qué es lo que hace temblar la Vía de los Herreros.","Una forja ha caído","Sigue a Stóthkell","'Poco más podéis hacer ya aquí, ${PLAYER}. ¿Deseáis marcharos conmigo?'","Ayuda a defender la Vía de los Herreros contra el asalto de Mazog.","'Ah, me temo que has perdido el tiempo viniendo aquí, ${PLAYER}. Con la puerta cerrada, no tendremos problemas con los orcos. Esos tontos no tienen ninguna posibilidad de forzar esta puerta.\
\
¡Me encantaría ver la cara de Amukh ahora mismo! Amukh es un trasgo que ha fabricado muchas espadas para sus amos orcos, y se jacta de que su trabajo es tan bueno como el de los enanos. ¡El tonto incluso pensó en reclamar estas obras de los enanos para sus propios fines malvados! ¡Mientras yo respire, eso nunca sucederá!'","Instancia: La batalla de la Vía de los Herreros","Has viajado a la Vía de los Herreros para ayudar en su defensa. Sigue las indicaciones de Stóthkell y ayuda a los Enanos de Moria a resistir el ataque.","Defiende la Vía de los Herreros","Evita que una forja caiga","Con los orcos expulsados, habla con Stóthkell para ver si hay algo más que quiera que hagas."},
[7164]={"'This is the passage my sister discovered. Judging from the air in here, few have come this way, but there has been no sign of Tatháta elsewhere in Kamrabezûr. If we can trust the words of the unseen ones, the Terâsi, she may have fled to this forgotten corner and gone into hiding.\
\
'I told Sigileth to wait, but she has gone ahead. Let us catch up to her, and quickly.'","Talk to Cruel Dancer and hear her last request","Galatâni lies dying in the moonlight.","Cruel Dancer shakes her head, but the motion causes her great pain and she winces.\
\
'I was the... deadliest woman... in all these lands, ${PLAYER}. But my luck... my fortunes... they have abandoned me. Did it happen... when I killed the Blade-twist? Ever since then I have had ill fortune. I never... considered... that Tatháta might possess... such power...'\
\
The dying woman gathers what remains of her strength.\
\
'I want to confess to you something, ${PLAYER}. Will you... bring me into the sunlight? I have spent... too long in darkness... too long as Cruel Dancer. I would be Galatâni again... instead.'","Stand your ground!","Exhausted by her tale and the loss of so much blood, Galatâni falls silent","'Yes, we can do as she asks. But I do not think she has very long left to her, ${PLAYER}. She may not survive the journey aboveground.\
\
'Still... we will make the attempt.'","Galatâni remained silent during the journey, preserving her strength","Corudan stands in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.","Galatâni asked that you bring her outside into the sunlight before she dies.","Follow Corudan and Sigileth down the forgotten passage","Instancia: La Bestia de Abajo","Talk to Corudan in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr","The rampaging beast escapes into greater Kamrabezûr and is gone","Corudan stands in a forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.","Listen to what befell Cruel Dancer when she caught up to Tatháta in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.","'I think we found the creature that escaped from the arena, ${PLAYER}. Let us hope it does no harm to the folk who dwell within Umbar-môkh!\
\
'We will hunt it later. For now let us continue on in search of our true quarry!'","Cruel Dancer lies dying in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.","You have accompanied Corudan and Sigileth into a forgotten passage in the depths of Kamrabezûr, the vaults beneath Umbar Baharbêl, in search of Tatháta.","Bring Galatâni into the sunlight before she dies","'She is gone. We should make a place for her here. Let us find stones with which to mark the grave before the sun rises.'","Talk to Galatâni in the moonlight","A dying Umbari woman lies in a pool of her own blood","'I hear movement ahead of us. Ready yourself!'","Talk to Corudan in the forgotten passage","Galatâni has one more thing to say to you.","Hear what Galatâni has left to say","The passage shakes as a mighty beast charges toward you and your friends down the forgotten passage!","Despite the appearance of the rampaging beast, Corudan and Sigileth have not abandoned their purpose to investigate the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.","Talk to Sigileth in the forgotten passage","Galatâni does not have much time to live.","Stand with Galatâni and observe her final moments","The woman blinks up at you through bloodshot eyes and her face is familiar. You have found Cruel Dancer.\
\
'${PLAYER}...' she manages, weakly. 'I do not have much... time... left to me...'","Sigileth waits for you and Corudan in the forgotten passage.","Listen to Cruel Dancer's story","'What bounties could be more dangerous... than those placed by Saklaphêl... on the Kindred of the... of the...'\
\
Frustration and sadness war upon her face as she lies dying in the moonlight.\
\
'If only... I could have chosen a different road. But that was... not to be. In my heart, I was... always... Hazêphen.'\
\
Galatâni's voice is little more than a whisper now.\
\
'Tatháta... kept me alive... for days... ${PLAYER}. With her terrible, secret power... she could have slain me... easily. But she had... she had questions. Questions about... you, ${PLAYER}...'","Judging from the quantity of blood spilled on the floor of this chamber, the Umbari woman does not have long to live.","Galatâni laughs weakly, a thin sound in the silence of the Umbari night.\
\
'It was too much to hope for sunlight... I suppose,' she murmurs.\
\
'I was not always as I am, ${PLAYER}. I was like you... an adventurer-for-hire, accomplishing the small tasks... that needed doing. It was a simple life, but a good one. There was food on the table for my husband, Jedûth, and my daughter Ashenâth. But it... did not last.\
\
'My husband was accused... of stealing a vase from a wealthy nobleman, a man called Phirasâkh. He did not! I know he did not... but he was slain for the crime. I had to take on even more dangerous tasks to support my Ashenâth... even murder. That paid the finest of all, ${PLAYER}, but the first victim of my knife was the sweetest: Phirasâkh, the nobleman who falsely-accused my Jedûth. He deserved the death I gave to him.\
\
'But I did not stop at Phirasâkh, for I had tasted the deadly nectar of death. I was away for longer and longer at a time; I told myself the coins I gave my neighbours to watch my daughter Ashenâth were all for her benefit. The name \\qGalatâni\\q no longer applied to me, for I had grown hard, and cold. I was now Hazêphen, \\qCruel Dancer,\\q and I delighted in the slaughter. Phirasâkh had deserved death. But he would not be the last, and some who died at the hands of Cruel Dancer deserved it less than he. Many did.\
\
'It was best for Ashenâth that her mother remain only a memory... for I had grown addicted to... the danger, ${PLAYER}, and the sight of the blood I spilled. It had... become an obsession.'\
\
She falls silent for a long moment, and you wonder if her life has ended, but then she coughs and sputters back to awareness.\
\
'The city was not a place of safety... in those years. The Church of the All-Seeing saw its... enemies everywhere. The neighbours who watched after my daughter were taken in sacrifice to the Mâkhda Khorbo, and their home burned. On that day Ashenâth joined her father, but when I returned to the burned frame that had been a home there was no vengeance to be had. The Dark Lord worshipped by the Church of the All-Seeing was not like... not like Phirasâkh. I could not be certain He even lived, and if He did not live... could He be slain?\
\
'I preyed upon the Church for a time, often for free, but when my coins ran out I had few choices left to me. I stopped returning to the burned husk where once I lived with my Jedûth and my Ashenâth. I only felt alive when I competed with other bounty-hunters for the most dangerous work I could find.'","Talk to the dying Umbari woman"},
[7165]={"'${PLAYER}! Surely you must recognize those items! That's Frodo's mail-shirt, the one he had from Bilbo! The grey cloak has an elven-brooch pinned to it, like the one I had from Lórien. And that's Sam's sword, or I'm a Boffin!\
\
'How did this terrible Messenger come to have those items, ${PLAYER}? What happened to Frodo and Sam?'\
\
You silence Pippin with a look, but he is crestfallen and his outburst cannot be taken back.","Instancia: La Puerta Negra","Collect the short-sword","The Mouth of Sauron has presented tokens for the perusal of the company.","Collect the mithril-shirt","Stand with the Host of the West in defiance of Mordor","Collect the Elf-cloak","You have taken the items that belonged to Frodo and Sam, and Gandalf has defied the Mouth of Sauron.","'All is still and silent, but I do not trust this emptiness. Do not be fooled by the quiet! There are eyes upon us, though we see them not.\
\
'Let us ride nearer, and I will call for Sauron's surrender.'","The Mouth of Sauron mocks the Host of the West, and prepares the terms of Aragorn's surrender. Remain alert.","Aragorn is at the Morannon, the Black Gate of Mordor, and prepares to challenge Sauron.","Mithrandir asked you to retrieve the items presented by the Mouth of Sauron.","Stand with Aragorn as he defies the Mouth of Sauron","The Mouth of Sauron smiles with cruelty and avarice","Mithrandir has asked for you to speak with him while he considers Sauron's terms.","On the very doorstep of Mordor, Aragorn commands Sauron to come forth and surrender.","Talk to Pippin and keep him quiet","'Steel your heart for the trials ahead, ${PLAYER}. That Sauron has either Frodo or Samwise in captivity seems certain, but you must have noticed, as I have, that this Messenger speaks only of one prisoner, not of two.\
\
'And yet, those items are unmistakable and were in the possession of both our hobbits. I do not want this vile Messenger to keep them. I will distract him, ${PLAYER}, and I want you to retrieve these items in memory of our friends.'","Aragorn has decided to call for the surrender of Sauron, and wishes for you to stand with him.","Listen to the demands of the Mouth of Sauron","Talk to Aragorn outside the Black Gate","Mithrandir has asked you to make Pippin hold his tongue lest he endanger the negotiations with the Mouth of Sauron.","Talk to Mithrandir","Stand with Aragorn as he defies the Dark Lord Sauron"},
[7166]={"Instancia: La Espada que Fue Quebrada","'Sé que Aragorn ha esperado durante mucho tiempo que esta noche llegara y temía que no lo hiciera. ¡Por fin, la espada ha sido reforjada!'","En las fraguas de Rivendel, los herreros élficos de Elrond trabajan arduamente rehaciendo la espada de los reyes.\
\
Los herreros élficos han comenzado la labor de reforjar a Narsil.","Aragorn está en las fraguas de Rivendel.\
\
Aragorn desea hablar contigo.","'Regresemos a la Casa de Elrond. Muchos amigos esperan dentro, y quiero mostrarles a Andúril para que sepan lo que se ha logrado esta noche.'","'¡A duras penas puedo creer que Narsil haya sido forjada de nuevo, pero sentir a Andúril en mi mano acalla toda duda! Esta noche ha tardado mucho en llegar, ${PLAYER}, ¡y me maravillo ante ella!'","Aragorn está esperando para hablar contigo justo afuera de las fraguas de Rivendel.\
\
Los herreros élficos están reforjando a Narsil, la espada que fue quebrada.","Sé testigo de la reforja de Narsil","Los herreros élficos de Elrond han comenzado a reforjar a Narsil, la espada que fue quebrada, reliquia de los herederos de Elendil.","'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}, ${PLAYER}? El aire esta noche se siente lleno de promesas, y he decidido dejar atrás cualquier duda. Que Narsil sea reforjada esta noche me parece irreal, como si fuera a despertar en la Casa de Elrond y descubrir que todo ha sido un sueño.'"},
[7167]={"You have come outside with your companions to see what has happened.","Watch the mighty force leaving Balewood","'We should go back inside and bring what people we can out here to see this sight, ${PLAYER}. Who can say when such a marvel will be seen again?'","Relax around the fire with your companions","Nona has leapt to her feet, and wants to see what you think of the rumbling sound.","Talk to Nona inside the cave","You have earned a moment's rest with your friends while you wait to see if Leaflock will come through with the aid Corudan thinks you have earned.","Your companions are transfixed by the sight. Only Corudan can manage the words to describe it.","'Leaflock has done as we hoped he would, ${PLAYER}. He has sent Huorns to seek Núrzum. Will they prevail against him? I cannot say, but I know this: my heart is stirred by their march!\
\
'They seem so different from you or I, and from Horn or Nona, so far removed from the daily worries of Men or Elves. But still they march for us against the evil of Núrzum, against the evil of Saruman.\
\
'Even now Leaflock and his herd have not retreated so far from Middle-earth as to abandon its people. It is worth remembering.\
\
'It seems our friends have remembered something as well, ${PLAYER}. I told you it would happen, did I not? I am certain I did.'","Instancia: El florecimiento","Talk to Corudan on the slope outside the cave","A mighty force of Huorns are leaving the Balewood. They can have only one destination: Núrzum!","Join Nona outside the cave","<rgb=#FF0000>Sit</rgb> by the fire with your companions","Your companions are sitting around the fire in Nona's cave, and you should do the same. Simply <rgb=#FF0000>sit</rgb> by the fire and relax while you can.","You suddenly hear a low rumbling from outside the cave!","Your companions are relaxing around the fire in Nona's cave, having earned a small, and overdue, respite.","'${PLAYER}, what do you think makes that sound? Is it Núrzum? Has he found this cave at last? We must see what has happened outside!'"},
[7168]={"Habla con Mílgamel","'Ese es el relato. Ahora debes comprender por qué insisto tanto en que la Anarlossë sea recordado tal como fue, y no como pretende un maestro de hierbas lejano.'","Haerandel desea hablarte de días muy lejanos, cuando él y su hermano Edlothon caminaban entre los Anarlossë que florecían en las tierras de los Hombres.","Nethlas da más crédito a las palabras de su maestro que a las de Haerandel, y no tiene reparo en decirlo.","Haerandel desea hablarte de la flor legendaria Anarlossë, desaparecida desde hace mucho de la Tierra Media.","Escucha el relato de Haerandel sobre la legendaria Anarlossë","Haerandel te ha hablado de la Anarlossë, la flor legendaria.","'Si esas flores altas fueron realmente plantadas por los Hombres del Oeste por toda la Tierra Media, ¿dónde están ahora? El Anorloth crece en muchos lugares, pero no he visto las flores que describes en Gondor. ¡Ni siquiera en Ithilien! Si no eres un mentiroso, quizá seas un necio, ¡y yo no deseo ser ninguna de las dos cosas!'","Instancia: Las Flores de Anarlossë","'No, tienes razón, Nethlas. No he obtenido este conocimiento mediante el estudio, o al menos no por el estudio de viejos libros o las enseñanzas de un maestro de hierbas.'","Mílgamel tiene algunas preguntas sobre el relato de Haerandel.","Habla con Nethlas","'No digo que crea lo que afirma este Elfo, ${PLAYER}..... pero me ha dado mucho en qué pensar.'","Habla con Haerandel","'Son muchas las variedades de flores que brotan en las Tierras Imperecederas, lejos del alcance de mortales, jamás vistas por hombre, enano o hobbit. Los Elfos las conocen por canto o por relato, aunque no siempre por la vista, y ese conocimiento nos trae alegría o tristeza, según el día.\
\
'Pero algunas flores llegaron a crecer en tierras distantes. La Anarlossë fue una de ellas, y floreció en abundancia en Númenor, allende el mar. Era alta, como los Hombres de aquella tierra, y al crecer se volvía hacia el este, hacia el sol naciente, coronada con la luz de la mañana.'","'Todo estudiante de historia conoce el relato de Elendil y su huida de Númenor, y que trajo consigo plantas y retoños de linaje alto y bajo a la Tierra Media. Pero si ordenó que se plantase la Anarlossë allí donde los suyos se asentaron, ¡entonces debería seguir creciendo en abundancia! Por eso mi antiguo maestro creía que el Anorloth era su verdadero descendiente, y no puedo decir que esté en desacuerdo.\
\
'¿Cómo ha llegado Haerandel a conocer la historia de esta flor?'"},
[7169]={"'¿${PLAYERNAME:Preparado[m]|Preparada[f]} para marcharnos? Ha sido un ejercicio excelente, ¡y me alegra que hayamos aguantado sin problema!'","'¡Buena suerte, ${PLAYER}! ¡Te estaré animando!'","'¡Se acabó la mala vida! ¡No me volverás a ver, te lo aseguro!'","Basil y tú habéis sobrevivido a la traición de Sprunt","'Sí, sí, eres fuerte, eso es cierto. ¡Te querría en mi banda si no fuera por ese afán de ser tan \\qdecente\\q !'","'¡Se acabó lo de esta banda, ya verás! ¡Dejaré atrás esta mala vida!'","Bsilio Resinas está en el Círculo de Duelo de Ost Forod.\
\
Basilio Resinas y tú habéis superado con éxito la traición de Cuthbert Sprunt. Deberías hablar con Basilio de inmediato.","Habla con Basil Resinas","Cuthbert Sprtun ha ofrecido una recompensa por tu cabeza y has decidido desafiarlo a un combate singular para que la retire.","Instancia: El cazarrecompensas","Basilio Resinas ha ido contigo al Círculo de Duelo en Ost Forod.\
\
Basilio Resinas te espera para hablar contigo dentro del Círculo de Duelo.","Te enfrentas en combate singular con Cuthbert Sprunt en el Círculo de Duelo.\
\
Basilio Resinas supervisa el combate para asegurarse de que Cuthbert no haga trampas.","'¡Me reformaré a partir de ahora! ¡Mis días de criminal han terminado!'","'¡Continúa, ${PLAYER}! ¡No te rindas, yo estoy contigo!'","Derrota a Cuthbert Sprunt","Cuthbert Sprunt ha revelado sus verdaderas intenciones y ha llamado a sus secuaces para que le ayuden.\
\
Basilio Resinas ha salido en tu defensa, y con su ayuda, debes derrotar al enemigo.","'Cuthbert Sprunt no está aquí todavía, ${PLAYER}, así que todavía tienes tiempo de cambiar de idea. Sprunt es un enemigo peligroso, pero no deberías tener ningún problema... asumiendo que juegue limpio.'","'Sabía que ese Sprunt planeaba hacer trampas, ¡lo sabía! Menos mal que yo estaba aquí, ${PLAYER}, aunque bien está lo que bien acaba, como siempre digo. O al menos, lo digo ahora.\
\
'Avísame cuando quieras volver. Le hemos dado a este villano una lección, y creo que sus secuaces no te causarán más problemas.'"},
[7170]={"Glorfindel waits for you to approach the council.","Glorfindel is come to the Council of War in the Court of Lothlórien. You, too, are expected to join them.","Hear what Galadriel has to say of the prophecy.","Approach the Council","Habla con Glorfindel","Instancia: El Arco está Tensado","You and Glorfindel have joined the Council of War. Talk to him to hear of the text he recovered.","'It is decided. The Elves of Lothlórien and the Elves of Mirkwood will make ready to assault Dol Guldur.'","'It is just as we saw in my Mirror, ${PLAYER}. There can be no doubt in the matter now. It is decided.\
\
'Take your place, I will address the Council of War.'","'As you are aware, I have recovered a text of the words uttered by Gil-galad long ago. I will speak only a little of what was written, which pertains to what is now coming to pass:\
\
'When the light first fades from the Golden Wood, then the Shadow in the Green Wood may be torn down. But if the Shadow be torn down, faster shall the Golden Wood fade.\
\
'I think the words are clear, and though it may give us great sorrow, still we know what course we must take.'","Habla con Galadriel","It is time to approach the Council of War.","Galadriel will now address the Council of War.","Hear Galadriel's pronouncement","'Gi suilon! They are waiting for us. Come.'"},
[7171]={"Your companions do not understand. You have to find Frodo and make him understand that the Ring must go to Minas Tirith.","Frodo is gone, and the anger has lifted from your senses much as a cloud moves on from covering the sun. You should return now to Aragorn and the rest of your party. Perhaps Frodo has returned to them and will forgive you your outburst.","Frodo is gone. You should return to the camp-site and see if he will forgive your outburst","Frodo will doom us all! You have to take the Ring from him before he ransoms Middle-earth to Sauron!","'Boromir, what have you done?'","'I believe we should go to Minas Tirith, Boromir. If it came to a vote, that would be my decision. You have told us of the Enemy's desire to destroy Minas Tirith, and I think that is where we are most needed.\
\
'But I will stand with Frodo, whatever his decision.'","Talk to Frodo and tell him of Minas Tirith's great need","The Elf, Legolas, is by the camp-fire.","Talk to Frodo and ask to borrow the Ring so you can save Gondor","Search the hollow log for the sneaking hobbit!","'Boromir, no! The Ring cannot save Gondor! It must be destroyed!'","He is not here! Where is the Ring?","The sneak must be hiding somewhere around here! Search the places he might be hiding, and seize the Ring!","Habla con Aragorn","Talk to Aragorn by the camp-fire","Seize the Ring from Frodo!","He is a fool! He will doom us all! He will give the Ring to Sauron!","Frodo has wandered partially up Amon Hen. He needs to be told of your city's great need for the Ring.","'I know Minas Tirith is endangered, Boromir, but I cannot bring the Ring there. You heard what Gandalf said at the Council, and Elrond... my road lies to the east, and to the Fire. The Ring cannot save Gondor. Its only power is the power to destroy.'","'Boromir, it is my burden, and I will not give it to you! You are not yourself! The Ring has influenced your words, do not let it influence your actions as well! I have nothing more to say to you!'","No! The fool! He has doomed us all!","Instancia: La Ruptura de la Comunidad","The Elf is a valuable companion, but his arrows are nothing compared to the power of the Ring!","Aragorn does not understand. My city needs the Ring to survive!","Show yourself, villain! Where is the Ring?","He is not listening! Elves and Wizards have already filled his head with nonsense!","A pox on all hobbits! Where is the cowardly creature?","Aragorn is by the camp-fire on Parth Galen.","Frodo is nowhere to be seen","'I understand, Boromir, but you know the words of Gandalf. Though there be strength in Minas Tirith, it is not a strength that will avail us in the matter of Frodo's burden. If this were a contest that could be won by strength of arms, I would readily agree to go at once to your city. But I fear it is not.\
\
'When Frodo returns he will give us his decision, and we will do what we can to support him, will we not?'","Search the leaf pile for the sneaking hobbit!","'You are very kind, Boromir, but I have seen no danger. If there are Orcs about, they must remain on the other side of the river. I have simply been walking and thinking about what I must do. But it is not an easy decision to make. I know what I must do, but... I am afraid.'","Frodo has wandered partially up Amon Hen. He needs to be told of your city's great need for the Ring. Perhaps he will lend it to you? You can use the Ring to save Minas Tirith, and all of Gondor!","You have found Frodo, but he has not seen you yet.","Frodo has asked for an hour in which to decide the course of the Fellowship, but you are worried he will not choose to bring the Ring to Minas Tirith.","Frodo has not yet made his decision! Perhaps he can be convinced!","Talk to the Elf, Legolas, by the camp-fire","Find Frodo and convince him to bring the Ring to Minas Tirith. He wandered somewhere to the north-west.","Search through the bush for the sneaking hobbit!","Talk to Frodo and see if he has yet decided what to do","Aragorn wants to know where you have been."},
[7172]={"<rgb=FF0000>Torferth was defeated</rgb>","'We are victorious, ${PLAYER}. Those of Ordlac's men who followed orders without true knowledge of their master's treachery have turned on their brethren and helped rout Oserley from Stoke.\
\
'The battle is over....'","Thane Torferth of Torsbury has brought his men to Stoke, where he prepares to march upon the Mead Hall and confront the traitor Ordlac.","<rgb=#FF0000>Torferth must not be defeated</rgb>","Arrived at the Mead Hall of Stoke","Defeat Ordlac and protect the children","Instance: The Broadacres Betrayed","Dudsig and his guards are blocking the way to Ordlac and the children. Defeat them and confront Ordlac.","Talk to Thane Torferth","Thane Torferth stands on the road to Stoke.\
\
You should speak with Thane Torferth before the attack.","<rgb=#FF0000>Torferth was defeated</rgb>","The Mead Hall of Stoke is at the end of the road.\
\
Torferth is making for the Mead Hall of Stoke, where he intends to confront Ordlac.","Ordlac is near the end of the Mead Hall, threatening Reeve Fríthild's children.\
\
Aid Torferth against Ordlac and protect the children.","Defeated Ordlac","Defeat Dudsig and his guards","'I will wish to speak with you later...come see me when you have rested a little.'","'We have come to it at last, ${PLAYER}, and it is a sad day. Brother must fight brother, and much blood shall be shed. Nevertheless, Ordlac cannot be permitted to continue his treachery.\
\
'Are you ready to march with us? I am sure that Ordlac has reinforced the road to the Mead Hall, but we cannot be delayed!\
\
'Forth the Toringas!'","'Look! Ordlac is threatening the Reeve's children! We must hurry!'","Thane Torferth is in the Mead Hall of Stoke.\
\
You should speak with Thane Torferth at once.","Defeated Dudsig and his guards","Fight through Ordlac's forces to the Mead Hall of Stoke"},
[7173]={"Your captor stands outside the cage for some purpose of her own.","Jajax sleeps on, oblivious to everything.","Talk to the mysterious girl","You never saw her face before now, but it was in Umbar-môkh that you spoke to Tephísa. She is one of the Terâsi, the forgotten children who make their way through hidden paths beneath the city. It must have been the Temámir Birûk who gave her this message to bring to you and Jajax.\
\
Tephísa studies your face closely.\
\
'I watched the flames destroy my home once, stranger. They were orange and red then, the embers lit by servants of Barkhûsh, but a fire is a fire. Those ships will set ablaze the homes of Gondor, but they will return, and when they return the conflagration will spread to the homes of Umbar.\
\
'I can help you escape, but I have a price.'","You tell Jajax that Hármelak is lying.\
\
'Aye,' he agrees. 'She lied before, and she lies again.'","A girl watches you from outside the cage","<rgb=#00FF00>Beckon</rgb> the girl to speak","Give Tephísa your answer","It is difficult to measure the passing of time in the cage.","Tephísa waits for your response.","'It will not be as you say. The people of the city will know why I could not close the river gate. If the Song of Waves and Wind could not leave the River Ikorbân, Nakási would have turned the Narghâk cannons upon Umbar Baharbêl! Should we have sacrificed our own city for the sake of Gondor?'\
\
You ask Hármelak if she truly believes that Nakási or Balakhâd would have destroyed their own city, and she waves a dismissive hand.\
\
'You believe the people of the city share your uncertainty, ${PLAYER}.'","Listen to the words of your visitor","The girl eyes you warily.","See what Jajax thinks","Listen to the words of your captor","Wait for the girl to speak","Perhaps if you <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> the girl she will speak to you.","You have given your answer, and must now wait to see her response.","Talk to your captor through the bars of your cage","Desperate for tidings from above, captives wrestle with their helplessness in the face of the evil that threatens Umbar and Gondor.","Wait to see what she will do","Instancia: La jaula y los cautivos","Talk to Jajax","'You might as well settle down. We're not going anywhere, ${PLAYER}.'","Pass the time in your cage","'I have a message for you from one of the Temámir. He says \\qThe work continues. We need many hands to mine the Abâshal, and will forge new medallions from it. Remain alert for its shine, and stay safe: the mine is treacherous, but there will be a light in the darkness.'\
\
The girl turns to go, but she hesitates. She faces you again, and you try to remember where you have before heard this voice.\
\
'We watched as the ships passed the city. One galley tried to block the way to open water, and it was sunk. The terrible smoke of the cannons smelled foul. We saw Orcs on the deck of one of the ships. They cheered as the ship of Umbar burned; the water could not quench the blue flames.'","There is nothing more you can do but wait.","Jajax rests on a cot by the entrance of the cage."},
[7174]={"Talk to Morflak in Isengard","Talk to Iwan at the gate into Isengard","'Let us go. I do not want to stay here any longer than I need to. I will leave you captives with someone and be back on the waggon headed for Tûr Morva before the next bell.'","Talk to Léolin in the prison-caves","Betrayal... you were attacked by two members of the Falcon-clan, but Lothrandir was able to turn the tables on them. You should speak with him now.","'You are Fâsh's problem now. He will find work for you! Ha!'","Talk to Lothrandir in the prison-caves","Instancia: El Cautivo","Talk to Nai in the prison-caves","'This is bad, ${PLAYER}, very bad! The Falcon-clan has turned on us! I do not know why, but we are betrayed, and many of our friends are still below!\
\
'We will cut our way out!'","'The cells further in are damper and less pleasant, filled with refuse and home to rats. The captive will have much to say of Saruman's plans for the Falcon-clan, I am certain of it.'","'We will make the captive sing for us, ${PLAYER}. He will sing of Saruman's plans, or I will end his captivity with steel.'","You have been brought to Isengard by waggon along a bumpy road.","'We will keep you busy, little ${RACE}, and your friend too. I think the Old Man will want to speak with him directly.\
\
'There's a place for you in the caves below, if Fâsh doesn't kill you first. If you have any fortune at all, you won't see me again, little ${RACE}.\
\
'You're ours now. Let's see how long you last.'","You have met Lothrandir in the prison-caves, coming back from an errand in the depths.","You have come with Lheu Brenin to speak with the captive emissary from Isengard one more time before he dies and hopefully learn something of use to the Falcon-clan and the Grey Company.","Nai is guarding the cell where Dondhreg is being held captive in the prison-caves.","Lothrandir has been badly beaten by your captors and is finding it difficult to go on.","Survive the waggon ride along a bumpy road","Follow Lothrandir into Isengard","'I cannot... go on like this... ${PLAYER}. What... can we...?'\
\
Lothrandir's pains are evident; both of you were cruelly-treated by the long waggon journey to Isengard and the whips of your captors, but Lothrandir bore the brunt of the ill treatment.","'Calenglad and some other Rangers are below, bringing up some of the supplies the Falcon-clan stored in the depths. The caves go quite some way into the mountain. Halbarad sent me to bring you down to help, but if you are busy with something else....'","An Uruk-hai named Morflak has made you pull up short before the tower of Orthanc.","Talk to Lothrandir at the gates of Isengard","Iwan is ready to bring you into Isengard.","You have been captured and brought to Isengard, home of the traitor Saruman","Lheu Brenin has come with you into the prison-caves behind Tûr Morva to speak with the captive emissary.","Léolin is waiting to speak with you in the prison-caves.","'See how weak our captive is! He will not live through the night if he does not have a meal and an escape from the damp.'","Lothrandir is running into the heart of Isengard by his own power. It is a small gesture, but it is something, and gives you a glimmer of hope.","Lheu Brenin has blocked your passage with a group of armed warriors. He wishes to speak with you.","'I am sorry that it turned out like this, ${PLAYER}. I mean that. These Rangers are good folk, strong folk, and I see in them an echo of my own people. But you told me yourself of the great armies Saruman has already amassed. He is prepared to give us back the lands that belong to us. It is so close now!\
\
'I am no Wizard's servant. Saruman prizes knowledge above all else, and now the Falcon-clan can give him that.'","Talk to Lheu Brenin in the prison-caves"},
[7175]={"'Our journey has only just begun, ${PLAYER}... are you prepared to continue aiding the people of the Sutcrofts?'","Gísling can be found along the road to Snowbourn.","Gísling was defeated!","'We have made it this far, ${PLAYER}, but I fear the road south will be fraught with danger.\
\
'You have done well to deal so severe a blow to our foes near Garsfeld, but the fields to the south may be rife with Orcs.\
\
'Let me gather the crofters, we must set out as soon as we are able!'","<rgb=#FF0000>The crofters must survive</rgb>","Gísling is walking with the crofters along the road south to Snowbourn.\
\
Gísling hopes you can aid him in escorting the crofters of Garsfeld to Snowbourn. However, he fears that Orcs lurk just beyond his sight and threaten to harm his people.","<rgb=#FF0000>Gísling must not be defeated</rgb>","'We have made it, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Perhaps you and I are worse for the wear, but thankfully, the crofters have made it here unscathed.\
\
'We have much to do in Snowbourn... let us get to it!'","Escort the crofters of Garsfeld to safety","Talk to Gísling","Instancia: La caravana a Río Nevado","Gísling is standing with the crofters at The Raided Crofts.\
\
Having made it this far, Gísling has asked for your aid in escorting the crofters of Garsfeld to Snowbourn.","The crofters have reached Snowbourn safely","At the order of Gísil, you are to aid to the crofters of Garsfeld as they travel south to seek safer shelter within the walls of Snowbourn.","A crofter has fallen!"},
[7176]={"Following Snaga's muffled shouts, you discover a ladder leading upward!","Shagrat chases a small Orc from the turret!","The gate of Cirith Ungol can be found at the easternmost point of Cirith Ungol.","Draw the phial of Galadriel and hold it aloft!","Search for Mr. Frodo in the Tower of Cirith Ungol","<rgb=#FF0000>No! The quest cannot end this way!</rgb>","'These notions are only a trick! Even if they were true, I cannot bear such a burden!'","Use your hobbit-sense","Confront Shagrat","After disguising themselves in Orkish armour and cloaks now kept by the Silent One, Samwise Gamgee and Frodo Baggins passed through Lhingris in their quest to reach Mount Doom.","Mr. Frodo must be in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol, and it sounds like he's in danger!","Talk to Mr. Frodo and escape the Tower of Cirith Ungol","Instancia: Las elecciones del Maestro Samsagaz","Shagrat stands alone. It's now or never!","'Am I still dreaming?'\
\
You embrace Frodo so hard that you nearly lift him off the ground.\
\
'You've found me, dear Sam! But where are we? And how did I end up here?'\
\
You tell Frodo that there's no time for tales until you get far, far away from this tower!","Upon seeing you, the Orc recoils and flees up the stairs of the Tower!","<rgb=#FF0000>Claim the One Ring!</rgb>","Spring past the Silent Watchers into Cirith Ungol!","You hear angry Orc-voices approaching from the turret! Hide!","Ascend the Tower of Cirith Ungol","Rescue Mr. Frodo from the Tower of Cirith Ungol","Wait for the right moment","An Orc has fled from you. You should continue higher into the Tower of Cirith Ungol in search of Mr. Frodo.","Harden your will and charge at the gate of Cirith Ungol!","You hear Orkish voices, and the familiar voice of Shagrat. Quickly, hide!","Mr. Frodo must be in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol. Keep climbing!","The Silent Watchers let out a shrill cry, and far above you, a bell rings in answer!","Pass through the gate of Cirith Ungol","Shagrat has chased the Orc, Snaga, onto the parapet of Cirith Ungol. You should remain hidden until the right moment.","The Ring has tempted you with visions of yourself as Samwise the Strong. Use your hobbit-sense, Sam!","Hide behind slain Orcs and wreckage!","The phial of Galadriel! Its light might overcome whatever force bars your path!","An unseen force seems to block your passage into Cirith Ungol.","'It's Sam! Mr. Frodo, my dear! I've come!'","As soon as you approach him, Shagrat darts past you and flees down the stairs of the Tower!","Something too strong for your will to overcome bars the way!","Mr. Frodo can be found somewhere in the Tower of Cirith Ungol.","Find the topmost chamber of Cirith Ungol","You've rescued Mr. Frodo!","You cannot pass! What else can you do in this moment of great need?","The Ring has begun to tempt you! You must resist and rescue Mr. Frodo.","See what could be if you were only to claim the Ring!","You feel the Ring begin to gnaw at your will and reason!","Shagrat is blocking your path into the heights of Cirith Ungol. It's now or never, Sam!","The Silent Watchers quail and their will is broken for a moment!","Now's your chance! Mr. Frodo needs your help!"},
[7177]={"Slagvi está a tu lado en la cámara de enfriamiento.\
\
Deberías hablar con Slagvi.","Slagvi quiere que el líder de los trasgos que ha tomado la cámara de enfriamiento sea encontrado y derrotado.","Habla con Slagvi","Slagvi se ha unido a ti en la cámara de enfriamiento","Repara el engranaje oxidado","Repara la rueda atascada","'Ah, así que aquí estamos. Qué lugar tan maravillosamente construido. Pero... me temo que estamos rodeados de enemigos. Haré todo lo posible por ayudarte a eliminarlos.'","Slagvi ha sido invocado","El jefe ha caído y los trasgos restantes huyen aterrados. La cámara de enfriamiento es segura por ahora.","Engranaje oxidado reparado","Un cuerno de invocación se encuentra en la parte frontal de la cámara de enfriamiento.\
\
El cuerno de invocación puede usarse para llamar a Slagvi a tu lado.","Habla con Slagvi. Puedes invocarlo si os separáis.","'Lo has hecho muy bien, amigo mío. Gracias por tu ayuda. No habría podido enfrentarme a tantos trasgos yo solo.'","Rueda atascada reparada","Slagvi invocado","La cámara de enfriamiento ha sido reparada","Instancia: La Cámara de Enfriamiento","Repara la palanca atascada","Los elementos que hay que reparar se encuentran al fondo de la cámara de enfriamiento.","Encuentra y derrota al jefe de Moria","Sal de la cámara de enfriamiento","Palanca atascada reparada","Es hora de salir de la cámara de enfriamiento.","Slagvi está listo para comenzar la investigación de la cámara de enfriamiento","Usa el cuerno de invocación para llamar a Slagvi","Slagvi desea investigar el fallo de los sistemas de agua en la Gran Excavación y cree que el origen del problema está en la propia cámara de enfriamiento.","(Puedes usar el cuerno de invocación en cualquier momento para llamar a Slagvi a tu lado)","Slagvi ha sido llamado"},
[7178]={"Talk to Doron","As Doron speaks, the din of a large force rises in the distance","Follow Doron outside Ost Celebrant","Doron is stationed outside of Ost Celebrant. You should follow him as he tells his tale.","Doron is inside Ost Celebrant with his men. You should listen as he continues his tale.","Having heard the roar of an approaching force, Doron and his men have decided to cross the bridge of Ost Celebrant and confront the invaders.","'Let us leave this memory, there is more to be said.'","Having survived an Easterling assault, Doron is entering Ost Celebrant, where he hopes to reunite with the rest of his men.","'The wrong choice was made, but how could I have known? Some of my men were overjoyed by our tainted riches, while others condemned my actions.\
\
'Cirion never forgave us...the oath we made to protect Gondor was broken by my actions, and all suffered for it.'","Follow Doron into Ost Celebrant","<rgb=#FF0000>Doron must not be defeated</rgb>","Doron is stationed outside of Ost Celebrant, after having patrolled the road down to the Limlight with his men.","Follow Doron through his memory","'In times long past, my men and I were stationed in Ost Celebrant, a gorgeous Gondorian fortress that overlooked the Limlight river. \
\
'We were under siege by a terrible force of Easterlings for some time before this, and eventually they claimed Calenardhon -- the land which became Rohan. They drove us north, into these fields, and it was here that we prepared to make our final stand.\
\
'My men and I guarded the Limlight, hoping to keep their forces from the south at bay, while our leader, Cirion and his force secured the rest of the field.\
\
'The night we were cursed began as I was patrolling back from the Limlight with my men....'","Doron, leader of the Oathbreakers in Parth Celebrant, has decided to tell you how he and his men came to be cursed. As he speaks, you find yourself drawn into a daydream, experiencing the tale alongside Doron and his men.","Instancia: El costo de la lealtad","Doron is standing on the edge of the bridge into Ost Celebrant."},
[7180]={"'The council has gathered, and the time has come to discuss our actions in response to the attack. We must attempt to secure Woodhurst and find a way to protect our people. There is something malevolent working against us here.'","'We will speak again shortly, once the others have departed. I may not know you well, but you told me of my family and of the scene at the mead hall, when the others would not. I believe you have earned my trust.'","Instance: The Council of Herubrand","Observe the council meeting","Herubrand's council is meeting in the cellar of the farmhouse, and Herubrand has invited you to join them.","Talk to Herubrand","You have joined Herubrand as he meets with his council to discuss what should be done in the aftermath of the attack on the Mead Hall of Woodhurst."},
[7181]={"'Durin is right. Sauron will hide in his tower until the Rhúnhoth horde arrives and destroys us! Why would he dare come out when his victory is all but assured? He has only to wait for it!\
\
'We have to think of something!'","With the triumphant Rhúnhoth horde of the Ghâzab Bôron on its way, the lords of the Great Alliance have called a council to determine what can be done to stave off defeat.","Tárandil is outside the pavilion where the council of the kings will take place.","Vëamacil is in the tent where the council of kings is underway.","Talk to Tárandil","'This is our opportunity! Now is our chance for glory!'","The council of the kings will soon begin, and the sons of Isildur are hopeful that their presence and yours will go unremarked.","Talk to Vëamacil","'Let us enter the tent, but do not walk with fear or nervousness! Stride, rather, as if we were invited and indeed the council cannot begin until we are in attendance.\
\
'That is always the advice of Vëamacil, and to speak truth I have yet to see it fail him.'","Lendelen of the Bright Company has proposed a dangerous plan by which Sauron's hold over the Ghâzab Bôron might be broken.","High King Gil-galad has reservations about your attendance and that of Isildur's sons.","'You will fight alongside the Bright Company for this undertaking, ${CLASS}, if that is the wish of Glorfindel and his counsellor Lendelen. It will be dangerous, but what matters of war are not? If they are Men, my grandsons will forgive you for being so-selected, and resent it not.\
\
'If the Bright Company fails in this, the Storm of Wrath will come for us all, and they will then have ample opportunity to die in glorious battle. If that is a comfort to them, let it comfort them. I will coddle them not.'","Wait for the council of the kings to begin","High King Gil-galad has called into question your presence, and that of the sons of Isildur, at the council of kings.","The council of kings is underway.","Observe the council of the kings","'I cannot believe this!'","Instancia: El Concilio de los Reyes","Talk to High King Elendil","The council of the kings continues, but not all in attendance are satisfied with its pronouncements.","'This pavilion seems more crowded already than it need be for such a council. Is it not better to limit those in attendance? I mean no disrespect to the sons of Isildur or their sire, but what is to be gained by their presence here, or that of a ${CLASS}? Can they, and you, not be told the decisions of this council once they are made?'","High King Elendil is inside the pavilion for the council of kings.","Habla con el Alto Rey Gil-galad"},
[7182]={"Instancia: El Consejo de Stoke","Talk to Reeve Fríthild","Speak with Reeve Fríthild.","Reeve Fríthild's sword, shield, and mail are on the table below the dais.\
\
Reeve Fríthild asked you to collect her arms and armour.","Observe the Council of Stoke","Bring the sword, shield, and mail to Reeve Fríthild.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you have arrived. Let us then begin this council....'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You have been of great service to the people of Stoke. Well have I named you friend.'","Collected Fríthild's mail","Collect Fríthild's shield","Reeve Fríthild has summoned together the Council of Stoke in order to come to a consensus regarding what action to take against the forces of the White Hand in the Broadacres.","'${PLAYER}, will you honour me by assisting me with my arms and armour? You will find it on the table behind you.'","'Have you not brought my armour?'","'I declare this Council dismissed!'","Collected Fríthild's sword","'Gird me, ${PLAYER}, friend of Stoke. This day I become Fríthild, shield-maiden of Rohan.'","Observe the Council of Stoke.","Bring the sword, shield, and mail to Reeve Fríthild","Collected Fríthild's shield","DNT -- Will not be seen","Collect Fríthild's mail","Collect Fríthild's sword"},
[7183]={"Instancia: El Consejo de los Capitanes","'You remember the words of Denethor, ${PLAYER}. In them I think there is much we might learn.'","Mithrandir is holding council inside Aragorn's pavilion on the Pelennor.","'The captains who fought on Pelennor are here now, ${PLAYER}, and it is time to begin.'","Aragorn has called for a council of the captains at his pavilion in order to decide what must be done.","'We must determine the numbers we will need. There is work still to do before we set forth.'","Observe the council of the captains","'There are some considerations that may slow his hand. The Ring can only be wielded by one, rather than by many. Sauron will expect a struggle among those who seek to wield it. He waits until one among us seeks to become greater than the others, and that is when he will act, seizing the advantage of our disarray.\
\
'His Nazgûl still fly overhead, seeking signs of our movement. He has not forgotten the sword of Elendil, and now he has seen it reforged. His first assault was turned back and his greatest Captain slain. The winds of fortune have begun to blow in our favour.\
\
'For the first time, doubt has begun to gnaw at him.'","'Legolas is right. We seek to capture Sauron's attention and keep it fastened upon us for as long as we can, but do not misunderstand.\
\
'If we march to the Black Gate, there will be nothing to keep him from sending the considerable forces within Mordor to crush us completely and without mercy. We will buy time for the Ring-bearer to complete his mission, but there will be no more time for us.\
\
'Any who go with me on this last march should know he goes to his death. There will likely be no returning from this. Still, I consider it my duty to try.'","Aragorn is inside his pavilion with many of the captains who fought at Pelennor.","Talk to Mithrandir inside the pavilion","Prince Imrahil is holding council inside Aragorn's pavilion on the Pelennor.","Aragorn and the captains of the armies are meeting to decide their next course.","Talk to Aragorn inside the pavilion","'We do not need a great force to march on the Black Gate. This is not an army with designs on victory. We will determine the numbers we bring east and the numbers we leave behind.\
\
'May this be the right choice, ${PLAYER}. I would rather die doing my part to bring about a new age than to do nothing and know the new age will never come.'","'If we cannot achieve victory, would you advise us to hide behind our walls, enduring siege after siege until we can last no longer?'","Talk to Imrahil in the pavilion"},
[7184]={"'Three only there are, but they are figures out of nightmare. Two are the beings we have come to know as the Nazgûl, the Ringwraiths of Sauron.\
\
'The third may have been a Man, once, but through the foul sorceries of his master in the Dark Tower, he has become something else. He is Ugrukhôr, the Captain of the Pit. He comes now to Durthand with an offer.'","Talk to Annoth during his recounting of the tale","It is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.","Annoth desires to tell you the tale of his ancestors, the Thandrim, who kept watch on Mordor from fortresses within the Black Land for more than a thousand years.","Listen to Annoth's account of the Thandrim","'I have heard tales of the bravery of the Thandrim for all my life: they were a shining light of Gondor's goodness, blazing within the shadows of Mordor. See them now, where they stand, defiant and bold!'","'That is the story of the Thandrim, ${PLAYER}. Only Halannon survived, and his account is kept in the archives of Minas Tirith. It is Trenarn Bronad, the Survivor's Tale.'","'Now you know the tale.'","Instancia: La cruel historia de Durthang","'Should they have refused? Every man there knew Ugrukhôr for a liar, but the pit of despair into which they had fallen could not be surmounted. They had been hardy men, once, but a year of starvation and fear must have taken its toll. No doubt their fear was made stronger by the presence of the Nazgûl, but I can understand the draw of even the faintest of hopes in that dark pit.\
\
'The Thandrim surrendered to Ugrukhôr. Durthand was lost.'","'The Thandrim cast aside their weapons, and beneath Ugrukhôr's watchful gaze they march to the Morannon, now held by the Orcs. The gate opens. Sixty men, all that remained of the Thandrim, pass through the Gate.\
\
'At a signal from Ugrukhôr, the archers on the walls fill the air with death.'"},
[7185]={"Listen to Malthellam and Rosfin","Listen to Malthellam","Talk to Rosfin","Malthellam is near his fireplace in his home.\
\
Malthellam and Rosfin spoke at length on the history of the vale, and Malthellam now desires to hear the rest of your tale.","Malthellam and Rosfin are speaking in Malthellam's home.\
\
You have informed them that the Dead continue to haunt the vale.","Malthellam can be found beside the fireplace in his home.\
\
You have come to tell Malthellam and Rosfin of what you have learned of the Dead and Tarlang's Crown. You should speak to Malthellam.","Rosfin can be found beside the fireplace in Malthellam's home.\
\
You have come to tell Malthellam and Rosfin of what you have learned of the Dead and Tarlang's Crown. You should speak to Rosfin while you wait for Malthellam.","Malthellam and Rosfin are speaking in Malthellam's home.\
\
You have told them of all that you experiencing in Alagrant and Sardol, and now Malthellam and Rosfin are discussing what is to be done.","Talk to Malthellam","'We have spoken enough on these matters, ${PLAYER}. The danger to the east has grown, and it must be dealt with soon, lest it spread south into Lamedon.'","'I am sorry to have kept you and Lady Rosfin waiting, ${PLAYER}. I was trying to find some sort of explanation as to why the Dead have returned to the Hill in such force....\
\
'I shall soon ask you more of your travels in the south, but first, let me tell you more of the vale's history.'","'Malthellam told me that you have much to tell us of happenings around Alagrant and Sardol... I hope what you have seen can offer us some hope, but your face seems to say otherwise.\
\
'Let us hear what you have to say then....'","Instancia: El Valle Maldito","DNT -- will not be seen","Malthellam can be found beside the fireplace in his home.\
\
You have finished discussing matters with Rosfin and Malthellam and should speak to Malthellam once more before readying yourself to journey into the vale once more.","'Let us be done with these talks.'","Recount your <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb> to Malthellam and Rosfin","After aiding the villages of Alagrant and Sardol, you have uncovered dangerous, new threats to Blackroot Vale that you must reveal to Malthellam and Rosfin."},
[7186]={"'Let us ride together, ${PLAYER}! Let us bring news of our defiance to Saruman himself!'","Talk to Cynstan on the east bank of the Isen","Théodred is on the eyot in the middle of the river Isen. Cynstan has asked you to tell him that the Ford will be in Cadda's capable hands while the Prince rides to Isengard.","'We have several hours' ride ahead of us, ${PLAYER}, then we will see if Saruman is prepared to face me in battle, or if he will cower behind his walls in perpetual caution.'","Cadda is on the east bank of the Ford, and he wants to speak with you.","Travel up the road to Isengard","The scout has returned from Isengard and brings word to Théodred that the number of Orcs and half-orcs outside the walls is not to be feared.\
\
Théodred wants to discuss this report with you.","'You have come a long way from your homeland, ${PLAYER}, and you have seen a great deal of danger. These battles in which you have fought...when you were embroiled in the thick of them, were you frightened? I cannot ask this of the men, they would think me a coward.\
\
'But I am already frightened, and we have not yet begun to march!'","Mount your steed and talk to Grimbold when you are ready to ride","You have come part of the way up the road to Isengard, and now Théodred is waiting for the return of his scout. You should speak with the Prince.","'I hope you don't mind getting your feet wet again, ${PLAYER}. Cadda is on the east bank of the river, and the stones can be treacherous.'","'Cadda is a man of Rohan and will understand what is needed of him. I will not advance through the front gate to victory while leaving the postern gate open to the enemy; someone must stay to hold the Ford in the event I have misjudged Saruman's mind.'\
\
Théodred lowers his voice and addresses you quietly.\
\
'You should go with Cynstan to deliver my words, ${PLAYER}. He is untested by battle, and the men see him still as a green boy. Cadda may be less bristly towards my esquire if you are there as well. I need a word with Athelard before we go. He is not pleased at the quality of the spears we have, but it is too late to make more. They will have to suffice.'","Théodred is waiting to speak with you on the eyot in the middle of the Isen.\
\
It is dawn and nearly time to begin the daring strike on Isengard. Théodred is waiting to speak with you before his host rides north.","'I did tell the Prince that Cadda would not be happy about staying here. You heard me tell him that.\
\
'I am going to stay here for a few minutes and see if I can find my missing bracer. You should cross the Ford again and tell the Prince that the Ford will be defended while we are away.'","You have travelled up the road towards Isengard with the host, and Grimbold wants to speak with you.","Talk to Théodred on the eyot in the Isen","Talk to Cadda on the east bank of the river Isen","Théodred has given Cynstan a message to deliver and is waiting to speak with you again.","Talk to Grimbold on the road to Isengard","Talk to Cynstan on the eyot in the Isen","Cynstan is on the eyot in the middle of the river Isen.","'I should not be left behind! My place is at the front of the column with my Prince!'\
\
Cadda's eyes flash angrily at you from beneath the rim of his helmet.\
\
'I will do as I am commanded, but I wish it were not necessary. My men will hold the Ford against whatever comes, as my Prince desires. But I think we wait here uselessly, while our brothers and our friends ride into battle against the armies of Saruman.\
\
'I understand the need for it. But I chafe at that need and do not want to sit here in idleness while Prince Théodred rides into danger!'","The sun rose on the Twenty-fifth of February, and Théodred and Grimbold made final preparations for a daring strike on the forces of Isengard.","Cynstan is on the east bank of the river Isen and wants to talk to you.","Talk to Cynstan in the middle of the Ford","Théodred has asked you to mount your steed and talk to Grimbold when you are ready to ride to Isengard.","'All is ready, then? Cadda will hold the east bank of the Ford with the men at his command, and the rest of us will ride north to Isengard. The Éored will follow my lead, and Grimbold will dismount and command the foot as a separate unit if the terrain off the road warrants it. Athelard will call the mark for his archers.\
\
'It will be some hours before we are in sight of Isengard. It is best we get started.'","Cynstan is in the middle of the Ford. He is concerned about something and wants to speak with you.","'I hope you have awakened refreshed, ${PLAYER}. I doubt not this will be a long day. I have a few matters left undone, which must be resolved, then we will ride.'","'It is a pleasant morning for riding, ${PLAYER}. If it stays thus, we will be at Isengard by mid-day and have brought Saruman to heel not long after!\
\
'Let us catch up to the Prince and get a good view of the road ahead.'","'This news lightens my heart, but we must not forget that Saruman is devious. This strike will remind him we are not to be lightly set aside and that he is not immune to attack. Any more than that is more than I expect.\
\
'The dawn has passed. It will be mid-day when we move to the next stage of my plan. Ready yourself for what comes next, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Théodred on the road to Isengard","Instancia: El Ataque Audaz, Amanecer","You have travelled up the road towards Isengard with the host.","Cross the Ford of Isen once more and speak with Théodred on the eyot","'We are nearly there, ${PLAYER}. I can smell the stench of Isengard even from here.'"},
[7187]={"Before the gates of Isengard, the Rohirrim led by Théodred have come under attack by an overwhelming force of Saruman's uruks.\
\
You need to speak with Grimbold amid the chaos of battle!","Talk to Grimbold at the head of the host","The riders have netted some of the attacking uruks, and Grimbold has charged you with defeating them in order to buy time for the retreat.","Defeat netted uruk-warriors at the gates of Isengard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated netted uruk-warriors at the gates of Isengard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Prince Théodred has asked you and Grimbold to cut through the brush on the eastern side of the road to attack the half-orc flank.","'Prince Théodred has routed the enemy! Victory is ours! ${PLAYER}, Grimbold, come with me, and we will send them howling back into the Ring of Isengard! We will send them back to Saruman!'","Prince Théodred and his host have come to the gates of Isengard, and it is now time for his daring strike to begin.","Instancia: El Ataque Audaz, Mediodía","'We will cut through the brush on this side of the road, ${PLAYER}, and attack our enemies' flank!'","Talk to Rungar","Théodred is waiting to address his assembled men, and you should speak with him.","'We are outnumbered, ${PLAYER}! The Prince has ordered a retreat, but first we must survive this attack!\
\
'Our riders have managed to net some of our foes! Attack the netted uruks and keep them from breaking through!\
\
'I will try to drive some of the others away!'","Talk to Grimbold before the gates of Isengard","Rungar has arrived on the flank of the main host, and you should speak with him.","Talk to Théodred","'Hildred spoke true. There are Orcs outside the walls, but their numbers should not be a problem for us, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Let us see what they think of my riders!'","'Are you ${PLAYER}? You are! We have to get out of here!'\
\
Shouts of despair and cries of terror rise from the pockets of Rohirrim still fighting for their lives. The archer looks at you with fear in his eyes and throws his bow down in the dust.\
\
'The day is lost! There are too many uruks!'\
\
The men begin to break for the road back to the ford, and all sense of order is lost as the uruks gather on all sides."},
[7188]={"Denethor has emerged from the tower, ready to die for his city and his people.","Talk to Imrahil","Your mind is filled with terrible visions, but the voice of the Steward cuts through the frightening images.","Talk to Denethor amid the terrible visions","Your mind is full of hazy, troubled images","Escape from the enemy and find Peregrin Took","Imrahil has slain many Orcs, and has called to you for news of the gate.","'Stay back, ${PLAYER}. You have become mighty indeed during your adventures, but the evil that now stands in the ruin of the gate is beyond your measure. Only I can stand against the Witch-king now.'","The Witch-king is victorious!","You have been captured by the Enemy!","Talk to Mithrandir before the broken gate","'What news, ${PLAYER}? I heard shouts of terror and dismay, but could not find what caused them!'\
\
Before you can say a word, his eyes widen in surprise.","Shake off your reverie, and talk to Denethor","Witness the confrontation between Mithrandir and the Witch-king of Angmar","Denethor is standing before you, his face an earnest mask of despair and hopelessness.","Talk to Denethor before he succumbs to his wounds","Wait for a chance to turn the tables on your captors","Talk to Gothmog atop the city","Fight alongside Denethor atop the city","'Do you understand, ${PLAYER}? It is not needless cruelty that drove this tale of mine. No, it is kindness. For my words wove a picture of the fate that awaits us all. It cannot be avoided. Better to accept the road and set our affairs in order than to fight it fruitlessly. In fewer than three hours it will be the fourteenth of March. We are unlikely to live until dawn on the fifteenth!'\
\
You shake your head to clear it, but still your mind is foggy. Is it really only half past nine in the evening of the thirteenth of March? The account seemed so vivid, so real...\
\
Your eyes turn toward the palantír. Denethor laughs, but there is no humour in it.\
\
'I have wrestled with the seeing-stone for many days, ${CLASS}. I am not surprised that the experience left you feeling unwell, and particularly susceptible to the words I spoke. Can you not see how the tale I spun you must surely follow from the images you beheld in the stone? The end has come. The end has come! The armies have not yet surrounded Minas Tirith, but they will. The folk have not yet thrown in with the Withered Tree, but they will! Grond has not yet come to the gates, but it will! How long can they stand against that ram? If they last even a minute longer than I believe, that will be a triumph. But it will not matter. All that I have told you will come to pass.'\
\
You try to tell the Steward that he is wrong, but you cannot find the words.\
\
'You have seen what I saw in the stone. Hirgon and the Red Arrow did not make it to Rohan, and the foolish one Mithrandir sent to Mordor is a captive in Cirith Ungol! Yes, I know of that errand. And I know it has failed! Whatever that fool brought with him is now gone, and if it is the weapon I perceive, it will not matter if the gates of Minas Tirith last five minutes or five hours. The end will come! It has already come!\
\
'Go, ${PLAYER}! Go and die! Every person in this city will follow you soon!'","Denethor has been wounded.","'Do you at last understand the words I have spoken, ${PLAYER}? Do you finally see that this doom cannot be avoided?'","You have hurried down to the ruin of the gates with Mithrandir. Only he can stand against the Witch-king.","Instancia: La hora más oscura","Peregrin Took is in grave danger!","'${PLAYER}... what could... we have done...?'","Gondor's darkest hour has come. The forces of Mordor have broken the gates of Minas Tirith, and the Witch-king of Angmar has brought his master's evil to bear upon the defenders of the White City.","'And so it ends, ${PLAYER}. The Wizard is slain, and will trouble my Master no longer. The city is taken!\
\
'What few defenders remain in the city will be rooted out and brought to this high place, and it is here they will die. You live only because I commanded it, but once the last cries of the dying have faded into the wind, you too will follow them.'","You must find Peregrin Took and protect him from the forces of the Enemy!","A shrill voice pierces the thin air above the city","Mithrandir stands alone before the Witch-king, blocking his passage into the city.","Gothmog stands before you at the top of the city, secure in victory.","Remain alert for any chance to help Peregrin or Denethor!","'Go and die, ${PLAYER}! There can be no avoiding the doom of which I have spoken!'"},
[7189]={"Instancia: El día que llegó el gigante","Something evil bears down on Dunfast.\
\
You should ensure that everyone has evacuated their homes.","You have gathered some meagre belongings, but you feel a great urge to keep moving","Ludeca is in Dunfast.\
\
You should speak with Ludeca.","Convince Forthere to evacuate","You find that you have not the will to go further. You are too afraid, brave though you are....","You have entered your own home","A terrible rumbling shakes the earth","Ask Ludeca about the snow","'O what will become of us? I am slow, but I will try to keep up.\
\
'Thank you, dear Gifemund, for coming to warn me! I am so afraid!'","Forthere's house is on the outskirts of Dunfast.\
\
You should break into Forthere's house.","Talk to Ludeca","Evacuate everyone! (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The rumbling came from north-west of town.\
\
You should search for the source of the rumbling.","The unearthly chill in Iothete's home reminds you that Iothete rarely comes here anymore. You hope that he is safe.","Léofburg reluctantly agrees to meet outside of Dunfast","You have come outside of your home in town to find the snow worse than any weather you have seen in this part of Rohan.","Break the lock to Forthere's home","Forthere is in his home in Dunfast.\
\
You should convince Forthere to evacuate immediately.","'I will be out to meet you shortly, Gifemund! I will not be much longer.\
\
'Between you and me, old friend, I have never been so afraid in my life! This unnatural winter has had me on edge, but...but this is worse....'","'You are pale as a ghost, Gifemund! Whatever is it?'\
\
You explain to your worried neighbours about the terrible force of menace and the blinding cold you felt north-west of the village.\
\
'We should evacuate! Whatever terror approaches, I do not like it!'","Ludeca is terrified of the sudden change of weather in Dunfast, as terrified as you are yourself","Listen to your neighbours","Search near the windmill for the source of the rumbling","'What is it, Gifemund?? Why does the earth shake?'\
\
You hastily tell Léofburg to gather warm cloaks, food, and water, and meet at Herethryth's farm.\
\
'I will do as you say, but...if we leave town, we shall all die of cold!'","You fear for your elderly neighbour, but an uncertain fate in the frozen wild is better than certain death in Dunfast","Get everyone out! Something evil bears down on Dunfast.","'The weather brought you out of your warm home as well, did it?\
\
'A little snow never bothered anyone, but this is indeed strange.'","Forthere's home is locked, as always. It is best to come back when all else is done.","'Only cowards flee their homes. Fight alongside me, Gifemund, and drive the enemy back!'\
\
Gifemund now recalls that he was still chilled by the icy power just outside of Dunfast. A heated argument between the two neighbours ensued, and Forthere became obstinate.","The rumbling sounded like it came from near the windmill","Forthere, beaten, was carried out and evacuated with the others....","'What in the world was that??\
\
'Gifemund, will you go look? You have experience in arms....'","Tell Ludeca of the terrible force north-west of Dunfast"},
[7190]={"Instancia: El entretenimiento del día","Watch the performance","Ulishár eagerly waits for the play to begin in the city of Zajâna.","'A hobbit? And so far from the Shire?\
\
'This performance has become most interesting, ${PLAYER}.'","Something has captured Inkanûsh's attention.","Talk to Inkanûsh in the audience","You and your companions have joined the audience to watch a theatrical entertainment performed by Têrkar's Travellers, a troupe to which Ulishár is indebted.","'I am so pleased to see that Têrkar's experience fighting in the north has not robbed him of his desire to perform!\
\
'I hope you enjoy the play, ${PLAYER}. They were most skilled when I met them, and their catalogue of entertainments was dense and varied!\
\
'Oh... they begin!'","While the performance continues, you should remain a model audience member.","'I have some criticisms about my portrayal, ${PLAYER}.'","'I enjoyed the performance, ${PLAYER}, as I knew I would, but... there are so many missing faces.\
\
'Did so few of my friends return from the war?'","Ulishár enjoyed the performance, but his expression is one of worry.","Talk to Ulishár in the audience"},
[7191]={"You hear a loud crash upstairs!","A loud crash came from upstairs.\
\
You should find the source of the crash.","Dagrun has been named Master!\
\
You should talk to Dagrun.","Instancia: La Cena Mortal","Hoskuld ran into the kitchen, seeming unwell.\
\
You should talk to Dagrun.","The dinner guests are conversing.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","Listen to the conversation","'Háta has been strangled?! Hoskuld's death could not have been an accident then. We are locked inside this manor with a murderer....'","You must accuse someone of murder!\
\
Choose wisely!","The dinner guests have all split up.\
\
You should talk to Dagrun.","Háta is dead!\
\
You should talk to Dagrun!","Maeriel has left the room, angered at the other guests' behaviour.\
\
You should go check on Maeriel.","A grand dinner is being hosted by the Elders of Lake-town, but the shadow of the late Master's murder still hangs over the manor. Something wicked is about to unfold.","'Master! I've been named Master! I wish it had not been in such gruesome circumstances. I think I'm in shock.'","Accuse someone of murder!","Maeriel lies slumped on the floor. She has been stabbed through the back with a carving knife!","'Let us give them some space to take the victims away.'","Háta did not return with the others.\
\
You should find Háta.","Find the source of the crash","Frekur did not commit the murders!","'Maeriel too... we must stay together now, ${PLAYER}. It is too easy for the fiend to end us one by one if we separate.'","Maeriel is dead!\
\
You should talk to Dagrun!","'Tell me, ${PLAYER}, how did these three behave in this time of crisis?'\
\
You tell the Elder of Orgrand's cowardice, Frekur's belligerence, and how Dagrun remained calm and collected while taking leadership.\
\
'I see. It is just as I thought. I will go and speak to the other Elders. Wait here.'","Hoskuld lies on the floor, unmoving, his face a deep maroon colour. You lean in closer and realize he is not breathing!","Find Háta","Thewár looks to have several broken bones from the fall, but the back of his head is bloody, as if struck by a heavy object. He is dead!","'It seems everyone else has already arrived! Let us join them at the dinner table. And do be on your best behaviour.'","Háta is dead!","Check on Hoskuld","'He is dead? How could this have happened?'","Orgrand seems disoriented and barely notices you approach.\
\
'What... what happened? I think someone struck me... Sútvif?'","Check on Thewár","Talk to Captain Álarr","Thewár has suddenly fallen down the stairs!\
\
You should check on Thewár!","Talk to Rikolf the Elder","'Fools, all of them! Panicking is not the solution here. Maeriel is a friend, however, and I do worry about her. Will you please go check on her?'","Háta lies on the floor. You see red marks around her neck. She has been strangled!","Dagrun has been waiting for you.\
\
You should talk to Dagrun.","Hoskuld ran into the kitchen, seemingly unwell.\
\
You should check on Hoskuld.","Orgrand did not commit the murders!","'I fear this will only become easier for the murderer as our numbers thin. Where is Orgrand? I realize I have not seen him in quite a while.'","You tell Captain Álarr all that has transpired.\
\
'The murderer must be someone present. There was no way into the manor from the outside. I no longer believe Skótmun was responsible for the Master's death either. Who had the most to gain by these deaths? It must be someone who would be in the running for the position; one of these four. I know it was not you, ${PLAYER}. You have been involved in the investigation from the beginning! Tell me who did this.'","Talk to Dagrun","Dagrun did not commit the murders!","Captain Álarr has arrived downstairs.\
\
You should talk to Álarr.","'Oh my, he did not seem well. Will you go check on him?'","You accuse Rikolf of murder!","Maeriel is dead!","Rikolf the Elder wants to speak with you.\
\
You should talk to Rikolf the Elder.","Hoskuld is dead!","Hoskuld is dead!\
\
You should talk to Dagrun!","Thewár is dead!","Check on Maeriel","Thewár is dead!\
\
You should talk to Dagrun!"},
[7193]={"'The Southrons will be upon us any moment. I dearly hope we are prepared. I am heartened that you are here with us, ${PLAYER}, at the very least.\
\
Now I must address the men.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Indir has been defeated!</rgb>","Baranor stands on the bridge before Arnach's keep.\
\
The Haradrim assault has be deflected. Baranor waits to talk with you.","<rgb=#FF0000>Dagor must not be defeated</rgb>","Talk to Baranor","'My arms are weary and sore, ${PLAYER}. I am not a young man! Let us retire and regroup.'","Defend Arnach","<rgb=#FF0000>Dagor has been defeated!</rgb>","Baranor stands on the bridge before Arnach's keep.\
\
Defend the keep with Baranor and his men.","'Oh, Dagor! What good can come of this folly? My heart cries, none, none at all.'","Instancia: La Defensa de Arnach","<rgb=#FF0000>Baranor has been defeated!</rgb>","Baranor stands on the bridge before Arnach's keep.\
\
The Haradrim are likely to attack soon. Talk to Baranor now.","<rgb=#FF0000>Indir must not be defeated</rgb>","'What madness is this? Running off into the night! Perhaps I was wrong... perhaps it is better he remained here in Arnach. Had he gone with Lord Forlong and behaved thus on the true field of battle... just think of the disgrace!\
\
'But I am rattled and winded from the combat. Let us retire, set the townsfolk at ease, and tend to the wounded. Then, without delaying overlong, we should set out in search of Dagor.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Baranor must not be defeated</rgb>","Baranor and his men brace themselves against the oncoming Haradrim assault."},
[7194]={"Nothwulf can be found to the south-west, along the road near the southern farms.\
\
Elfmar has asked you to aid Nothwulf defend the southern perimeter.","Nothwulf can be found to the south-west, along the road near the southern farms.\
\
Nothwulf will need your aid to defend the southern perimeter.","'The invading forces are in utter disarray. The loss of their leaders has caused great chaos, resulting in many of their riders and infantry retreating back north, towards Elthengels.\
\
'The Elfward continue to drive back those intent on pursuing the assault, but I believe we have saved the village and its people.'","Botglim has been defeated","Elfmar and members of the Elfward await at the opening to the mead hall of Faldham.\
\
Elfmar and the Elfward must be notified that you have defeated the commanders of the attacking army.","Speak to Nothwulf along the road to the south-west","Osin has approached Nothwulf from the west","Nothwulf is prepared to defend the southern border","Speak to Thane Elfmar at the mead hall gates","Defeat Urbhár, the Orc commander","'I am pleased to have you along with me, ${PLAYER}. Let us show these invaders the merit of the Elfward!'","Defend Faldham with the help of Thane Elfmar","Ride with Osin to defend the south-west edge of Faldham","Langfrith defends the gate to the mead hall of Faldham.\
\
Langfrith has been guarding the mead hall entrance, and Osin believes that he may need your assistance.","The enemy forces have been routed","Elfmar has asked you to aid Nothwulf to the south-west","Elfmar remains ready, just north of the road fork at the north edge of Faldham.\
\
The defence against the White Hand forces has begun, and Thane Elfmar seems both confident and prepared.","'The initial surge of riders has been dealt with, and I will be able to hold the North-east edge on my own.\
\
'Nothwulf was protecting the perimeter of the farms a short distance to the south, I would ask that you see to his success there.'","'The enemy forces have reached the threshold of Faldham. The Elfward have  taken up positions around the perimeter to defend our borders, but they will need your assistance.\
\
'I expect the first waves to come from the north. Ride with me as we watch the northern borders. Take courage, and fight well.'","Urbhár has been defeated","'Elfmar holds the east? Then we must defend the other borders! Will you ride out to meet the enemy at my side?'","Defeat Botglim, the Uruk commander","'Exceptional work at the borders, ${PLAYER}. Few Orcs have made it this far into the village.\
\
'I noticed a few of the invaders shouting about their war-chieftains, commanding from just north of the mead hall. Defeat this Urbhár and this Botglim, and throw the attacking force into chaos.'","'To the west, I spotted several bands of Orcs headed towards Faldham. They seem to be pressing from every flank.\
\
'I came at once. I require your aid if we are to dispose of the attacking foes.'","Ride with Nothwulf to defend the southern perimeter","Thane Elfmar has gathered the Elfward and prepared for a strike against the village of Faldham. The Rohirrim intend to defend against the waves of Orcs and Uruks without the aid of Athelward or Théoden's riders.","Speak with Nothwulf about the defences","'I will gather up the others when the last enemy has been driven back, and we can discuss matters when all is quiet again.'","Langfrith believes the invading commanders can be found north of the mead hall","Urbhár and Botglim can be found north of the mead hall.\
\
Langfrith believes that defeating the commanders of the invaders, Urbhár and Botglim, may disrupt the ongoing assault.","'We still hold the southern edge intact, the enemy shall not penetrate from this side while I remain vigilant.\
\
'The enemy will try to find another way around our defences. Osin will need your aid to the west, while I remain behind to watch the flank.'","Elfmar remains ready, just north of the road fork at the north edge of Faldham.\
\
Thane Elfmar wishes to speak with you about the defences of Faldham.","'Make haste, friend! Langfrith awaits at the mead hall entrance, to the north.'","Speak to Langfrith guarding the mead hall gates","Nothwulf has asked you to aid Osin defend to the west","Speak to Thane Elfmar","Nothwulf awaits at the southern edge of Faldham.\
\
Nothwulf wishes to speak about the ongoing defence of the town.","Instancia: La defensa de Faldham"},
[7195]={"The servants of Isengard want revenge for the uprising of the people of Galtrev.","'We will await your return and welcome you as a friend.'","'Thank you, Duvodiad, for your aid... the people of Galtrev are in your debt.'","The Gathering Hall cannot be saved","Defeat the Uruk-hai master and his forces","Galtrev is safe for now","Defend Galtrev from the White Hand forces.","Do not allow the Gathering Hall to burn","The White Hand is attacking","Bron is in Galtrev.","'Saruman's Orcs have come to burn out the village. There are many people inside... we must defend them!'","Instancia: La defensa de Galtrev","Talk to Bron","You should talk to Bron."},
[7196]={"Has defendido Puente de Caballetes","Habla con Halbarad","'Los orcos están casi sobre la ciudad. ¡Ven rápido conmigo, debemos convencer a la señorita Bosquejo de la amenaza que se le viene encima!'","Has viajado con Halbarad a Puente de Caballetes para ayudar en su defensa contra los orcos de la tribu Ongbúrz.","'¡Hoy lo hemos hecho bien! También te estoy en deuda por tu ayuda, pues temo que la batalla se habría vuelto en contra de los Pueblos Libres si no hubieras estado aquí.\
\
Debo irme ahora, y espero que no sea mucho pedirte que te quedes. Te pediría que asegures que Puente de Caballetes permanezca a salvo durante la noche y luego regreses conmigo a Esteldín.\
\
¡Ha sido una gran victoria, amigo mío, una gran victoria de verdad!'","Halbarad se encuentra en Puente de Caballetes, cerca de Nellie Bosquejo.\
\
Junto a Halbarad y el pueblo de Trestlebridge, has defendido la ciudad contra los orcos Ongbúrz.","Ayuda a Halbarad en la defensa de Puente de Caballetes.","Instancia: La defensa de Puente de Caballetes","'Te llevaré de vuelta a la casa de Nellie.'"},
[7197]={"Has defendido Puente de Caballetes","Habla con Halbarad","'Los orcos están casi sobre la ciudad. ¡Ven rápido conmigo, debemos convencer a la señorita Bosquejo de la amenaza que se le viene encima!'","Has viajado con Halbarad a Puente de Caballetes para ayudar en su defensa contra los orcos de la tribu Ongbúrz.","'¡Hoy lo hemos hecho bien! También te estoy en deuda por tu ayuda, pues temo que la batalla se habría vuelto en contra de los Pueblos Libres si no hubieras estado aquí.\
\
Debo irme ahora, y espero que no sea mucho pedirte que te quedes. Te pediría que asegures que Puente de Caballetes permanezca a salvo durante la noche y luego regreses conmigo a Esteldín.\
\
¡Ha sido una gran victoria, amigo mío, una gran victoria de verdad!'","Halbarad se encuentra en Puente de Caballetes, cerca de Nellie Bosquejo.\
\
Junto a Halbarad y el pueblo de Trestlebridge, has defendido la ciudad contra los orcos Ongbúrz.","Ayuda a Halbarad en la defensa de Puente de Caballetes.","Instancia: La defensa de Puente de Caballetes","'Te llevaré de vuelta a la casa de Nellie.'"},
[7198]={"'Tárandil! You have to keep fighting! We are going to get through this!\
\
'What did father give to Ohtar? This is not the time for this, brother! Keep fighting!'","Instancia: El desastre","Vágari believed Isildur attempted to swim across the river in order to escape.","Find some sign that Isildur made for the river-bank","Hear the words of Vëamacil as remembered by Vágari","'I found him at last, but could make no sense of his expression: mixed pain and elation.'","Talk to Vágari the Wanderer","Talk to Tárandil","Vágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.","'Tárandil, you are alive! Thank the Valar!\
\
'Things go ill for us, brother. Father sent his esquire away before the fighting became too thick, entrusting Ohtar to bear the shards of Narsil away from the battle. But I fear he did not give him the object of the Orc's desire, and if we do not do something they will seize it!'","Vágari believed Isildur ran for the river-bank, and he desperately searched for some sign of the king's escape.","'Had Ohtar taken the Ring? I had to know!'","Swim across the river to find Isildur","'His armour lay among the reeds, discarded. He must have intended to swim!'","'But for men such as me, death was no escape.'","The shade that came to be called Vágari the Wanderer desires to confess to you the misdeeds of his past.","'My muscles ached. The swim had taken its toll on me, and I knew I must rest before attempting the return journey. I would hide among the reeds and wait until the Orcs prowling on the distant shore had abandoned their vigil; then I would swim back with my prize.\
\
'Despite my exhaustion, I had to complete the task I had set for myself. It was time.'","'The river-bank! He must have escaped to the river-bank!'","'He discarded his armour on the bank of the river.'","'All is lost, all is ashes! A thousand curses upon you!\
\
'Without the Ring I cannot fulfill my bond... I cannot save my family! Bravantel, Héol, I tried! I tried, I tried!'","Hear the words of Meldaran as remembered by Vágari","'I became separated from Isildur during the fighting, and while I was engaged with the Orcs on one flank of our diminishing circle, he gave something to his esquire Ohtar.\
\
'Ohtar vanished during the fighting. Did he escape? And more importantly: what was he given? What was he given?'","Listen to Vágari's account","'During the confusion, I lost sight of Isildur. Where had he gone, and did he still have the Ring? If he escaped now, my bargain with the Nazgûl would come to naught!'"},
[7199]={"Survive the reemergence of Hrímil Frost-heart","Instancia: Las lealtades divididas de Glúrkub el Trasgo","Acquiring the mithril hammer for Gorgar was only the beginning.","Carry out Gorgar's plan","Gorgar has chosen you for some unknown purpose.","The War of Three Peaks is underway!","You have run with Muzmák from the War of Three Peaks... but how far will be enough?","Command Ránulur to fight on behalf of Gorgar","'Count me in, Glúrkub. This place won't be safe for us when the hobgoblins take over!\
\
'Who plans to lead the raiding-party we will join? Natsatúg? Ah, that is good to know. It won't be easy, but I think I can get my hands on some of the badges his boys wear when they leave the mountain. You know the ones, with the thunderclouds on 'em?\
\
'We'll blend right in, and when we're safely in the country we'll slip away for our better lives. It's a good plan.'","Glúrkub tiene una historia que contar... pero ¿cuánto de ella se puede creer?","Continue working for Gorgar","'This is... this is not far enough....\
\
'We have to... we have to keep going....'","Hrímil Frost-heart has emerged from her icy prison behind the Anvil of Winterstith!","'If what the Dragon has said is true... the dwarves are doomed to fail. Do we flee from certain victory, Glúrkub?'\
\
Muzmák stares into the sky.\
\
'We should return to Gundabad. I do not know what ever compelled us to leave. That is our place. The new Lord of Gundabad commands it.'","Muzmák stands in silence upon the snowfield.","Talk to Muzmák in Durshulot","Gorgar has need of a goblin to acquire a valuable treasure for him.","'I need you to come with me, goblin. You are just what I need for my purposes.'\
\
Gorgar scowls at the line of goblins, every one of whom wears a relieved expression.\
\
'I have seen the glint of mithril inside an old tomb, but the entrance is sealed by a great rock-fall. No Orc can make it through the opening, and it might be too small for most goblins. But you, I think, will serve. You will bring me this treasure, and be rewarded by Gorgar the Generous.'","Continue your flight from the war","Muzmák gave you the names of three similar-minded residents of Durshulot who might help you escape from the growing conflict beneath Gundabad.","An unexpected visitor has interrupted your plans.","You ran far from the battle-lines, eventually finding yourself on distant snowfields.","'You're part of Muzmák's gang, eh? If we get found out I'm tellin' Gorgar it was all his idea. Are you all right with that, Glúrkub?\
\
'Then I'm in. Gorgar is losing his power to the hobgoblins, day by day. Won't be good for any of us to still be here when he loses the last of it!'","'Are you sure this plan of yours is going to work, goblin? I'm taking a real risk siding with you, and it'll be our heads if we're discovered!\
\
'The dragon who commands the hobgoblins might be trapped behind the Anvil of Winterstith, but that has not decreased their numbers here! They're pushing us out, Orcs and goblins both! I don't like it. And why hasn't Gorgar stood up to them? Bah.'\
\
Muzmák peers around suspiciously and lowers his voice.\
\
'So the plan is still on? We'll join the next raiding party heading south, and once free of the mountains we'll slip away? We'll set up somewhere far from Gundabad, far from Gorgar, and far from these accursed hobgoblins? All right. I've chosen three others who might join us. Speak to them and see what you think, goblin. Their names are Shulgolb, Lumbag, and Zogmauk, and they're all here in Durshulot.'","Collect the mithril treasure sought by Gorgar","Muzmák is waiting to speak with you.","Talk to Zogmauk","Talk to Muzmák during the War of Three Peaks","Gorgar believes there is a mithril treasure in the room on this side of the rock-fall.","Talk to Shulgolb","'I could join your little band, it's true.\
\
'Or I could turn you and your friends in for traitors and cowards!'","'Are they with us? Ah, I wondered about Zogmauk. At least he has been dealt with before he could cause us any more -'\
\
Muzmák suddenly stops speaking.\
\
'What is that? Someone comes!'","You served Gorgar faithfully and well.","Carry out the wishes of Gorgar the Ruthless","Talk to Lumbag","Talk to Muzmák as he catches his breath","Gorgar the Ruthless has sent you to command the loyalty of Ránulur, Chieftain of Wargs.","Remain alert during Gorgar's inspection","'What did you say? A great force of dwarves approaches the mountain? Even now they near Elderslade, and Gorgar commands that I fight on his behalf?'","Talk to Gorgar the Ruthless","Talk to Muzmák","'We are taking a big risk trusting you again, Glúrkub. How are we to know you don't plan to trick us, and turn us in to Gorgar?\
\
'Pox and maggots, there's nothing for it. We'll fight through the dwarf-lines and make for freedom... and if you betray us, Glúrkub, I'll see that you die for it!'"},
[7200]={"Debes encontrar las Forjas de los Anillos de Tham Mírdain.","'Fui un necio al dejarme engañar tan fácilmente por Amarthiel, y eso nos ha llevado hasta aquí. Sin embargo, aún hay esperanza, pues me dejó con vida. Tal vez, si logramos impedir que reforge a Narchuil, Narmeleth pueda ser recuperado.\
\
'Para entrar en Tham Mírdain, necesitarás derrotar al Gorthorog que guarda las llaves de las forjas. Su nombre es Strok, y es un enemigo formidable.\
\
'¡Date prisa, ${PLAYER}! ¡No hay tiempo que perder!'","Aunque gravemente herido, Laerdan aún respira débilmente.","Sigue a Amarthiel y a Mordrambor","Amarthiel no te presta atención alguna, consumida por completo por su aflicción. Aunque ha sufrido terriblemente a manos de sus antiguos aliados, todavía puede representar una amenaza para el Norte. Debes llevarla como prisionera de los Pueblos Libres y dejarla a su merced.","Un Laerdan gravemente herido yace al pie del puente","Has llegado cerca de las ruinas de Tham Mírdain, las Forjas de los Anillos de Eregion, donde Amarthiel pretende reforjar a Narchuil. Debes encontrar la manera de poner fin a su plan.","Strok derrotado","Entra en Tham Mírdain","Has encontrado a Laerdan en la entrada de Tham Mírdain, gravemente herido. Deberías averiguar a través de él qué ocurrió.","Encuentra las Forjas de los Anillos de Tham Mírdain","Debes encontrar a Amarthiel antes de que pueda reforjar a Narchuil.","Has descubierto las Forjas de los Anillos de Tham Mírdain","Has entrado en Tham Mírdain","Instancia: El Destino del Norte","Derrota al guardián de la puerta, Strok","Amarthiel fue interrumpida por la llegada del Númenóreano Negro Mordrambor. Deberías seguirlos para descubrir qué nuevo mal ha surgido.","Laerdan te indicó que encontraras y derrotaras al Gorthorog Strok, quien posee las llaves de Tham Mírdain.","Debes enfrentarte a Amarthiel en las Forjas de los Anillos de Tham Mírdain.","Enfréntate a Amarthiel","Deberías usar las llaves recuperadas de Strok para ingresar en Tham Mírdain.","Encuentra a Amarthiel en algún lugar dentro de Tham Mírdain"},
[7201]={"Fasti is speaking with the owner of the tavern in order to arrange a table for you.","Talk to Ránnvig in the Dragonbone Inn","Talk to Kólfith in the Dragonbone Inn","'Ránnvig has been a good friend to my family for many years. Do not cause any trouble for her and we will get along fine, stranger.'","'This town is built upon the Lake, ${PLAYER}, and the water rises and falls around it. There is an order to this place. If that balance is upset, Lake-town suffers. You should know your place here, ${PLAYER}. It's dangerous to ask questions about Karazgar here. You might not like the answers.'","Follow Fasti to your table","Wait inside the Dragonbone Inn for Kólfith to arrive","Return to your table by the fire","Authi Gem-cutter is in the Dragonbone Inn, and he wishes to speak to you.","This patron of the Dragonbone Inn has had more than his share and pays you no mind.","Survive the confrontation in the Dragonbone Inn","'That was an invigorating fight, ${PLAYER}, and all the better because I did not expect it! Perhaps I must elevate this tavern one place in my personal ranking of drinking spots; now it is my second-favourite, and not my third!'","Talk to Fasti inside the Dragonbone Inn","'Hello there, friend. I hope you do not mind my intrusion, but I have not seen you at the Dragonbone Inn before today, and it seems to me you must have an interesting story or two to tell! This is my third-favourite drinking spot, and I never miss an opportunity to sample the local brew whenever chance brings me through Lake-town, as it has today. Another opportunity I never miss: learning more about the folk who cross my path, and the adventures that led them to cross it!'\
\
The dwarf laughs heartily and strokes his beard.\
\
'I am called Authi Gem-cutter, and I am at your service, of course! What brings you to the Dragonbone Inn? Men and women are no rarity in Dale and Lake-town, but I can tell from your dress and bearing that you have passed through many lands to come here. Which is the furthest, would you say?'\
\
You consider your travels and hazard a guess. Authi nods wisely.\
\
'That is quite a ways, friend! I am something of a traveller myself, for it runs in my family, but I take most joy in the fashioning of complex trinkets and the improvement of my handiwork. Of late I have been less successful, I'm afraid, and it is not just my own craft that suffers!'","'You should keep moving. We don't need your company today.'","'It is long past time someone stood up to Kólfith. He has been a source of much trouble for the patrons of my inn, and I am glad he has been put in his place. He will not dare to show his face around here for some time, and when he does I wager I will have no trouble finding folk to show him the door.\
\
'Is it true he worked for Karazgar? That explains much about his dealings and about the company he has kept. Good riddance to him!\
\
'You, however, will always be welcome at the Dragonbone Inn, ${PLAYER}!'","You have some time to wait before Kólfith arrives","The dwarf ignores you. He seems content to sit and take in the scenery, keeping to himself.","'Smaug has been dead these many years! I say let him lie, and forget him, even if the Lake will not!'","'Bah, nothing but fanciful imaginings. There are no more dragons about, no matter what the old folk may say.\
\
'Drink up, stranger, and pay no heed to such stories!'","You should return to your table in the Dragonbone Inn.","'I always have time for a good brawl and a refreshing ale! Let us speak outside, ${PLAYER}. I have something I'd like to ask you.'","Fasti told you to wait for Kólfith to arrive.","A man of Lake-town has offered you information on Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and agreed to meet you inside the Dragonbone Inn.","'Have you seen the bones of the Dragon, stranger? They are hard to miss, for even a cursory glance will reveal their blanched horror, and none could mistake them for anything but the legacy of their cruel owner, no longer living.\
\
'We were just discussing what has caused their emergence from the Lake. My wife believes that soil and other deposits washed downstream have collected beneath the buildings of Old Lake-town, raising both the pilings and the Dragon's bones above the water.\
\
'I think the Lake cannot bear to hold Smaug's malice any longer, and belches him forth, revealing him to the sun and to the stars. What say you?'","A dwarf has come to your table in the Dragonbone Inn.","'There are many forces at work in Lake-town, friend. You had best keep to yourself or you might get hurt. Most of the folk here are good people.'\
\
The man shares a look with his companion before turning back to face you again.\
\
'Most,' he says.","'Lake-town has always been good to me. It is not an easy life, but if you work hard the Lake will provide. Years ago it was different. You know when I mean: the days of the Dragon. But he is long gone, and only his bones remain.\
\
'I raise a mug to his ferocity, and to the memory of those good folk who lost their lives to it!'","Authi Gem-cutter has been defeated!","Talk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Dragonbone Inn","This man of Lake-town spends most of his days in the Dragonbone Inn, deep in his cups. He has no information for you, or if he does he is in no condition to share it with you.","Fasti is inside the Dragonbone Inn, waiting to show you to a table where you can wait for Kólfith.","'You aren't from around here, are you? Keep to yourself and cause no trouble, and you should have no problems in Lake-town. I have lived here all my life, and I come often to the Dragonbone Inn for Ránnvig's finest ale.\
\
'Why, it has been almost an entire week since the last brawl! Time passes swiftly in safety, I suppose.'","'I am sure Kólfith will be along to speak with you shortly, ${PLAYER}. There are two taverns in Lake-town, but the Dragonbone Inn is always full of patrons; the noise makes it most well-suited to conducting discreet business.'","Instancia: Los Huesos del Dragón","Kólfith has come to the Dragonbone Inn, seeking to punish you for asking about Karazgar.","Kólfith has come to the Dragonbone Inn, but his friendly demeanor has fallen away and he seems eager for a fight.","<rgb=#FF0000>Authi Gem-cutter must not be defeated</rgb>","Remain alert for signs of trouble","Ránnvig, the proprietor of the Dragonbone Inn, has some words for you."},
[7202]={"Witness the visions granted by Mótsog","'They called it Durin's Bane, but I knew it by another name, in another age. Long before the creature came to hide in this forgotten cavern I knew it as Askâdurs, and the memory of its scorching passage through my city in the heights is cruel.\
\
'But that was long ago.'","Durin stands in the forgotten chamber deep beneath Gundabad, boiling with rage.","The dwarf claiming to be Mótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.","'Something is not right, ${PLAYER}. Some servant of Mótsog the Traitor may lie in wait, seeking to harm us.\
\
'Remain on your guard.'","The dwarf claiming to be Mótsog says he can show Durin what he has forgotten.","A strange sorcery envelopes the forgotten chamber deep below Gundabad. What secrets lie within?","'You are a friend of Durin? Then you too will see what I have to show him.'","Witness the visions granted by the stranger","Durin has asked you to remain alert for any sign of danger.","Talk to Mótsog","'It has been both curse and blessing to see these trials, for it was the will of the First Crafter that I should be unable to look away.\
\
'I have seen moments of triumph, but so too have I seen defeats that would scar the iron heart of any dwarf, marking him forever with its imprint.'","Mótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.","Instancia: El Enano Soñador","'It has always been difficult for me to see these trials, unable to intervene.\
\
'It is no reward, friend of Durin, to remain helpless in this. But it could not be otherwise. The dreaming sight cares not.'","Mantente en guardia","Talk to Durin in the forgotten chamber","It cannot be denied that Mótsog possesses a curious power. How can he reveal these visions to you?","'Aye. That is the fate of Durin in every age in which he appears.'\
\
Mótsog's expression is devoid of emotion and impossible to read.\
\
'I have seen them all.'","Talk to the strange dwarf"},
[7203]={"'Salgamos de aquí, ${PLAYER}. Me alegro... de no morir aquí...'","Entra en Ghân-gharâf a través del pasaje despejado","A través de pasajes secretos llenos de agua, el Guardián del Agua ha regresado a Ghân-gharâf para descubrir algo inesperado: aventureros que desean desafiarlo.","'Yo... no puedo creer que...'\
\
Temblando de todo su cuerpo, Bróin tiene muchas dificultades para expresarse.\
\
'¡El... el monstruo... en el agua... Tengan mucho cuidado, amigos...'","Habla con Bróin","Bori ha despejado un camino hacia Ghân-gharâf y ahora deberías adentrarte por él.","'Si tú y tus aliados logran despejar los pasajes inundados que hay entre Gundlajân y Ghân-gharâf, quizás aún podamos encontrar las armerías de las que se habla en el Libro de Mazarbul.\
\
'¿Podría ser que encontremos Zigilburk allí? ¡Eso espero, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Si los registros que he estudiado son correctos, los enanos erigieron grandes mecanismos aquí para sellar varios de los pasajes cuando los grodbogs se volvieron demasiado numerosos. Tendrás que lidiar con las criaturas y aprender a operar los mecanismos para despejar el camino. Te seguiré una vez que haya terminado de examinar el mapa de estos lugares, porque es muy confuso y necesitaremos orientarnos.'","Instancia: La Tesorería Ahogada","Bróin está débil, pero quizás puedas rescatarlo de las profundidades inundadas antes de que el Guardián regrese furioso.","Habla con Bori","Los túneles inundados que conectan Gundlajân y Ghân-gharâf están bloqueados por antiguos mecanismos de fabricación enana, y también están infestados de todo tipo de criaturas horribles. Ambos problemas deberán ser resueltos.","Has acompañado a Bori a los pasajes inundados bajo las Obras Hidráulicas, donde él cree que aún podría encontrarse Zigilburk.","'¿Realmente... estás aquí... mis amigos? ¿Es esto una... aparición?'\
\
Bróin tose, y por primera vez ves el hacha que brilla a su lado: un hacha tan hermosa, brillante y fría que sólo puede estar hecha de mithril.\
\
Bróin se da cuenta de tu mirada y sonríe débilmente.\
\
'La bestia me trajo a este lugar... pensando en guardarme para más tarde... supongo; una de sus víctimas llevaba esto. Ahora es todo huesos, pero le debo la vida, quienquiera que fuera. Podía mantener a la bestia a raya... con el hacha de mithril... pero no tenía la fuerza para escapar. Habría... muerto de hambre.\
\
'¿Dices que Bori está contigo? ¡Qué... maravilla! ¡Le daré una sorpresa, supongo! ¡El buen viejo Bori!'","Enfréntate al Guardián del Agua","Bori está justo dentro de la puerta que da acceso a Gundlajân.\
\
Bori te espera para explicarte su plan.","Despeja un camino a través de los túneles inundados para llegar a Ghân-gharâf","Has descubierto a Bróin en las ruinas inundadas de Ghân-gharâf. A pesar de su lucha contra el Guardián del Agua frente a las Puertas de Durin, sigue vivo."},
[7204]={"Find Frodo on the slopes of Orodruin","You have found Frodo and Sam on the slope of Mount Doom, but you do not have long before the slope will be engulfed in flame!","You have obtained the Phial of Galadriel","'Frodo has fulfilled the Quest of the Ring, and he may still live! We must act quickly, ${PLAYER}, or he will never come alive from the Black Land. If Gwaihir and his brother will bear us into Mordor, we may yet come to Frodo in time!\
\
'Gwaihir, Lord of Eagles! Two times have you borne me, my friend, and this will be the last and the most needed! If your brother Landroval will bear ${PLAYER}, we will have the best chance of finding Frodo before he is overcome!\
\
'Fly now to Orodruin! Fly now to Mount Doom!'","'${PLAYER}! Is that... is that you...?'","'${PLAYER}... is that... really you...?'\
\
Sam looks at you with bleary eyes; his exhaustion is apparent, and he seems to disbelieve that you are really standing here.\
\
'We can't... go any further.... We got this far... but...'\
\
Sam reaches into one of his pockets and withdraws a small item. He presses it into your hand.\
\
'Where there's... life... there's hope...' he says.","'Gwaihir and the Eagles will keep the Nazgûl occupied, but the battle still rages upon the ground, ${PLAYER}! Let us press the advantage given to us by our winged allies and set the Orcs upon their heels!'","Mithrandir is on the slag-hill before the Black Gate.","Remain on your guard!","Aragorn is on the slag-hill as the Battle of the Morannon rages all around him.","You found Frodo and Sam... they are alive!","You must stand on the edge of the outcropping if Gwaihir and his kin are to see you!","'Do you sense that? Something is amiss, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot discern what it might be. Some new artifice of the Dark Lord may be revealed to us!\
\
'Stay near to me!'","Instancia: ¡Vienen las águilas!","Talk to Samwise Gamgee on Orodruin","Talk to Aragorn on the slag hill","The Eagles have come to the aid of the Host of the West, and the tide of battle has turned!","Talk to Mithrandir on the slag hill","Landroval has set you down upon the slope of Mount Doom while the Eagles circle the Mountain and seek for Frodo on the far side.","Talk to Mithrandir on the slag-hill","Walk to the edge of the outcropping... there is little time to spare!"},
[7205]={"Hersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
After encountering a large company of Angmarim during your attempted escape, you have found the way out of Mîn Lorg blocked. You should talk to Hersegg.","'Of all the things I thought we might find in Mîn Lorg, another dwarf was not among them!\
\
'It won't be long before the Iron Crown discovers what has happened. And despite his age, Thrástan looks a hale enough dwarf...\
\
'We should leave this place while we still can, ${PLAYER}.'","Hersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
You have come to the entryway of an ancient dwelling at Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.","Thrástan can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
After rescuing Thrástan from the Iron Crown at Mîn Lorg, the old dwarf seems to be struggling to speak. You should talk to Thrástan.","The Iron Crown has sent a company of Angmarim to block your escape!","'What... has happened? Who are you... and how did you come to this place?'\
\
You introduce yourself to the old dwarf and explain that the Angmarim of the Iron Crown discovered the old delving after gaining entry to Gloomingtarn.\
\
'It... should not be so, and yet... it is. I am... Thrástan.'\
\
You ask Thrástan if he can stand. The old dwarf nods weakly.","Within the deepest reaches of Gloomingtarn, the Angmarim of the Iron Crown have unwittingly discovered a long-forgotten passage rumoured to conceal the greatest secret of Gloomingtarn.","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow Hersegg to be defeated</rgb>","Instancia: La Casa Mayor","'What... what is this place, my friend?\
\
Hersegg glances around the entryway of what appears to be an ancient dwelling in the caverns of Gloomingtarn.\
\
'It looks nearly untouched, ${PLAYER}, but how can that be so? Neither Orc nor dwarf have walked these halls in thousands of years, and yet, it is as neatly kept as any dwelling in the Lonely Mountain.\
\
'Perhaps the notes of the Iron Crown were not so far from the truth after all. Could it truly be that Durin the Deathless once dwelt within this... house?\
\
'We cannot allow the Angmarim to lay claim to it!'","'Another dwarf? What is he doing here?'\
\
Hersegg looks at the Angmarim standing over an old dwarf.\
\
'Let's listen for a moment and see if we can't learn more, ${PLAYER}. But if they even hint that they're going to harm him, I'm not going to let that happen!'","'Look what the Angmarim have done to this place, ${PLAYER}... it is terrible!\
\
'No matter what they have planned, we must put a stop to it. And not just for the Gabil'akkâ—the Iron Crown is defiling the very heritage of the Longbeards!\
\
'I just hope we're not too late!'","'${PLAYER}, are you all right?\
\
'When you and Hersegg did not return, my warriors feared the worst. And from what I can tell, that was very nearly the case!\
\
'Who is this now?'\
\
You tell Hermáth Stormhammer you discovered a dwarf named Thrástan captured by the Angmarim in Mîn Lorg.\
\
'Very well! Let us speak more of this at Watchers' Roost... and I shall have to have words with my granddaughter as well!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Hersegg has been defeated!</rgb>","Hersegg pauses, studying the structure around you","Rescue the dwarf captured by the Iron Crown","Fight through Mîn Lorg with Hersegg","Hersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
After helping Thrástan to his feet, you grow concerned that the Angmarim will soon return to Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.","Hersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
You have found an old dwarf captured by the Iron Crown at Mîn Lorg. You should rescue the dwarf.","'We mustn't stay here, ${PLAYER}. Let us return to Watchers' Roost!'","Escape Mîn Lorg with Hersegg and Thrástan","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
To your surprise, Hermáth Stormhammer and his warriors arrived to rescue you from the Angmarim of the Iron Crown. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","'We're cut off, ${PLAYER}. The only way out is through these Angmarim and we're outnumbered!'\
\
Hersegg glances at Thrástan.\
\
'Stay back, Thrástan. We'll protect you... no matter what.'","As the last of the Angmarim falls defeated, Hermáth Stormhammer calls you over","Hersegg and Thrástan can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
You should attempt to overcome the Angmarim of the Iron Crown barring your escape from Mîn Lorg.","Talk to Hersegg","As the Angmarim fall defeated, the old dwarf looks to you","Hersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
You have entered Mîn Lorg to confront the Iron Crown with Hersegg. You should talk to Hersegg.","After spying something in the distance, Hersegg quietly calls you over","Hersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.","Talk to Thrástan","Hersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.\
\
Hersegg has spied something in the distance at Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.","Defend Thrástan from the Iron Crown","Hersegg and Thrástan can be found at Mîn Lorg.","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer"},
[7206]={"'¿Cuáles eran los medios secretos para abrirlo que recuperaste de Katûb-zahar, ${PLAYER}? ¡Ah, sí! El gran herrero Ongli no deseaba ser molestado, ni siquiera por el propio Durin, a menos que se le saludara con elogios dignos de su estatus.\
\
'Debes <rgb=#FF0000>saludar</rgb> o <rgb=#FF0000>felicitar</rgb> o <rgb=#FF0000>honrar</rgb> su memoria, ${PLAYER}. ¡Espero que hayamos interpretado correctamente las pistas!'","'Las tres poderosas forjas de Nâr-khelab me llenan de asombro, ${PLAYER}; aún no puedo acercarme a ellas. Permíteme este momento para contemplar humildemente su majestad.\
\
'Si quieres, acércate a cada una de las tres forjas y busca el hacha de mithril Zigilburk. ¿Me atrevo a esperar que todavía pueda estar allí?'","<rgb=#FF0000>Saluda</rgb> o <rgb=#FF0000>felicita</rgb> o <rgb=#FF0000>honra</rgb> la memoria de Ongli","'¡Gracias por tu ayuda contra los trasgos, y contra los grodbogs antes que ellos!\
\
'¡Volvamos a la Cámara de la Encrucijada para contar nuestra victoria, y que el Corazón de Fuego ha sido desvelado!'","Has protegido a Bósi de los trasgos","'¿No encontraste Zigilburk, ${PLAYER}? No, no te disculpes -- no debería haber dejado que mis esperanzas se elevaran tanto. Seguramente han pasado muchos cientos de años desde que el hacha contempló el calor de estas forjas.\
\
'¡Volvamos a la Cámara de la Encrucijada y contemos a mi gente que el Corazón de Fuego ha sido encontrado!'","Viaja con Bósi al Corazón de Fuego","'Espero que esta aventura no sea en vano. Encontrar las legendarias forjas de Nâr-khelab sería un gran impulso para la moral de mi gente. Y si Zigilburk, el hacha de mithril, se encontrara dentro... no puedo describir lo mucho que nos ayudaría.\
\
'Continuemos, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Nos estamos acercando a la pared que podría estar ocultando la puerta que buscamos.'","Bósi está en el Corazón de Fuego, contemplando las majestuosas forjas ocultas.","Tú y Bósi han llegado a un pasillo descuidado en las Profundidades Occidentales, con la esperanza de encontrar una entrada a Nâr-khelab, el Corazón de Fuego.","Busca en las forjas de la derecha","La suposición de Bósi era correcta, y has encontrado la ubicación del Corazón de Fuego.","'Si el Corazón de Fuego existe realmente, creo que debe estar detrás de esta pared.\
\
'¿Cuál es el medio secreto de abrirlo que recuperaste de Katûb-zahar, ${PLAYER}? ¡Ah, sí! El gran herrero Ongli no quería ser molestado, ni siquiera por Durin, a menos que se le mostrara un gesto ceremonial de reconocimiento digno de su rango.\
\
'Deberías <rgb=#FF0000>saludar</rgb> o <rgb=#FF0000>felicitar</rgb> o <rgb=#FF0000>honrar</rgb>lo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Espero que hayamos leído las pistas correctamente!'","Busca en las forjas del centro","No hay señales de Zigilburk cerca de estas forjas","Busca en las forjas de la izquierda","Bósi te ha pedido que investigues el Corazón de Fuego, buscando a Zigilburk, el hacha de mithril.","Bósi está en el pasillo donde cree que se puede encontrar la entrada al Corazón de Fuego.\
\
Bósi te está esperando para hablar sobre cómo buscar la entrada.","¡Runas de plata brillan intensamente en la pared del túnel!","Bósi está en el pasillo donde cree que se puede encontrar la entrada al Corazón de Fuego.","Bósi cree que saludando o felicitando la memoria del enano que construyó el Corazón de Fuego, podrás acceder a él.","Instancia: El Pasaje Vacío","Habla con Bósi."},
[7207]={"'Tu oferta no me interesa, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué uso tengo yo, Gorothúl, de un orco tan inútil como Mazog? ¿Señor de las cuevas? ¡Es señor de nada! ¡Los enanos se arrastran por sus cuevas como gusanos sobre pan mohoso! ¡Bolgo estaría avergonzado de su hijo, y Azog lo mataría por deshonrar la línea de su familia!\
\
'Pero me divertiría tener a Mazog en las mazmorras de esta fortaleza hasta el fin del mundo, para que tenga tiempo de pensar en cómo ha fallado a su amo.\
\
'Aceptaré tu oferta.'","El Guardián de la puerta te ha llamado a pasar por la puerta de Dol Guldur para discutir el intercambio de Mazog por los enanos prisioneros.","Habla con Bróin","'No me gusta esto, ${PLAYER}. Debemos hacer que Gorothúl nos entregue a Bori, además de estos tres enanos, o habremos fracasado. ¿Qué podemos hacer?'","El intercambio ha sido un fracaso, y debes escapar... si puedes!","Ha llegado el momento de realizar el intercambio de Mazog por los enanos prisioneros. Muchos destinos pueden decidirse por el resultado de esta negociación...","Sigileth te ignora, su rostro es una máscara de ira y dolor. Decides dejarla en paz.","'El señor Celeborn creía que algunos de los Nazgûl habían venido a Dol Guldur, pero no sabía con certeza cuáles de los Nueve lo habían hecho. Ahora lo sabemos, aunque eso nos consuela poco.\
\
'El Teniente de Dol Guldur dirige a los demás; es el segundo solo después del Rey Brujo, aquel que provenía de Angmar en el norte. El Teniente de la Torre gobierna la fortaleza; es él quien abatió a Achardor.\
\
'La Languidez de Nurn era un hombre salvaje de esa tierra; ahora solo está poblada por esclavos de Mordor. Empuña un martillo de guerra en combate.\
\
'No sé nada de la Espada Negra salvo que una vez provenía de Lebennin. Ahora es completamente un siervo, al igual que todos los Nazgûl, aunque no siempre fue así.'","Sobrevive y escapa, si puedes","Bróin está apoyado en un bastón, esperando para hablar contigo.","Achardor se encuentra en la cima de la colina que lo separa de Bróin.","Achardor está esperando para hablar contigo sobre el próximo intercambio de Mazog por los enanos prisioneros.","Habla con Sigileth","Permanece junto a la Guardia Oculta mientras el guardián de la puerta considera la oferta","Habla con Achardor","Achardor ha pedido hablar contigo antes de que continúes hacia la puerta.","'Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Se siente bien tener una razón más allá de la venganza para esta misión nuestra. Aún ardo de odio hacia los Orcos, pero ahora también deseo rescatar a los enanos, mientras que antes solo era un propósito vago. \
\
'Haremos esto ahora por Bróin.'","La Guardia Oculta está lista en las puertas de Dol Guldur, esperando el regreso del Guardián de la puerta.","'Me equivoqué mucho sobre el enano Bróin, ${PLAYER}. Me arrepiento de lo que dije sobre él y sobre todos los enanos. Realizar un viaje aparentemente tan inútil para salvar a alguien que apenas conoce, alguien que ni siquiera es de su raza...demostró una fortaleza que pensé que solo los Elfos podían poseer. ¡Y lo hizo con mucho menos quejas de las que yo he hecho!\
\
'Pero míralo. Su viaje hacia el norte, a las lejanas regiones de los Lindes Oscuros, ha pasado factura incluso a su robusta forma; necesita descansar. Los guardias en la puerta de adelante verán su agotamiento como una debilidad, y no podemos permitir eso.\
\
'¿Le dirás que se quede aquí de tal manera que le ahorres sus sentimientos? Se ha demostrado a sí mismo para mí y para los demás por el resto del tiempo; no tiene necesidad de acompañarnos el resto del camino. Ayudó a Issuriel, y ahora deseo ayudarlo a salvar a su primo y a los demás enanos.'","Bróin ha regresado, pero ¿con qué propósito dejó Gadorgar sin previo aviso?","Achardor está tratando de decidir qué se puede hacer.","Viaja con la Guardia Oculta hasta las puertas de Dol Guldur","'Ninguno de esos enanos es Bori, ${PLAYER}? Lo sospechaba. Han sido cruelmente maltratados y parecen al borde de la muerte. ¿Dónde está Bori?'","Los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta tienen una decisión que tomar: esperar a que Bróin regrese o llevar a Mazog a las puertas de Dol Guldur sin él.","Instancia: El intercambio","Espera a que la Guardia Oculta decida qué se puede hacer","La Guardia Oculta se ha retirado de las puertas de Dol Guldur para reagruparse en Ost Galadh, su misión ha fracasado.","Sigue a la Guardia Oculta más allá de la puerta","Los Elfos de la Guardia Oculta lidian con la frustración y las palabras maliciosas de Mazog mientras deciden qué hacer.","'¿Qué significa esto, ${PLAYER}? Mientras llamabas a los exploradores en el perímetro de Dol Guldur, el enano Bróin desapareció de Ost Galadh. No le dijo a nadie a dónde iba... ¡y justo en la víspera del intercambio de Mazog por los suyos!\
\
'Habías hablado por él, ${PLAYER}. ¡No hablaste de su cobardía! ¿Acaso todos los enanos abandonan a sus compañeros cuando el camino se vuelve traicionero?'","Achardor está preocupado por los términos del acuerdo tal como los presentó Gorothúl.","'Lo siento, ${PLAYER}. Dame solo un momento....'\
\
Bróin se apoya en su bastón y trata de recuperar el aliento.\
\
'He caminado muchas millas hacia el norte en busca de la flor de Sereglos, y aunque tengo la resistencia de mi padre... todavía fue un viaje muy agotador. Que haya terminado con éxito, y que Issuriel se recupere del veneno de Gwigael, fue suficiente para darme más fuerza, pero...\
\
'Un momento más, amigo. Recuperaré el aliento en un momento...'","Continúa las negociaciones","'Se ha acabado, ${PLAYER}. Han muerto tantos, y aún así Bori languidece en las mazmorras de Dol Guldur. ¿Cómo podemos esperar luchar contra semejante mal?'","'¡Mira! ¡Ya vuelve la fuerza de Issuriel! ¡El Laidhris está funcionando para combatir el veneno de Gwigael!\
\
'Yo... no sé qué decir. Mientras me quejaba del destino injusto, el enano peinó el bosque durante muchas millas para encontrar una manera de salvar a Issuriel. ¡Debería haber sido yo, ${PLAYER}...\
\
'¡No puedo creer que estaba empezando a escuchar las palabras de Mazog! Ahora no habrá más retrasos. Iremos a las puertas para intercambiar a Mazog por los prisioneros y finalmente nos desharemos de él.'","Habla con Cúcheron","El guardián de las puertas de Dol Guldur está considerando la oferta.","Bróin se encuentra abajo de la colina que lo separa de Achardor y el resto de la Guardia Oculta.","La Guardia Oculta ha llegado a las puertas de Dol Guldur con el prisionero Mazog.","Gorothúl ha usado sus poderes para congelarte en el lugar, como lo hizo antes de Zabadgathol.","Habla con Gorothúl","'No sirve de nada, ${PLAYER}. Hemos fracasado. Vamos ahora dentro de Ost Galadh, aunque haya poco que podamos hacer ahora.'","'¡Hay poco tiempo para explicar, ${PLAYER}, así que debo ser rápido! Después de que le diste el Laidhris a Mazog y cuanto más lo pensaba, más me arrepentía de esa necesidad. ¡Si tan solo se pudiera hacer otra dosis!\
\
'Hablé con la Elfa Barvessain en la cima de la gran torre aquí en Ost Galadh, y me dijo que podrían encontrarse más sacos de veneno sin marcar de la Saewethil, con el tiempo, pero que la flor de Sereglos es tan rara que encontrar otra sería imposible. Las condiciones para que tal flor crezca son tan específicas que solo si se pudiera ralentizar la temporada de crecimiento podría encontrarse tal flor.\
\
'Caminé por el bosque durante muchas horas, dirigiéndome hacia el norte, y pasé a tierras más allá del alcance de la Hueste Dorada. Caminé, y caminé, y caminé, y justo cuando estaba a punto de darme la vuelta en derrota, vi un túmulo entre la maleza enmarañada. Un arroyo fluía a su lado, y de vez en cuando gotas del agua salpicaban sobre el túmulo, donde, brotando, crecía una sola flor, aún en temporada.\
\
'¡Con esta segunda flor de Sereglos, y otro saco de veneno sin marcar, se podría hacer otra dosis de Laidhris!'","Gorothúl ha salido de la fortaleza para negociar el intercambio de Mazog por los enanos prisioneros.","'Bueno, aquí estamos, ${PLAYER}. Ahora veremos si esta misión no fue tan temeraria como parecía al principio.\
\
¡Tendré a Cúmaeth listo por si nuestra primera creencia se confirma!'","'No quiero que los guardias de la puerta piensen que somos débiles, ${PLAYER}. ¡No lo pensarían si supieran la distancia que recorrí, y en tan poco tiempo!'\
\
Bróin se ríe.\
\
'¿Me pregunto si ese será el verso principal de \\qLa gloriosa historia de Bróin el poderoso,\\q después de todo? No parecía tan glorioso cuando me apresuraba a través de la oscuridad, tropezando con piedras y raíces traicioneras, buscando una flor que podría no existir en el mundo por mucho más tiempo.\
\
'Tal vez mi parte en todo esto ha terminado, ${PLAYER}. No quiero perjudicar las negociaciones por Bori. Me quedaré aquí y protegeré la retaguardia. Confío en que Achardor y los demás podrán cumplir esta misión.'"},
[7208]={"'${PLAYER}, ¿por qué has venido aquí? Esta no es tu lucha. Necesito enfrentar a Amarthiel a solas, como debí haber hecho hace mucho tiempo.\
\
'Pero ya es tarde para eso. Si logro mantener la atención de Amarthiel el tiempo suficiente, podrás apoderarte de la Piedra Vidente. La enfrentaremos juntos y quizá no perciba el peligro. Cuando te dé la señal, debes tomar la Piedra Vidente y correr de inmediato hacia la entrada de Barad Tironn. ¡No te demores! Llévala a Calenglad y tal vez pueda enmendar mis antiguos errores.\
\
'Que los Valar sonrían a tu empeño y al mío, ${PLAYER}. Vamos.'","'¡No hay tiempo que perder, ${PLAYER}! Lloro por Laerdan, pero debemos recuperar la Piedra Vidente y sacarla de Annúminas.\
\
'¿Está todo listo?","Entra en Barad Tironn y busca la Piedra Vidente","La Piedra Vidente está sobre su pedestal en lo profundo de Barad Tironn.\
\
Laerdan ha dado la señal: alguien del grupo debe tomar la Piedra Vidente y llevarla a Calenglad en la entrada de Barad Tironn. ¡Rápido!","Calenglad se encuentra en la entrada de Barad Tironn.\
\
Debes proteger a quien transporte la Piedra Vidente y asegurarte de que llegue a manos de Calenglad en la entrada de Barad Tironn. ¡Rápido!","Has entregado la Piedra Vidente a Calenglad","La Piedra Vidente se encuentra en algún lugar dentro de Barad Tironn.\
\
Debes encontrar la Piedra Vidente y robarla antes de que Amarthiel pueda usarla para descubrir la ubicación de Narchuil.","Entrega la Piedra Vidente a Calenglad en la entrada de Barad Tironn","¡El terrible poder de Amarthiel te ha vencido","Amarthiel y la Piedra Vidente están dentro de Barad Tironn.\
\
Laerdan se ha enfrentado a Amarthiel y ahora aguardas su señal para tomar la Piedra Vidente y sacarla de Barad Tironn.","Sobrevive al encuentro con Amarthiel","'La Piedra Vidente está en algún lugar dentro de Barad Tironn, ${PLAYER}. Mi gente ha logrado llevarte hasta aquí, pero debemos mantener la línea. Tendrás que encontrar la Piedra Vidente por tu cuenta.\
\
'Si puedes ayudar a Laerdan de algún modo una vez dentro, hazlo, pero la prioridad es recuperar la Piedra Vidente. En cuanto la tengas, tráela aquí con toda la rapidez posible. Si Amarthiel se da cuenta de lo ocurrido, hará todo lo que esté a su alcance para impedir que escapes con ella, así que debes actuar con rapidez.'","¡No lograste escapar con la Piedra Vidente!","Instancia: El Ojo de Angmar","Alguien debe tomar la Piedra Vidente","Laerdan escuchó de manera imprudente las palabras de Mordrambor y se internó solo en Barad Tironn para desafiar a Amarthiel. Calenglad te ha pedido que le robes la Piedra Vidente y ayudes a Laerdan si es posible."},
[7209]={"You have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Agalûnu wants to talk to you.","You have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should stop and appreciate the beauty of the grove with Agalûnu.","'I did not expect this ${PLAYER}. Have I and my forebears really been party to the destruction of a forest that covered the entire Ikorbân Valley? That is just awful. I can see why this Elf would not like us overmuch!'","Shanthar gazes at the woman, his expression unreadable.\
\
'You know not of which you speak, child. I have sworn an oath to steward these grounds and protect them with my life. Why I have done so is none of your concern. What I do not understand is why Men insist on destroying everything beautiful in Middle-earth.\
\
'Trees provide shade, they disrupt harsh winds, they protect the soil from the river. They provide homes to birds, squirrels and insects. They provide food for all. Long ago, this entire valley was a forest, dense with trees exactly like these. Then Men came and 'put them to use' as you would do. They are already in use, only you do not see it.'","Talk to Agalûnu","'Oh, ${PLAYER}, this place is so lovely! Just look at it!'","Instancia: El desvanecimiento de los bosques","Outraged that a Kinta Elf shot her with an arrow in an attempt to get her to leave Arwáth, Agalûnu has asked you to escort her into the grove to confront Shanthar.","Listen to the conversation","Talk to Shanthar","'${PLAYER}, can you believe him? How galling!'\
\
Agalûnu turns to Shanthar.\
\
'I understand that you wish for solitude and to hoard this wood for yourself, but what I do not understand is why. Why should one Elf sit upon this grove like a dragon sitting upon piles of gold?'","The secluded grove is peaceful and majestic","You have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should listen to their conversation.","You have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should talk to Agalûnu.","You have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Shanthar has something to say to Agalûnu.","'Come ${PLAYER}, let us return to my camp. I have much to think about, and I am also not feeling so well.'","'It is a beautiful day, but we should not dally overmuch. Is that the Elf's abode just ahead?'","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the beauty of Arwáth"},
[7210]={"'¡Excelente, amigo mío!¡Mostremos ahora a los elfos la inmensa riqueza de mithril que aún custodian las profundidades de Khazad-dûm!'","Habla con Náin","Durin VI se encuentra junto a la comitiva en las profundas cavernas bajo Khazad-dûm.\
\
Durin espera hablar contigo.","Náin se encuentra con lo que queda de la comitiva en las profundas cavernas de Khazad-dûm.\
\
Durin ha caído ante la terrible criatura que dormía bajo Khadaz-dûm, y ahora Náin es el soberano del reino de los enanos.","'Gracias, Nafni. Veo que ya han llegado; estoy listo pra hablarles sobre la perdurable amistad de los enanos.'","¡Escapa!","¡Ahí estás, Nafni! ¿Dónde te habías metido? El señor Durin ha estado preguntando por ti; los delegados de Lothlórien están al llegar y él tiene asuntos que debes atender antes de su llegada.\
\
'Está en su trono. Ve con Durin y préstale tu ayuda, como es tu costumbre y tu deber.'","Durin VI, Señor de Moria, se encuentra en el estrado al norte del gran salón del trono.\
\
Está esperando para hablar contigo sobre cierto asunto antes de que llegue la comitiva de elfos de Lórien.","Corría el año 1980 de la Tercera Edad. Eres Nafni, un fiel sirviente de Durin VI, señor de Khazad-dûm, y no tienes la menor idea de lo que les deparará a tus hermanos enanos en esta fatídica noche.","Durin VI se encuentra junto a la comitiva en las profundas cavernas bajo Khazad-dûm\
\
Durin está esperando a que limpies la caverna de rascacuevas y rascabismos.","Sverri se encuentra en la enterada principal del salón del trono, al sur del gran estrado de Durin.\
\
Durin te ha pedido que hables con él y aguardéis a la comitiva de elfos de Lórien.","Rascacuevas y rascabismos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Durin VI se encuentra en el estrado, al norte del salón del trono.\
\
Náin te ha pedido que le comuniques a su padre que la hueste de elfos de Lothlórien ya ha llegado.","'¡Iremos de inmediato para deslumbrar a nuestros visitantes con la gloria y la abundacia de los enanos!'","Un gran terror dormido bajo Khazad-dûm durante una larga edad.","'Están impresionados, ¿a que sí, Nafni?¡Pero no hagas esperar a Náin! Ha pedido hablar contigo!'","Sverri se encuentra ante las puertas, frente al gran trono de Durin.\
\
El portero del salón del trono está esperando para hablar contigo sobre cierto asunto.","Durin VI y su comitiva se dirigen a los yacimientos de mithril, en las profundas cavernas bajo Khazad-dûm.","Instancia: La Caída de Moria","'Melkólf Tallapiedras es mi escultor de la corte y hace un trabajo excelente. Esculpirá uan estatua digna de mi hija Náin quien, si la fortuna es propicia, reinará en Khazad-dûm dentro de muchos años, cuando yo ya no esté.\
\
'Háblale en el lado oeste de este salón, donde suele quedarse cuando no está trabajando.'","'¡Nafni, hola, hola!¡Es un honor hablar con alguien a quien mi señor tiene en tan alta estima!'\
\
Le describes la estatua que Durin desea que Melkólf talle para Náin.\
\
'Se hará, amigo Nafni, con toda presteza; pero no tan rápido como para que la obra sufra! Capturará el semblante señorial del joven Náin y, si se queda muy quieto,¡ningún enano de Khadaz-dûm notará la diferencia!\
\
'¡Por favor, dile a mi señor Durin que empezaré de inmediato!'","'Nafni, dile a mi padre que la comitiva de Lothlórien ya ha llegado. Lo encontrarás como siempre en el estrado, al norte del salón del torno.'","'Nafni, estos son los Elfos de Lórien, que vienen a tratar con mi padre los acuerdos comerciales y la buena voluntad entre nuestros pueblos.¿Podrías anunciar a mi padre que hemos llegado?'","'Nafni, necesito que rompas el muro.¡Seguro que hay mithril al otro lado!'","Ayuda a romper el muro agrietado","¡Los enanos huyen del gran terror que ha despertado bajo Khazad-dûm!","Melkólf Tallapiedras se encuentra en el lado oeste del salón del trono de Durin.\
\
Este te ha pedido que le encargues una estatua de su hijo Náin.","'Los elfos están al llegar, Nafni, escoltados por Náin, hijo de Durin. Seguro quedarán impresionador por la majestuosidad de estas estancias, pero no mostremos nuestro orgullo; ya sabes que el proceder del enano es la humildad ante sus invitados.\
\
'No podrán sino maravillarse ante los salones de Durin. Ellos viven entre árboles, pero los grandes pilares de nuestra ciudad son como troncos tallados desde las raíces mismas de la piedra con un arte asombroso!.'","Desde su estrado, al norte del trono.\
\
Durin ansía deslumbrar a los elfos de Lothlórien con la magnificencia de las minas de mithril.","'Gracias, Nafni. Melkólf es todo un artista, su obra siempre será recorada por el lugar que ocupa en Khazad-dûm.\
\
'Ve a ver a Sverri, en la puerta principal del salón del trono, y espera a los delegados de Lórien. Mi hijo los escoltará hasta aquí.'","Durin VI se encuentra junto al estrado del gran salón del trono.\
\
Regresa con él e infórmale de que Melkólf Tallapiedras ha aceptado esculpir una gran estatua para su hijo Náin.","'¡Debemos retirnarnos, Nafni!¡No queda otra opción!\
\
'Pero juro por el nombre de mi padre que abatiré a este Balrog: este horror antiguo, este mal de una edad olvidada!\
\
'Khazad-dûm no caerá!'","Sigue a Durin VI y a su compañía","'Gracias por venir, Nafni. La delegación élfica llegará pronto y quería consultarte algo.\
\
'Nuestros tratos con los elfos ya no son los de antaño, y espero que este encuentro reavive nuestra vieja amistad. Aunque el mithril escasea cada año, la gloria de Khazad-dûm es infinita; con su ayuda, podríamos expandir nuestras excavaciones aún más lejos.\
\
'Debemos mirar hacia el futuro. Por ello, deseo hacerle un regalo a mi hijo Náin, quien me sucederá en el trono dentro de muchos años.\
\
'Habla con Melkólf Tallapiedra, al oeste de la sala, para encargarle una estatua. Presidirá este trono cuando llegue el momento de su reinado.'","Durin VI se encuentra junto a la comitiva en las profundas cavernas bajo Khazad-dûm\
\
Durin está esperando a que le ayudes a atravesar el muro agrietado bajo Khazad-dûm.","Habla con Sverri","Habla con Melkólf Tallapiedra","Sobrevive!","'¡Nafni, despeja esta caverna de rascacuevas y rascabismos! Debemos poder avanzar hacia los yacimientos de mithril de forma segura.'","Durin VI se dirige a los elfos de Lothlórien.","'¡No debes hacer esperar a nuestro señor!Habla con Durin junto al estrado, al norte de este gran salón!","'Nafni, esta caverna es profunda y salvaje; algo ha perturbado a las garras de cueva y garras profundas que anidan aquí.\
\
'Despeja la cueva de estas bestias para que podamos alcanzar los depósitos de mithril sin peligro.'","Derrota a rascacuevas y rascabimos(${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}","Habla con Náin, señor de Moria","Espera a que Durin VI termine de dirigirse a los Elfos","Habla con Durin VI","Náin se encuentra ante las puertas del salón del trono de Durin junto a la comitiva de elfos de Lórien\
\
Náin espera hablar contigo."},
[7211]={"Instancia: El Premio Fatal","Wait with Captain Lachír for his men to return.","You have found Captain Lachír. He, in turn, has found ingots of metal he believes are imbued with great power, and ordered his men to gather all they could find.","Wait with Captain Lachír","Defend yourselves from Captain Lachír's men","Defend yourselves once more","There is a pause in the onslaught. Captain Lachír wishes to speak.","Help clean off the encrusted object in front of Captain Lachír.","Something has come over Captain Lachír's men and they are attacking without regard.","When you meet Lachír's eyes in the light, there is a wildness behind a mask of bravery. It is fear.\
\
'Have all my men turned on me? Can I have pushed them too far in search of something powerful, something truly magnificent? Can sullen resentment - or greed, greed and jealousy have driven them to such ends?\
\
'But what am I saying? Did you see their faces? It was madness, madness and not mutiny written there, plain as day.'\
\
The captain falls silent abruptly, brooding.","Talk to Captain Lachír while you wait for his men to return.","'Ah, and then there is this artifact! It is something else, entirely! It looks almost crusted over intentionally. Help me clear it off and we shall see what lies beneath.'","Talk to Captain Lachír","With an anguished cry, the captain runs off and is lost to the deepening shadows","Clean off the artifact","More of Captain Lachír's men are attacking."},
[7213]={"Derrota a Naegir y a los buscadores de restos","'No, ${PLAYER}. Tampoco creo que sea el Ectheldur. Algo no está bien...'\
\
Tarneth mira alrededor, y un repentino crujido cerca de los árboles del islote llama su atención.\
\
'Espera... ¿oíste eso?'","Tarneth se está preparando para regresar a Tinnudir.","Naegir te ha tendido una emboscada en el islote del Lago Evendim.","Sigue a Tarneth","'Bueno, bueno, ¿qué tenemos aquí?'\
\
Naegir te mira con desdén.\
\
'Se nota que seguiste mi mapa, ¿eh? Un trabajo ingenioso, ese. Tuve que dibujar tantos, pero sabía que atraparíamos a uno de esos Montaraces tarde o temprano.\
\
'Sé que estos restos no son del Ectheldur. Si estoy en lo correcto, está en el fondo del lago, justo al sur de este islote. Supuse que si estuviera sobre el agua, habría sido saqueado hace siglos. Dejé fuera ese detalle, claro, pero ahora que sabemos dónde está, estoy seguro de que mi gente encontrará la forma de llegar a él. Deberían, al menos.\
\
'¡Estuve tan cerca, sabes! Solo necesitaba un poco de ayuda para orientarme, y ustedes dos hicieron un buen trabajo guiándonos hasta aquí.'\
\
Naegir sonríe con burla.\
\
'No puedo agradecértelo lo suficiente.'","¡Naegir y los buscadores de restos te atacan! Debes derrotarlos.","Los restos se encuentran en el extremo sur del islote en el Lago Evendim.","Habla con Tarneth","Tarneth ha viajado a un islote en el Lago Evendim.","Examina los restos en el pequeño islote del Lago Evendim","<rgb=#ff00ff>Mira alrededor</rgb> a los restos en el pequeño islote del Lago Evendim","'Nunca antes había conocido a la Dama Azul. Y que se me conceda el bastón forestal de Alwedion... es un honor más grande de lo que jamás imaginé.\
\
'Me alegra que nuestra búsqueda no haya sido en vano, y más aún que sepamos el destino real del Ectheldur. Me reconforta saber que permanecerá fuera del alcance de los saqueadores de tumbas del sur.\
\
'Mi gente querrá saber lo que ha ocurrido aquí, ${PLAYER}. ¡Regresemos a Tinnudir!'","Tarneth ha viajado a un islote en el Lago Evendim. Debes seguirla y explorar el islote.","Enfrenta a Naegir","Parece poco probable que estos restos sean del Ectheldur, así que quizá el mapa de Naegir estaba equivocado.","Presencia el encuentro de Tarneth con la Dama Azul","Los Montaraces del Norte en Evendim han buscado durante mucho tiempo los restos del Ectheldur, el antiguo navío insignia de Annúminas, pero sus esfuerzos no han pasado desapercibidos por un grupo de saqueadores de tumbas del sur.","'¿Estás... estás bien, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Tarneth se toma un momento para recuperar el aliento.\
\
'Si lo que Naegir dijo es cierto, entonces nos han tomado por tontos. Todo esto fue en vano, ¿no es así?'\
\
Tarneth patea la arena.\
\
'Todo en vano...'","Instancia: El destino del Ectheldur","Una brisa fresca recorre el islote mientras Naegir y los demás caen derrotados","La Dama Azul se desvanece en las aguas del Lago Evendim","Este es un buen lugar para <rgb=#ff00ff>mirar</rgb> los restos","'Lo hemos logrado, ${PLAYER}. Fue un viaje más largo de lo que esperaba, pero tu remo fue una bendición. Después de todo, no me entusiasmaba la idea de cruzar el Lago Evendim nadando.\
\
'Según pude discernir, el mapa de Naegir parecía señalar este islote, así que veamos qué podemos encontrar.'","Gwindeth, la Dama Azul, ha aparecido en las aguas del Lago Evendim.","'Es hora de volver a Tinnudir, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.'"},
[7214]={"Fastred is standing outside Dagred's Grave.\
\
Having defeated the Orcs brought to his father's grave by Crúmgam, you should return to Snowbourn with Fastred.","As the last Orc falls to the ground, a moment of peace returns to Dagred's grave","'I come here often for peace, ${PLAYER}... though I seldom find it.\
\
'The Orcs of these lands are relentless, yet... they find a far more dangerous foe in me than I them.\
\
'You have much still to learn of my people and the troubles that come to the Sutcrofts. Come, walk with me.'","Talk to Fastred","Fastred wants to speak to you of his father, Dagred, the past Reeve of the Sutcrofts.","A chill fills the air as a Man in the garb of Mordor approaches...","'I know not what dark machinations that man has laid for my people, but his presence here fills me with dread.\
\
'I am certain this is not the last we shall see of him, but Snowbourn shall stand prepared against any terrors that come for us. In this, I shall not falter.'","Crúmgam stands at the eastern side of Dagred's Grave.\
\
The darkening of the sky has heralded the arrival of a fierce Man of Mordor, Crúmgam. You and Fastred should confront this Man.","Walk with Fastred","<rgb=#FF0000>Fastred must not be defeated</rgb>","Instancia: El Padre de los Sutcrofts","'Come, let us allow my father his rest. Are you ready to depart this place?'","Confront Crúmgam","Fastred is standing just outside his father's gravesite with Framferth.\
\
Fastred wishes to speak to you about his people and his father's legacy.","Fastred is walking through his father's gravesite."},
[7215]={"Observe the ritual as it unfolds","The Feast of the Running Stag has been disrupted by the ill omen...","Join the Stag-clansmen and observe the rites","The crow's wing appears twisted, as if someone attempted to break it cruelly. The message it bore is still attached to its leg.\
\
You recognize at once that this was the crow you sent to the southern farm. Something very unfriendly intercepted this poor bird.\
\
It is clear that the farmer's family never received this summons.","Bring the Elder what he asks for when he is finished speaking","You have brought the Elder the final piece of the ritual set","'Good evening to you! You are just in time -- the Elder is still preparing, but the clan has gathered already.\
\
'Come, follow me! This is the most important night of the year for my people.'","This looks like a good place to sit and watch","The Elder smiles at you as you place the crown at his feet","Talk to Elain","Instancia: El banquete del ciervo corredor","'We should leave, ${PLAYER}. I will talk to you again before I go to scout the farm.'","The Feast of the Running Stag has begun.","The Feast of the Running Stag is about to begin.","You should perform the <rgb=#FF0000>/sit</rgb> emote near the bonfire to observe the festival.","You have placed the horse-tail at the Elder's feet","The Elder's ritual crown can be found at the doorway from which he entered.\
\
You should collect the crown and carry it carefully to the Elder.","The Elder has called an early end to the Feast of the Running Stag this year, due to likely danger in the south where some of his people live.","The crow was intercepted before it could reach the farm in the south","You should observe the Feast of the Running Stag.","The Feast of the Running Stag continues.","Observe the Feast of the Running Stag","Observe the rites","You have arrived at Lhan Tarren as the Feast of the Running Stag began and have been invited to join the Stag-clan for the evening.","The Elder has asked you to fetch the crown","The Elder's ritual horse-tail can be found at the doorway from which he entered.\
\
You should collect the horse-tail and carry it carefully to the Elder when he is done speaking.","The Elder's ritual spear can be found at the doorway from which he entered.\
\
You should collect the spear and carry it carefully to the Elder when he is done speaking.","Listen to the Elder","Bring the Elder what he asks for","Elain is at the Feast of the Running Stag.\
\
You should speak with Elain about the injured crow and the missing southern family.","'This is very unsettling. The poor bird tried to land, but friendly hands did not receive it. We will surely scout at first light.\
\
'You heard the Elder, ${PLAYER} -- our festival is at an end. You should take some food and rest, for you have earned it.'"},
[7216]={"Elrond se encuentra frente a su casa, observando cómo la Compañía se marcha.\
\
La Compañía ahora se dirige hacia lo salvaje en una misión secreta sobre la cual descansan las esperanzas de todos los Pueblos Libres.","Gandalf se encuentra frente a la Casa de Elrond, preparándose para partir con la Compañía.\
\
Los habitantes de la casa de Elrond se han reunido para despedirse de la Compañía mientras se preparan para partir.","'¡Samsagaz, gran tonto! ¡Has olvidado traer un poco de cuerda contigo! ¡Sabía que había algo que habías olvidado!\
\
'Bill aquí tendrá demasiado que llevar tal como está, y he aligerado su carga tanto como he podido.'","Boromir se encuentra orgullosamente frente a la Casa de Elrond, preparándose para partir con la Compañía.\
\
Los habitantes de la casa de Elrond se han reunido para despedirse de la Compañía mientras se preparan para partir.","Ha llegado el momento de despedirse de la Compañía, que parte para su misión secreta.","Instancia: La Comunidad Parte","'Está hecho, y están más allá de mi ayuda. A pesar de toda mi sabiduría, no puedo ver el final de su camino. Que lleguen a él con seguridad y regresen a Rivendel con victoria.'","Los miembros de la Compañía se encuentran frente a la Casa de Elrond, preparándose para partir.\
\
Los habitantes de la casa de Elrond se han reunido para despedirse de la Compañía mientras se preparan para partir.","'Volvamos adentro, ${PLAYER}. No hay nada más que podamos hacer por ellos: la Compañía ahora debe confiar en su propia fuerza y sabiduría.'","'El número de la comunidad ha sido elegido, ${PLAYER}, y cualquier miembro más podría comprometer el éxito de su misión.\
\
'Tienes asuntos pendientes en Eriador, valiente ${RACE}: defiende a su gente de las sombras que se alargan. Si la misión de esta Compañía fracasa, Eriador necesitará héroes antes de la oscuridad final.'","'Así comienza un nuevo viaje. ¡Avancemos con valentía, digo yo, en lugar de escondernos de sombra en sombra, y que el Enemigo se estremezca ante nuestra llegada!'","'Cuida de estas tierras mientras estamos fuera, ${PLAYER:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Nuestra misión es peligrosa, pero también dejaremos muchos peligros atrás, y mis pasos serán más ligeros si sé que ${PLAYER} se queda para protegernos de ellos. Mi propio viaje me llevará lejos de aquí.'","Frodo está en el frente de la Casa de Elrond, preparándose para partir con la Compañía.\
\
Los habitantes de la casa de Elrond se han reunido para despedirse de la Compañía mientras se preparan para partir.","'Esto es todo, ${PLAYER}. Deséanos suerte, y nos aseguraremos de salir bien. Al menos, nos aseguraremos de brindar toda la ayuda posible a Frodo y hacer lo que Gandalf necesite que hagamos.\
\
'¡Te veremos cuando regresemos, y eso es una promesa!'","'Todo parece estar listo, ${PLAYER}, y estamos a punto de partir. ¡Espero verte de nuevo una vez que todo esto haya terminado!'"},
[7217]={"'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'No matter how I try to sway her, my daughter idolises Éowyn. While I admire her passion, she is still too young of age to follow such a charge.\
\
'Come, let us return to the Mead Hall. There we can talk more of what is to be done.'","After an argument with her daughter, Ellen shifts her focus back to her people","'Come, there are many matters to be dealt with!'","Lady Fremedon of Underharrow finds herself at odds with Éowyn as she makes ready for the impending migration to Dunharrow.","Ellen Fremedon can be found outside the Mead Hall of Underharrow.\
\
You have arrived in Underharrow and should acquaint yourself with Ellen Fremedon and her family.","DNT -- Players will not see","Ellen Fremedon can be found around Underharrow.\
\
You have asked to speak more with Ellen Fremedon, and she is now telling you of the burdens that fall on Underharrow.","Ellen Fremedon can be found near the river Snowbourn in Underharrow.\
\
You have finished speaking to Ellen Fremedon and met her daughter. You should now aid her in helping the people of Rohan.","Talk to Ellen Fremedon","Instancia: El Violín y el Tambor","'Come, let us talk of other things.'","Walk with Ellen Fremedon"},
[7218]={"The Mead Hall lies in north-east Walstow.\
\
Winsig has called for aid from her men, and they now endeavour to put out the fires now that the Orc force is broken.","Defend the second stable of Walstow","Winsig is standing outside the Mead Hall of Walstow.\
\
The Orc force has been repelled, and Winsig and her people are free, at least for the moment, from the danger that consumed their home.","'Let us speak more of this attack in a moment. For now, I must ensure my people are safe.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Winsig must not be defeated</rgb>","The first stable lies just to the west of the Mead Hall of Walstow.\
\
Winsig hopes to keep the Orcs from slaying the steeds of her people.","Follow Winsig into Walstow","Walstow is under siege by Orcs of the East Wall who have finally brought their plans to fruition. Winsig and her folk require aid or another settlement of the Sutcrofts will fall to the same grim fate as Hytbold.","Having witnessed the slaying of many steeds, Winsig sets off to the other stable of Walstow","Gadhumúrz stands just beyond the bridge of Walstow.\
\
Winsig must reunite with her men, but a menacing Orc blocks your path.","Derrota a Gadhumúrz","Talk to Winsig","The nearby stables burst into flames!","Winsig stands just outside Walstow.\
\
The town is under siege by the Orcs of the East Wall. You should speak to Winsig and begin your assault.","Winsig is in Walstow.\
\
Nearby homes have been set ablaze by Orcs, and Winsig hopes to keep her town from ruin.","As you cross the bridge, a large, vicious Orc blocks the way","'Our message was received! Thank goodness someone has come... we have no time to waste, we must move now or risk losing all to the Orcs!'","As you approach the stable, a group of Orcs ambushes you","Instancia: El Primer Asalto","With the Orcs defeated, Winsig moves to rally the riders","'Time and time again, ${PLAYER}, your aid has proven invaluable to me and my people.\
\
'The Orcs cannot be allowed any more footholds in the Sutcrofts... to this day, I still mourn Hytbold. That is a matter for another time, though....\
\
'In the wake of such destruction, I must tend to my people.'","The second stable lies to the south of the Mead Hall of Walstow.\
\
Winsig requires your aid in defending the stable from the vicious assault of the Orcs.","The bridge of Walstow passes through the middle of the town.\
\
While you defeated the Orcs at the second stable, the rest of the town has burst into flame. Winsig desires to reunite with her men and put out the fires.","Winsig has been defeated!","Follow Winsig to the Mead Hall","As the last of the Orcs falls, you notice black clouds of smoke rise through the air near the mead hall","Cross the bridge with Winsig","Defend the first stable of Walstow","Follow Winsig to the second stable","The second stable lies to the south of the Mead Hall of Walstow.\
\
In the wake of seeing so many steeds slain, Winsig hopes to protect any that remain alive."},
[7219]={"The fearsome Sûhalar, Korpûrta, must face the consequences of his actions for the slaughter of Gilgír and Tolwin's older brothers.","<rgb=#FF0000>Tolwin must survive</rgb>","Cross the bridge to Cair Andros and find The First Blade.","'We have accomplished what we came here for. Let us retreat to Crithost.'","Instancia: La Primera Hoja","Defeated enemy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Dúneth","Tolwin has fallen in battle!","'We shall not tarry here much longer. We have finished what we have set out to do. It would be foolish to take on the entire army gathered within these walls.\
\
'Let us all retreat to Crithost.'","Defeat enemies at Jal Kepir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat The First Blade.","Find The First Blade","Korpûrta looks amused at your presence","You have slain the fearsome First Blade of the Sûhalar","Defeat Korpûrta","Stay close to Tolwin and Dúneth and defeat enemies at Jal Kepir.","<rgb=#FF0000>Dúneth must survive</rgb>","You should speak with Dúneth.","Dúneth has fallen in battle!"},
[7220]={"Durin fights against the onslaught of dragon-kind at the upper courtyard of the fortress and needs your help.","Durin has seen that the dwarves operating the siege defences are in need of help, and asked you to attend to them.","Bótuz Frostblood fights among his people in an upper courtyard of the fortress, but the drakes and other dragon-kind do not relent.","Catch up to Durin at the bottom of the stairs","'What do we do? I know what we must not do... we must not give in to despair! But anyone can see there are too many drakes and not enough dwarves to repel them. Think! We must think! How can we drive them away from the fortress? What would Uncle Náin do? Bah! I cannot think of anything!\
\
'Come with me, ${PLAYER}! I saw Bótuz Frostblood fighting down below. Let us go to him and see if he has a plan!'","Talk to Durin in the courtyard at Skarháld","Fight alongside Durin at Skarháld","The fortress of Skarháld is under attack! Durin raced ahead and already engages in battle at the bottom of the stairs.","Instancia: La primera promesa","'Karazgar left us no time to prepare! But how has he brought these drakes and dragons to bear against us? Let us drive off these winged beasts and prove to the Weeping Warrior that dwarves cannot be intimidated so easily... neither Longbeard nor Zhélruka!'","Durin is in the courtyard of Skarháld. Most of the dragon-kind army has retreated.","Climb the central platform and assist the dwarves operating the siege defences","At Karazgar's signal the dragon-kind retreat, their victory assured and unnecessary to prove","The siege defences are being overrun!","Talk to Durin in the upper courtyard of the fortress","Before the dwarves at Skarháld have had the chance to properly prepare, Karazgar launches the first of his promised attacks upon the fortress.","'It is done, ${PLAYER}. Karazgar could have slain us all, killed to the very last dwarf, but he chose to spare us instead. Hah! It is no mercy. He seeks to use fear as a weapon against us.\
\
'Alas for Bótuz Frostblood! We must not let the Zhélruka despair at his loss, or the fortress is as good as fallen. I tell you dwarves are resilient. May we prove it!'","The drakes and other dragon-kind have begun to overwhelm Skarháld. Durin calls for you to help him turn the tide."},
[7221]={"Talk to Imrahil","'This wraith speaks ill of the dead - I shall not believe what he claims! Eärnur is lost to the Enemy's trickery... and to his own brashness. Such troubles are not for this day... when such a battle surrounds us even now.\
\
'I saw a bold rider of Rohan and his company rush by to the south as we fought on. Éomer, they called him, chanting and slaying as they rode. A great fury had taken him, for he and his kinsmen screamed of death and destruction to be done upon our foes.\
\
'If we are to survive the Enemy's renewed strength and the might of Gothmog, we must rally at Éomer's side atop the Hillock.'","You find your path blocked by a terrible wraith!","Stand back as Duilin and Derufin clear a path","Reach the Hillock with Imrahil and Ingbert","Battle across the Pelennor Fields","You have discovered Duilin and Derufin scouting a path through the nearby battlefield","The Hillock lies to the south-east of Minas Tirith.\
\
Ingbert has decided that the best course is to reach the Hillock and make a stand against the Enemy's reinforcements there. You should follow him.","Duilin and Derufin are scouting ahead and attempting to slay the Mûmakil.\
\
You should stand back and allow them to weaken the beasts before proceeding.","The Orc encampment is ahead.\
\
Duilin and Derufin have been slain by the Haradrim and their Mûmakil. You should flee into the nearby Orc encampment.","The wraith vanishes, leaving behind only a pile of robes...","You spot Prince Imrahil and his Swan-knights battling against the Haradrim","Orolang is standing at the cross-roads to the north of the Hillock.\
\
You have found your path blocked by a dreadful wraith and must defeat him if you are to reach the Hillock.","Talk to Ingbert","Aid Imrahil and his Swan-knights","The Haradrim have momentarily stopped their attacks, allowing you a chance to reach the Hillock","'Gothmog! These are ill tidings, ${PLAYER}. We must meet Éomer upon the Hillock - I only hope we are enough to stand against Gothmog's forces.'","Instancia: El Enemigo Resurgente","With the Witch-king now dead, a new commander has taken control of the enemy forces on the Pelennor Fields.","'I know not who could command such a force in the absence of the Witch-king.\
\
'These fields churn with battle and blood, but we must learn more of this new commander. Who could lead so many with nary an ebb in the flow of battle?\
\
'He shall surely come forth from Osgiliath as so many of his reinforcements have, but we cannot afford to hold here and allow his forces to overwhelm us.\
\
'Let us move to a more fortified position and hope that we might learn of his identity.'","The brothers of Blackroot are slain and the Mûmakil are maddened! Flee!","Ingbert is on the Pelennor Fields just ahead of you.\
\
You have begun your foray from King's End to discover the Enemy's new commander and should now talk to Ingbert.","Reach the Hillock with Ingbert","Imrahil and his Swan-knights can be found to the north of the Hillock on the Pelennor Fields.\
\
Imrahil is under attack! You and Ingbert should come to his aid.","Ingbert is battling on the Pelennor Fields.\
\
Ingbert has asked you to join him in searching for the Enemy's new commander.","Defeat Orolang","The Mûmakil have not pursued you, but you have been spotted by Orcs!","Imrahil is at the cross-roads to the north of the Hillock.\
\
You should speak to him about what is to be done.","The Hillock is due south of your position.\
\
Ingbert and Imrahil have begun their journey to the Hillock. You should accompany them.","Flee to safety in the Orc encampment!"},
[7222]={"'The gangrel-creature had come to the Forbidden Pool, and too close to Henneth Annûn...'","Faramir, Anborn, and Frodo came to the overlook of Henneth Annûn.\
\
You should listen to Anborn's tale.","Instancia: El Estanque Prohibido","'I bound the creature and blinded him with a hood lest he discover the way to Henneth Annûn...'","'The Halfling told of his connexion with the creature and offered to lead him to us...'","'And that is all I have to say on the matter, my friend.'","Listen to Anborn's tale","Anborn recalls the tense exchange when the gangrel-creature came unbidden to the Forbidden Pool beneath Henneth Annûn.","With Frodo's aid, Anborn hopes to capture Gollum at the Forbidden Pool.\
\
You should listen to Anborn's tale.","Anborn and Frodo travelled down to the Forbidden Pool.\
\
You should listen to Anborn's tale."},
[7223]={"Follow the other soldiers in retreat","Grimbold stands at Prince Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen.","Grimbold's voice is low when next he speaks....","The men have retreated backwards into the Westfold, and you should follow.","Tell Grimbold that it is over","Defeat enemies at the Ford (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Uruks have us nearly surrounded. There has been enough death today.'","You return to the fords from pursuing a band of Uruks to no avail, and find a scene of utter chaos and despair....","You should look back to see if Grimbold is following","This man draws no breath....","Grimbold is at the Fords.","Fight your way to Grimbold at the Ford.","Tell Grimbold <rgb=#FF0000>no</rgb>","Erkenbrand cannot help now, for the Uruks have come between you","<rgb=#FF0000>Beckon</rgb> to Grimbold","Grimbold stands at Prince Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should tell Grimbold no.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest requires emotes. Select your target and perform the desired emote.</rgb>","Find Grimbold amongst the chaos","Grimbold stands dumbfounded at Théodred's grave, unmoving....","See if any of the fallen soldiers live (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Leave with the soldiers while there is still time. Grimbold will follow if he is wise....","See what the soldiers choose to do","'Elfhelm! You are back! Now we can give them a battle to remember.'","An injured soldier lies ahead at the river's edge.\
\
You should run to the injured man's side.","This soldier is unwilling to lay down his life for a lost cause","Fallen men are scattered upon the ground at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should search the men on the ground.","Ask the dying soldier what happened while you were gone","Has derrotado a un enemigo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","It is clear that the battle has taken a dire turn. There is no hope....","Ask the soldiers what they wish to do","'We must hurry, Lord Elfhelm! The Uruks are everywhere, and our escape will be narrow....'","'My...my lord Elfhelm!'\
\
You ask the dying man what happened here.","'You...you do not mean to fight.' His expression is devastated.\
\
You tell Grimbold the truth -- that the battle is lost, and it is time to retreat to rally what little strength is left.","Instancia: Los Vados han caído","Grimbold is still standing at Théodred's grave.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF0000>beckon</rgb> to Grimbold.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You should select your target to perform this emote.</rgb>","Search for Grimbold among the chaos at the ford.","Elfhelm, one of the leaders fighting alongside Erkenbrand at the Fords of Isen, wishes to fall back at once.","The soldiers have gathered around Grimbold and yourself.\
\
You should ask the soldiers what they think.","Approach the ford"},
[7224]={"Defeated Orc-smiths of Saruman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Saruman is attempting to forge legendary weapons of his own to get the upper hand in his war against the Horse-lords of Rohan.","Defeated Uruk-hai Slave-masters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated the Master of the Forge","Instancia: Las forjas de Isengard","Enemies in the employ of Saruman can be found throughout the Forges of Isengard.","Defeat the Orc-smiths of Saruman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat the Master of the Forge","Defeat the Uruk-hai Slave-masters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7226]={"Place the final stone on Cynegar's grave","Listen to Gárwig speak about Gársig","Listen to Gárwig speak of Edsig and Gárferth","Pick up the stone for Gársig's grave","Place the final stone on Thrymm's grave","Join Gárwig near the grandson's graves","Join the others at Cynegar's grave","'I think most of the Reeve's family has gathered, and we are about to get started.'\
\
'Please, walk with me to the others.'","Pick up the stone for Cynegar's grave","Leave the funeral with Cyneberg","Listen to Gárwig speak about Cynegar","Speak with Cyneberg","Instancia: El funeral en Forlaw","Place the final stone on Gársig's grave","Walk with Cyneberg to the funeral","Every living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.","You picked up the stone.","Many were lost in the battle at Scylfig, but none were more important to the people of Wildermore than their hero Thrymm Red-beard. A funeral is being planned by Gárwig and Cyneberg so that the people of Forlaw can pay their respects and say good-bye to those who lost their lives.","Join Gárwig near the twins' graves","Join and watch those gathered for Gársig","The final stone has been placed on Thrymm's grave.","'It is done. The fact they are gone seems a little more real now than it did earlier....\
\
'I need to go home and sit by a warm fire for a while.'","'Let us make our way to Thrymm's home in Forlaw.'","Listen to Gárwig speak of Humbald and Grimgar","The final stone has been placed on Gársig's grave.","The final stone has been placed on Cynegar's grave.","Join and watch those gathered for Thrymm","Pick up the stone for Thrymm's grave","Listen to Gárwig speak about Thrymm","Listen to Gárwig speak"},
[7227]={"Defeat the leaders of Fushaum Bal","Talk to Mâlatuk.","'You are a cunning one. That much is true. I have no quarrel with you. In fact, I admire what you have done here. You helped resolve our matters. Though your means of doing so evaded even me until just now.\
\
'Leave Khirgi to me. I will push his corpse into the flames below us. Only a fitting burial for such a foul man.\
\
'If you leave me be, I shall honour you in return and vacate Mordor as soon as my men and I are able. We do not wish to stay here any longer. It only brings us thoughts of crushed hopes and riches that never were.'","Meet with the divided leaders of Fushaum Bal","Meet with the divided leaders of Fushaum Bal.","Defend yourself.","<rgb=#FF0000>Beckon</rgb> the leaders of Fushaum Bal to come forward","Defeat the leaders of Fushaim Bal.","Defend yourself!","Instancia: La Resolución Fushaum","The camp of Fushaum Bal is a lawless home to evil men once under the command of Sauron.","Defeated Thâng","Talk to Mâlatuk","'Farewell, ${CLASS}.'","Beckon the leaders of Fushaum Bal to come forward.","Defeated Khirgi"},
[7228]={"'Bien, hasta ahora hemos pasado inadvertidos por el Enemigo. Ahora debemos ver si podemos encontrar a mi padre.\
\
'No tengo certeza de dónde exactamente pueda estar... Raghnall no me dijo en qué parte de Rhunendin lo encontraríamos. Tendremos que hacer una búsqueda cuidadosa.\
\
'Prepárate, quién sabe qué nos aguarda más adelante...'","Habla con Golodir","Golodir espera para hablar contigo.\
\
Has encontrado a Golodir y ahuyentado a Mordirith, pero a un costo terrible.","Instancia: Las Puertas de Carn Dûm","Protege a Lorniel mientras busca a Golodir, su padre.","Usa la palanca al otro lado de la puerta.\
\
Al adentrarte más en Rhunendin, encontraste una puerta que la llave de Carn Dûm no pudo abrir. Debes dirigirte hacia la palanca y abrir la puerta para Lorniel.","'Mi padre no está aquí. ¿Cómo pudieron resultar falsas las palabras de Raghnall? ¡Temo que tendremos que entrar en Carn Dûm mismo!'","'¡Deprisa ahora, usa la palanca al otro lado de la puerta y abre el camino!'","Has viajado a Rhunendin con Lorniel. Usando la llave que ayudaste a forjar, va a buscar a su padre.","'Es muy extraño que la llave no haya funcionado en esta puerta. Espero que no encontremos más sorpresas inesperadas al continuar.'","Habla con Lorniel","Tras encontrar a Golodir, Lorniel fue asesinada. Ahora el Falso Rey se alza ante ti, lejos de su fuente de poder. Ha llegado la hora de derrotar a Mordirith.","Derrota a Mordirith, el Falso Rey.","Golodir habla entre sollozos ahogados: ¡No, no... Lorniel!\
\
'Tenía razón... Mordirith tenía razón. Solo estaba jugando conmigo... contigo. Podría haberte derrotado hoy si realmente lo hubiera querido.\
\
'Todo ese tiempo mirando a través del palantír pensé que vería la victoria... que Lorniel y tú... que ustedes me liberarían, que provocarían la caída de Angmar. Todo se ha desvanecido... todo está perdido...'","'Rápido, debemos salir de este lugar terrible...'","Derrotaste a Mordirith, el Falso Rey.","Abre la puerta para Lorniel"},
[7230]={"Nona is prepared to become Wadu's Ghost and slay her former lover... but you cannot stand idly by.","Reminisce about your adventures","Stand beside the fire with your friends","'${PLAYER}, my dear friend! It is good to see you again at last! If you waited a few more months you might meet my son or my daughter... but I am glad you did not wait.\
\
'No, I do not yet know what my child will be! When the days feel longest I wonder if Hildegard would tell me whether I am having a son or a daughter... but I cannot bring myself to return to the soothsayer's cave. If she had not spoken as she had, perhaps Horn...\
\
'It does not matter. It has been months but my anger has not cooled. It is said the Uch-lûth love even more fiercely than they fight, and you should cross them in neither! Someone should have told that to Horn before he sent me away, the fool. Yes, I know he thought he was doing right. He was wrong, and should have listened.'","It is a reunion of friends and adventurers near the summit of Lhanuch, but not everyone is welcome.","Enter Lhanuch and climb the hill","Suvulch stands partway up the hill in Lhanuch.","... and promptly fell down on his rump when the shrew within leapt out of its hiding-place","'This is Lhanuch, the village of the Uch-lûth from which Nona came? I am pleased to see it. She did not speak of it often, but when she did her voice was fond... despite her attempts to prevent it, I think.\
\
'You had better go on ahead, ${PLAYER}. Nona's people will remember you. The rest of us will be considered... what was the word? Duvodiad? Yes, that was it.\
\
'The rest of us may be duvodiad, but in Lhanuch I believe you will be welcomed.'","Corudan has asked to go with you to visit an old friend.","Instancia: El Fantasma Regresa","You prevented Nona from becoming Wadu's Ghost... but it was a close thing.","Corudan encouraged you to climb the hill into Lhanuch and ensure that your group will be welcome.","Find Nona up the hill near the summit of Lhanuch","<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> by the fire and reminisce about your adventures","Talk to Suvulch in Lhanuch","Nona smiles as you approach","Talk to Nona by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch","After a lengthy journey, Corudan and your other companions stand outside the village of Lhanuch.","Nona has called for you and the others to <rgb=#00FF00>sit</rgb> and reminisce about your adventures.","Talk to Nona and keep her from once again becoming Wadu's Ghost","Talk to Corudan outside Lhanuch","You and your friends sit by the fire and reminisce about your shared adventures.","Suvulch told you Nona is further up the hill within Lhanuch, and will be delighted to see you.","Suvulch nods in greeting","'Stand aside, ${PLAYER}. To return here, after sending me away... his wits are more addled than they used to be! How can you explain his presence here?'\
\
Nona's eyes boil with fury, but your keen eyesight reveals that the hand holding her brother's sword trembles. She does not want to become Wadu's Ghost again, despite her words and the anger she has nursed for Horn since he sent her away from the war. If only there was some way for you to break the tension. You cast your thoughts back to the days you spent travelling with Horn and Nona, and then you have it.\
\
You recount your cautious steps within the deserted village of Dunfast, in Wildermore, when Nona had left your little party, leaving you in the company of Horn, the minstrel Gléowine, and Corudan. The Elf felt eyes upon your group, and it was with heightened senses that the four of you crept towards the bush that seemed to contain the unwelcome and hostile eyes. Horn valiantly approached the bush, his hand upon his sword, prepared to face whatever evil lurked within...","Nona sits by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch.","'I knew you would one day climb this hill and come again to Lhanuch, ${PLAYER}. I saw it in the Pool of the King only weeks after my daughter Nona departed, following the dream that carried her away to fight another kingdom's war. She returned months afterward with a broken heart and a child in her belly, and I thought you would return in the company of this man, this Horn who was the father of the child. But sun and moon rose and fell, and he never showed his face.\
\
'My daughter sits by the summit of the village, by the fire on the right. She will be glad to see you. As for the others who wait below... who can say? If they do not speak the right words, they may learn the daughter of Suvulch can be even more dangerous than he is, and that is no small amount!'"},
[7231]={"Examine the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepare","It is a reunion of friends and adventurers near the summit of Lhanuch.","Reminisce about your adventures","Stand beside the fire with your friends","Enter Lhanuch and climb the hill","Suvulch stands partway up the hill in Lhanuch.","Nona is grateful for the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepare.","Corudan has asked to go with you to visit an old friend.","'${PLAYER}, my dear friend! It is good to see you again at last! If you waited a few more months you might meet my son or my daughter... but I am glad you did not wait.\
\
'No, I do not yet know what my child will be! When the days feel longest I wonder if Hildegard would tell me whether I am having a son or a daughter... but I cannot bring myself to return to the soothsayer's cave. When Gléowine came to Lhanuch and told me of what transpired before the walls of Minas Tirith... it was as if I was hearing of it for the second time, seeing it again, feeling anew all the pain of it. So I will not return to Hildegard.\
\
'Gléowine spoke also of your deeds, and I know Horn was avenged. I would have become Wadu's Ghost once more and done it myself, but you can see that I am somewhat occupied for now. So I thank you, and I know Horn does as well, and so does his child.'","Instancia: El Fantasma Regresa","Corudan encouraged you to climb the hill into Lhanuch and ensure that your group will be welcome.","Find Nona up the hill near the summit of Lhanuch","<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> by the fire and reminisce about your adventures","Talk to Suvulch in Lhanuch","Nona smiles as you approach","'This is Lhanuch, the village of the Uch-lûth from which Nona came? I am pleased to see it. She did not speak of it often, but when she did her voice was fond... despite her attempts to prevent it, I think.\
\
'You had better go on ahead, ${PLAYER}. Nona's people will remember you. Caebar and my sister and I will be considered... what was the word? Duvodiad? Yes, that was it.\
\
'The three of us may be duvodiad, but in Lhanuch I believe you will be welcomed.'","Talk to Nona by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch","Nona has called for you and the others to <rgb=#00FF00>sit</rgb> and reminisce about your adventures.","Talk to Corudan outside Lhanuch","You and your friends sit by the fire and reminisce about your shared adventures.","Suvulch told you Nona is further up the hill within Lhanuch, and will be delighted to see you.","Suvulch nods in greeting","Nona has set down the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepare.","Nona sits by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch.","'I knew you would one day climb this hill and come again to Lhanuch, ${PLAYER}. I saw it in the Pool of the King only weeks after my daughter Nona departed, following the dream that carried her away to fight another kingdom's war. She returned months afterward with a broken heart and a child in her belly, and I thought you would return in the company of this man, this Horn who was the father of the child. But sun and moon rose and fell, and it was not you who first came to Lhanuch with tidings.'\
\
Suvulch frowns, and you remember that he considers himself more gifted with weapons than with words.\
\
'It was a minstrel, an old one with white hair and a solemn face. He said he served a king of the horse-lords who perished fighting the Dark Lord, and he had sad tidings for Nona. \\qHorn is dead,\\q he said to her, and while she had raged with anger in the wordless months that passed, her fury was replaced all at once, and with sorrow. I wept with the two of them. Yes, even I! But I am her father, and I raised my Nona to be strong. Her tears showed to me how deeply she loved this Horn, even though she buried that love beneath the rage she held for him, and which he deserved! So I wept alongside them, and when the minstrel departed I embraced my daughter and I told her that I would never again say a cross word about the man Horn.\
\
'I meant it even then, but in time I have come to understand he was a man of courage who believed he was not courageous, ${PLAYER}. That is a curious thing, and not common among the Uch-lûth. But perhaps not all can be as honest as Suvulch, who is certain of his courage and acts upon it every day.'\
\
He roughly clasps your arm, and then points up the hill.\
\
'My daughter sits by the summit of the village, by the fire on the right. She will be glad to see you.'","After a lengthy journey, Corudan and Caebar stand outside the village of Lhanuch."},
[7232]={"Armero maldito destruido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Debes destruir a los espíritus caídos que moran en esta cámara, así como a su maestro, si quieres alcanzar la forja y completar la cualidad que buscas.","Instancia: La Forja de los Espectros","Debes destruir a los armeros malditos y a su maestro espectral para disipar el mal que han urdido en esta forja ancestral.","Has creado un zafiro potenciado","Usa la antigua forja para potenciar tu zafiro infundido.","Maestro de la forja de Cargûl derrotado","Usa el yunque antiguo","Derrota al Maestro de la forja de Cargûl","Destruye a los armeros malditos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7233]={"Habla con Hórin","Find the ice-giant chieftain","'Here we go. Remember, be polite and respectful. Keep your weapons sheathed. They should at least hear us out, as long as we do not agitate them.'","Hórin is waiting to proceed inside Thyrstáth.\
\
You should talk to Hórin.","You should walk through Thyrstáth with Hórin until you find the ice-giant chieftain.","'I am both angry and embarrassed to have fallen into such a trap! We need to move quickly, before those Angmarim return.'","Broke free of the dark force (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You are held in place by a dark force!","Hórin believes the best course of action is to enter Thyrstáth on a diplomatic mission. Your aim is to prevent the ice-giants from falling under the sway of Hrímil and her Frost-horde.","Listen to the conversation","'I did not see any hobgoblins or Angmarim on the way in. That's a good sign, but now we will really put my skill at diplomacy to the test! I have never spoken to a giant at length before, much less a chieftain of that people! I hope I don't accidentally offend him. Be ready just in case this goes poorly.'","Break free of the dark force (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You are bound in place by a dark force!","Instancia: La guarida del gigante","Hórin is standing outside the throne-room in Thyrstáth.\
\
You should talk to Hórin.","Hórin is negotiating with the ice-giant chieftain.\
\
You should listen to the conversation."},
[7234]={"While waiting for Grimbeorn's answer, Legolas recalls a recent story told to him by King Thranduil.","<rgb=#FF0000>Listen</rgb> to Legolas","Let Legolas tell his story.","<rgb=#FF0000>Listen</rgb> to Legolas.","'Now you too know how the Woodmen were granted the middle woods of Eryn Lasgalen. I hope this story will be helpful in your dealings with the Woodmen in the Vales of Anduin.'","Let Legolas tell his story","Instancia: El Regalo de Hojasverdes"},
[7235]={"Bregoleth teje un relato de Caras Gelebren en la Segunda Edad de la Tierra Media.","Deja atrás a Bregoleth para escuchar el final de su relato, que se encuentra más adelante dentro de la Montaña de Fuego","'Aunque Galadriel se había marchado, Celeborn permaneció en Caras Gelebren. Como principal defensor de Eregion se negó a abandonar estas tierras, y buscó en cambio protegerlas del extraño que había captado el oído de Celebrimbor.\
\
'Annatar odiaba a la Compañía Brillante y sus hazañas, y convocó una amenaza tras otra para atormentarlos; Celeborn y sus guerreros eran a menudo alejados de la ciudad, y muchos nobles elfos cayeron en estos enfrentamientos. Pero aun así el Señor de la Compañía Brillante no lograba relacionar estas crecientes amenazas con el recién llegado Annatar y sus sonrisas demasiado dispuestas.'","Escucha mientras Bregoleth teje su relato","Bregoleth ha aceptado hablarte de los años que vivió en Eregion, y del Enemigo que vino a amenazar a su pueblo y a toda la Tierra Media.","Habla con Bregoleth en su memoria de Caras Gelebren","'Annatar regresó a Mordor, y en el corazón de su reino dejó de lado su aspecto hermoso. Ya no necesitaba engaños.\
\
'En Mordor, el Señor Oscuro Sauron buscó consumar el plan que había trazado, caminando inadvertido entre sus odiados enemigos durante tantos años.'","Sigue a Bregoleth y escucha mientras teje su relato","'La Ciudad de las Joyas y el Bastión de Plata prosperaron, y la gloria de Celebrimbor y sus joyeros no hizo más que crecer, año tras año.\
\
'Pero la verdadera obra maestra de Caras Gelebren era su fragua de anillos.'","Bregoleth teje un relato de Caras Gelebren tal como era durante los años que vivió allí en la Segunda Edad de la Tierra Media.","'Celebrimbor entregó a los reyes de los enanos y de los Hombres los anillos que había forjado, y durante un tiempo conoció la paz, sin saber que había sido engañado, sin saber que lo que había hecho casi desharía el mundo.\
\
'Poco después, Annatar partió. Solo regresaría a Eregion una vez más, y cuando lo hiciera traería consigo muerte y destrucción. Pero una vez que se hubo ido, Celebrimbor comenzó a dudar. Con el tiempo, la sospecha despertó en su corazón, y empezó a preocuparse de que Annatar lo hubiera atrapado mediante su propia codicia en algún plan perverso.\
\
'Decidió usar el arte que había aprendido para forjar tres Grandes Anillos más, desconocidos para el traicionero Señor de los Dones. Creía que él y los suyos podrían usar estos tres anillos para protegerse, si las cosas se torcían.'","'El Bastión de Plata se convirtió en una joya resplandeciente por sí mismo, un faro de arte, música y cultura que atrajo la atención y el amor de muchos de tierras distantes. Caras Gelebren y Mirobel se tornaron lugares de tal belleza que recordaban los legendarios salones élficos de antaño, y el comercio con Lindon prosperó.\
\
'Pero no todos los que observaban esto desde lejos lo hacían con ojos amistosos. En la tierra de Mordor, a la que huyó tras la caída de su maestro Morgoth, Sauron hervía de ira. Temía el creciente poder de Númenor y, pese a haber reunido orcos y otras criaturas funestas a su servicio, sabía que no poseía los números abrumadores con los que su maestro dominó el mundo en días pasados de triunfo. Ideó un plan mediante el cual usaría las debilidades de sus enemigos contra ellos.\
\
'Y así llegó a Eregion con un aspecto hermoso, ocultando su verdadera naturaleza.'","Bregoleth habla de un lugar que nunca ha visto, un lugar de mal indescriptible: el interior de Orodruin, la Montaña de Fuego en la Tierra Negra de Mordor.","Habla con Bregoleth en un lugar de mal indescriptible","Instancia: El Dador de Dones","'Annatar había ido primero a Lindon, pero Gil-galad desconfió de él y se negó a tratar con el extraño recién llegado.\
\
'Fue en Caras Gelebren donde el Señor de los Dones encontró a alguien cuya estirpe y ansia por el conocimiento secreto lo convertían en el blanco perfecto para las promesas de Annatar. Celebrimbor no pudo resistirse, y pronto el recién llegado se convirtió en su mentor y en el de los maestros joyeros de Eregion.'","'Los estudiantes no eran sus únicos discípulos. Con los años, Annatar se volvió cada vez más descarado. Celebrimbor y sus joyeros cayeron aún más bajo su dominio, atrapados por sus promesas de conocimientos secretos y artes tanto hermosas como poderosas.'"},
[7236]={"Follow the Bright Company into the upper chambers of the tower","You have come face to face with Sauron in an upper chamber of Barad-dûr, and must distract the Dark Lord from his real danger.","'I have walked this Middle-earth for the long years of this Third Age, sent by the Powers to oppose Sauron. But this was not the first time the Valar sent me hither, though they hid the truth of it from my memory's sight! For what purpose?\
\
'It is true. I remember the Bright Company, not only from the tales of Glorfindel but as if I were there... for so I was, in different form. I know the torments Lendelen suffered within the dungeons of Barad-dûr, for it was I who suffered them, and though Sauron be gone the memory of those days fills me with a terror I thought never to know.\
\
'But this cut is the worst: I have known these Elf-lords for so long, and this secret they kept from me. Why? Why did you keep this truth from me, Glorfindel? Have I not been a friend to you, no matter the name I wore? You knew me first as Olórin, and now you know me as Gandalf, or Mithrandir. Why would you keep the knowledge of Lendelen from me?\
\
'No, I am not angry. Perhaps it was a kindness to keep this from me. What say you to this?'","'I will think no worse of you if you choose to turn back.\
\
'No? You wish to stay? Then you are truly one of us, mellon.'","Follow Glorfindel and escape from the tower!","The veil of the Valar abates!","Stand with Glorfindel and Lendelen","'Lendelen has never been one to exercise caution, not when he knows his fellows could be endangered by some approaching threat. On any other day I would appreciate that trait, but on this day Lendelen is the only Elf among us with the ability to break Sauron's hold upon the Vandassar! His role is crucial, and he must be protected!'","Lendelen and Glorfindel have rejoined you atop the stair, and now their mission, and yours, must be completed.","<rgb=#FF0000>If you do not escape in time you will fail the quest.</rgb>","'I thought he was right behind us, but it is not so!\
\
'Lendelen, forgive me, my friend! Alas that we must bring word of both your triumph and your loss to the Great Alliance! By your hand the Vandassar is broken, and Sauron's control over the Ghâzab Bôron must begin to wane, and you should celebrate with us! But it is not to be.\
\
'Quickly, mellon. There is no time to spare.'","Talk to Glorfindel on Tol Send","Talk to Glorfindel in Barad-dûr","'Listen to me very carefully, friend ${CLASS}. Ahead, a stair spirals to the upper chambers of the tower, where the Vandassar awaits me. That is our destination.\
\
'But we will be exposed on the stairs, and I fear the hateful eyes that may watch our ascent. This I suggest: that you go first.\
\
'Nay, do not protest! I do not jest. I wish for you to climb first so I may cover your ascent with my bow. I will slay any foes that think to threaten you from afar, and then the rest of us will follow. We will meet you atop the stair.'","Glorfindel relates to you the last glorious mission of the Bright Company, but he seems to harbour some hesitation, reluctant to share the tale with you.","Talk to Glorfindel in the tunnel of Halroth","Talk to Sauron","'Your people believe they are strong, gathered beneath their banners and behind their kings. For how long has this \\qGreat Alliance\\q lasted? No more than a handful of years. It needs but one hammer-stroke, well-aimed, and it will crumble into dust. So it always is with Men.\
\
'I have called into being a Storm, and it is on its way. Your Alliance will be swept away by the wrath of it.'","Glorfindel has halted, waiting for Lendelen.","Glorfindel stands on Tol Send, ready to conclude his tale.","Lendelen wants you to climb the spiral stair to the upper floors of the tower, where other Elves of the Bright Company will join you.","Now that you have passed beyond the wall of Barad-dûr with the Bright Company, Lendelen wishes to speak to you.","Follow Glorfindel and Lendelen to the chamber of the Vandassar, and stand with them","'We cannot stay here, though it grieves me deeply to leave my friends to their doom.\
\
'Our goal lies above! Lendelen must reach the Vandassar!'","Talk to Gandalf on Tol Send","Lendelen has successfully broken Sauron's hold upon the Vandassar, and now you must escape from the tower!","Instancia: La Gloria de la Compañía Brillante","'The passage begins to rise. We must be nearing the mountainside well-nigh to the side of the tower.'","<rgb=#FF0000>All of your allies must survive</rgb>","Glorfindel is in the tunnel of Halroth, prepared to fight through the dark passage to Barad-dûr itself.","Gandalf stands on Tol Send, the events of the past newly-awakened in him.","Death has come to the Bright Company, and you have failed!","The Bright Company stands against the Nazgûl in a high chamber of Barad-dûr, but the mission of Glorfindel and Lendelen remains higher still.","Climb the spiral stair and speak with an Elf of the Bright Company outside the upper chambers","Talk to Lendelen inside Barad-dûr","'I remember little of our last desperate flight down the stairs and through the tunnel of Halroth. When we returned to the relative safety of Adambel, we were greeted with more sorrow than we brought with us. Men spoke in hushed tones of the last ride of noble Anárion, son of their High King, slain on the field before the Dark Tower. It was a great stone, cast from the heights, that laid him low and ended his life. But I will never forget that it was his riding that granted us access to Halroth, and enabled Lendelen to break Sauron's hold upon the Vandassar.\
\
'For so it was. Without the power of the Oath-stone, the Ghâzab Bôron splintered. No longer unified, the Storm of Wrath dissipated, falling apart into its component tribes. The Easterlings fled, no longer dominated by Sauron's will, and they turned instead for their own lands. Their appetite for conquering was sated, and it would be many years before their return. Even so, Middle-earth has never seen so great a horde as the Ghâzab Bôron in all the time since, and we have Lendelen to thank for that.'","You failed to escape, and Sauron's victory was complete","Listen to the words of Glorfindel","Glorfindel has concluded his tale of the last glorious mission of the Bright Company, in which Sauron's control over the Vandassar was broken.","The mission of the Bright Company all comes down to this moment, high in the chamber of the Vandassar.","'It is time. Lendelen and the other Elves of the Bright Company have gone ahead to secure the tunnel, but we must still remain alert for any threats that might have arisen behind them.\
\
'Stay near to me.'"},
[7237]={"Investigate the cave","'There are a few goblins milling around out here, but this cannot be all of them. There must be more, and I would bet a crate of honeycakes they must be in that cave behind the village.\
\
'Here is what we should do. You go closer, and when you are ready, give the signal. I will shout and roar and draw them from their hiding holes. You then sneak inside the cave, and find out what is really going on here.\
\
'That sounds like a plan to me. Does it sound good to you?'","Enter the cave behind the village","You should return to Langhár with this information","This spot is close enough to signal Langhár","Instancia: El Gran Trasgo en el Exilio","Get into position next to the village gate","<rgb=#FF00FF>Wave</rgb> at Langhár when in position","Langhár is ready to explain her plan to enter the goblin hideout.\
\
You should talk to Langhár.","Habla con Langhár","'Come, let's move.'","You have learned much about the Great Goblin's situation.\
\
You should return to Langhár and tell her this new information.","You should investigate the cave to find evidence of why the goblins are here and how many they number.","Langhár has asked you to get closer to the cave entrance before she alerts the goblins.\
\
You should get into position, and then <rgb=#FF00FF>wave</rgb> at Langhár to give the signal.","'Hah! A great battle, but these tiny things are no match for a Beorning! Now, tell me what you have learned!'\
\
You tell Langhár of the large number of goblins inside, the takeover of Goblin-town by hobgoblins from Gundabad, and the exile of the Great Goblin.\
\
'That has given me much to think about, ${PLAYER}. Let us move away from the goblins before more come to investigate, and we will find somewhere to think this through.'","Return to Langhár","You have found the Great Goblin and his host","You have found the Great Goblin and a large number of goblins loyal to him.\
\
You should listen to him speak to his followers to see what you can learn.","A horde of goblins has departed Goblin-town, wreaking chaos in their path. We have followed, and come to their new hiding place. Now, we have them cornered. It is time we found out exactly what is going on here.","Langhár has drawn the attention of the goblins in Waldfast.\
\
You should sneak behind them and find the cave she mentioned.","Eavesdrop upon the Great Goblin"},
[7238]={"Habla con Dómárr","Instancia: El Gran Salón de Durin","Dómárr ha descubierto algunos asuntos desagradables en el Gran Salón de Durin, y cree que puede aportar pruebas de que Zelem-melek es extramadamente vulnerable.","'¡Bien por Reinn! Quizá ahora la Sala Vigesimoprimera pueda estar debidamente para ser una fuerza a tener en cuenta en Zelem-melek.\
\
'Sería una desgracia perder la posición que hemos ganado allí simplemente porque el capataz no vea los peligros que acechan.'","'Aquí están: los malvados orcos de Gazatu-ru, ¡adorando al señor de Mordor! Ten cuidado, ¡y escóndete bien!'","Dómárr y Reinn se encuentran en el Gran Salón de Durin.","Escucha la discusión de los enanos","Dómárr se encuentra en el Gran Salón de Durin.\
\
Deberías hablar con Dómárr.","'¡Debería alegrarme de poder contar a mis compañeros de viaje mi desdichado relato al pasar por este camino! Debes escuchar mi historia, y tener cuidado.'","Escucha a Reinn y a Dómárr","'Volvamos al campamento, ${PLAYER}. Este no es lugar en el que debamos entretenernos, y debo reflexionar. Quizá pueda hacerse algo con estos orcos.'"},
[7239]={"Wait for your cue to arrive, and then run up the stairs on the right side","The play is almost over, and you should join the other performers on the stage.","Now is your chance! Slip inside the hallway while the audience is distracted.","Talk to Ulishár in the back-stage chambers","Ulishár has found an unsent letter in the Lord's Study.","'Me!' you exclaim with your most theatrical voice","'The first part of our mission has gone smoothly, ${PLAYER}: we have infiltrated the very belly of Emax Dûl without raising the suspicion of the lords and ladies of the keep. So far they seem entertained by Satagêra's words and the performances of Asharmûl, Zimêlkha, and Mashkânu... to say nothing of Jêsamin, who always obtains the most laughter and the greatest applause!\
\
'But our role in the performance approaches. Let us join Satagêra by the door to the stage, and await our cue.'","Ulishár has joined you in the hallway west of the stage, in the belly of Emax Dûl.","'The lords and ladies of Emax Dûl seem enraptured by the play to this point... let us hope that continues!\
\
'Remember, ${PLAYER}. Mashkânu will say \\qSome heroes of Gondor still remain,\\q and then Asharmûl will ask \\qWho?\\q At that moment you are to run up the stairs directly opposite us and stand by the entrance to the hallway. I will tell you the precise moment when it happens.\
\
'Then, you will wait until the mûmak makes its appearance, and when Mashkânu asks you \\qWell?\\q you are to dramatically faint. Afterwards, while the audience is distracted, you and Ulishár will slip into the hallway and search the Lord's Study for the information Inkanûsh desires.'","Ulishár stands with you in the back-stage chambers of the performance hall in Emax Dûl.","Satagêra has told you to wait for your moment to run onto the stage.","Talk to Ulishár in the hallway west of the stage","Take your <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb>","Join the other performers on the stage as the play comes to an end","Wait for your next cue","Slip inside the west hallway while the audience is distracted","You should join Têrkar's Travellers on-stage for your bow","You have infiltrated the city of Emax Dûl in the guise of a performer with Têrkar's Travellers.","Listen to Ulishár read the unsent letter he has found","'Khóbagach was in poetic mood when he named Barkhûsh's fleet \\qThe Song of Waves and Wind,\\q believing it would be the greatest accomplishment he would oversee as Hûl. The wide, dark mere was new and appeared on no map, overlooked only by the skeletal gaze of the ruins of Kasukhín, and it was large enough to hold a vast number of warships. The River Ikorbân remained navigable all the way to the sea, and with sharp-eyed archers and spearmen stationed upon the bounds, the lake and its accompanying shipyard could remain a secret for as long as it proved necessary.\
\
'Nisigím lay nearby, but its trees were blighted and it rapidly became a ghost-forest; few of its timbers were suitable for firewood, let alone for shipbuilding. Timbers for the fleet and stone for the ship-yard and its wharves had to be carted by mûmakil from the Mûr. Waggons departed from Khanâg Valoyar and elsewhere every few days, the Temámir accepting payments of silver and gold and asking few questions.\
\
'Khóbagach Hûl died of the gout long before the Song was completed, but Mordor and Ordâkh worked together to finish the weapon that could destroy their shared enemy. The arrival of the Song of Waves and Wind on the shores of Gondor would signal the beginning of the war, but for some unknown reason Barkhûsh launched the attack before the fleet was ready. It stood idle at Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater, for the duration of the war. It stands there still, even as a new king rules in Gondor and all believe Ordâkh to be defeated. - Prepared for Góramul Sai by Laghíl of Emax Dûl, Scribe of Ordâkh'","Talk to Satagêra by the rear entrance to the stage","Take your <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> with the other performers.","Run up the stairs and deliver your line","The papers in the Lord's Study may provide the information you seek. Search them and learn what you can!","<rgb=#00FF00>Faint</rgb> at the sight of the impressive Mûmak","<rgb=#00FF00>Faint</rgb> at the sight of the impressive Mûmak.","'We have made it, and I believe the audience suspects nothing!\
\
'Follow me, ${PLAYER}. Let us keep our voices down as we make for the Lord's Study.'","Your big moment has arrived! Run up the stairs on the right side of the stage and stand by the door to the west hallway.","Join the other performers on the stage","Satagêra stands by the doorway leading to the stage.","Read the papers in the Lord's Study","'We have learned something of great import, ${PLAYER}: a secret fleet of warships has been in construction for many years at the head of the River Ikorbân, and even now it nears completion! This must be enough for Inkanûsh; we have been away for too long!'","Read more of the papers in the Lord's Study","Return to the rooms backstage and wait for the rest of Têrkar's Travellers","You learned what you came for, and should now return to the rooms backstage to wait for the rest of Têrkar's Travellers.","Instancia: El Gran Triunfo de Mordor y Ordâkh","Talk to Ulishár in the Lord's Study","'I have had my attendants gather the notes we possess about the Song of Waves and Wind and I am studying them for good news. I need something with which I can prove my worth to the frightful ones who came from Damudûr. My mind is my own... for now... for now. If the fleet being built at Starkhaven in Sûg Nidar can restore Ordâkh to glory, Thothril may see my value.\
\
'I will write more later. I will double my efforts, and study once more the record of the Song's construction. -GS'","Ulishár wishes to speak with you in the Lord's Study.","Now you must wait for your second cue. Once Mashkânu says 'Well?' you must faint... but not before!"},
[7241]={"Mótsog weaves to you the tale of his treachery's foundation.","Habla con Durin","'How could Durin the Deathless entrust one such as Mótsog with the rule of his kingdom? It beggars belief, ${PLAYER}! Were there no indications of Mótsog's evil, or of his treacherous nature?'","Durin has challenged Mótsog to deny his treachery, but the mysterious dwarf insists he will not.","'The sight of mithril weapons in the hands of the Elves had kindled a dark flame of greed and envy in my heart. How many of my people might have been spared had Durin given such true-steel to we who remained? How many of my sons might have survived battle with the Orcs and trolls that sought to conquer the Mountain-home, had they possessed weapons of such quality?\
\
'Only one son remained to me on that dark day, and it was he who slew the Elf-captain. His people leapt to the defence, wielding their mithril blades with deadly skill, but Módvit was not alone, and my worthiest commanders stood with him.\
\
'When the fighting was ended, my spear too dripped with the blood of my guests.'","Mótsog has agreed to speak of the treachery for which he is remembered.","'Orc and dwarf and troll marched side by side in the Misty Mountains for the first time, and as Durin's own army approached Gundabad my combined force fell upon his with a ferocity he could never have anticipated. The rout was total and complete, and the finest warriors of Khazad-dûm fled from the hammers of the Greymauls and the fangs of the Orcs and the clubs of the mountain-trolls.\
\
'Durin's eldest sons were slain by Orcs in that first battle, and I thought it meet; had I not lost my own sons, save Módvit, to such as they? It seemed little different to me at the time, though I had joined hands with the forces of Morgoth and his commander Sauron; it was Durin drove me to do so, and if there was to be blame let it lie with him!\
\
'My forces returned in triumph to Biriz-zahar, and my commanders believed the war had reached a decisive end. I knew it was not so. I knew it for what it proved to be: the beginning only.'","'With its thick walls and defensible approaches, my new stronghold of Biriz-zahar in the high mountains to the south was secure from any assault. My loyal Greymauls stood at the parapets of my city and gloated, insisting that Durin's warriors would be unable to ascend the heights and the former king would meet our demands.\
\
'But I wondered, and I worried. The defences of Biriz-zahar were strong... but I feared they would not be strong enough. Word reached me that the former king had assembled a vast army of Longbeards, and even now he marched at its head to put down the revolt. We could not hope to match such numbers as Durin levied, and the size of the approaching host was more than double my own.\
\
'In Biriz-zahar I had built my tomb. This truth came slowly to me, but it did not come to me alone.'","Durin cannot understand why his namesake would have trusted Mótsog with the lordship of Gundabad.","Instancia: La Rebelión de los Mazo Gris","Talk to Mótsog","'Durin took the greater portion of the Longbeards with him to found the Dwarrowdelf of Khazad-dûm, and I governed those who remained behind. Those years were hard and bloody, for the Orcs had been emboldened by the exodus of so many dwarves; they sought to conquer Gundabad.\
\
'We held them back, but with so few defenders the cost was high. Six of my seven sons were slain in those wars, and only the youngest, Módvit, survived to be named my sole heir. My heart grew cold, and only Orc-slaying could bring me any joy. The heads of our enemies adorned the gates of the Mountain-home.\
\
'Some among my people whispered that Durin had abandoned us to the encircling Orcs. During the years that followed the whispers grew, and with them my own legend: noble Mótsog who stood alone against all the forces of Morgoth, fighting to preserve his people. My son Módvit became the fiercest of my adherents, and in time he had me believing what was said of me: that I was equal to, or perhaps even greater than, the king himself.'","Listen to the tale of Mótsog"},
[7242]={"'Vamos, debemos buscar refugio de esta tormenta.'","'Reunamos a los Ancianos y vayamos al encuentro de ese emisario de Angmar.'","Yrjänä y los Ancianos de los Lossoth deben reunirse con el emisario de Angmar.","Instancia: La Mano de Angmar","Yrjänä te dijo que los Angmarim también han llegado a Sûri-kylä, liderados por un Númenóreano Negro.","Acompaña a Yrjänä para encontrarte con el emisario de Angmar."},
[7243]={"Faramir has recovered, and now Aragorn goes to see if Éowyn's condition has improved.","Instance: The Hands of a Healer","Habla con Aragorn","Walk to Merry's bedside","'Thank you for all your help, ${PLAYER}. We have done much good here, and there is more to do before I can rest. But I am glad that some of the evils that befell us upon Pelennor have been remedied.'","Aragorn has gone to Merry's bedside to see if his work has aided the hobbit's recovery.","Follow Aragorn to Éowyn's bedside","Aragorn is by Faramir's bedside in the Houses of Healing.","Capítulo 5: La reunión de la Compañía Gris","Aragorn is by Merry's bedside in the Houses of Healing.","Remain alert in the event you are needed","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! Do you remember when we crept to see Théoden's war-council in the Drúadan Forest? It feels to me as if that was years and years ago, but it cannot have been. I have been caught in a terrible dream, but already the memory of it is fading.\
\
'I think supper will be just the thing, and afterwards perhaps a pipe. No, not a pipe. I don't think I will ever smoke again. Théoden was sorry he would not be able to speak of herb-lore with me, smoking our pipes in comfort and peace. I will never be able to smoke without thinking of him.'","'Let us see if Faramir's condition has improved, ${PLAYER}.'","Aragorn's skill at healing will be put to the test in the Houses of Healing.","Merry is still in bed, but he seems to be recovering.","Aragorn is by Éowyn's bedside in the Houses of Healing."},
[7244]={"Sigue al jefe de correos Ganapié hasta el sótano de la Oficina del Servicio Postal Rápido","Doblas la última de las cartas y la devuelves a su sobre","Montones de cartas olvidadas dirigidas a Halson Cleary se encuentran en el sótano de la Oficina del Servicio Postal Rápido.","'Muy bien, he vaciado la caja de cartas antiguas sobre la mesa del sótano. Puedes revisarlas y ver si hay algo importante.\
\
'Recuerda, esto es muy inusual. ¡En la Oficina de Correos Rápidos no recomendamos mirar el correo de otras personas! Pero estas cartas son tan antiguas que no debería haber ningún problema.'","Lee una de las cartas olvidadas","'Vaya. ¿Siempre ha estado al revés la inscripción en este mapa? Qué curioso que no me haya dado cuenta antes. Supongo que debería bajar aquí más a menudo, pero entonces podría sentirme obligado a ordenar el lugar, y eso parece mucho trabajo.'","Habla con el jefe de correos Ganapié en el sótano de la Oficina del Servicio Postal Rápido","El jefe de correos Ganapié podría tener una pista para que sigas sobre los misteriosos eventos que involucran a Wistmead.","Estudia las cartas en busca de alguna pista sobre el misterio de Wistmead","Estudia las cartas para encontrar alguna pista sobre el misterio de Wistmead","El jefe de correos Ganapié ha regresado al sótano de la Oficina del Servicio Postal Rápido y está esperando escuchar lo que has aprendido.","Habla con el jefe de correos Ganapié en la Oficina del Servicio Postal Rápido","Estudia las cartas para encontrar alguna pista sobre la aparición de Wistmead","Montones de cartas olvidadas dirigidas a Halson Cleary se pueden encontrar en el sótano de la Oficina de Correos Rápida.","'El jefe de correos Ganapié está en la Oficina de Correos Rápidos, y dice que puede mostrarte las cartas que podrían contener lo que buscas.'","'¿Hemos llegado al fondo del misterio? ¡Me parece que solo hemos descubierto más preguntas!'","Instancia: La aparición de Wistmead","'¿Qué has descubierto en esas cartas, ${PLAYER}? ¿Has aprendido algo útil?'\
\
Describes brevemente algunas de las cosas que Ivy Forjaroja escribió a Halson Cleary, y a medida que tu relato avanza, las cejas de Hugo se fruncen y se acaricia la barbilla, sumido en sus pensamientos.\
\
'¡Estas cartas son realmente muy antiguas! Me parece que Ivy y Halson vivieron durante el tiempo del Largo Invierno, que azotó la Comarca hace más de doscientos cincuenta años. ¡Ese invierno fue el más largo jamás registrado, y fue seguido por los Días de Escasez, un período de hambruna e infelicidad como nunca se ha visto antes! Se dice que muchos hobbits murieron durante ese invierno y la escasez de alimentos que siguió. Espero que ese destino no les haya tocado a Ivy o Halson, pero si no hay más cartas parece probable que hayan tenido un triste final.\
\
Me pregunto por qué estas cartas nunca fueron entregadas. Los hobbits de la Oficina del Servicio Postal Rápido debieron tener las manos llenas tratando de sobrevivir al Largo Invierno, pero aún así esperaba que hicieran un esfuerzo, al menos antes de que se hiciera evidente que el invierno era peor de lo habitual. Me parece algo extraño que las cartas anteriores a las nevadas no hayan sido entregadas.'","Se pueden encontrar montones de cartas olvidadas dirigidas a Halson Cleary en el sótano de la Oficina del Servicio Postal Rápido.","El jefe de correos Ganapié se ha ofrecido a mostrarte las viejas cartas dirigidas a Halson Cleary, que se han mantenido en el sótano de la Oficina del Servicio Postal Rápido durante todo el tiempo que él recuerda."},
[7246]={"This small stack of crates contains broken pieces of wood and metal, and nothing of use","Talk to Khîl in his father's house","Khîl is standing in front of the secret door, but it remains closed.","You inspect the desk Khîl moved away from the wall and note the scrapes on the floor caused by the movement. The drawer contains nothing of interest, and although you search beneath and behind the heavy stone of the desk, you find no apparatus that might connect it to the secret door.\
\
The desk does not appear to be involved with opening the door, and served only to keep its location a secret from idle eyes.","You reach under the corner of the table and disturb an insect that flies away, buzzing angrily. You doubt the insect knows anything about the secret door so you let it escape.","The secret to opening this door must be somewhere within the house","The grain in these sacks has long since rotted. The sacks themselves hide nothing of note","Stretching further you find a hidden lever, which you pull. There is a snap elsewhere in the house!","You are disappointed to see that the hidden door remains closed","'Did Vóin write in this book? Many of the pages are blank, but the writing within seems to be of many different languages; one of them seems to be in the Zhélruka mode. But what would my thrice-great grandfather have to do with artifacts of Mordor? I do not like this, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'We must tell Lord Náin about this. We have no choice!'","It is impossible to tell exactly when this illustration might have been painted. An armoured dwarf commands his warriors to assault a forest encampment of Orcs against a backdrop of flames. Is this a painting of Mirkwood, or other woods entirely?\
\
You feel around the edges of the frame and behind the painting for a hidden lever or other device, but find nothing.","Khîl has discovered the word that opens the secret door: Vóin, the name of his great-great-great-grandfather.","The stone bench is heavy, but you study it closely and find nothing unusual","Khîl has discovered the word that opens the secret door: Vóin, the name of his great-great-great-grandfather. Now he wishes to explore the chamber.","Khîl stands by the secret door, studying the runes that appeared on its face.","Listen to Khîl's explanation","You stretch your arm beneath the mattress and find nothing unusual within reach","Thinking the ore-filled barrow might contain a hidden lever or other mechanism, you search it closely but find nothing out of the ordinary. It rolls on its front wheel and is not rooted to the floor as you might have expected.\
\
At last you dig around in the contents of the barrow, but your search reveals nothing suspicious.","Khîl has brought you to his father's house. He is consumed with worry about something he discovered there.","You cannot move the heavy stone of the bed by yourself, but you inspect its sides and back for hidden sigils or devices and find none. Reaching under the mattress, you disturb only dust and long-dead insects.","Behind these crates you find that a young Khîl scratched his name in the wall, but nothing useful","'I am pleased we managed to open the door, but I tremble to think what may lie beyond it! And why should the name of my thrice-great grandfather prove the secret to its opening? My family is long-lived, but Vóin died almost a thousand years ago, if I remember the lineage aright; his name is rarely spoken in my family, and were I not a teller of tales with an iron-clad memory I might not have remembered it at all!\
\
'Why did Vóin delve this hidden chamber? What terrible secrets might lie within?'","'Take a look at these runes, ${PLAYER}! What do they say? My father Bránit always thought I should pay more attention to my learning. Was it because of this?\
\
'Ah, how could it be? He died before telling me anything about this secret door, and I was no longer welcome in his house.\
\
'But I think I can read these runes.'","The chest is locked and you can find no way to open it","'I have not been back here for many years. My father Bránit and I had a falling out and he told me never to return. He died some time after that, neither of us having apologised, and I could not bring myself to come back.\
\
'But when I did live in this house, I never knew of anything like this!'","Explore the hidden chamber with Khîl","Search the house of Khîl's father for some means of opening the secret door","Khîl has asked you to search his father's house for some means of opening the secret door he discovered.","Khîl is inside the hidden chamber in his father's house.","Instancia: La Cámara Oculta","Talk to Khîl outside the secret door","Return to Khîl","Help Khîl discover the words that will open the door","You search among the crates, but find nothing of note","These crates contain assorted home goods, and you find nothing suspicious among them","'What's that? You found a secret lever hidden in one of the beds? This is preposterous, ${PLAYER}! What secrets did my father keep in this house, and did my mother know about them? No, I cannot believe that dear Zéma knew anything about secret levers and chambers and hidden doors!\
\
'I heard a loud snap earlier. It must have been when you pulled that secret lever. Something must have changed, but what?'","Khîl is standing in front of the secret door, trying to learn the words that will open it.","You reach under this corner of the table and find it covered in a film of ancient dust. The dirt smears and you wipe it off on your clothes.","This bed is too heavy to move. You search all around its sides and back but find only cobwebs and dust, and nothing suspicious.","This chest used to be locked, but now it stands open and reveals its contents: glittering gold and shining gemstones. The riches are impressive, but you are not here for the fortunes of Khîl's forebears. Instead you reach into the treasure and feel around the edges until you find a small recess on the inside of the chest. You press the indentation and hear Khîl give a whoop of triumph from the other room.","You reach under the corner of the table and find only dust. Even so, it does not dissuade you from your search and you only relent when you are certain this corner of the table holds no secrets.","Khîl has found something in his father's house that fills him with worry, and he has asked for your help to investigate it.","This table bears the scuff-marks of heavy use but nothing of use to you now","The metal-banded chest contains only rags and moth-eaten clothes","This chest contains old clothes that likely once belonged to Khîl's mother","Talk to Khîl inside the hidden chamber","You reach under this corner of the table and feel a series of small scratches that merit closer inspection. You study the scratches and discover a crude picture of what seems to be a bed, with a line emanating from its very centre.","Talk to Khîl by the secret door"},
[7247]={"'La herida... es tan fría....\
\
'La voz... la voz me habla. Me ordena. Me dice cosas. Me habla del fin de todas las cosas... el comienzo de nuevas cosas. Me llama... me llama al servicio....\
\
'Debo hacer lo que dice... debo seguir.... Sirvo... debo servir al Señor Oscuro....'","Habla con Toradan","Instancia: El escondite","Zorrillero reside en algún lugar dentro del escondite.\
\
Has engañado para entrar en el escondite de los Montebruno. Ahora debes encontrar a Zorrillero y hablar con él para conocer el paradero de Amdir.","Amdir yace en las mazmorras al final del escondite de los Montebruno.\
\
Zorrillero te dijo que Amdir estaba encerrado y que lo que le estaba pasando parecía antinatural. Deberías encontrar a Amdir rápidamente.","Habla con el guardia de los Montebruno. Si tu engaño tiene éxito, debería darte acceso al escondite.\
\
Toradan te envió al escondite de Zorrillero para rescatar a Amdir y poner fin a las travesuras de los Montebruno.","Busca a Amdir","Habla con el guardia de los Montebruno","'Dios mío, ¡qué vista tan terrible para estos viejos ojos! La hoja que hirió a Amdir ha hecho su trabajo, y me temo que no es más que un sirviente del Enemigo ahora. Deberías intentar detenerlo, si puedes.\
\
'Y no te preocupes por mí. Ahora que estoy libre de esa horrible celda, estaré bien. Y tengo mi bastón de vuelta. No sé qué habría hecho sin él.'","Ayuda a Toradan","Has escoltado a Sara Roblecorazón de manera segura","Toradan tose sangre. 'Amdir está... más allá de la salvación ahora. Debes advertir... a mis parientes....'\
\
'Mundol está en la Cueva de Reunión de los Montaraces. Él... ayúdalo....\
\
'Ve a Sotomonte... pregúntale si... si Tanglerush entregó mi mensaje....'","Una anciana en la parte trasera de la celda que albergaba a Amdir te llamó para pedir ayuda. Deberías ayudarla a escapar.\
\
Sea lo que sea lo que le está pasando a Amdir, lo ha vuelto completamente loco, y es mucho más poderoso de lo que parecía al principio. Su grito ensordecedor te aturdió momentáneamente y abrió la puerta de su celda.","Habla con William Zorrillero","Habla con Sara Roblecorazón","Intenta ayudar a Toradan a derrotar a Amdir.\
\
Al acercarte a la entrada del escondite de los Montebruno, te encontraste con Toradan y Amdir.","Después de ayudar a Sara Roblecorazón a salir del escondite de los Montebruno, Toradan entró y vio en qué se había convertido Amdir. Al ver que su pariente estaba demasiado lejos para ayudarlo, Toradan intentó matarlo, pero en su lugar fue derribado.\
\
Deberías hablar con Toradan antes de que muera.","'Ah, así que eres tú de quien he oído tanto hablar por parte de Ellie. Perdimos a muchos buenos hombres en Archet, y me alegrará tenerte en el grupo.\
\
'Dices que has oído hablar de ese Montaraz? Tengo que decirte, lo que le está pasando a ese tipo es claramente antinatural. Éogan me dice que será una gran ayuda para nosotros, pero por ahora es solo un loco delirante.\
\
'No me importa dejarte echar un vistazo. Está en la mazmorra al final de la caverna. Mi guardia allí te dejará pasar.'","'¡Oh, gracias por venir a salvarme, joven! ¡He estado cautiva aquí durante mucho tiempo! He visto muchas cosas, y si fueras tan amable de ayudarme a salir de esta mazmorra, podría contarte un poco de lo que le pasó a tu amigo Amdir.'","Toradan habló sobre Amdir tratando de matar a los otros Montaraces y te pidió que hablaras con el Condestable Sotomonte sobre un mensaje que envió a alguien llamado Tanglerush.\
\
Sin embargo, antes de salir del escondite, deberías hablar nuevamente con Sara Roblecorazón para ver si necesita más ayuda.","El guardia de los Montebruno te mira desde debajo de una ceja fruncida. Escupe al suelo y estudia tu rostro durante unos segundos antes de darte una sonrisa irónica y siniestra.","Habla con la vieja prisionera","Habla con Amdir","Has descubierto a Amdir y has encontrado que se ha transformado parcialmente en un espectro. Dejó de delirar al verte, así que tal vez todavía haya algo de esperanza para él.","Toradan te envió al escondite de Zorrillero para rescatar a Amdir y poner fin a las travesuras de los Montebruno."},
[7248]={"Instancia: El Cuerno de Gondor","Aragorn has given you an important charge, perhaps the most important charge you have been given on this entire journey: keep the hobbits safe!","Blow the Horn of Gondor to summon aid!","The number of the Uruks is overwhelming! You need aid! Blow the Horn of Gondor!","Come to the aid of the hobbits!","Meriadoc and Peregrin need your help. They are not safe of the Uruks yet!","You have to protect the hobbits, at any cost!","The hobbits need your help, Boromir!","You have done what you could, Boromir.","This fallen Uruk is barely alive, but the mark of the White Hand on his armour is unmistakeable.\
\
'Seize... the halfling...' he moans, his wounds bubbling painfully.\
\
These Uruks are here for Frodo! You have to stop them!","Defeat the Uruk that threatens the hobbits!","The hobbits Meriadoc and Peregrin are in danger! You have to come to their aid!","'He came out of the woods in that direction, Boromir! And it sounds like he was not alone!'\
\
You are struck by the hobbit's suddenly-fierce countenance. They look so much like children, yet you begin to see some of the resolve of which Gandalf spoke.\
\
'We have to find Frodo, Boromir! If you had some cause in his disappearance, help us now and make it right!'","An Uruk threatens the hobbits!","The Uruks are closing in...","You need aid! You must blow the Horn of Gondor!","Talk to Meriadoc","Defend the hobbits","Examine the dying Uruk in the middle of the glade","'The Orcs seem endless! How can we hope to fight them all? We are not as strong as you, Boromir! Merry has shown them a thing or two, but I just cannot do it!'","Talk to Peregrin"},
[7249]={"En el año 1975 de la Tercera Edad, un grupo de Dúnedain liderado por los hermanos Laegened y Haerdor viajó hacia el norte, a Forochel, para recuperar las reliquias dejadas atrás durante la huida del naufragio de Fornost.\
\
Haerdor ha explorado los alrededores y desea hablar contigo.","Aragorn y Túgonn se han encontrado con un anciano en el camino a través del Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.","'Elrond me ha hablado de Gandalf el Gris, y me avergüenza no haberlo reconocido al principio, Túgonn.\
\
'Aun así, tiene cierta calidez, aunque trate de ocultarla. Tenía tantas preguntas que desearía hacerle si alguna vez lo encontraba... ¡y ahora no puedo recordar ninguna!\
\
'¡Qué encuentro tan inesperado! Continuemos hacia Lothlórien; quizás entonces recuerde lo que quería preguntar.'","Hasikkä, el caudillo de los Lossoth, desea hablar contigo.","Escucha el intercambio entre Aragorn y el anciano","Los trolls de las colinas han sido derrotados, pero es demasiado tarde para Arador, Capitán de los Dúnedain.","Habla con Haerdor al pie de la colina, al oeste","Haerdor desea hablar contigo.","Es el año 1965 de la Tercera Edad, y el viaje de Laegened y Haerdor los ha llevado a las orillas de la Bahía de Hielo en busca de su rey.\
\
Haerdor ha llegado a la Bahía de Hielo, contemplando la nave destrozada enviada a rescatar a Arvedui, y desea hablar contigo.","Habla con Hasikkä","Instancia: La Casa de Isildur","Habla con Glangon","Habla con Aragorn","'Hemos llegado hasta aquí sin contratiempos, Laegened, pero el camino hacia el norte sin duda se volverá más peligroso. Poco se sabe de los Hombres de las Nieves de Forochel, pero si se oponen al Rey Brujo, seguramente podremos hallar en ellos aliados.\
\
'Aun así, la nave que llevaba a Arvedui debería haber retornado ya, y su ausencia me llena de preocupación. Debemos continuar, pase lo que pase. ¡Cuanto antes sepamos qué ha sido del rey Arvedui, antes podremos dejar estas tierras heladas!\
\
'Mira, Laegened. Hay sierpes más adelante en el paso... Usa tus habilidades de sigilo y despeja el camino, para que podamos subir con el carro a salvo. Las mercancías que traemos quizás puedan soltar la lengua de los Hombres de las Nieves acerca del destino de nuestro rey.'","'Somos maestros en atacar desde las sombras, Laegened, lo sabes bien. Usa tu sigilo para sorprender a los sierpes y despejar el camino para nuestro carro. Debemos averiguar qué le ha ocurrido al rey Arvedui.'","Es el año 2956 de la Tercera Edad, y Aragorn, hijo de Arathorn, se dispone a iniciar los grandes viajes mediante los cuales conocerá el mundo. Está esperando hablar contigo, pues desea despedirse antes de partir hacia las tierras del sur.","'Grandes cosas aguardan a Aragorn, tu capitán, Túgonn, pero debe alcanzarlas en su debido momento. Es deber solemne de todos los Dúnedain protegerlo, pues desciende de Isildur en línea ininterrumpida, y un día deberá reinar en Gondor.'\
\
Gandalf sonríe con diversión, mirándote por debajo de las cejas.\
\
'Pero estas son palabras elevadas, y ese tiempo aún está lejos. Todos tenemos trabajo que hacer antes de que ese día llegue: no solo Aragorn, ni solo —en nuestro pequeño papel— los Magos, sino también tú, Túgonn. No viajarás con Aragorn en su camino hacia los reinos del sur, pues él ya ha tomado su decisión, pero aún tienes tu papel que desempeñar. Con amistad lo cumplirás, y tendrás victoria, estoy seguro, porque es un arma que ningún siervo del Enemigo comprende del todo.'","Candaith ha decidido contarte algunos acontecimientos clave de la historia de los Dúnedain.","Aragorn desea hablar contigo.","Haerdor espera escuchar que los sierpes invernales han sido despejados del paso.","Es el año 2930 de la Tercera Edad, y Arador, el Capitán  de los Dúnedain, no ha regresado de la Cima de los Trolls, a donde se aventuró para velar por la seguridad de su pueblo. Glangon teme lo peor.\
\
Glangon espera hablar contigo al pie de la Cima de los Trolls.","Derrota sierpes invernales en el paso hacia Forochel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Es el año 2956 de la Tercera Edad, y Aragorn, hijo de Arathorn, se prepara para comenzar los grandes viajes con los que conocerá el mundo. Pero primero debe despedirse de los amigos de su infancia.","Habla con Haerdor","'Oh, no... ¿qué puede haber ocurrido?'","'Hemos sido amigos muchos años, Túgonn, y juntos hemos explorado las tierras salvajes de Eriador. Tu amistad significa mucho para mí. Pero no he dicho nada por lo que debas enfadarte. Ya te dije que planeaba aventurarme en las tierras del sur y volver cuando mis hazañas fueran dignas de mi padre y mi abuelo. No puedes venir conmigo, amigo mío.\
\
'Si he de liderar a los Dúnedain, debo realizar hechos dignos de ese deber. Es algo que debo hacer solo, Túgonn.'","'¡Hemos llegado al final de nuestro camino, Laegened! ¡Mira allí! ¡El barco que debía traer de vuelta al rey Arvedui yace en ruinas!\
\
'¡Desea ahora como nunca antes que él no estuviera a bordo cuando la nave se hizo pedazos!\
\
'No podemos quedarnos aquí, por más que el horror me oprima el corazón. ¡Deprisa, Laegened!'","Habla con Gandalf el Gris","'¡Debe de ser el Anillo de Barahir! No posee poder alguno salvo su valor como reliquia de la Casa de Isildur, pero su valía antigua es indudable.\
\
'¿Habrá presentido el rey Arvedui su destino? Seguramente no, pero es curioso que este anillo haya escapado donde él no pudo.\
\
'Hemos traído abundantes provisiones. Las usaremos para negociar la devolución del anillo, que regresará al sur con nosotros, aunque su dueño no pueda. Debemos contentarnos con eso.'","'El viaje ha sido largo y será aún más largo. ¡Vamos al auxilio de nuestro rey, ocurra lo que ocurra!'","Es el año 1965 de la Tercera Edad, y el viaje de Laegened y Haerdor los ha llevado a las orillas de la Bahía de Hielo en busca de su rey.\
\
Haerdor desea hablar contigo en las orillas de la Bahía de Hielo.","Escucha la narración de Candaith","Los trolls de las colinas de las Landas de Etten capturaron a Arador, el Capitán de los Dúnedain, y deben ser derrotados si ha de ser rescatado.","'¡Muy bien, Laegened! Ahora que los sierpes han sido despejados del paso, podemos reanudar nuestro viaje hacia el norte, rumbo a Forochel, para descubrir lo que podamos.'","Derrota a los trolls de las colinas que capturaron a Arador","Gandalf el Gris desea hablar contigo.","'Estamos casi allí, Corugúr, para bien o para mal. Temo que no encontraremos vivo a Arador, nuestro capitán, pero no podemos abandonar la búsqueda hasta saberlo con certeza.\
\
'Los trolls de las colinas de las Landas de Etten viven aquí, en la Cima de los Trolls, y las huellas llevan justo al desfiladero de adelante. Subiré la pendiente para explorar desde arriba. También hay trasgos por estos lares; te dejo decidir su destino, pero recuerda que los trolls son nuestra principal preocupación.\
\
'¡Buena suerte, Corugúr! ¡Que no lleguemos demasiado tarde para nuestro capitán!'","'Me alegra que el gran rey tuviera un hijo que continuara su gobierno. ¡Que sus herederos reinen largo tiempo sobre su pueblo lejano!\
\
'Habló de grandes tesoros y cosas valiosas. Dijo que los traía el lomo del monstruo marino, y que podrían usarse contra el Rey Brujo para el bien de ambos pueblos. Pero ahora todo está perdido. Nada vuelve a salir de las aguas heladas.'","Es el año 2930 de la Tercera Edad, y Arador, el Capitán  de los Dúnedain, no ha regresado de la Cima de los Trolls, a donde se aventuró para velar por la seguridad de su pueblo. Glangon teme lo peor.","Hay sierpes en la ladera al este de Haerdor.\
\
Tu hermano Haerdor te ha pedido que uses tus habilidades de sigilo para despejar el camino de gusanos.","'¡Ay, llegamos demasiado tarde! ¡Arador ha sido asesinado! ¡Malditos trolls!\"\
\
Glangon se enjuga una lágrima y se recompone como puede.\
\
'Ahora su hijo Arathorn es capitán de los Dúnedain, aunque no lo desee. ¡Y recién casado, además! No hay nada que hacer, Corugúr. Debemos regresar con la triste noticia. Siento lástima por Arathorn, por la carga que ahora recae sobre él, pero debemos consolarnos sabiendo que la línea de Isildur seguirá. ¡Qué desgracia sería que terminara en este mundo!\
\
'¡Que Arathorn alcance un destino distinto al de su padre! Que nadie venga a esta Cima de los Trolls sin recordar el destino del Capitán de los Dúnedain. En adelante, estas alturas serán conocidas como el Fin de Arador, una advertencia para todos.'"},
[7250]={"'¿Colmilloamarillo ya no está? Me sorprende, , pero no tengo razón para dudar de tus palabras. Puede que haya juzgado mal tu valía como ${PLAYERNAME:cazador[m]|cazadora[f]}.'","'Colmilloamarillo se esconde en algún lugar del Bosque Viejo, pero deberás demostrar algo de astucia tú ${PLAYERNAME:mismo[m]|misma[f]} si quieres encontrarla, .\
\
'Esperaré a que derrotes a la poderosa loba. Si eres ${PLAYERNAME:digno[m]|digna[f]} de llamarte ${PLAYERNAME:cazador[m]|cazadora[f]}, deberías ser capaz de cumplir esta hazaña.'","Instancia: El Camino del Cazador","Colmilloamarillo está en algún lugar del Bosque Viejo.\
\
Gytha Lainey te ha encomendado la tarea de derrotar a Colmilloamarillo, una loba mortal que acecha en el Bosque Viejo. Te advirtió que Colmilloamarillo es astuta, y deberás idear alguna forma de hacerla salir de su escondite.","'Te guiaré de regreso al Campamento de Adso, , si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.'","Gytha Lainey te ha llevado al Bosque Viejo para poner a prueba tu habilidad como ${PLAYERNAME:cazador[m]|cazadora[f]}.","Gytha Lainey te espera en algún lugar del Bosque Viejo.\
\
Gytha se alegrará —y se sorprenderá— al saber que has derrotado a Colmilloamarillo."},
[7251]={"Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, wishes to learn more of the political tensions that arose during Fram's reign over the Ai-thúda.","Talk to Léothred","'All the guests arrived, excited to meet the one who had slain Scatha, the Worm. The feast began with lively song and joyous laughter....'","Listen to Léothred's tale","'What began in celebration might have ended in a declaration of war, had it not been for Wandalb who was able to steer the Men and dwarves back from the brink of battle.'","Instancia: El festín desafortunado","Talk to Léothred.","Listen to Léothred's tale."},
[7252]={"'Mira esto. Todos mis amigos se han reunido para sorprenderme con una celebración de cumpleaños. No puedo creerlo.\
\
'Gracias, a todos, gracias.'","Habla con Sig Mandrake","'Aún no he desempacado mis cuerdas. Resistirán, estoy seguro, pero necesito mas tiempo. Hay muchas cosas que aún debemos izar.\
\
'Oh, después de tanta planificación, que todo se arruine al final por falta de tiempo. Vi lo afilado que está el cuchillo de Culver. Si no me apuro podría usarlo conmigo después.'","Garrett el Retorcido está en el Escondite de los Infiltradores.\
\
Debes ver si puedes detener la sorpresa que traman los infiltradores.","Habla con Artie Raíz","Habla con Culver el Ingenioso","'Desilusionado? En absoluto. No me interesa mucho la sopa de tortuga, para empezar. Y mira a todos esos pequeños amigos, corriendo como si fueran los dueños del lugar.\
\
'Quizás deberían serlo. Tengo un hogar espacioso no muy lejos de aquí, y entiendo que el alcalde suele hacer la vista gorda respecto a quienes tienen numerosas mascotas en sus casas en Bree. Podría darles a estas pequeñas tortugas mansas una buena casa.\
\
'Se quedarán conmigo. Decidido. Este es el mejor cumpleaños de todos. He sido sorprendido por mis viejos amigos, y he adquirido numerosos nuevos amigos, ${RACE} y tortugas por igual.'","Culver el Ingenioso está dentro del Escondite de los Infiltradores.\
\
Debes ver si puedes detener la sorpresa que traman los infiltradores.","Sig Mandrake está en el Escondite de los Infiltradores.","Encuentra y habla con Garrett el Retorcido","Has llegado al escondite de los infiltradores en Bree, y debes ver si puedes detener la sorpresa que han planeado.","'Casi olvido el plato principal, Artie. De qué sirven las rebanadas gruesas de pan crujiente sin nada en qué mojarlas?\
\
'Todos juntamos unas monedas para comprar un gran pedido de sopa de tortuga en la conocida tienda de Sig Mandrake. Debería llegar con la sopa en cualquier momento.'","'Te mostraré mi hogar, ${PLAYER}. Puedes ayudarme a llevar a algunos de mis nuevos amigos con pico.'","'Pensé que esto era una fiesta de disfraces. Soy el único que lleva disfraz? Por qué SIEMPRE me pasa esto?\
\
'Es tan difícil enviar una nota diciendo que no debo usar mi disfraz de esqueleto? Tomaría solo un momento, pero nooooo, de alguna manera siempre se les pasa.\
\
'Hmm. Al menos están estos pequeños aquí para hacerme compañía. Es como si ellos también llevaran disfraces, no es así? Pequeños compañeros con armadura. Míralos. Me gustan las tortugas, bien?'","Habla con Artie Root","Instancia: La Sorpresa de los Infiltradores","'No pude hacerlo, ${PLAYER}. Después de ver a todas esas pequeñas tortugas, con sus caparazones diminutos y sus pequeños picos mordedores, simplemente no pude convertirlas en sopa.\
\
'Las traje aquí, atadas en un saco que me dio el sobrino de Grobo. Lo dejé allí, junto a la puerta. Quizás podamos devolverlas a la naturaleza, y mis clientes me perdonarán por no cumplir con el trato.\
\
'Reembolsaré sus monedas, por supuesto.'","Encuentra y habla con Culver el Ingenioso","Artie Raíz está en el Escondite de los Infiltradores.","Culver el Ingenioso está en el Escondite de los Infiltradores.","'No te he visto por aquí antes. ¿Seguro que eres uno de los nuestros? Esto se ha estado preparando desde hace mucho, y no quiero que algún forastero lo arruine.\
\
'La gente no olvidará pronto lo que haremos hoy, no si mi nombre es Culver el Ingenioso. Que lo es. Ves esta hoja? Puedo cortar limpiamente cualquier cosa que me proponga, así de afilados son ambos filos: la hoja y mi mente.\
\
'He estado cortando cosas toda la mañana, y cortaré mas antes de que termine el día. Ya lo verás.\
\
'Ve a la sala principal y fíjate si Garrett ya está listo. No queda mucho tiempo.'"},
[7253]={"Scout-master Ausma intends to find a way deep into Shakhajât in order to learn more about Warlord Dushtalbúk and his advisors.","Talk to Scoutmaster Ausma","'Well, we're inside now, but who knows where? Stay close to me, and keep to the shadows. Let's see if we can't find the warlord.'","Talk to Scout-master Ausma","Enter Shakhajât","Ausma is pleased with your progress so far.","'Let's get out of here before we're seen. We can talk about what we just learned back at camp.'","Listen to the conversation","Instancia: El Círculo Íntimo","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow the hobgoblins to see you!</rgb>","You should eavesdrop and see what can be learned.","You should follow Ausma.","You have found another way into Shakhajât","Ausma is continuing to explore, and will need your help.","Follow Scout-master Ausma","'Good, we managed to get this far unseen. We're on the west side of the pit now. I noticed there are quite a few catwalks and scaffolding on the exterior of Shakhajât. I have a hunch we'll be able to use them to find another way inside the fort. Are you ready to move in?'"},
[7255]={"Ingold is concerned that in defeat, Dulgabêth and his followers may direct their wrath upon Gondorians in Mordor.","Listen to the conversation","<rgb=#FF0000>Listen</rgb> to the conversation","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave your hiding place!</rgb>","Follow Ingold","Talk to Ingold.","'I am not sure what it is we are seeing over there atop that rock. Its glow is soft, almost Elven. Do you suppose it is some sort of weapon perhaps?'","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso.","This is a good place to listen","'Argh! This certainly did not go as planned, ${PLAYER}. This is not the fault of either of us. Not a one of us expected these Morroval to descend and snatch the Ithil-stone from us all!\
\
'Now we must return empty handed. Our only solace is that we have defeated The Black Word's lieutenants once again.\
\
'Come let us start on the return.'","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso","'We should return swiftly and tell the Elves of our company about what we have seen here. They may want to investigate this further.'","Talk to Ingold","'We have made it this far undetected. The path ahead to Barad-dûr will be difficult.\
\
'What's this?! Look ahead ${PLAYER}. There seems to be some sort of meeting taking place on the road between us and the ruined tower.\
\
'You have dealt with some of these foes before. Still, a meeting of Dulgabêth's minions does not bode well for us.\
\
'We must attempt to get closer and listen in on their plans, whatever they may be. From there we should have enough information to devise a proper plan.'","Instancia: La piedra de Ithil","Defeat Dulgabêth's servants.","You see something glinting from atop a rock spire","Get closer so that you may overhear the conversation","Defeated Krassa-phûrsa","Confront Dulgabêth's servants and retrieve the Ithil-stone.","Defeat Dulgabêth's servants","Follow Ingold.","Get closer so that you may overhear the conversation.","¡Te han descubierto!","Listen to the conversation.","Confront Dulgabêth's servants and retrieve the Ithil-stone","Defeated Glúrugoth"},
[7256]={"Agelwyn and her party are by the river-bank in the southern Westfold.\
\
You should speak with Agelwyn.","Follow Agelwyn","'That did not go well at all, but it is done. I will not look back now. Let us get this journey over with.\
\
'We ride at once!'","The first people you met in the Westfold have been murdered by the White Hand... innocent people.","<rgb=#FF0000>Mourn</rgb> the slaughtered innocents","'We have been blessed with a safe journey thus far! I hope it stays that way. Helm's Deep draws near.\
\
'Take heart, people of Marton! We are almost there.'","Agelwyn needs your aid in escorting her people to Helm's Deep across the dangerous plains of the Westfold.","You should speak with Agelwyn.","'Did you know these poor people, ${PLAYER}? I am so sorry.\
\
'...They were like us, were they not? Unarmed people, fleeing to the Hornburg for safety. If you had not been with us, this would have been us.\
\
'Helm's Deep is so near! Let us continue, ${PLAYER}.'","Listen to Agelwyn","Agelwyn is undeterred by the rebellion of half of her followers","Agelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton.\
\
You should help Agelwyn lead her people to Helm's Deep.","Follow Agelwyn and keep her people safe.","Agelwyn's speech did not go as well as she hoped, but several people are still willing to follow her","'Everyone has gathered. I must address the people of Marton now....'","Keep the people of Marton safe","Agelwyn is heartened by the good fortune encountered on the journey","Agelwyn has died","Elstan has died","Speak with Agelwyn","Agelwyn and her party are travelling along the river-bank towards Helm's Deep.\
\
You should keep the people of Marton safe as they travel.","You should <rgb=#FF0000>mourn</rgb> the refugees.","Talk to Agelwyn","You recognize this person -- you saw these refugees on the road when you first entered the Westfold.\
\
These poor folk never made it to Helm's Deep, for the plains were crawling with deadly servants of the enemy.","Instancia: El viaje al Abismo de Helm","'We are almost there, and then we part ways. I cannot thank you enough for getting us through this.'"},
[7257]={"'The host is assembled and ready to ride, ${PLAYER}, but there is still one matter I would see resolved. Will you find Gléowine and bring him before me?\
\
'There is still the matter of his punishment to be settled.'","'Farewell, until we meet once more, ${PLAYER}. Watch over the people of Rohan while Théoden is away, and trust not too easily! There are foes hidden in plain sight. We have Saruman, and Gríma, to thank for that.'","'I understand your path leads elsewhere, ${PLAYER}, but still we may yet meet again. There are dangers aplenty in Rohan, and not enough good-hearted folk to defeat them. If only there were two of you, or four, or six!'\
\
Aragorn laughs, and some of the Riders nearby look at him curiously.\
\
'Sounds of merriment are rare in these times, ${PLAYER}, and defeating Saruman will not change that. Gandalf is quick to remind me that the real foe lies East and not West, but if Rohan is to survive we must do something about the enemy that is nearest. And we will.'","'Gandalf was right, ${PLAYER}. I have sat in the shadows of my hall for too long. It is good to breathe the clean air once more, and to feel the breeze upon my face. Gríma's whisperings made me forget, but now the memory of good has returned to me, and in greater force than before!\
\
'Walk with me a ways, ${PLAYER}. I have a request to make of you.'","Gléowine is somewhere outside Edoras.\
\
Théoden has asked for you to bring Gléowine before him.","Talk to Aragorn outside Edoras","Listen to Théoden issue commands before the host","Instancia: El Rey Cabalga hacia el Poniente","Théoden is outside Edoras, ready to ride to war.","Théoden is outside Edoras, among the host that plans to ride to Isengard.","Talk to Gimli outside Edoras","Talk to Théoden outside Edoras","Aragorn, Legolas, and Gimli are by the side of the river outside Edoras, waiting for the host to depart.","Théoden has called Gléowine before him.","Éomer is outside Edoras, with the great host that has assembled to ride with Théoden.","'I know you are needed elsewhere, ${PLAYER}. Still I would feel more at ease if you rode with us.'\
\
Éomer hesitates, and you can see him struggling with the weight of a decision.\
\
'I do not want to add my own worries to those that already concern you, but if you find yourself in the Eastfold, perhaps you will cast an eye toward my own home? The town of Aldburg is my home, when I am not in Edoras, and it is now left in the care of my steward Arcil. It has been a long while since I returned to Aldburg, and I worry that the dangers that threaten the rest of the Mark may also affect my home. You need not go there in haste! Help my sister with her own task first, but it would ease my mind if I thought you might go to Aldburg afterward.\
\
'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Éomer outside Edoras","Théoden wishes to speak with you before the host departs.","Find and talk to Gléowine outside Edoras","Talk to Théoden before the host","Théoden has mustered a great host, more than a thousand spears, to ride to Isengard and bring war upon the Wizard Saruman.","'There you are, ${PLAYER}! Did you not recognize me? Théoden gave us raiment of war from his own hoard. I prefer my own garb, but we ride now to war and this shining mail will serve me better. Still I appreciate the gift.'","'The King has chosen this moment to reveal his punishment? I am prepared, ${PLAYER}. Whatever my King decides will be just.'","Talk to Legolas outside Edoras","'It is done, ${PLAYER}. Each of the three of you: Gléowine, Horn, and the ${RACE} with whom I now speak, will serve Rohan in the ways for which you are best suited, and scrub away the black mark incurred by defying my command.\
\
'Now it is time to depart. Aid my sister-daughter Éowyn as the people journey to Dunharrow, and wish us well in the battle! With good fortune we will overcome, and put an end to Saruman's treacheries at long last!'","'The armour of this land is not made for dwarves, ${PLAYER}, but the king gave to me a shield bearing his device: a white horse on a green field. I am proud to bear it, but I am less pleased at the prospect of being borne by such a creature on the journey to Isengard!\
\
'I have had enough of bouncing around on the back of such beasts like a sack of meal! Éomer says that I may ride with him, and I have agreed to take him up on his offer, as long as Legolas will ride beside us. Together we will teach young Éomer how mistaken he has been concerning the Lady of the Golden Wood. We will be good company, assuming he learns this lesson well, and quickly!'","Talk to Théoden among the host"},
[7258]={"Defeat Dómor","Instancia: El Rey Bajo la Montaña","Remain on your guard and protect the king from danger","Hrostyr, the personal guard of King Thorin, will bring you to see him.","Wait with Bósi for your audience with King Thorin","Evil has come to the Lonely Mountain, and the dwarves fight to defend their home.","Talk to Hrostyr","'You desire an audience with King Thorin? He will grant it, I am sure, but right now he is meeting with another. It should not be long. He hears a report from Dómor, one of the heroes that adventured in Mordor. He has returned with tidings for the king.'","You have come with Bósi for an audience with King Thorin III.","King Thorin has commanded you to keep Dómor from escaping.","You are waiting for an audience with King Thorin.","Remain on your guard for further danger","A sensation of great evil emanates from the fallen helm!","Knock the helm from Dómor's hand before he gives it to Thorin","'Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. I will question Dómor before he is brought to the dungeons, but it seems clear what I will learn: he betrayed Eirek and Mogi to their deaths.\
\
'Do not go just yet. I will have further need of you in this matter.'","Something is not right! You have to stop Thorin from wearing that helm!","Something is not right. You are overcome with an evil sensation!"},
[7259]={"Gondor has a king again!","Talk to Imrahil before the gate of Minas Tirith","Witness events as they transpire before the city","The Host of the West has come to the gate of Minas Tirith, and Faramir, Steward of Gondor, greets Aragorn outside the city.","'It will not be long now, ${PLAYER}. Find a place to stand among the ranks here on the right side, and I will rejoin you shortly.'","After so long, Gondor at last has a king again.","Instancia: El Rey y el Senescal","Prince Imrahil told you to find a good place to stand among the townsfolk on the right side as you approach the city.","Find a good place to stand among the townsfolk on the right","'Ah, have you come to see the ceremony? I have been telling my kinswoman from the country some of the finer points she might otherwise miss. Life in the city can be very different from that in the smaller villages, as I am sure you are aware!\
\
'Why, there are so many great folk coming hither and thither on important errands! And now one is to be made king! My cousin disbelieves that I have rubbed elbows with one such as he, but I say truly that is the case, and who would doubt Ioreth in this? None who know her reputation for speaking truth would dare it!\
\
'Now shush, for the Steward prepares to begin!'","You have come with the Host of the West to the gates of the White City, where the future rule of Gondor will be determined.","'My heart swells to see this day, ${PLAYER}! May the reign of King Elessar be long and fruitful, and may Gondor prosper beneath his rule!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Cheer</rgb> for the king and for Gondor","Ioreth nods at you conspiratorially as you approach","Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth is before the gate of the White City, waiting to speak with you."},
[7260]={"Instancia: El Campeón de la Dama","Defend Lúfa against the White Hand's hirelings.","Talk to Lúfa in Ordlac's house","Lúfa is at Ordlac's house in Oserley.\
\
Speak with Lúfa and make sure that she is unharmed.","Lúfa has retired for the evening, leaving you to stand guard against the anticipated attempt upon her life.","Check the corpse of the brigand leader for evidence","Defend Lúfa against the White Hand's hirelings","Defended Lúfa against the White Hand's hirelings","Secure the windows and door","'Aye, I am unharmed...is that all of them? Are there any hiding in the shadows?'","Check the corpse of the brigand leader for evidence.","Check the windows and doors to make sure they are secured.","You have found a dagger, covered with a slimy black substance","'You...you saved my life! How may I repay you?'","The windows and door are securely locked"},
[7262]={"Derrota a Gorgar el Despiadado","'Durin's forces have opened an aisle for us. We must pass through it, and climb the mountain!\
\
'Let none stand in our way.'","'We are nearly there.'\
\
Mótsog looks out over the yawning brink, unconcerned by the great height. The waning light of day occupies his every thought.\
\
'I will face the dragon, but I will need you to stand against her minions. Can you do this?'","Stand with Mótsog","You have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.","As the sun sets behind distant hills, Mótsog's time on this world draws near its end.\
\
The dragon still lives.","Instancia: El Último Mazo Gris","Talk to Mótsog beneath the peak","Defeat Ailgar and Rúvaran","Confront Hrímil Frost-heart","A great cheer sounds from far below!","Gorgar has succumbed to the voice of the dragon. He must be defeated if Mótsog is to face Hrímil Frost-heart.","Two leaders of the Angmarim have blocked your way up the slope to Hrímil Frost-heart, and they must be defeated if Mótsog is to reach the dragon.","Talk to Mótsog","'It is a long way to the summit, friend of Durin. We cannot stop now.'","Mótsog has fallen, and you have failed!","Prince Durin has asked you to accompany Mótsog to the peak, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.","Talk to Mótsog on the slope"},
[7263]={"Instancia: El Último Refugio","Con tu ayuda, Glóin pudo obtener la Piedra Clave de la entrada secreta que lleva al torreón interior de la fortaleza enano ubicada en el paso de Gabilazan. Junto a su hijo, Gimli, te ha pedido que entres en esta fortaleza y pongas fin al Nazgûl y a Skorgrím.","'Parece que estos Duramano no esperaban que viniéramos por la puerta oculta, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Esto es divertido, pero me canso de tratar con Duramano menores. ¡Encontrémonos con Skorgrím sin más demora!'","Habla con Gimli para comenzar tu incursión en la fortaleza enana.\
\
La fortaleza enana en el paso de Gabilazan podría ser tanto el último escondite de los Duramano liderados por Skorgrím como del Nazgûl al que has perseguido a través del Bosque de los Trolls y hasta las Montañas Nubladas.","Habla con Gimli para continuar tu incursión en la fortaleza enana.\
\
La fortaleza enana en el paso de Gabilazan podría ser tanto el último escondite de los Duramano liderados por Skorgrím como del Nazgûl al que has perseguido a través del Bosque de los Trolls y hasta las Montañas Nubladas.","'Estoy listo para continuar, si tú también lo estás. Retaré a Skorgrím a que baje, y si no lo hace, buscaremos la puerta oculta.'","Gimli está de pie en el patio de la fortaleza de Gabilazan.\
\
Has derrotado con éxito a Skorgrím Duramano, pero el significado de su muerte aún es incierto.","Enfrenta al Nazgûl y a Skorgrím","'¡Has luchado bien, ${PLAYER}, y hemos puesto fin a la amenaza de Skorgrím! Me preocupa la huida del Nazgûl y la aparición que surgió tras la muerte de Skorgrím, pero por ahora nada podemos hacer al respecto. ¡Al menos hemos hecho pagar a los Duramano por su traición! ¡Ja, ja!'","'Skorgrím ya no tiene dónde esconderse, , y creo que ahora lo comprende. Su perdición está frente a su puerta, y no le queda otra opción que afrontarla.\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para la batalla?'","Has avanzado hasta lo profundo de la fortaleza enana. Está casi a punto el momento de enfrentar al Nazgûl y a Skorgrím. Habla con Gimli para comenzar la batalla final.\
\
La fortaleza enana en el paso de Gabilazan podría ser tanto el último escondite de los Duramano liderados por Skorgrím como del Nazgûl al que has perseguido a través del Bosque de los Trolls y hasta las Montañas Nubladas.","'Skorgrím debe pensar que los muros de su fortaleza lo mantendrán a salvo, tan altos y anchos como son, pero no conoce la Piedra Clave que recuperaste.\
\
'Lucharemos contra sus defensas restantes, y quizás le dé una oportunidad de salir por las puertas principales de la fortaleza para enfrentarse conmigo en combate. No tiene honor, así que probablemente mi desafío quede sin respuesta. Lo mismo da, ¡mi hacha ansía la ocasión de acabar con este necio duramano!\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}? ¡Los Duramano no pueden esperar resistirnos!'","Habla con Gimli","'Ha sido una buena batalla, pero creo que es hora de marcharnos. Estoy listo para regresar a las habitaciones de invitados en Rivendel cuando tú lo estés.'","Skorgrim fue derrotado"},
[7264]={"Habla con Ravaedron frente a la Cabaña del Helechal","Himeinior ha accedido a ayudar a Ravaedron con su último plan, y está esperando para hablar contigo.","Ravaedron ha terminado lo que fuera que estuviese haciendo y ya está listo para agradecerte tu ayuda.","Te ha tocado la poco envidiable tarea de soportar el disgusto de los Astaciervo con Ravaedron.","Has venido con Ravaedron a la Cabaña del Helechal.","Ravaedron te ha pedido que llames a la puerta de la Cabaña del Helechal.","'¿Te dijo Ravaedron cuánto iba a tardar esto? Porque a mí no me dio ninguna indicación, ¡y esta no es la única tarea que tengo hoy por delante!\
\
'Esperemos que sean minutos y no horas.'","Habla con Ravaedron","'Debo prepararme, ${PLAYER}. Llama a la puerta mientras me alisto.'","A Ravaedron se le ha ocurrido otro plan con el que espera arreglar las cosas con los Astaciervo.","Llama a la puerta de la Cabaña del Helechal","Habla con Himeinior","'Nuestro próximo destino es la Cabaña del Helechal, ${PLAYER}. Con tu ayuda arreglaré esto.'","Instancia: La amistad duradera","Ravaedron os ha pedido a los Astaciervo y a ti que lo sigáis a un lado de la Cabaña del Helechal.","Soporta la tormenta de indignación de los Astaciervo con Ravaedron","Sigue a Ravaedron"},
[7265]={"'Good. We are convened. Let us learn the weaknesses of our enemies.'","Mizâdi is ready to meet with her allies and plan her strategy for Idagâl.\
\
You should speak to Mizâdi to begin the meeting.","Listen to the conversation","Our pursuit of Bârshud has led us to Idagâl, a scorched land of scavengers and cruelty. Here we will stand defiant and push the empire of Ordâkh out of the region for good. But first, we need allies.","Talk to Mizâdi","'That is the plan. We gather more allies... and then we strike.'","Instancia: La balada de la tierra seca","Mizâdi is speaking with her advisors about the situation in Idagâl.\
\
You should listen to the conversation."},
[7266]={"Listen to Durin conclude the tale","'A simple dwelling was fashioned in the caverns deep beneath Gundabad, and it was there that Mótsog went to live out his remaining years. I brought supplies and provisions to that deep cavern from time to time, for Mótsog refused to walk among the dwarves who lived in the halls above. As a hermit he lived, he who once pretended to kingship. He never again raised a weapon in anger.\
\
'Was I his jailor or his friend, ${PLAYER}? I see now that I was both, but it was not I alone who kept him here. Mótsog remained in this place for the guilt he felt, and as the years passed, folk who lived in Gundabad and elsewhere forgot the dwarf he had been and remembered only his name and the ill repute of his deeds.'","Habla con Durin","The curtain of memory has pulled back, revealing to Durin the lives he lived and the places he saw. He knows now what before he did not.","Durin has the knowledge now to finish the tale of Mótsog.","Durin has more to say of the Sunder-battle's aftermath.","Instancia: El Legado de Durin","'The Greymauls who survived the Sunder-battle, though they were few in number, were granted mercy. They were made to shear their beards short as penance for raising weapons against their proper king and for allying with the Orcs, and for generations after no child of a Greymaul was permitted to wear his or her beard longer than a hand's breadth.\
\
'Many dwarves looked upon the Greymauls with distrust for years afterward, but none more so than Ragna the Fierce. She it was who suggested that dwarf-women should remain ever-vigilant in the halls of their folk, for hearth and home can be endangered when watchfulness fails. Ragna swore to never again allow such rebellion to grow and thrive in the halls of her people, and for all her remaining years and for those of her daughters, it did not.'","Durin wishes to conclude the tale.","'The two armies of the dwarves had won the day, but each had suffered grievous losses. And yet their wounds did not quench their battle-fury; Longbeard and Greymaul alike pursued the retreating Orcs, slaying them by the thousand. The Orc-host was so badly-defeated it would not trouble the Misty Mountains for the remainder of the age.\
\
'Consumed with frustrated wrath, Morgoth's lieutenant Sauron witnessed his allies' defeat and fled with the surviving dragons back to Thangorodrim, where he would face his master's displeasure.\
\
'Let us hurry. The memory of the charnel house that Biriz-zahar became pains my heart.'","Durin has agreed to conclude the tale of Mótsog, for it is not that dwarf's tale alone, but Durin's as well."},
[7267]={"Find Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth and invite them to the Feast of Durin's Folk","Witness the arrival of King Thorin's final guest","King Thorin III beckons you to his side...","Talk to King Thorin III","'It is a day of great celebration for Durin's Folk, ${PLAYER}. All around us the halls of Erebor echo with laughter and merriment!\
\
'As well they should! This day, we honour our friends and our kin, and we proclaim our victory over the Enemy and those that followed him.\
\
'Come, my friend. Let us join the others at my table!'","King Thorin III has planned a great celebration for the Dwarves of Durin's Folk.","Spakorth can be found among the revellers in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You have found Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth and should now request that they join King Thorin at his table.","'Oh! ${PLAYER}, how good it is to see you!\
\
'It has been quite the celebration already, don't you think? I have never heard such songs or seen such... dances, but I am pleased to be welcome among Durin's Folk. Do you wish to join us?'\
\
You inform Spakorth that he, Dréri, and Náth have been summoned by the King Under the Mountain and have been granted seats at his table.\
\
'Of course we accept his invitation! It would be a great honour to feast with King Thorin, and to thank him again for the kindness he has shown my people.\
\
'Dréri! Náth! Come with me!'","Attend the Feast of Durin's Folk with King Thorin","Find Gimli, Dori, and Nori and send them to the Feast of Durin's Folk","King Thorin's speech is interrupted by frantic shouting echoing through the Hall Under the Mountain!","Your seat can be found next to Dwalin at the leftmost end of the table.\
\
King Thorin has offered you a seat at his table, and you should now inspect it as King Thorin asked.","Amid the din of the Feast of Durin's Folk, Gimli is speaking to Dori and Nori in hushed tones...","'Oh, ${PLAYER}, I did not realize we had been speaking for so long!\
\
'You see, I have been talking to Dori and Nori about my adventures, and I had just mentioned the book I discovered in the halls of Khazad-dûm. It concerns their brother, Ori, and Balin's expedition, but I should not tell such stories on a day of celebration. It is not the time for such things....\
\
'We shall go to join the King Under the Mountain at his table at once! All of this talk has made me hungry!'","Instancia: El Legado del Pueblo de Durin","'It is a fine work, is it not? I did not choose it for you on a mere whim!'\
\
King Thorin glances at the remaining empty seats at his table.\
\
'Ah, but a few of my guests are still absent. I sent word to Spakorth and his warriors, but I do not know if they understood my meaning. I am certain they are about in the Hall, but I wish for them to join me at my table. Spakorth and his kin are our new friends and allies, and I would not deny them a warm welcome to Erebor.\
\
'Would you seek out Spakorth and his kin? Send them here, and we shall soon be able to begin our feast!'","'It brings me great joy to see the many Dwarves of Durin's Folk and our kin from the East united as one. If we do not recognize and celebrate such times of peace, it is certain they will be lost to us evermore.'\
\
King Thorin III pauses for a moment.\
\
'Ah... I have spoken enough! Let us share in this feast together!'","Gimli, Dori, and Nori can be found somewhere in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
Glóin has asked that you find Gimli, Dori, and Nori and send them to join the Feast of Durin's Folk at King Thorin's table.","You have summoned the Stout-axes to the Feast of Durin's Folk, and you should now return to your seat at King Thorin's table.","Glóin can be found at King Thorin's table in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You have returned to King Thorin's table, but just as you were about to take your seat, Glóin tried to get your attention. You should speak to him.","Inspect the seat King Thorin has chosen for you","'Enough talk! Let us eat, ${PLAYER}!'","'Hail, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I am glad to see you here at our table. You are a fine adventurer and ever a friend to those in need, and your presence here is well-earned. You are not unlike my Gimli, except you were courteous enough to attend at the time King Thorin requested.\
\
'I know Gimli is here in the Hall, but I have not seen him in some time. I think he has gone off with Dori and Nori, but who can say? Will you find him and send him here? For that matter, send Dori and Nori as well!\
\
'We cannot wait all day to begin the feast!'","King Thorin III is standing beside his table in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
All of King Thorin's guests have arrived, and now the feast can begin. You should talk to King Thorin.","Nár shuffles up the stairs to greet King Thorin III...","Listen to King Thorin III","King Thorin III was hoping that one more dwarf would attend the Feast of Durin's Folk, but he is uncertain when or if he will arrive.\
\
You should wait with King Thorin III.","The Stout-axes can be found somewhere among the celebrations in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
King Thorin III has asked you to find Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth in Erebor and offer them an invitation to join the King Under the Mountain at his table.","Gimli, Dori, and Nori can be found on the upper level of the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You have found Gimli, Dori, and Nori and should now urge them to attend the Feast of Durin's Folk at King Thorin's table.","Return to your seat at the Feast of Durin's Folk","King Thorin gestures to the end of the table...","King Thorin III is giving a speech to the Dwarves of Durin's Folk in attendance.\
\
You should listen to King Thorin III.","This stone-wrought chair bears few marks of age, and appears surprisingly comfortable...","Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth appear to have joined Durin's Folk in the celebration!","King Thorin III can be found at his table in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You have found all the missing dwarves and should now return to King Thorin III and attend the Feast of Durin's Folk.","Invite Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth to the Feast of Durin's Folk","Habla con Glóin","King Thorin's feasting table can be found on the landing before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You should attend the Feast of Durin's Folk with King Thorin.","King Thorin is standing beside his table in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You have inspected the chair King Thorin chose for you, and you should now speak to King Thorin.","'Thank you for gathering my folk, ${PLAYER}. There is little sense in having a feast if there is no one with which to share it.\
\
'This is a fine assemblage of friends and kin, but one of my guests has still not arrived. It was he I hoped to see most of all, for his long absence from his people should be ended.\
\
'Let us wait just a few more moments more on his arrival, and then we shall begin the feast.'","Await the arrival of King Thorin's final guest","Disappointed that his guest must not be coming, King Thorin shuffles impatiently and begins to speak...","Listen to King Thorin III and Nár","Glóin tries to get your attention!","King Thorin III is standing before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
At King Thorin's request, you have come to attend a great feast and celebration in Erebor.","Frantic shouting has interrupted King Thorin's speech to the Dwarves of Durin's Folk.\
\
You should remain alert and witness the arrival of whoever has been shouting.","Habla con Gimli","King Thorin III is speaking to the Dwarves of Durin's Folk and welcoming Nár back to Erebor.\
\
You should listen to King Thorin III and Nár."},
[7268]={"Verify the Boar of Everholt has succumbed to its wounds","The strong musk of boar wafts in from the north","The Boar of Everholt is nearby.\
\
The Boar's trail leads to the north, towards the sound of running water.","The fabled Boar of Everholt has finally been defeated.\
\
During the battle, you suffered severe wounds and now fight to retain consciousness.","The Boar of Everholt has sustained grave injuries and is heading towards the stream.\
\
Follow the Boar of Everholt to ensure that you have finally defeated the great beast.","Do not succumb to the wounds suffered during the battle","Defeat the Boar of Everholt","The Boar of Everholt is near.\
\
You should slay the great beast.","The Boar of Everholt has sustained grave injuries","'I think that I have spoken enough for one night, ${PLAYER}.'","Follow the trail of the Boar of Everholt to the north","Follow the scent of the Boar of Everholt.","The musky scent of the Boar draws nearer","The fabled Boar of Everholt collapses as pain overcomes you from a vicious wound suffered during battle","The Boar of Everholt is drinking from the stream. You should attack while it is unaware","Meregyth begins to regale you with the tale of King Folca the Hunter and the Boar of Everholt.","Instancia: La Leyenda de Folca","Continue to follow the trail of the Boar of Everholt to the north","The Boar of Everholt is very close.\
\
You should approach the great creature quietly.","Find the trail of the Boar of Everholt"},
[7269]={"Tamper with the Narghâk weapons aboard the Kosagháti (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Rothog beside the burning wreck of the Orc-ship Grishúlvosh","You have come with Jajax, Rothog, and Belondor to destroy the Narghâk weapons used by the Song.","'I was too late, ${PLAYER}... too late to save him.'\
\
Rothog looks up from his fallen comrade, the half-troll's own body singed and crackling in the heat.\
\
'I battled the captain of this ship in combat while Belondor went to disable the Narghâk weapons. Something went wrong... the Hungry Fire...\
\
'The Orcs knew our purpose here, and set a trap for us. They damaged the mechanism of the Narghâk weapons, and when Belondor...'\
\
Rothog bares his fangs at you.\
\
'After the explosion, I ran into the flames and carried Belondor out of the inferno... but it was too late. He completed his mission, but he has left us.'","Stand by Jajax and decide your next course","Talk to Jajax on the Kosagháti","You have successfully disabled the Narghâk weapons aboard the Ordâkhai ship Kosagháti.","Talk to Jajax on the dock","Instancia: La lección de las llamas","Together with Belondor and Rothog, you and Jajax are determined to destroy the Narghâk weapons on two of the ships of the Song.","Rothog grieves beside his fallen comrade.","Narghâk weapons aboard the Kosagháti rendered unusable (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Something has happened to the Orc-ship Grishúlvosh. Jajax demands your attention.","'I have overheard the speech of our enemies, ${PLAYER}, and learned the names of their ships. The Ordâkhai ship Kosagháti is moored nearby. The Orc-ship Grishúlvosh lies at the end of this dock.\
\
'You need not commit those names to your memory, for they will not long matter! We will teach their captains the lesson of the flames: that he who sets a fire may be the one who burns!'","'That explosion came from the direction of Grishúlvosh!'","If you tamper with the Narghâk weapons aboard the Ordâkhai ship Kosagháti, you should be able to prevent their further use."},
[7270]={"Oshadhúr derrotado","Usa la antigua forja para potenciar tu adamantita infundida.","<rgb=#FF0000>Espíritus de fuego presentes (${VALUE}/10)</rgb>","La Biblioteca de Acero está siendo atacada por una banda de Orcos de Fuego de las profundidades de Moria. Están intentando invocar suficientes espíritus de fuego para romper las protecciones que protegen la biblioteca y convertirla en un infierno. Debes proteger la biblioteca y derrotar a los Orcos si deseas hacer uso de la antigua forja que hay dentro para completar tu calidad.","Has creado una adamantita potenciada","Usa el yunque antiguo","Derrota a Oshadhúr","Derrota a los invocadores de orcos de fuego (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Invocadores de orcos de fuego derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Debes derrotar a los invocadores de orcos de fuego para evitar que invoquen suficientes espíritus para destruir la biblioteca. Si se reúnen demasiados espíritus dentro de la biblioteca, será consumida en un infierno y se perderá. Una vez que te hayas encargado de los invocadores, deberás enfrentarte al líder de los orcos...","Instancia: La Biblioteca de Acero"},
[7271]={"The Jangovar are conversing.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","Habla con Náin","Náin would like to speak with you.\
\
You should talk to Náin.","'Come, we have much to discuss.'","The Jangovar leaders are defeated!","Listen to the conversation","Talk to Tuhâl","Náin the Slakeless has engaged the Jangovar in battle!\
\
You should defeat the Jangovar!","Escape Utterby with Náin and Tuhâl","Tuhâl is nervously waiting to speak to the Jangovar leaders.\
\
You should talk to Tuhâl.","Náin has attacked the Jangovar!","Defeat the Jangovar","'Here we are, ${PLAYER}. Let us not reveal ourselves now that we are so close to our goal! Just behave as a Jangovar would, and keep your head down.'","You have escaped the chaos in Utterby","Instancia: El Enano Solitario","The dwarves have attacked Utterby!\
\
You should follow Náin and escape!","Náin cracks his neck and stretches his arms.\
\
'Hah! Those foolhardy Easterlings were no match for Narag-felak, the Blackhewer!'\
\
He gently pats his mattock.\
\
'Your prowess in battle impresses me, ${CLASS}. Now that the Jangovar leaders are dealt with, we have much to discuss.'","You have secured an audience with the Jangovar leaders, but time runs short. Lord Náin's attack comes soon."},
[7272]={"You have crossed the lake with Bori, and now he waits to speak with you before you climb to the threshold of Gundabad to meet up with Durin's fighting force.","Enter Gorgar's arena and join Durin and his allies","Prince Durin and his allies stand bravely in the arena of Gorgar the Ruthless on the very threshold of Gundabad.","Instancia: El Señor de Gundabad","The gate to the threshold of Gundabad lies ahead of you, where Gorgar has devised an arena to challenge Prince Durin and his allies.\
\
Bori needs your help to push open the gate that lies between you and Durin's fighting force.","Bori is eager to follow Durin to the threshold of Gundabad, where he hopes to observe the prince's defeat of Gorgar the Ruthless and acquisition of the title 'Lord of Gundabad.'","Remain on your guard!","Talk to Bori on the path leading to the threshold of Gundabad","Push open the gate to Gorgar's arena","'We'll have to fight our way up the slope and to the threshold of Gundabad if we do not wish to miss Prince Durin's victory. Let's go!'"},
[7273]={"Habla con Náin","Tuhâl is speaking to Lord Náin.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","'I apologize for putting this on your shoulders, ${PLAYER}, but from what I have heard, you are more than capable of this task. Keep an eye on our \\qfriend\\q here. His words are convincing, but I am not quick to trust any foreigner. Do what you can from within to clear the innocents out and undermine their operation. I will come to finish the task when the time is right.'","The time has come for Tuhâl of Chayasír to stand before Lord Náin and speak for the Easterling refugees.","'Wish me luck, friend.'","Listen to the conversation","Talk to Tuhâl","'I am so relieved that Lord Náin heard my words. Now, we must come up with a plan.'","You have been tasked with infiltrating Utterby!\
\
You should talk to Náin.","Instancia: El Señor de Hierro"},
[7274]={"Habla con Náin","'Here we are at last!\
\
'Owing to his wounds, King Thráin and his guard were forced to remain behind at Durin's Stone, but his son, Thorin, has come to aid us. In so short a time, he has made a name for himself by wielding that oak branch—the Oakenshield, they call him. Hah!\
\
'Ever since Bolg fled our arrival at Durin's Stone, my father, Náin, has pursued him... now all the way to the gates of Khazad-dûm! When we catch him, he will fare no better than his other brothers... or his father for that matter!\
\
'It's time, Hermáth. Let us join in the final attack!'","Defeat Azog","Azog's bodyguards can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm.\
\
After slaying Náin, Azog has set his bodyguards upon the Iron-folk. You should defeat Azog's bodyguards.","Azog can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm.\
\
In answer to Náin's taunts, Azog has come out of the shadows of Khazad-dûm. You should confront Azog with Náin and the Iron-folk.","Wait for Dáin","Dáin can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm.\
\
After entering Khazad-dûm, Dáin has returned deeply troubled. You should talk to Dáin.","Defeat Azog's bodyguards","Náin can be found outside the gates of Khazad-dûm at Muru Azog.\
\
Náin Orcsfoe has driven off the coward Bolg, leaving Azog to face the Haban’akkâ. You should talk to Náin.","Náin and Azog can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm.\
\
Azog has answered Náin's challenge. You should witness the battle between Náin and Azog.","Dáin has walked into Khazad-dûm.\
\
You should await Dáin's return.","Azog rushes forth!","Dáin can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm.\
\
Dáin has slain Azog. You should talk to Dáin.","Witness as Náin confronts Bolg outside Khazad-dûm","'Hah! See what the line of Azog has been reduced to!'\
\
'I'm glad to see you here at the end of this war, Hermáth. I trust you and my son have slain your fair share of Orcs!'\
\
Náin glances into the shadows beyond the gates of Khazad-dûm, gripping his mattock tightly.\
\
'We have waited long enough for our vengeance. Let us see if this coward has found his spine!'","Follow Dáin and join in the assault on the gates of Khazad-dûm","Instancia: El Señor de Moria","Dáin disappears into the shadows","Witness Náin as he battles against Azog","Atop the stairs, you find Náin Orcsfoe and his warriors prepared to confront Bolg","Azog can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm.\
\
After slaying Náin, Azog hopes to escape the wrath of the Iron-folk. You should aid Dáin and defeat Azog.","Dáin can be found just outside Muru Azog at Azanulbizar.\
\
After overcoming Azog's forces at Durin's Stone, Náin Orcsfoe and the Iron-folk have begun their assault on the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should talk to Dáin.","As the last of Azog's bodyguards falls dead, Dáin rushes forth","Too fearful to answer Náin's challenge, Bolg flees back into Khazad-dûm!","With a sickening crack, Náin's neck snaps beneath Azog's blow and Azog roars triumphantly","Talk to Dáin","Dáin can be found at the East-gate of Khazad-dûm.\
\
After slaying Azog, Dáin has chosen to enter Khazad-dûm. You should watch as Dáin enters Khazad-dûm.","Witness as Dáin enters Khazad-dûm","As you approach Dáin, he appears to hardly notice you.\
\
After a moment, he opens his mouth as if to say something, but remains silent.","Confront Azog","Dáin can be found at Muru Azog.\
\
You have joined in the assault on the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should follow Dáin and aid the soldiers of the Haban’akkâ.","'Thrór is avenged.'\
\
Dain's face is fraught with sorrow as he glances to where his father lays slain outside Khazad-dûm.\
\
'Alas, there is one more thing to be done. Wait here, my friend.'","Náin Orcsfoe and the Iron-folk have broken through Azog's defences at Muru Azog.\
\
You should aid Náin and the Iron-folk as they approach the gates of Khazad-dûm.","Without another word, Dáin turns and walks toward the threshold into Khazad-dûm","Dáin stands over Azog's broken body, and with a swift slice, he beheads the Orc","After the horn-call of Grór sounded, Náin and the Dwarves of the Iron Hills charged forth to challenge Azog and put an end to the battle.","Dáin remains silent.","Dáin runs out of the shadows of Khazad-dûm, his face grey with unknowable fear"},
[7277]={"In desperation you call her name, but Silirtas remains frozen, unaware of the evil that threatens her.","Awaken Silirtas from the enchantment that keeps her from moving","A sense of exhaustion has overcome you once again, as happened earlier when you journeyed within Maurûsh.","Prevent Azagath from inflicting great harm upon Silirtas","Place Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (1/3)","Stand your ground","Instancia: La locura en sus ojos","Check on the group placing the Narghâk on the other side","You and Sigileth have volunteered to place the Narghâk on the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr.","Place Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (0/3)","You need to seal the entrance to Utug-bûr before the Thardúth emerge and levy their full power against you.","Listen to the threatening voice within your mind","At the urging of his Thardúth masters, Azagath intends to do great harm to your friends.","The Thardúth turn their attention elsewhere in the battle. The sorcerous exhaustion that troubled you has been lifted.","'If the Thardúth were truly once of my people, I want to do my part in sealing them away, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I and Corudan will set the Narghâk to the right of the entrance. You and Sigileth can place the Narghâk on the left side. We will seal the entrance to Utug-bûr and these fallen Kintai will no longer trouble the world!'","The ethereal voice speaks threatening words from within the confines of your mind.","Talk to Silirtas outside Utug-bûr","Place Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (2/3)","Grieving that the Thardúth had their origins as ancient Kintai, Silirtas greatly desires to do her part in sealing them away.","Frozen, unmoving figures stand near at hand","Silirtas is in grave danger! She must awaken at once!"},
[7278]={"'I -- where am I? How have I come here, among the reeds. Oh,  ${PLAYER}. What terrible dreams I have had. I... I think I have not been myself.'","Fight the Orc captain among the reeds by the River Anduin.\
\
Just as Lady Vanyalos fainted, the Orc captain, Tenakrul, came upon you.","Lady Vanyalos stands between two trees, off the northward road.\
\
You have found Lady Vanyalos. You should approach her and see if she can be persuaded to return to Imloth Melui.","Protect Lady Vanyalos","Talk to Lady Vanyalos","Lady Vanyalos stands among the reeds by the River Anduin.\
\
Having come to her senses at last, the Lady Vanyalos looks ready to talk to you.","Defeated Tenakrul","Instancia: La Locura de Vanyalos","Lady Vanyalos left Imloth Melui unescorted and unguarded. Merenir, fearing for her safety and state of mind, sent you after her. You have found Lady Vanyalos just off the northward road.","Defeat Tenakrul","You hear an Orkish shout, followed by footfall. You are discovered!","<rgb=#FF0000>Lady Vanyalos has been defeated!</rgb>","'Please, would you see me home? To Imloth Melui? I fear... fear that I am unwell.'","Lady Vanyalos is wandering on the greensward by the River Anduin.\
\
You should protect the Lady Vanyalos and see if you can get her to come to her senses.","Approach Lady Vanyalos","<rgb=#FF0000>Lady Vanyalos must not be defeated</rgb>"},
[7279]={"La caza de Tasgall los ha llevado a las laderas de Nád Nathair.","'Lo hemos hecho muy bien este día, ${PLAYER}, a pesar de la interferencia de los Trév Duvárdain. Dime si estás listo para volver a mi campamento; no hablaré de Drostan y su calaña hasta que estemos a salvo del peligro.'","El plan de Tasgall está listo, y ustedes dos deben intentar acabar con la amenaza de Bangrath y Murragrath.","Habla con Tasgall","Instancia: La Matrona y el Maestro","'Tengo los restos de gusano que recogiste, ${PLAYER}; ¿hueles su horrible hedor? ¡Para las bestias de las colinas, este olor será imposible de resistir!\
\
'Comencemos nuestra caza, y atraeremos a Bangrath y Murragrath para que salgan de su escondite. Mantente atento, porque las bestias de las colinas se sentirán atraídas por el olor del cebo que llevo.'"},
[7280]={"The overseer does not seem very forgiving","The half-orc to whom you spoke seems unreasonably angry.\
\
You should defend yourself and the townsfolk from the wrath of the servants of Isengard.","Tomos is searching for his wife, Mari.\
\
You should follow Tomos through Galtrev.","'We are safe, even if only for a short time. Rest, friend. Retribution may still come, but I hope it will not be soon.'","Thank you for helping my husband, ${PLAYER}! You did what many of us could not: stand up to the injustices of Isengard. You were a great boon to the people of Galtrev today.","Try to appease the White Hand overseer","Mari is in Galtrev.\
\
You should speak with Mari.","Tomos stands nearby.\
\
You should speak with Tomos.","Defeat the servants of the White Hand.","A White Hand overseer has been defeated; this act of defiance will surely enrage the servants of Isengard","Talk to Mari","Instancia: El significado de la alianza","Help defend the people of Galtrev","Tomos has died","Tomos must not fall","An angry White Hand overseer has appeared to make Tomos answer for his crime of missing the day's work.\
\
You should speak with the overseer to try to appease him.","'Two little mongrels went rogue today and missed their day's work, ${PLAYER}. How do you propose to make up that labour to Saruman?\
\
'You had best start running, little ${RACE}, you and your friend Tomos. I will not be merciful....'","'I believe my people are ready to be free of this burden... but there is only one way to find out. But first, I must find my wife.\
\
'Come, my friend. She will be glad to know that you survived the ordeal as well.'","Follow Tomos","An angry White Hand overseer approaches...","Talk to Tomos","Tomos is searching for his wife, Mari.\
\
You should follow Tomos to Mari's side.","The people of Galtrev wish to free themselves from the unfairly one-sided alliance with Isengard's White Hand presence.","Help the people of Galtrev"},
[7281]={"Derwent no entiende por qué crees que Altapiedra tiene fama de ser peligrosa.","Ha ocurrido algo que no sucedía desde hace ocho días:\
\
¡Los orcos han llegado al pueblo de Altapiedra!","Derwent Correhuela está asustado, pero por lo demás ileso.","Derwent Correhuela ha hecho un descubrimiento desagradable, aunque no especialmente sorprendente.","'¡${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]} a Altapiedra, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! Estaré encantado de mostrarte el lugar.'","'¡Una vez más has demostrado que fue una gran idea tenerte cerca, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Pero, ¿qué quería decir ese orco cuando preguntó quién de nosotros venía de Bree? Parecía como si estuviera buscando a alguien en particular... pero ¿con qué propósito?'","Habla con Derwent Correhuela en Altapiedra","Habla con Derwent Correhuela","Instancia: La pelea en la plaza","Derwent Correhuela dejó atrás un pueblo peligroso, solo para encontrar otro.","'¡Es Bill Helechal, tiene que serlo! ¡Ese villano! ¡Dirigió a estos orcos para que vinieran en mi busca!\
\
'Qué suerte que estuvieras aquí, ${PLAYER}.'","Reúnete con algunos de los vecinos de Derwent en Altapiedra","Derwent está encantado de mostrarte su nuevo hogar, el pueblo de Altapiedra.","'Todos en Altapiedra tienen un pasado, eso seguro; ¡Derwent encajará perfectamente! Lo ayudaremos en lo que podamos. Es lo propio entre vecinos.'","Protege a Derwent y a sus vecinos de los orcos","'¡Una vez más has demostrado que fue una gran idea tenerte cerca, ${PLAYER}!'"},
[7282]={"Galadriel te espera en el centro del jardín.\
\
Galadriel te ha hecho llamar a su jardín de Lothlórien, porque desea hablar contigo.","'Sé que Gwaihir encontrará a Mithrandir, si es que hay que encontrarlo.\
\
'Haldir te mostrará el camino desde este lugar, ${PLAYER}. Lo llamaré.'","Escucha las palabras de Galadriel sobre tu destino","Gwaihir, el Señor de los Vientos, ha venido a descansar en el jardín de Galadriel.\
\
Galadriel te ha pedido que vayas a hablar con Gwaihir sobre el destino de Gandalf el Gris.","Galadriel te espera en el centro del jardín.\
\
Has visto cosas extrañas en el Espejo de Galadriel, incluyendo imágenes confusas de Gandalf y una terrible criatura: un Balrog, el Daño de Durin.","'Soy consciente de la bondad que has mostrado hacia Magor bajo las montañas, ${PLAYER}. Ahora te tiene en alta estima, y te tiene un gran aprecio por tu parte en su rescate.\
\
'Hechos extraños se desarrollan en los muchos caminos de tu viaje, pues a medida que tus pasos te llevan de aquí para allá, percibo que muchos destinos están entrelazados con el tuyo. Algunas de tus historias parecen haber terminado, pero las puertas cerradas aún pueden ser forzadas a abrirse.\
\
'Mi Espejo puede mostrar muchas cosas, y puedes pedirle lo que quieras. Pero ten cuidado antes de mirar en el agua: muchas respuestas valiosas pueden venir sin ser solicitadas. Mira ahora, y ve lo que puede ser visto.'","'Ahora se arroja algo de luz sobre los enigmas, ¿no crees? Las pistas que quedaron entre las Fundaciones de Piedra comienzan a formar una imagen clara por fin. Gandalf el Gris luchó en Moria contra la Sombra y la Llama, y ambos cayeron, y quizás se levantaron de nuevo. ¿Quién tuvo la victoria?\
\
'Se ha dicho que mis ojos ven más lejos que muchos que son considerados sabios, pero necesitamos ojos más agudos para penetrar la oscuridad que oculta a Mithrandir a mi vista. ¿Quién puede espiar Moria desde todos los lados y obtener rumores sobre el destino de Gandalf? Solo Gwaihir el Señor de los Vientos puede hacer esto.'","Habla con Gwaihir","Habla con Galadriel","El Espejo de Galadriel se encuentra en el centro del jardín.\
\
Galadriel te ha invitado a mirar en su Espejo y a preguntarle lo que quieres ver.","'Gwaihir se encuentra descansando al fondo de mi jardín. Ve a hablar con él, y le pediremos que intente espiar desde las alturas para obtener rumores sobre Gandalf. Puede que aún esté vivo... No creo que su papel en la Tierra Media haya terminado tan pronto, pues tendrá mucho que hacer antes del final...'","'He llevado a Gandalf antes, y si aún vive, lo llevaré de nuevo. Enviaré a las águilas de vista más aguda para que lo busquen por cada rincón de esta tierra, y volaré hasta que sepamos qué le ha sucedido.\
\
'Si es posible encontrarlo, mis congéneres y yo lo encontraremos.\
\
'Vuelve con la Dama y dile que haré esto.'","Instancia: El Espejo de Galadriel","La Dama Galadriel desea hablar contigo en su jardín, en Lothlórien.","Galadriel te espera en el centro del jardín.\
\
La Dama Galadriel ha visto más que el destino de Mithrandir en su Espejo; también ha visto algunos indicios de tu propio destino.","Mira en el Espejo de Galadriel"},
[7283]={"You have found a chamber of cages, and some old friends","Survive the return of the Orcs to Burg-shápol","Corudan is in the depths of Burg-shápol.","'I hear Orcs approaching, ${PLAYER}, not from ahead of us but from behind!\
\
'I will stay here to delay their approach, but you should press on into the cave to see what has become of the missing craftsmen. Perhaps one of them has escaped and we have him to thank for the dead Orcs we have seen already, but even so they are all likely still in danger. Go, and quickly!'","You have found Burg-shápol, a cave in the Everholt where the missing craftsmen may be found.","Instancia: Los Desaparecidos","You have found Nona and Corudan in the depths of Burg-shápol.","Talk to Horn in Burg-shápol","Horn is inside Burg-shápol, the cave in the Everholt where the missing craftsmen might be found.","Talk to Nona in Burg-shápol","'I will tell you the story of how Corudan and I came to be here, ${PLAYER}, but not just now. Let the tale wait until we are in the sunlight again. We have slain many Orcs to free these people, but the woods crawled with more of their kind and we should not tarry here.\
\
'Is Horn here with you?'","Many Orcs have returned to Burg-shápol, and you must defeat them!","'This was a pleasant surprise, ${PLAYER}! Now let us return to town and see what tale Nona and Corudan have to share!'","This chamber contains more dead Orcs, but no sign of the missing craftsmen","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. We thought to find you in Edoras, but on the way we found an overturned waggon and sign of struggle, and thought to look for these folk. I am glad we did, for today we have saved some lives. These Orcs were ferocious. It is fortunate that most of the creatures were away when Nona and I entered the cave.'","You hear raised voices from further ahead, but cannot make out any of the words","Horn has stayed behind to delay the approach of the following Orcs, while you search the tunnels of Burg-shápol for the missing craftsmen.","Talk to Corudan in Burg-shápol","Horn is in the tunnels of Burg-shápol.","Search the tunnels of Burg-shápol for the missing craftsmen"},
[7284]={"Utiliza la antigua forja y los fragmentos de mineral de mithril que has recogido para potenciar tu granate imbuido.","Debes encontrar suficientes fragmentos de mineral de mithril para poder aprovechar la forja de fundición y obtener la calidad que buscas. Con suerte, los trasgos esclavizados habrán logrado recolectar suficiente mineral para satisfacer tus necesidades... ahora es poco probable que se desprendan de él por las buenas.","Capataz de la mina derrotado","Has creado un granate potenciado","Recoge fragmentos de mineral de mithril (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota al capataz de la mina","Instancia: Los esclavos del mithril","Te han hablado de una mina de mithril agotada hace mucho tiempo en cuyo interior se encuentra una antigua forja de fundición. Allí dentro deberías ser capaz de sentar las bases de la calidad que buscas. Sin embargo, una despiadada banda de orcos ha esclavizado a sus propios hermanos trasgos para rebañar los últimos residuos de la mina, lo que dificultará enormemente tu acceso a la forja.","Usa el yunque antiguo","Fragmentos de mineral de mithril recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7285]={"Talk to Rothog the Storm","Instancia: La Luna sobre Ambarûl","Talk to Rahâzi","'I will hurry on to Iridír with Surdûsha and tell my mother about these newcomers, ${PLAYER}. If they are friends of yours, I believe she will give them leave to move freely within Ambarûl.'","The Dumûri warriors Rahâzi and Surdûsha have suggested that you return with them to Iridír where you can speak of your shared triumph over the Ordâkhai remnant.","'A number of difficulties threatened to delay us too long, ${PLAYER}, and it was decided we could wait no longer. The caravan driver and the warehouse master suffered our displeasure for the obstacles they placed in our way, and they will suffer even more in the days ahead, for Hármelak has a mind for punishment.\
\
'At last we set out, and it would appear we arrived at a fortunate time. Who are these warrior-women, and can we count them friends to Umbar, and to the Kindred of the Coins?'","'One more thing, ${PLAYER}, before we follow those warriors to their village and meet with their chief.\
\
'I think it will be best not to mention that Tatháta is a member of the Kindred of the Coins. She currently works at cross-purposes to us, and while she may not be allied with Azagath, neither does she work to help us. It can give us no advantage to tell the people of this land that she is a member of Umbar's ruling council.\
\
'Now let us proceed. We have traitors to find and a mission to complete, and I do not like to spend this long away from my city, and away from my other endeavours.'","Khôltekh has some words for you before you continue on to Iridír.","Stand your ground against Tatháta and protect the Dumûri warriors.","Rothog and Khôltekh have arrived in Ambarûl, and they seek to gain permission from its people to carry out the mission they share with you.","The remainder of your travelling company has arrived","'Quiet! There it is again: the sound of voices. More of the Ordâkhai have come in search of their fellows, and now they seek to surprise us.\
\
'Let us teach them to fear the defenders of this land!'","Khôltekh coughs, drawing your attention from Rothog's lion","Death comes even for a Dumûri warrior. You have failed!","Rothog the Storm has arrived, and his arrival may have saved you and the Dumûri warriors from Tatháta's wrath.","'What caused Tatháta to attack you, ${PLAYER}? She and I have faced each other in battle before, and when I tell you she is a deadly opponent you can believe me. Ours was a friendly competition, and it came to a draw, but in return she made a gift to me of Húrshauk here.\
\
'I did not plan to bring Húrshauk with me on this adventure, but he has grown so large and so ferocious that no one at Dahâl Huliz dares to approach him without me. We could delay no longer, so my good friend accompanies me. That will not be a problem.'","Rahâzi waits to speak with you before she departs.","Talk to Khôltekh","Observe the meeting of Khôltekh and Rahâzi","Stand your ground against Tatháta and protect the Dumûri warriors","Khôltekh has arrived in Ambarûl.","Rahâzi and Surdûsha have triumphed over the Ordâkhai, but now a new threat emerges.","Part of the way back to Iridír, Rahâzi has called for a halt.","'Do you know what terrible creature makes this sound, ${PLAYER}? Your eyes tell me that you do!'\
\
Hurriedly, you advise Rahâzi and Surdûsha to take defensive stances and prepare once again for battle."},
[7286]={"Derrotada la señora de los morroval","Debes derrotar a los ladrones de morroval y recuperar las herramientas que han tomado de la forja. También debes evitar que los carroñeros que huyen escapen de la forja, para que no se lleven demasiadas piezas importantes de equipo.","Has viajado a una antigua forja donde una vez se fabricaron algunas de las mejores armas de Moria, pero una banda de merrevail expulsados de sus propias cavernas ha comenzado a saquearla y a llevarse las herramientas y los materiales que hay dentro. Debes derrotar a los merrevail y recuperar las herramientas robadas antes de que dejen la forja al descubierto si deseas poder potenciar la gema que llevas.","Derrota a la señora de los morroval","Has creado un zafiro potenciado","Un carroñero morroval intenta escapar","Usa la antigua forja para potenciar tu zafiro infundido.","¡Un carroñero fugitivo ha escapado!","<rgb=#FF0000>Evita que los carroñeros que huyen escapen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>","Instancia: Los Marginados de Morroval","Usa el yunque antiguo","Recoger herramientas robadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Herramientas robadas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7287]={"Tell Grimbold the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of Elfhelm's regret","Grimbold has stopped short, his voice dropped to a whisper.\
\
'Look out ahead. Do you see the size of that troll?\
\
'We must try to take him down. I do not think we will die today, ${PLAYER}, however the odds may be against us. For Rohan!'","You must convince Grimbold that he is wrong....","The troll Bosnauk is at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should defeat Bosnauk with Grimbold, if you can.","'You have found Grimbold, and Erkenbrand has found us! This is an unexpected turn of fortune indeed. \
\
'I am sorry that your reunion must be swift, but we cannot tarry here, my friends. It is to the Hornburg that we must look.'","You must convince Grimbold to rally his spirits and help to defend the King at Helm's Deep.","Habla con Gandalf","'If my aging king can bring himself from a warm hearth and soft chair, then I will not yet condemn Rohan as lost. I will fight for Théoden, as I have always done!\
\
'Erkenbrand, Erkenbrand. We must find him, for he had good soldiers with him before we were split asunder. Erkenbrand! He cannot be far.'","Grimbold sits stubbornly, his eyes fixed upon the ground","Grimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of Hildith's regret.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You must select your target and perform the emote.</rgb>","Tell Grimbold the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of Hildith's regret","Speak with Grimbold","Grimbold is at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should speak with Grimbold.","Grimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of the king's recovery.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You must select your target and perform the emote.</rgb>","'Erkenbrand, lead on! We will go to your encampment, for we must plan our next move at once.'","Try to defeat Bosnauk with Grimbold","The shadow of despair is lifted from Grimbold's brow","Bosnauk is defeated!","Grimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should speak with Grimbold.","Observe the meeting at the fords","Help Grimbold fight!","Grimbold is unmoved by your account","Grimbold is at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should speak with Grimbold.","Grimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of Elfhelm's regret.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You must select your target and perform the emote.</rgb>","Listen to Grimbold","Tell Grimbold the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of the king","Gandalf is at the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should speak with Gandalf.","'Leave me be and let the enemy come. Just let them come! I will fall here with Prince Théodred.\
\
'I should have been the one to die, not him, for I had nothing to live for.'","Instancia: El Reclutamiento"},
[7288]={"Return to the trap.","Talk to Sírithon","Instancia: El Ladrón Misterioso","Check on the trap.","Nothing is missing","Investigate the noises","Having found convincing proof, Sírithon devises a plan to catch the Loeglond thief.","Check on the trap","Investigate the noises.","'It would seem that Esgaroth may house our thief.'","There seems to be noises coming from the other side of Loeglond!","'We laid our trap so carefully, only to be fooled by a ruse! These are sly and attentive thieves, indeed, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Sly - but not stealthier than the eyes of an Elf, ${PLAYER}. Not quite! For as we returned, I caught a glimpse - no more than a glimpse, though alas - of some shadowed figure fleeing the cart! The direction they fled, however, was plain as day. They fled towards Esgaroth.'","Return to the trap","Patrol Loeglond (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The supplies are gone!","All is quiet (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Not one movement or sign of an intruder?'\
\
Before he can speak again, shouting erupts from the other end of Loeglond.\
\
'What is that commotion? ${PLAYER}, go quickly. See what it is!'","Patrol Loeglond.","Talk to Sírithon.","The noises seem to have been a decoy!"},
[7289]={"Witness the completion of the mosaic... again","'A mosaic is not a painting, ${PLAYER}. You can change the picture by putting the stones in different places. What if... what if the mosaic Stáli assembled beneath the Lonely Mountain is not the same as this one after all?\
\
'What if this mosaic once displayed a different picture than that one?'","Observe the restoration of the mosaic","Stáli and Fastrith have finished assembling the mosaic.","Talk to Stáli the Hewer","Fastrith is eager to carry out her idea.","Stáli and Fastrith have once again finished assembling the mosaic.","Durin stands in the chamber of Zul-mazal, ready to learn whatever secrets may remain between its walls.","Remain vigilant while the dwarves consider the chamber","'Can this be anything but the work of the First Crafter, who made the dwarves? How else would the most renowned sculptor of his day, by which I mean ME, the great Stáli the Hewer, come to this chamber at this time?\
\
'I need not wait for Prince Durin's command. I will restore this mosaic to its original state, and no reward will be too great for the work at hand!'","Talk to Fastrith","Instancia: El Misterio de Zul-mazal","Witness the completion of the mosaic","Bósi and Durin have heard the sounds of approaching enemies.","Bósi, former leader of the Iron Garrison, has warned you that more hobgoblins approach.","Fastrith has had an idea.","Observe the completed mosaic","You and the dwarves have uncovered the secret of Zul-mazal, and now Durin must decide what should be done.","The dwarves believe they have uncovered the key to the mystery of Zul-mazal.","Stáli the Hewer believes his time has come at last.","Durin has come to the chamber of Zul-mazal with the intention of laying bare its mysteries.","'The hobgoblins must have sent a raiding-party in search of plunder, but they will discover their deaths by the blade of the Red Axe instead!\
\
'We will not let them disturb the work of Stáli and Fastrith, but they are more than welcome to be a part of our own work, ${PLAYER}: for that work is the slaying of hobgoblins!'","Habla con Durin","Durin and the dwarves examine the chamber for clues.","'For how long has this door remained hidden beneath Zul-mazal, ${PLAYER}? The secret craft of ancient dwarves masked it from detection by the Orcs who long resided in the mountain, but it could not escape my notice.\
\
'It was no simple mechanism that hid this trap-door for all these years, but also the working of an ancient spell. Two keys served to keep it secret, for so long as the mosaic remained incomplete and the mithril hammer was absent, none could open the passage. Now we have turned both keys, and it is time to see what lies beneath the cold stone of Zul-mazal.\
\
'Leave the mithril hammer where it lies, and I will instruct Bósi and these others to stand guard. You and I will climb through the trap-door, ${PLAYER}, and we will see what there is to see, and learn what we may of Gundabad's secrets.'","'There is something here, ${PLAYER}. I am certain of it. Is this room, like others in the Pit of Stonejaws, the tomb of a forgotten noble?\
\
'My eye is drawn to the structure in the centre of the chamber. There is a hole in the top of that curious block; it leads me to believe no body ever lay within.'","Habla con Bósi.","'Once more, my friends! Protect our prince and the artists!'"},
[7290]={"Instance: The Narrow Way","Talk to Ianudirel","Speak with Ianudirel and fight your way across the bridge to Krul Lugu.","Ianudirel has made it across","'It was a pleasure fighting by your side, ${PLAYER}. I will be able to make it back to my brother's camp easily enough from here.\
\
'You should report to him as well. I am sure there is more to be done here.'","The Elf-scout Ianudirel has been trapped across the river from Krul Lugu. She must return to the near side, but expects to be ambushed when she attempts to cross the bridge.","Talk to Ianudirel to return to Iavassúl.","'Let us be off before the fell spirits find us!\
\
'Are you ready to go?'"},
[7291]={"Listen to the Kindred discuss the disappearance of Balakhâd","Within a tower room inside the Citadel of Winds, the Kindred of the Coins discuss the days to come.","Talk to Sirgon in the tower room","The Kindred of the Coins discuss the mission to pursue Azagath and Nakási.","'Are you with me, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You assure Sirgon that you will stand with him on this adventure, and he smiles broadly.\
\
'I did not doubt it for a moment, my friend! I dare say the Elves will also wish to accompany us. I met each of them only days or weeks ago, but already I know them to be strong and capable, each in their own way. And I witnessed Sigileth's great courage when fortune ill and storm unnatural threw the Wave-hunter onto the rocks of the Shield Isles!\
\
'Who else will accompany us?'","'A new adventure begins, ${PLAYER}! The weight of the years has fallen from my shoulders, and I am ready to set foot upon the unknown road once again. Let us prove our mettle and that King Elessar chose his champions and his friends well and ably!'","Instancia: El siguiente movimiento","'Azagath hid his true nature from us. None suspected his true allegiance lay with Sauron, and now he seeks to follow the map he took from the Mâkhda Khorbo to some unknown end. I say we cannot know his purpose in this, but can there be any doubt that such a map can lead only to sorrow for the people of Umbar Baharbêl?\
\
'There was a time when Nakási Wave-reaper would not have followed Azagath on such an adventure, but I deem her mind is now clouded by the grief and rage that swirls within her breast. If the map taken by the two of them leads to some weapon of evil, can you say for certainty that it would not be used first against Umbar, and then against Gondor?\
\
'I see two important purposes along the road ahead, ${PLAYER}: first we must prevent Azagath and Nakási from locating the evil they seek. Secondly, we must find Balakhâd, son of Balakhôr, and make him once again our captive. Only then will we reacquire our bargaining power over Saklaphêl and the Heirs of Castamir.\
\
'These twin courses will bring the instruments of our will out of the city and into the wild lands of the east and south.'","Talk to Hármelak inside the tower room","'Much will depend upon how well you perform upon this adventure, ${PLAYER}. I have not forgotten that the people of my city think highly of you, and believe you should join our Kindred. Let this quest serve as your trial, with Rothog, Belondor, and Khôltekh to serve as your judges. They will assess your performance and how you conduct yourself on behalf of our shared interests: those of Umbar, and those of distant Gondor.\
\
'Prevent Azagath and Nakási from following their map to whatever evil Sauron left behind and making use of it against us. So too should you seek Azagath's former servant Sadûkh, if he seeks to rejoin his master. He may tell you what he has done with Balakhâd, son of Balakhôr the Scourge. If you can recover Balakhâd, alive, we may be able to end the threat posed by the Heirs of Castamir forever... and that will benefit not just Umbar but Gondor as well.\
\
'The lands outside the city contain perils and dangers the like of which few among you have ever faced. It will take some time to prepare the caravan that will take you out of Umbar and into the lands where your prey has vanished. Come to Dâr Laja after this and we will make such preparations as you will need.'","Listen to the Kindred discuss the adventure to come","The Kindred of the Coins discuss the recent past with you and Sirgon in a tower room in the Citadel of Winds.","Talk to Sirgon inside the Citadel of Winds","'I am pleased the two of you accepted our invitation to meet. We have much to discuss about the days ahead, and I believe the decisions we make here today may affect the fortunes of both Umbar and Gondor.\
\
'The people welcomed my Kindred with glad hearts, and cheered as we cast off the yoke placed upon our city by the Empire of Ordâkh and the Heirs of Castamir. But such a change was not without cost, and the coffers of the city are at a low ebb. I have contributed much of my own fortune to the effort, but even my own great wealth cannot support the city indefinitely.\
\
'War is expensive. Our wish is to spend no further, unless we must. How does Gondor feel on this matter? Does this King Elessar desire peace? He must know the Corsairs of Umbar retain ships enough to make him suffer for any war he begins anew.'","Hármelak and other leaders of the Kindred of the Coins await you in a tower room inside the Citadel of Winds.","Talk to Belondor inside the tower room","Hármelak wishes to discuss with you the road ahead.","Sirgon has volunteered for the dangerous mission to pursue Azagath and Nakási into the wild lands of the east and south.","Hármelak wishes to address you before you depart.","'Only members of the Kindred of the Coins knew the identity of the man we kept in this room, ${PLAYER}. Even the guards did not know. They were told he was awaiting execution for crimes against the city; their loyalty to the Kindred cannot be questioned. One day Balakhâd was safely imprisoned, as he had been for months, and then one day he was not. If the guards can be trusted, how did Balakhâd leave this tower room without being seen?'\
\
Belondor shakes his head.\
\
'The problem is more difficult than that, for the Citadel of Winds stands upon an island. Could he escape onto one of the ships, and flee that way? It is hard to imagine. But neither could he walk past the many guards posted on the island and then across the bridge back to the city without being seen.\
\
'He is not the only person who seems to have disappeared that day. One of Azagath's servants, a water-carrier by the name of Sadûkh, cannot be found. Did he help Balakhâd to escape? And if so, where might he have hidden the son of Balakhôr now? It beggars belief that such an important figure for the Heirsworn can remain hidden for so long.'","Attend your meeting with the Kindred of the Coins","You and Sirgon have been escorted to an upper level of the Citadel of Winds.","The Kindred of the Coins discuss the disappearance of Balakhâd with you and Sirgon in a tower room in the Citadel of Winds.","'How many hallways and staircases must we take to arrive at our destination, ${PLAYER}? I have already lost the path back to the entrance, despite my best effort to remember it.\
\
'What must the Kindred say to us that they cannot say in Dâr Laja, or in the main hall of this Citadel?'","You have come with Sirgon of Lebennin to an upper level of the Citadel of Winds to meet with the Kindred of the Coins.","Talk to Hármelak in the tower room","Belondor wishes to tell you what the Kindred knows concerning Balakhâd's escape from the Citadel of Winds.","'The Empire of Ordâkh and its Church of the All-seeing held Umbar in the grip of fear while the Heirs of Castamir carried out their commands, but that fear was founded upon terror of the Dark Lord and his powerful servants. When the great quake sundered his land of Mordor and caused the collapse of his temple, we who watched and waited knew our time had come. The number of our conspiracy was few, but we believed the people would join us when they witnessed the vulnerability of the Empire, and how near the Heirs of Castamir were to defeat. When no vengeful wraith emerged from the ruins of the temple or swept towards us from Mordor, the people knew Umbar could be theirs again.\
\
'With a fleet from the south, Azagath Sea-shadow swept into the Gulf of Umbar. It was poorly-defended now, with much of its power gone to the coast of Gondor, captured or burned. The Umbari rose up in open revolt, thus beginning the Sea-stone Mutiny. Those of the Heirs who resisted were slain without mercy; others either lacked courage or possessed wisdom, and fled. Some of these were Saklaphêl, the widow of Balakhôr the Scourge, and a number of her personal guards. It is believed she hides now among the Shield Isles and seeks to retake the city and her husband's rule, but she has not the numbers.\
\
'Not all of the Heirs were slain or escaped. Before he could take command of a ship and flee the Sail-haven, our forces captured Balakhâd, the twenty-year-old son of Balakhôr. We held him here in the Citadel of Winds, in this tower room, and counted him a valuable hostage.'"},
[7292]={"'I will be pleased to be away from this accursed hut. Let us go and quickly.'","'Are you prepared, ${PLAYER}? With this hag's ties to Saruman and the evil creatures haunting these fells, I fear the Old Woman of the Mountain may be more than just a simple old mountain-woman.\
\
'Be wary!'","'It is time to deal with Gwyllion!'","Defeat Gwyllion and her lieutenants","Speak with Saeradan to return to Echad Saeradan.","Saeradan must survive","Instance: The Old Woman of the Mountain","'Gwyllion has escaped, ${PLAYER}. While she may no longer bring terror to the Uch-lûth, I fear we have not yet seen the last of her.\
\
'Speak with me again when you are ready to leave.'","Accompany Saeradan to confront Gwyllion","Seek out Gwyllion at her hut beyond Gwyllion's Gate.","Habla con Saeradan","Speak with Saeradan at Gwyllion's Gate.","Saeradan has charged you with confronting Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, and driving her forth from the Windfells of Enedwaith.","Gwyllion has retreated","Saeradan has been defeated"},
[7293]={"Ask Noriel if Wynmar will live","Rothulf and Wynmar are at their camp in Thinglad.","'Do you think that was all of them, ${PLAYER}? I am weary, but I could stand another attack.\
\
'I wonder who leads this rabble.\
\
'I think I am all right. What of Wynmar? He looks tired to my eyes.'","'¿Qué está pasando?'","Talk to Rothulf","'I suppose it is time to let her go. I must. But... this all just seems so wrong now.\
\
'Why did this happen, ${PLAYER}? Have you ever felt this backwards sense that your life was fine until you met someone you could not have, then nothing would ever be as it should again?'","'He is poisoned, ${PLAYER}! I was coming to make amends for my coldness from our earlier meeting... if only I had been one moment sooner!\
\
'There is nothing I can do. It will not be long now. Poor Wynmar!'","Instancia: El ataque de los orcos","Wynmar is at his camp.","Noriel and Wynmar are speaking quietly between themselves.","The Orcs have begun their attack on the Rohirrim's vulnerable encampment in Thinglad.","See if Wynmar and Noriel need your help","Orcs are attacking! You must defeat them.","Rothulf is at the camp.","Wynmar, Rothulf, and the other Rohirrim hunters now brace themselves against an onslaught.","Noriel is tending to Wynmar's wounds.","'Let us say our good-byes, dear friend....'","'They are coming any moment, ${PLAYER}. I can sense it... we must wake Wynmar from this foolish stupour, or he will surely die in this battle!'","Defeat the attacking Orcs","Help Rothulf rouse Wynmar from his woe","Too many have died...","Noriel has slain the attacker, but Wynmar lies wounded","Talk to Wynmar","See if Wynmar is ready to fight"},
[7294]={"What is going on?","You found two ruffians beating Sâdikiz as he lay on the floor. You should stop them and defeat the ruffians.","Derrota a los rufianes","Talk to Sâdikiz","TBD","Sâdikiz the Sky-hungry can be found at Khanâg Gur, and is said to be often found at the tavern there. You should go into the tavern to find him.","Is there a fight in the tavern? You should get closer to see what is going on.","Instancia: El marginado","The ruffians have fled","You have defeated the ruffians who were beating Sâdikiz as he lay helpless on the floor. You should talk to the relieved dwarf.","'To whom do I owe my thanks, stranger? You came in just in time!'\
\
You introduce yourself and tell him you are friends with Mêshaget, who wanted you two to meet.\
\
'Did he, now? In that case, I shall send him my thanks for my timely rescue also! Come, let us talk outside.'"},
[7296]={"Talk to Felgúr","'Listen, and I will speak of his arrival: Rûkhor… the Pale Herald.'","Instancia: El Heraldo Pálido","Listen to Felgúr's story","'Do you understand? The dark man cannot be trusted! He will lead the Ungoledain to death and dishonour.'","Felgúr has a tale to tell about a dark man who came to lead his people astray."},
[7297]={"'Debemos apresurarnos si queremos encontrar tu anillo, ${PLAYER}.'","Proteje a Saija","Busca a Narchuil","Habla con Saija","Saija ha prometido guiarte en tu búsqueda de Narchuil.","Saija ha muerto","Instancia: El Sendero de Aearil","Habla con Saija dentro de Halla-kolo.","Busca a Narchuil en Halla-kolo."},
[7298]={"'¡Me gusta esta joven hobbit! Es muy atenta, y me recuerda un poco a mí cuando tenía su edad.'\
\
Haley se pone intensamente roja.\
\
'Oh, lo siento mucho. Los hobbits envejecen de manera diferente a mi gente, ¿no es así? ¿Caléndula es realmente una niña? Aun así, lamento haber hablado tan a la ligera. ¡Pasar tanto tiempo cerca de Teodoro debe haberme vuelto descuidada como él! ¡Qué pensamiento tan aterrador!'","'${PLAYER}... No sabía adónde ir. Vagaba sin rumbo, sin saber por qué los Montaraces me habían perdonado la vida, o por qué Bingo me mostró bondad. Mis pasos sin guía me llevaron al norte, sin plan alguno, solo porque mis pies me llevaron allí. ¿Me llevarían a Angmar donde habitaba Avair, o a Forochel, morada de Gun Ain? ¿Dónde podría empezar de nuevo, como Clemencia?\
\
'En Galtrev encontré un pergamino flotando en el viento. Era una invitación a una cena, dirigida a un hombre al que nunca conocí, alguien llamado Hunfredo. Debió dejarla caer, y así llegó a mí. No sabía a dónde ir... pero no había olvidado la bondad de Bingo, y no la olvidaré. Quería decirle que le estaba agradecida, y así mi viaje hacia el norte encontró su destino.\
\
'En el camino me crucé con varios hombres, antiguos bandidos, que hablaban en voz alta de las hazañas de Bingo. Parece que serán granjeros. No sé si ese será mi destino, pero quizá pueda encontrar mi propio camino una vez que haya agradecido a Bingo su bondad.'","'¡Estoy listo para cenar, amigo mío! ¡Unámonos a los invitados y comamos hasta saciarnos!'","Habla con Bert Bartolín fuera del agujero hobbit de Bingo","Instancia: La receta perfecta","'Esta es una mesa muy bonita. No veo ni una sola marca en ella. Y, sin embargo, sabiendo cómo bailaba Bingo sobre las mesas del Poney Pisador, ¡debe haber practicado en algún lugar!'","Ha llegado el día de la fiesta de Bingo... ¿vendrán los invitados?","'Esta muchacha no ha dejado de bailar desde que llegó. Parece encantada... aunque admito que no entiendo por qué.'","Habla con el recién llegado","Caléndula y Spalvi escuchan embelesados las aventuras de Haley","'¡Bingo ha reunido una colección de libros bastante impresionante! Me impresiona su dedicación académica, y me pregunto qué les falta a las grandes colecciones de mi pueblo por no incluir literatura hobbit.\
\
'¡Fue muy amable de parte de Bilbo Bolsón darme su invitación cuando visité Imladris!'","¡Más invitados están llegando a la fiesta de Bingo!","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Sé que no recibí una invitación para la fiesta de Bingo... no, ¡no te preocupes! No le guardo rencor, ni tampoco lo esperaba. Hablé con él solo brevemente hace mucho tiempo, y entonces me reclamaban otros deberes.\
\
'Hace poco estuve en Rivendel a petición de la Dama Galadriel, y allí hablé con un personaje muy interesante. Bilbo es su nombre, y parece estar muy ansioso por leer el libro de Bingo. Me contó sobre esta fiesta y que, lamentablemente, no podría asistir. Yo le dije que vendría en su nombre y que le informaría del progreso del libro.\
\
'Con ese fin he preparado una gran cantidad de tinta y la he traído como regalo para Bingo. ¡Que su pluma nunca se quede sin tinta!'","'¿Es fiable este mapa? Hay realmente muchos pueblos en la Comarca. Respeto sus madrigueras, y un agujero hobbit parece un lugar muy ordenado para vivir, pero no me vendrían mal unas cuantas cámaras grandes y resonantes. ¡Y ni un gran salón a la vista!\
\
Ketill suspira.\
\
'¿Cómo viven así los hobbits, ${PLAYER}?'","Recibe a las nuevas llegadas","Bingo está recordando aventuras con Egwylf y Langhár","Teodoro y Bert intentan superar las historias del otro, ¡pero los hobbits solo quieren comer!","Entra en la casa de Bingo para la fiesta","La familia de Willem recibe mucha atención por parte de los jóvenes hobbits","¡En poco tiempo, la fiesta está en pleno desarrollo!","Bert Bartolín ha llegado fuera del agujero hobbit de Bingo, ¡y está listo para comenzar el banquete!","'Mi hermana está muy interesada en ese tal Merrimac. ¡No creo que él esté tan contento al respecto como ella!'","Myrtle Cenagales encabeza un pequeño grupo de vecinos de Bingo en el sendero fuera de su agujero hobbit.","¡La fiesta está en pleno apogeo!","'Esta ha sido toda una aventura, ${PLAYER}. No sé qué haremos Haley y yo a partir de ahora, pero no dudo que será una experiencia llena de peligro y emoción.\
\
'No se lo digas, pero creo que sin ella a mi lado podría haberme metido en problemas una o dos veces durante esta aventura. Nada que no pudiera resolver por mí mismo, ¡por supuesto! Tú también ayudaste, de vez en cuando, una o dos veces. Lo que intento decir es que incluso un aventurero experimentado como Teodoro Gorse necesita amigos de vez en cuando.'\
\
Teodoro tose con vergüenza, y su habitual fanfarronería vuelve.\
\
'¡Bien! ¡Suficiente de palabras empalagosas! ¡Mi pasado es magnífico! ¡Mi presente es satisfactorio! ¡Desafío al futuro a decepcionarme!'","'¡No esperaba que viniera tanta gente a mi fiesta! ¡Seguro que no envié tantas invitaciones!\
\
'¡Hasta Willem ha venido... y trajo a su compañera y a todos sus cachorros! Los hijos de Prisca parecen encantados con ellos... ¡tendré que recordarle a Willem que cuente bien a sus pequeños cuando llegue el momento de que mis amigos lince regresen a casa!'","'Es agradable sentarse un momento. Todos mis hijos están ocupados por ahora, ¡y puedo tener un rato para mí!\
\
'Debo decirle al primo Bingo que organice estas fiestas más a menudo!'","'¿No se supone que esta es una cena? ¿Por qué tarda tanto en aparecer la comida?\
\
'¡El gruñido de mi estómago ahogará todas las conversaciones si no comemos pronto!'","Recibe a los vecinos de Bingo fuera de su agujero hobbit","Donnamira Tuk examina el manuscrito de Bingo para ver si sería adecuado para su biblioteca","'¡Ooooh, mira qué adorables son! ¡Y su pelaje parece tan suave! ¡Los amo a todos!'","'Debo preguntarle a Teodoro dónde consiguió su sombrero. ¡Quiero añadirlo a mi colección!'","Bingo está cerca de la cocina de su agujero hobbit. Ahora que ya has conversado con algunos invitados, deberías ver cómo está disfrutando tu anfitrión de su fiesta.","Los vecinos de Bingo y los visitantes de Maur Tulhau intentan encontrar puntos en común","'¡No he podido meter ni una palabra! No recuerdo haber aceptado dejar la Comarca, ¡pero Violed parece convencida de que sí lo hice!\
\
'¿En qué lío me ha metido esta fiesta, ${PLAYER}?'","'Ya casi es hora de cenar, ${PLAYER}, pero aún hay un pequeño asunto al que me gustaría atender. No tomará mucho tiempo.\
\
'¿Tienes un momento?'","'Bueno, supongo que sería grosero no asistir a la fiesta de Bingo, así que aquí estamos, ${PLAYER}. ¿Crees que habrá olvidado aquel asunto de la petición que comencé antes de que se marchara en su aventura? Te agradecería que no se lo recordaras.'","'Hay muchas criaturas feroces en los bosques de los Valles Sombríos, pero siendo primos lejanos debéis poseer las mismas habilidades que nosotros. ¡Podrás evitar que te noten, Merrimac, y venir a visitarnos sin problemas!\
\
'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! Les estaba diciendo a estos buenos amigos que deberían venir a visitarnos a Maur Tulhau y disfrutar de un tradicional Festín de Bienvenida, ¡como hizo Bingo!\
\
'Y si comen tanto como lo hizo él, también deberán disfrutar de la tradicional semana de recuperación después de un festín así, ¡pero encontraríamos un lugar para ellos! ¡Espero que vengan a visitarnos!'","Habla con Myrtle en el sendero fuera del agujero hobbit de Bingo","Myrtle Cenagales está fuera del agujero hobbit de Bingo. ¿Viene también a la fiesta?","La casa de Bingo está llena de muchos de los amigos que hizo durante su viaje, y deberías socializar con los invitados antes de que suene la campana para la cena.","'¡Ah, recuerdo fiestas tan buenas como esta! Ha pasado tanto tiempo, y aún más que la muerte, pues en Audaghaim no había ocasión para festejos. Pero cuando era apenas una niña, de ocho o nueve años, recuerdo la emoción de reunirme con amigos.\
\
'¿Cómo llegué aquí? Pues he sentido una extraña afinidad por esa herradura que llevas contigo. Quizá una pequeña parte de su metal vino alguna vez de Audaghaim, hace mucho tiempo, y se mezcló con otros metales con los años. No puedo asegurarlo... pero al estar ligada al lugar de mi maldición, esa explicación es tan buena como cualquier otra que pueda imaginar.\
\
'Me alegra ver una reunión tan alegre una vez más, aunque no la merezca. ¡Aun así, gracias por traerme aquí, aunque fuera sin saberlo!'","Habla con Bingo en su casa","'¡Haley es increíble y extraordinaria, especialmente para ser una de la Gente Grande! Me está contando todas sus aventuras. ¿De verdad descendió a la guarida de un DRAGÓN... y logró salir de allí, DESPUÉS de despertarlo?\
\
'¿Tú estabas allí también, ${PLAYER}? ¡Vaya! ¡Necesito encontrar un dragón al que vencer yo también!'","Siguen llegando invitados a la fiesta de Bingo, pero no hay garantía de que todos se lleven bien.","'Realmente vivimos una buena aventura, ¿no es así, ${PLAYER}? Espero que le recuerdes a Bingo nuestra participación para que no deje fuera nuestra contribución en su relato. Él pasó buena parte de mi parte empapado y sin saber quién era, así que quizás no tenga mucho que decir.\
\
'Pensándolo bien... quizá no deberías recordarle mi contribución, ${PLAYER}. Puede que no todos los enanos debamos ser mencionados en los libros.'","'Me entristece decir que ninguno de mis hermanos podrá venir a la fiesta hoy, ${PLAYER}. Todos tienen obligaciones en otras tierras, pero prometí que el viejo Rattlepacks y yo representaríamos a la familia Bartolín lo mejor posible.\
\
'Ahora bien, ¿dónde está nuestro anfitrión? ¡Estoy listo para servirme uno o dos platos de sabrosas viandas! ¡Entremos!'","'Cuando tú y Bingo vinisteis a visitarme a Newbury, me visteis en mi peor momento, ${PLAYER}. ¡Pero tras un año de cortejo, Celandine Brandigamo por fin aceptó asistir a una reunión social conmigo! ¡Solo necesitaba una fiesta para venir con ella!\
\
'Y cuando mi madre dijo que Bingo, mi primo segundo, estaba organizando una cena... bueno, ¡me pareció una oportunidad providencial!\
\
'¡Pero ay! ¡Se ha pasado todo el tiempo encariñándose con estos cachorros de lince y no me ha dedicado ni un momento! ¡Cruel destino!'","'El manuscrito de Bingo es muy bueno hasta ahora, ${PLAYER}, pero me gustaría que mostrara un poco más de destreza con la ortografía y la gramática. ¡Este libro necesitará algo de refinamiento antes de que me sienta cómodo colocándolo en una estantería de biblioteca!'","¡Socializa!","Siguen llegando más invitados a la fiesta de Bingo, y deberías recibirlos para que se sientan bienvenidos.","Recibe a los invitados de la fiesta de Bingo a medida que llegan","La expresión recelosa de Myrtle sería más adecuada para una batalla que para una fiesta"},
[7300]={"Examine the indistinct figures","'I should have known, ${PLAYER}. I should have read the signs.'","Gandalf flips through the pages of the Black Book","Vóin writes of his adventures in the Grey Mountains, where he encountered Magoldir the Elf and the two became fast friends.","Listen to the words of Gandalf concerning his discoveries","Gandalf is in the Grey Mountains as they are depicted by the Halls of Memory.","Two thousand years following his survival of the Siege of Barad-dûr, Magoldir adventured in the Grey Mountains... but he did not travel alone.","Gandalf speaks to you of the discoveries he made while studying the Black Book.","Move through the twisting passage until you reach the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","'From my earlier study of the Black Book, we learned of Vóin's encounter with Magoldir the Elf in the Grey Mountains and their subsequent friendship. Unremarkable, perhaps, and yet we marked it, for an air of mystery surrounds this tome; both the circumstances in which it was found and the writing between its black covers fill me with intrigue and unease in equal measure.\
\
'From the shade of Isildur we learned somewhat of Magoldir the Elf, and few of his deeds seemed notable. It is no slight to him, merely the truth that his most significant achievement appears to be his survival; nearly two thousand years passed before his name surfaced anywhere, and that in the Black Book.\
\
'What, then, of Magoldir's inclusion? Why did Vóin see fit to write of this Elf?'","'What has Vóin to say about this meeting? Listen well, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Gandalf in the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Habla con Gandalf","Gandalf has made a worrisome discovery while continuing his study of the Black Book of Mordor.","Examine the indistinct figure that remains","Instancia: El cuadro pintado"},
[7301]={"Enter the combat area","'Err, great work defeating all those filthy snaga! Thought you wouldn't make it there, yes.\
\
'Looks like they know you're ${RACE} now, yes. No more fooling them.'","Now that you have been entered in the pit-fighting tournament, you should show these Orcs what is what.","Defeat the first opponent","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the combat area!</rgb>","The first opponent enters the arena!","Defeat the second opponent.","Defeat the first opponent.","Enter the combat area.","Defeat the third opponent.","You have defeated Dhárpush the Foul!","Hear Gumog's words.","You have defeated Búkra the Scratcher!","Talk to Párgrub","Defeat the third opponent","Instancia: El luchador de foso -- Día uno","'Err, let us go and train for tomorrow, yes.'","The Uruk, Gumog, starts to bellow to the crowd","You forfeit the challenge!","Defeat the second opponent","Talk to Párgrub.","You have defeated Gúgru the Gangly!","Hear Gumog's words"},
[7302]={"Enter the combat area","Now that you have been entered in the pit-fighting tournament, you should show these Orcs what is what.","Defeat the first opponent","'Oh no, this can't be. You must've cheated, yes. Err, Párgrub is ruined.'","You have defeated Mozrúf Blade-storm!","'We should leave before more Orcs attack you, and poor snaga.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the combat area!</rgb>","Defeat the second opponent.","Defeat the first opponent.","Enter the combat area.","Instancia: El luchador de foso -- Día tres","You have defeated Núghorg the Scar-webbed","Defeat the third opponent.","Hear Gumog's words.","Defeat the previous tournament's victor","You have defeated Gorzum the Finisher!","Fight off the hoards of Orcs!","Defeat the previous tournament's victor.","Talk to Párgrub","The previous tournament's victor enters the arena!","Defeat the third opponent","Fend off the hordes of Orcs!","You forfeit the challenge!","Defeat the second opponent","Talk to Párgrub.","You have defeated Úrzot the Ravenous!","Gumog bellows to the crowd","Hear Gumog's words"},
[7303]={"Enter the combat area","Now that you have been entered in the pit-fighting tournament, you should show these Orcs what is what.","Defeat the first opponent","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the combat area!</rgb>","Defeat the second opponent.","Defeat the first opponent.","Enter the combat area.","Defeat the third opponent.","You have defeated Ghárnakh Steelfist!","You have defeated Khûr the Ripper Twin!","You have defeated Maushak the Marrow-drinker!","Instancia: El luchador de foso -- Día dos","Talk to Párgrub","Defeat the third opponent","'Come, let's go and rest for the next fight. Párgrub has to, err, plan for things.'","The Uruk, Gumog, starts to bellow to the crowd","You forfeit the challenge!","Defeat the second opponent","You have defeated Karg the Ripper Twin!","Talk to Párgrub.","'Gah, you won! Err, good work, yes. You fight well and make Párgrub, err, a name around other snaga.'"},
[7304]={"The leaders of the rebellion have gathered in Ahâba to plan their attack.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","Defeat the attacking Ordâkhai","Instancia: El plan de ataque","Ahâba is under attack!","Listen to the conversation","Travelling in these lands, I have made bonds with many whose stories are like mine. The tyranny and depravity of Ordâkh has armed us with a common resentment. As rebellion gathers at my back and allies join my table, we plan to besiege Emax Dûl.","The Ordâkhai retreat!","Talk to Mizâdi","The leaders of the rebellion have gathered in Ahâba.\
\
You should talk to Mizâdi to begin the meeting.","'Good, you are here right on time. Our meeting can now proceed.\
\
'Despite our growing numbers, this will still be a difficult battle. Let us hear how everyone thinks we should proceed.'","Someone approaches in the darkness.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","Ahâba is under attack!\
\
You should defeat the attacking Ordâkhai!","'Please, hear my words. I wish only to save my family.'"},
[7305]={"In desperation, you slip the Ring on your finger!","Consider the thoughts of Galadriel","You have managed to remove the Ring, narrowly avoiding the wrath of Sauron.\
\
Gandalf is brought once again to mind, and as you stand among the ruins atop Amon Hen you ponder your course.","You manage to remove the Ring. Now you know what you must do.","Walk north-west of Parth Galen so you may be alone with your thoughts","Sauron has sensed the Ring! Even now he looks for you!","Thoughts of Bilbo have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.","The terror of your recent experience is still with you, but you conjure the kindly face of Gandalf from your memories to try and fight back the dread. You can almost hear his voice, as clearly as when he spoke to you thusly in the library at Rivendell.\
\
'There are a great many dangers facing Middle-earth, Frodo, and your Ring is responsible, even indirectly, for all of them. The Orcs of the Misty Mountains stir, and Lórien is threatened with fire. The horsemen of Rohan fight back the wolves of Isengard. Corsairs put to sea from Harad and endless armies march from the east. The Mountain of Fire is aflame, and the Dark Lord's forces are in motion.\
\
'There are men who stand against him, men like Boromir, son of the Steward of Gondor and your companion. He and the men like him will fight, for as long as they are able, but when all is finished it seems to me they will be simply men, and for how long can men stand against such evil?\
\
'No, Frodo, I fear that when all is reckoned, it will come down to one hobbit, after all, and the strength he himself can bring to bear. Perhaps that is always the way it was meant to be.'","'You need time to decide? I understand. It is no easy decision. None of these have been easy decisions! If only Gandalf were here....\
\
'I have tried to play his part as best I can, but I am not he and the ways of Wisdom are shut to me. I am sorry I cannot help you with this decision, Frodo, but it is yours to make and I do not want to sway your mind one way or the other.'","'Few know the inner strength of hobbits as I do, Frodo Baggins. Many, even among the Wise, would think this task too much for you. But I have seen the bravery of a Baggins when put to the test, and I know you will do what you must.'\
\
The memory of Gandalf's warm smile fills you with a deep regret.\
\
'Yes, there is sadness on any difficult road. You must prepare for more if you are to face what must lie ahead.'","'Oh, Frodo, my lad. What have we gotten ourselves into? Trouble and bother!'\
\
Your memory of the old hobbit makes you smile in spite of yourself, and you realize how badly you miss him.\
\
'Something has to be done, Frodo. All these important people with their endless meetings and councils, weighing important matters, when all it needs is the application of some good hobbit-sense.'","Walk further west so you may be alone in your thoughts","Sauron can sense the presence of the Ring! He searches for you!","The words of Gandalf are foremost in your thoughts.","You feel a presence behind you","Consider thoughts of Gandalf in the ruins atop Amon Hen","'Some rings there are that Sauron never touched, and they were not used for Evil. They were used for growth and prosperity, and much beauty was wrought with these. The Three Elven Rings belong to this worthwhile group.'\
\
You remember the look of sadness on Galadriel's beautiful face when she spoke of this in Lothlórien.\
\
'If you fail in your quest, Frodo Baggins, the workings of the Three will be laid bare before Sauron, and he will control all. But if you should succeed, even then there will be little happiness for Elves. We will diminish, and all that was wrought with the Three shall fade.'","Talk to Boromir on Amon Hen","Aragorn and the rest of the Fellowship are camped on Parth Galen, in the East Wall.\
\
The time has come to decide which of the Company will go with Boromir to Minas Tirith, and which will go to Mordor, if any do.","A madness has taken Boromir!","A madness has taken Boromir! With the Ring on he cannot find you to harm you! Climb to the summit of Amon Hen to escape!","You have asked to be alone with your thoughts while you decide what must be done.\
\
Perhaps a short walk will help, as long as you do not stray out of call of the Fellowship.","The words of Galadriel are foremost in your thoughts.","Boromir has followed you part of the way up Amon Hen, and is waiting to speak to you.","'How can you say that? You have the very thing we need to defeat the Dark Lord, but you refuse to use it! You run knowingly to your death, and you bring with you the only hope we ever had of surviving this war!\
\
'The Ring should be mine! Give it to me! Give it to me, you foolish halfling! You have no right to it!\
\
'If you will not give it to me, I will take it! I will take it by force!'","Climb the stairs to the south-east so you may be alone in your thoughts","'Well, Frodo, the choice is upon us at last. In Rivendell you were appointed the bearer of a great Burden, and this Company has escorted you through the wilderness, beneath the mountains, and along the Great River. All of us have done so in friendship and with an understanding of the errand's great need.\
\
'But now the path splits. Boromir has said from the beginning that his road leads to Minas Tirith and the war against the Shadow that must surely be coming. But that way is not the way to the Fire, and it is to the Fire that your burden must be carried.\
\
'What is the fate of this Company? Do we go to Boromir's city, to Minas Tirith? Or do we cross the river and make for the Land of Shadow?'","'It will not be easy, Frodo, my boy, but it would be for the best. As long as our friends accompany you, their lives are in danger. You don't want that!\
\
'Best to go alone to Mordor. Aragorn and Boromir are strong Men, and they will take care of our friends. Gimli and Legolas will watch out for them as well. Sam will not understand, but in time he may forgive you.\
\
'What did Elrond say in Rivendell? That it was perilous to study the arts of the Enemy, as Saruman did? That must be because they can corrupt even the purest of hearts, no matter its intention at the outset.'","Instancia: El punto de decisión","Consider thoughts of Bilbo","Thoughts of Galadriel have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.","Consider the thoughts of Gandalf","Talk to Aragorn on Parth Galen","Thoughts of Elrond have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.","'Yes! You hear the wisdom in it! I am glad, Frodo. I had feared you would not wish to speak to me, but it lightens my heart to know that you respect the wisdom of Gondor.\
\
'For Gondor is where the greatest strength of Men can be found, and it is where the Dark Lord's gaze is most drawn!'","Thoughts of Galadriel rise unbidden in your mind","'No? Why do you resist the course of wisdom? These Elves and Wizards speak only of hiding, and sneaking, and they would have us destroy the very thing we need to defeat Sauron!\
\
'Why do you listen to them, and not to me? It is my people who will pay the price for the failure of this foolhardy errand! My people will pay, not yours, hiding far away in some hidden dell where the Enemy will never find them, if he even thinks to look!\
\
'But he looks at Gondor, yes he does, and he will kill its people, and they will look to me and ask why I was not able to protect them! And I will say I had this chance, and I let it slip away!'","Consider the thoughts of Elrond","Thoughts of Gandalf have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.","'I know you said you wanted to be alone, Frodo, but you are simply too important to go wandering alone. If Aragorn is correct in his guess, it means the Orcs have already crossed the river. They could be in the woods even now.'","Thoughts of Elrond rise unbidden in your mind","The Fellowship of the Ring has come at last to the ultimate decision: the East road or the West?","The words of Elrond are foremost in your thoughts.","'The Ring you bear is the One, the Ruling Ring sought by Sauron above all else. The evil he could work with it would be incurable.\
\
'It must be destroyed.'","Thoughts of Gandalf rise unbidden in your mind"},
[7306]={"You must be close now!\
\
You should help Arvedui reveal the hidden door!\
\
Say the password 'Dolen uin Belegoth' aloud to reveal the door.","Arvedui and Lothrandir are having a conversation outside Sûri-kylä.\
\
You should talk to Lothrandir when they are finished.","Talk to Lothrandir","Arvedui and Lothrandir are talking.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","Speak to Arvedui to travel to Jä-reitti","Frost grims block your path deeper into the ice caves.\
\
You should defeat the frost grims.","Instancia: El poder de los juramentos","Defeated the frost grims","With the key of Agoroth in hand, the time has come to find the door to the hidden fortress, deep within the caves of ice.","Listen to the conversation","Say the password to reveal the door","'I will lead us to Agoroth.'","'The way is open. When you are ready, we shall enter.'","Arvedui is ready to show you the way to Agoroth.\
\
Talk to Arvedui to travel to Jä-reitti.","The door to Agoroth has been revealed!","Arvedui and Lothrandir are conversing outside Sûri-kylä.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","'I have been telling Arvedui of his heir, Aragorn, and his desire to reunite the kingdoms. Hearing such things seems to have lifted his spirits! I believe he blames himself for his death ending the line of Kings. Perhaps we are making progress on two fronts, ${PLAYER}! Did you acquire the key from the Lossoth?'\
\
You tell Lothrandir and Arvedui that you acquired the key but promised to destroy the Oath-stone that the Lossoth believe is inside Agoroth. Lothrandir looks at you curiously.\
\
'Quite a promise to exchange for something so valuable, ${PLAYER}! I truly hope we are able to keep it.'","Derrota a los macabras de escarcha"},
[7307]={"'I want you... to know...'\
\
Théodred coughs weakly. He is clearly near the end of his strength.\
\
'My father... cannot stand... alone...'\
\
He closes his eyes for a moment, but keeps speaking.\
\
'My father... the King...'","Grimbold is on the eyot in the middle of the Isen, with Théodred.","Théodred does not have much time left. He wants to speak to you.","Instancia: El Príncipe de Rohan, Noche","Prince Théodred is dead. Grimbold wants to speak with you.","Elfhelm wishes to speak with you now that the battle has been won.","'I am ready for this day to be done, ${PLAYER}. I know it is the same with you.'","'You are ${PLAYER}? Grimbold spoke to me of you. He says you fought bravely today.'\
\
Elfhelm looks across the waters of the Isen into the distance.\
\
'Many men fought bravely today. For many a man this was his last battle.'","'Prince Théodred is dead. We will bury him here, as was his wish, alongside his men. They will not return to Rohan, but will keep the Ford alongside their Prince until the end of all days.'","Talk to Elfhelm","The unthinkable has happened: Théodred, the Prince of Rohan, has sustained a mortal wound and lies dying at the Ford of Isen.","Talk to Grimbold","Talk to Théodred","'Prince Théodred's wounds are grievous, ${PLAYER}. He does not have much time left. I have given him a bedroll and tried to make him as comfortable as I can, but....'\
\
He shakes his head, a haunted look in his eyes.\
\
'I am a veteran of many wars, ${PLAYER}, and have seen death in all its forms, but to see Théoden King's heir like this...more than my Prince will die tonight. I fear Rohan dies with him.'"},
[7308]={"'¿En qué estará pensando nuestra Maestra? ¿Por qué asignar a los Tarkrîp a esta torre en lugar de a una de las tribus más formidables? Seguro que tiene algún plan.\
\
'No logro entender cuál. Quizá, después de matar a estos prisioneros, dedique un tiempo a reflexionar sobre los designios de nuestra Maestra.'","'¡No permitiré que los Tarkrîp pasen este tiempo dormidos! ¡Despiértalos a todos, y también a ese Gorthorog inútil!'","'Con un poco de suerte, Lozudurkh no regresará de su puesto.'","Despierta a los guardias dormidos en Sammath Baul (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Laerdan se encuentra en estado de sometimiento en la cámara del piso superior de Sammath Baul.\
\
Morven te ordenó que lo regreses a su celda.","'Desde que fue asignado aquí, Lozudurkh no ha hecho más que dormir, el necio. Su fracaso en Annúminas es bien conocido.\
\
'Yo mismo lo destriparía, pero parece que la Maestra tiene algo previsto para él. ¿Por qué si no lo habría nombrado Maestro de las Llaves de la torre, cuando tantos otros sirvientes lo merecen más?'","'Morven ha recibido carta blanca para hacer lo que quiera en Sammath Baul. Si ella lo permite, ¡estos Trév Gállorg no verán la luz del amanecer! Ya oigo sus gritos... hermoso.'","'¿Has limpiado la torre de sanguijuelas? Llegarás lejos, Sangrador. Tal vez hable de tu dedicación a nuestra Maestra cuando llegue.\
\
'¿Qué? ¿Todos los Tarkrîp están dormidos, y Lozudurkh también? Jamás cuestionaría a nuestra Maestra, pero no comprendo por qué enviaría a esos cobardes inútiles a custodiar Sammath Baul. ¿Acaso los sangradores bajo mi mando no bastan?\
\
'¡Despierta a todos los Tarkrîp dormidos y a ese Gorthorog inútil también! Si va a ser el Maestro de las Llaves, debería estar en su puesto, fuera de la torre. Usa tu bota si es necesario, Sangrador.'","Un estruendo ensordecedor retumba por la sala","Amarthiel está interrogando al elfo Laerdan en el piso superior de Sammath Baul.\
\
Se te ha concedido el gran honor de presenciar el interrogatorio de Amarthiel al elfo Laerdan.","Morven se encuentra en la cámara del piso superior de Sammath Baul.\
\
Amarthiel ha terminado su interrogatorio y ahora Morven desea hablar contigo.","Alimañas eliminadas de Sammath Baul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Morven se encuentra en el piso superior de la torre.\
\
Has despertado a todos los guardias dormidos y ahora deberías regresar junto a Morven.","Se pueden encontrar sanguijuelas de sangre por toda la torre de Sammath Baul.\
\
Morven te pidió que erradicaras las sanguijuelas que infestan la torre como preparación para la visita de Amarthiel.","Laerdan se encuentra en estado de sometimiento en la cámara del piso superior de Sammath Baul.\
\
Sammath Baul está siendo atacada por aliados de Laerdan, y Morven moviliza sus fuerzas para defender la torre.","'Es una pena que hayas tenido que destruir las sanguijuelas... pero volverán. Se reproducen en los cadáveres, ya lo sabes.'","'Estos Trév Gállorg llevan solo unos días en Sammath Baul y ya estoy cansado de sus lamentos. Quizá le pida a Morven permiso para matarlos.'","'Los Tarkrîp no valen nada. Sammath Baul estaba mejor protegida antes de su llegada. ¿Qué se le habrá pasado por la cabeza a la Maestra?'","'Tengo un encargo importante para ti, Sangrador; si lo cumples bien, quizá te permita elegir entre los tesoros de nuestros cautivos más recientes. Los Trév Gállorg son pobres, pero a veces fabrican objetos de gran valor, y podrías ganarte una bonita baratija.\
\
'He recibido noticias de que nuestra Maestra acudirá a Sammath Baul para interrogar al elfo Laerdan, y quiero que todo transcurra sin contratiempos durante su visita.\
\
'Los cadáveres de la torre han dado lugar a enormes sanguijuelas de sangre, y su suciedad y enfermedades han sido... una distracción... para el resto de mis servidores. Quiero que destruyas esas sanguijuelas antes de que llegue la Maestra.'","Elimina las alimañas de Sammath Baul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El elfo Laerdan ha sido aprisionado en Sammath Baul, donde permanece bajo la atenta vigilancia de la torturadora Morven y de sus sangradores angmarim.","Devuelve a Laerdan a su celda","Los orcos Tarkrîp y Lozudurkh el Gorthorog se encuentran dormidos por toda Sammath Baul.\
\
Morven te envió a despertar a Lozudurkh y a todos los Tarkrîp dormidos en la torre.","Espera a que Amarthiel termine su interrogatorio","'¡Nuestra Maestra ha llegado, Sangrador! Como has sido de tanta utilidad, te concedo este privilegio: presenciar su interrogatorio del elfo Laerdan. Algunos de tus hermanos también han recibido este gran honor, para que sean recompensados.'","Instancia: El Prisionero de Sammath Baul","'¿Te ocupas de las sanguijuelas? Qué lástima. Es un placer verlas alimentarse de los cadáveres.\
\
'Aun así, la palabra de Morven está solo un escalón por debajo de la de nuestra Maestra; haces bien en obedecer.'","Morven se encuentra en la cámara del piso superior de Sammath Baul.\
\
Has eliminado por ahora las sanguijuelas de Sammath Baul y deberías informar a Morven en el piso superior.","'¡Ese Gorthorog inútil! ¿Podrías preguntarle a Morven si puedo acabar con Lozudurkh? Su hedor atrae a las sanguijuelas.'","Morven se encuentra en la cámara del piso superior de Sammath Baul.\
\
Morven te espera para darte tus instrucciones.","'Los Tarkrîp necesitan aprender disciplina. Podríamos enseñársela tú y yo. Desangra a algunos y mata al resto. Los que queden serán más... vigilantes.'","'¡Has oído a nuestra Maestra! Los aliados del elfo llegarán pronto para liberarlo.\
\
'Regrésalo de inmediato a su celda, Sangrador. No daremos a sus amigos el placer de verlo con vida.'","Guardias dormidos despertados en Sammath Baul (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Si demoras un instante más, te haré ejecutar, Sangrador. ¿Disfrutarías que tus iguales te desangren y te arrojen a una celda a pudrirte en los últimos momentos de tu patética vida?\
\
'¿No? Entonces elimina de una vez las sanguijuelas de Sammath Baul, ¡y rápido! ¡Nuestra Maestra llegará pronto!'"},
[7309]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Huneric must survive</rgb>","Defeat the raiding party.","Instancia: La Partida de Saqueo","Huneric, Lord of the Thíuda, has noticed forces gathering at Mokh Darga and wishes to halt a raid before it begins.","Talk to Huneric","The raiding party has been defeated and no longer poses a threat to Adambel","<rgb=#FF0000>Huneric has fallen in battle!</rgb>","Talk to Huneric.","'You have fought well. Come, let us return to Adambel.'","'The raiding party prepares their assault! Now is the time to attack. Follow me into battle!'","Defeat the raiding party"},
[7310]={"Confront Athálrik","Instancia: El alcance de la justicia","Pursue Athálrik.","An anguished cry rises suddenly up ahead, followed by a laugh, then a growl","Defeat Athálrik.","You find the memory-cloth clutched in his hands.","'You will find him between here and the bluffs to the north-east that overlook the Long Lake. That is where he roams. I do not follow him, no. I leave him to himself and his moods.'","A man who must be Athálrik stands, holding something up before him","Pursue Athálrik","You have found Athálrik. Now confront him.","TBD","Find Athálrik","Follow the sounds eastward.","It is serene here among the pines, the wind brushing thoughtfully through the grass","You have tracked Athálrik to his retreat in the highlands west of Lake-town.","Athálrik falls, a look of malice, fervour, and disbelief twisting his face","You should look for Athálrik, eastward from Víthog.","Search Athálrik","You should search Athálrik for the Chayasír's memory-cloth.","Defeat Athálrik"},
[7311]={"Some of the enemies flee on horse","The last few Haradrim have escaped to Cair Andros","Talk to Elfhelm at the river crossing in Talath Anor.","Instancia: La Reclamación de Talath Anor","Defeat enemies alongside Elfhelm","Enter the destroyed farm","With renewed spirit, Éomer, king of Rohan, has decided to send Elfhelm to lead an attack against a band of Haradrim who has fled into Talath Anor.","Enter the destroyed farm.","Defeat enemies at the farm alongside Elfhelm and his men.","'${PLAYER}, I thank you for lending your hand in combat and for your invaluable knowledge of Talath Anor and the Haradrim. It has made this ride a success, as we no longer need worry about a Haradrim ambush near Minas Tirith. I am concerned about Cair Andros however. We should tell Éomer and Aragorn of what we have seen.'","'There is nothing more we can do. Most of the Haradrim forces gathered in Talath Anor are now defeated. Let us return to Aragorn's Pavilion.'","Talk to Elfhelm","Pursue the Haradrim.","Pursue the Haradrim","Elfhelm has fallen in battle!","<rgb=#FF0000>Elfhelm must survive</rgb>"},
[7312]={"Listen to Rhadrog's story","'We were tasked with keeping a watch on Seregost. Things had been mostly quiet for a while, though I was beginning to grow tired of the colour red!'","Instancia: El cielo rojo se oscurece","Rhadrog is telling you the tale of why he left Agarnaith with Faeron.\
\
You should talk to Rhadrog to begin.","Rhadrog is telling you the tale of why he left Agarnaith with Faeron.\
\
You should listen to Rhadrog's story.","'We then left Agarnaith and followed the merrevail to the Morgul Vale.'","Talk to Rhadrog","Rhadrog has a tale to tell about his departure from Agarnaith."},
[7313]={"Instancia: El Reeve del Valle del Entaguas","'Let us return to my men and set our trap.'","'So, ${PLAYER}, you have struck at the heart of the Orcs' encampment? Perhaps between us, we may break the siege, or at least weaken it enough to enable Reeve Ingbert to send a company of men to Harwick.\
\
'What say you? Will you help me lay a trap for the Orcs?\
\
'Good!'","'It is settled then. As we proved the Easterlings no match for the Riders of the Mark, so shall we teach the Orcs a lesson in fear!'","Speak with Burnoth.","Watch the discourse between Burnoth and Ingbert","Watch the discourse between Burnoth and Reeve Ingbert.","Talk to Burnoth","You have accompanied Burnoth as he comes before Ingbert, Reeve of the Entwash Vale."},
[7314]={"Ahora que has llegado al patio de Edhelion, sigue a Dorongúr Espinablanca hacia él.","Derrota a los invasores Duramano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instancia: El Refugio de Edhelion","Habla con tu maestro, Talagan Lenguadeplata","'¡, mi ${PLAYERNAME:querido[m]|querida[f]} estudiante! Ojalá pudiera dejarte a salvo dentro de estos muros, pero Elrond me dice que Skorgrím se dirige directamente a esta biblioteca.\
\
'Me temo que debes sobrevivir a la batalla en el exterior. ¡Me preocupa tu seguridad! ¡Duélate conmigo una última vez, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}, y muéstrame que estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}! ¡Eso aliviará mi corazón!'","Elrond el Medio Elfo necesita hablar contigo","Talagan Lenguadeplata te ha dicho que desea que te dirijas al patio de Edhelion y ayudes a defenderlo de nuevos ataques.","Habla con Talagan Lenguadeplata afuera de la biblioteca","Encuentra al Maestro Talagan afuera","'¡Ve, ${PLAYER}! Aquí es donde convergerá la tormenta. Edhelben está abajo — él te dejará pasar por la puerta para proteger lo que queda de este refugio.'","Habla con Elrond <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre Elrond para interactuar)</rgb>","<rgb=#00ff00>Has vencido a Talagan</rgb>","Tu amado maestro, Talagan Lenguadeplata, se ha sacrificado para asegurarse de que los artefactos de Edhelion no cayeran en manos de Skorgrím.\
\
Ahora debes hablar con Elrond sobre todo lo que ha sucedido.","Un gran estruendo ha sacudido la biblioteca. Habla con Elrond para saber qué debes hacer.","Sigue a Elrond y a Dorongúr Espinablanca","La alforja está en el suelo cerca de Elrond.\
\
Deberías revisar la alforja en busca de armas que puedas usar para protegerte mejor, pues una guerra se libra afuera.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre los objetos brillantes para interactuar con ellos. Para recoger el contenido de la alforja, haz clic en el botón marcado como 'Recoger todo', y los objetos aparecerán en tu inventario.)</rgb>","Sigue a Elrond y a Dorongúr Espinablanca hasta la entrada de las salas de Edhelion.\
\
Poco después de que entraste al patio de Edhelion, los Duramano derribaron la puerta. Skorgrím y un grupo de enanos corrieron hacia la entrada de las salas de Edhelion.","'Temo por Edhelion. ¿Cuánto más podremos resistir? Y he oído que Skorgrím ni siquiera se ha mostrado aún... lo que significa que lo peor está por venir.'","Elrond el Medio Elfo te llama para que vayas a hablar con él, pues una guerra se libra afuera.\
\
Habla con Elrond. <rgb=#00ff00>Haz clic derecho sobre los personajes para interactuar</rgb>","Mientras visitabas Edhelion con tu maestro, un Elfo llamado Talagan, el refugio montañoso fue atacado repentinamente por un enano violento y sediento de sangre llamado Skorgrím, rey de la familia Duramano.","'Bien, joven , estás ${PLAYERNAME:entero[m]|entera[f]}. No te preocupes por mí, estaré bien. Es solo una herida menor. Una vez que la haya vendado, me dirigiré al patio para ayudar en lo que pueda. Pero no me esperes: ve al patio ahora y ayuda en su defensa hasta que Elrond llegue.\
\
'Esta puerta está atrancada, por temor a que las otras no resistan, pero la entrada trasera podría estar abierta. Sube las escaleras hacia el oeste y sigue el camino hasta llegar a la puerta trasera. Una vez allí, Dorongúr te dejará entrar.\
\
'Ten cuidado, sin embargo: puede que aún queden algunos rezagados.'","Abre la alforja <rgb=#00FF00>(Haz clic derecho sobre la alforja para recoger lo que hay dentro)</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Los archivos que necesitas para continuar tus aventuras en la Tierra Media deberían terminar de descargarse en breve. ¡Gracias por tu paciencia!</rgb>","Habla con Elrond","Sigue a Dorongúr Espinablanca","Hay un arma en la alforja. Deberías recogerla y equiparla antes de intentar luchar.","Invasores Duramano vencidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sigue a Edhelben","'Bien — estás mejor ${PLAYERNAME:armado[m]|armada[f]}. Tu maestro Talagan desea verte antes de que te aventures en la refriega. ¡Pero apúrate! Este lugar no es seguro para ti.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>ACCEDER A TU INVENTARIO: Presiona 'i' para abrir tu inventario y ver el arma, o haz clic izquierdo en los íconos de las bolsas en la parte inferior de tu pantalla.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>EQUIPAR TU ARMA: Haz clic derecho sobre el arma en tu inventario para equiparla. Esto reemplazará el arma endeble que tienes equipada actualmente.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>CONSEJO: Deberías equipar tu mejor arma antes de intentar entrar en combate.</rgb>","Lucha hasta llegar al patio de Edhelion.","Habla con Dorongúr","'¡Esos Duramano estaban por todas partes! Honestamente, no creí que sobreviviríamos, pero Dorongúr tuvo el buen juicio de atrancar las puertas del patio. Con el patio como nuestro último reducto, pudimos hacer retroceder a los enanos Duramano.\
\
'Sin embargo, sé que si el patio cae, todo Edhelion podría caer con él. Debes ayudar en la defensa del patio. Sube las escaleras hacia el oeste y sigue el camino hasta llegar a la puerta trasera. Una vez allí, Dorongúr debería dejarte entrar.\
\
'Ten cuidado; puede que aún queden algunos invasores por los alrededores.'","Acércate a Elrond <rgb=#00FF00>(Avanza presionando W)</rgb>","'No puedes quedarte aquí por más tiempo, ${PLAYER}. Las fuerzas de Skorgrím están sobre nosotros, y temo que se dirigen directamente a esta biblioteca.\
\
'Busca los artefactos de Edhelion, aunque no sé qué podría querer un enano con ellos. Estos artefactos fueron codiciados en su día por un Señor Demacrado. Creo que el necio cree que puede volverse inmortal si los consigue.'","Tu maestro Talagan desea ver que estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para enfrentar la batalla más allá de las puertas de la biblioteca.\
\
Para comenzar a luchar contra Talagan, <rgb=#00ff00>haz clic derecho</rgb> sobre él para iniciar tu ataque estándar. Para usar tus <rgb=#ffff00>Habilidades, haz <rgb=#00ff00>clic izquierdo</rgb> en los <rgb=#ffff00>Botones de Acción</rgb> en tu <rgb=#ffff00>Barra de Acciones Rápidas</rgb> (ubicada en la parte inferior de la pantalla) o presiona la <rgb=#ffff00>Tecla Rápida</rgb> correspondiente.\
\
Derrota a Talagan para avanzar.","'Los que están en el patio necesitarán tu ayuda hasta que Elrond regrese. Las puertas principales están atrancadas, así que deberías viajar hacia el oeste y subir las escaleras. Desde allí, sigue hasta la entrada trasera. Con suerte, alguien te dejará entrar.\
\
'Ten cuidado... puede que aún queden algunos rezagados con los que debas enfrentarte.'","Ahora que has adquirido nuevas armas, deberías equiparlas.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>ABRIR TU INVENTARIO: Presiona 'i' para abrir tu inventario y ver el arma, o haz clic izquierdo en los íconos de bolsa en la parte inferior de tu pantalla.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>EQUIPAR TU ARMA: Haz clic derecho sobre el arma en tu inventario para equiparla. Esto reemplazará el arma endeble que tienes equipada actualmente.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>CONSEJO: Deberías equipar tu mejor arma antes de intentar entrar en combate.</rgb>","Sigue a Edhelben mientras te guía hacia el patio de Edhelion.\
\
Tu maestro Talagan Lenguadeplata te ha dicho que quiere que vayas al patio de Edhelion y ayudes a defenderlo de nuevos ataques.","'No hay tiempo que perder, ${PLAYER}. Sal con Talagan y ve qué puede hacerse para detener el avance de Skorgrím. Los Duramano no deben apoderarse de los artefactos del Señor Demacrado; he jurado mantenerlos a salvo.\
\
'Esconderé los artefactos, luego me uniré a Talagan para proteger la biblioteca. Cuídate, joven ${CLASS}.'","Habla con Dorongúr Espinablanca.","'Ay... ${PLAYER}... has perdido a tu amado maestro. Puedes culparme por su muerte — podría haberlo salvado, pero él me pidió que fuera contigo en su lugar. Talagan fue valiente al sacrificar su vida por la tuya.\
\
'Edhelion está ahora en ruinas... Talagan no fue el único Elfo que murió hoy. Skorgrím ya no nos molestará, y los artefactos están enterrados a salvo, pero ¡fue una batalla tan innecesaria!\
\
'Edhelion se desvanecerá...'"},
[7315]={"Find Hogawise within the prison-caves","Herestan and Hogawise are ready to fight the defenders at two rooms of cells within the prison-caves.","Halbarad and the sons of Elrond are further within the prison-caves.","'You will pay for your treachery, honourless ones! To battle, ${PLAYER}!'","'Another room of Rangers to free! Let us give them their freedom, ${PLAYER}.'","'We can do nothing more from here. We must lick our wounds, bury our dead, and wait for another time.\
\
'But I swear it: before this war is over, the Falcon-clan will taste our vengeance!'","'Release your prisoners or die, low ones! To battle!'","You have freed a room of captives","Habla con Halbarad","Talk to Lheu Brenin","'That was good work, ${PLAYER}, but I fear it was only a start. More of your friends are being held below.'","Lheu Brenin guards a bridge that leads deeper into the caves, but you cannot pass. Archers of the Falcon-clan make crossing impossible.","'Penrod thought to bring us before Lheu Brenin. He did not choose men strong enough for the task.\
\
'I am glad to see you, ${PLAYER}! Let us go to see Lheu Brenin now, and on our own terms!'","Théodred and some of his loyal men have come with you to the prison-caves behind Tûr Morva to try and rescue the Grey Company.","Return to Théodred in the prison-caves","'None of your friends have been imprisoned in this room of cells. Lheu Brenin must be keeping them further ahead, away from the entrance.\
\
'My men have gone on ahead. Join them at each room of cells and fight for the freedom of your friends! I will scout around for sign of our enemies.'","Talk to Théodred within the prison-caves","Find Herestan within the prison-caves","Théodred is in one of the tunnels of the prison-caves you passed through to reach the prisoners.","'You are full of surprises, ${PLAYER}. I did not think that you would cross my path again in this life. How is it that you came to escape the clutches of Saruman?'\
\
Lheu Brenin smiles mockingly at your silence.\
\
'You were a fool to return here. You may have freed some members of your company, but I have exacted my price from the Grey Company.'","Théodred is within one of the rooms of cells within the prison-caves.","Théodred is a short way ahead in the prison-caves.","Halbarad needs to speak with you.","'He is right, ${PLAYER}. We cannot raise a hand against him in this position. They are too many, and we are too few.\
\
'There may be another time, but this is not it.'","Talk to Théodred in the prison-caves","Find Halbarad and the sons of Elrond, deeper within the prison-caves","Instancia: El Rescate"},
[7316]={"Defeat Sárgrish","<rgb=#FF0000>Tolwin must survive</rgb>","Defeat Thaukbag","Talk to Duinhir","Defeat Ursajun","Talk to Dúneth","'I knew in my heart that I would see you again. I knew it was you when I saw the smoke of battle rising from off the island. We rushed over as quickly as we could muster. I wanted to be there on the day that Cair Andros once again belonged to Gondor. I want to help restore the home of my dearly departed husband, Gilgír.'","Defeat the four lieutenants of Cair Andros as you fight along side Tolwin, Dúneth, and Duinhir.","Walk together to the prow of Cair Andros.","'I see your friend Dúneth and the boy Tolwin. You have done much to improve their lives as they faced devastating hardship.\
\
'I, too, should thank you for lifting my own shadow. I was wholly overcome with sorrow for the loss of my sons. I could not see my hands held out before me. What folly! Instead of honouring their sacrifice, I tarnished my name and theirs.\
\
'I am not fool enough to think that Cair Andros will undo my mistakes. No, my friend, I shall need to take charge in the future. I shall make sure that those from Harad will pay for the crimes against Gondor and against my family.'","Tolwin has fallen in battle!","Defend your ground in hope that additional support arrives to aid in the fight.","Defeated Hurshála","With the Enemy alerted, the Faint-hearted are left with no choice but to retake the island with haste.","Talk to Tolwin","Instancia: La reconquista de Cair Andros","Defend your ground","Fight through Cair Andros with Duinhir and his men.","<rgb=#FF0000>Duinhir must survive</rgb>","'Come, there is much to do in securing this island.'","Dúneth has fallen in battle!","Defeated Sárgrish","Duinhir has fallen in battle!","Walk together to the prow of Cair Andros","Fight through Cair Andros with Duinhir and his men","'${PLAYER}! It is good to see you again! You kept your word, like you said you would. You vowed to help retake my home for my family. I have trained and waited for this day ever since you departed Crithost. Now, let us reclaim the rest of Cair Andros!'","Defeated Ursajun","<rgb=#FF0000>Dúneth must survive</rgb>","Talk to Duinhir.","Talk to Tolwin and Dúneth.","Defeated Thaukbag","Defeat Hurshála"},
[7317]={"Weaken the Balrog Thaurlach to allow Glorfindel to defeat it","Habla con Glorfindel","Defeated Pale-folk Defenders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota al troll","Search the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu for clues of Glorfindel's whereabouts.","Continue to look for clues of Glorfindel's whereabouts.","Continue following Glathlírel to seek clues of Glorfindel's whereabouts","'I felt the dark presence brooding nearby when first I entered this place, but the prize I sought was too important and I was not to be deterred. Still, I had hoped to slip away as quietly as I came, and instead I walked nearly into its opened maw!\
\
'Fortune smiled upon me, however, and you came upon us at just that moment. Not the mightiest warrior of Elves or Men would face a Balrog alone, willingly -- though I yet flatter myself I might have been its match.\
\
'We should not tarry here, I think. I have found what I came here seeking, though I must take some time in secluded peace to read it over and pierce its deeper meaning. I cannot pause overlong, however, for I am expected in the Court of Lothlórien. Ah, but I see you knew that.\
\
'Perhaps, then, you may do me a double service. First, return there forthwith and assure Galadriel and Celeborn I am on my way. Second, tell Galadriel that I wish to give the Gwedluith I entrusted to her to Arwen, as a betrothal gift. Indeed, I would have you bear the gift to her, ${PLAYER}.'","'Balrogs are not so easily slain. Though they may seem defeated, they may heal and even regain form with time. This lesson I have learned, painfully, in ages past.\
\
'Fortunately, I possess the art required to fully extinguish such a foe. Come and fight by my side. Together we will put a final end to this fell servant of Morgoth.'","Find a way past the locked gate.","Examine the clue","You have found a clue and should examine it.","Defeat the Darklings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","With the guidance of Glathlírel, search for Glorfindel in the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.","Follow Glathlírel to search for clues of Glorfindel's whereabouts","Glathlírel is ready to explore the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu once again, in search of Glorfindel.","Find a way past the locked gate","Defeated the troll","Fend off the attacking Pale-folk Defenders.","Follow the clue to Glorfindel.","Weaken the Balrog Thaurlach so Glorfindel can finish it once and for all.","'${PLAYER}, we must look for clues as to the whereabouts of Glorfindel.\
\
'We know not what lurks in the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu now, so prepare yourself.'","Hear what Glorfindel has to say.","Follow the clue to Glorfindel","'It is time to leave this place. I must seclude myself a little while and consider the prophecy of Gil-galad I have found. Then, as soon as I am able, I shall find my way to Caras Galadhon.'","Thaurlach has been defeated!","Defeat attacking Pale-folk Defenders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Glathlírel","Defeat the Darklings.","Stand by Glorfindel's side","Defeat the troll.","Stand by Glorfindel's side.","'I thought I knew all there was to know of the Balrog Thaurlach. How mistaken I was! I have much yet to learn.'","Instance: The Return","You should talk to Glorfindel, now that Thaurlach is defeated.","Defeated Darklings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7318]={"Zarhal Kôz can be found somewhere within Uya Hujûm.\
\
You have arrived in Uya Hujûm and should now battle through the encampment until you find Zarhal Kôz.","Zarhal Kôz can be found deep within Uya Hujûm.\
\
Zarhal Kôz has called forth his men and now attacks. You should defeat him.","Jarl Gurthilm and his company have travelled to the stronghold of Uya Hujûm to deal their vengeance upon Zarhal Kôz and the Khundolar.","Zarhal Kôz's men leap forth from the tent!","A great tent stands before you... and you can hear hasty chatter within!","Talk to Jarl Gurthilm","'The day is won, ${CLASS}. Let us begone from this place!'","Instancia: Las Riquezas de Rhûn","Defeat Zarhal Kôz and his men","Zarhal Kôz can be found deep within Uya Hujûm.\
\
You have discovered Zarhal Kôz's whereabouts and should now confront him with the Variags.","'Are you prepared, ${CLASS}?\
\
'The blades of my men have tasted much of the blood of the Khundolar, but our foe eludes us still. A coward to the last, I do not doubt!\
\
'We shall press onward into the mountainside... and soon there shall be nowhere left for him to hide!\
\
'Ready your arms and let us go.'","Jarl Gurthilm is standing with his men in Uya Hujûm.\
\
You have come with the Variags to Uya Hujûm and should now speak to Jarl Gurthilm.","Confront Zarhal Kôz","Fight your way through Uya Hujûm and find Zarhal Kôz","Zarhal Kôz lies slain amidst his wealth of gold and treasures!"},
[7319]={"The battle is joined!","Mount your steed and talk to Éomer","Ride for battle!","Listen to Théoden address the Rohirrim","'The men have passed ahead, through the gap in the wall. Let us join the line, and prepare for the glorious battle to come!'","Éomer is ready to join the line of horsemen, and he wants you to follow him.","Théoden, King of Rohan, prepares to address his people.","Instancia: La cabalgata de los Rohirrim","Join Éomer in the line","The Rohirrim have passed through the gap in the Rammas, and prepare to ride for the besieged city.","The Rohirrim have formed a line just south of the Rammas, preparing to ride for the city."},
[7320]={"You have defeated the Nazgul. The battle is won for now.","Chase the Nazgul","TBD - Talk to Rohirrim Captain","Speak to the TBD Rohirrim Rider","TBD: OMG it's coming right for us!","Ride with the Rohirrim!","TBD","'TBD - Great job! We won, yes?'","TBD Chase the Nazgul","Kill the Nazgul","Instance: The Rider's Retreat","TBD - Kill the Nazgul","TBD - Talk to Rohiriim Dude again","'TBD - Let's go get that Black Rider!  He needs to be stopped!'","The Rohirrim Captain has fallen!","Don't let Rohirrim Captain die!"},
[7321]={"Burnoth invited you to speak with him and his companions to learn more about the Riders Four and their mission in the Eastemnet.","Léofdag eyes you warily.\
\
'Few care to know my tale, for it is one of shame. But if know it you must....'","Ulf stares at you darkly, as though uncertain whether to speak or fight.\
\
'My past is my own, stranger, but for Burnoth's sake, I will speak a little of it....'","Talk to Burnoth, son of Baldeg","Talk to Ulf the Reaver","Burnoth is at the refugee camp outside Harwick.\
\
You should return to Burnoth and let him know that you have spoken with his companions.","'Return to me later, and we will speak more.'","Talk to Léofdag, son of Winedag","Talk to Hutha, son of Hengest","Burnoth is near the camp-fire of the Riders Four in the refugee camp outside Harwick.\
\
You should speak with Burnoth to learn his story.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. My road has not been an easy one....'","Talk to Burnoth","Instance: The Riders Four","The young archer eyes you a little suspiciously.\
\
'You wish to speak with me? Ah, Burnoth sent you. So be it....'","'There is much more to tell, but not enough time for it. Perhaps at another time, we may speak more freely?'"},
[7322]={"'Es tradición que el Clucath se celebre en Fail-a-Khro. Allí, en la cima de esa colina y a la vista del Cairn de Honor, se han llevado a cabo innumerables ritos a lo largo de los largos años de Angmar.\
\
'Después de que los Trév Duvárdain tomaran la Piedra del Clucath del Cairn de Honor, era nuestro deber responder a su desafío, y así lo hicimos. Crannog nos llamó, sus guerreros más poderosos, para acompañarlo a Fail-a-Khro.\
\
'Con nuestras hojas afiladas y nuestras provisiones para el viaje preparadas, partimos desde Aughaire.'","Con el regreso de la Corona de Hierro y sus leales entre los Trév Duvárdain, ahora divididos, a Carn Dûm, se rompió una paz frágil y los antiguos enemigos de los Trév Gállorg buscaron un nuevo dominio sobre Angmar.","Nekhtan ha ofrecido relatar la historia del rito de Clúcath.\
\
Debes hablar con Nekhtan.","'Si tan solo eso fuera el final de la historia...'","'Después de que Clucath terminó, no tuvimos más opción que regresar a Aughaire. ¿Qué más podíamos hacer?\
\
'Pocos hablaron durante el viaje de regreso, y creo que todos temíamos lo que podría sucedernos en los días siguientes.\
\
'Pero no pasó nada. Quizás nos habíamos equivocado, pensé.'","Escucha el relato de Nekhtan sobre el rito del Clucath","Instancia: El rito deshecho","Nekhtan ha concluido la historia del rito de Clúcath.\
\
Debes hablar con Nekhtan.","Habla con Nekhtan","Nekhtan está relatando los eventos del rito del Clucath entre los Trév Gállorg y los Trév Duvárdain."},
[7323]={"Crannog está esperando para caminar contigo al sitio donde se realizará el Clúcath.","Derrota a los guerreros de los Trév Duvárdain","'¡Déjame en paz! ¡No necesito tu simpatía! ¡Maldigo a los Trév Gállorg, y a ti más que a nadie, tonto ${RACE}!'","'Mi corazón está tranquilo, ${PLAYER}. Mi padre ha sido vengado y he defendido los principios de los Trév Gállorg y de Clúcath. Te debo mucho.'","Observa cómo se desarrolla el Clúcath","'Luchaste bien y con valentía, ${PLAYER}. Fue un honor estar a tu lado.'","Has salido victorioso en el rito de Clúcath","'¡Los Trév Gállorg han triunfado, ${PLAYER}! Has traído la victoria a Fail-á-Khro, donde el dolor ha reinado demasiado tiempo.\
\
'Habla conmigo cuando estés listo para volver a Aughaire, y nos iremos.'","Instancia: El Rito de Clúcath","Habla con Crannog","El Clúcath está a punto de comenzar: Crannog de los Trév Gállorg y Domongart de los Trév Duvárdain están cara a cara.","Crannog está en Fail-á-Khro, esperando para felicitarte por tu victoria.\
\
Has salido victorioso en Clúcath y ahora deberías hablar con Crannog.","'Volveremos a Aughaire en triunfo, ${PLAYER}. Cuando lo dejamos, lo dejamos en duda. Volvemos ahora con la certeza de la victoria.'","¡El Clúcath ha comenzado, pero las reglas del rito no se han seguido! Ahora debes luchar para defenderte del enemigo, porque no habrá piedad.","'No entiendo, ${PLAYER}. ¿Por qué me perdonaste la vida? ¿Para qué tengo que vivir, ahora que he sido expulsado de los Trév Duvárdain y me han quitado mi nombre? Ya no soy Drostan... pero, ¿quién seré ahora?'","'¿Estás preparado, ${PLAYER}? El rito de Clúcath determinará la suerte de los Trév Gállorg, pero debemos estar en guardia: Domongart ha sido traicionero en el pasado, y hay pocas razones para esperar que hoy sea diferente.\
\
'Pero si sales victorioso, significará mucho. Hay que arriesgarse.'","Has venido a Fail-á-Khro para participar en el rito ceremonial de Clúcath en nombre de los Trév Gállorg."},
[7324]={"You and Jajax have done what you could. Now it must be up to others.","At a gesture from the Golden Queen, the guards encircle you","You and Jajax stand alone against the guardsmen in Dâr Laja.","Convince Hármelak that the river gate must be closed","'So it is a fight, then. Fine! There are not enough of them to best both Jajax and ${PLAYER}!'","'A hostile fleet approaches? My business with the Kindred can wait!\
\
'There is coin to be made, ${PLAYER}!'","'You know there is little to be gained by dying here, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Khôltekh lowers his voice so only you can hear him.\
\
'Hármelak might have pretended she first heard the name \\qThe Song of Waves and Wind\\q from you, when you visited her in her manor, but she is not as clever as she thinks herself to be. Wealth cannot buy wisdom; only experience can do that.\
\
'When Azagath told us of the Song's existence, neither of us believed in it. If the Dark Lord of Mordor could not rely upon such a fleet, of what use could it be to us? But it seems Nakási has done the impossible. The Narghâk I sent her from Ashâgir will prove the difference, I think.\
\
'When Gondor burns, the folk of Umbar Baharbêl will rejoice.'","'Looks like this is it, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We have to put our faith in Daxamat now.'","Talk to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja","Instancia: La Puerta del Río","Khôltekh has stepped through the line of Temámir archers to address you.","Assure Hármelak that <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, you have seen it","Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja","Only the Kindred of the Coins can command the river gate be closed. You and Jajax must convince Hármelak to issue the order.","Hármelak stands upon the dais in Dâr Laja.","Hármelak stares at you in disbelief, waiting for you to answer her question with a <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>.","'If by our warning we save the city, the Kindred will surely seek to reward us for our actions today, ${PLAYER}. Let us hurry!'","'Your face is lined with worry, ${PLAYER}. What brings you with such urgency to Dâr Laja?'\
\
You tell Hármelak that Nakási Wave-reaper sails a secret fleet armed with Narghâk cannons and crewed by Orcs of Mordor and soldiers of Ordâkh down the Ikorbân River. She frowns uncertainly.","'${PLAYER}! I have not seen you since your steps brought you to Umbar-môkh. I have come aboveground to ask Khôltekh... but my errand can wait. Something troubles you?'\
\
You quickly tell Birûk that Nakási Wave-reaper sails a hostile fleet toward the city, and the banks of the Ikorbân River are not safe.\
\
'I will delay you no longer! Tell the Kindred of the Coins what you have told me!'","Jajax has come with you to Dâr Laja to warn the Kindred of the Coins about the approaching danger.","Temámir archers hold you at bay. You can fight no longer","The haste of your errand permits no delay: the Kindred of the Coins must be warned of the approaching danger!","Talk to Jajax in Dâr Laja"},
[7326]={"Éowyn is standing outside Dimholt at Dunharrow.\
\
You should talk to Éowyn.","<rgb=#FF0000>Éowyn must not be defeated</rgb>","The Orc stands waiting outside the Dark Door","DNT -- Players will not see","Defeat Ur","Éowyn can be found on the Firienfeld at Dunharrow.\
\
You have arrived at Dunharrow, and now Éowyn wishes to speak with you.","The pale figure has fled deeper into the Dimholt.\
\
You should pursue it.","'Hail, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We met with no resistance on our journey, and I believe I have you to thank for that.\
\
'I would like to speak with you in private. The people will manage on their own for now, I am certain.'","Éowyn, Mágla, and Ellen Fremedon have made their preparations, and now, they stand ready to guard the people of Kingstead as they travel to Dunharrow.","Éowyn has been defeated!","Instancia: El Camino a Dunharrow","Explore Dimholt with Éowyn","Talk to Éowyn at Dunharrow","Frantic screams echo from the Paths of the Dead","'Are you ready to venture into the Dimholt, ${PLAYER}?'","Éowyn is walking near the edge of Dimholt at Dunharrow.\
\
You should walk with Éowyn.","Éowyn can be found outside the Dark Door in the Dimholt.\
\
You have defeated the Orc-leader and brought peace to the people of Kingstead.","'The Orcs are vanquished, and my people are safe. Those Orcs knew not the warriors they faced! \
\
'Dunharrow shall once again be a haven for the people of Rohan, and my people will remain free of the Enemy's grip.\
\
'Let us not tarry long here, ${PLAYER}, for this place fills me with dread.'","Talk to Éowyn","Ur can be found outside the Dark Door.\
\
You have cornered the Orc and should now defeat it.","Walk with Éowyn","Pursue the pale figure through the Dimholt","'My people are safe, ${PLAYER}. Let us return to them.'","A pale figure stands in the distance...","Éowyn is inside the Dimholt.\
\
You should explore the Dimholt and discover what lurks nearby."},
[7327]={"Instance: The Roots of Fangorn","The venomous brood of Gurthúl has burrowed its way beneath the Roots of Fangorn - they must be destroyed before they can poison the forest above!","Defeat Frûshkul the Orc captain","A root has been poisoned! (${VALUE}/6)","A band of Moria Orcs have been ruthlessly enslaved by the spider queen Gurthúl and made to dig a secret tunnel into the natural caverns beneath the Limlight Falls at the edge of Fangorn.\
\
They are led by a powerful Orc named Frûshkul, who has been left to guard the passages as Gurthúl takes her brood ahead to corrupt and poison Fangorn's deepest roots.","Defeat the spider-queen Gurthúl","Defeat Gurthúl and her venomous brood beneath the Roots of Fangorn in Great River before they corrupt and sicken the forest above!","You have defeated Frûshkul the Orc captain!","You have defeated Gurthúl!","<rgb=#FF0000>Forest roots poisoned (${VALUE}/6)</rgb>"},
[7328]={"Defeated the frenzied grodbog","A ritual obelisk of the Iron Crown has been constructed in the caverns!","Explore the cave and learn of what stirs the beasts in Máttugard.","Defeat the frenzied beasts guarding the ritual obelisk.","Something stirs the creatures of Máttugard from within the caverns, deep under the Mighty Court.","The ritual obelisk has been destroyed!","Defeated the frenzied deep-claw","Talk to Varthmath","Defeat the frenzied grodbog","Destroy the ritual obelisk.","Talk to Varthmath.","Destroy the ritual obelisk","Search the cave for what stirs the beasts in Máttugard","Instancia: Las Runas de la Malicia","'The cavern is vast. Well, shall we continue then?'","'That obelisk was certainly a creation of the Angmarim. Come, let us return to the Steepset and report what we have found.'","Defeat the frenzied deep-claw"},
[7329]={"Waldere is in the tunnel before you, injured and exhausted.","Talk to Waldere and declare your intentions","Talk to Elfdag in the Paths of the Dead","Waldere told you that his men were slain outside of a passage in the south-west of a cavernous chamber, and thinks you should search that tunnel for Elfdag.","A great city of the Dead stands beneath the mountains.\
\
You have found Elfdag in the Paths of the Dead, and now must fight to free him from the Dead.","Elfdag is in the empty streets of the city of the Dead beneath the mountains.","You have found Elfdag! He cowers in the court ahead, frightened by the Dead","'Have you come here seeking Elfdag? I ventured beneath the mountain with several of my men, but we ran afoul of the Dead, and only I survived the encounter. I fled the cavernous room where they fell, but I feel no shame for it. It was folly to come here.\
\
'There was a passage we thought to search, in the south-west wall of the cavernous room, but we were set upon before we could venture that way. If you seek Elfdag, that is a good place to begin.\
\
'But wait! Before you go: are you journeying within by yourself, or do you have a Fellowship near at hand? Speak to me again and give me your answer.'","You have proven your persistence to the Dead, and they retreat warily","Talk to Waldere","'Do you plan to venture further within by yourself, or do you have a Fellowship near at hand? Speak to me and give me your answer.'","'We should get out of here... and at once!'","Search the south-west tunnel in the Paths of the Dead for Elfdag","Instancia: Los Muertos Despiadados","Waldere has asked if you plan to venture deeper into the Paths of the Dead by yourself or if you have a Fellowship near at hand.","Fight off the Dead Men and rescue Elfdag","You have come to the Paths of the Dead in search of Elfhelm's grandson Elfdag, who may have ventured beneath the mountain.","'You are a great adventurer, I can tell! But I think we should leave at once... these Dead Men won't stay away for long, no matter how often they are defeated!\
\
'We will speak once we are above-ground, yes? I overheard some things you will want to know!'"},
[7330]={"Habla con Hórin","The Angmarim are attempting a ritual that will empower Loknashra!\
\
You should defeat the cultists performing the ritual!","Defeat the approaching fell spirits","The Angmarim are attempting a ritual that will empower Loknashra!\
\
You should defeat the approaching fell spirits!","Hórin is ready to stop the ritual taking place in Bagud-dum.\
\
You should talk to Hórin.","Do not allow the ritual to succeed","Ugarad the Harbinger intends to perform a secret ritual to impart the strength of the Gauntlord Drugoth to Loknashra of the Frost-bound. You and Hórin must stop this ritual before it is too late!","Instancia: El ritual secreto","'Ugh, my head! We made it outside. Are you all right?'","'We must find Loknashra quickly, before this ritual can be completed!'","Defeat the Angmarim cultists"},
[7331]={"Orvar te ha dicho que busques a Bori, el cautivo, en el gran campamento orco de la sala del trono.","'¡Enfrentaremos a Mazog directamente, ${PLAYER}, y lo obligaremos a decirnos dónde ha sido encarcelado Bori!'","Habla con Bróin","Con la aparición repentina de Bróin y los Elfos de Buzun-ghâr, Mazog ha sido derrotado.","'Me puse a pensar, ${PLAYER}, después de que te fuiste, en todo lo que tú y otros han pasado, y me di cuenta de algo: ya no puedo quedarme de brazos cruzados mientras otros luchan mi batalla.\
\
Una vez que decidí dejar atrás mi autocompasión, corrí a Buzun-ghâr y convencí a los Elfos allí de que me acompañaran en tu búsqueda. La suerte nos acompañó y llegamos justo cuando más se necesitaba.\
\
Debo esperar que Bori siga vivo y que sea uno de los dos enanos enviados a Dol Guldur. Solo esa esperanza puede mantenerme luchando.'","Protege a Orvar mientras enfrenta a Mazog","Debes despejar el camino para que Orvar te siga cuando esté listo.","No hay señales de Bori entre los orcos.","'Busca a Bori en el campamento orco, ${PLAYER}. Yo esperaré aquí y protegeré nuestra retaguardia de los ataques lanzados desde Zurr-thurkh.'","Has venido con Orvar a Rushdurinul, la sala del trono donde Mazog tiene su guarida, y ahora enfrentarás al líder orco.","Busca a Bori en el campamento orco","Sin señales de Bori en el campamento orco dentro de Rushdurinul, Orvar ha decidido enfrentar a Mazog directamente.","Has venido con Orvar Martillo de Campana a Zurr-thurkh, el 'camino secreto' que fue construido como pasaje de escape desde la sala del trono de Durin, y lo usarás para acceder a la fortaleza de Mazog.","Habla con Orvar en Rushdurinul","'¡Tenías razón, ${PLAYER}! Esto fue una vez Rushdurinul, la gran sala del trono de Durin. Los orcos seguramente le han dado un nuevo nombre burdo, pero para los enanos siempre será Rushdurinul.\
\
¡Lucha en el campamento orco y busca a Bori, hijo de Bósi! Yo vigilaré la retaguardia para asegurarme de que ninguna criatura de Zurr-thurkh nos sorprenda mientras luchamos contra los orcos.'","'Esto es increíble, ${PLAYER}. ¿Realmente podemos usar este pasaje para llegar detrás de los muros de Zabadgathol? ¿Por cuánto tiempo ha permanecido este túnel sin ser descubierto por enanos u orcos?\
\
¡Vamos a averiguarlo!'","Nadie ha recorrido el 'camino secreto' desde antes de la Caída de Moria, pero ahora tú y Orvar Martillo de Campana lo usarán para llegar detrás de los muros de la fortaleza de Mazog, Zabadgathol.","Habla con Corunothiel","'Dejemos este lugar, ${PLAYER}, y aseguremos que el prisionero sea mantenido en algún lugar seguro. Mazog no nos molestará en el viaje o perderá la vida, ¡y dolorosamente!'","Habla con Orvar en Zurr-thurkh","Habla con Orvar","Despeja el camino para Orvar","'El enano Bróin llegó a Buzun-ghâr poco después de que te fuiste, y dio un discurso tan inspirador que no pudimos hacer otra cosa que seguirlo hasta aquí. ¿Quién hubiera pensado que los enanos podían hablar con tanto vigor?\
\
Y ahora tiene un prisionero y ha hecho un juramento además. Espero que no termine mal para Bróin o sus amigos, porque los juramentos hechos a la ligera tienen un curioso poder.'","Instancia: El camino secreto","Orvar está esperando fuera del camino secreto, en Rushdurinul."},
[7332]={"Mithrandir pauses before the looming shadows","Allow Mithrandir to banish the shadows in Falch Gurth","You and Mithrandir are walking through Falch Gurth.","Allow Mithrandir to banish the shadows of Thuringwath","'It... cannot be.\
\
'I thought I had seen the last of the Enemy's great works brought to ruin, but I see now I was mistaken.'\
\
Mithrandir leans on his staff, seemingly barely able to support himself. You try to aid him.\
\
'No! No... there is no time for rest, ${PLAYER}.'","With a sudden flash of light from Mithrandir's staff, the shadows give way","Follow Mithrandir","'I have not seen the like of this enchantment before in Middle-earth. Perhaps you might wish that I not say so... but I find myself uneasy, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Let us continue, but not in haste.'","You should talk to Mithrandir.","Mithrandir's light pierces the shadows, revealing a blanket of darkness upon Thuringwath","You are following Mithrandir.","Thuringwath, the Valley of Secret Shadow, has remained hidden among the slopes of Ephel Dúath since the Second Age of the world.","As the pass widens into Thuringwath, great shadows loom before you","Mithrandir falls silent.","Mithrandir can be found in Falch Gurth.","'It... should not be far now to the end of the pass.'\
\
Mithrandir appears to be tiring in a way you have never seen.\
\
'Come, ${PLAYER}.'","Instancia: La Sombra Secreta","Again, the shadows give way to Mithrandir's light","Talk to Mithrandir","Dark shadows again loom in your path","'Acompáñame, ${PLAYER}.'","You should follow Mithrandir."},
[7333]={"The dwarf catches his breath.\
\
'I... I am surprised to be alive, and surprised to see a ${RACE} in Stormwall. I am Drengur. Have you come to search for me and my companions? I fear they are all dead. We were ambushed on the path. I ran into the ruins and found myself in an old spider cave. Little did I know that those beasts dwelled there as well!\
\
'I was lost, hiding myself from worms and drakes. And then... and then I saw her. A dragon, slumbering in the caves! It is true! We must leave this place at once. I only escaped the tunnels thanks to your distraction.'","Talk to the dwarf","Deep within Stormwall lies a fiery secret, slumbering in the shadows.","Defend yourself against the dragon-kind.","Instancia: El Secreto de Stormwall","Defend yourself against the dragon-kind!","You should speak with the dwarf.","'Now let us leave this place!'"},
[7334]={"Náth has fallen!","<rgb=#FF0000>Rúzat must survive</rgb>","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso.","Approach the dwarves","'Rákhrum is of no concern. I say leave the goblin to sulk in the hills.\
\
'Come, let us leave Sundergrót.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Agátur must survive</rgb>","Defeat Rákhrum and his forces.","Approach the dwarves.","The goblins of Sundergrót have set up a secret meeting within the old dwarf ruins.","Agátur has fallen!","Defeat Rákhrum and his forces","Rúzat has fallen!","Instancia: Los secretos de Sundergrót","Deja que acontecimientos sigan su curso","<rgb=#FF0000>Náth must survive</rgb>"},
[7335]={"The time has come to enter the dwarf ruin, Shathur-munzu. The woodmen warned us of 'monsters' and 'The Shadow Hunter', but I remain unconvinced. Whatever lies inside, we are capable of defeating it.","You wake up in a cage inside what must be Shathur-munzu","You find yourself inside a cage in Shathur-munzu.\
\
You should wake up.","Knock out the Orc jailor","Talk to Baradal","'Something is approaching, I can hear it in the brush. Soft paws, and a low growl.... It is moving quickly towards us! Look out!'","Baradal is standing by outside Shathur-munzu.\
\
You should talk to Baradal.","Instancia: El Cazador de Sombras","An Orc has approached your cage, taunting you.\
\
You should knock out the Orc.","The Orc jailor crumples to the ground. The key to your cage is in reach!","You should be able to reach the key and free yourself from this cage.","Defeat the attacker"},
[7336]={"Rovalang has been defeated, and you have failed!","Climb the slope and stop the Nazgûl from learning of Aragorn's passage. Rovalang must not be defeated.","The Nazgûl has not yet learned of Aragorn's passage. Hope remains, for now!","'Before we proceed, are there any companions on which you can rely? Are we on our own, or do you have a Fellowship near at hand? Speak to me again and tell me which is true!'","Time until Nazgûl encounters Drugât:","You must find the Nazgûl and prevent it from learning of Aragorn's passage.","Rovalang is waiting to speak with you.","Defeat the Nazgûl before Drugât emerges from the Paths of the Dead. Rovalang must not be defeated.","You and Rovalang have gone to the foot of the White Mountains in search of the creature he saw.","Talk to Rovalang and declare your intentions","'We will speak when we have left this place, my friend.'","You have struck the Nazgûl a grievous blow: you have kept from it dangerous knowledge","Instance: The Shadow in Morthond","Time until the Nazgûl learns of Aragorn's passage:","If the Nazgûl is able to learn of Aragorn's passage, the Ranger's advantage will be lost. You must defeat the Nazgûl before he can meet with Drugât!","Drugât emerges from the Paths of the Dead, and your mission has failed!","You have come to the foothills of the White Mountains in the company of Rovalang, searching for the terrible beast he saw flying above the Blackroot Vale.","Talk to Rovalang","'I have never before been in the presence of such evil, ${PLAYER}! Let us leave this place, and then we will speak of it... but not before!'","Rovalang has asked if you and he are on your own, or if you have a Fellowship near at hand.","'A cold sensation has gripped my heart, ${PLAYER}. Do you feel it too? I believe we draw near to the creature I beheld above the mountains!\
\
'Before we proceed, are there any companions on which you can rely? Are we on our own, or do you have a Fellowship near at hand? Speak to me again and tell me which is true!'"},
[7337]={"Advierte a los Duramano que no sigan a Skorgrím (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Recoge un arma abandonada para defenderte","Habla con Dwalin","Con un grito desafiante, Vaski atrae la atención de Ushgrat. ¡Corre mientras puedas!","Divisas a un uruk encorvado sobre un Hachetón herido, bloqueando la salida","'Bueno, eso bastará. No hay tiempo para rebuscar entre el resto con tantos orcos alrededor...'\
\
Lethi mira hacia la Escalera Retorcida.\
\
'Tendremos que bajar para llegar a las puertas. ¡Rápido ahora!'","Defiende a Lethi de la criatura pálida","'Todo esto no puede ser obra nuestra..... ¿o sí?'\
\
'¿Por qué luchan los orcos entre sí mientras nuestros hermanos avanzan hacia las puertas?\
\
'¡Quizá al fin hemos encontrado algo de buena fortuna!'","'¡Bah! ¡Qué desastre han dejado atrás!'\
\
'¿Quién eres tú y qué asuntos tienes en la mansión de Thorin Escudo de Roble?'\
\
Te presentas ante Dwalin como ${PLAYER:un[m]|una[f]} Hachetón de Mordor que escapó de la prisión del Enemigo y huyó a tierras lejanas en busca de refugio. Explicas que encontraste a Skorgrím e Ivar en el camino a la Mansión de Thorin, y que Skorgrím afirmó que los barbiluengos masacraron a los Duramano\
\
'¿Una masacre? Sí, podrías llamarlo así, pero fue obra de Ivar Manosangrienta, ¡no de los barbiluengos! Fue Ivar quien despertó a Skorgrím de su largo descanso. Pero no fue un milagro del destino... fue la vil hechicería de Ivar y el sacrificio involuntario de muchos Duramano lo que ató un espíritu terrible a sus restos. Sea lo que sea que piensen los Duramano de Skorgrím, él no es quien aparenta ser\
\
'Aunque creo que tu amigo duramano no desea hacernos daño, aún tiene mucho que responder, y no dudo que quiera oír la verdad de este triste asunto por sí mismo\
\
'Si buscas refugio, puedes ganártelo ayudándonos a restaurar estos salones tras años de abandono por parte de los Duramano. Incluso si no hubiera caído en la maldad, Gormr igualmente falló en la tarea que mi señor le encomendó. Si Nagli demuestra ser digno de confianza, podrá vivir en el Patio de Frerin....... pero queda desterrado para siempre de la Mansión de Thorin\
\
'¿Aceptas estos términos, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Asientes.\
\
'Bien, bien. Ahora, nunca he oído el nombre del clan que mencionaste, esos hachetones, pero eres ${PLAYER:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} en la Mansión de Thorin mientras trabajes para ayudar a los barbiluengos'","'Vaya historia, ${PLAYER}. Creo que nos tomó a todos por sorpresa... ¡una grata sorpresa, claro está! ¡No cualquier enano podría hacer lo que tú has hecho!\
\
'Ha sido una semana larga para nosotros, los Duramano. Nuestro Senescal, Gormr Forjadura, estaba preparando una gran celebración para Skorgrím, nuestro antiguo rey —un Ritual de Conmemoración, lo llamaba. Pero después de que los barbiluengos vinieron a Ered Luin exigiendo tributo, nos envió aquí abajo para cerrar el paso. Llevamos casi una semana trabajando y, si no me equivoco, nos perdimos la celebración hace dos... no, tres noches. ¡Vaya agradecimiento el nuestro!'\
\
Nagli parece darse cuenta de que sus quejas palidecen frente al sufrimiento de los Hachetones.\
\
'Aquí estoy, quejándome de perderme una fiesta contigo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Perdona mi necedad!\
\
'No puedo hablar por todos, pero creo que nos alegraría oír más de tus historias cuando regresemos a la Mansión de Thorin. Incluso puede que disfrutes de nuestra hospitalidad por un tiempo....... si el Senescal lo permite'","Habla con Nagli en la Mansión de Thorin","Ashaug puede encontrarse cerca de Hakal-kúnug, la Escalera Retorcida dentro de Barad-dûr.\
\
Ashaug ha recibido una herida grave en la lucha dentro de Barad-dûr, pero sus heridas parecen venir de una fuente inusual. Deberías hablar con Ashaug.","Rethvárd se encuentra en la Puerta Oxidada en Ered Luin.\
\
Nagli te ha llevado ante Rethvárd, un guardia Duramano, con la esperanza de que pueda concederte una audiencia con Gormr Forjadura, el Senescal de la Mansión de Thorin. Debes hablar con Rethvárd.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡No escapaste a tiempo!</rgb>","Lethi ha avanzado hacia los pasillos sombríos de Barad-dûr\
\
Debes seguir a Lethi y continuar hacia las puertas de Barad-dûr.","Disfrázate como un capitán orco","'Creo que con esto los engañarás...\
\
'Ahora escucha, ${PLAYER}. Hay un largo pasadizo justo delante, doblando esa esquina, y al final... las puertas de la Torre Oscura\
\
'Ya que pareces un orco de verdad, ¿por qué no te adelantas y miras más allá de la esquina? ¡Si el camino está despejado, correremos hacia allí!'","Medio oculto tras un brasero, Lethi observa a lo lejos","Cuando Lethi se acerca a la criatura pálida, ¡esta salta de pronto y ataca!","Lethi se encuentra en Barad-dûr.\
\
Has descubierto al uruk Ushgrat custodiando las puertas de Barad-dûr. Peor aún, parece haber sometido a Vaski. Debes hablar con Lethi.","El capitán orco muerto se encuentra justo delante de Lethi en Barad-dûr\
\
Tras divisar a un capitán orco muerto, Lethi te ha pedido que te disfraces con su armadura para engañar a los habitantes de Mordor. Debes disfrazarte.","Algunos de los Duramano han elegido seguir a Skorgrím, pero parece que algunos aún podrían ser persuadidos.","Después de frustrar la huida de Vaski, Ushgrat vigila ante las puertas de Barad-dûr.\
\
Deberías confrontar a Ushgrat y abrirte paso luchando para salir de Barad-dûr.","Sigue a Lethi","¡Escapa de Barad-dûr y encuentra una salida de Mordor!","'¿Era ese... el prisionero del Señor Oscuro? ¡Con razón Él quería deshacerse de él!'\
\
Lethi suspira y recupera el aliento.\
\
'Es bueno que lo hayas ahuyentado, ${PLAYER}. Juro que parecía tan enfermizo y marchito, pero ¡tenía la fuerza de un enano!\
\
'Ah, pero no hay tiempo para pensar en eso ahora. Debemos seguir...'","Mientras te ajustas el yelmo mal encajado, Lethi te llama","Advierte a Rethvárd que no siga a Skorgrím","Instancia: La Sombra de Mordor","Habla con Ashaug","Skorgrím, y muchos de los Duramano que lo siguen ahora, marchan desde la Puerta Oxidada.\
\
Debes mantenerte alerta.","Lethi se encuentra en Barad-dûr.\
\
Después de repeler a la criatura pálida que lo atacó, Lethi está trastornado. Debes hablar con Lethi antes de continuar hacia las puertas de Barad-dûr.","Mientras Dwalin mira hacia la Mansión de Thorin, se acaricia la barba con inquietud","La criatura pálida escupe y maldice mientras huye","'Pareces un buen enano, ${PLAYER}, pero debes entender... nosotros los Duramano también somos un pueblo perdido. Custodiamos la mansión de Thorin Escudo de Roble por muchos años, ¿y qué agradecimiento nos dieron los barbiluengos? ¡Escuchaste a Skorgrím! ¡Nada sino la masacre de nuestros hermanos y hermanas!\
\
'Sea lo que sea que pienses que es el rey Skorgrím... él y el poder de Angmar podrían ayudarnos a salir de la sombra de los barbiluengos y reclamar nuestra antigua gloria. Huye con los barbiluengos si debes, pero si lo haces, debes saber que no dudaré en levantar mi hacha contra ti.'","Lethi se encuentra en Barad-dûr.\
\
Te has disfrazado como un capitán orco, lo cual podría ayudarte a escapar de la Tierra de Mordor. Debes hablar con Lethi.","Nagli te ha hablado de un enano llamado Dwalin, quien lideró la reciente expedición Barbiluenga a la Mansión de Thorin\
\
Con la esperanza de conocer la verdad de las afirmaciones de Skorgrím y buscar refugio, Nagli te ha pedido que viajes con él a la Mansión de Thorin.","Habla con Lethi","Manchado con sangre negra, Ashaug yace moribundo entre varios orcos y Hachetones caídos","Lethi puede encontrarse cerca de Hakal-kúnug, la Escalera Retorcida dentro de Barad-dûr.\
\
Deberías seguir a Lethi y encontrar el camino hacia las puertas de Barad-dûr.","Nagli se encuentra en la Puerta Oxidada en Ered Luin.\
\
Nagli te ha sugerido que pidas refugio entre los Duramano en Ered Luin. Sin autoridad para decidirlo, Nagli te ha pedido que hables con Rethvárd para que él pueda llevarte ante el Senescal de la Mansión de Thorin.","Escapa de Barad-dûr y encuentra una salida de Mordor","Hasta aquí hemos llegado. Será mejor no dejarnos ver","El camino hacia las puertas de Barad-dûr está justo delante de ti.\
\
Lethi te ha pedido que mires más allá de la esquina y veas si la salida de Barad-dûr está despejada.","Dwalin puede encontrarse en algún lugar dentro de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Tras entrar en la Mansión de Thorin, los barbiluengos han vigilado de cerca a Nagli. Debes encontrar y hablar con Dwalin.","Enfrenta al Uruk","Sigue a Nagli","A medida que la sombra de Mordor se alarga sobre la Tierra Media, el Enemigo ordena la liberación de un prisionero misterioso, provocando intrigas y revueltas en Barad-dûr.","'¡Ja! ¿Pensaste que el Gran Ojo te dejaría simplemente caminar fuera de Lugbúrz, shakglob?'\
\
Ushgrat azota a Vaski antes de volverse hacia ti.\
\
'¡Tú... orco! ¿Por qué ese no está encadenado? ¿Y de dónde sacó ese cuchillo?'\
\
Los ojos de Ushgrat se entrecierran mientras te observa.\
\
'Listo, listo. Ese es tu plan, ¿eh, basura de piedra?'","¡Debes escapar de Barad-dûr antes de que sea demasiado tarde!","'Si pudiera mover aún mi brazo, te cortaría el cuello...'\
\
Ashaug tose y sangre negra se escurre por las comisuras de su boca.\
\
'El Escurridizo iba camino de salida como el Alto lo quería... y entonces ustedes entran blandiendo cuchillos y lo espantan. Para cuando me di cuenta, uno de los nuestros fue mordido... y otro cayó por las escaleras. A ustedes es fácil tirarlos, pero él no... y aunque quisiéramos no podríamos, o nos mandarían a los Pozos. Ah... pero algunos pensaron que valía los Pozos destripar a ese renacuajo.'\
\
Ashaug ríe débilmente.\
\
'Nos lanzamos unos contra otros en un instante... y nos olvidamos por completo de su pequeña revuelta, shakglob. Siempre es así. Unos pocos escapan, pero no tardan en atraparlos. Incluso si encuentran una salida de Lugbúrz, nunca... escaparán... de Mor...'\
\
Ashaug se ahoga y sus ojos se abren de par en par.","'Supongo que hasta aquí llego yo, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Con una mirada de desdén apenas disimulado, Nagli observa a los barbiluengos que lo han detenido en la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
'Cuando la expedición Barbiluenga llegó, reconocí a algunos de ellos. Están liderados por un enano llamado Dwalin, y es aclamado como héroe por muchos barbiluengos. Es un enano viejo, de barba blanca, y no sería extraño que hubiera asumido el manto de Senescal en ausencia de Gormr.\
\
'Si su gente realmente masacró a la nuestra, habrá más derramamiento de sangre entre nosotros... pero ya no estoy tan seguro de quién busca hacer daño a los Duramano. Tú conoces mucho de los caminos del Enemigo, y debo saber si nuestro pueblo ha sido engañado con algún propósito maligno.\
\
'Te ruego, ${PLAYER}, que hables con Dwalin en mi nombre.'","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Debes escapar antes de que Ushgrat domine a Lethi y Vaski!</rgb>","Lethi y Vaski han atraído la atención de Ushgrat lejos de ti.\
\
¡Debes escapar de Barad-dûr antes de que sea demasiado tarde!","Armas abandonadas pueden encontrarse cerca de los orcos muertos en Hakal-kúnug, la Escalera Retorcida dentro de Barad-dûr.\
\
Deberías encontrar un arma adecuada para defenderte antes de avanzar más en Barad-dûr.","La criatura pálida se encuentra en Barad-dûr.\
\
A pesar de parecer muerta, la criatura pálida se ha puesto de pie y ha atacado a Lethi. Debes defenderlo y ahuyentar a la criatura.","Habla con Nagli","Nagli puede encontrarse en la Puerta Oxidada en Ered Luin.\
\
Todos los Duramano excepto Nagli han partido con Skorgrím. Deberías hablar con Nagli.","Nagli puede encontrarse en la Puerta Oxidada en Ered Luin.\
\
Después de que contaste a los Duramano tu escape de Mordor, un enano llamado Nagli ha pedido hablar contigo. Deberías hablar con Nagli.","'¿Qué viste? ¿Está despejado el camino?'\
\
Le dices a Lethi que espiaste a un enorme uruk y a un Hachetón herido en la calzada, y que muchos otros hachetones han caído intentando escapar.\
\
'Sabía que nos pondrían una trampa... ¡lo sabía!'\
\
Lethi rechina los dientes de rabia.\
\
'¡Bah! Quizá si finjo ser tu prisionero, podamos engañar a ese uruk. Si no, bueno...\
\
'Es nuestra única oportunidad, ${PLAYER}. ¡Sígueme!'","Lethi se encuentra en Barad-dûr.\
\
Lethi avanza hacia las puertas de Barad-dûr. Debes seguirlo.","Lethi se encuentra en Barad-dûr.\
\
Lethi está de pie junto a un brasero en Barad-dûr. Debes hablar con Lethi.","Se puede encontrar a Lethi cerca de Hakal-kúnug, la Escalera Retorcida, dentro de Barad-dûr.\
\
Debes hablar con Lethi","Habla con Rethvárd","'¿Sí?'\
\
Nagli relata tu historia rápidamente a Rethvárd. Al terminar, Nagli pide a Rethvárd que te lleve ante el Senescal de la Mansión de Thorin para que juzgue tu valía ante los Duramano.\
\
'Sí, puedo hacerlo....... tan pronto como Bjarni llegue para tomar la guardia. Ya lleva casi una hora tarde. No es propio de él.\
\
'Me gustaría oír el relato de ti mismo, ${PLAYER}, si no es mucha molestia. ¡Haría más rápido el viaje a la Mansión de Thorin para ambos!'\
\
Rethvárd se estremece visiblemente.\
\
'Sopla un viento frío. ¿Lo sientes?'","Permanece alerta","Lethi se encuentra en Barad-dûr.\
\
Has tomado un arma. Debes hablar con Lethi y seguirlo hacia las puertas de Barad-dûr.","Rethvárd puede encontrarse en la Puerta Oxidada en Ered Luin.\
\
Ninguno de los otros Duramano que advertiste pudo ser disuadido de seguir a Skorgrím. Deberías advertir a Rethvárd.","'No falta mucho ahora... pero temo que lo peor aún nos espera.\
\
'Ashaug tenía razón en algo. Incluso si escapamos de la Torre Oscura, no llegaremos lejos sin ser notados. Y no será Udûn para nosotros después de todo esto, te lo prometo. Terminaremos en los Pozos Negros o...'\
\
Lethi se estremece visiblemente.\
\
'...o nos llevarán a la Ciudad Muerta. Yo... bueno, esperemos que no llegue a eso.'","'Algo en las palabras de Skorgrím me inquieta, y ese Hombre funesto me causa desasosiego.\
\
'Quiero confiar en las palabras del rey Skorgrím, pero no puedo. ¿Habla por sí mismo o es Ivar quien habla por su boca? Es cierto que el Senescal Gormr dejó de enviar tributo a la Montaña Solitaria hace algunos meses, pero nuestras disputas con los barbiluengos nunca terminaron en sangre... hasta ahora.\
\
'Quiero escuchar lo que los barbiluengos tienen que decir sobre estas acusaciones. ¿Ha hablado con verdad el rey Skorgrím o es esta una conspiración guiada por la mano de Angmar?.\
\
'¿Me acompañarás, ${PLAYER}? Quizá la voz de un Hachetón pueda traer más calma que la de un duramano...'","Asómate por la esquina y <rgb=#FF00FF>mira</rgb> si las puertas de Barad-dûr están sin guardia","Habla con Skorgrím","Encuentra a Dwalin, el líder de la expedición Barbiluenga, en la Mansión de Thorin","Skorgrím te fulmina con la mirada. Sus ojos destellan con un brillo antinatural\
\
'Estás lejos de casa, ¿no es así?'","Skorgrím Duramano se encuentra en la Puerta Oxidada en Ered Luin.\
\
Seguido por un número considerable de Duramano, y un Hombre de aspecto mortecino, Skorgrím ha pedido hablar contigo. Debes hablar con Skorgrím.","Dwalin puede encontrarse en la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Has encontrado a Dwalin en lo profundo de la Mansión de Thorin. Debes hablar con él en nombre de Nagli y pedir refugio en la Mansión de Thorin.","Los Duramano pueden encontrarse en la Puerta Oxidada en Ered Luin.\
\
Skorgrím Duramano afirma haber sido resucitado por un Hombre de aspecto mortecino llamado Ivar Manosangrienta, y ha convocado a todos los Duramano leales al servicio de Angmar. Sin embargo, algunos han dudado en responder a su llamado. Deberías advertirles que no sigan a Skorgrím."},
[7338]={"'That was far too close, ${PLAYER}! Hurry, let us return before others appear and overwhelm us or follow our path to the camp.'","Ides has ventured with you into the woods.\
\
Ides wishes to speak with you about the Uruk-hai.","'Something approaches, ${PLAYER}. What seeks us here among the trees?\
\
'Be ready to stand your ground.'","Defeat the Uruk-hai scouts","Instancia: El entrenamiento de la doncella escudera","Ides has ventured into the wooded area adjacent to the training grounds, to test her skill against the wild bears. She is eager to prove herself in battle.","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow Ides to be defeated</rgb>","The Uruk-hai scouts have invaded the woods by the training grounds.\
\
Uruks have begun to attack Ides while searching for the location of the training grounds.","'Come now, we must not risk being seen here again. Let us head back to the mill.'","Ides can be found waiting along the road.\
\
Ides wishes to speak with you about hunting the wild bears.","Talk to Ides","You have successfully hunted bears with Ides","'The wild bears are oft seen among the trees nearby. We must look only for the largest, most ferocious bears; they must offer a challenge if I am to improve my abilities.\
\
'Let us begin the hunt. I am eager to learn through observing your skills.'","Ides has ventured with you into the woods.\
\
Ides wishes to speak with you about the hunt."},
[7339]={"Instancia: La Hoz, el Loto y el León","Spread the map out on the table.","You have brought the leaders of Ambarûl, Khûd Zagin, and Imhûlar together in Iridír. Mizâdi has much to do before Girhâzi and Amalíbi trust her or her leadership.","Speak with Mizâdi in the war room.","'The alliance proffered here is uneasy, and fragile, but it is there. Let us venture back outside into Iridír. We have preparations to make.'","Gather the map from near the Subuzûri","Listen to the conversation","Join Mizâdi around the war table","Speak with Mizâdi in the hall","Speak with Mizâdi","Speak with Mizâdi in the hall.","Spread the map out on the table","'Thank you for coming, friend. It is quite the aid, let me tell you. I know not how to make my words persuade others, I haven't the talent. What's worse, it seems my passion has gotten the better of me again. I wish I had not said what I did to Amalíbi.\
\
'Could you gather the map from near the Subuzûri guard and spread it on the table? Now that we are discussing tactics and troop movements I feel much more in my element.'","Listen to the conversation.","Join Mizâdi around the war table.","Gather the map from near the Subuzûri."},
[7340]={"Los Elfos han lanzado un ataque para recuperar Barad Morlas de los dunlendinos que han invadido Eregion. Aunque el ataque inicial tuvo éxito, una fuerza mayor de dunlendinos cayó sobre los Elfos mientras atendían a sus heridos. Ahora, atrapados entre las ruinas y sometidos a los asaltos constantes de las máquinas de guerra, los Elfos necesitan desesperadamente ayuda.","Un defensor Elfo ha caído","Aunque los Elfos son guerreros hábiles capaces de repeler sin dificultad los asaltos de los dunlendinos, las máquinas de asedio en el campo los tienen inmovilizados y están mermando su número. Debes salir al campo, encontrar las máquinas de asedio y derrotar a sus equipos, otorgando un respiro a los defensores élficos.","Tras derrotar a los dunlendinos y dispersar a sus fuerzas, ahora puedes usar la antigua forja para potenciar tu zafiro infundido con las bendiciones de los Elfos.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para regresar a Echad Dúnann ahora?'","<rgb=#FF0000>Defensores Elfos caídos (${VALUE}/14)</rgb>","'Lamento no haber podido ayudarte durante la batalla. ¡Mi agradecimiento por salvar a mis parientes!'","¡Has creado un zafiro potenciado!","Con sus máquinas de asedio fuera de combate y su ataque debilitándose, el comandante dunlendino dirige un asalto final contra el puente. Debe ser detenido.","Derrota al comandante dunlendino","Usa el yunque antiguo","Habla con Perimbant para volver a Echad Dúnann.","Derrota equipos de armas de asedio (${VALUE}/4)","El comandante dunlendino ha sido derrotado","Instancia: El Asedio de Barad Morlas","Habla con Perimbant","Equipo de arma de asedio derrotado"},
[7341]={"You hear the clamour of fighting echoing all around you","You and Razâl must find a way into the gate-house to open the gates of Emax Dûl.\
\
You should explore the caves with Razâl and find the entrance to the gate-house.","Razâl is standing by to begin the infiltration plan.\
\
You should talk to Razâl when you are ready to begin.","Exit the gate-house","This is surely the gate-house","You have successfully taken control of the gate-house.\
\
You should find and use the lever for the main gate.","'We hold the city, but Bârshud and Góramul Sai have eluded me. We must take a moment to catch our breath, assess our casualties, and then pursue the prince.'","Find Mizâdi","Instance: The Siege of Emax Dûl","Defeat Góramul Sai","Talk to Razâl","Razâl is with you and ready to begin.\
\
You should enter the secret cave system.","Mizâdi's forces have begun the invasion of the city.\
\
You should exit the gate-house to the streets of Emax Dûl.","'Kotráka Saiya says the secret way into the city is through here. The two of us will enter the cave system, find the way to the gate-house, and open the main gates to the city, allowing our forces through.\
\
'Everyone is counting on us. Let us go!'","Emax Dûl, the ancient Nêshakari stronghold overlooking Idagâl, has long been known to be an impenetrable fortress. Many invasions have failed at its gates. The prince of Ordâkh and his forces are counting on this to protect themselves from the growing rebellion just outside their walls, but unknown to them, the fortress has a weakness.","Góramul Sai has retreated into the palace","Mizâdi has cornered Góramul Sai at the steps to the palace.\
\
You should help your allies defeat Góramul Sai.","Defeated the guards in the gate-house","You have found the gate-house.\
\
You should defeat the guards in the gate-house before they can signal the alarm.","Defeat the guards in the gate-house","Find the entrance to the gate-house","Mizâdi's forces are fighting for control of Emax Dûl.\
\
You should find Mizâdi somewhere up ahead.","Enter the secret cave system","Use the gate lever"},
[7342]={"Ha llegado el momento de despedirte de tus hermanos antes de salir hacia el mundo más amplio.","El Mago Radagast ha venido al refugio de Grimbeorn, y tu mente corre intentando averiguar la razón. Tu hermano Sterkist quiere tu ayuda para descubrir qué ha traído al Mago desde su hogar en el Bosque Negro.","Instancia: La Herencia del Cambiapieles","'¿No te dije que tu momento llegaría pronto, mi ${PLAYER:hermana[f]|hermano[m]}? ¡Quizá sea tan Mago como el propio Radagast!'\
\
Langhár se ríe alegremente.\
\
'No, eso no es lo que quiero. Quiero explorar las tierras más allá de nuestro hogar, , como tú estás a punto de hacer. ¡Quiero buscar aventura! Te seguiré más pronto que tarde, , ¡te lo aseguro!\
\
'¡Hasta que nos encontremos de nuevo, ${PLAYER:hermana[f]|hermano[m]}! Encuentra a ese Montaraz, entrega el mensaje de Radagast, ¡y no sacies tu sed de aventura hasta que Sterkist y yo podamos unirnos a ti!'","Parece que Radagast ya sabía del movimiento de los trasgos, y que su visita a Grimbeorn está relacionada de algún modo con los crecientes problemas del mundo.","Habla con Sterkist y convéncelo de que no permanezca como un oso malhumorado","Langhár te sonríe, pero antes de hablar con tu hermana deberías terminar tu primera tarea: derrotar a las moscas guadaña que zumban cerca.","Habla con Sterkist frente al refugio de Grimbeorn","Grimbeorn ha tomado su decisión: te enviará en el encargo de Radagast, para llevar una advertencia sobre la oscuridad creciente que amenaza la Tierra Media.","Te has preparado para el viaje, y ahora ha llegado el momento de dejar la tierra de tu hogar en busca del Montaraz Aragorn.","Habla con Radagast y Grimbeorn, llena las alforjas del caballo y parte de viaje","Has vivido en los valles protegidos del Río Anduin toda tu vida, pero ahora las tierras salvajes te llaman, y la aventura se abre ante ti.","Encuentra a la vaca lechera que anda vagando y convéncela de regresar a su corral.","'¡Bien, bien, bien! Temía que Grimbeorn no comprendiera la urgencia de este asunto, pero la razón ha prevalecido. Siempre he tenido mano con osos y bestias, y bueno... ya ves... nada, nada. ¡No es importante!\
\
'Un poder oscuro está creciendo, ${PLAYER}. No puedo ponerle un nombre, si es que tiene uno, pero algo ha alterado el mundo natural. Buscaré al mayor de los Cinco Magos, pues él ha estudiado muchas cosas que desconozco y puede saber qué está ocurriendo.\
\
'Quiero que tú busques a otra persona. Es un Montaraz, y su nombre es Aragorn. Ha estado enredado en los asuntos de los Magos desde hace tiempo, y si los temblores que percibo representan un peligro real, como temo, sé que Aragorn deberá tener especial cuidado para no caer presa de ellos.\
\
'Lo último que supe de él es que viajaba por las Tierras de Bree, más allá de las montañas.'","Varthmath quizá sepa qué trajo a Radagast fuera del Bosque Negro, y deberías encontrarlo en el corral de animales al oeste del refugio. Tu primo es un hombre de pocas palabras, pero sus oídos atentos no se pierden nada.","Una de las vacas lecheras ha salido del corral, y Varthmath quiere que la encuentres y la envíes de vuelta antes de que salga del recinto de Grimbeorn.","Habla con Sterkist afuera del refugio de Grimbeorn","'Aragorn es un Montaraz, lo que significa que viaja a menudo por lo Salvaje, y la gente de las aldeas más allá de las montañas lo mira con desconfianza. ¡Muy parecido a mí, ahora que lo pienso!\
\
'Aquí, te acompañaré un trecho, y te contaré lo que sé del camino a través de las montañas, y cómo encontrar las Tierras de Bree...'","Sterkist gruñe en el lenguaje de los osos, pero tus palabras están llenas de afecto. Él se eriza, y finalmente cede.","Ofolmóth quiere que pongas a prueba tu temple contra las moscas guadaña alrededor de la cerca. Si rodeas la cerca hacia el oeste y el sur, encontrarás suficientes molestias para obtener una buena práctica.","'¿Hemos llegado a esto, ${PLAYER}? ¿Sirves a quienes son más perezosos que tú, buscando vacas perdidas y haciendo recados?'\
\
Ofolmóth ríe con rudeza.\
\
'Eres del linaje de Beorn, igual que yo, pero no he olvidado lo que eso significa. ¡Para ti significa poco! Deberíamos vivir nuestras vidas con ferocidad, aprovechando cada momento con dientes y garras. Nadie es mi amo.\
\
'Temo que te has vuelto ${PLAYER:blando[m]|blanda[f]}, . ¡Solo aprovechando tu Ira en combate podrás honrar verdaderamente tu herencia! ¡Prepárate para la batalla y pon a prueba tus habilidades contra mí!'","Corre al refugio de Grimbeorn para advertirle de los trasgos","Ofolmóth está rodeado por los cuerpos de trasgos","Habla con Ofolmóth y descubre qué quiere de ti.","Le cuentas rápidamente a Sterkist sobre los trasgos que te atacaron a ti y a Langhár.\
\
'¡Eso es muy extraño, ${PLAYER}! Beorn infundió el miedo de los nuestros en los trasgos cuando acechaba estos valles, y nosotros hemos hecho nuestra parte para mantener su terror de nosotros, ¿no es así? ¿Qué podría hacerles pensar en volver una vez más a este lado del río?'","Habla con Langhár","Habla con Radagast","Habla con Ofolmóth cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para entrar en combate con él.","Ofolmóth cree que el linaje de Beorn se sirve mejor mediante batalla constante y feroz. Quiere asegurarse de que seas tan fuerte como puedas ser, y quiere que pongas a prueba tus habilidades contra él en combate.\
\
Te ha pedido que hables con él cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}.","'¿Cuántas tardes hemos pasado así, ? Una vez terminado el trabajo y las tareas hechas, parece que todos los días nos encuentran mirando el estanque del viejo Grimbeorn, pensando pensamientos livianos.'\
\
Sterkist suspira, como suele hacerlo en estas tardes, y se rasca distraídamente el brazo.\
\
'Eres mi ${PLAYER:hermana[f]|hermano[m]}, , y no guardamos secretos entre nosotros. ¿Es esto todo lo que podemos esperar? ¡La sangre del cambiapieles fluye en nosotros y debe impulsarnos a hazañas mayores que estas!'","Tu hermana Langhár suele pasear por los campos de trébol, vigilando cualquier amenaza que se acerque demasiado al hogar de Grimbeorn. Ella te llamó después de que derrotaras a muchas moscas guadaña, y puede encontrarse al suroeste.","'¡No pensaba volver a verte hoy, mi ${PLAYER:hermana[f]|hermano[m]}! La mayoría de las tardes las pasas soñando al sol con Sterkist. ¿Qué tiene de diferente este día?'\
\
Le dices a Langhár que Radagast el Mago ha visitado a Grimbeorn, y que Ofolmóth te puso a luchar contra moscas-guadaña como práctica. Tu hermana sonríe y adopta una voz ronca y feroz.\
\
'¡Lucha! ¡Ruge! ¡Batalla! ¡Gruñe! ¡El linaje de Beorn es el mejor de todos!', vocifera, en una imitación aceptable de Ofolmóth.","Te acercas a la vaca lechera y ella brama nerviosamente. Algo la ha alterado. ¿Qué podría ser?\
\
Cuando eras joven desarrollaste la habilidad de comprender muchos de los lenguajes animales, un don de tu ancestro Beorn. Ahora recurres a esa facilidad natural para hablarle suavemente a la vaca lechera.\
\
Al poco tiempo recupera la calma y comienza a volver lentamente a su corral.","'¿Qué te trae por aquí, ${PLAYERNAME:primo[m]|prima[f]}?'\
\
Le cuentas a Varthmath que Radagast el Mago ha dejado el Bosque Negro y está hablando con Grimbeorn, y que esperabas que él hubiese oído por qué. Varthmath responde con un resoplido brusco.\
\
'Sé qué lo trae aquí: sus propios asuntos. Si llega a ser un tema nuestro, Grimbeorn nos lo dirá. Hasta entonces deberías atender tus propios asuntos. Mejor aún: deberías hacer algo útil para mí.\
\
'Una de nuestras vacas lecheras se ha alejado del corral. Encuéntrala antes de que salga del muro que rodea, y dile que regrese.'","Escucha las noticias de Radagast sobre el mundo más amplio","Moscas-guadaña derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los trasgos han convergido en el corral de Grimbeorn, y deberías llevarle noticia de su ataque.","Los trasgos han llegado a los valles del Anduin, y deberías volver al refugio de Grimbeorn y advertir a tu familia del peligro.","Radagast tiene un encargo urgente para ti, y te llevará lejos de las tierras familiares de tu hogar.","Habla con Langhár en los campos fuera del corral de Grimbeorn, al suroeste.","'Nada me enoja tanto como la debilidad, ${PLAYER}. ¡Expúlsala de tu cuerpo con entrenamiento y práctica! El linaje de Beorn no merece menos.\
\
'Sigue la cerca que rodea y practica tus habilidades contra las moscas-guadaña que encuentres. ¡Ese entrenamiento te hará más fuerte y más feroz!'","Necesitarás algunos suministros si quieres tener éxito en tu viaje.","'Sí, joven. He tomado mi decisión. Dejarás esta tierra protegida y llevarás un mensaje de advertencia donde el Mago crea que debe ir. Por mucho tiempo pensé que nuestro pueblo podía permanecer separado de las demás gentes, como deseaba mi padre, pero esos días han quedado atrás.\
\
'Quizá envíe a otros en los días venideros, pero por ahora tú representarás el linaje de Beorn en el mundo más amplio. Actúa con fuerza y claridad de propósito, , y que todos los que te vean digan: 'Allá va ${PLAYER:una mujer[f]|un hombre[m]} del linaje de Beorn. ¡Crúzate con ${PLAYER:él[m]|ella[f]} bajo tu propio riesgo!'.\
\
'No creo en despedidas largas, joven. Aprende tu tarea del Mago, despídete de tus hermanos, y no traigas deshonra a nuestro linaje.'","Tú y tu hermano Sterkist han pasado muchas tardes mirando las aguas quietas del estanque junto al refugio de Grimbeorn una vez terminado el trabajo.\
\
Sterkist está filosófico esta tarde en particular y desea continuar vuestra conversación.","Habla con Grimbeorn","Los trasgos han llegado a los valles del Anduin, y deberías llevar noticia de su presencia a Grimbeorn en su refugio.","Date prisa y vuelve a la entrada del refugio de Grimbeorn","Habla con Varthmath en el corral al oeste del refugio de Grimbeorn","Ofolmóth ha pronunciado tu nombre. Está de pie justo más allá de la puerta del corral de Grimbeorn.","Habla con Sterkist junto al estanque de Grimbeorn","'¿Estos trasgos creyeron que podrían superarme? ¡Criaturas necias! Harían falta dos docenas de trasgos para sacarme una gota de sangre, ¡y aun así yo sería superior!\
\
'Date prisa hacia el refugio y dile a Grimbeorn que los trasgos han perdido cualquier pizca de sensatez que quizá tuvieron alguna vez.'","'He visto a Radagast solo una o dos veces, y fue cuando éramos muy pequeños; ¿lo recuerdas? Éramos muy pequeños entonces, y él fue amable con nosotros, pero no creo que disfrutara dejar su hogar en el Bosque Negro.\
\
'¡Algo serio debe haber ocurrido para traerlo hasta aquí, mi ${PLAYER:hermana[f]|hermano[m]}! Olfatearé alrededor del refugio e intentaré escuchar algo de su conversación con nuestro padre, y tú deberías hablar con Varthmath en los corrales. Nuestro primo habla poco, pero oye mucho, y podría saber algo.'","Derrota moscas-guadaña fuera de la cerca que rodea (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Somos pocos como nosotros, ${PLAYER}. Por eso te pongo a prueba como lo hago. El legado de Beorn es raro y menguante. ¡Debemos usarlo para ser los más fuertes de sus hijos y nietos! Mientras combatimos, la Ira llena nuestros corazones y nos impulsa con gran ferocidad, potenciando las habilidades que usamos en batalla.\
\
'¡Que nuestros enemigos tengan cuidado! ¡Se enfrentan al linaje de Beorn bajo su propio riesgo!'"},
[7343]={"¡Los rufianes atacan!","Derrota a los rufianes.","Derrota a los rufianes","Deja que los acontecimientos sigan su curso.","Lanza bombas fétidas a los Fronteros de Lotho.","'Ya conoces el plan. Sabes qué hacer. No hay nada más que discutir.\
\
'${PLAYERNAME:¿Preparado, amigo?[m]|¿Preparada, amiga?[f]} ¡Es ahora o nunca!'","Instancia: El olor de la revuelta","Deja que los acontecimientos sigan su curso","Los planes de Lotho de cambiar las fronteras de la Comarca Allende deben ser detenidos.","Lanza bombas fétidas a los Fronteros de Lotho (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Ja, eso mantendrá a Lotho ocupando un rato!'","Con los rufianes derrotados, es hora de centrar tu atención en Lotho","Habla con Fredegar"},
[7344]={"'I wandered for what seemed like hours. I should have given up, but I didn't.\
\
'My thoughts turned to the family I no longer had. I remembered that father had allowed me to accompany him on a hunt not long before Amelina was taken. A hart was grazing in the lowlands, unaware that father's eyes were upon him. Father drew his bow, and though the creature must have sensed its peril, the arrow was loosed. The hart darted, but father's arrow had flown true. It pierced the hart's hind leg, and the beast stumbled. The hart fled as fast as its hooves could bear it, but father carefully followed its uneven, bloodied tracks. \
\
'By the time we came upon it, the hart had collapsed in pain. Father slew it that its suffering might be ended, but as my thoughts returned to that dreary night, I felt no such duty.'","Atta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher.\
\
You should talk to Atta.","Instancia: El Arrebatador","'I ran and I ran and I ran. I darted behind bushes, leapt over fallen trunks and branches, and cast down anything that might slow the Snatcher's pursuit.\
\
'My throat was raw and my legs burned, but it did not matter. I knew if I gave in, if I dared to grow weary, the Snatcher would kill me. But what if it did? Would I see Amelina again? And what of mother and father? What would one more moment of pain in my life be worth?\
\
'The Snatcher suddenly stopped. For a moment, it stood still as if transfixed by an unseen spirit, but then it began to speak. What a horrible voice it had! It choked between its words, but it seemed to be speaking to someone. \
\
'As I watched it carry on in heated conversation, my breath returned to me. I began to hope that it had forgotten its pursuit.'","Atta has offered to tell you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher.\
\
You should talk to Atta.","Atta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher.\
\
You should talk to Atta before allowing him to continue his tale.","When Atta was a boy, the creature known as the Snatcher returned to the Vales of Anduin and once again sought to prey on the weak and helpless.","Listen to Atta and follow along with his tale","'What would father have thought of me? What a fool I had been!\
\
'I was no practised warrior... no hunter of beasts. I was a boy swinging a dagger in the rain!\
\
'The Snatcher twisted and slithered away from me like some sort of demon-serpent. It cackled and sputtered at me, and with a single lunge, it wrest the dagger from my hand. A cruel delight gleamed in the Snatcher's eyes as it flung father's dagger into the Anduin, but there was no time to mourn its loss.\
\
'The Snatcher bared its teeth with a dreadful, rotten grin.'","Talk to Atta","Atta falls silent.","'I thought I was dead.'\
\
'When I opened my eyes, I saw the skin-changer, Beorn, standing above me. It was a trick of the mind, some dying fantasy, I thought. But it wasn't.\
\
'Beorn lifted me from the ground and held me in his arms. He tore some cloth from his own breast, wrapped me in it, and he delivered me to Hultvís.\
\
'Without a word, Beorn left. I never saw him again.'","'It was very long ago, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The Snatcher had vanished for hundreds of years, and my people had abandoned their vigil. I was a boy then... only days past the start of my eighth year. My sister, Amelina, was nigh to her fourth, but her birth had taken our mother. If only it had ended there....\
\
'One night, I woke to a great clattering. The shutters were open, and Amelina was gone. Muddied footprints had been left in Amelina's bed, but no other sign of her remained. After that day, my father rarely spoke. In the mornings, he rose with the sun to search for Amelina, and when darkness fell, he would stand watch at the gates of Hultvís.\
\
'And so it continued. Until one night not one month later....'","'I did not understand. The Snatcher had fled in plain sight, and none in Hultvís pursued it. My father was dead. And for what?\
\
'Sorrow turned to anger, and I ran to the home where my family had once lived. I tore through father's belongings with tears in my eyes, but it was not long before I found his dagger. If revenge was to be taken, I thought, it would have to be by my own hand.'","Atta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher.\
\
You should listen to Atta as he tells his tale."},
[7345]={"Jump off the edge of Byre Tor's cliff.","Núrzum has arrived; run! Run the other way!","Run north","Defeated attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Jump off the cliff, quickly!","Two more uruks stand in the road in north-west Byre Tor.","Defeat the Uruk scout","Run north, to the edge of Byre Tor.","Núrzum is close behind!\
\
You should run in the opposite direction.","You do not remember any more -- only staggering blindly away, far away from Byre Tor","Defeat attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Enemies are behind you!","A cold wind blows from the north-west of town.\
\
You should speak to the Uruk in the north-west of Byre Tor.","Jump off the cliff","Instancia: Las nieves vuelven","Run east!","'I hope you're ready to die.\
\
'The boys are right behind me, and behind them... well, you'll just have to hope that you survive long enough to meet him, eh?'","Talk to the Uruk standing in the road","Uruks approach...","Two more Uruks appear to block the path...","Run east, away from Núrzum's forces!","Uruks approach from behind!\
\
You should defeat the attacking Uruks.","Try to escape Byre Tor by heading north-west","Run away from Núrzum!\
\
You should approach the glowing path markers.","Run away from Núrzum, east!","The snows and the enemies have come to Byre Tor once more.","Run along the road, away from Núrzum"},
[7346]={"'I will not apologize to these cowards, ${PLAYER}. They are children, playing at war while the sun is in the sky, and called in for bed at sundown.'","Linadar is by the camp-fire near where the waggons have stopped for the night.","'I don't care what he says for himself. I don't trust him. That Easterling would stick us with a blade without a second thought; how many good men of Gondor have already died at his hands, or at the hands of his fellows?\
\
'I will not sleep tonight. I will keep one eye open, and make sure this Ayorzén does not try anything. You should do the same!'","'Do these men think I have no ears? I hear what they whisper behind their hands. It bothers me not. I can say the same of them, and much worse! They do not have even a portion of Ayorzén's courage, or his fine features.\
\
'They are right to worry. If I wanted them dead, they would not see this sun come up in the morning. Lucky they are to have seen the end of the war. Do they know it is done? I do not fight for Sauron any longer.\
\
'Did I say they were cowards, and ugly of face? Dim-witted they are also, to think the war still needs fighting. Join them at their camp-fire, if you wish. I am content to stay right here, and need neither the warmth of their fire nor their company.'","Talk to Linadar by the camp-fire","'You may as well get some rest while we are stopped, ${PLAYER}. I hope Rathnor wakes with the sun and we can be off again as soon as possible!'","A brief respite on the way to Minas Tirith will be welcomed by all.","Talk to Rathnor by the waggons","'These waggons travel more slowly than they did on the way to the Black Gate! Does Rathnor spare his horses the exertion of a reasonable pace? He does them no favours. Shadowfax is made the better by haste, and revels in the lands passing by at speed!\
\
'Bah. These horses could do with some feed, and the evening will be rest enough, but I am impatient to reach Minas Tirith. The scrolls and tomes of the White City will be of use to me, but I need you there if we are to cover them sufficiently.'","Listen to the conversation by the camp-fire and remain alert","'I will not repent of my words, ${PLAYER}, but... I will confess to you that I paid no heed to events beyond the borders of Gondor. That Sauron first conquered the lands to the East was known to me, but I did not consider what that must have meant to the people who lived there. I believed the Easterlings worshipped him as their Dark Lord, and no doubt many of them did, but the words of Ayorzén have planted seeds of doubt in my mind.\
\
'I do not like him, and I still do not trust him. But perhaps his people... bah! I do not know, ${PLAYER}. Would we have succumbed to the domination of Sauron, as did the Easterlings? I did not believe so, but perhaps it is a more difficult question to answer than I thought it was.'","Talk to Ayorzén south-west of the waggons","Rathnor has stopped the waggons on the road to Minas Tirith, and will wait for the onset of morning before he drives them the rest of the way to the White City.","Talk to Mithrandir south-east of the camp-fire","'Good, the soldiers have started a fire. We will take some food and some rest, and when the sun comes up once more we will continue on to the city. This is a pleasant enough place to wait out the evening... much nicer than the lands we have left behind us! It will be good to have a reprieve from the choking fumes of Mordor and the wastes that border that foul land.\
\
'But do not be lulled into complacency by the pleasing scenery! Keep an eye on that Easterling. He has caused no trouble thus far, but I do not want him to take advantage of our kindness. His sort are deceptive and untrustworthy, and we must not forget it!'","Talk to Ayorzén by the camp-fire before the situation worsens","Talk to Mithrandir south-east of the waggons","Mithrandir is near the fire where the waggons have stopped for the night.","Talk to Linadar west of the waggons","Tensions run high by the side of the road where the waggons to Minas Tirith have stopped for the night, and you should try and defuse the situation, if you can.","Ayorzén is looking at the sunset not far from where the waggons have stopped for the night.","Instancia: La canción de la dulce Lara","The men have called for you to <rgb=#00FF00>sit</rgb> by the fire with them.","'We cannot believe everything that Ayorzén says, ${PLAYER}, but I detect in his words some elements of truth. That his people pass down legends of the creatures that stalked their lands cannot be questioned, and I know the inspiration for the one he calls \\qSweet Lara.\\q\
\
'She was called Lhaereth the Stained, a creature of fell reputation. Once she made her home in Mordor, and it seems Agarnaith has not forgotten her, for the touch of her corruption remains. Many were the hurts she perpetrated upon the lands of the Easterlings, and her foul touch was felt even in Gondor.\
\
'But that is not a tale to be told in the dark, even by fireside. Lhaereth is gone with her master, though her presence can still be felt in Mordor today.'","Tensions run high by the side of the road where the waggons to Minas Tirith have stopped for the night.","<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> by the camp-fire near the waggons","The waggons have stopped for the night, and the folk that travel with you prepare to rest."},
[7347]={"Talk to the Gondorian soldier","Tárandil is at Díngarth.","The sons of Isildur are sharing a meal and conversation around a camp-fire at the encampment of Díngarth.","Talk to Tárandil","Vëamacil and Ornaher are at Díngarth, relating stories told by their eldest brother Meldaran, who remained at the Black Gate.","A soldier of Gondor has asked the sons of Isildur for tidings of the Ghâzab Bôron.","Talk to Vëamacil","Listen to the sons of Isildur discuss the Ghâzab Bôron, the Storm of Wrath","Vëamacil is at Díngarth.","Tárandil has returned with the wine, but he is displeased to be the subject of his foster-brothers' gibes.","'Ornaher says he cannot remember life before the siege? I know it was years ago, but that still seems a foolish thing to say; I cannot agree with him. Were he my brother by blood, perhaps it would be different, but it is not so. He and the other sons of Isildur are my foster-brothers, for the king took me to foster following our arrival on the shores of Middle-earth.\
\
'But I did not come here to argue with them or with you. I came here to eat, and I suggest we commence that undertaking with no further delay!'","'They do not make merry at Meldaran's expense. It seems I am always to be the subject of their taunts. Were I their true brother...'","'Vëamacil exaggerates the story somewhat, but only somewhat... in its broad strokes, that is much as Meldaran conveyed it to the two of us. Likely it was some feat of Elf-magic that destroyed the gate. And has Tárandil not affirmed that was the way of it?'","Ornaher is at Díngarth.","The sons of Isildur wait for you to sit by their camp-fire and share a meal.","Instancia: Los Hijos de Isildur","Talk to Ornaher","'Ah, it is probably time for us to begin the inspection. Let us see if Díngarth's defences remain secure.'","'My brother told you I am to be called Ornaher? Very good, very good. He cannot always be trusted with serious matters, for he is prone to jests and flights of fancy, but it is good to find he has not endangered our well-being. Not on this day, at least.\
\
'This siege has dragged on for so many years, it becomes difficult to remember what life was like before we came to be encamped within Mordor. Every semblance of a normal life fades, replaced with the deeds we accomplished in the war. Hearken to this: while our brothers fought at Dagorlad, Vëamacil and I marched to Imlad Ithil alongside other soldiers of Gondor and fought to drive the Orcs from that valley. And yet, if you ask me of my life before the war, I would find myself quite tongue-tied! Now there is only battle, and waiting.\
\
'To speak true, there is more waiting now than battle. I do not have the stomach for sieges.'","'My youngest brother, Valandil, was born in Rivendell, and he remained there with my mother when we returned to Gondor and the war. I have not seen him since we departed, and he was a lad of just four years. Why, he must be nearly eleven now! A pox on this everlasting siege! He will be a man grown by the time I see him again!\
\
'The rest of my brothers have each seen battle during the long years of the siege, and they have acquitted themselves most admirably. Two of them have come with me to Díngarth, and will be happy to meet you. The third will still be at the Black Gate, I expect.'","A Gondorian soldier has interrupted the merry-making to ask a concerning question of the sons of Isildur.","Listen to the sons of Isildur discuss the war's progress","Listen to the conversation of the sons of Isildur","<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> by the fire","'I give you the advice I gave him: do not despair! If the Rhúnhoth that make up the Ghâzab Bôron were to be a threat to us, they would have arrived by now. The Longbeards and the Thíuda will defeat the Storm of Wrath, and return in victory. Their fighting prowess is well-known, and their foes cannot match them. It is not the fate of King Durin to be slain by Easterling warriors, and I daresay Huneric Hundred-slayer will need a new epithet once his victory against the horde is complete!\
\
'Fear not. Word must soon arrive of the Storm's defeat. It will be any day now... perhaps in time for Tárandil's birthday!'","Vëamacil has suggested that you take a meal with his brothers before the sons of Isildur conduct their inspection of Díngarth's defences.","'I beg you will take no offence, for I do not mean to disturb the noble ones, but the boys of my company were hoping to find out if they knew anything recent of the Ghâzab Bôron.\
\
'Men such as they are can sometimes hear things sooner than the rest of us, is all. Do they know what has happened to the men and dwarves that went to face the Ghâzab Bôron?'"},
[7348]={"'I cannot believe Horn would act this way, ${PLAYER}! Has he closed his eyes to everything we have experienced on this journey? He shares the maddening outlook of his people! Suvulch will not understand him.'\
\
Nona clenches her fists and tosses her hair in frustration.\
\
'We cannot choose to whom we give our hearts, ${PLAYER}. That is our lot, but I might have chosen one less stubborn, from out of all the kingdoms of Men!'","You give Hildegard your name and she nods.\
\
'It is a pleasure to meet you, friend of Herubrand. Many are the roads you have walked to get here, and many more you will walk before you are at last given rest.'","Hildegard stands, unblinking, but does not appear to see you or Nona any longer.","Hildegard stands, unblinking, but does not appear to see you any longer","Hildegard stares sightlessly forward.","Hildegard looks at you curiously. Her face is a quiet mask, and you cannot tell what hides behind her calm expression.","'This woman speaks in riddles and rubbish, ${PLAYER}. If she has knowledge of days to come, why does she not spell it for us plain? Were she to do that perhaps I would give her my belief, but until then I remain unconvinced.'","Talk to Herubrand inside Orlag Den","Listen to Horn's confrontation with Hildegard in Orlag Den.","Horn has made his disbelief of Hildegard most plain.","The soothsayer Hildegard stands upright, staring forward sightlessly. She still breathes, but she no longer appears to see either you or Nona.","Listen to the words of Hildegard","Answer Hildegard's questions, and hear what she has to say","Talk to Horn in Orlag Den","Hildegard is inside the cave of Orlag Den, where she makes her home.","Hildegard has asked you what adventuring discipline you follow.","Instancia: El Adivino","Nona is in Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.","Herubrand has brought you to Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.","Talk to Nona in Orlag Den","Talk to Hildegard in Orlag Den","Hildegard has asked to speak with Nona.","Horn is in Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.","'We have arrived, ${PLAYER}. Hildegard has sight of many things still to come, and the source of her power is unknown to me. Many of my kinsmen call it witchcraft, sorcery such as that practiced by the Elves, but I say Hildegard was a woman of Rohan, and remains so.\
\
'Speak to her with courtesy.'","Listen to Horn and Hildegard's confrontation","Herubrand is inside Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.","'${PLAYER}, what can we do? If Hildegard speaks the truth, it means Horn will fall in battle. A good death for any warrior, but he is not just any warrior, ${PLAYER}. He is mine, and it is not glory he seeks. I know this to be true!\
\
'I will keep Horn from meeting this end. Others have fought their fates. Why not Nona, daughter of Suvulch, sister of Wadu? You will help me in this, ${PLAYER}. You will say none of this to Horn. Do you understand?'"},
[7349]={"Khaljûn asks you to accompany him further into the Blade-horn to further investigate the wailing spirit and his brother's journal.","Defeat the attacking spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Investigate the strange crack left by the wailing spirit within the Blade-horn.","Attempt to calm the mysterious spirit within the Blade-horn.","The spirit turns and flees like the wind, moving through a seemingly solid wall","Investigate the strange mechanism in the torch near the wall of the Blade-horn.","Defeat the attacking spirits!","Investigate the strange mechanism near the wall of the Blade-horn","Attempt to calm the mysterious spirit","Defeat the mysterious spirit within the Blade-horn","Defeat the mysterious spirit within the Blade-horn.","Spirits descend to attack you!","Instancia: El Espectro y la Sombra, Parte 3","You see a similar mechanism to the first wall in Blade-horn. Another secret passage?","Press further into the Blade-horn, behind the broken wall.","A secret door shudders and opens, leading to a deeper part of the Blade-horn","Defeated attacking spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Press further into the Blade-horn","Investigate the strange wall within the Blade-horn"},
[7350]={"Get close to the first secret door inside the Blade-horn","Defeat Valrazâr in the crypt","Listen to the conversation","Defeat Valrazâr in the crypt.","You must press even further into Bâdrasag, the Blade-horn, to uncover its closely kept secrets.","Listen to Khaljûn in the crypt of the Blade-horn.","Listen to the conversation between Khaljûn and Valrazâr.","Listen to Khaljûn in the crypt of the Blade-horn","Defeated spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Join Khaljûn at the tomb at the end of the corridor.","Listen to the conversation between Khaljûn and the mysterious man.","The wall pushes back and lifts, revealing another corridor and an even deeper area","Listen to the conversation between Khaljûn and Valrazâr","Examine the suspicious wall the spirit went through in the Blade-horn.","Join Khaljûn at the tomb at the end of the corridor","Examine the suspicious wall the spirit went through in the Blade-horn","Instancia: El Espectro y la Sombra, Parte 4","Defeat the angry spirits within the passage!","The door opens, seemingly without activation or interference","Fight off the spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Get close to the first secret door inside the Blade-horn."},
[7351]={"'Dejemos atrás este bosque, ${PLAYER}. Ya he tenido suficientes aventuras por hoy, ¡muchas gracias!'","Le hablas al ciervo con palabras tranquilizadoras en la lengua de los animales, palabras que Grimbeorn y otros de los tuyos te enseñaron en tu juventud. El pánico del ciervo se atenúa poco a poco, aunque sus orejas aún se agitan ante cualquier sonido.\
\
La actitud de la criatura asustada te indica que Clothar tiene razón en preocuparse: un gran depredador anda cerca.","Has encontrado al oso que amenazó y aterrorizó a Clothar.\
\
Parecía que casi lograbas calmar al gran oso con tus palabras, pero la criatura logró sacudirse tu influencia.","Clothar Hojarena se encuentra en el Bosque Viejo y apenas puede creer lo que ven sus ojos y oyen sus oídos.","Vuelves a tender la mano hacia el oso, recurriendo a tu afinidad natural con las criaturas. Un gruñido bajo confirma tu sospecha: algo ha infundido en el oso un miedo grande y terrible, poniendo en marcha este ataque frenético.\
\
'Amigo', le hablas con tono tranquilizador, y el oso te dice su nombre.\
\
De pronto, un fuerte estremecimiento sacude el cuerpo de la criatura, ¡y vuelve a atacar!","'Oh, no sé nada de esto, ${PLAYER}. Sé que dije que te mostraría dónde vi al oso gigante, pero cuanto más nos acercamos, menos me gusta estar aquí. ¡Esto fue un error!'","Clothar se sobresaltó por la aparición repentina de un animal, pero solo era un ciervo nervioso, no el oso gigante que esperaba ver.\
\
Deberías hablarle en la lengua de los animales y averiguar si ha visto al oso enloquecido.","El miedo ha desaparecido y ahora ves algo distinto en los ojos de Zarzagruño: respeto y admiración. Has salvado al oso de sí mismo.","El miedo ha desaparecido de los ojos de Zarzagruño y ha sido reemplazado por otras emociones: respeto y admiración.\
\
Tus palabras apaciguadoras y la firmeza de tu determinación han devuelto a Zarzagruño la razón. En la lengua de su especie, te cuenta sobre un espectro aterrador que rondaba las llanuras donde yacen los túmulos de Hombres muertos hace mucho tiempo. El rostro de ese terrible rey despertó en Zarzagruño un miedo primigenio, y no pudo sacudirse la locura que se apoderó de él.\
\
Con un resoplido agradecido, Zarzagruño se da la vuelta y se interna de nuevo entre los árboles.","Ves algo en el ojo de la criatura que te hace dudar","'¿Qué es, qué es? No puedo soportarlo... ¿es el oso?\
\
'¡No! ¡No me digas!'","Derrota al gran oso","Clothar Hojarena te ha llevado al Bosque Viejo en busca del oso gigante que tanto lo aterrorizó.","Te encontraste con un ciervo nervioso en el Bosque Viejo y supiste que hay un depredador cerca. ¿Podría ser el oso gigante con el que se topó Clothar Hojarena?","Has aprendido el nombre del gran oso, Zarzagruño, y que algún mal ha infundido en la criatura un miedo grande y terrible, llevándola a un estado de frenesí.","Habla con Clothar en el Bosque Viejo","Enfréntate al gran oso, pero no lo mates","Instancia: El lenguaje de los animales","'¡Sabía que había algo peculiar en ti, ${PLAYER}! Después de todo, no cualquiera puede hablar con los animales. ¡Tú... tú eres ${PLAYER:una[f]|un[m]} cambiaformas! ¡No solo son historias... también escorias, como decía mi viejo padre! ¡No puedo creer que de verdad exista gente como tú en este mundo!\
\
Por un momento, Clothar parece a punto de desmayarse, pero luego se recompone y extiende la mano.\
\
'Sería un honor estrechar tu mano, . Debe de haber muy poca gente como tú en este mundo. Es una lástima, porque podrías haber matado a ese oso y elegiste no hacerlo. En cambio, mostraste contención y misericordia. ¡Este mundo necesitaría más gente como tú, si este hobbit tiene voz!'","Habla con la criatura recién llegada en la lengua de los animales","Salva a Zarzagruño","Ahora estás seguro: el miedo se refleja en los ojos del oso","Habla con Zarzagruño en la lengua de su especie","¡Has encontrado al oso que amenazó a Clothar y lo llenó de miedo!","Tu ancestro Beorn tenía un vínculo especial con las criaturas que vivían cerca de su morada, y tú también has heredado parte de esa cualidad.\
\
Intentas recurrir a ese aspecto de tu naturaleza para calmar a la poderosa bestia que tienes delante. ¿Qué ha llevado a esta criatura a semejante furia?\
\
Parece que tus palabras surten efecto, pero de repente la criatura sacude su enorme cabeza y redobla su ataque.","Clothar Hojarena se encuentra en el Bosque Viejo y no está nada contento con ello.","'Te oí, ${PLAYER}, ¡y ese ciervo también! Y no en el sentido de hablarle a los conejos que rondan un jardín para ahuyentarlos con la voz. Lo que sea que le dijiste a ese ciervo, te entendió, ¡igual que yo!\
\
'¿Cómo aprendiste la lengua de los animales?'","Has visto miedo en los ojos del gran oso y ahora estás seguro: algo contrario a su naturaleza ha empujado a esta criatura a atacar.","Habla con el gran oso en la lengua de su especie","El oso es enorme y parece dominado por la furia, pero aun así ves algo en su mirada que te hace dudar."},
[7352]={"Madre de la prole de cristal derrotada","Rescatar enanos envueltos en capullos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instancia: El nido de arañas","¡Una cría voraz ha devorado a uno de los enanos!","Una cría voraz ha salido del nido...","<rgb=#FF0000>Enanos devorados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>","Usa la forja antigua para potenciar tu adamantita infusa.","Derrota a la madre de la prole de cristal","Debes rescatar a los enanos envueltos en capullos dentro de la antigua armería antes de que sean devorados por las crías voraces del nido.","Enanos envueltos en capullos rescatados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Usa el yunque antiguo","Has creado una adamantita potenciada","Se te ha pedido que rescates a la expedición de enanos que ha sido capturada dentro de la antigua armería antes de que sean devorados por las viles arañas que han tejido un gran nido en su interior. Si tienes éxito, tienes la bendición del Pueblo de Durin para hacer uso del yunque que hay allí para potenciar la adamantita infusa que llevas."},
[7353]={"Mira desde el lado de babor del Saervig y busca la Corona de Durin","'Creo que es hora de que naveguemos de regreso a Mekhem-bizru, ${PLAYER}.'","Byrski Proadura ha navegado el Saervig hasta el Lago Espejo.\
\
Has buscado la Corona de Durin en varios lugares, pero tu búsqueda no ha tenido éxito. Debes hablar con Byrski Proadura.","'¿Nada? ¿Sin suerte en absoluto?'\
\
Byrski suspira.\
\
'Esperaba que fuera más fácil que esto, mi amigo. Echaré un último vistazo y luego podremos navegar de regreso a Mekhem-bizru. ¡No quiero decepcionar a la Guarición de Hierro!'","Has sido envuelto en una luz blanca y brillante, y aunque no puedes identificar su origen, su calidez eleva tu espíritu.","El destello que Byrski vio puede encontrarse en el lado de estribor del Saervig, más cerca de la proa.\
\
Byrski Proadura te ha pedido buscar el destello que vio en el Lago Espejo y decirle si también crees que es la Corona de Durin.","Babor se encuentra en el lado izquierdo de un barco cuando se mira hacia la proa.\
\
Byrski Proadura te ha pedido mirar hacia el lado de babor del Saervig y buscar la Corona de Durin.","La proa se encuentra en la parte frontal del Saervig.\
\
Byrski Proadura te ha pedido mirar desde la proa del Saervig y buscar la Corona de Durin.","Instancia: El Favor de las Estrellas","Ves muchas estrellas en el Lago Espejo, pero no la Corona de Durin","'¡! ¿Estás bien?\
\
Estabas mirando hacia el Lago Espejo y luego me pareció que te quedaste perdido en una profunda ensoñación. ¿Es algo común? No quiero alarmarte, ¡pero han pasado casi diez minutos! ¿Qué ocurrió? ¿Viste la Corona de Durin?'\
\
Le dices a Byrski que fuiste envuelto en una luz brillante, y que su calidez elevó tu espíritu y te dio un renovado sentido de propósito como ${PLAYERNAME:Marinero[m]|Marinera[f]}. Sugieres que podría haber sido la legendaria Estrella de Eärendil, aunque no estás ${PLAYERNAME:seguro[m]|segura[f]}.\
\
'¿La Estrella de Eärendil? Pensé que era solo un viejo cuento de marineros: una estrella guía para encontrar refugio en el Mar. ¡Y además, yo no vi ninguna luz! Puede que me falte un ojo, ¡pero creo que habría notado algo así! Quizá tus aventuras recientes te han agotado, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.\
\
'Ah, pero estoy... bastante seguro de que vi la Corona de Durin. Tenía el número adecuado de estrellas y parecía tener forma de corona, así que creo que nuestra expedición ha sido un éxito!'","Habla con Byrski Proadura","Byrski Proadura ha navegado el Saervig hasta el Lago Espejo.","Mira desde la proa del Saervig y busca la Corona de Durin","Cuando la luz se desvanece, ¡parece que Byrski ha estado tratando de llamar tu atención!","¡Cuando miras hacia el Lago Espejo, una luz brillante te envuelve!","¿Podría ser esta la luz de la Estrella de Eärendil?","La popa se encuentra en la parte trasera del Saervig.\
\
Byrski Proadura te ha pedido mirar desde la popa del Saervig y buscar la Corona de Durin.","'¡Ah, el Saervig es un buen barco. Y mira, el mismo Durin nos saluda!'\
\
Byrski se detiene un momento para mirar alrededor en las cubiertas del Saervig.\
\
'¡Muy bien! Comencemos nuestra búsqueda de la Corona de Durin, ${PLAYER}. Y recuerda, buscas siete estrellas con forma de corona. Yo empezaré por aquí, así que ¿por qué no miras desde babor?'","Estribor se encuentra en el lado derecho de un barco cuando se mira hacia la proa.\
\
Byrski Proadura te ha pedido mirar hacia el lado de estribor del Saervig y buscar la Corona de Durin.","Busca el destello en el Lago Espejo","Mira desde la popa del Saervig y busca la Corona de Durin","Byrski Proadura ha navegado el Saervig hasta el Lago Espejo.\
\
Has sido envuelto en una curiosa luz, pero Byrski parece preocupado. Debes hablar con Byrski Proadura.","Mira desde el lado de estribor del Saervig y busca la Corona de Durin","Byrski Proadura se ha ofrecido a buscar la Corona de Durin en el Lago Espejo, con la esperanza de que anuncie un final auspicioso para la reclamación de Khazad-dûm por parte de la Guarnición de Hierro."},
[7355]={"'The Orcs have unwittingly helped me, ${PLAYER}. During the battle, I had no thought at all for Wyrgende or her Curse.\
\
'I have made up my mind. I will not allow the Curse of Wyrgende to control my actions. I am my own man, Éomund's son, and I do not fear the memory of ill deeds done or vengeance sought! I will fight for the people of Rohan until I no longer can do so, and even then I will keep fighting!\
\
'I have given Wyrgende the time I thought she was due, and now I put the Stone behind me and will think of it no more! Onward, to Snowbourn! We are needed!'","Instancia: La Piedra de Wyrgende","Talk to Éomer by the Stone of Wyrgende","Orcs are attacking the area near Wyrgende's Stone!","Defeat Vale-scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Horn and Corudan are at Wyrgende's Stone.","You have come to the Stone of Wyrgende with Éomer, the nephew of King Théoden.","'The deeds of the past often have grave effects on the present, ${PLAYER}. Curses have power, and with the force of belief behind them they can become even more powerful. How else can the misfortune of Fengel's line be explained? And how will knowledge of the Curse affect Éomer's actions now?\
\
'The people of Rohan need him to be strong. He cannot cower in fear of Wyrgende's memory, or his people will suffer.'","Éomer has come to the Stone of Wyrgende, but you have not entirely divined his purpose for doing so.\
\
You should speak to Éomer to learn why he has come to this grim place before continuing on to Snowbourn.","'The Stone of Wyrgende is a place of great sorrow for the people of Rohan, and for its Kings.'","Éomer is at the Stone of Wyrgende.","Talk to Horn at the Stone of Wyrgende","'Oh my! I cannot concentrate during an Orc attack!'","'We are needed in Snowbourn! We will not delay!'","'It was thought for many years that Wyrgende's Curse had already expired. My uncle's father, Thengel, lived in Gondor, and the lords of Rohan called a witan and begged him to return to the Mark and take the throne. They said he was virtuous enough and would be such a good king that his reign was certain to end the curse; indeed, Thengel lived long, and his son Théoden now has many years behind him.\
\
'It seems now, with the death of Prince Théodred, that the Curse merely slumbered. Perhaps it did not affect Thengel or my uncle because they were already born, or because they were not in the Riddermark when it was set. None but Wyrgende can know, and she is long-dead.\
\
'The Curse that did not affect Thengel did affect his daughters, and few of their sons survived to reach adulthood.'","Defeated Vale-scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I had been so certain the Curse was broken, as had been all of Rohan. What must it be like to labour 'neath the shadow of such a thing, and never know when it will reveal its fangs?\
\
'If Éomer out of fear refuses to fight the evils that face our land, then King Fengel's greed will have struck the death-blow for Rohan.'","Talk to Corudan at the Stone of Wyrgende","'There it lies, ${PLAYER}: the Stone of Wyrgende. Do you know the tale?'\
\
Éomer seems surprised to hear that you have been told the tale of Wyrgende the Crone and King Fengel, but then realization dawns.\
\
'Ah, of course you would know it. How could you travel with a bard such as Horn and not know it? It is a popular tale, though it be grim and unpleasant. I expect it is true in all lands: the people enjoy stories that seem to explain their poor lot or continued hardship.'","Talk to Éomer at the Stone of Wyrgende"},
[7356]={"'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER}. Your work has been excellent and revealed many problems for me. That being said, I may have work for you in the near future.'","Instance: The Storm Abated","'I am glad that I have an avenue to gain my freedom, but saddened that this treachery was not enough to gain it. I understand the ruling and will abide by it.\
\
'Ragrekhûl is known to be a dreaded beast, I only hope that I may be capable of capturing the beast.'","Fight off the ambush awaiting you in Rothog's chambers.","Speak to Shaidal about his task.","Speak to Rothog the Storm and watch his reaction","Speak to Shaidal about his task","With the ambush survived, Rothog enters into the room","'${PLAYER}, these rabble! How dare they invade my quarters?! There will be swift vengeance upon those who would do such a thing. I will have my guards take the bodies and feed them to the lions.\
\
'Anyway, you had mentioned that you managed to gather information that might be of interest to me?'","Armed with proof of Shaidal's innocence, you approach Rothog the Storm with your findings.","Defeat ambushers"},
[7357]={"Talk to Iothete","Iothete is in his hut in the Whitshaws.\
\
You should speak with Iothete.","'I will tell you everything I remember, ${PLAYER}. You will wish me dead when you hear what I did to Wildermore.'","Listen to Iothete","An old man stands ahead","Instancia: La historia de una piedra extraña","'Yes... do come rest at my home. We can discuss whatever you'd like.'","Iothete's voice paints a picture in your mind of his walk on the fateful day a year or so ago.\
\
The woods of the Whitshaws feel very different than the bare white tines protruding from the snow today.","Follow Iothete","'And now you see what the stone has wrought? The cold came over our lands not long ago, and it was as unnatural as this stone that froze my home a year ago.\
\
'Is it my fault? Is it because I told him so much?'","Iothete remembers sitting for a long while with the old wanderer","Listen to Iothete's memory","'And that was when he placed the stone exactly where you found it. The cold came instantly! I was so afraid...'","Iothete is in the woods in the northern Whitshaws.\
\
You should speak with Iothete.","Listen to Iothete's tale","You should follow Iothete's memory into his home in Dunfast.","Iothete remembers being entranced by the old traveller at once","Iothete remembers walking in the green woods of the Whitshaws","The fragment of stone you recovered from Iothete's home has a story behind it, and you are ready to hear it.","Iothete is in the woods of the Whitshaws.\
\
You should speak with Iothete and listen to his memory of a fateful day.","'He wanted to know everything about Wildermore. I do not know why...'","Iothete concludes his tale:\
\
'The memory is strange, foggy, unsettling. I do not feel like I was there -- merely looking on from a distance while I spoke too much of things that do not concern strangers.\
\
'I told my neighbours, but they dismissed me as being mad. The stone terrified me. It made me cold.\
\
'So I left.\
\
'Now it is cold everywhere, and it is my fault.'"},
[7358]={"Mótsog continues his tale of the Sunder-battle.","Climb the stairs to Biriz-zahar","'But an army cannot remain silent for long, and when Ragna's warriors reached the upper levels of the city, my warriors were made aware of their presence. They raced to engage the interlopers.'","Talk to Mótsog atop Biriz-zahar","Mótsog's tale is nearly complete.","Follow Ragna the Fierce through the burning city","Talk to Mótsog and hear his tale","'It was Ragna the Fierce, Durin's queen, who led them in secret across the river and to the base of Biriz-zahar. She was a mighty warrior and had slain Orc and Greymaul alike during the war, but now she found the gates of my city unguarded; too many of my folk desired to be present at Durin's defeat.\
\
'So it was that Ragna and her army entered the city unopposed. They found a stair to the heights and began to climb.'","The words of Mótsog have painted the picture of a dwarf woman who will stop at nothing to rescue her husband and king. You can almost see her striding through the burning streets of Biriz-zahar, calling for Durin to answer her, as Mótsog's voice fades. The heat of the flames feels so real.","Mótsog has brought his tale near to its conclusion.","'Durin was brought in chains to the very summit of Biriz-zahar, where my people and their Orc-allies gathered to see the fallen king and make mock of him.\
\
'He suffered their taunting and their jests for many an hour, but I could see no sign of despair upon his face. I noted it even then.'","Instancia: La batalla de la Separación","Ragna the Fierce renewed her attempt to rescue her husband and king.","The army led by Ragna the Fierce climbed the unguarded stairs to the high places of Biriz-zahar.","'Despite the danger and the foes arrayed before her, Ragna the Fierce did reach the high places of Biriz-zahar, and she freed her husband and king from his bondage. But that was not enough for victory.\
\
'Durin picked up a fallen blade and joined the battle, but the Orcs were too many and the dwarves too divided; the Longbeards feared to present their backs to the Greymauls lest their foes take advantage of their distraction, and the Greymauls feared the same of the Longbeards. By the time Ragna freed Durin, two thirds of the dwarves had perished to flame and black steel. Sauron and his master, watching from afar, delighted in the carnage: the Orcs would win the day, and no dwarf would leave Biriz-zahar alive.'","Hear the tale of Mótsog","Mótsog speaks of Sauron's betrayal of the Greymauls, and of Ragna's race through the blood-drenched city of Biriz-zahar.","'Morgoth and his lieutenant Sauron had not been idle during the ten years of conflict between the dwarf clans. In secret they devised a plan by which Longbeard and Greymaul alike might be destroyed, and the dwarves swept entirely from Middle-earth.\
\
'And so it was that while Longbeard and Greymaul battled in the heights of my golden city, Sauron watched from afar. With malice afire in his heart, Morgoth's cruel servant sent a preordained signal to his legions.'"},
[7359]={"'The fine weather of our departure did not last,' Gandalf reads solemnly","Move through the twisting passage to another of the Halls of Memory","Talk to Gandalf in the Grey Mountains as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Approach the band of adventurers in the tavern depicted by the Halls of Memory","Talk to Gandalf in the Minas Anor tavern depicted by the Halls of Memory","Talk to Gandalf in Durthang as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Vóin and his companions met at a tavern in Minas Anor one night, and planned a dangerous excursion.","Further information about Vóin's journey to Gondor as one of Eärnur's boon companions lies beyond the Grey Mountains, in the Halls of Memory.","Listen to the conclusion of Eärnur's doomed adventure within Durthang","'For three years, Vóin and his new companions adventured the length and breadth of the Grey Mountains and the northern reaches of the Misty Mountains, hunting down the remaining vestiges of Angmar and bringing battle to the evils dwelling in Gundabad. Never did they know defeat, and their triumphs emboldened Prince Eärnur.\
\
'He remembered a promise he had made years before. Intent on seeing it fulfilled, he invited his companions to make the southward journey to his home, to Gondor. They would stay for a time in Minas Anor, as his city was then called, and plan the occasion of their next victories.'","'Yes, I believe it may have been the Merry Swan,' Gandalf muses, stroking his beard","Gandalf is in Durthang, as depicted by the Halls of Memory.","Gandalf's study of the Black Book has revealed an excursion by Eärnur and his companions to recapture the fortress of Durthang, in Gorgoroth.","Listen to the account of Vóin and his friends at the tavern depicted by the Halls of Memory","'The adventurers knew they could not reclaim the fortress without first slaying Ugrukhôr, but for as long as he eluded them Durthang would remain the property of Mordor. Their spirits low, they resolved to leave.\
\
'And that, Vóin tells us, is when they felt a new presence upon the battlements.'","Return to the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","Gandalf has continued his study of the Black Book of Mordor.","'When last we left Vóin and his companions, they adventured in the Grey Mountains. Let us turn our attention to the Ered Mithrin, and pick up the thread of that tale.'","Gandalf speaks to you of the discoveries he made while studying the Black Book.","Move through the twisting passage until you reach another of the Halls of Memory","'Their experience in Mordor was bleak. To hear Vóin tell it, nothing went right for them once they passed into that land. The fortress that was once called Durthand became far more inhospitable with its transformation into Durthang; it was more well-defended than the adventurers expected, and they faced strong opposition from the very beginning. Silmahtar soon changed his opinion of their fortunes, receiving a leg-wound that caused him a great deal of pain and put a limp in his step.\
\
'They found no sign of Ugrukhôr within the fortress, and as their dream of slaying the Captain of the Pit faded, tempers in the fellowship ran hot. Eärnur dulled his sword on the thick hide of a mountain troll, and with each combat the blade weakened further. At last it snapped, and the prince of Gondor was left weaponless.'","'It was in the Grey Mountains that Vóin's path entwined with that of Prince Eärnur,' Gandalf reads","Listen to the account of Eärnur's doomed adventure within Durthang","Gandalf wishes to resume the tale of Vóin in the Grey Mountains as they are depicted by the Halls of Memory.","Gandalf is in the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory.","'The plans were made, and they were kept secret from all but Eärnur's band. Even his father the king did not know what they intended.\
\
'Vóin says this of their departure: \\qPleasant weather, few clouds. Warm, but not uncomfortable. Left the city without incident. Silmahtar thinks so highly of our chances that he believes the prince will be made king upon our successful return.\\q'\
\
Gandalf frowns.\
\
'It was not to be so, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Gandalf in the Halls of Memory","Instancia: La Espada y la Doncella de Piedra","'And so the survivors of Eärnur's band returned to Minas Anor, defeated and mourning the loss of their friend. Silmahtar's hopes as they set forth did not come to pass; indeed, King Eärnil was more wroth than they had ever seen, and he forbade his son from leaving the city without his consent. To Vóin's eyes, the prince was made a prisoner, and every day the flame of Eärnur's rage grew hotter still.\
\
'Eärnur met with Vóin and his knights in secret to weave elaborate plots of revenge against those he blamed for the death of Magoldir: Urudanî Stonemaiden for the deed itself, and Ugrukhôr for his absence at Durthang. \\qIf he had been there,\\q Vóin writes, \\qthe whole adventure would have gone differently. The prince is sure of it.\\q'\
\
Gandalf strokes his beard.\
\
'I see in this account much that is familiar, ${PLAYER}. No, not the deeds themselves, for I have never seen any record of this doomed expedition to reclaim Durthang in the texts of Gondor. What I find familiar is this description of Eärnur, son of King Eärnil II. Even the known records of his disposition describe Eärnur in life as bold, brash, and reckless. I wonder if he remained so as Mordirith, and now as Gothmog?\
\
'That is enough for now, my friend. And Faramir! I trust you paid attention as well? These are matters that concern you closely, for this foe now lurks upon the very edge of your lands, and in a city that will demand your protection and that of your king, once it is retaken!'","'Vóin does not record the name of the tavern. Might it have been the Merry Swan?'","Gandalf is in the tavern depicted by the Halls of Memory."},
[7360]={"Let the events transpire.","You should run after Tolwin so that you may speak with him.","There is a bear trap on the slain body.\
\
You should examine the bear trap.","There are footprints around the slain body.\
\
You should examine foot prints.","You see another Sûhalar and by the looks of him, slain not long ago","Investigate the slain Sûhalar","Examine the foot prints","These fresh foot prints are very small. Too small for a man.","Tolwin looks glum as he starts to tell his tale","Nearby is another slain body.\
\
You should investigate the slain Sûhalar.","The slain body of a Sûhalar leads you on the trail of a mysterious Sûhalar slayer.","'Now I search for my mother who I have not seen since that dreadful day. I fear the worst but I will not give up searching for her until I know for certain her fate.\
\
'A few of us who survived the invasion have taken shelter in the small village of Crithost. They are mostly farmers and a few soldiers from Cair Andros. We should head there at once as Crithost is in need of help.'","This trap looks new and was recently constructed","'You are no Easterling after all. I am sorry for leading you on a chase. \
\
'My name is Tolwin. My father was in command of Cair Andros when it was taken from us by invaders. Much has led me to where I stand now...'","Instancia: La historia de Tolwin","The Sûhalar slayer must be nearby.\
\
You should search nearby for more signs of conflict.","Let the events transpire","You noticed the Sûhalar was caught in a bear trap","You should speak with Tolwin.","Examine the bear trap","Run after Tolwin so that you may speak with him","Let Tolwin tell his story.","Search nearby for another sign of this Sûhalar slayer","Let Tolwin tell his story","Speak with Tolwin","'Meet me at Crithost. There are people there that need your help.'"},
[7361]={"Talk to Léothred","Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, seeks to learn more of his people history in Misthallow.","'And that is the end of Eorl's tale.'","Listen to Léothred's tale","'Eorl, with bow in hand, ran into the woods....'","'Where before, the lords of the Éothéod, even mighty Léod, had sought to break the mearas, Eorl had treated his father’s animal as a friend and it had met him in kind.'","Talk to Léothred.","Listen to Léothred's tale.","Instancia: La doma de los Mearas"},
[7362]={"Instancia: Los lazos que unen","'¿Qué hace Kaj aquí, Sivullinen?\
\
'Olvídalo. ¡No hay tiempo! ¡Esa cosa se ha vuelto salvaje y hay que domarla!'","Habla con Pinja","Impide que los hermanos de Pinja interrumpan el ritual","'¿Quién eres? ¿Qué haces aquí?\
\
'¿Ese fanfarrón de Kaj? No merece a Pinja, ¡y me da igual que sea el hijo del jefe!\
\
'Apártate de nuestro camino. ¡Le daremos una lección que no olvidará en mucho tiempo! ¡Si intentas detenernos, la recibirás tú en su lugar!'","Pinja tiene tres hermanos. Asegúrate de que no interrumpan el ritual de Kaj.","Habla con Kaj.","Doma al mamut","El mamut ha sido domado","Habla con Manu","Impide que los hermanos de Pinja interrumpan a Kaj","'Creo que a partir de aquí podremos encargarnos de este asunto.'","Doma al mamut y protege a Pinja","La valentía de Kaj parece haber impresionado a Pinja","'¿Había un viejo ritual con el que Kaj pensaba conquistar mi corazón? Qué considerado por su parte. Siempre me han interesado las viejas costumbres. Pero ha encontrado una aún más antigua, una hazaña de valentía que ha impresionado incluso a mis tres hermanos. ¡Jamás creí que algo así fuera posible!\
\
'Oh, habrá boda. Kaj ya no puede echarse atrás, y si lo intenta descubrirá que el mamut no es nada comparado con mi desagrado. Tendremos que encontrar algo que hacer con nuestra nueva mascota mamut durante la ceremonia... ¿quizá llevar a los niños a dar una vuelta?\
\
'Gracias por tu intervención en todo esto. Podemos ocuparnos del resto nosotros mismos, aunque puede que vuelva a pedirte ayuda con algunas de las cosas que necesitaré para la boda.'","Calma al mamut y evita que se desboque","Manu reclama tu atención.","'Eres ${PLAYERNAME:afortunado[m]|afortunada[f]} de poder presenciar este ritual; pocos Sivullinen llegan a verlo. Ha... bueno, caído en desuso en tiempos recientes.\
\
'Solo necesito preparar las cosas con estos componentes.\
\
'Haz todo lo que esté en tu mano para que esto se desarrolle sin contratiempos. Puede que algunas personas se opongan a este ritual, ¡pero nadie resultará herido! Te lo prometo.'","'Ya veo lo que ocurre aquí, ${PLAYERNAME:forastero[m]|forastera[f]}. Has venido a ayudar a Kaj a raptar a mi hermana. Muchos otros lo han intentado, y mis hermanos y yo siempre les hemos demostrado que eran demasiado débiles para casarse con ella. Y, sin embargo, solo tú y Kaj os habéis plantado con valentía ante este mamut indómito...\
\
'Si deseas unirte a nuestra familia por matrimonio... pero no, veo que Kaj ha logrado robar algo de Pinja antes de que tú tuvieras ocasión. Se ha llevado su corazón, de alguna manera. Bah.\
\
'Tal vez acabemos apreciándolo, pese a sus costumbres anticuadas. Es al menos parcialmente responsable de haber domado a este mamut, y eso no es poca cosa... ¡es una cosa mamútica! Perdona mi broma, Sivullinen.'","Kaj quiere que lo protejas mientras invoca un ritual lossoth ya en desuso.","Manu ha regresado arrastrando a un mamut salvaje.\
\
Deberías ayudar a calmar a la bestia."},
[7363]={"Klúso is ready to describe what he saw earlier.\
\
You should talk to Klúso.","Follow Klúso","'It wasn't long after that the hobgoblins and Orcs started fighting. I think they're still fighting right now!'","Talk to Klúso","'I was scouting near Bazan-medan, the gate to the Clovengap, when I heard the stomping of many heavy feet.'","Klúso is describing what he saw transpire between the hobgoblins and ice-giants.\
\
You should follow the hobgoblins to listen to the conversation.","Klúso begins to conclude his story...","Listen to the conversation","Klúso is describing what he saw transpire between the hobgoblins and ice-giants.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","Klúso is concluding his story.\
\
You should return to him.","Klúso is describing what he saw transpire between the hobgoblins and ice-giants.\
\
You should follow Klúso.","Return to Klúso","Instancia: El punto de inflexión","Scout Klúso has an interesting report to share: relations between the Orcs and hobgoblins may have finally reached a tipping point....","Follow the hobgoblins to listen to the conversation"},
[7364]={"Encuentra el Silithar","'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! Has hecho un gran esfuerzo al adentrarte tanto en las tinieblas, ¡pero el Silithar ya no está aquí!\
\
'¡Escúchame bien y te diré dónde se encuentra ahora!'","'Abandonemos este lugar, ${PLAYER}. El Silithar debe llegar a la superficie de forma segura, y me gustaría hablar con Calenglad antes de volver a mi hogar.'","'¡Has hecho un gran trabajo al derrotar a Nornagol, ${PLAYER}! He tomado el Silithar y lo he entregado a Calenglad. ¡Vuelve con él y comparte con él el relato de tu aventura!\
\
'Te enseñaré el camino a la superficie a través de senderos ocultos.'","Has viajado hasta la Tumba de Elendil en busca del Silithar necesario para reforjar Narsil.","El Silithar está en algún lugar de las cavernas bajo la tumba de Elendil.\
\
No has encontrado el Silithar en la última cámara de la tumba de Elendil... debe haber sido arrastrado a otro lugar cuando las aguas se retiraron.","Instancia: La tumba de Elendil","Gwindeth ha venido a la tumba de Elendil, y está esperando para hablar contigo en su cámara más profunda.\
\
Te has encargado de Idella Abrecriptas, pero no hay signos del Silithar.","Idella Abrecriptas está en algún lugar de las profundidades de la tumba de Elendil.\
\
Calenglad tenía razón... La banda de saqueadores de tumbas de Idella Abrecriptas ha aprovechado la ventaja de las recién retiradas aguas para sondear las profundidades de la tumba en busca de tesoros. Debe ser detenida.","Gwindeth está ahora en la cueva bajo la tumba de Elendil.\
\
Has recuperado el Silithar, y Gwindeth espera para hablar contigo."},
[7365]={"Recover a crude key from the guards","Release the first captive.","Discover and open a locked cell with the crude key that you recovered.","The Houndmaster Laodegan has heard that an outsider has attacked the dungeon and is guarding the entrance.","Within the depths of this cavern, several of the Uch-lûth clansmen and women have been locked away in cages awaiting a grisly fate.","Release the first captive","Unlock the cell door for a prisoner","Unlocked the cell door for the last prisoner","'Thank you for dispatching these filthy creatures. I was taken several weeks ago, and I thought that I would never escape. Thank you and may the blessing of the Uch-gwirod be with you.'","Defeat Laodegan near the entrance","Seek out guards within the cavern and recover a crude key from them.","Free the second captive","'I do not care how you came upon this place, Duvodiad; however, your generosity shall be rewarded. May your ancestors find peace and your heirs be hearty and strong.'","Release the last captive.","Recovered a crude key","Defeated Laodegan near the entrance","Freed the second captive","Release the last captive","Recovered a crude key from the guards","Released the first captive","Instance:  The Trail Ends","Unlock the cell door for the last prisoner","Thank you for dispatching these filthy creatures. I was taken several weeks ago, and I thought that I would never escape. Thank you and may the blessing of the Uch-gwirod be with you.'","Release the second captive.","Released the last captive","Unlocked the cell door for a prisoner","'These duhirun attacked our hunting-party several days ago. Sadly, I have heard the screams of friends being dragged out of the cavern to a grim fate.'"},
[7366]={"Utiliza la forja ancestral para potenciar tu granate infundido","¡Has creado un granate potenciado!","Instancia: La Sala de Entrenamiento","Una disciplinada hueste de orcos de Moria se ha asentado en una de las antiguas salas de armería y la está utilizando como sala de entrenamiento en preparación para su próxima ofensiva contra los enanos. Si quieres llegar a la vieja forja de armas que alberga dicha sala y potenciar el granate infundido que llevas contigo, tendrás que abrirte paso a la fuerza entre los orcos.","Debes derrotar a los reclutas orcos antes de que estén listos para lanzar su ofensiva contra los enanos, y abatir al uruk que supervisa su entrenamiento.","¡Reclutas orcos derrotados!(${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los reclutas orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Usa el yunque antiguo","¡Maestro de batalla uruk derrotado!","Derrota al maestro de batalla uruk"},
[7368]={"'${PLAYER}, are you alight?! What is wrong?!'","For those reclaiming Minas Ithil from the grasp of darkness, a trial of madness has begun.","Overcome the Trial of Madness.","Overcome the Trial of Madness","Find the artifact","Destroy the Orb of Madness","You have survived the Trial of Madness and successfully destroyed the artifact!","Find the artifact.","Instancia: La prueba de la locura","A strange haze clouds your vision!","Destroy the Orb of Madness."},
[7370]={"Watch events unfold","Náin wishes to speak with you.","Habla con Náin","Troops sent out to war (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should continue observing the interrogation.","You should defeat the hobgoblin raiders.","Fill weapon barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Gorgar would leave us to die and his generals would execute us for deserting. Right then I knew. Didn't matter if I was fighting hobgoblins, dwarves, or my own people -- if I kept fighting for Gorgar, I'd find myself bleeding out one day.\
\
'After we lost the war in Elderslade, I'd hoped for a rebellion but, well... fear is a useful tool for dividing people.'","Return to Shúkurz and listen to his story","Weapon barrels filled (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Féli is waiting for you before he starts the interrogation.","Defeat the hobgoblin raiders","The time has come to interrogate the Orc prisoner.","You should talk to the Orc captain.","Talk to Féli","Deliver orders to Orc soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'That's why I want to leave. Far as I'm concerned, there's only death left for me if I stay in Gundabad.\
\
'I-I mean no harm, honest.'","Talk to Shúkurz","You should follow Féli to the interrogation and see what happens.","Instancia: La verdad del asunto","'Come, let us continue talking.'","There are empty weapon barrels and Orc soldiers waiting on orders throughout the camp.\
\
You should fill the barrels and deliver orders.","Listen to the interrogation","You should watch the events before you unfold.","Talk to the Orc captain","'You! Quit standing around like a limp worm! Don't you know we're about to go to war?\
\
'Fill up the barrels 'round camp with weapons and deliver these orders to soldiers. Make it quick!'","'I've been told that ever since Bolg rallied folks to Erebor, things have gone downhill for us. Still, we didn't have outright war for a while; we were just surviving. Suppose you could call it a sort of peace.'","'But peace never lasts, not for us. Mordor came calling, and Gorgar answered.'","You should continue interrogating Shúkurz.","'Be wary, my friend, for the Orc speaks poisoned words. What does his kind care for other than destruction and slaughter? I've been faced with many a difficult choice throughout the years, but this situation is simple enough to understand.\
\
'Still, I was... wrong to pull out the Black Mattock. The Orc may be luring us into a trap, but Féli is right. If there truly are dwarves to be saved, then we cannot leave them to their fates.'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. It's unpleasant business, but it helps to have another person who isn't as openly hostile. I have worked with Lord Náin for years and respect him in the utmost, but sometimes his distrust can lead to tricky situations.\
\
'Even if we aim to defeat Gorgar, we are woefully unprepared. We need more information before we can act -- not just about Gorgar's location, but also those closest to him. And what of the hobgoblins? Where does the power truly lie? I do not know how quickly we'll find these answers. But acting rashly won't get us far, either.\
\
'As it stands right now, this Orc -- Shúkurz -- knows more than we do currently. It would be prudent to give him the benefit of the doubt and proceed cautiously.'","You should return to Shúkurz and continue listening to his story.","'The end of the war brought trouble. Wasn't long before the hobgoblins came down from the north to overthrow Gorgar and claim Gundabad for themselves.\
\
''Course, I don't need to tell you the end of that story, do I?'"},
[7371]={"Ramalarga se ha unido a ti en la batalla para destruir tanto a Putrecorazones como al ucorno conocido como el Corazón Retorcido.","Habla con Ramalarga","'¡Bien peleado! ¡Hoom! El Corazón Retorcido ha sido arrancado de raíz, y la Putrecorazones destruida. Su corrupción no se extenderá más.'","'¡Ta-rum! Tenemos mucho trabajo que hacer aquí. ¡Sígueme!'","'Con el tiempo este bosque volverá a ser lo que era, pero la curación llevará tiempo.\
\
'Vámonos de este lugar oscuro, ¿te parece?'","Debes hablar con Ramalarga y ayudarlo contra el Corazón Retorcido.","La Arboleda Retorcida ha sido purificada","Debes hablar con Ramalarga.","Instancia: El Corazón Retorcido"},
[7372]={"Legolas está esperando para hablar contigo\
\
Tú y Legolas del Bosque Negro habéis seguido las huellas de los trolls silvanos a través de la naturaleza salvaje del Bosque de los Trolls.","Legolas es amenazado por trolls silvanos que atacan en el Gladdalf.\
\
Tú y Legolas del Bosque Negro habéis seguido las huellas de los trolls silvanos a través de la naturaleza salvaje del Bosque de los Trolls.","Legolas es amenazado por hordas de arrastreros corrompidos en el Gladdalf.\
\
Tú y Legolas del Bosque Negro habéis seguido las huellas de los trolls silvanos a través de la naturaleza salvaje del Bosque de los Trolls.","Legolas ha guiado el camino hacia lo profundo del Gladdalf, un rincón remoto del Bosque de los Trolls, siguiendo el rastro de los trolls silvanos.","'Supe en el mismo instante en que derrotaste al Invocador del Pantano, ${PLAYER}, pues su control sobre las criaturas de la marisma se desvaneció de repente.\
\
'Aún queda algo en el Gladdalf, pues el mal que corrompe este lugar no desapareció con tu victoria sobre el troll silvano que nos enfrentó.\
\
'Hay algo más detrás de esta desgracia.'","'Yo también estoy listo para continuar. El Gladdalf fue un lugar de paz en días pasados, pero ahora es un cubil de maldad, y me alegraré de dejarlo atrás.'","'La tierra gime bajo la pisada del mal, ${PLAYER}. Hay trolls silvanos cerca.'","'¡Ven ahora...! Alguna bestia convoca a los arrastreros del pantano. Debemos acabar con esta criatura si queremos seguir las huellas a través del Gladdalf.'","Habla con Legolas.","'Si estás listo para regresar a Imladris, iré contigo. Debemos informar lo que ha sucedido aquí, aunque las noticias sean sombrías.'","'Estas huellas son inusuales, ${PLAYER}. Que son las pisadas de trolls silvanos no puede negarse, pero son demasiado grandes incluso para aquellos de su especie que a veces merodean en el sur del Bosque Negro.\
\
'Entremos en el Gladdalf, pero con cautela. Es seguro que hallaremos a los trolls dentro.\
\
'¡Permanece alerta! Los trolls silvanos no se habrían organizado lo suficiente como para ejercer influencia sin ayuda, y aún queda un Nazgûl en estas tierras.'","Legolas sigue un rastro misterioso hacia el Gladdalf.\
\
Tú y Legolas del Bosque Negro habéis seguido las huellas de los trolls silvanos a través de la naturaleza salvaje del Bosque de los Trolls.","'El Nazgûl desapareció de mi vista, pero no partió de inmediato. La leyenda cuenta que uno de los Espectros del Anillo fue un rey oriental con gran habilidad para rastrear y moverse en sigilo... solo el temor que pesaba fuertemente sobre mi corazón delataba su presencia. Ahora eso ha desaparecido, pero el recuerdo permanece oscuro.\
\
'Es bueno que derrotaras a Taushakh, pues el Nazgûl le había otorgado cierto poder con el que podía reunir a los trolls silvanos. ¡En gran número, podrían haber amenazado a Imladris misma! Individualmente, son una amenaza mucho menor.\
\
'Debemos regresar, ${PLAYER}. El Gladdalf se vuelve frío y triste.'","Ayuda a Legolas.","Instancia: El sendero sin marcas","Legolas ha seguido un rastro misterioso hasta un montículo de tierra rodeado de agua en el centro del Gladdalf.\
\
Tú y Legolas el Elfo habéis seguido las huellas de los trolls silvanos a través de la naturaleza salvaje del Bosque de los Trolls."},
[7373]={"Khilbakh has been defeated!","Talk to Vaskorn","Vaskorn has fallen!","'Quickly now, follow me. We attack!'","'We are victorious and Limlók remains safe, for now.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Vaskorn must survive</rgb>","Runerik Knotbeard fears an assault upon Limlók may be imminent.","Talk to Vaskorn.","Find and defeat Khilbakh","Instancia: Las tierras salvajes indómitas","Find and defeat Khilbakh and the Warg raiding party.","You have defeated the raiding party!","Defeat the raiding party"},
[7374]={"You found a ring containing keys to the cages in the Fleetfast gaol!","Belondor and Rothog have come to free you from the Fleetfast gaol.","'Sotóka is a fast ship, but the Song departed many hours before us. We may be too late to prevent Nakási from completing her mission.\
\
'She is driven by vengeance, ${PLAYER}: not just for the death of Tumúldo, but for every injury and injustice she has suffered during her years of life. Each of these wounds has fed her hatred, and now she has been blinded by her desire for vengeance.'\
\
Tatháta smiles grimly, a most rare sight indeed.\
\
'That is the meaning of \\qSotóka,\\q ${PLAYER}: Vengeance. Is it chance or plan that speeds us in pursuit of Nakási aboard a ship of vengeance? I cannot say. The world is a curious place.'","Talk to Rothog in the ship Sotóka","Talk to Jajax in the ship Sotóka","There is a commotion outside the cage in the Fleetfast gaol.","Talk to Tatháta in her ship Sotóka","'Sirgon has been upon my mind these last few hours, ${PLAYER}. What would he say to know that now I sail to his home of Gondor in a desperate bid to defend it from destruction?\
\
'Ah, I know the answer. He would smile and clap me upon the back, and say he would do the same for my own home. What do Gondor and Umbar have in common? Sons and daughters who would die for them, against any threatening danger.'","'Did he say DAXAMAT leads the uprising against the Kindred? My brother Daxamat? There has not been some misunderstanding? My brother is one who follows, not one who leads! I am the one who leads!\
\
'I know I said we should put our faith in Dax, ${PLAYER}, but I did not expect something like this! We had better go. I have to see it before I will believe it!'","Talk to Tatháta in the Fleetfast gaol","'I am sad, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
You ask Rothog why he is sad, and he grumbles something you cannot hear. When you ask him to repeat it, he heaves a heavy sigh.\
\
'I did not think to bring Húrshauk with me when we came to rescue you from the gaol, and Tatháta says there is no time for me to go get him. Now he must stay behind in the city instead of joining the battle in Gondor.\
\
'He will miss all of the fighting! Perhaps one of the members of Ilma-ghôli will bring him to Dâr Laja to slay Hármelak or Khôltekh? He would like that. Oh, I hope they do!'","Tatháta stands by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh.","Make your way to the hidden harbour","Talk to Belondor in the Fleetfast gaol","Your foes now defeated, the way to the hidden harbour is open to you.","After travelling for a short distance, you hear the sound of foes ahead of you","You and Jajax have escaped from the gaol, but there are foes between you and the hidden harbour.","Pursue the Song to Gondor","Board Tatháta's ship and go belowdecks","Descend into Umbar-môkh","Permanece alerta","'The Kindred of the Coins is dead, ${PLAYER}. It was created to protect the people of the city, not to burn them alive as did the Church of Barkhûsh. If the Umbari do not slay Hármelak and Khôltekh for their betrayal, I will do it myself.\
\
'Below the city I witnessed Belondor and Rothog travelling with great speed, and pursued them. Had they supported Hármelak's treachery they would be dead already, but it seems these two have not abandoned their wits.\
\
'We are to bring you by paths beneath the city to the hideout where the uprising began. Are you ready?'\
\
You hesitate. Images of thatched Gondorian cottages wreathed by blue flame flash before your eyes, followed by homes in the Umbari style suffering the same fate. You remember a small voice asking you to destroy the ships and their masters.","Tatháta eyes you carefully","Jajax is in the Fleetfast gaol.","Jajax is in one of the cages of the Fleetfast gaol.","Tatháta's ship Sotóka is moored in the hidden harbour","Tatháta and Jajax stand by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh","Belondor stands by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh.","The path of your escape leads into Umbar-môkh.","Your pursuit of the Song begins.","Search the bodies of the slain guards for the keys to the gaol","Make your way downstairs to the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh","This guard does not have the keys to the gaol","'I wonder if Gondor has already been defeated, ${PLAYER}? It is difficult to tell the passage of time from down here, but if the weapons of the Song are as dangerous as you say, it will not take long for Nakási to complete her mission.'","'Ah, this is more like it. I have always been more at home aboard a ship, even if that ship carries me to dangerous battle in defence of Gondor, of all places! At least the legend of Jajax will continue to grow!\
\
'We will leave the uprising against Hármelak and Khôltekh in Daxamat's capable hands. Ha! Capable? There is a first time for everything, I suppose.\
\
'I hope we are not making a grave mistake, ${PLAYER}!'","'My ship Sotóka is moored in a hidden harbour not far from here, ${PLAYER}, and none can match her speed when her sails are full.'\
\
You ask Tatháta if she would be willing to pursue the Song of Waves and Wind to Gondor, despite the danger, and she stares at you seriously.\
\
'On my last voyage with Nakási, we sailed around the coast of Outer Gondor. Our purpose was to prove to the new King of Gondor that despite the defeat of Umbar in the war, the Kindred of the Coins was not without strength. Umbar would not be subservient; Umbar must be treated as a powerful neighbour, worthy of respect.\
\
'But then Tumúldo was slain, and the light in Nakási's eyes changed. Hatred drove her. We encountered the grove of a tree-tender on the cape of Anfalas. Later I learned from Nestinanessornë that his name, at least in the tongue used by Elves and Men, was Leafshade. Nakási threatened to burn his grove as a message to Gondor, and I told her I wanted no part of it... but had Nestinanessornë not surrendered to her I know she would have burned that grove with fire and torches, and all of Gondor beside.\
\
'Now she possesses the ability to do just that, ${PLAYER}. If my ship Sotóka can stop her, I cannot remain idly by and claim to have not aided her. For Leafshade, if not for any others, my ship is yours. Agents of Khôltekh and the Heirsworn stand between you and the hidden harbour. I hope you are ready.'","'The hidden harbour is just ahead. We must cut through these foes if we are to reach Tatháta's ship!'","'What is the cause for this delay, ${PLAYER}? The city above is a tinder-box ready to catch fire at the slightest spark, and Ilma-ghôli cannot now be stopped.'\
\
You tell Belondor that you fear for the people of Gondor, unaware of the deadly danger that sails toward them, and for the people of Umbar. He nods.\
\
'It had occurred to me that Nakási will not give up this fleet when her business in Gondor is completed,' he replies.\
\
'She will return with it to Umbar Baharbêl, and any passing whim will be enforced by cannon and with Hungry Fire.'","Jajax has suggested that you search the bodies of the slain guards to see if either of them have the keys to the gaol.","Instancia: Comienza el levantamiento","Tidings from the city outside are cut off from the prisoners in the Fleetfast gaol. What is happening in Umbar Baharbêl?","Talk to Jajax","Jajax sputters with flustered surprise","Talk to Belondor in the ship Sotóka","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}, but we have not the time to catch up! Rothog and I will stay and guard the rear while you and Jajax make your escape; the way out is downstairs.\
\
'Daxamat leads the rebellion against Hármelak and Khôltekh. With every passing moment, more and more of the people join Ilma-ghôli, the rising tide.\
\
'I am sorry this has happened, my friend. I thought the sickness in the Kindred ended with Azagath, but it was not so. Hármelak and Khôltekh have betrayed the city, and I must make it right.'","Your allies stand ready to pursue the Song.","Talk to Jajax in Umbar-môkh","Belondor and Rothog entered the gaol from a hatch downstairs that leads to Umbar-môkh. Now you should find your way downstairs to escape!","You should board Tatháta's ship so you may pursue the Song."},
[7375]={"Instancia: La Voz del Dragón","Habla con Durin","Stand with the dwarves","The Dwarrowmoot has begun.","Hrímil has escaped on powerful wings, making for the high peak, but her terror is plain to see.","Observe the Dwarrowmoot","'The Dwarrowmoot is over, ${PLAYER}. Now we have no choice.\
\
'All will be decided in the moments to come!'","The Dwarrowmoot has been interrupted by the dragon!","Remain on your guard!","'Wish me good fortune in this, ${PLAYER}.'","The Dwarrowmoot came to a sudden end, but Durin has made a decision: it is time to face the dragon and reclaim the Mountain-home!","Prince Durin stands at the Thing-fold to begin the Dwarrowmoot for which he has called.","Durin has called for Dwarrowmoot, a gathering of the dwarves that will decide what can be done to wrest Gundabad from the claws of Hrímil Frost-heart.","Their laughter is disturbed by the sound of a rushing wind!"},
[7376]={"Escucha la conversación de tus compañeros y permanece alerta.","Habla con Boromir","'Te conté del asalto sobre Osgiliath en los días de junio, ¿verdad?, y de los extraños presagios que rodearon la batalla. Uno de ellos fue un sueño, un sueño con aire de profecía. No te lo mencioné antes, porque no sabía qué pensar; en Gondor confiamos en la espada brillante y el escudo firme, y con razón. ¡Un sueño es algo fugaz, y qué hombre confiaría en algo que vive solo en la oscuridad y desaparece con el amanecer!'\
\
Boromir se acaricia la barba pensativamente.\
\
'Digo que los sueños son fugaces, pero este fue peculiar. Le vino a mi hermano Faramir la víspera del ataque a Osgiliath, y luego muchas noches después, siempre el mismo. Me vino una vez a mí, y aunque mi hermano me habló de sus sueños, fue con mis propios ojos que contemplé estos detalles; me parecen tan reales.\
\
'En el sueño, vi el cielo oriental volverse oscuro, y hubo un estruendo como de trueno. Pero una luz permanecía en el cielo occidental, y una voz clara me llamó. \\qBusca la Espada que fue quebrada\\q, decía, \\qen Imladris mora. Allí se tomarán consejos más fuertes que conjuros de Morgul.\\q\
\
'Eso es de gran interés para cualquier hijo de Gondor, ${PLAYER}. ¡Cualquier medio de enfrentar los males que surgen del Valle de Morgul es bienvenido en Minas Tirith! Pero la voz no terminó allí. Hablando de Imladris, continuó:\
\
'\\qSe mostrará una señal de que el Destino está cercano, pues se despertará el Daño de Isildur y el Mediano se alzará.\\q'\
\
Boromir te mira con solemnidad.\
\
'Que mi hermano soñara con esta perdición, la perdición de Minas Tirith, tantas noches... y que luego el mismo sueño viniera a mí... temo que el tiempo se nos está acabando. Gondor necesita la sabiduría que yace oculta en Imladris. Pero ahora desperdiciamos las horas escondidos en esta posada, cuando deberíamos avanzar siempre hacia adelante.'","Habla con Aberthol en la sala principal","Los residentes de Herne están de bastante buen ánimo considerando los peligros que podrían amenazar su pueblo.","'Es reconfortante estar dentro en una noche como esta, incluso si aquello que vino antes no regresa.\
\
'A veces, la conversación se apaga, y creo oír lamentos afuera, junto a las paredes de la posada. Pero eso es solo mi imaginación... o quizás es el viento.\
\
'Estamos a salvo en la Posada de la Encrucijada, eso espero. Tus compañeros tienen sus armas, y tú también. Nos mantendréis a salvo si algo ocurre. ¿Verdad?'","Habla con Meneldir en la Posada de la Encrucijada","<rgb=#FF0000>Meneldir, Egfrith y Boromir deben sobrevivir</rgb>","'Te diré la pura verdad, ${PLAYER}, pues tú y tus compañeros contáis con mi respeto, y no puedo guardarte secretos. Ojalá no hubiera venido aquí esta noche. Maddoc ha sido generoso con su cerveza especiada, y lo agradezco, pero eso no cambia nada.\
\
'Puedo ver en el ojo de mi mente la forma reptante que encontré aquella noche en el pueblo, y sé que si miro por encima del hombro veré a su compañera, sentada sobre un corcel negro como la noche. ¡Están esperando justo afuera de las paredes de la posada, esperando que salga!\
\
'Oh... lo siento... es solo que es una sensación muy intensa. Yo era un aventurero, ¡y ahora soy vencido por el más leve susurro de un recuerdo! Me avergüenzo. Hay tanta gente aquí, y algunos de ellos héroes: Boromir de Gondor, Egfrith de Rohan... ¡y no te excluyo a ti, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Perdóname. Recuperaré mi valor. Hay seguridad entre tanta buena gente, después de todo. Esas sombras no se atreverán a molestarnos aquí.'","Instancia: La Noche de la Espera","Habla con Boromir junto a las ventanas","¡Has fallado en defender el pueblo!","'No hay nada afuera. Al menos, nada que yo pueda ver.\
\
'Ya me he dado un par de sustos esta noche, cuando el viento sopla y tira de los postigos de la posada. Pero eso es todo... por ahora, al menos.\
\
'Me alegra estar aquí dentro con mis vecinos, y no allá afuera en la oscuridad.'","'¡La sensación de temor crece! ¡Preparaos!\
\
'¡Algo se acerca!'","Habla con Maddoc en el mostrador","Habla con Meneldir fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada","'Se acabó, ${PLAYER}. Estamos vivos.'","Boromir muestra una expresión preocupada.","Escucha la conversación de tus compañeros","Meneldir te ha invitado a <rgb=#00FF00>sentarte</rgb> en su mesa.","Boromir está junto a una de las ventanas. ¿Ha visto algo afuera?","Una sensación de temor se ha asentado sobre la Posada de la Encrucijada. ¿Qué ha ocurrido afuera?","'Es un alivio para mí que tantos de la gente de Herne nos escucharan, ${PLAYER}. Espero que las paredes de la Posada de la Encrucijada sean lo bastante fuertes para mantenerlos a salvo... o que el mal ya se haya marchado, y este plan sea innecesario. Pero no puedo arriesgarlo.\
\
'Estas primeras horas no han sido difíciles para la gente de Herne, pues Maddoc tomó la sabia decisión de dejar correr su cerveza especiada libremente, y de poner abundante comida sobre sus mesas. La verdadera prueba llegará en las horas por venir.\
\
'¿Hablarás con algunos de los aquí reunidos en la Posada de la Encrucijada y averiguarás su ánimo?'","<rgb=#00FF00>Siéntate</rgb> en la mesa de Meneldir","La gente de Herne se refugia en la Posada de la Encrucijada por la noche, temerosa de que cualquier mal que pasó por Herne pueda regresar.","Regresa a tu mesa","Meneldir quiere hablar contigo en la Posada de la Encrucijada mientras esperáis que pasen las horas.","Habla con Bledri arriba","'No he visto la Posada de la Encrucijada tan concurrida en muchos meses. ¡Ojalá fuera en mejores circunstancias!\
\
'Algunos de mis vecinos creen que esto es una artimaña mía para aumentar mi clientela. ¡Ja! ¡Si tan solo pudiera presumir de haberlo ideado! Lamentablemente, no soy tan listo.\
\
'Parece que nada vendrá a Herne esta noche. Aun así, tú y tus compañeros tienen mi agradecimiento. Es mejor estar a salvo que lamentarlo, ¿no?'","Meneldir te ha pedido que hables con algunos de los habitantes que se reúnen en la Posada de la Encrucijada y que los tranquilices diciéndoles que estarán a salvo.","Habla con Aldyth arriba","'No hay nada afuera, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Solo viento y oscuridad.'","Sal fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada e investiga","Tus compañeros están listos para defender a la gente de Herne."},
[7377]={"Vágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.","'I was born in Númenor, two scant years before its fall, but I cannot trust my memories of that land. Are they true recollections, or the fleeting shadows of stories I was told, the impressions of others? I cannot say. But I know the name I was given. I was born Adûnzagar. It was only the first of my names, and not the last.\
\
'My father was Ûrizagar, the captain-general of Númenor's fleets, and his title was Sword of the Sun. Do I remember his cruelty, or his worship at the temples of Sauron? I thought I did. Do I remember the warmth of my mother Abrazâni, or is that memory a creation too, balm for the hurts of my heart?\
\
'This I do know: my mother pleaded with the sons of Elendil to make a place for me on their ships when the deluge came to Númenor. In later years, when I was older, Isildur told me that my father's spies prevented her from reaching the ships in time. Was it so? I do not know.\
\
'But that is how I came without father or mother to the shores of Middle-earth when Númenor sank beneath the waves.'","The shade that came to be called Vágari the Wanderer desires to confess to you the misdeeds of his past.","The shade of Tárandil says nothing, dwelling upon his old sorrows.","Talk to Rioc","'I know now who despoiled my daughter, faithless invader from beyond the Sea!\
\
'My rage will follow you forever, though I remain bound to pass no further than Erech! You will never be free of it, for my howling anger will pursue you wherever you think to go!\
\
'But that is the least of the daggers with which I cut thee. This will be the sharpest: there can be no escape for my daughter and her child. You will share my sorrow, detestable thief, for she and the child will remain with me forever!'","Listen to the shade's account","'I pleaded with Isildur to show mercy, to forgive Rioc and his people of their oath-breaking, but my foster-father's wrath at their treachery was so great I feared for my life. I quailed before the storm of his rage, and told him not of Bravantel my wife or Héol my son. Would that truth-telling have changed his mind? Would it cause him to repent of his curse? My mind dwells ever on this, not the earliest of my wrongs but the first I regret.\
\
'I went north with Isildur and my foster-brothers to summon aid from Arnor and from the Elves, and every night my heart pleaded with me to speak the truth, and every day the guilt pressed heavily upon me and weighed my lips shut. For all my time with the Great Alliance, I kept secret my marriage to Bravantel and the duty I owed my son; my brothers goaded me with the thought I might never marry, and each of their barbs pricked more deadly than they intended or imagined. I feared for Bravantel and for Héol, and when the war finally ended I was frenzied with worry for them.\
\
'Isildur offered me the chance to be the captain-general I had dreamed of becoming, commander of all the armies of the Dúnedain, but no longer did my heart desire it. I longed only to return to the White Mountains so I could find my wife and son. \\qThen I will make you more than a mere lord, my son-of-no-blood,\\q Isildur said to me, \\qbut rather a prince, for Ëartur and all his sons perished during the war. Belfalas needs a new master. Go, and take my blessing with you.\\q\
\
“I will take your blessing,” I said to him, “but not for me. Show mercy instead for the Men of the Mountain, and lift the curse you have placed upon them. I will bring you their false king’s head, and his people shall swear their oath anew.\\q\
\
'But he refused. Always did Isildur refuse me this one request.'","Instancia: La confesión del errante","Listen to Vágari's account","The shade of Tárandil falls silent, overcome with ancient grief","Talk to Vágari the Wanderer","'King Rioc was enraged, for he was certain that his grandson had been born a bastard, but Bravantel soothed his ire with reassuring words. She told the king she had been married in secret, not to an invading Númenórean but to one of his own warriors, who had recently been slain in battle with Orcs. Héol was born of that union, she said, and therefore the stain of dishonour could not cling to him. Rioc's anger cooled, and he agreed to raise the boy as his own grandchild.\
\
'I grieved that my son would not know his true father, but there was nothing I could do. I stole gold from the treasury of Prince Eärtur of Belfalas and sent as much as could be done secretly to Bravantel to provide for the boy. But then I was summoned back east by my foster-father Isildur, for the host of Mordor had come down the valley and overthrown Minas Ithil. Sauron's war had begun, and the kings sent word to all their allies that it was time to honour their vows.\
\
'It was then that Rioc learned the truth.'"},
[7378]={"'Thank you for staying for the night, ${PLAYER}. You will not regret it!\
\
'We've prepared a fine supper, and it would be our honour to share it with you.\
\
'I've prepared a place for you at the fire. Come!'","The Want-kin begin their supper, and you should too!","'Ah, that warms my bones! Thank you for fetching that firewood, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'It is true enough that you've come to aid Durin in his quest, but what else brought you here to the Slade? Where have your past adventures led you?\
\
'I know my companions and I are eager to hear more about you. What do you say?'","This will do...","Sit on the log beside Nagli at the camp-fire at Khadâsh-gâra","Tell Nagli and the Want-kin the <rgb=#00ff00>story</rgb> of your adventures before coming to Elderslade","Nagli set your supper beside you at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
The Want-kin have begun their meal. You should share a supper with them.","Sigue a Nagli","Neither Longbeards, Zhélruka, nor Stout-axes, a company of clanless dwarves known only as the Want-kin have made camp in Elderslade.","Beside the fire, plates of food have been prepared","Stórath scoffs and wanders off to his bedroll","The Want-kin listen closely to your tales of adventure","Share a hearty supper with the Want-kin at Khadâsh-gâra","A suitable log for sitting can be found beside Nagli at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
Nagli has asked you to join him and the other Want-kin at the camp-fire at Khadâsh-gâra.","'Do not let Stórath's words bother you, ${PLAYER}. I think perhaps the ale has gone to his head!\
\
'I know the others and I were glad to hear your tales of adventure. I have a feeling we've not even heard the half of it, but that's enough for one night. It was a fine evening, and I am glad to have shared it with you.\
\
'It is late. Your adventures with Durin can wait until morning, I think.\
\
'Come, I've prepared a bedroll for you.'","Instancia: Los Want-kin","Nagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
You have brought more firewood to the fire at Khadâsh-gâra as Nagli asked. You should talk to Nagli.","'Ah! While you are standing, could you fetch some more wood for the fire?\
\
'It's just over there. But do try to be quiet, Lapis doesn't like to be startled in her sleep!'","Listen to Nagli and the Want-kin","Nagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
Nagli has asked to hear more tales of your adventures before coming to Elderslade. You should tell Nagli and the Want-kin of your adventures in Middle-earth.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will need to select Nagli before emoting to advance this quest.</rgb>","Nagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
You should follow Nagli.","'It has been a long day, ${PLAYER}. Let us take our rest!'","Nagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
Nagli has asked to speak with you. You should talk to Nagli.","Nagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
You should talk to Nagli.","Listen to Nagli and Stórath","Firewood can be found at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
Nagli has asked you to fetch some firewood to stoke the fire at Khadâsh-gâra. You should collect the firewood.","Nagli and Stórath are talking about the tales you told.","The Want-kin are preparing to have supper.","It is hard to imagine a finer meal prepared in the wilds of Elderslade","Habla con Nagli","As the wood crackles, the fire's warmth can be felt throughout Khadâsh-gâra","Collect firewood to stoke the fire at Khadâsh-gâra","Nagli can be found at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
After Stórath expressed his displeasure in hosting you, Nagli and the other Want-kin defended your presence at Khadâsh-gâra. You should talk to Nagli.","Nagli sits down beside the fire and gestures to a log","<rgb=#00ff00>Sit</rgb> on the log beside Nagli at the camp-fire at Khadâsh-gâra"},
[7379]={"Durin has commanded that the assault on Gundabad begin by seizing a foothold further ahead in the foothills of Elderslade: the ruin of Zarkul-sulûn will become the base of operations for the Gabil'akkâ!","Zarkul-sulûn has been occupied, a new foothold for the Gabil'akkâ!","Talk to Durin during the assault on Zarkul-sulûn","'We need to seize Zarkul-sulûn if we are to push through Elderslade toward Gundabad! The Zhélruka will lead the way behind their prince, and my Longbeards will follow them!\
\
'We have Orcs to slay, ${PLAYER}! Stay close to me!'","Prince Durin has commanded that the Gabil'akkâ seize the ruin of Zarkul-sulûn from the Orcs.","'All around me I see only Longbeards! Where are the Zhélruka? Where is Ingór?'","Instancia: La Guerra de las Tres Cumbres"},
[7380]={"You see Gorgar standing alone at the edge of the cliff","You have tracked the hobgoblins to the end of the road.\
\
You should follow Hórin and find the hobgoblins.","The hobgoblins will soon be upon you!\
\
You should blow the horn to summon your forces!","Listen to the conversation","You are clear of the hobgoblins! Blow the horn to summon your forces!","Blow the horn to summon your forces!","The hobgoblins are just ahead!","You have reached the end of the Father's Path, and Warlord Dushtalbúk must be ahead. His reason for marching to the mountain's peak is about to be revealed....","'We don't know what we're walking into here, so I will hold back the main force for the moment, but this is the end of the road! Dushtalbúk MUST be up here. The two of us are going to go ahead, and sound the horn when we want our forces to advance.'","The hobgoblins will soon be upon you!\
\
You should wait for your forces to arrive!","Instancia: La táctica del señor de la guerra","Hórin is standing by with the dwarf forces.\
\
You should talk to Hórin.","The Gabil'akkâ has arrived!","Find the hobgoblins","Habla con Hórin","You have found Gorgar at the end of the road. He must be the hobgoblins' reason for coming here!\
\
You should watch and listen as events unfold!","The Voice of the Dragon is wearing off! You can move again!","Return to the Gate of Uzdarulzahar","Wait for your forces to arrive","Follow Hórin to the hiding spot","'The hobgoblins and our own forces are approaching! Be ready for a battle!'","The hobgoblins will soon be upon you!\
\
You should return to the Gate of Uzdarulzahar and summon your forces!"},
[7381]={"Remain alert for any treachery by Karazgar","Bótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.","Habla con Bótuz Sangrehielo","'Remain on your guard, my warriors, and keep watch for Karazgar. He will not surprise us as he surprised Vútro.'","Bótuz Frostblood has some words for you now that Karazgar has departed.","'I have taken the measure of these Zhélruka, but you... you are a curiosity to me.'\
\
Even behind his mask, you feel the piercing eyes of Karazgar upon you. The urge to draw your weapon and cease their study rises in your heart, a sensation made more unpleasant by this lingering doubt: does this urge come from you or from the Warrior himself? If Karazgar notices your struggle, he gives no sign of it when next he speaks.\
\
'There is a smell about you, ${PLAYER}, the odour of all your kind. But there is something else, too: the reek of subservience. I know the Master you serve. I have cast off the shackles that once bound me, and now I shall take what is mine. Why should you not do the same?'","Karazgar has asked to speak with you.","Instancia: El guerrero encontrado","'Let us return to Skarháld. If these words signify anything more than idle boasting we should prepare for Karazgar's attack.'","'Karazgar speaks nonsense. He is one man, too cowardly to show his face. Without his fell Master he is nothing. Let him come to Skarháld once, twice, thrice, it matters not how often. The Zhélruka will make him regret the visits. Aye, even the Longbeards will oppose him!'","Search for Karazgar with Bótuz and his warriors","Bótuz Frostblood and his warriors have left Skarháld in search of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior.","Talk to Karazgar, but remain alert for treachery"},
[7382]={"'My tale is at its end, ${PLAYER}, but the wraith that was once Eärnur troubles Gondor still.'","Habla con Aragorn","Aragorn has agreed to tell you what he knows of King Eärnur's last days.","Aragorn has agreed to tell you the tale of Eärnur's last days, known only to the wise and to those of Isildur's line.","'Eärnur was hot of temper, and surely would have ridden forth at once, were it not for the intervention of his advisor Mardil. A wise man and studied, Gondor remembers him as Mardil the Good, and his actions on this day forestalled some measure of doom. Not forever, alas! But for a time.\
\
'Mardil stepped forward. \\qWe know who your master is,\\q he declared. \\qWe know how much he can be trusted, or how little. If he is so eager for this combat, let him ride here, to the Tower of Guard, and show his true worth before all.\\q\
\
'The emissary bridled at this response and departed, but his anger was as nothing compared to the wrath of Eärnur. He brooded and raged in the time that followed, but whenever he thought to dare the shadowed vale, his Steward was on hand with soothing words and reminders of his duty. The Morgul Vale remained silent.\
\
'So passed seven grim years. Seven years following the day that he first came to Minas Tirith, the messenger returned.\
\
'This time he was not alone.'","Instancia: El Guerrero rehecho","Listen to the words of Aragorn","Aragorn has agreed to tell you what he knows of Eärnur's last days.","'You have heard the story of Egalmoth's Onslaught against the forces of Mordor that came to seize Minas Ithil? It is a popular tale, oft-told in Gondor even today, for it is heroic and tragic in equal measure. Lord Egalmoth had the command of Barad Cúron, and his charge through the city into the invading Orcs is now the province of legend. He and all his men died in that sally, but when the last defender was dead and the Witch-king entered the tower, he learned of Egalmoth's other purpose. The palantír was missing. One of Egalmoth's riders had carried it from Barad Cúron, casting it into the Ithilduin lest it be claimed by the Nazgûl.\
\
'Like many victories of the Dúnedain over the years, this one was short-lived. Servants of the Witch-king found the Ithil-stone fetched up upon a rock in the current, and they brought it to their master. Gloating over his victory, the Lord of the Nazgûl used the palantír only once before bringing it personally to Sauron, as he was commanded. The Witch-king made contact with the Anor-stone wielded by King Eärnil, showing him that Egalmoth had failed and the city belonged now to him. \\qMinas Ithil has fallen,\\q the Nazgûl sneered. \\qYou look now upon Minas Morgul.\\q\
\
'Eärnil despaired, and he forbade any of his subjects or his line from using the Anor-stone. \\qIt is no longer safe,\\q he declared. The Ban of Eärnil would last for nearly a thousand years, unbroken until the time of Steward Denethor. It may be that the Ban prevented Sauron from achieving his goal of a corrupted Gondor centuries before he nearly succeeded... but I cannot say for certain.'","'Before his blood had cooled, Eärnur and a company of his bravest knights rode from Minas Tirith for the last time. They entered the Morgul Vale and were never seen again.\
\
'The common belief in the years that followed was that the Witch-king treacherously trapped the king and his knights in Minas Morgul, and they perished there in torment. No proper claimant to the throne could be found, and the Line of Kings was ended. Mardil did not don the crown himself; instead, he became the first of the Ruling Stewards, swearing to govern Gondor only until the king returned. And you know how that tradition reached its ending, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'But when Eärnur succumbed to the taunts of the Witch-king and rode to Minas Morgul, we know now what was hidden for those many centuries. Through the dark arts of the Lord of the Nazgûl, Eärnur was corrupted and changed into the fell wraith Mordirith. Bound to the Witch-king, he served Mordor as the False King of Angmar until his defeat last year. When next he crossed our paths, he had been given a new form with which to wage Sauron's war: Gothmog, commander of Mordor's armies.\
\
'Better to have died as Eärnur, ${PLAYER}, than be reborn as a tool of evil, again and again. It saddens me to think of that fate.'","Listen to the words of Aragorn concerning Eärnur"},
[7383]={"Brogur ha venido a la orilla del Lago Negro, a pesar de los deseos de su primo.","'No sé cómo agradecerte esto, ${PLAYER}. No solo has ahuyentado a la bestia que nos impedía entrar en Moria, sino que también has vengado a mi hijo. Nunca olvidaré lo que has hecho por mí, y siempre estaré en deuda contigo y a tu servicio.\
\
'Bróin hablaba a menudo de grandes batallas y heroísmos; se habría maravillado de tu batalla contra el feroz Guardián del Agua.'","Bósi se encuentra en la pendiente que conduce al lago frente a las Puertas de Durin.\
\
Bósi te espera para desearte suerte contra el Guardián del Agua. Está seguro de que el mordisco de tu arma prevalecerá.","Bosi y Brogur se encuentran en la orilla del lago.\
\
El Guardián del Agua ha sido ahuyentado, y ahora deberías hablar con Bosi y Brogur.","'¡La inmunda criatura que nos acecha desde las profundidades del lago sentirá el mordisco de tu arma y aprenderá lo que es el miedo! ¡Dale una lección que no olvidará pronto!\
\
'Y hazlo no solo para proteger Khazad-dûm, sino también en memoria de Bróin, que pereció a manos de ese monstruo innoble. Mi sobrino merecía un destino mucho mejor que morir entre los tentáculos de esa cosa.\
\
'Cuando hayas matado o ahuyentado a la criatura, podremos entrar en Moria sin que nada ni nadie nos lo impida !\
\
'He enviado a uno de mis exploradores a reconocer a la bestia. Ve a verlo, pero ten cuidado, sobre todo !'","Brogur ha sido derrotado.","'¡Hay ondas en el agua, pero no veo al monstruo! ¡Ten cuidado, porque puede atacar sin previo aviso, como el desafortunado Bróin aprendió a su costa!'","Bósi ha enviado a algunos enanos al lago para que reconozcan a la bestia.\
\
${PLAYERNAME:Armado[m]|Armada[f]} con tu nueva arma, estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para enfrentarte al Guardián del Agua.","'¡Debemos regresar ahora para contarle al resto de la expedición lo que has logrado, y que ahora podemos entrar en las Minas de Moria!'","'¡No me dejaré vencer por la tristeza, ${PLAYER}! ¡Al contrario! ¡Vengaré a mi hijo en combate, y maldición a la criatura que me lo arrebató!'","El mordisco de tu arma tendrá que prevalecer contra la gruesa carne de los muchos tentáculos del Guardián.","'¡Lo hemos conseguido, ${PLAYER}! Hemos ahuyentado al Guardián del Agua de las Puertas de Durin, y ahora los enanos de nuestra expedición pueden entrar en las Minas de Moria! Las armas que encontramos han marcado la diferencia, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}; sí, mis enanos se han equipado con el mismo botín, y la criatura ha aprendido a temer el mordisco de la Guarnición de Hierro.\
\
'También has vengado a mi sobrino Bróin, así como a todos los enanos que han sido perdidos por esta criatura. Ahora se retira por oscuros pasajes; ojalá sus tentáculos retorcidos y apestosos no nos molesten nunca más.'","Instancia: El Guardián del Agua","Protege a Brogur del Guardián del Agua","Habla con el explorador de Bósi.","Habla con Brogur.","El Guardián del Agua se esconde bajo la superficie del lago, pero sus tentáculos salen para atacarte.\
\
Debes derrotar los tentáculos del Guardián y ahuyentarlo de la entrada a Moria.","Brogur ha desafiado al Guardián del Agua, decidido a vengar la muerte de su hijo.","Ahuyenta al Guardián del Agua","'Está ahí fuera... la bestia que mató a mi hijo. No descansaré hasta que Bróin sea vengado.'","Habla con Bósi.","'Busca a mi explorador un poco más arriba de la pendiente, al borde del lago. Él te dirá dónde ha visto a la bestia, para que puedas atacarla con tu nueva arma.'"},
[7384]={"A great commotion draws your attention to the west side of the feast-hall","Instancia: El banquete de bodas","Talk to the wine steward downstairs","Prince Imrahil told you a wine steward working at the wedding-feast wanted you to meet with him downstairs.","'The Grey Company rode from Eriador to aid the chieftain of the Dúnedain, and now many of us will return to our homes; but not all. We all have our own reasons, for the king has not set a bond upon us that we do not choose for ourselves.\
\
'But there remains the question: what shall be done about the land that lies on Gondor's doorstep? Mordor lies there, the Black Land, and who knows what sorceries of the Witch-king may lurk within the Morgul Vale. I will help my king to combat these evils, and so too will Dagoras, and Faeron, and Mithrendan.\
\
'Others of the Grey Company may decide to do the same... but they must choose for themselves. We have done what we intended, but I wager that some may discover they wish to do more. Gondor awaits an era of peace... but it will not arrive without we who are willing to fight for it.'","Merethien, the Master Foodmonger of Minas Tirith, has some questions for Merry and Pippin concerning what qualifies as a 'banquet' at their home, the distant Shire. Furthermore, she is pleased to have an excuse to leave Ioreth's chatter and Galathir's lecture behind her.","Samwise Gamgee is at the head table in Merethrond.","The Grey Company has gathered to celebrate the wedding of their chieftain, and to honour the great deeds done on his behalf.","The wine steward is being regaled with tales of Thrymm's heroics, and he wishes to speak with you.","Listen (again) to Thrymm's tale of his exploits","'One of the wine stewards came by earlier, before our friend from Rohan launched into his... full-throated... tales of bravery. This steward asked if we would do him the kindness of delivering you to him if you chanced to come by our table.\
\
'He said he would be downstairs, ${PLAYER}. Now that I have executed this charge, perhaps I will learn what else my daughter would hear of the new king of Rohan, and why the speaking of his name brings such a blush to her cheeks....'","'What do you think, Pip? What would old Flourdumpling have to say about the courses on offer here? Oh yes, Merethien, I think this wedding-feast can stand quite comfortably alongside the very finest of Shire banquets!'","A loud disturbance has caused a commotion on the western side of the feast-hall.","Pippin wants to return to his own table for a bit, and wishes for you and Merry to follow him.","'Dear me! I am pleased that Prince Faramir has made up his mind, but to be completely honest with you, ${PLAYER}, I had not quite gotten around to the advice I intended to give to him!\
\
'Still, all is well when it ends well... which it will, if Lady Éowyn agrees to his proposal. If she does not, I fear the reputation of hobbit-wisdom may suffer in Ithilien and Gondor! Oh dear!'","Go outside and confront the 'rough sorts' described by the wine steward","Follow Pippin back to his table","Prince Imrahil was given a message for you.","The wine steward gave you some fine bottles of Gondor's finest to use as a peace offering with the 'rough sorts' gathering outside.\
\
You have been tasked with leaving Merethrond by the front doors and confronting the group of rough sorts the wine steward described.","Talk to King Elessar","Talk to Prince Imrahil","Talk to Prince Faramir of Ithilien","Talk to Culang","Talk to Beregond","Talk to the wine steward","'Thank you for rescuing me, ${PLAYER}. I intend no disrespect for any of the fine folk at my table, for they are all worthies of Gondor in their own ways... but some of them can be most tiring.\
\
'Come with me, my helpful friend. I see the hobbits with whom I spoke right over there.'","Talk to King Elessar upstairs, on the western side of the feast-hall","Merethien wants to know if Merry and Pippin are satisfied that the wedding-feast she has helped to prepare can compare with the banquets they described in the Shire.","'${PLAYER}, it is my pleasure to introduce you to my wife Gilithel, and I believe you have already met our son Bergil. He was quite the trouble-maker in Minas Tirith, running through the lower tiers with his friends, and he has found new ways to cause mischief in Ithilien. But he is a good lad, and at his age I was much the same.\
\
'I must confess to you I did not think I would be welcomed back to the city for the King's wedding, but word was sent to Lord Faramir, and we could not refuse.'","'Ah, there you are, ${PLAYER}! I am pleased the Prince of Dol Amroth gave you my message, for it is urgent and I did not know where else I might turn. There is something of a problem, you see, and I need you to ensure it does not get any worse!\
\
'Some rough sorts have gathered outside. I am afraid they might intend to disrupt the wedding-feast in some way. They were asking for you!\
\
'Here, take these bottles of wine out to them. It could be that an offering of peace will send them happily on their way. And if not, well... your deeds are well-known, and such rough sorts as these may take one look at you and decide it would be best for them to go elsewhere!'","Talk to Samwise Gamgee","'I hope you are enjoying yourself, ${PLAYER}. I confess to you that much of tonight has passed by with dizzying speed, but it is a joyful motion and I would trade it for nothing else.\
\
'Might I ask a favour of you? Earlier I spoke with Faramir about a matter of some importance, and I am interested to learn if he has come to a decision. Would you speak with him and determine if this be so?'","'It is a pleasure to speak with you, my friend. I saw you earlier, when our Halfling friends ran by the table on their way to do some mischief... it was a spirited chase, and brought a smile to my lips; that has been rare enough in the days since... well, in the past few days.'\
\
Faramir falls silent, and you take the opportunity to ask if he has considered the topic about which King Elessar inquired. Faramir studies you quietly.\
\
'He told you not the subject of our discussion? He is more subtle than I expected, or perhaps it is the hand of his Queen that makes him so! Ah, ${PLAYER}, you are a friend, so I will speak freely.\
\
'The king knows that my heart has been captured by the Lady Éowyn of Rohan. She returned to the Riddermark in the company of her brother while they prepare for the funeral of Théoden, and while she has been gone my heart has been in darkness! Ever she occupies my thoughts, and I know I will never again feel happiness or joy while we are apart. I dare not hope she feels the same, and would not! For I would wish her no unhappiness.'","The wedding-feast continues into the night and you should speak with King Elessar before the festivities conclude.","The ceremony may be over, but the festivities continue! The great wedding-feast will last well into the night, with the noise of celebration continuing nearly until dawn.","Talk to Thrymm Red-beard","Thrymm Red-beard has obtained a captive audience, and is regaling them with tales of his adventures.","He hands you a number of wine bottles to use as a peace offering","King Elessar wishes to speak with you.","Investigate the disturbance on the western side of the feast-hall","Talk to Merethien","'Who can say when we will all be once again together, ${PLAYER}? Each of us has business elsewhere: some in the north, some here in the south. It would have been a shame not to mark the occasion. Is that so unusual? We all feel a kinship with each other, borne of our shared duty; it is strange to me that we must now separate.\
\
'Lothrandir wishes to return to Forochel, the land of the Snowmen, so I will travel with him part of the way with some others of the company. Techeron will reside once again in Evendim, but on the way we will pay a visit to Saeradan and learn the tale of his own return to Eriador with our fallen brothers. Idhrien and Langlas plan to stay for awhile at Esteldín with Mincham. Angwedh has not yet decided where he will travel, just that his road lies to the north. If he has a place in mind, he has not shared it with us; I think the wilderness calls to him.'\
\
Radanir smirks at you.\
\
'Do you know what calls to me? The food of the north-lands! The food at this feast is too richly-made, too covered in sauces, too soft, and there's too much of it. There isn't anything to sink your teeth into, ${PLAYER}. Give me the crusty bread and old cheese of the Forsaken Inn, a day's ride east of Bree... that is all I need.'","Talk to Radanir","You should return to the wedding-feast, which will likely soon be winding down.","Listen to the words of the Grey Company","Capítulo 5: La reunión de la Compañía Gris","'And so, with our horses refreshed, we crossed the Mering-stream and rode hard through the Beacon Hills. We were so close, but not yet close enough: we were beset by Orcs and Variags near Amon Dîn! We broke through the line of Variags, but they did not pursue us. I think now I know the reason: they knew the road ahead would be held against us!'\
\
Thrymm pauses in his tale, seeming to see you for the first time.\
\
'Oh, ${PLAYER}, pull up a seat! I was just telling these fine folk of Gondor about some of my recent adventures!'","Beregond and his family sit at Pippin's table with a number of Gondorian nobles.","Go back inside Merethrond and rejoin the wedding-feast","'I played my part as well as I could, ${PLAYER}! Were your friends able to surprise you?'\
\
The wine steward glances at Thrymm Red-beard, whose long-winded description of past glories has shown no sign of cessation; indeed, he may have started anew.\
\
'Perhaps you can go back upstairs and see if my services are needed? I am sure there must be a need for more wine... there simply must....'","'I expect Grimbeorn and his animals will enliven Merethrond for a time. Good! It will give us a brief respite from all this celebration!\
\
'Arwen and I would like to speak to you, ${PLAYER}, in a more quiet setting. Let us find one.'","Prince Faramir of Ithilien is at the head table in Merethrond."},
[7385]={"Beckon Bryn to you.","Follow Bryn to meet his friend","Listen to the Weeping Warrior.","<rgb=#FF0000>Beckon</rgb> Bryn to you","Follow Bryn and meet his friend.","'Though I can barely face my family right now, I know that we should return and tell them of rust-man and of what evil deceits he is capable.'","The Weeping Warrior looks coldly at you","Listen to Bryn's exchange with Akshir","Erna is worried about her son Bryn who has become more and more distant and aggravated.","The Weeping Warrior escapes","Talk to Bryn.","Before you stands Akshir, the Jangovar leader","Try to speak with Bryn.","Listen to the Weeping Warrior","'What do you want of me, ${PLAYER}? Have you come to mock me again, or to shame me before my mother and brother?\
\
'Look around you. Beyond Dale's walls, our kingdom hangs by a thread. We say the Easterlings are our vanquished foes, and yet they roam freely through the Dale-lands. We say many things that are wrong. My friend has shown me much, and my eyes are opened now. He has shown me how much I could accomplish if I were king instead of Bard.\
\
'I see that mocking look in your eye. You think me a child. You disbelieve me. Come with me then and you'll meet him for yourself. Then he can explain it. Oh, he does so, so much better than I do!'","Talk to Bryn","Listen to Bryn's exchange with Akshir.","Instancia: El Guerrero Lloroso","'Who was that - that deathly creature? What had Akshir to do with him? And why did it sound as if he were taking orders from him? Tell me, ${PLAYER}! Akshir would take orders from nobody - he is wise and...\
\
'Oh! What a fool I have been. And to think he had near convinced me to kill my own brother. Did you see? He gave me the knife to do it with. Bah! I can barely look at the awful thing. What sorcery did Akshir cast upon me? What shall I do? Flee in exile and never return?'\
\
You speak gently to Bryn, and convince him to return home, be brave and honest, and confess the truth.\
\
'That is the thing that most terrifies me, ${PLAYER}, and so it must be the brave and right one.'"},
[7386]={"Bori está esperando a que hagas <rgb=#FF0000>saludos</rgb> para saber que entiendes la señal.","Bori está esperando bajo las vías del carro minero para hablar contigo sobre la fuerza principal de los orcos.","Llega debajo de las vías sin ser visto","Ha llegado el momento de abandonar todo sigilo; tú y Bori están lo suficientemente adentrados en el campamento como para que el líder de los orcos de la Mano Blanca esté sin la protección de sus guardianes.","Espera a que llegue Bori","'El edificio justo delante, construido en el costado de la pared de roca, es a donde debes dirigirte. ¡Evita acercarte demasiado a los orcos!\
\
'Cuando llegues al edificio, haz <rgb=#FF0000>saludos</rgb> para que sepa que la costa está despejada. Asegúrate de que es seguro y que no hay orcos en mi camino antes de hacerme señales!'","Habla con Bori","'Es demasiado peligroso para nosotros viajar juntos. En su lugar, tú irás por delante, y cuando llegues a un lugar seguro, harás <rgb=#FF0000>saludos</rgb> para que yo sepa que puedo correr allí también.\
\
'<rgb=#FF0000>Saluda</rgb> ahora para que pueda ver cómo será la señal.'","'Corre hacia esa plataforma de madera; ¿la ves, justo delante de nuestra posición? Cuando estés debajo, <rgb=#FF0000>saluda</rgb> para que me una a ti... ¡pero solo si la costa está despejada!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Saluda</rgb> a Bori para que te siga cuando no haya moros en la costa","Espera a que los orcos abandonen Stazgnâkh","Bori te ha pedido que lo sigas a Stazgnâkh.","¡Has perdido el elemento sorpresa, y los enanos están condenados!","Llega al lado del edificio sin ser visto","<rgb=#FF0000>Saluda</rgb> para que Bori te siga cuando no haya moros en la costa","La plataforma hacia la que debes correr está justo delante de la posición de Bori, construida sobre un hueco en la pared de roca. Asegúrate de mantenerte alejado de los orcos que patrullan, o tu misión terminará en fracaso.","'Debemos observar y esperar. Ahora depende de Wíli y Stilling. Si no pueden atraer a la fuerza principal de los orcos fuera de Stazgnâkh, no podremos avanzar.'","Instancia: La Mano Blanca en la Oscuridad","Bori está esperando para hablar contigo sobre su plan.","Bori está mirando hacia la oscuridad que rodea Stazgnâkh y espera para hablar contigo.","<rgb=#FF0000>Saluda</rgb> a Bori para que te siga cuando la costa esté despejada","El edificio al que debes correr se encuentra justo delante de la posición de Bori, construido en el costado de la pared de roca. Asegúrate de mantenerte alejado de los orcos en patrulla, o tu misión terminará en fracaso.","'¿Ves justo delante, donde las vías del carro minero pasan por encima de ese hueco en las paredes de roca? Ahí es a donde debes ir, evitando las patrullas de orcos.\
\
'Una vez que estés debajo de las vías y sea seguro para que me una a ti, haz <rgb=#FF0000>saludos</rgb> para que sepa que puedo correr hacia ti.'","Párate cerca de Bori","Llega al andamio sin ser visto","'Aquí estamos, ${PLAYER}. Si somos capaces de derrotar al líder de estos orcos de la Mano Blanca, ¡deberíamos ser capaces de expulsarlos de Moria sin mucha dificultad!\
\
'Pero debemos ser cautelosos. No quiero atraer ninguna atención hasta que estemos cerca del líder. No deberíamos viajar en grupo, porque entonces seríamos demasiado fáciles de detectar por las centinelas. No, debemos viajar en fila india.\
\
'Irás primero, y luego cuando la costa esté despejada, me darás una señal para que pueda seguirte. Nuestra señal será un <rgb=#FF0000>saludo</rgb>. Solo <rgb=#FF0000>saluda</rgb> cuando sientas que puedo correr hacia ti sin ser visto. <rgb=#FF0000>Saluda</rgb> ahora para que pueda ver que lo entiendes.'","'¡Lo hemos conseguido! Desde aquí, solo nos queda una corta carrera para enfrentarnos al líder de los orcos de la Mano Blanca. El tiempo de la discreción ha terminado. ¡Ya no puede esconderse de nosotros!\
\
'¡Vamos a acabar con él, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! ¡No temas a las centinelas!'","Llega debajo de la plataforma sin ser visto","Las vías del carro minero a las que debes correr se encuentran justo delante de la posición de Bori, construidas sobre un hueco en la pared de roca. Asegúrate de mantenerte alejado de los orcos en patrulla, o tu misión terminará en fracaso.","Sigue a Bori","El andamio hacia el que debes correr está justo delante de la posición de Bori; él quiere que lo esperes en su sombra. Asegúrate de mantenerte alejado de los orcos que patrullan, o tu misión terminará en fracaso.","Has llegado a Stazgnâkh con Bori para ejecutar su audaz plan: infiltrarte furtivamente en la parte trasera del campamento y matar al líder de los orcos de la Mano Blanca.","El plan de Bori está en pleno efecto; ahora depende de los valientes esfuerzos de Wíli y Stilling atraer a la fuerza principal de los orcos fuera del campamento.","Bori se está adentrando más en Stazgnâkh.","'¿Ves el andamio justo delante de nosotros? Corre hacia su sombra, evitando a los orcos patrullando. Cuando llegues allí, y esté seguro, <rgb=#FF0000>saluda</rgb> para que me una a ti.'","'Ten cuidado. ¿Ves a los orcos patrullando? No podemos dejar que nos vean, o nuestra misión será un fracaso.\
\
'Vamos hacia el edificio construido en la pared de roca, justo delante. Parece que los orcos no le prestan atención, y estaremos fuera de su vista si logramos llegar allí.\
\
'Corre hacia allí sin acercarte demasiado a ningún orco. Una vez que llegues, saluda para que sepa que la costa está despejada, y correré hacia el edificio. Asegúrate de que los orcos no puedan verme, ${PLAYER}. Tu posición te dará una mejor vista que la mía.'","Ashpar ha sido derrotado.","'¡Lo han conseguido! ¡Wíli y Stilling han atraído la atención de la mayoría de los orcos de la Mano Blanca!\
\
'¿Ves la plataforma de madera justo delante? Corre hacia ella, y una vez que estés debajo, <rgb=#FF0000>saluda</rgb> para que me una a ti... es decir, si no hay moros en la costa.\
\
'¡Aún debemos proceder con cautela! Hay menos orcos ahora en Stazgnâkh, gracias a nuestros héroes amigos, pero todavía hay centinelas vigilantes.'","'¡Volvamos a la Cámara de Liderazgo, ${PLAYER}, cantando la canción de nuestra victoria mientras vamos! Moria será nuestra de nuevo, en gran parte gracias a nuestras valientes hazañas de hoy!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Saluda</rgb> a Bori para demostrar la señal"},
[7387]={"Protect the Spirit of Wisdom","'Welcome. Thou face now the final of the Huntsman's challenges.\
\
'Should thou prove keen of wit and wisdom, then thou shall pass -- but should thou falter now, then it may be that thy story ends here.'","The stag-spirit has been defeated","You have chosen a deadly spirit","Accept the stag-spirit's challenge","The spirit of Wisdom has been defeated","Speak with the Stag-spirit","You have discovered the spirit of Wisdom","After speaking with the Stag-spirit, you must drink from the strange pool to escape from this eerie realm of spirits.","Accept the stag-spirit's challenge of wisdom.","Instance: The Wild Hunt -- Arassiel's Spirit","Five spirits stand before you. One is the spirit of Wisdom, the other four are spirits of Anger, Greed, Vengeance, and Fear. You must find the spirit of Wisdom among them -- but decide carefully for your choice is perilous.\
\
The stag-spirit told you this:\
\
Firstly, you must know that Fear can be found directly to the right of Vengeance. Secondly, you must know that Anger is directly left of Greed. Lastly, the spirit of Wisdom cannot be found next to Greed, Anger, or Vengeance. Choose wisely.","You stand before an ancient spirit imbued with great wisdom. You must pass through its trial if you wish to gain the Huntsman's favour.","Protect the stag-spirit","You have completed the test of Wisdom","Talk to the stag-spirit","'The test of Wisdom now lies before you. Listen carefully, Mortal.\
\
'Five spirits stand before you. One is the spirit of Wisdom, the other four are spirits of Anger, Greed, Vengeance, and Fear. You must find the spirit of Wisdom among them -- but decide carefully for your choice is perilous.\
\
'I can tell you but three things about these spirits: Firstly, you must know that Fear can be found directly to the right of Vengeance. Secondly, you must know that Anger is directly left of Greed. Lastly, the spirit of Wisdom cannot be found next to Greed, Anger, or Vengeance. Choose wisely....'","'You have proven your wisdom, now leave whence you came before you become a part of our world forevermore.'","Speak with the stag-spirit and confront its challenge.","As you lean down and drink from the pool, strange visions dance before your eyes, and the odd mist that had fallen upon the forest begins to lift.","'The test of Wisdom now lies before you. Listen carefully, Mortal.\
\
'Five spirits stand before you. One is the spirit of Wisdom, the other four are spirits of Anger, Greed, Vengeance, and Fear. You must find the spirit of Wisdom among them -- but decide carefully, for your choice is perilous.\
\
'I can tell you but three things about these spirits: Firstly, you must know that Fear can be found directly to the right of Vengeance. Secondly, you must know that Anger is directly left of Greed. Lastly, the spirit of Wisdom cannot be found next to Greed, Anger, or Vengeance. Choose wisely....'","Identify the spirit of Wisdom"},
[7388]={"You have reached the third lith","'You have run swiftly ${PLAYER}, and have proven your worth - but linger upon my words no longer!\
\
'Those who dally here may never again awaken in mortal realms.'","You have reached the first lith","Gwenaewen has bidden you challenge an ancient spirit of winds in the Wild Hunt that the Huntsman has set before you.","You have reached the second lith","Challenge Gwenaewen's spirit","Approach the falcon-spirit and prove your quickness in following it.","'Por aquí...'","'Time is always of the essence, for ever is the world changing about us - it will not wait for us to catch up.\
\
'Upon this hill are five points arranged as a star, and between them we shall race. Can you follow me, little ${RACE}?\
\
Come then, and let the challenge begin! If you lose sight of me, you shall be lost....'","Follow the spirit to the second lith","After speaking with the Falcon-spirit, you must drink from the strange pool to escape from this eerie realm of spirits.","You must follow Gwenaewen's spirit!","You have reached the mystic pool!","Follow the spirit to the third lith","As you lean down and drink from the pool, strange visions dance before your eyes, and the odd mist that had fallen upon the forest begins to lift.","Follow the spirit to the mystic pool","Speak with the Ancient Spirit","Instance: The Wild Hunt -- Gwenaewen's Spirit","Follow the spirit to the fourth lith","Follow the spirit to the first lith","You have reached the fourth lith"},
[7389]={"'Go now little one. You have proven yourself, but this is not your place. The waking world awaits you.'","Instance: The Wild Hunt -- Lavaneth's Spirit","Challenge the boar-spirit","The boar glowers at you, temperamentally pawing at the ground as you approach. Its white tusks are long and deadly, glimmering in the starlight.","As you lean down and drink from the pool, strange visions dance before your eyes, and the odd mist that had fallen upon the forest begins to lift.","Speak with the Boar-spirit","You have defeated the boar-spirit","After speaking with the Boar-spirit, you must drink from the strange pool to escape from this eerie realm of spirits.","Lavaneth has bidden you challenge an ancient spirit of strength in the Wild Hunt that the Huntsman has set before you.","Approach the ancient spirit and prove your strength in challenge against it."},
[7390]={"'Welcome, little ${PLAYER}. You are prepared to endure the crashing waves of brutal fate?\
\
'They come even now as a howling fury in the night. Jaws that would tear and crush, heartless as the darkest moon.\
\
'Stand ready!'","Speak with the Ox-spirit","The ox-spirit has set before you a challenge of endurance. You must both survive against the waves of crushing despair before you.","As you lean down and drink from the pool, strange visions dance before your eyes, and the odd mist that had fallen upon the forest begins to lift.","Munfaeril has bidden you challenge an ancient spirit as a test of endurance in the Wild Hunt that the Huntsman has set before you.","'I have seen you stand fast and endure what many could not. I cannot say that you will survive what lies before you unbowed, but you are prepared.\
\
'Now return to your place in the world lest you become lost in dreams.'","Challenge the ox-spirit","Having faced your challenge and emerged unbowed, you may now return to the waking world through the waters of the pool.","The ox-spirit has perservered","Instance: The Wild Hunt -- Munfaeril's Spirit"},
[7391]={"Talk to Penrod","You have come into Tûr Morva to meet with Lheu Brenin, leader of the Falcon-clan.","Lheu Brenin is waiting to speak with you.","'It is nothing, ${PLAYER}. The stone only grazed me. I am fine.'","Follow Léolin through Tûr Morva","Meet with Lheu Brenin, leader of the Falcon-clan","Talk to Léolin","Mair is not pleased at whoever threw the rock at Saeradan.","'We will help them make their preparations, ${PLAYER}. Our aims do not line up perfectly with those of the people of Dunland, but we do share a common enemy. Let Saruman be distracted by the Falcon-clan while we make our way through the Gap of Rohan unobserved.'","Habla con Halbarad","Talk to Lheu Brenin","'This way, please. I have sent word ahead to Lheu Brenin, and he is awaiting your arrival.'","Saeradan has been hit by a stone thrown by a Dunlending. You should check to make sure that he is all right.","Instancia: La voluntad de resistir","Follow Léolin into Tûr Morva","Halbarad is on the path leading up to Tûr Morva.","'I am sorry your welcome to Tûr Morva was marred in this way, ${PLAYER}. Saruman will never command the loyalty of the Falcon-clan, and the more he tries, the stronger my resolve will grow. I had thought my people stood with me in this, but it seems some are unwilling to respect my wishes.\
\
'The Wizard sent an emissary to buy our loyalties with gold and silver. I have him locked in the dungeon. It will not be long before he sends another, but this one may have an army at his back. We can help you against Saruman, but first we need to prepare our own defences.'","'I will find out who threw that stone, and they will pay for it. You are the guests of my father, and you are under his protection while you are in our village!\
\
'It is an affront to my father, it is an affront to me, and it is an affront to the Hebog-lûth!'","Léolin is leading you up the hill to meet with Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva.","Habla con Saeradan","Lheu Brenin's first Brehur, Penrod, is ready to speak with you.","Léolin is on the path leading up to Tûr Morva.","Halbarad is waiting to speak with you.","'Remain alert, ${PLAYER}, but try not to offend them. This is their land, and passage south will be easier if we can count the Falcon-clan among our allies. If half the stories they tell in Lhanuch about Lheu Brenin are true, we do not need him as an enemy.'","Léolin is leading you through Tûr Morva to meet with Lheu Brenin, the leader of the Falcon-clan.","'Welcome to Tûr Morva, travellers from the north! It is the hope of Lheu Brenin that you share our desire for peace. Can there be friendship between our people?'","Talk to Mair","The Grey Company has come to Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras, to meet with Lheu Brenin, the leader of the Falcon-clan.","'Penrod will tell you what still needs to be done. I will show you to him.'"},
[7392]={"Mithrandir is by the young sapling atop Mindolluin.","King Elessar is by the young sapling atop Mindolluin.","Talk to King Elessar on the slope of Mindolluin","Find the sapling amid the snows atop Mindolluin","You have come with King Elessar and Mithrandir to a secret path high above Minas Tirith, on the slopes of Mount Mindolluin.","You have come with King Elessar and Mithrandir to a secret path high above Minas Tirith.","'I see in this discovery a sign that Gondor will once more come to prosperity, and the line of kings will survive the numbering of my own days. My heart is made glad!\
\
'I will remove this sapling with care, and bring it to the Court of the Fountain, there to be planted. The White Tree will grow there, once again, and may the voices of the people sing with joy at the sight!'","Instancia: El Mago y el Rey","'I do not know why Mithrandir wished for us to climb the slope of Mindolluin, but I am pleased you are here as well, ${PLAYER}. It will do us much good to breathe the cold, clear air of the heights!\
\
'Remain alert for members of the Withered Tree. They have continued to speak against my rule, and while there has been no outright violence since the slaying of Mauthoi, still I fear it may come.'","A sapling grows by the snow line high atop Mount Mindolluin.","'In shape and form this sapling is unmistakable, ${PLAYER}! This can be nothing other than young growth of the White Tree, but that has been dead for hundreds of years and this sapling can be no more than seven years old!\
\
'How can this wonder be possible?'","Remain alert for any sign of danger","At the very edge of the snow grows a young sapling","Talk to King Elessar on Mindolluin","Talk to Mithrandir on Mindolluin","You have come with Mithrandir and Elessar to a secret path high above the city.","'I see in this sapling much that identifies it as descended from the royal line of Telperion, Eldest of Trees, from which came through several generations the White Tree that grew in the Court of the Fountain. But that tree withered and died, and was left atop the city.\
\
'But it seems now that a fruit was taken from it before it died, and was brought to this high hallow by unknown hands. It was left here on the mountainside, and the life within it lay sleeping. It remained here hidden for hundreds of years, much as the line of kings stayed hidden in the North.\
\
'As the new age approached, the life sleeping within the fruit gave rise to this sapling, and it has grown here on the snow-line for a few years only. Remember this, King Elessar! The fruit ripens but rarely, yet if it does, one should be planted or the line might die out of the world.'"},
[7393]={"You are Gríma Wormtongue, advisor and servant to Saruman the White. He has been visited by Radagast the Brown, and you and Acca are waiting to hear if your master has any commands for you.","Acca wants to speak with you on the pinnacle of Orthanc.","Saruman is in the gardens of Isengard and wants to speak with you.","'Promise me that you will not tell our master about this. We have done nothing wrong, of course, but there is no sense in disturbing him. What is one more loaf of bread? No one will miss it.'","'Our master was right, Gríma! The guards report that Gandalf was seen riding hard alongside the river, and now he is here! Radagast has done as he was asked!\
\
'Let us go meet Gandalf and bring him to Orthanc!'","Saruman listens as you breathlessly recount Acca's recent delivery of a loaf of bread to Gandalf, and their ensuing conversation. His face is a thundercloud.\
\
'Why did you allow Acca to do this? Dog! What would you have done if he allowed Gandalf to come down? What would have been your answer if my worthless steward had freed him?'\
\
Saruman masters his anger, but his tone is no less stern.\
\
'From this point onward, none will climb the steps to the pinnacle save myself. I will have Acca thrown in the dungeons, where he will have time enough to consider this betrayal. He will have not even a crust to chew upon; let him eat slop instead.\
\
'You will perform Acca's duties in his stead, until I have others for you. And I will, Gríma. Soon you will return to your homeland. But not yet.'","Talk to Acca on the pinnacle of Orthanc","Talk to Saruman in the gardens of Isengard","Acca has come to the pinnacle of Orthanc with a basket of bread for Gandalf. You should talk to him.","Listen to Acca's story continue","Saruman is on the steps of Orthanc.","Talk to Acca in the gardens of Isengard","Acca is telling you the story of his downfall as the steward of Saruman's household.","Acca is near the steps of Orthanc, listening to the conversation of Gandalf and Saruman. You should speak with him.","Talk to Acca outside Orthanc","Listen to Acca's story continue.","'No, I will not be dissuaded, Gríma. He is an old man and does not deserve this treatment at the hands of our master. If Saruman fears Gandalf plans to hatch an evil plot, keep him imprisoned, yes, but in comfortable quarters. The pinnacle is exposed to the elements. It is cruel treatment, not befitting Saruman the Wise.\
\
'It is not our place to challenge Saruman's decisions, but I will do what I can to ease Gandalf's stay with us. An extra ration of bread will do no harm.\
\
'There is no need to tell Saruman of this, of course.'","See to Gandalf's horse while Acca escorts the Wizard to Saruman","Listen to Acca continue his story.","You have overheard Saruman speaking of some troubling things, but Acca can make no sense of them.","'Gandalf seems much older than I remember from his last visit, older and weaker. Look at him there, then look at our master. See how Saruman's raiment glows! Gandalf's cloak seems so tattered.\
\
'It is charitable of our master to offer his wisdom to the Grey Wizard. Perhaps he could offer some finer clothing, as well!'","Talk to Saruman on the steps of Orthanc","Talk to Acca near the gates of Isengard","Instancia: El Valle del Mago","Acca is waiting to speak with you.","You are to take care of Gandalf's horse while Acca brings the Wizard to speak with Saruman.","'They have been long in conversation, Gríma. What do you think they are speaking about?'","'Could you make any sense of that, Gríma? Our master holds you in closer confidence than he does me. Have you heard nothing of these matters?\
\
'I need not be counted among the Wise to know that they have Radagast worried, and that gives me reason to worry as well!\
\
'I am sure our master will know what must be done. That is why he is the Wizard, and we are the servants! We know our place, do we not? We do!'","Gandalf's horse is tired from its long journey and will benefit from a stay in the stables with food and water.","Acca's story continues.","Listen to Acca continue his tale","Find Saruman within Orthanc and tell him of Acca's sympathies","You must find Saruman within Orthanc and tell him of Acca's sympathies.","'Stay out from underfoot. I do not want to be disturbed until I send for you.'","'It is done. Radagast will find Gandalf, if he is to be found, and I doubt not he will speed with all haste here to Isengard.\
\
'There are some other small matters I need you to attend to before my guest arrives....'"},
[7394]={"Attend the meeting of the Kindred of the Coins and Shâra Mizâdi of Renewed Hamât","An Umbari guardsman has asked you to speak on behalf of Inkanûsh.","'Well? Who is this old man who speaks so to Umbari guardsmen?'\
\
You explain that Inkanûsh is a Wizard both powerful and wise, and he is a friend to Umbar. The guard looks from you to the Wizard and back again.\
\
'If you vouch for this man, ${PLAYER}, then I believe he is as you say. I have heard of your deeds on behalf of Umbar Baharbêl.'","Talk to Hármelak at the gate","Investigate the commotion at the gate with Inkanûsh","'You and your companions are of course welcome to accompany my forces as we move south in pursuit of Bârshud and his Ordâkhai! You have proven yourself a mighty ally already, ${PLAYER}, and have lent me aid and support beyond my most hopeful expectations.\
\
'I know little of Wizards, but if your friend has powers to lend to my cause, I invite him to use them openly and as he will!\
\
'Renewed Hamât welcomes you and your companions. My army will march south from the Ikorbân Valley and into Mûr Ghala, the Ridge of Plenty. We will put an end to Bârshud and prevent the Ordâkhai from ever again threatening our lands.'","It has not taken long for Mithrandir, now using the name Inkanûsh, to involve himself in the affairs of Umbar and Shagâna.","Enter the Citadel of the Winds as a guest of the Kindred","Talk to Shâra Mizâdi in the Citadel of Winds","Observe the confrontation at the gate and be ready to intervene if it comes to violence","Mizâdi calls for you to speak with her","The others have already gone ahead, but Rahâzi has lingered","Rahâzi has stayed behind to speak with you in the Citadel of Winds.","You have helped to ease some of the tension between the two groups at the gate, but you should remain on guard just in case.","Hármelak motions for you to come speak with her","Hármelak has indicated that she wants to speak with you before you leave.","'I know what your Wizard seeks, ${PLAYER}. He believes these ancient creatures, these Thardúth, remain a danger to us. I have heard the report of Kinsman Belondor's soldiers about the fighting at Utug-bûr, and to me it sounds like madness: the ravings of frightened men caught in the middle of a battle they cannot understand. Azagath perished at the hands of the Thardúth, and will not emerge from the darkness of Utug-bûr, but so too did those terrible creatures... is it not so? Who is it that remains to endanger us?\
\
'Ordâkh remains, ${PLAYER}. This has always been the true threat, not the ancient demons from which your Wizard would have us cower. This is why Umbar will support Mizâdi's pursuit of her foe south across the Ikorbân and into Mûr Ghala. We are allies in this, for Ordâkh threatens us all.'","A commotion at the nearby gate has drawn your attention.","'It is fortunate that his wisdom aligns with mine, or I would disregard his opinion on the subject. But it is not seemly to leave foreign dignitaries on the doorstep.\
\
'Shâra Mizâdi and her assemblage will enjoy the comforts of the Citadel of Winds while I summon the rest of the Kindred of the Coins. I invite both you and your Wizard to attend our council as well, ${PLAYER}. These matters affect us all.'","Hármelak has come to the gate, and she has questions for you.","The guardsmen at the gate have stopped a group of warriors from entering the city.","Talk to the Umbari guardsman","Talk to Hármelak in the Citadel of Winds","Stand ready to prevent the outbreak of violence","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! My mother Girhâzi asked that I join Shâra Mizâdi's forces to oppose the Empire of Ordâkh and keep safe my homeland of Ambarûl, and so I have done. Already there has been fighting! The Battle for Hamât ended in victory, of a sort, but the villain Bârshud escaped with his life.\
\
'Shâra Mizâdi gifted me the blade of one of her Subuzûri, and I will wield it on her behalf for the good of Renewed Hamât, and for the protection of Ambarûl and Iridír!\
\
'But we should not delay. The council may have already started!'","Shâra Mizâdi desires to speak with you before the attendees disperse.","The Kindred of the Coins meets with Shâra Mizâdi of Renewed Hamât to discuss the relationship between their two powers and the days to come.","Talk to Rahâzi in the Citadel of Winds","You and Inkanûsh have been invited to attend the meeting of the Kindred of the Coins with Shâra Mizâdi within the Citadel of Winds.","Instancia: El Mago, la Reina y los Hermanos"},
[7395]={"Habla con Huldar","Huldar está en las minas de Othrikar.\
\
Has repelido el ataque a Othrikar, y ahora debes hablar con Huldar.","'Mis heridas no son graves. Déjame recuperar el aliento y estaré bien.\
\
'Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}. Mis enanos y yo tuvimos la fortuna de que llegaras a Othrikar cuando lo hiciste, ¡y tu habilidad durante esta batalla no será olvidada!'","Evita perder a tres centinelas de Othrikar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instancia: La Palabra de un Sanador","Huldar está en el centro de Othrikar.\
\
El enano Huldar está esperando para hablar contigo.","El ataque de los Duramano ha sido repelido","Apoya a los centinelas de Othrikar en la posición de Huldar","El ataque de los Duramano es inminente, y Huldar te ha pedido ayudar en la defensa de Othrikar.","Huldar ha sido herido en batalla, y ahora las centinelas de Othrikar en las minas están sin su Maestro Rúnico. Debes reemplazar a Huldar antes de que sea demasiado tarde.","'Los Duramano estarán aquí en cualquier momento, ${PLAYER}, y debemos estar listos.\
\
'Ven conmigo, y te mostraré tu posición.'","Apoya a los centinelas de Othrikar contra los Duramano","¡Una centinela de Othrikar ha caído en batalla!","Los Duramano planean atacar Othrikar, y se te ha encomendado mantener a los defensores enanos luchando el mayor tiempo posible.","'Si me ofreces tu brazo, te agradeceré el apoyo mientras caminamos de vuelta al centro del puesto avanzado.'"},
[7396]={"Haldir espera hablar contigo sobre las preocupaciones del Señor Celeborn.","'El Señor Celeborn está esperando, ${PLAYER}. Ven conmigo, pues desea mucho hablar contigo.'","Celeborn te ha llamado a una audiencia en Caras Galadhon.","Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:llamado[m]|llamada[f]} a hablar con Celeborn de Lórien tras la derrota de Mazog.","Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:convocado[m]|convocada[f]} a una audiencia con el Señor Celeborn de Lórien, y ahora debes hablar con Haldir.","Escucha lo que Celeborn tiene que decirte","Instancia: Las preocupaciones del Señor Celeborn","Habla con Haldir","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir, ? Comparto las preocupaciones del Señor Celeborn; hablemos de ellas mientras caminamos.'"},
[7397]={"Instancia: Cavaron Demasiado Rápido","Independientemente de lo que Balin haya logrado aquí, este lugar ya no es seguro para ningún minero","Gufi cree que estás exagerando los peligros con los que te topaste durante tu misión de exploración, y te ha pedido que explores un posible yacimiento minero de la época de Balin.","Has encontrado los picos de los mineros de Balin, y nada más que peligros.","Recupera los artefactos de la expedición de Balin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pico de minero conseguido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Un silencio sepulcral envuelve la mina, solo interrumpido por los sonidos extraños de los Gredbyg. Averigua todo lo que puedas sobre la expedición minera de Balin."},
[7398]={"Los saqueadores de tumbas han sido derrotados","Los Montaraces no deben ser derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instancia: El Azote de los Ladrones","Los Montaraces han venido a Rantost para expulsar a los saqueadores de tumbas y recuperar las reliquias robadas.","Habla con Eliot Bencroft","Los Montaraces han tomado posiciones en tres campamentos en la isla de Rantost.\
\
Defiende a los Montaraces de los ataques de los saqueadores de tumbas y sus aliados.","Un Montaraz ha caído (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para reunirnos de nuevo en nuestro campamento? Háblame cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para partir.'","'Aún no deseo revelar a los saqueadores de tumbas que soy el espía. ¡No pienses mal de mí por quedarme aquí escondido! Debes apresurarte a ayudar a los Montaraces en la isla. Creo que han establecido campamentos en los tres lugares donde encontraste montones de reliquias.\
\
'Uno está justo aquí, otro en el centro de las ruinas y otro al oeste de las ruinas. ¡Es probable que los saqueadores de tumbas asalten a los Montaraces en los tres sitios!'"},
[7399]={"Sigrun knows of Thorog and will lead the way to examine the dragon's corpse.","Experience the vision","Examine the corpse of Thorog.","Experience the vision.","Instancia: El Legado de Thorog","Examine the rust spot.","Examine the corpse of Thorog","'Not much to see here but some old bones. You are ready to leave already?'","The strange vision disperses","Another vision comes over you","Examine the rust spot","It is unmistakable: some of Thorog's bones are missing"},
[7402]={"Habla con Dewernt Correhuela","Has ayudado a Derwent Correhuela a enfrentarse a las exigencias de Bill Helechal.","Quédate junto a Derwent Correhuela y luce amenazante","Instancia: La Amenaza de un Buen Golpe","Habla con Derwent Correhuela","'¡Lo logramos, ! Bueno, lo lograste tú, y no puedo agradecerte lo suficiente. ¡Parece que es bueno tener luchadores cerca cuando hay matones que necesitan una lección!\
\
'Déjalos. Esos golpes y moretones les enseñarán a no meterse con nosotros.'","Derrota a los matones de Bill Helechal","No quiero tener nada que ver contigo, ${PLAYERNAME:Luchador[m]|Luchadora[f]}. Pero vas a querer cuidarte de Bill Helechal. Ese nunca olvida.'","Derwent Correhuela, de Bree, ha solicitado ${PLAYERNAME:un Luchador[m]|una Luchadora[f]} de aspecto feroz que se ponga a su lado cuando se reúna con varios rufianes que pretenden estafarlo de su paga.","Bajo la cobertura de la oscuridad has venido con Derwent Correhuela al lugar de reunión en el sur de Bree.","'Ya casi estamos, ${PLAYER}. Yo haré la parte de hablar... pero tú deberías lucir tan feroz como puedas.\
\
'¡Esperemos que esto no termine en violencia, pero si ocurre dejaré las peleas en tus capaces puños!'"},
[7403]={"Examina el cofre del tesoro que William quiere darle a Bingo","Bingo está en el bloqueo del norte de Enedwaith.","Uno de los antiguos bandidos te hace señas para que hables con él.","'¿William quiere que tenga el tesoro? Bueno, supongo que podemos llevarlo con nosotros. No hice nada para merecerlo, pero sus dueños legítimos probablemente no vendrán a buscarlo. Los orcos que lo reunieron se habrán encargado de eso.\
\
'Me alegra que no haya habido derramamiento de sangre hoy, ${PLAYER}. Solo tuve que mirar a los bandidos para saber que no podían compararse con ninguno de nosotros. Necesitaban palabras, no castigo por su pobre decisión de detenernos.\
\
'¡Estoy listo para continuar nuestro viaje de regreso a casa!'","Habla con Bingo en el camino a través de Enedwaith","El pequeño cofre contiene muchas monedas de oro","¡Bingo ha sido derrotado!","Habla con William en el bloqueo","'Cuando Teodoro y yo pasamos por aquí en nuestro viaje hacia el sur, había una gran concentración de orcos y semiorcos en las ruinas justo más adelante. Pudimos escabullirnos sin ser vistos, pero no creo que tengamos tanta suerte esta vez.\
\
'Si llega a haber combate, deberías intentar proteger a Bingo de las espadas y flechas de los orcos. ¡Yo tendré las manos llenas tratando de evitar que derriben a Teodoro con un golpe afortunado!\
\
'Quizá podamos rodear las ruinas si su número ha aumentado. No lo sabremos hasta acercarnos.'","Habla con Bingo en la barrera","Bingo está en el camino a través de Enedwaith, preparándose para enfrentarse al bloqueo orco.","Deja que Bingo diga lo suyo, pero permanece alerta","'Quiero darte las gracias por dejar que tu amigo hiciera entrar en razón a Graham. No estaba seguro de que este intento fuera a funcionar, y cuando vimos a tu grupo acercarse por el camino, me convencí de que íbamos a morir todos. Nuestra carrera como bandidos ha sido corta, pero mejor eso que que nuestras vidas fueran cortas.\
\
'Los orcos habían abandonado este bloqueo cuando llegamos. Graham cree que algo tuvo que alejarlos, y deprisa. Sea cual sea la razón, dejaron algo de botín atrás. Quiero que se lo des a Bingo, ¡como regalo de quienes salvaron su vida hoy!\
\
'¡Adiós! Ahora nos volveremos granjeros, como siempre deberíamos haber sido.'","Haley está en la carretera norte a través de Enedwaith y quiere decirte algo antes que sigas tu ruta.","El líder de los bandidos te hace señas para que te acerques.","'Este camino lleva hacia el norte durante muchas millas. ¡Haley me dice que nos llevará a las Tierras de Bree!'","El largo camino hacia el norte ha sido bloqueado por gente poco recomendable, pero Bingo deberá pasar de algún modo si quiere llegar al final de su viaje.","'No me gusta nada este asunto del bloqueo orco, ${PLAYER}. Aplastar bichos en la guarida de un dragón es una cosa, ¡pero luchar contra orcos es otra muy distinta! No creo estar preparado para esto.\
\
'Haré lo que Haley sugiere y te dejaré todo el combate a ti.'","Habla con Graham el Cruel, el líder de los bandidos","Habla con Haley en el camino a través de Enedwaith","'¿Os creéis aventureros, eh? Será mejor que nos deis lo que queremos o acabaréis en el lado equivocado de nuestras armas.'\
\
Evalúas en silencio a la banda de bandidos, observando su ropa despareja y la mala calidad de sus armas. Son hombres inexpertos, más habituados a palas y arados que a cuchillos y espadas. Son nuevos en esto del bandidaje y, si llega a haber combate, sabes algo más: todos morirán antes de que Bingo se quite las manos de los ojos.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Bingo no debe ser derrotado!</rgb>","Bingo tiene algo que decirles a los bandidos.","Bingo tose y avanza a zancadas","Elimina a todos los bandidos","Los bandidos no te dejarán pasar y deben ser eliminados.","William te dijo que parte del botín fue dejado atrás por los orcos y quiere que Bingo lo tenga.","Instancia: A través del bloqueo"},
[7404]={"The farmers are gathering near the barn, and are concerned that Ragnold may not be safe. He was on the far side of the farm when the western side was attacked.","Instancia: La granja de Thrymm","Talk to Oter","<rgb=#FF0000>You let Ragnold die!</rgb>","Defeat Warg-riders from the west (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defend Thrymm's Farm from the final assault","Follow Oter to the centre of Thrymm's Farm","The Warg-riders at Edsig's Farm were disrupted by your efforts, and their organized raids on the farms should stop. The farmers should finally be able to repair Thrymm's Farm and begin work on the fields.","Oter and the others have been cornered near the barn. The enemy is burning the farm to the ground. The chances of the farmers escaping and making a run for Forlaw are slim.","<rgb=#FF0000>You let Oter die!</rgb>","Observe what Laudh has to say","Warg-riders defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not let any farmers die</rgb>","The farmers were prepared to begin working the fields, but the enemy has begun a surprise attack on Thrymm's Farm!","<rgb=#FF0000>You let Torwulf die!</rgb>","Follow Oter to the western fields","'We are in trouble. They have us surrounded! The only way we can survive is to fight. There is no way we can escape this time....'","Defeat Warg-riders from the south (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Laudh is capturing the farmers and leaving you at Thrymm's Farm, to either die there or to inform Forlaw of what happened. He is convinced Núrzum will kill you eventually.","The rebuilding of Thrymm's Farm is underway. Oter has brought tools to the fields, and would like your help preparing the fields to produce crops for Forlaw.","'A few of the tools you collected were in pretty good shape, and should help us prepare these fields. Torwulf and Siric took tools out to the far field with them to begin working. Lets hurry over there to help them!'","The enemy is attacking from the south and are trying to trap you and the farmers on Thrymm's Farm while they burn it down.","Laudh has sent the captain of this band of Warg-riders to attack you and the farmers. He seems intent on capturing the farmers for some nefarious purpose.","<rgb=#FF0000>You let Siric die!</rgb>"},
[7406]={"Talk to Horn and approach the king","Horn is inside Meduseld, waiting to approach the king.","Instancia: Théoden, hijo de Thengel","Talk to Gandalf in Meduseld","'So that is done. I think that went rather well, considering what is at stake. We have so little time to waste, and much depends on haste! We cannot spend these precious moments squabbling among ourselves when the real foes lie without!\
\
'Save one: Gríma, son of Gálmód, called the Wormtongue. He is an enemy of Théoden and of Rohan, and he remains within. His fate will rest with the king, as it should.'","'We are not alone in the hall of Théoden, ${PLAYER}. Let us approach and see who has the ear of the king, but we will interfere only if it be in the interest of Rohan to do so!'","Witness the confrontation of Gandalf and Théoden, and allow harm to come to none","Inside Meduseld, Gandalf has revealed his nature and his good intentions to Théoden King. What will the king make of the tidings he brings?","Gandalf is in Meduseld and has attempted to lift the veil from Théoden's eyes as it concerns the plight of his people.","A hush hangs over the hall","You have returned to Meduseld against the wishes of Théoden, and now must see if he is receptive to the warning you bring.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. I am glad you made it here from Wildermore so quickly, but I will need to hear your report of that land at another time. All of us have work to do, for the king is not yet free of danger! Keep an eye on Gríma, if you would. He is slippery, and I fear he may intend further harm to the king. Whether he can work greater harm than he has already performed is a question for which I have no answer.\
\
'Stay on your guard.'","'Rohan, and Théoden, are not free of danger yet. Still we have work to do.'","Inside Meduseld, Gandalf appeals to Théoden. Will the king heed the warning he brings?"},
[7407]={"Ausma is frozen in a block of ice!","Find Ausma","Help Ausma while the Trio fights the hobgoblins!","Talk to Kyrstig","You have to escape!","Break ice block (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Broke ice block (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The plan to rescue Ausma begins with Kyrstig.","Instancia: En ayuda de Ausma","Escape with Ausma","The scouts Kyrstig, Molkha, and Klúso have stormed the hobgoblin fortress Shakhajât to rescue their master, Ausma. But it is unclear if they are too late, or if their help is needed at all.","You need to find Ausma.","'Come on, let's get back to camp. I need some time to lick my wounds and wallow in my failure.'","'Ausma must be in here if she went after Dushtalbúk. I hope you're ready for a fight.'","Stand by with the Scout Trio"},
[7408]={"Langlas requiere tu asistencia para encontrar y liberar a Avorthal. Debes cuidar las espaldas del otro, no sea que fallen.","'Ha sido una travesía larga y peligrosa, pero me alegra haberte tenido a mi lado durante todo este tiempo.\
\
'Vamos, ¡terminemos con esto!'","Habla con Langlas","Este es el corazón del campamento. El teniente de Skorgrím te está esperando. Habla con Langlas cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para enfrentar al villano y descubrir qué pasó con Avorthal.","Hakon Puñohierro ha sido derrotado, pero parece que Avorthal no está aquí. Habla con Langlas cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para regresar a la cabaña de caza.","'Debemos proceder sin demora. ¡Juntos, podemos derrotar a los Duramano y rescatar a Avorthal!'","Has viajado con Langlas hasta el campamento de los Duramano en un esfuerzo por rescatar al príncipe elfo Avorthal.","'Esto ha sido una pérdida de tiempo y sangre, ninguno de los cuales podemos permitirnos. Discutamos nuestros posibles caminos de regreso en la cabaña.'","Instancia: Evitar una guerra","'Ahora saben que estamos aquí. La lucha será peor más adelante.\
\
'Ahora. Es hora de irnos.'","Has avanzado en el campamento de los Duramano, pero el esfuerzo no fue fácil, y Langlas te ha aconsejado descansar antes de continuar. Debes hacerle saber a Langlas cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para continuar.","'Rápido, debemos regresar.'"},
[7409]={"Derrota a Amdir","Habla con Reniolind","Derrota a Amdir.\
\
Amdir se escondía en lo más profundo de las ruinas y abatió a Reniolind antes de centrar su atención en ti.","Reniolind se encuentra en el Fuerte de Aguas Pantanosas, al oeste de la Cueva de la Reunión.\
\
En su último suspiro, Mundol el Montaraz te suplicó que salvaras a Reniolind, otro de su gente, de la furia asesina de Amdir.","Al entrar en la Cueva de la Reunión, descubriste que era demasiado tarde para ayudar a Mundol el Montaraz. Amdir ya lo había herido de muerte. Mundol te pidió que llevaras un aviso a Reniolind, un joven erudito Montaraz que está estudiando las ruinas del viejo Fuerte de Aguas Pantanosas.","Instancia: A la ayuda de un Montaraz","'Toradan y Mundol han muerto los dos? ¡No puedo creerlo! Me enviaron aquí para vigilar después de que los Nazgûl nos echaran de la Comarca, pero ahora parece que mi vigilancia no ha servido de nada.\
\
'Debemos ir a ver al jefe de mi gente. Los hombres de Bree lo llaman Trancos.\
\
'Hay un camino más rápido que el que tomaste para volver a Bree. Sígueme y te guiaré por las cuevas que se extienden bajo los pantanos.'","Reniolind yace moribundo en el suelo de las cuevas.\
\
Reniolind te ha mostrado un pasaje secreto bajo los Pantanos de Moscagua, en las cuevas que se encuentran bajo las ruinas. Al final, encontraste a Amdir esperándote. Amdir hirió mortalmente a Reniolind antes de huir. El Montaraz moribundo desea hablar contigo.","'Amdir está... libre. Vete sin demora... encuentra a Trancos en Bree. Él es... mi jefe y debe... saber lo que ha pasado. Habla con Cebadilla Mantecona... en El Poney Pisador. Él sabrá... dónde encontrar a Aragorn.\
\
'Toma la puerta de esta habitación y te... encontrarás en el extremo oeste de los Pantanos de Moscagua. Ve al oeste... desde allí, luego al sur y al oeste... por el camino hacia Bree.'","Amdir invocó a una reina araña gigante antes de huir. Mata a la araña y habla con el Montaraz moribundo."},
[7410]={"Ashâmi is too injured to continue. You have failed","Instancia: Juntos ahora","You, Raphûz, and Ashâmi are distracting the enemy forces from a main assault on Kûr Anzar.","The words from the cultist linger in the air","'What did he mean, 'The Firstborn return from their long slumber?' What evil grows beyond Imhûlar? Let us return to Numûru with haste.'","Your assault was successful, but the madness of the cultists weighs on Ashâmi and Raphûz. You should make haste and return to Urmâkh.","Speak with Raphûz to begin the assault","Speak with Ashâmi to return to Urmâkh","'We will do what must be done. Let us fight through the enemy and give the main force the distraction they need to retake parts of the ruins.'"},
[7411]={"Gandalf has commanded you to ride for the city of Minas Tirith, while he follows with Prince Imrahil and the wounded Faramir.","Ride for the gates of Minas Tirith","Instancia: Demasiado lejos de la ciudad","'Faramir has sustained a wound, ${PLAYER}. Soon the enemy will surround us... he cannot stay here.\
\
'Ride for the city! I will follow with Faramir and Prince Imrahil. Go now!'","Talk to Faramir on the Pelennor Fields","Faramir has fallen from his horse! He seems to have suffered a terrible injury.","A dart flies right by your head, missing by inches, and then another!","Talk to Gandalf on the Pelennor","You have come to Minas Tirith in time!","Faramir, Captain of Gondor, is beset on all sides by the forces of the enemy! You must help him reach Minas Tirith!","Gandalf has crossed the field in the company of Prince Imrahil and his swan-knights, and he motions for you to speak with him.","Ride across the Pelennor toward Minas Tirith","'I do not know you, stranger, but I can tell by your livery you are a friend! My men and I must reach the White City, but we were pursued. Southrons harry us on foot and on horseback, and terrible wraiths attack from the skies!\
\
'Fight them off, my friend! We must reach the city, if we can!'","You can hear the sound of fighting ahead of you, in the middle of the Pelennor. Someone needs your help!","Stand beside Faramir, and defend him from his foes","You have found Faramir, but the young captain is hard-pressed on all sides!","The time has come for you to ride to Minas Tirith, but the enemy will be close on your heels."},
[7412]={"Flee Middlemead with Thane Mágla","You have discovered steeds left unharmed","A din rising outside the Mead Hall signals the arrival of the White Hand","Approach Thane Mágla in the Mead Hall","Travel out of the Mead Hall with Mágla","Listen to Mágla","Defeat Hildulf","DNT -- Players will not see","Mágla can be found at the table.\
\
Mágla sees no hope for Rohan. You should tell him of your journeys in the Eastemnet.","Thane Mágla can be found in the Mead Hall of Middlemead.\
\
You should listen to Thane Mágla.","Mágla can be found in the Mead Hall.\
\
You should travel outside to confront the White Hand with Mágla.","Mágla is in Middlemead.\
\
You should aid Mágla in escaping Middlemead.","Mágla can be found at the table.\
\
Mágla sees no hope for Rohan. You should disagree with him.","'We must flee, ${PLAYER}. Let us ride to Edoras, and rejoin with the others.'","'What madness has fallen on Middlemead?'","'Let us flee with haste, ${PLAYER}.'","Thane Mágla has been defeated!","Mágla is in Middlemead.\
\
You should fight through Middlemead with Mágla.","Mágla is at the table in the Mead Hall of Middlemead.\
\
You should wait with Mágla as he decides what action to take.","After sending his people to safety, Thane Mágla remains behind to defend Middlemead from the White Hand.","Listen to Thane Mágla","Thane Mágla is sitting at his table.\
\
Mágla has asked you to speak with him.","Talk to Thane Mágla","Instancia: Intercambiando Destinos","'Alas for Middlemead! Look what the White Hand has done already!\
\
'We must move swiftly if we are to escape with our lives!'","Mágla must be convinced to stand with his people","Tell Mágla a <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb> of your adventures in the Eastemnet","Tell Mágla <rgb=#FF00FF>no</rgb>","<rgb=#FF00FF>Challenge</rgb> Mágla to lead once more","Thane Mágla can be found outside the Mead Hall of Middlemead.\
\
You have escaped the White Hand forces and made your way to the horses. You should speak to Thane Mágla and flee!","Horses can be found to the south-east of the traders' pavillion.\
\
You should now escape Middlemead.","Share mead with Mágla","Hildulf can be found at the traders' pavillion in Middlemead.\
\
You have encountered Hildulf and Uruks, and should now defeat them.","<rgb=#FF0000>Thane Mágla must not be defeated</rgb>","Fight through Middlemead with Thane Mágla","The mead can be found on the table.\
\
Mágla has asked you to share a drink with him.","Mágla can be found at the table.\
\
Mágla is beginning to believe that hope remains. You should challenge him."},
[7414]={"'¿Es un pueblo lo que se ve allá abajo, al otro lado de la llanura? ¡Vayamos de inmediato y dejemos atrás a este dragón!'","La voz de Bingo es poco más que un susurro.\
\
'Camina con cuidado, ${PLAYER}. No queremos despertar a este dragón.'","Bingo ha entrado en la guarida del poderoso Draigoch para rescatar a Teodoro Tojo... ¡si no es ya demasiado tarde!","¡Bingo ha sido derrotado!","Corre hacia la cuerda y escapa de la guarida de Draigoch","Has encontrado a Teodoro Tojo en las profundidades de la guarida de Draigoch.","Hasta ahora, la suerte te ha acompañado. El dragón está dormido","'Bueno, ¡eso estuvo cerca! Aun así, todo salió bien, ¿no? ¡Y me alegra haberme deshecho de la Piedra de Roth!\
\
'Entonces, ¿qué haremos ahora, mis amistades aventureras? ¡Teodoro Tojo está listo para lo que sea!'","Habla con Teodoro Tojo en la guarida de Draigoch","¡Has fallado, y Draigoch se cobra otra víctima!","<rgb=#FF0000>Escapa antes de que la guarida se llene de fuego</rgb>","'No podía esperar más, ${PLAYER}, y menos mal que los seguí cuando lo hice, porque parece que no tienen forma de bajar desde este saliente hasta el fondo de la guarida. ¿Cómo van a rescatar a Teodoro si no pueden llegar hasta él?\
\
'Bueno, tengo una cuerda. La ataré a una roca aquí arriba y podremos bajar hasta el fondo para salvar a Teodoro. Tendremos que ser muy, muy sigilosos, así que actúa con cuidado.\
\
'¡Bien, dejemos esta cuerda atada!'","¡El dragón está despierto! ¡Debes llegar a la cuerda antes de que la guarida se llene de fuego!","Teodoro hace lo posible por susurrar.\
\
'La Piedra de Roth estará a salvo aquí, ${PLAYER}. ¡Que le dé a este dragón toda la mala suerte que pueda producir y nos deje en paz a Haley y a mí!\
\
'Es curioso, pero al mirar todo este tesoro me doy cuenta de que no deseo ni la porción más pequeña. Tal vez ya haya terminado con la búsqueda de tesoros, después de todo. No tenías por qué venir a buscarme, pero aun así me conmueve. He entregado un tesoro, pero he encontrado otro: ¡qué buenas amistades tengo!\
\
'Deberíamos ir hacia la salida antes de que esta criatura despierte. Yo sé que cuando me levanto por la mañana, ¡lo primero que quiero es algo para picar!'","Habla con Bingo en la guarida de Draigoch","¡El dragón empieza a despertarse!","Instancia: Tesoro perdido, tesoro encontrado","Bingo está en la entrada de la guarida de Draigoch y espera rescatar a Teodoro Tojo antes de que sea demasiado tarde.","Desciende por la cuerda para llegar al fondo de la guarida de Draigoch","Escabúllete junto al dragón dormido con Bingo","Haley Pradodulce desenrolla su cuerda y la ata firmemente a un saliente rocoso","'Oh cielos... ¡mira a este pobre infeliz! Este no es un lugar seguro en absoluto, ${PLAYER}. Parece que ladrones han entrado aquí de vez en cuando, y quienes no cayeron víctimas del fuego del dragón quizá encontraron su final a manos de quienes los acompañaban. Cuando hay tesoro de por medio, incluso los buenos amigos pueden convertirse en enemigos por el reparto de una sola moneda.\
\
'¡Pero ahora mismo es el dragón lo que debe preocuparnos!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Bingo no debe ser derrotado</rgb>","Habla con Haley en la guarida de Draigoch","Habla con Teodoro Tojo fuera de la guarida de Draigoch","Teodoro Tojo está en el fondo de la guarida de Draigoch y debes descender para alcanzarlo.","Habla con Bingo en el fondo de la guarida de Draigoch","Bingo está en el fondo de la guarida de Draigoch y quiere hablar contigo de algo urgente.","Abandona la guarida con Teodoro Tojo, Haley Pradodulce y Bingo","Haley Pradodulce te ha seguido hasta un saliente con vista al dragón dormido.","¡Has encontrado a Teodoro Tojo en la guarida de Draigoch!","¡Has escapado de la guarida del dragón... pero justo a tiempo!"},
[7415]={"Return to Akhiz","Talk to Lacheg","Placed the ransom in the chest","'Listen!'\
\
His voice drops to a whisper.\
\
'Are we really to give these honourless men ransom-gold for their villainy? You look a capable fighter. Let us instead create a distraction. I have managed to get a small blade in my  hands, here. When I hear a commotion, I will cut our bonds and we will make for the door. Then we shall meet up at whatever place my brother chooses.\
\
'Will you do it? Say you will!'","It is time to meet with Jarl Akhiz and free Glánhar's sons.","Now that you have seen Lacheg and Togbor, return to Jarl Akhiz for the ransom payment and choose which of the brothers to heed.","Create a distraction","Talk to Togbor","Show Jarl Akhiz that you have brought the ransom.","It is time to leave the cellar in Bâr Nadhron.","Leave the cellar!","Go down into the cellar","'You are satisfied? Good! Then place the ransom in the chest there and all shall be arranged. You will leave first, and the brothers will be sent out separately after you. \
\
'This is how it is done. No trickery. I give you my word.'","'If you honour the agreement, so shall they. The Variags have this much of a sense of honesty, at any rate.\
\
'I hope I shall see you east of Bâr Nadhron, under the  bent tree by the Mouths of the Entwash, ${PLAYER}.'","'Did you heed my words? Create a distraction, and we shall cut our bonds and fly, and they will have not a single ransom-coin for their brigandry!'","You see Akhiz and some of his men up ahead, waiting for you.","'So our ransom will be paid, finally? Good. \
\
'Listen to me. These are dangerous men. But I have come to believe that they do have their own kind of blackguard's honour. If you do as they ask, they truly will set us free. If you do aught to alarm them, they will respond swiftly and ruthlessly. You must not listen to my brother's hot-headed prattling. Let us part with our gold and take our lives with us when we go.\
\
'They are likely to send us out one at a time. We must have an agreed upon place to meet. Hm... East of Bâr Nadhron, under the bent tree by the Mouths of the Entwash would do.  Yes, let us find each other there.'","Show Akhiz the ransom","Go down into the cellar in Bâr Nadhron and find Akhiz.","Place the ransom in the chest","Now that you have seen Lacheg and Togbor, return to Jarl Akhiz to complete the ransom.","Go past the opened gate and see that the hostages are all right.","'You have the gold and the brooch I asked of you? Tut tut! I can see it well enough from there. We will do this after the Variag fashion. Now you will go and see that the two brothers are safe and well.\
\
'I have only the two. Trust me, if I had the father and the other two, you would need tenfold the ransom you have brought.\
\
'Now go. You will find them to the right, that way beyond the gate.'","Instancia: Tratando con sinvergüenzas","'This is the Variag way: you go and see that the two brothers are hale and unharmed, and then you shall return and pay their ransom.'","The brazier post falls over with a crash!"},
[7416]={"Tras un momento de silencio tenso, los tres notáis que los temblores han cesado","<rgb=#FF00FF>Acuéstate</rgb> en tu litera e intenta descansar","Núluzagar puede encontrarse en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Tu breve descanso fue interrumpido por la dura voz del sectario Núluzagar. Debes escuchar a Núluzagar antes de que su paciencia se agote.","Lethi y Vaski pueden encontrarse en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Ansioso por compartir rumores mientras la Orden del Ojo está ausente, Vaski desea contarte lo que ha escuchado.","Lethi puede encontrarse en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Te has despertado de un breve descanso y encuentras a los otros Hachetones en tu celda también despiertos.","Estás intentando descansar.","Escucha a Vaski y Lethi","Vaski puede encontrarse en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Vaski ha oído varios rumores inquietantes en la Torre Oscura y desea compartirlos contigo.","Intenta descansar","Tras un día de arduo trabajo en Barad-dûr, regresas a las mazmorras para un breve respiro. Sin embargo, una repentina serie de temblores te ha sacado del descanso.","Núluzagar te mira impasible.","'No sé cómo puedes comer eso... hasta las ratas saben mejor.'\
\
Vaski mira hacia los pasillos de las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
'Ah, pero no creo que ninguno de los dos tenga que comer como orcos por mucho más tiempo. Ha habido rumores, ¿sabes...?\
\
'¿No los has oído?'","'Aún es temprano. Incluso para Él.'\
\
Lethi mira hacia arriba.\
\
'Lleva cerca de una hora, calculo. Supongo que es una vana esperanza creer que podremos descansar más antes del amanecer.\
\
'Aún te quedan un poco de tus raciones, ${PLAYER}. Deberías comer mientras puedas.'","Recoge tu plato","Habla con Vaski","Tu litera se encuentra en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Tras un tenso intercambio entre Lethi y Vaski, Lethi ha sugerido que todos intentéis descansar en vuestras literas antes del amanecer.","Tus raciones están sobre un pedazo de escombro cerca de tu litera en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Despertado por temblores y con pocas probabilidades de encontrar más descanso, Lethi ha sugerido que termines tus raciones antes de que los sectarios de la Orden del Ojo regresen a las mazmorras.","Termina tus raciones","Terminas tus raciones a regañadientes","Instancia: Temblores bajo Barad-dûr","Vaski puede encontrarse en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Después de dejar tu plato, Vaski te ha llamado. Deberías hablar con Vaski.","Los platos repiquetean al temblar de nuevo Barad-dûr","Dile a Vaski <rgb=#FF00FF>no</rgb> y pídele que comparta lo que oyó","'¿Eso es todo entonces, Vaski? ¿Nada más que la Orden deba oír?'\
\
Vaski abre la boca, pero al notar la severa mirada de Lethi, decide guardar silencio.\
\
'Me lo imaginaba.'","Lethi puede encontrarse en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Frustrado con la imprudencia de Vaski, Lethi ha puesto fin a la conversación.","Habla con Lethi","Habla con Núluzagar","Tu plato vacío de raciones está cerca de tu litera en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Deberías añadirlo a la pila de platos junto a la puerta de tu celda.","Justo cuando empiezas a dormirte, una voz familiar te increpa"},
[7417]={"Speak with Andreg at the Slade of Shadows.","Stop the elhudan from entering the cauldron","'${PLAYER}, you told me that the altars bore the same marks as the tokens you brought from Saeradan. If this is indeed the case, the tokens may perhaps be used to call Gwyllion and her allies to the Slade.\
\
'Come with me to the Slade of Shadows. There, we will see how the tokens may be of use to us.'","Collect the Token of the Ox from the second altar","'Enter the Slade and place the tokens upon the altars, then return here to me. If I am correct, we may soon see the end of the Old Woman of the Mountain.'","Andreg has a plan to draw forth and ensnare Gwyllion and her allies at the Slade of Shadows.","Andreg must not be defeated","Andreg is lying among the shards of the Dutegelh.\
\
You should see if there is anything you can do to help Andreg.","Defeat the Tribunal of Shadows.","Stop the elhudan and defeat the Tribunal of Shadows","Collect the Token of the Goat from the first altar","Defeated the Tribunal of Shadows","Follow Andreg to the Slade of Shadows.","Instancia: Tribunal de Sombras","Andreg is hiding near the Slade of Shadows.\
\
You should return to Andreg at once.","Talk to Andreg","Collect the Token of the Stag from the third altar","Wait with Andreg to see what happens","Place the Token of the Goat on the first altar","Place the Token of the Ox on the second altar","You should speak with Andreg to learn his plan.","Place the Token of the Stag on the third altar","Andreg has been defeated","'I shall not...be returning with you...${PLAYER}. The cost of defeating...death...is the life...of the living.\
\
'Return to...Saeradan and tell him...of our victory. Fare...well....'","'Unnh...${PLAYER}...when Gwyllion...said what she did...about the living...it...it reminded me of the...rest of the legend.\
\
'The Dutegelh's weakness is the...living spirit...the gift of life. It has...ended the darkness.\
\
'Collect the tokens of the gurach...from the altars, then...return to me...while I still have...breath....'","Andreg is lying mortally wounded among the shards of the Dutegelh at the heart of the Slade of Shadows.\
\
You should bring the tokens of the gurach to Andreg at once.","The three altars can be found between the trees at the heart of the Slade of Shadows.\
\
Andreg instructed you to place the tokens of the gurach on the altars within the Slade of Shadows.","Wait with Andreg to see what happens.","'Let us see if my plan will bear fruit....'","'The Old Woman of...the Mountain...lingers still, but not...unharmed. Now is the time to...strike. Now is the time to...move....'","The tokens of the gurach are upon the altars at the heart of the Slade of Shadows.\
\
Andreg instructed you to collect the tokens of the gurach and return to him."},
[7418]={"You are held in the grip of a dream","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.","'Sneaking and creeping, precious! Floating and hiding, no splishing and splashing! Like the fishes, gollum! Gollum!'\
\
The creature Gollum stares past you with its eyes like lamps, but even in the grip of the dream you feel a chill at the thought you might be seen.\
\
'Are you a nice fishy? Tasty? We need to keep up our strength, gollum, gollum. We can't take the precious if our handses are too weak to wrap and squeeze... we needs our strength.\
\
'Tasty fishy. Eat, and then we follows the precious, gollum! Gollum!'","Your sleep is troubled by dreams of ill omen. Do they hold any significance, or are they just dreams?","'¡No puedes esperar derrotarme!'","You are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Golodir on the shore of Lake Evendim","'What is it, Mister Frodo? You do not look well, and have not since we came back to the shore. That shape won't be coming back, I wager. Legolas saw to that with his arrows, he did, and a good thing it was, too!\
\
'You clutched your shoulder when it appeared, and looked to be in a great deal of pain. Are you sure you are feeling all right?","You are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith.","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\
\
Candaith is waiting for you by the entrance to Grimbold's camp.","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\
\
Morflak looms large in your memory, casting his shadow over all things.","Estás atrapado en un sueño.","Listen to Peregrin Took on the banks of the Anduin","You are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Frodo Baggins on the banks of the Anduin","'It was a good shot, Legolas, I will give you that. But up close? Nothing can best an axe in the hand of one of Durin's Folk. If that winged shadow had come just a hair lower I would have proven it, and you would have saved an arrow!\
\
'Your gift has proved useful, I grant that, but when I can make use of the Lady Galadriel's gift to me you will see a thing of wonder and beauty!'","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\
\
Lothrandir stands before you on the shore of Lake Evendim.","You are held in the grip of a dream.\
\
Candaith stands before you once more, looking puzzled about something.","Lothrandir stands before you, struggling against his bonds, but his eyes show no sign of despair. Defiance shines from those wells of blue, and his mouth is a resolute line.","You are held in the grip of a dream.\
\
Familiar faces have emerged from the fog of sleep.","You are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Aragorn on the banks of the Anduin","'He is your own foe to face, ${PLAYER}. I will not be able to help you stand against him, and you will be on your own. Let the knowledge that you have already proven the stronger lighten your heart and bring you courage!'","Instancia: Sueños Turbulentos","'Do not lose sight of who you are, my friend, and do not despair. I would give my life a thousand times to be even the smallest help to Aragorn, my chieftain. That is what it means to be one of the Dúnedain.\
\
'It was no different for these men of Rohan, or for their Prince. They strove to protect their people, and would do so again if given the opportunity. Weep for the need of it, but do not mourn their choice. I know they must be content.\
\
'Someone comes. Let us meet him at the gate, and keep him from further disturbing your rest!'","You know Théodred did not die at this place, but the sight of the fallen Prince still fills you with regret and with worry for the future of his kingdom.\
\
The dream holds you in its grip, and refuses to let you go.","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\
\
You have encountered Candaith, and even though you know you are asleep, it is still painful to see him.","You are held in the grip of a dream. Search the camp for survivors","'How are you feeling, Pip? When that winged shadow came out from behind that cloud, I thought we were done for. I was wrong, though! Thank goodness for the quick wits and quicker bow-strings of Elves!\
\
'I don't want to think too much about that dark shape, at least, not tonight! Maybe the memory will be less frightening in the daylight tomorrow.'","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\
\
No living person seems to be left in Grimbold's camp.","'Our journey leads us from danger into greater danger! To have lost Gandalf, to be pursued by Orcs from behind and to paddle into them ahead... what awaits us further down the river?\
\
'And Gollum is still behind us. If he were not so cunning, perhaps I could catch him with an arrow, but it seems he has learned something about staying alive.'","You are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith on the shore of Lake Evendim","'Your thoughts turn to your friends, but remember you are held in the grip of your dreams. Nothing you have seen here is real, ${PLAYER}. I am sure our friends will be fine.'\
\
Candaith does not sound as certain as you might wish, and you cannot help but wonder if that is proof of your own worrying doubt or something more.\
\
'What is this place, ${PLAYER}? That river could be the Anduin, but... have you ever seen this place? I wonder what has called it to your memory?'","Listen to Legolas on the banks of the Anduin","You are held in the grip of a dream. Walk with Candaith and see what he shows you","Candaith looks around at the corpse-strewn camp.\
\
'Your journey must have been an arduous one, ${PLAYER}, if this is the tapestry of your dreaming! May you find restful sleep at the end of your road, my friend, for I fear you will have little of that for a while.\
\
'Walk with me a ways, ${PLAYER}. There are some things we need to discuss.'","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\
\
Candaith is waiting for you on the shore of Lake Evendim.","You are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith before he goes","You are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Boromir on the banks of Anduin","Calenglad stares out at the lake, his eyes glassy. He takes no notice of you.","Golodir stands before you, tall and proud, but his eyes burn with fire and his lip is twisted into a sneer.","Boromir stands apart from the rest of the group, staring across the water to the far bank, but every now and then his eyes drift in the direction of the hobbits.","'Gimli says that shape we saw in the sky was a Balrog. You don't think it was, do you, Merry? I didn't get a good look at it, but that's what Gimli said. A Balrog, he said. You don't think it was, do you?'","Nothing moves within Grimbold's camp","You are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Samwise Gamgee on the banks of the Anduin","You are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Morflak and resist your fear","'I am fine, Sam. I felt a chill in my heart, and the pain in my shoulder reminded me of... well, it is gone now, nothing more than a passing memory. I think we will be fine for a while. The Orcs that attacked from the other shore were dismayed by the fall of... whatever that shadow may have been.\
\
'And yet, every paddle-stroke on the River brings us further south, and as it does my heart sinks southward still. Tonight the bow of Legolas saved us, but for how long will our fortune hold?\
\
'I am sorry, Sam. I do not want you to worry.'","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\
\
Golodir stands before you on the shore of Lake Evendim.","'In your hands, the bow of Galadriel is deadly indeed, Legolas! The entire company is in your debt. Did you mark how the shadow's fall dismayed the Orcs on the far shore? I feel they will not attack us again tonight.\
\
'My guess is that our clever waterman set them on us. We have evaded his tricks thus far. May our fortune hold!'","Your mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\
\
Calenglad stands before you on the shore of Lake Evendim.","You are held in the grip of a dream.\
\
A giant sword rises from the misty swamp before you.","You are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith at the gate before he goes","Listen to Gimli on the banks of the Anduin","You are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Merry Brandybuck on the banks of the Anduin","You are held in the grip of a dream. Examine the enormous sword that rises from the swamp before you","'Your dreaming mind roams far afield, ${PLAYER}. Asleep, you are much like a Ranger. I hope you do not mind my saying so.'\
\
Candaith chuckles, but the pleasant familiarity of the sound rings hollowly in the still air of the dream, and is soon gone.\
\
'Our friends have their own road now, ${PLAYER}. May they reach Aragorn in time to be of use to him! It is my hope the most dangerous leg of their journey is behind them, but I fear it is not so.'","You are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Calenglad on the shore of Lake Evendim","As you stare at Nona's lifeless body lying among the mist and the reeds, you feel the waking world beginning to rip away the veil of sleep from your eyes..."},
[7419]={"Talk to Getfleda and let her know what her friends had to say.","Hear Brunstan's side of the story","'Oh dear, you say that another of my friends was actually to blame for the loss of Sperling's sword? Oh my....'","Instancia: Amistad problemática","'Sperling has accused me of stealing the toy sword his father gave him, but I tell you I did not! I am no dishonourable dog that would steal from his friends!\
\
'Sperling lent me the sword, and I returned it... I swear it! He only blames me because he does not want to blame himself for the loss of it.'","Talk to Getfleda.","'I heard and saw nothing... I swear it!'","'N-nay, I saw nothing! I-I....'\
\
The child sighs and looks distraught.\
\
'I cannot tell a lie. I borrowed the sword from Brunstan and was playing in the burned yards to the south. When my mother called me to dinner, I forgot the toy and left it behind. When I went back, I could not find it again.\
\
'Please, do not tell Sperling and Brunstan! They are both bigger than me!'","Talk to the children observing the fight between Brunstan and Sperling","'If Brunstan stole Sperling's sword, he should be fed to the Orcs. Sperling's da gave him the sword before he went away....'","'Oh, you must hurry, kind ${CLASS}! Brunstan and Sperling will surely harm each other if they continue fighting!'","Talk to Getfleda","This child confessed to misplacing Sperling's toy sword","Hear Sperling's side of the story","Talk to Brunstan and Sperling.","'I am pretty sure I saw someone playing with Sperling's sword down in the southern part of the city, but it was not Brunstan.'","'I never liked either one of them to begin with... I am only here to watch the fight.'","You have accompanied Getfleda, a girl of Eaworth, to help break up a fight between two of her friends, Brunstan and Sperling.","'Brunstan is a liar and a thief! My father gave me a wooden practice sword before he went away to fight, and I let Brunstan play with it... now it is gone.\
\
'He swears that he returned it to me, but I swear he did not! He is a liar without honour!'","Talk to the children observing the fight between Brunstan and Sperling and learn if any of them saw what happened.","'Oh my! I do not know who to believe! I cannot believe that Brunstan would be so dishonourable, but I also do not believe that Sperling would accuse him without cause!\
\
'Perhaps one of the other children saw something... would you ask them?'","'Let us talk somewhere else....'"},
[7420]={"Destroying the siege-engine has caused the camp to catch fire","'You fought with honour. I do not have much time left. Take my horse and ride away. Tell any who will listen of Saruman's treachery.\
\
'Do not let the end of the Avanc-lûth be for naught. Be well....'","Destroy the next siege-engine further in the camp","Flee on Elder Déin's horse","Instance: Tusks of the Boar","Speak with Elder Déin again.","Talk to Elder Déin","Tecwin kneels before you. Speak with him to discuss his plans.","Defeat the Dunlending siege-captain quickly.","Destroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.","Sounds of a massive battle reach your ears","The fire in the camp is spreading all around you","Defeat Dunlending siege-captain","Talk to Tecwin","Choose 4 soldiers to assist you","'We will take the main force up the river-bank and attack the gates. You must fight through the chaos and destroy as much as you can.\
\
'We are few against an entire army, but we must do all we can. Probably most of us will not survive. Do your part for the good of Dunland.\
\
'Take four of my best warriors to help you. Some of them will help in healing, some will help protect you, and some will attack from a distance. Go now!'","'We have little time. The enemy is too great. We broke into this courtyard, but I fear the nest is truly stirred now.\
\
'We must hold out as long as we can. It has been an honour knowing you, ${PLAYER}. May your name be heard in the songs of legends.\
\
'Brace yourselves for the final attack.'","Talk to Elder Déin quickly","Wait for the Dunlendings to move out","Flee upon Elder Déin's horse before the chance to survive is no more!","Destroy the first siege-engine","You have made it out of Wulf's Cleft alive","Speak with Elder Déin in the centre of the conflagration.","Elder Dein has been defeated!","The Boar-clan is assaulting Wulf's Cleft in an effort to hinder the army there.","The fire is raging everywhere now","Don't let Elder Dein be defeated","'We have been holding the line for as long as we can. If the Elders want us to attack, then we will! We will head to the right... you must go straight ahead and destroy those siege-engines.\
\
'Wait for our assault; otherwise, there will be too many guards for you to handle.'","Elder Déin has asked you to choose four of his finest soldiers to join you in your attempt to destroy the siege engines of the Dunlending army.","Destroy the next set of siege-engines","Choose four warriors to assist you","Speak with Gwin at the front lines. The Boar-clan will move out and attack the main camp, while you destroy as much of the camp as possible.","Speak with Elder Déin as he addresses the warriors.","Talk to Gwin","'This horde is greater than we could have possibly imagined. We have defeated the forces holding the beach, but more will arrive soon.\
\
'We are too small a force to do much against such a massive army. Let us talk to the Elder.'","Destroy the final siege-engines"},
[7421]={"Instancia: Dos Hobbits","'Why do you look so worried, Sam? You heard what Aragorn said. Frodo is just going to think about what to do for an hour, and then he'll come back and we'll all set off in whatever direction he's decided.\
\
'We've got a job to do, after all. I'm sure Frodo will come up with something.'","'I know it isn't easy for your friends to hear, Sam, but I think it is the best course. Frodo has probably come to the same realization, that both ways are desperate. He may in fact be trying to decide which way is most desperate, in order to make his choice more clear.'\
\
You think Aragorn may not fully understand your master, and apologetically tell him that Frodo probably has no intention of going to Minas Tirith at all. He intends to go east, to Mordor, but he's afraid for those of the company that go with him.\
\
'You may be right, Sam. The hour is just about up. We should call for him.'","Merry is sitting by the camp-fire at Parth Galen.\
\
You should talk to Merry to see if he is as concerned as you are.","Talk to Pippin by the camp-fire","'It has been half an hour, perhaps, or maybe an hour. I do not know! I do not know.'","Talk to Aragorn by the camp-fire","Pippin is at the camp-fire on Parth Galen.\
\
You're worried, and should talk to your friends. Pippin is young and might need a friendly word.","Frodo has already taken one of the boats! You have to swim as best you can out into the lake to reach him before he gets too far away!","'We will go wherever Frodo goes, won't we, Sam? That's what we decided, even before we knew the far-off lands through which his road would take him, but nothing has changed, has it?'","Use your hobbit-sense to learn where Frodo has gone","Talk to Merry by the camp-fire","Frodo may be in danger! Stay with Aragorn!","Frodo may be in danger! You have to stay with Aragorn!","Boromir has returned to the camp-fire on Parth Galen.","'Frodo can't fly, and he has no gear. So he needs to get back to the boats!'","One of the boats is missing! Frodo has already taken it!","Aragorn is standing by the camp-fire on Parth Galen.","Frodo must be on this boat!","Swim out into Nen Hithoel and find Frodo's boat!","Talk to Frodo on the boat","'Sam, what a nuisance you are! Don't you know you can't really swim? What would you have done if I had not grabbed you?'\
\
He shakes his head in an exasperated way.\
\
'Sam, I need to go on to Mordor alone. It's the only way!'\
\
You refuse to be left behind, to Frodo's growing consternation.\
\
'Do not hinder me, Sam! The others will be back soon, and if they catch us here they will make us explain, and argue, and I will not be able to resist. If we are going, we have to go now.'\
\
Frodo laughs.\
\
'Oh, Sam. You have spoilt my plan, but... I am glad of it. We were meant to leave together, that much is clear to me now. Let us be off!'","Talk to Boromir by the camp-fire","Get back to the boats, Sam!","You need to use your plain old hobbit-sense to figure out what has happened to Frodo!","You're in quite a pickle, Samwise Gamgee. You know what Frodo thinks he has to do, but you want to ensure that he doesn't go off without you.","'Hold on a minute, Sam,' you say to yourself. 'This is a time for plain old hobbit-sense.'","Frodo needs to get back to the boats if he plans to leave for Mordor alone, and that means you need to get back to the boats if you are to catch him!"},
[7422]={"Fight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the fourth leg of the assault.","<rgb=#FF0000>Béortnoth must survive the assault</rgb>","Fight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the third leg of the assault.","<rgb=#FF0000>Béortnoth has been defeated</rgb>","'Let us return to camp... we will prepare for another assault.'","Béortnoth wishes to speak with you.","Fight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the fourth leg of the assault","<rgb=#FF0000>Wadel must survive the assault</rgb>","Fight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the first leg of the attack","<rgb=#00FF00>You have earned another respite</rgb>","You have accompanied Thane Béortnoth and Wadel of Thornhope into the ruins of their village to wreak vengeance upon the Orcs there.","<rgb=#00FF00>You have a moment to rest</rgb>","'Let us bring death and ruin to the destroyers! Let us take blood for the blood of the fallen! Let the waters run black with the grume of the Orcs!'","Speak with Béortnoth.","Talk to Béortnoth","Fight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the second leg of the assault","<rgb=#00FF00>You may take a moment to rest</rgb>","Instancia: Ira desenfrenada","Fight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the first leg of the attack.","Fight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the third leg of the assault","<rgb=#FF0000>There are too many enemies to push out of Thornhope</rgb>","'There are too many Orcs to dislodge from the city with but one assault... we must retreat and recuperate for the next assault.'","Fight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the second leg of the assault.","<rgb=#FF0000>Wadel has been defeated</rgb>"},
[7423]={"Speak with Arvaethor at the head of the cave.","'Let us push these Orcs back into the depths of the mountain. We will strike fear into them and they shall never again return to the surface!'","Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated","Arvaethor is out of breath but wishes to speak with you","Defeat the Orc chieftain.","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Push the Orkish forces further into the mountain","Stay in the cave and learn of what is happening","Escape the Dead and return to where you entered the cave","Speak to Arvaethor","Instancia: Bajo la Montaña Blanca","Arvaethor asks for you to accompany him into a cavern under the White Mountains and drive the Orkish forces back.","A foreboding chill permeates the air of the cave","Defeat the Orc chieftain","Quickly, escape with your life!","You and Arvaethor enter the cave.\
\
You should speak to Arvaethor.","Escape the Dead and return to where you entered the cave.","Defeat Orcs under the mountain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Orc chieftain guards the entrance to an ancient hall","'I do not believe these Dead are simply passing through my Vale. More seems to be at play here and why do the Orcs and dead share this cave? Quickly, let us return to Ethring with this grim news.'","Dead seep into the room.\
\
You should stay in the cave and learn of what is happening.","Speak with Arvaethor","Push the Orkish forces further into the mountain.","¡Se te acabó el tiempo!","'To Ethring!'"},
[7424]={"The central chamber can be found deep within Ushkútoz.\
\
You have found no sign of Kraznákh, but the central chamber of Ushkútoz is filled with Orcs. You should defeat them before continuing your search for Kraznákh.","As Kraznákh taunts you, you discover the trench-tunnel has been collapsed behind you!","Agnar Brokentooth can be found in Ushkútoz.\
\
Agnar Brokentooth has led you to Ushkútoz to aid in sabotaging the Orcs' trench-tunnel and the defeat of Kraznákh, a lieutenant of Gorgar the Ruthless.","As the last Orc falls defeated, Agnar beckons you over","Clear the central chamber of Ushkútoz","Talk to Agnar Brokentooth","Defeat Kraznákh's Orcs and survive the ambush","As the last of Kraznákh's Orcs falls defeated, the lieutenant of Gorgar attacks!","Kraznákh can be found in Ushkútoz.\
\
You have been trapped in the central chamber of Ushkútoz by Lieutenant Kraznákh and his Orcs. You should confront Kraznákh.","Determined to break a bloody stalemate, Agnar Brokentooth has devised a plan to infiltrate the Orkish trench-tunnel of Ushkútoz.","Confront Kraznákh","'It is time, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I hear Orcs ahead. It will not be long before they discover us here. I hope that Lági and Reithvald have reached the western entrance without incident or our mission may well be over before it begins!\
\
'Let us fight our way through Ushkútoz and put an end to Kraznákh!'","Agnar Brokentooth can be found in Ushkútoz.\
\
With the sudden aid of Lági Helmbiter and Reithvald Red-ember, you and Agnar Brokentooth have defeated Lieutenant Kraznákh. You should talk to Agnar Brokentooth.","Fight through Ushkútoz and find Kraznákh","Agnar Brokentooth can be found in Ushkútoz.\
\
You have defeated the Orcs in the central chamber of Ushkútoz, but you have found no sign of Kraznákh. You should talk to Agnar.","With a sputtering cry, Kraznákh falls defeated!","Agnar Brokentooth is leading the attack on Ushkútoz.\
\
You should follow Agnar Brokentooth and defeat the Orcs inhabiting Ushkútoz as you search for Kraznákh.","'Let's get out of here!'","Kraznákh's Orcs can be found in Ushkútoz.\
\
After trapping you in the central chamber of Ushkútoz, Kraznákh has set his Orcs upon you. You must defeat them.","Lieutenant Kraznákh eyes you with disdain.","You do not see Kraznákh, but the central chamber of Ushkútoz is teeming with Orcs","Defeat Lieutenant Kraznákh","'You were a great help in battle, ${PLAYER}... but if it's all the same, I am glad my old companions came to our aid when they did!\
\
'Kraznákh is dead, and his little trap did half the work of destroying Ushkútoz for us.\
\
'We've... done it.'","Agnar Brokentooth can be found in Ushkútoz.\
\
Agnar fears Kraznákh has lured you into an ambush. You should remain alert.","Kraznákh can be found in Ushkútoz.\
\
After you and Agnar defeated his retinue, Kraznákh has entered the fray in a fury. You must defeat Lieutenant Kraznákh.","Remain alert!","'Bah!\
\
'All of our reports led us to believe Kraznákh would be here! I do not like this, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I need a moment to think. Keep your wits about you!'","Instance: Undermining Ushkútoz"},
[7425]={"Talk to Mekhnet","'Good riddance. I can never get back the months I spent recovering, but at least this will prevent more of our comrades from experiencing the same pain.\
\
'Now, let's head back. I'm sure Lúka is worried sick. Heh, sometimes I think she'll never relax.'","Defend Mekhnet","You should defend Mekhnet as you both face Thraunákh.","<rgb=#FF0000>Mekhnet has been defeated!</rgb>","Instance: Unfinished Business","Thraunákh has been defeated.","Before delving deeper into Atrad-zarakh, you should talk to Mekhnet.","You have found Thraunákh, though Mekhnet wishes to speak with you before facing him.","'Lead the way.'","'That must be him. He seems like a nervous worm, but putting together these sapper-bombs requires careful planning and thought. If only that intelligence was not used for such a destructive purpose.\
\
'Well, enough talk. Let's finish what we set out to do, yes?'","With Atrad-zarakh finally breached, it is up to you and Mekhnet to stop Thraunákh and his sapper-bombs.","You should help defend Mekhnet.","'Look at us; we're in Atrad-zarakh and the Orcs outside are none the wiser! You made short work of those sentries earlier.\
\
'Thraunákh's creations have caused no small amount of woe for us. With him out of the way, we stand a chance to claim Atrad-zarakh for good.\
\
'Of course, we can't claim the watch-tower tonight with just the two of us, but let's find Thraunákh and leave our mark. Shall we?'"},
[7426]={"Present yourself to the Knight of Dulgabêth at Amon Thaur","You have obtained the disguise of a Nurnhoth slave, and now seek to infiltrate the meeting of the Masters of Mordor at Amon Thaur.","Lhaereth barely looks at you as she takes the pouch from your hands.\
\
'Stay here, slave. I may have further use for you,' she says, an unmistakable air of menace in her voice.","Lhaereth has commanded you to remain where you are.","You collected the fallen pouch, and now Lhaereth wants you to bring it to her.","'You did not arrive with the others. Do you not fear the lash?\
\
'Ha! It is no concern of mine! Climb the stairs and look for the others of your kind, if you dare! Dulgabêth will deal whatever punishment he deems sufficient. I look forward to the music of your screams, slave.\
\
'Now go! Go!'","Other slaves have already arrived. You should climb the stairs at Amon Thaur and join them.","Lhaereth has summoned one of the Nurnhoth slaves.","You have infiltrated the meeting of the Masters of Mordor at Amon Thaur, on the slopes of Mount Doom.","Talk to the Nurnhoth slave","Instancia: Unión del Mal","The slave dropped a pouch when he died, and now Laereth calls for you to bring it to her.","You have come in disguise to the base of Amon Thaur. Will Dulgabêth's knights permit you to gain access to the meeting?","Escape down the stairs without being discovered","Join the Nurnhoth slaves to the south-east, among the pillars of Amon Thaur","'I do not... feel well...\
\
'What did the Mistress... give to me...?'","From this landing, you can see other slaves by the pillars to the south-east","The slave collapses, and as he falls a pouch drops from his hand","Pick up the fallen pouch where it lies","'I... I cannot...\
\
'Something is... wrong...'","<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid getting too near to Urudanî, or she will see through your disguise</rgb>","Yadêphal looks at you with disinterest, but there is no recognition in his eye. The clothes you wear blind Dulgabêth's emissary to your identity. He does not know you.\
\
'Move along, slave!' he barks at you.","Dulgabêth and his knights have been betrayed. You should escape down the stairs and away from Amon Thaur before it is too late for you to get away!","Urudanî has seen through your disguise!","Bring the fallen pouch to Lhaereth the Stained","You can see other slaves to the south-east of the landing, among the pillars of Amon Thaur. You should join them in order to avoid arousing the suspicion of the enemy.","You have learned much, but now you should escape down the stairs before you are discovered!","Observe the meeting of the Masters, and remain beneath their notice","Climb the stairs at Amon Thaur and look for other Nurnhoth slaves"},
[7427]={"Talk to Girhâzi","Talk to Amâsu","Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should join them at the odd wall.","Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. Amâsu wants to talk to you.","Join Amâsu and Girhâzi at the wall","Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. Girhâzi wants to talk to you.","'This is very exciting, ${PLAYER}. I have not been on an adventure in many years! You should have seen me in my younger days. I was quite rough and tumble!\
\
'Lead on, my dear. Do watch your step though, it seems there are a few usan-kûni in here.'","Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. After leading them to the odd wall you found, they were able to open the secret door, discovering the Dubarâkh. Girhâzi wants to talk to you.","'Are we almost there ${PLAYER}? Amâsu wishes to travel quickly, but I believe we should slow down. She will not tell us if the journey is difficult for her. If we are close, I believe we should walk the rest of the way, for her sake.'\
\
You assure Girhâzi that it is just ahead.","From here the odd wall is to the north","Intrigued by your discovery of a curious wall inside another salt mine tunnel, Amâsu has asked you to escort her there to see it for herself. Girhâzi, who would not want to be left out, is accompanying you.","'You are quite right that this wall does not look like the others in this mine. Do you truly think it may be a door, though? What do you suppose may open it? This a puzzle indeed!'","Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should talk to Amâsu.","Observe Girhâzi and Amâsu","Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. With Girhâzi's help, you have thwarted an attack by giant scorpions. Amâsu would like to talk to you.","Girhâzi must survive","<rgb=#00FF00>Think</rgb> about which way to go from the first crossway","Lead Amâsu and Girhâzi to the odd wall","Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more, and have led them to the odd wall you found. You should listen to their conversation.","'Níkhu, ${PLAYER}, we found it! I am stunned. I confess there was a part of me that believed it would never be found in my lifetime, and yet, here we are. This is a beautiful treasure trove of knowledge. The culture and history of Ambarûl has been preserved for us in this room. This will restore our sense of identity and help us to rebuild, to uphold our independence. Thank you, ${PLAYER}, you have done our people a great service, and we will never forget it.\
\
'I will place guards here to ensure the safety of Dubarâkh, and you are always welcome to return here, should you desire it.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Think</rgb> about which way to go from the second crossway","'Those usan-kûni are quite large! I am glad to have both you and Girhâzi here with me. Let us move quickly though. This does not seem like a place where we should dally.","Instancia: Desbloqueando la historia","Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should lead them to the odd wall you found.","East seems to be the best way to go"},
[7428]={"Gléowine is outside the village, waiting to speak with you.","Horn is ready to seize the mysterious watcher in Dunfast.","Horn could use your help to stand up and salvage as much of his dignity as possible.","Talk to Corudan in Dunfast","Corudan senses that you are being watched.","You still sense a watchful presence in Dunfast, and should find who or what it is that watches.","Nona stares at you with haunted eyes, a look of surprise on her face","'I don't understand, ${PLAYER}. It has been days since last I beheld Nona, and my affection for her has only grown during that time. The fondness she felt for me before we came to Eaworth... has it gone? Did I imagine it? I cannot have!'\
\
Horn is greatly distressed, but you have no easy words of comfort.","'From here Dunfast looks much as I remember it, but... where are all the people? Let us walk into the village and see if anyone remains who can tell us what happened!'","Horn believes he has found Corudan's mysterious watcher, and is ready to seize the opportunity to reveal it!","'That is the woman who has taken Horn's heart from him? He has spoken of her a great deal to me since we have been journeying together, but not once did he mention she was a Dunlending tribes-woman!\
\
'And she came to this town, the town of my childhood, seeking to steal its goods and provisions?'\
\
Gléowine shakes his head.\
\
'Ah, I remember what it was like to be young, when blood and passions flared in spring-time. I am not fit to judge them. If Horn misses her so, I hope she will reconsider her dismissal of him.'","Instancia: Invierno antinatural","You sense someone staring at the four of you","Horn is down-hearted following your encounter with Nona in the empty village of Dunfast.","Talk to Gléowine outside Dunfast","'I feel eyes on us, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot tell if they be hostile or friendly eyes. Stay on your guard.'","Horn, Corudan, and Gléowine are exploring Dunfast, and you should do the same.","Be ready for anything! Horn is prepared to seize the mysterious watcher in Dunfast","'I do not know what to think, ${PLAYER}. That reunion did not proceed as I might have wished.'","'I think I have found the location of our mysterious watcher, ${PLAYER}. There is someone hiding in this bush. Be ready for anything, and I will seize this person before he can pose a threat!'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. It is better to be safe and to bruise one's dignity a small amount than to be surprised by some dangerous foe, is it not?\
\
'This time it was a shrew. Next time it might be a hidden enemy. Perhaps Corudan can flush the next watcher out of hiding, and I will be the one laughing?'","You are investigating what has happened to Dunfast, the village where Gléowine was born.","Listen to what befell Nona after she left your fellowship in the Entwash Vale","'One look at Nona's face told me she had not been prepared to see Horn in Dunfast. She has not yet resolved her feelings for him. Caring for the injured folk she mentioned may have caused her to delay in resolving her thoughts, or perhaps it is so difficult a riddle she needs more time to untangle a solution, even without the distraction of responsibility.\
\
'Horn may appear inconsolable, but he need not despair. I have not given up on our Dunlending fire-brand, and neither should he.'","Talk to Gléowine in Dunfast","Explore Dunfast with Horn, Corudan, and Gléowine","Talk to Horn in Dunfast","Nona has returned, but she does not seem happy to see you. What will this mean for Horn?","Help Horn brush himself off and salvage his dignity"},
[7429]={"'Es un día triste y alegre a la vez. Me apena que nos viéramos obligados a matar a Amdir, pero es un alivio que ahora conozca la paz.\
\
'Te llevaré de vuelta a Trancos. Yo volveré a mi campamento.'","'Ven conmigo. Es hora de ocuparse de Amdir y esos bandidos. Si Amdir escapa, podría significar el fin de la Tierra Media.'","'¿Sientes el frío en el aire? No es frío natural, sino el frío del miedo, del mal. No dudo que Amdir esté aquí, pero también hay un mal mayor. Debemos dividir nuestras fuerzas.\
\
'Por el bien de la Tierra Media, no podemos permitir que nadie escape. Lenglinn y yo buscaremos otra forma de entrar, mientras tú y Torthann buscáis a Amdir.\
\
'Debemos ser rápidos ahora, antes de que el mal salga de aquí y amenace a toda las Tierras de Bree.'","'¿Quién era ese Enano y qué energía tiene para comandar a los tumularios? Que los Montebruno estaban aterrorizados por esa criatura es cierto, pero aún siento algo más grande en estas ruinas.\
\
'¿Y dónde está Amdir? Tal vez más allá de esa puerta.'","Instancia: Desenredar el hilo","Trancos te ha pedido que le ayudes a acabar de una vez por todas con el alboroto asesino de Amdir.","Ayuda a Torthann a entrar en el campamento de Montebruno","Descubre la causa del miedo de los bandidos","Torthann percibió la fuente del miedo de los bandidos en la esquina sur del campamento. Debería investigar.","Torthann te llama.","'El aire parece contaminado por los asuntos de esta noche. No deberíamos quedarnos aquí más tiempo.'","Habla con Torthann","Torthann no está convencido de que el mal finalice con el tumulario y cree que Amdir está en algún lugar cercano. Tal vez haya algo más en el campamento.","'Allá abajo, en la esquina sur del campamento... ¡la fuente del miedo de los Montebruno está allí! ¡Ven!'","'Anhelo acabar con estos bandidos, pero antes deberías hablar con Trancos. Él dirige nuestros esfuerzos.'","Trancos te ha dicho que hables con Torthann cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para comenzar la búsqueda de Amdir. Trancos y Lenglinn encontrarán una entrada por detrás.","Trancos y sus parientes, Torthann y Lenglinn, te han conducido a las afueras del campamento de los bandidos. Trancos te hace señas."},
[7430]={"'It is done, ${PLAYER}. My father's memory is no longer defiled and the Bloodletter's grip on the Wastes is broken...'","Attempt to free yourself from Burudagath the Bloodletter","Faramir can be found at Ondoher's Folly.\
\
Burudagath has been defeated and Faramir has reappeared within the Fane of Screaming at Ondoher's Folly.","Defeat every Orc at Ondoher's Folly","Faramir is just outside Ondoher's Folly in Dagorlad.\
\
You should speak to Faramir when you are ready to assault Ondoher's Folly and confront the Bloodletter.","Listen to Burudagath","Burudagath has survived his encounter with the Wainriders, but appears to be severely wounded.","Burudagath rises from the ground!","Burudagath the Bloodletter is outside the Fane of Screaming at Ondoher's Folly.\
\
You have defeated every Orc in Ondoher's Folly and should now confront Burudagath.","Slain by their own master, the last Orcs fall...","Darkness creeps into your vision and you fall to the ground...","As Burudagath succumbs to his visions of the dead, you are able to break free!","In a desperate bid to free the Wastes of two threats to the Host of the West, Faramir, son of Ondoher has set a plan in motion to stop Burudagath the Bloodletter by setting the Wainriders against him.","Remain on guard as Zhan Ashû speaks","'Although I have spent many years upon this hill, never once have I raised a weapon against the Orcs. They came to regard me as nothing more than some sort of twisted amusement for their Master, and in time, I began to believe it myself.\
\
'You have freed me from such delusions, my friend. It may have been folly for me to join the battle long ago, but to flee this fight could bring ruin to Gondor -- to my people!\
\
'${PLAYER}, we must rid the hill of Orcs and leave none but the Bloodletter to the Wainriders. If they encounter even one Orc that is loyal to him, it may reveal our deception... and that is a chance we can ill-afford to take.\
\
'We must move now! I shall do what I can to aid you!'","Zhan Ashû is addressing you before the Wainriders return to Dol Acharn.","'I am filled with sorrow that I could not aid you further before the battle's end, ${PLAYER}, but I am glad the Wainriders arrived in time to draw his attention from you. It seems the folly of my past has been answered this day -- perhaps it was once true that my allies were fated to a greater end without my hand in battle, but no more!\
\
'As I look at my father's banner now, I see the might of a Gondor that once was... and may be again. For all the defilement Burudagath brought upon it, it resisted any final destruction. Gondor itself must now press onward through the darkness in much the same way, it seems.\
\
'We have won a great victory this day... but I believe it time I leave this place and its painful memories behind.\
\
'Go, return to your friends in the ruins and tell them of our victory. I shall see you again soon enough, ${PLAYER}...'","Orcs can be found throughout Ondoher's Folly.\
\
Faramir has asked you to aid him in defeating the Orcs of Ondoher's Folly so the Wainriders remain deceived upon their arrival.","Instancia: Venganza de los Caídos","Confront Burudagath the Bloodletter","The Wainriders have come to Ondoher's Folly and are now confronting Burudagath the Bloodletter.","Talk to Faramir inside the Fane of Screaming at Ondoher's Folly","Speared by Zhan Ashû, Burudagath falls to the ground defeated!","Talk to Faramir at Ondoher's Folly","You are trapped in the Fane of Screaming at Ondoher's Folly.","At the last moment, a familiar chill rushes into the fane as the Wainriders appear!","Observe the confrontation between Zhan Ashû and Burudagath"},
[7431]={"Nobor can be found in the back of the Old Archives, on the left side of the second floor.\
\
Nobor has revealed his intent. You must convince him to abandon his plans against the Steward!","The rogmul writhes and disappears in the darkness of the Old Archives...","The area Gúldil mentioned can be found in the back of the Old Archives on the second floor.\
\
Gúldil has asked you to search the second floor of the Old Archives.","Confront Nobor","Hoping to confront the thief before the words on the stolen scroll can be spoken, Maenir directs you to the Old Archives.","Examine Nobor","Nobor can be found in the back of the Old Archives, on the left side of the second floor.\
\
Nobor was slain by the summoning of the rogmul. You should examine his body before leaving the Old Archives.","Nobor's body lies motionless on the floor of the Old Archives - his face frozen in horror. His body bears no wounds, but all life is gone from him.\
\
The scroll's origin may or may not have been unknown to Nobor, but it is clear that the power it contained was beyond his imagining and control.\
\
Mithrandir's warning was not misplaced - he must be told of what has occurred.","It has been a day filled with ill omens. Nobor's was a cruel fate - even for one of the Withered Tree.","Gúldil can be found in the Old Archives.\
\
Gúldil has offered to help you confront the thief in the Old Archives. You should speak to him.","You warn Nobor that he does not understand that the scroll is a tool of the Enemy.\
\
'The words of yet another dog, happy to feast on scraps at the feet of the Steward! The Enemy shall claim all soon enough - better we position ourselves to be spared his full wrath. \
\
'The Steward is powerless, and his mind betrays him! If he would treat his own son so shamefully, then how lowly are we to him?\
\
'No, I cannot surrender now. The Steward must be slain!'","Instancia: Lenguas viles","Listen to the scroll-thief","Defeat Vadokhar","Vadokhar can be found in the back of the Old Archives, on the left side of the second floor.\
\
Vadokhar has appeared in the Old Archives. You should defeat the rogmul before it can cause any more harm.","Search the Old Archives for the scroll-thief","The scroll-thief can be found in the back of the Old Archives, on the left side of the second floor.\
\
You have found the man you presume to be the scroll-thief and should now confront him.","You have found a man surrounded by scrolls and barricaded into a corner of the archives","Talk to Gúldil","'We are nearing the proper section, ${PLAYER}. It is just ahead - up the stairs and to the left.\
\
'It is there that we have catalogued our extensive, albeit woefully incomplete, knowledge of the various languages of Gondor, Rhûn, Harad, and beyond. If the scholars of Minas Tirith have what this scroll-thief seeks, it must be among the texts stored there.\
\
'You may proceed at your own discretion, but I urge you to be swift. I will remain here and ensure that no one makes for the door.'"},
[7432]={"Return to Faeron","Instancia: Viznak vive","<rgb=#FF0000>Faeron has fallen!</rgb>","The merrevail retreat!","Listen to the conversation","<rgb=#FF0000>Faeron and Rhadrog must survive!</rgb>","Dolenthol has just learned that Viznak is actually a goblin.\
\
You should listen to the conversation.","<rgb=#FF0000>Rhadrog has fallen!</rgb>","You are under attack!\
\
Defeat the merrevail attackers!","'The more Rangers there are that know my true identity, the harder it will be to maintain my deception. Alas, it was necessary to reveal myself to them. Let us return to the tower. The city continues higher still.'","With Rhadrog and Dolenthol in tow, you should return to Faeron and see how you can help.","Faeron and Viznak are about to be overrun by merrevail and need your help!","Defeat the merrevail","Viznak has regained consciousness and is speaking with the Rangers.\
\
You should listen to the conversation."},
[7433]={"'We survived. I will have an opportunity to speak with her now.'","Defeat the Alad of Er-atûr","Speak with Raphûz","Ashâmi, begrudgingly, accepts your assistance","'Come, my friend, Shonith awaits.'","You and Raphûz discovered Ashâmai amongst a section of dead trees in the grove. She does not look happy to see you. Approach her and allow Raphûz to explain why you are here.","Cautiously approach Ashâmi","Allow Ashâmi and Raphûz to finish their discussion","Raphûz is too injured to continue, you have failed","Raphûz is preparing for battle through the grove to find Ashâmi.","'Prepare yourself. We must use caution and haste as we search for Ashâmi. The reports I received about this dead land speak of fell and wrath-filled spirits. I will take the lead.'","You have defeated the Alad of Er-atûr","Ashâmi begins to make her way toward Shonith","You approached Ashâmi in the ruined grove. Allow Raphûz and her to speak.","Assist Ashâmi and Raphûz to defeat the Alad","Ashâmi begins the grisly business of collecting a trophy from the Alad. Raphûz shifts nervously.","Ashâmi is concerned you and Raphûz are over-matched in the fallen grove. She warns that the Alad is a powerful creature and suggests you may not survive this attack.","Raphûz asked you to accompany him to find Ashâmi. He wanted to apologize to the woman and to help her.","Speak with Raphûz to begin the search for Ashâmi","You found Ashâmi","Raphûz follows Ashâmi","Ashâmi scowls.","Instancia: Voz en el Viento","As Ashâmi begins to walk away, Raphûz looks at you excitedly and smiles. You should speak with him.","Ashâmi finishes her task and she and Raphûz move to speak to one another. Allow them to have their conversation.","Wait for Raphûz and Ashâmi to finish speaking"},
[7434]={"'I am all right now, ${PLAYER}. It was simply the sight of Daxamat clambering out over the railing of the ship that made me feel queasy. I think I will remain below decks for the rest of the voyage, unless you need me above. I cannot imagine you will. The sailors of Anfalas seem very capable.'","'Oh, excuse me, ${PLAYER}, I did not mean to be rude. I was contemplating the bridge over the Lagorduin: such an impressive feat of stonework!\
\
'The City of the Corsairs has been many things over the years, but for some of that time it was a sea-haven of Númenor. There must be architectural wonders there too, and I am eager to see them. My wife Bruidis cares less for such things. Where is she now? She has gone below decks, intending to assess our stock of supplies. I told her the voyage itself should not take more than a few days, but still she wanted to ensure we have food and water enough.\
\
'I told you before, did I not? I am a swan-knight, and my martial skill is well-developed; but my wife Bruidis is the strategist of the family. If there is thinking to be done, she is the one to do it!'","'The storm rages and the seas are wild! We have to take down the sails, or the wind will tear our masts to splinters! The sailors and the Elves have gone above, but I cannot tell if they are still alive!'","Talk to Sirgon on the deck of the Wave-hunter","Go back up on deck","Talk to Sigileth on the deck of the Wave-hunter","Gwallang the Limlinn hops excitedly up and down, occasionally cracking the shell of a snail he has caught on the railing of the Wave-hunter. He seems very happy to be sailing with Sirgon again.","Caebar has suggested you go above and take in the fresh air.","Talk to Daxamat and learn about Umbar","Legolas calls for your help.","Waterlogged but alive, you have found where the Wave-hunter ran aground on the Shield Isles.","'This ship is unlike those of my people, ${PLAYER}. No, I do not intend that to be an insult! Even a ship made of rough-hewn timber is still to be prized if it stays afloat and keeps you from a watery grave! I think it is simply the way of the Men of Gondor to value the use of a thing higher than the beauty of its form.'","Caebar stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, already concerned about something.","'The voyage is well underway, and now our thoughts turn to our arrival at the City of the Corsairs. What will we do if the Kindred of the Coins greets us at the dock, ${PLAYER}? I said we would once again become the Hidden Guard, but there is very little that will be hidden about our mission if our foes see us arrive from atop the walls or from the watch-towers of Umbar.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Beckon</rgb> for Daxamat to come down","Sigileth stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter.","'The sails have been taken down, but we are not yet safe! There is a presence in the wind, and it seeks to batter our ship beneath the waves!'","When you have learned enough, find Caebar below decks","Talk to Caebar on the deck of the Wave-hunter","Listen to the concerns of your crew","'I am not much of a teacher. My brother Jajax is the talker in the family.\
\
'But I hope to be a help to you. What do you want to know?'","'I have never been to Umbar, ${PLAYER}, and neither has my brother... unless he has somehow managed to escape my notice and had some adventure about which he has told me nothing! But I find that unlikely.\
\
'I wonder if Elves live among the sea-folk that call Umbar their home? I will have to put this question to the Corsair Daxamat sometime in the next few days. It could be he has seen Elves in the city or along the cape during his time there, before the Kindred came to power.'","Spirits are light as the Wave-hunter begins its voyage to Umbar.","Sirgon calls for you as the storm rages outside and the Wave-hunter is tossed on wild seas.","'How fares my husband Rossaran? No doubt he gawks at the scenery through which the ship passes?\
\
'Oh, he is a dear man. Two things he loves besides me, ${PLAYER}: faithfully serving his King, and marvelling at the great feats performed by the prospectors and stonemasons of Gondor. Sometimes I wonder if he should have been born a dwarf!\
\
'But I have been checking our store of food and water, and it seems that we should have enough for the voyage to Umbar and back. The Wave-hunter is well-prepared for the journey; I confess to you that it is our arrival at the City of the Corsairs that now most concerns me!'","As he said he would, Caebar prefers to remain below decks.","Caebar is worried that Daxamat will fall, and he has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> the Corsair to come down.","Talk to Legolas on the deck of the Wave-hunter","Sirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter as its voyage begins.","Find the Wave-hunter","'This blade has to earn its name, ${PLAYER}. I cannot give it a name that might prove to be the wrong one! Weapons are like children, or so I have heard it said.\
\
'The Elves of Lórien called my brother Corudan \\qthe River-walker,\\q for he was often away from home, exploring the lands up and down the Anduin. Will this adventure now make him \\qthe Sea-strider,\\q or \\qthe Bay-rider?\\q\
\
'I will have to tell him this when we rescue him. He will laugh to hear it, once he is safe.'","Thrown from the ship during the storm, you have washed ashore and must now return to the Wave-hunter.","Talk to Sirgon inside the Wave-hunter","'What's that? Oh, nothing. I am just thinking.\
\
'What goods do you think the people of Umbar might value? If I were to establish a market along the docks of the city, what things would fetch the highest price? Will items from Gondor be considered valuable or worthless, ${PLAYER}? I cannot decide! At least I will have a few days to think it over.'","'I know I suggested that you recruit the Corsair Jajax for the crew and he refused the offer, but I was under the impression that his brother Daxamat would be a little less... I don't know... a little less wild, perhaps? But he is clambering all over the Wave-hunter as if he has not a care in the world, and without the slightest thought that he might fall from any of these perches, each more perilous than the last!\
\
'Will you <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for him to come down? He is making me nervous!'","'I have not yet needed the seasickness remedy you and Legolas procured for me, ${PLAYER}, but all the same I believe I will stay below decks for now. Do you think I should share it with Caebar? I will have it ready if he asks me for it, but I do not want to give it all away, just in case.\
\
'We are not yet out in the Bay, after all. Legolas says he expects the rocking of the ship to become more pronounced when we leave the river behind us.'","Wait with your crew","'I am not much of a teacher, but I hope to be a help to you. What do you want to know?'","'I have been thinking about something, my friend. So much good stone is covered by rivers and by lakes... and by the Sea as well, I imagine! What precious gemstones lie hidden down there, out of our reach? Is that the secret of the Temámir? Do the arid lands of their birth yield such valuables to them more easily than ours? And yet they still need water to drink....\
\
'I look forward to learning how it is done when we arrive in Umbar. The gemstone worn by Khôltekh the Cunning is an intriguing mystery, but it is one I intend to solve!'","'Thanks for checking in on me, ${PLAYER}. You say the Corsair Daxamat spoke about what we can expect when we reach Umbar? I should have liked to hear that... assuming it was good news!'\
\
You tell Caebar what you learned, and he nods.\
\
'A little good and a little bad, then? It sounds to me as if we have our work cut out for us when we arrive. At least the sailing has been easy. I expected worse!'","Some members of your crew are talking and enjoying the breeze off the sea","Instancia: Viaje del Cazador de Olas","The storm rages!","Talk to Caebar below decks in the Wave-hunter","Sirgon recommended that you speak with the crew-members you recruited for the voyage as the Wave-hunter sails to Umbar.","Talk to your crew and make your way to Caebar below decks","Now that your preparations have been made, it is time for the voyage of the Wave-hunter and the completion of your secret mission.","Go up on deck and weather the storm","'I have not felt this youthful in years! Our course leads down the Lagorduin to the Bay of Belfalas, and then we will truly be on our way.\
\
'Like young Caebar, not all of the Wave-hunter's crew have before been at sea. I suggest that you speak with the folk you recruited and learn how the river-passage treats them. The waters in the Bay will be more unruly than this, and if the rocking in Lagorduin disturbs them it may be helpful to know, and guard against further upset! I understand the dwarf Gimli has in his possession a remedy for seasickness? He may need to share it, with Caebar at least, and perhaps with others!'","Meet with Sirgon","'Thank you for keeping me company, ${PLAYER}, but I will not ask you to remain below decks for the whole voyage! Feel free to go above and take in the fresh air.'","'The one who abducted my son Thorongil, this Nakási Wave-reaper... you said you know who she is?'\
\
You tell Nauriel of the cellar encounter between Nakási and the Heirs of Castamir that resulted in the death of her husband Tumúldo. Nauriel stares at you with narrowed eyes.\
\
'She will have no sympathy from me. Bad things happen. If she does not return my son to me, unharmed, I will send her to see her husband at once. I may do this anyway. Let her and her masters beware: a Knight of the Green Hills does not grant mercy without good reason... and the mother of an endangered child never does.'","Caebar is below decks, waiting to hear how the crew is enjoying the voyage.","Some members of your crew discuss the situation that awaits them in Umbar.","Daxamat has agreed to tell you what he can about the City of the Corsairs.","'I have given some thought to our voyage, ${PLAYER}. I believe the City of the Corsairs must remain a bustling port-city, despite the defeat of Balakhôr the Scourge and the Heirs of Castamir during the War of the Ring. Do you think the arrival of the Wave-hunter can go unnoticed when we draw near the port?\
\
'I cannot decide if it is more or less suspicious of us to arrive by night. Perhaps some of Golasgil's sailors will give me their opinions.'"},
[7435]={"'This is hard reading,' Gandalf says, looking up from the pages of the Black Book","Hidden within the secret runes, Vóin speaks of his journey to Mordor.","Talk to Gandalf on the slopes of Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory","'After many months,' Gandalf reads, 'at last I found him.'","'Like a grinding wheel, time moved ever onward,' Gandalf reads","The hidden runes left by Vóin in the Black Book of Mordor describe a difficult choice made within the dungeons of Minas Morgul.","Listen to Vóin's tale as recorded in the secret runes","'To Mordor I went then, seeking word of my vanished friend,' Gandalf reads aloud","'I am beginning to worry, my friend. There must be some means of escape, some way to free you from the Nazgûl's grasp. I have searched this tower high and low, and delved into every corner of the vale, but... there is nothing.\
\
'What is that? What did you say? You have thought of something? At last, Eärnur! Speak! Tell me what you have devised, and I will carry it out!\
\
'What? Thafar-gathol? Why do you speak its name, here in the darkness of Morgul? That is of no use to us now, friend. We must think only of escape!'","'It was in the city of Minas Morgul that I came to live, hiding in plain sight among the other wicked dwarves that served the Orcs and their foul masters. It was unpleasant work and cruel, but every disagreeable task elevated my position in the city and brought me nearer to my goal. Other dwarves claim the Zhélruka have no patience? I proved them all wrong, and was rewarded. In time the bosses gave me a new post: steward of the chambers within the tower atop the city.\
\
'It was there I at last found Eärnur, and the few of his knights who yet survived.'","Vóin recorded the words of Eärnur in hidden runes within the Black Book of Mordor.","Delve deeper into the Halls of Memory","'And so ends the hidden runes Vóin left within the Black Book of Mordor, ${PLAYER}. If the knight Macilnis escaped Imlad Morgul and came to free lands again, Vóin does not tell. And yet... I think we have learned enough from this Black Book for me to suggest some possibilities.\
\
'I believe Macilnis escaped the bounds of Mordor still in possession of Orthadel, the Rising Star, but not without injury. For how long did she journey, and to where did she go? We cannot know for certain, but it seems she did not make for Minas Tirith or word of her would appear once again, and it does not. I think she turned northward in an attempt to put as much distance between herself and the Witch-king as she was able. Did she survive the journey, and live out her days in peace? Did she succumb to wounds freshly-inflicted during her escape, or those she endured during the years of her torment in the dungeons? Was she recaptured by hunting-parties sent by the Witch-king? Vóin never learned which of these came to pass, and I cannot say.\
\
'But of this I am quite certain. Whatever may have been the fate of this knight of Gondor, the blade she carried out of the Morgul Vale survived. Orthadel was of Elf-make, wielded first by Magoldir the Elf during the Siege of Barad-dûr and later by King Eärnur of Gondor, but in time its history was forgotten, and its name was lost. It became just a sword, handed down from bearer to bearer for many years. Somehow it found its way into the hands of a Dúnadan, and became an heirloom of his house.\
\
'That is how it came to the Ranger Golodir, ${PLAYER}. Yes, though it endured much over the years, I think the sword that would be remade in the forges of Rivendell and renamed Dúnachar was once known as Orthadel. And so the Rising Star became the Avenger of the West.'","Gandalf is in the Halls of Memory, ready to read the secret writing of Vóin's tale.","'My mind wandered on the hard journey. I remembered our adventures together, and they brought a smile to my face even in that dark land. But there were other memories, too, and regrets, and those were less welcome.\
\
'He had just become king of Gondor, and the crown was an ill fit. The taunts of the Witch-king at Fornost ate away at him. \\qIf my horse had not bolted...\\q he often began, but one of us was always there to keep him from dwelling upon it. If Magoldir had lived, his words might have kept Eärnur from going to Minas Morgul, but Magoldir was dead, and would never return from Durthang.\
\
'Could I have stopped him? This is the thought that comes back to me again and again, as I write these passages in the dim light of the accursed beacon. He had just become king, and I trusted that his knights would keep him safe. Gondor was no land for Zhélruka, and I had deeds of my own to perform. I remember his words to me before I returned to the northern mountains. \\qGo find your city, Vóin. Go find Thafar-gathol!\\q I embraced him then, and bid him farewell. \\qI will!\\q I told him.\
\
'\\qGood!\\q he responded. \\qPerhaps then you will stop talking about it morning and evening!\\q\
\
'Seven years after that parting, I learned from travellers upon the road that King Eärnur went to Imlad Morgul with a band of knights, and vanished. I set out at sunrise the following morning, bid farewell to my wife, and resolved to find Eärnur.'","Vóin joined a group of wicked dwarves bound for service in Minas Morgul.","'But the grinding wheel showed no mercy. Time moved onward,' reads Gandalf","'Think, Eärnur, think! There is still time, but... there is less now than there was. I have devised a hundred plans, each of them less likely to succeed than the previous one. But that does not mean escape is impossible. Never think that!\
\
'I do not want to worry you, but... you should know. Silmahtar is... no more. The Houses of Lamentation claim another of our friends.\
\
'No, we should not weep for him. Let his fate inspire us to escape, and we can mourn him when we are both free of the Black Land! Not just he, but Silmahtar and Calatúr both. Think!'","'I believe this will be our last delve into the words of our distant friend Vóin, ${PLAYER}. Yes, I say friend, for though the tome he left us comes from Mordor and bears the sigil of Sauron upon its cover, I have detected little malice on the part of the Zhélruka who wrote it. He has expanded our knowledge of the past, and for that I call him friend!\
\
'The shard of glass reveals hidden writing that speaks of Mordor. That is where Vóin picks up the tale, and that is where we should follow in these Halls of Memory.'","Instancia: El cuento de Vóin","'Time was no friend of ours,' Gandalf reads aloud","'We will think of something. There is still time.\
\
'The Witch-king's pride will be his downfall. He thinks to rob you of the spark that drives you, Eärnur, the fire that so infuriates him. As long as that passion to resist him burns within you, he will not know victory over you.\
\
'I have stayed here too long. I will be back tomorrow, my friend.'","Listen to Eärnur's plan as recorded by Vóin in the secret runes","Hidden within the secret runes, Vóin speaks of the dungeons of Minas Morgul.","'Every step I took in those dungeons was the heaviest of my life,' reads Gandalf","Gandalf has finished reading the hidden runes Vóin left within the Black Book of Mordor.","Hear the words of Eärnur","Gandalf believes he can reveal the rest of Vóin's tale using the shard of glass you discovered in the locked box inside Khîl's home.","Talk to Gandalf in the Halls of Memory","The hidden runes left by Vóin in the Black Book of Mordor describe the time he spent within Minas Morgul, seeking to free Eärnur.","'Yes, it is conjecture only... but I believe it is true.'","'Only one of Eärnur's knights could escape, but even that would require the guardians in the Vale to be occupied with some distracting mission. Something was needed to draw their attention away from the bearer of the sword.\
\
'I knew Macilnis was more fleet of foot than Orolang, and would have the greatest chance of escaping the valley, so I gave to her the sword Orthadel and set her free. Only after she was fled did I go to release Orolang, but there was little time to waste: I sent the tower's guardians after him almost immediately, and he led them on a desperate chase... away from Macilnis. Alas, my friend! I had no choice! Anyone could see that.'","'For all the time I have known you, Vóin, you have dreamed of finding your lost city. I do not want you to waste your years here in this tower seeking to prevent something I know to be unpreventable.\
\
'Yes, I know my doom. Here in the heart of his power, I cannot hope to resist the Lord of the Nazgûl for much longer. He knows this. But he seeks not only a thrall. He wants something else: he wants to destroy my spirit, the fire inside me that so infuriates him. He wants me to despair, to fall upon my own sword, to say with word and deed \\qyou have the victory, and I am bested.\\q You were right, Vóin. That would be no escape, and would bind me to his will.\
\
'Know you of Egalmoth? He was the lord of this city when it fell, but he did not wait in the tower for the Nazgûl to slay him. He rode out, defying the armies of Orc and wraith, and though he came in the end to death, I think his Onslaught will be long-remembered. I cannot do as he did, and I cannot keep the Lord of the Nazgûl from dominating my mind. But I can hinder the scheme he has devised for me, and cheat him of the total victory he seeks.\
\
'None will know of this save you, Vóin. My own Onslaught will not become song or tale or legend. But it will be the deed of Eärnur, who resisted evil to the last.'","'Vóin! What news of Eärnur? Tell me he still resists the torments of the Nazgûl!\
\
'What? Escape? What has changed? I will not leave without Eärnur! You say he is already fled? Happy news! If you will open my cell, I will follow him to freedom! Dear, sweet Vóin!\
\
'What of Macilnis? You go to free her now? Then I will away, and let us meet again when we are safely outside the Black Land! Farewell, Vóin, bearer of happy tidings and welcome escape!'","Vóin writes of his difficult choice in the dungeons of Minas Morgul, and his words return to the slopes of Mordor."},
[7436]={"Instancia: La guerra llega a Rohan","You should find Utred's war-steed by following Cíllan and her children.","Invading brigands are at the north gate of Langhold.\
\
You should hurry to the north gate and fight back the brigands.","The sounds of battle ring in the north of town...","Hear Thane Utred's decision on the fate of Langhold","Ready Utred's war-steed for carrying the Thane's family to safety","The Thane convinces his children to go willingly with Cíllan","The Thane has fallen, and madness comes over all","Run after Dala to escape","'${PLAYER}, we must run! The Thane is dead, and Langold burns as we speak. Run, run!'","Thane Utred needs a moment alone to collect his thoughts","You should watch the evacuating women and children, and ensure that they get a safe start on the road.","'My poor city! What now, ${PLAYER}? My Thane is dead, and my city burns....\
\
'We survivors must make for Harwick. I can only hope Harding has room for us.'","Thane Utred refuses to abandon his city","'They are upon us! Go, ${PLAYER}, with Dala -- we will be fine. We will leave immediately. They come from the north, and we make for the south.\
\
'Be safe, ${PLAYER}!'","Hurry to meet the invaders in battle","Langhold is on the brink of a worrisome attack by unified forces of vengeful brigands and blood-thirsty Easterlings, backed by Mordor.","Follow Dala","'Do not look at me that way, ${PLAYER}; you need not pity me. My husband is strong and stubborn, and does his duty with pride.\
\
'Yes, I would rather have him safe by my side, but that is not the way of the Rohirrim.\
\
'Come, we must make towards the stables. Utred wants us to take his war-steed to Harwick....'","The war-steed is prepared for the evacuation","'Thank heavens they left willingly, the brave dears. I must collect myself before I go out and rally the men.\
\
'Please... will you go see them off safely, ${PLAYER}? I need a moment to myself.'","'We made it out....'","Leave the Mead Hall and search for Cíllan outside","In the chaos of Langhold's fall, Dala calls your name.","Help fight for Langhold","Find Dala in the chaos and follow him","See if Utred is all right","Talk to Cíllan outside the Mead Hall","Thane Utred of Langhold has a decision to make.\
\
You should speak with the Thane of Langhold.","Talk to Cíllan","Thane Utred is in the Mead Hall of Langhold.\
\
You should listen to the Thane's conversation with his family, and then follow them outside when they are finished speaking.","Observe the Thane's conversation with his family","Observe the battle for Langhold.","The magnificent horse looks ready to bear the Thane's family to the end of the world and back. It must have sensed its master's need, for it is prepared to carry its precious riders to safety at once.","'These \\qNazgûl\\q of Mordor cannot be so strong as to lay low a strong city such as Langhold, full of hale Rohirrim warriors and war-steeds. I will not let the brigands refute their exile while I live!\
\
'The women and children are to leave, but the Men of Langhold will stand and defend the city.'","Make sure the innocent denizens of Langhold get a safe start to Harwick","Cíllan is on the steps of the Mead Hall.\
\
You should speak with Cíllan.","The battle is near!","The evacuees are safe; you should run to the defence of Langhold","Follow Dala."},
[7439]={"Habla con Olgir","Derrota a Mazog","El Libro de Mazarbul está sobre la tumba que se erigió para Balin en el centro de la cámara.\
\
Thíli te ha pedido que termines de escribir el relato de los enanos en el Libro de Mazarbul.","'Ahora que todo ha llegado a esto, capitán, me entristece que nuestro regreso a Moria haya sido tan breve y tan lleno de tristeza. ¿Fue un error de Balin llevarnos aquí, y esperar que la maldición que pesaba sobre estas salas se hubiera levantado?\
\
'Ya es demasiado tarde para hacerse esas preguntas, pero no quiero que este viaje lleno de esperanza termine así, para ser olvidado para siempre, para no llegar a nada.\
\
'¡Capitán Ori, te lo ruego: termina de escribir nuestra historia en el libro donde se registran estas cosas! Está ahí, en la tumba que erigimos para el Señor Balin; otros lo comenzaron, pero quiero que tú lo termines. ¡No quiero que nuestro destino sea olvidado!'","Resiste a Mazog hasta el final","Mazog, un joven orco descendiente de Azog el trasgo, ha liderado el asalto contra los enanos y debe ser derrotado.","'No estaba seguro de que aún estuvieras vivo, capitán Ori, pero me alegra verte así. Quería que estuvieras aquí para nuestra última defensa. Todavía estamos esperando noticias de los exploradores que enviaste al oeste, pero hasta ahora no ha habido nada.\
\
'Y ahora los orcos han tomado el puente y la segunda sala, y se acercan a nuestra posición desde todos los lados. Estamos seguros de seguir a Frár, Lóni y Náli, mi capitán, incluso si resistimos un poco más.\
\
'¡Escucha! ¿Quién es ese? ¿Es uno de los exploradores?'","'¡Capitán Ori, por fin has llegado! Temía que nos abrumaran antes de tu llegada, pero con tu fuerza aún podemos repeler a los orcos.\
\
'¡Ojalá Balin aún estuviera vivo! Necesitamos su liderazgo; contra esta horda de orcos debemos actuar con una sola mente, o no sobreviviremos al anochecer.\
\
'Fui separado de Lóni y Náli durante el último ataque. Debemos unirnos a ellos al otro lado del puente, pero muchos orcos han salido de la fosa y se interponen entre aquí y allá. ¡Debemos derrotarlos antes de que lleguen más!'","Frár está en el pasaje al este del Puente de Khazad-dûm.\
\
Tu resistencia contra los orcos te ha llevado a ti y a Frár al pasaje al este del puente.","Espera a que Frár decida qué hacer","'¿Qué podemos hacer, capitán? No tenemos ninguna esperanza de resistirlos aquí en la sala. Nos van a abrumar con su gran número.'\
\
Thíli escucha tu plan, y su rostro se endurece, sus ojos se vuelven severos y brillantes.\
\
'Tienes razón, capitán. Nos retiraremos a la Cámara de Mazarbul, y haremos lo que podamos para resistir allí. ¡Allí podremos aguantar lo suficiente para que sientan el aguijón de nuestras hachas y escuchen nuestros gritos de guerra!'","Sigue a Thíli hasta la Cámara de Mazarbul","Termina de escribir el Libro de Mazarbul","Frár está en el pasaje al este del Puente de Khazad-dûm.\
\
Un gran mal ha llegado a Khazad-dûm, y su sombra ha llenado a Frár de temor. Está esperando para hablar contigo.","Habla con Lóni","Instancia: No podemos salir","'¿Entonces, está decidido? ¡Una última resistencia gloriosa contra los orcos! Lloro que nadie cante esta batalla, capitán Ori, pero me alegra que tenga a mi lado a enanos tan honorables y confiables para llevarla a cabo.\
\
'¡Por Balin! ¡Por Khazad-dûm y por la gloria de los enanos!'","Frár, Lóni y Náli han decidido hacer una última resistencia contra los orcos. Tú, Ori, estarás con ellos.","Thíli está en la sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Tú y Thíli han escapado de los orcos que se estaban reuniendo en el Puente de Khazad-dûm, pero se están cerrando alrededor de ustedes.","El asalto final contra los enanos ha comenzado.","'¿Tuvimos un error al regresar a Khazad-dûm, capitán? Con Balin muerto, este esfuerzo parece condenado: ¡los orcos son demasiados!\
\
'¡No, no! ¡Nos mantendremos firmes! ¡Moriré como un enano! ¡Que nadie llame cobarde a Lóni!'","Sobrevive al asalto de los orcos","Habla con Thíli","Habla con Náli","Siguiendo tu sugerencia, los enanos se están retirando a la Cámara de Mazarbul, que puede ser más fácilmente defendida contra la horda que se aproxima.","Thíli está en el lado occidental del Puente de Khazad-dûm.\
\
Frár ha decidido enfrentar su destino, ralentizando el avance de los males que aún esperan a los enanos para que puedas escapar a la sala Vigesimoprimera con Thíli.","Uno de los exploradores que enviaste hace días ha regresado a la sala Vigesimoprimera.","Los orcos son demasiados, y las fuerzas de Mazog se acercan para dar el golpe fatal.","'¡Mi capitán, traigo malas noticias! La piscina ha llegado hasta el muro de la puerta oeste; no hay esperanza de escapar por ese camino. La misión del noble Óin ha terminado, y en fracaso -- por sorpresa fue capturado por el Guardián del Agua, y el arma que portaba no le sirvió de nada.\
\
'¡Los pasillos circundantes se están llenando de orcos, capitán! Hice todo lo posible por regresar aquí, ¡pero ha sido en vano!'","Frár está esperando en el lado occidental del Puente de Khazad-dûm.\
\
¡Frár necesita desesperadamente tu ayuda si los orcos deben ser rechazados!","Thíli está en la Cámara de Mazarbul, esperando para hablar contigo mientras el resto de los enanos preparan las defensas.","'¡Las cosas no van bien, capitán! No hay fin a las criaturas: por cada orco que matamos, dos más salen de la oscuridad.\
\
'¡Pero somos los enanos de Khazad-dûm! ¡No dejaremos que estos malditos nos echen de las galerías en las que hemos vivido tan poco tiempo!'","Habla con Frár","'No me gusta esto, capitán. Hay una sombra delante de nosotros. Mira cómo tiemblan mis manos, ¡y nunca he temblado ante ningún enemigo! Un gran mal espera en este pasaje, peor que todos los males que hemos visto hoy. No... no creo que podamos enfrentarnos a esta cosa.\
\
'¡Debemos retirarnos! ¡Debemos retroceder! ¡Debemos escapar a través del puente!'","'¡Tenemos que sacarte de aquí, capitán Ori! ¡Debemos retirarnos a la Sala Vigesimoprimera y esperar que podamos contenerlos allí!'","Thíli está en la sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Te quedan pocos enanos y todo parece perdido. Thíli está esperando para hablar contigo sobre la situación.","Lóni y Náli están en el lado este del Puente de Khazad-dûm.\
\
Has luchado hasta llegar a los enanos al otro lado del puente y deberías hablar con ellos sobre la situación crítica.","El año es 2994 de la Tercera Edad, y la expedición de Balin en Moria está llegando a su destino sombrío. Eres Ori, uno de los enanos encargados de defender Moria tras la muerte de Balin.","Habla con Frár y escapa"},
[7440]={"After fighting through the dead, you and Raphûz see the treasure he seeks. A small cadre of guards stands between you and Raphûz's goal.","In the shadow of an ancient tomb, Raphûz awaits your counsel.","'There is fear in my heart, yes. But your resolve strengthens mine, ${PLAYER}. We will find what we need and I prove my worth to Igbâl. I know this. We should press on.'","'The wealth within should command Igbâl's attention. I could not have succeeded in this venture without your aid. Please, visit me at my camp in Jirush. I wish to speak more before I bring this to Igbâl, and prove myself worthy to court his daughter.'","Raphûz wishes to claim a treasure from a wealthy tomb in Nirgambâr. You agreed to assist him as he searches this place of the dead.","Raphûz eyes the chest and beckons you closer","Raphûz looks concerned, you should speak with him","Raphûz confirms his resolve and continues forward","Tell Raphûz you are ready to claim the chest","Speak with Raphûz","Raphûz awaits your counsel and assistance to begin","You ventured deeper into the ruins of Nirgambâr. Raphûz's resolve is holding, but he looks nervous.","'There, my friend, do you see? A chest. Undoubtedly it holds the treasure we seek. I have not faced such enemies until now and I will not let these few more deter me from this prize.'\
\
Raphûz adjusts his weapon.\
\
'Come, ${PLAYER}. Let us finish this!'","You fought your way through the Dead at Nirgambâr to obtain a chest containing riches for Raphûz. Raphûz stands near the prize and looks pleased.","Raphûz paused his advance and looks in need of reassurance","Instancia: Riqueza de los Muertos","'I am prepared if you are, my friend. I do not wish to linger near this place any longer than we must. I will admit, there is a sense of dread washing over me.'"},
[7442]={"This is a good place to sit","Speak with Harding","'Ah! The ${RACE} of the hour. Please, take a seat at my right hand, and join your friends at my table. I am honoured to welcome you to my council, ${PLAYER}.'","After helping out the people in and around Harwick, word has gotten back to Harding of your goodness, and he has called a council to hear of your deeds.","<rgb=#FF0000>Sit</rgb> at Harding's right hand","Speak with Harding, Reeve of the Wold","Harding gestures for you to sit at his right hand","Tell Harding you are ready to begin","Instancia: Bienvenido a Harwick","'All settled? Good. Let us begin.'","'Shall we adjourn, ${PLAYER}? I am sure you have much to do here in town.'","Harding holds his council in the upper level of the Mead Hall in Harwick.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF0000>sit</rgb> in the chair to Harding's right.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest requires that you perform an emote while in the appropriate place.</rgb>","Harding holds his council in the upper level of the Mead Hall in Harwick.","Observe Harding's council","'I meant what I said, ${PLAYER}. I am truly sorry for my treatment of you when first we met.\
\
'My behaviour towards outsiders is always suspicious, and for that Harwick is safe, but I see that I close us off from good as well as evil.'"},
[7443]={"Do not hand them all the gold, dwarf, for it is not yours","Talk to Gradrágh","Defeat Grúshat the Thrasher","A covert meeting between the forge-workers and the Easterling contingent might just yield a way out of Udûn.","Indeed, all your lives are forfeit for treachery against Ugrukhôr, Captain of the Pit","A louder, more dismayed murmur rises from among the forge-workers","Instancia: Lo que se dijo y lo que se reveló","'Fah! This is not the way. No, no.'\
\
But rather than speak, Kurtil kicks Overseer Gradrágh in the foot. The two meet eyes and the overseer clears his throat.","See who approaches","What menacing voice spoke those words? See who approaches.","Talk to Kurtil","The enforcer and Rogmul are defeated, but the parley is lost beyond hope.","'${PLAYER}, why is the meeting flag still raised? We are all here. It draws attention. I do not like it.\
\
'Go, pull it down.'","The meeting is underway. The forge-workers are presenting their case.","Take down the meeting flag","It seems that Kurtil wants to whisper something to you.","The meeting is underway. Can Gradrágh salvage the situation?","Defeated the Rogmul Rúthragon","The meeting is beginning.","The meeting is underway. The two sides do not yet see eye to eye.","Defeated Grúshat the Thrasher","'It goes, it goes! You and I listen and watch, yes? Let others do the talking. That is best.'","Gradrágh asked you to pull down the meeting flag, as it is no longer needed and only draws attention to the covert gathering.","Watch and listen","All hope is lost","Gradrágh has beckoned you over.","Defeat the Rogmul Rúthragon","A murmur issues from the gathered crowd","Gradrágh beckons you over","Things are not going well. Kurtil has motioned you over."},
[7444]={"'I have seen a great deal in the seeing-stone, ${CLASS}, but these terrible visions fill me with dread as never before!\
\
'You have seen what I saw in the stone. Hirgon and the Red Arrow did not make it to Rohan, and the foolish one Mithrandir sent to Mordor is a captive in Cirith Ungol! Yes, I know of that errand. And I know it has failed! Whatever that fool brought with him is now gone, and if it is the weapon I perceive, it will not matter if the gates of Minas Tirith last five minutes or five hours. The end will come!\
\
'Listen to my words, ${PLAYER}. Hear what I say, and tremble at the truth in them! There can be no turning back from this doom. It comes even now...'","The images fade, becoming more and more difficult to see clearly.","Steward Denethor has summoned you to an audience in the Tower of Ecthelion.","Denethor has instructed you to look into the depths of the palantír.","Talk to Denethor","Follow Denethor","You are standing by the palantír in Denethor's secret chamber, trying to shake the troubling images from your mind. Even so, they linger still.","Talk to Denethor in the Tower Hall","Instancia: Lo que vio el Senescal","'Hirgon was to present the Red Arrow to Théoden of the Riddermark, and by doing so summon the Riders of Rohan to our defence. He has been gone for more than a week, and now I see that he is slain!\
\
'No one is coming to help us!'","Slowly, your mind clears, and you shake the visions from your sight","Hazy images swirl before your eyes!","'This is the Tower Hall, ${PLAYER}. Do not tell anyone, but the Steward makes me nervous. I will show you where to go and then return to my posting outside, glad he does not need me at the moment!'","'Listen to my words... hear them and know they are true, for the doom of Gondor is at hand!'","Denethor has brought you to a secret chamber high in the Tower of Ecthelion.","'Osgiliath was our last line of defence, and now it is taken! The armies of the Enemy spill onto the plain, and their siege engines and weapons of war eagerly follow!\
\
'The forces arrayed against us are vast, and they hunger for our destruction!'","Peregrin Took has led you into the Tower of Ecthelion for your audience with Steward Denethor.","You recognize the captive immediately. It is Frodo","'Imrahil told me you were with my son when he fell before the city, ${PLAYER}. Would that you had drawn his foes away, or put yourself between his horse and the wraiths! He fights still, but it is an unnatural wound. It saps his strength, and his body is wasting away. My son!'\
\
Denethor's voice breaks, and his eye is drawn back to Faramir's bed. He shakes his head, and when he speaks again his voice is full of iron and his fists are clenched.\
\
'Do you know what it is like to live so near to Mordor, ${PLAYER}? Do you know what it is like to stand on the wall of your city and see flames on the horizon, knowing that they signal some terrible work of evil? Do you know what it is to be always in the thought of creatures so vile and so terrible that even Death cannot master them?\
\
'I know what it is like, ${CLASS}. Every morning I wake up knowing it, and every evening I retire to my chamber knowing it. And in the darkest reaches of the night, I wake from troubled dreams knowing it.\
\
'I have struggled long with this knowledge, and I struggle still, though my sons and heirs be taken from me. I struggle for my people.'","Hazy images swirl before your eyes.","Examine the captive hobbit","Talk to Peregrin Took in the Tower Hall","Denethor has brought you to a secret chamber high in the Tower of Ecthelion","The hazy images become more indistinct!","Look into the depths of the palantír","'Mithrandir does not share his mind with me, but I know of the dream that came to my sons, the dream that tried to snare Faramir but stole Boromir instead. This must be the Halfling, captured by the Enemy and held in his tower!\
\
'We are undone by the folly of Mithrandir!'","'No one comes to this chamber without my leave, ${PLAYER}, and I grant that sparingly! When I look at you I see a student of Mithrandir. The Wizard has been a friend to Gondor, so far, but he does not have the full measure of my trust. Why should he possess it? He is not of this land, and if the battle turns ill he will simply leave it, leaving my people to suffer and die!\
\
'I am not without weapons, ${PLAYER}. I brought you here so you will see that I still fight the Enemy, though none appreciate the battle I wage within this high chamber!\
\
'This is a seeing-stone, an heirloom of the Kings of old. I have turned it to my will.'","Talk to Denethor in his secret chamber","Denethor wishes to show you something, and has invited you to a secret chamber in the Tower of Ecthelion.","Steward Denethor is in the Tower Hall, waiting to speak with you."},
[7445]={"You have descended a secret stairway into a hidden wing of the dungeons of Dol Guldur, where intense shadow covers its lost chambers.","Sigileth of the Hidden Guard lives still!","Examine objects within the Room of Voices","Witness the shadowy impressions evil has left upon this chamber","An old companion steps into the room","A powerful presence has left its mark upon this chamber, and fell voices whisper of the past.","Your reverie is broken by the sound of footsteps in the west passage!","Cautiously investigate the western passage","Shadowy impressions from the past unfold before your sight","Someone is approaching from the western passage!","You thought her dead, but somehow Sigileth of the Hidden Guard is still alive!","Instancia: Susurros de los largos años","Intense shadow blankets the area. What evils might this forgotten chamber have held before the fall of Sauron?","'Is it really you, ${PLAYER}? I feared all my companions among the Hidden Guard were dead, but here you stand!\
\
'I made a place of my own in these dungeons and levied terror upon their fell inhabitants in the name of my Lady. Let us return to my secret lodgings before we press through the Room of Voices, and I will collect the few belongings I left behind. I could not pass through its deep shadow on my own, but together I believe we can.\
\
'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}.'","Cross the bridge and explore the room beyond","There may be more to discover within this Room of Voices.","Talk to Sigileth in the Room of Voices"},
[7446]={"Sigileth is standing at the edge of the Room of Voices in Gostador.\
\
You have witnessed many events of Karazgar's past, but did not find Karazgar in Gostador. After waiting for a time, Sigileth has come to find you.","'What has happened, ${PLAYER}? Did Karazgar escape by some secret path?'\
\
You explain to Sigileth that shadowy impressions revealed much of the history of Karazgar and Sauron in Dol Guldur. After the impressions were interrupted when you first came to Gostador and discovered Sigileth, you were meant to return and witness the last remnants of the Necromancer's evil lingering within the Room of Voices.\
\
'I am not certain I understand, but I believe your words. Karazgar is an elusive foe, but it seems something of his mind was revealed to you. Let us hope there is an advantage to be gained from it!\
\
'The Orcs that remain here have grown hungry and wild. If you have found what you sought, we should leave this place.'","Witness the shadowy impressions evil has left upon this chamber","'Are you ready? Let us climb from this ruin, and leave this place behind evermore!'","A powerful presence has left its mark upon this chamber, and fell voices whisper of the past.","Karazgar may be found somewhere within the ruins of Gostador.\
\
You have returned to Dol Dhannen in search of Karazgar and have descended into Gostador. You should search for Karazgar.","Instancia: Susurros en los Fosos","As you approach the throne of the Necromancer, a vision comes over you...","Shadowy impressions from the past unfold before your sight","Examine objects within the Room of Voices in Gostador","As the shadowy impressions fade, you hear a familiar voice calling out for you...","Although Galadriel remains doubtful that Karazgar has returned to the ruins of Dol Guldur, she has mustered a company to aid you in your search for the Weeping Warrior in the depths of Dol Dhannen.","There may be more left to discover within the Room of Voices.","Talk to Sigileth in the Room of Voices","Search for signs of Karazgar in Gostador"},
[7447]={"When the guard starts walking again, distract him by waving <rgb=#00FF00>/bye</rgb>","You distracted the guard and Ayaluk escaped","The guard returned to his post and Ayaluk was caught","Distract the guard with a <rgb=#00FF00>/hail</rgb>","Keep the guard distracted for one full minute","Distract the guard by clearing your throat <rgb=#00FF00>/ahem</rgb>","'I only need you to distract the guard for a few moments while I search the office. Distract the guard however you can. Annoy them if you must. Wave bye, hail them, clear your throat at them. Anything to keep them occupied.'","You distracted the guard well enough for Ayaluk to search and escape. Return to his hiding spot near the building east of Ulanor's office.","Speak with Ayaluk at a building near Ulanor's chambers","Ayaluk asked you to distract the guard while he sneaks into Ulanor's office to find proof of her wrongdoing.","Instancia: Susurros de la Forja","Meet Ayaluk at the edge of the building near the overseer's chambers.","You agreed to assist Ayaluk in obtaining proof of the overseer's wrongdoing in Rakhatâb.","Speak with Ayaluk near his original hiding spot","'What I found is worse than I feared. I need some time to review this information. Meet me at my home. Now I must go!'","'Let's make haste and do not be seen.'"},
[7449]={"'I have explored many of the dwarf-holds that stand still in Middle-earth, but few can compare to the grand chambers within and beneath the Lonely Mountain. Look about you at Mazal Akrâz, and know that its beauty and grandeur is deserved by those who rest within!'","You have come with Thorin's Company, his sister Dís, and Gandalf the Wizard to ensure the Arkenstone still remains entombed with Thorin Oakenshield within Mazal Akrâz, the Chamber of Glory.","'It eases my heart to know the Arkenstone remains with Thorin, but this means the decline of his people's craft-skill must have another cause. A wizard's guess is not the same as any other's, ${PLAYER}, and it is the guess of this wizard that the loss of the dwarf-rings might be to blame for this decay. The ring Angya, called Handórm by the dwarves, was taken from Thráin by Sauron and must have perished in the fall of Barad-dûr.'","'I am ready, ${PLAYER}. Let us see what there is to see.'","'Bifur and Bósi tell me you fought alongside my son when the Iron Garrison failed. I thank you for standing by him, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Bofur stands silently for a moment, gazing away into the darkness of Mazal Akrâz.\
\
'I had hoped he would live a long life, and when his days were spent at last he would be put to rest beside me and our kin in the Blue Mountains, but that is not to be. Instead he departs soonest, and lies now in a tomb even grander than this, for he rests in Khazad-dûm. Alas for Brogur, alas for my son! He was a finer dwarf than I, and had more to offer his people.'","'It has been some time since my son Brogur has written to me of his adventures with the Iron Garrison in Khazad-dûm. By all accounts, the avenues and halls of that kingdom make for beautiful sights like no other!'","'Thank you for suggesting this excursion, ${PLAYER}. I enjoyed seeing my kin again, though they be gone these many years. You will always be welcome at Raven-hill whenever you wish to visit me.\
\
'As for your wizard, he talks too much. Leave him behind when you come to visit.'","'I and my retinue arrived during the Battle of Dale, and joined the fighting with great relish. This visit to the tomb of my cousin fills me with more worry than did the exertion of that battle. If the Heart of the Mountain does not lie within, what then will we do?\
\
'Bah, we will soon know. We are near to the platform.'","'The Battle of Five Armies claimed the lives of Thorin Oakenshield and his nephews Fíli and Kíli. All three of them fought bravely and well, and without their courage things that day might have gone differently. We owe them each a debt, even today, so many years later.'","'From Dál-haim came Dálheim, which passed then to Dale-home, and is now Dale. Geirjarn became Girion, whose necklace caused much trouble between Thranduil of the Wood and the dwarves of the Mountain. Of all my many names, that which I wear in the North was not first; even that came from Wandalb, for Frumgar called me the Elf of the Wand, not knowing my true nature. Wood, Lake, Mountain, and Stone... each has their own words, and even when they speak of the same thing they may not find understanding.'\
\
Gandalf looks at you closely, a curious look in his eye.\
\
'${PLAYER}, what if the artifact for which we seek, this Bugdatish, never existed at all? Since this journey began neither friend nor foe have learned aught of it. No sign of this relic can be found. What if Ugrukhôr seeks an artifact that never was? Words can mean different things in different contexts, my friend, and even a small change can greatly affect a word's meaning. Can it be that Ugrukhôr does not look for that which we assumed?'","Instancia: Madera, Lago, Montaña y Piedra","'It seemed appropriate for Dís to go on ahead and for the rest of us to follow along behind. Her brother Thorin and her sons Fíli and Kíli lie entombed within, and while our purpose here is one of importance, I do not wish to work any disrespect upon the fallen.\
\
'I will meet you at the bottom, ${PLAYER}. Keep watch upon your footing.'","'Mazal Akrâz was delved deep, fashioned with the labour of our finest dwarves, for Thorin and his nephews deserved a grand tomb. But it cannot hold a flickering candle to the glory of Khazad-dûm, where my son now adventures! The reports I have heard from Bósi and the Iron Garrison fill me with pride, and I delight at their successes!'","Dís stands by the tomb of her brother and her sons, in Mazal Akrâz, the Chamber of Glory.","Remain alert while Gandalf and the dwarves open the tomb","Gandalf is waiting to speak with you at the top of Mazal Akrâz, the Chamber of Glory.","Gandalf agreed to meet you by the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield, at the bottom of Mazal Akrâz, the Chamber of Glory.","Talk to Gandalf in Mazal Akrâz","Gandalf is by the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield, in Mazal Akrâz.","Talk to Dís in Mazal Akrâz","Talk to Gandalf at the top of Mazal Akrâz","Listen to the words of Gandalf","'I wanted to say something to you, ${PLAYER}, but I have not seen an opportunity before now. I wish to thank you for the aid you supplied to my son Bósi during the expedition of the Iron Garrison to Khazad-dûm. It has ended in failure, to his grief and shame, but that does not eliminate the efforts you and other good-hearted folk supplied to him in their attempted conquest.\
\
'I thank you on his behalf. We will not forget the Iron Garrison; neither will we forget those who fought alongside our dwarves in the darkness of that kingdom, though it remain lost.'","Relieved that the Arkenstone remains with Thorin, Gandalf wishes to say a few words to you and to the dwarves.","'Thorin was my cousin. I hope he rests well, and still keeps the Arkenstone safe. He came to regret some of the words he spoke to Bilbo; in the end he repented of them and they parted in kindness. We all thought it right that the Heart of the Mountain be laid to rest with Thorin. The disagreements concerning its disposition came later.'","'We must take a brief rest, and then we will be off again. Do not wait on my account, ${PLAYER}! I will be along shortly. These steps are perilous for the young, but what can be done? Nothing. I show them as much patience as I am able, and I ask you to do the same.'","The dwarves of Thorin's Company, his sister Dís, and Gandalf have come to Mazal Akrâz to see if the Arkenstone remains within.","Listen to Gandalf's lecture on the evolution of words","Descend the steps in Mazal Akrâz and make your way to the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield"},
[7450]={"'You and I will take the right side. Gifemund and Nothmar should be able to handle the left. Keep your eye on them and help if they need it, but you should stick with me.\
\
'We will make quick work of the defilers of our great hall.'","'Arnwi's fate was sealed when he killed Calin, and turned on all of us with the White Hand.\
\
'They are likely prepared for us inside. We need to be careful. The time to end this is now.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Herubrand has been defeated</rgb>","Speak with Gifemund ahead of you.\
\
The time has come to re-capture the fountain area, but you will need Gifemund's aid.","<rgb=#FF0000>Herubrand must survive</rgb>","Speak with Gifemund","Herubrand is near the throne in the mead hall.\
\
Herubrand would like to thank you for your part in aiding their victory.","<rgb=#FF0000>Manna must survive</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Gifemund must survive</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Nothmar must survive</rgb>","'If any enemy still remain in the city they will be routed out. With their leaders defeated there will no longer be organized resistance. The city is finally ours again.'","Defeat Thurferth and the enemy at the throne","The White Hand have conquered Woodhurst and are now openly marching in the streets. You must aid Herubrand, Gifemund, and Nothmar in reclaiming the city.","Herubrand is standing outside the mead hall door.\
\
Herubrand wishes to speak with you after defeating Arnwi.","<rgb=#FF0000>Gifemund has been defeated</rgb>","Instancia: Woodhurst ha Caído","<rgb=#FF0000>Manna has been defeated</rgb>","Make your way to the throne","Herubrand has arrived at the fountain.\
\
Herubrand wishes to speak with you about the plan to retake the mead hall.","'This is only the beginning. We need to make our way to the mead hall door. Nothmar's men will stay with Manna and Scurfa, and will hold the fountain area behind us.'","Thurferth, a White Hand Emissary and a Dunlending named Cadwalader are standing in front of the throne.\
\
Those who organized the fall of Woodhurst now boldly claim ownership of the city.","Capture the fountain area","Herubrand waits to speak with you before approaching those waiting for you at the throne of the mead hall.","Speak with Herubrand","'We are victorious! ${PLAYER}, I cannot thank you enough for your aid in reclaiming Woodhurst from the cruel grip of the White Hand. We could not have claimed victory today without you.\
\
'Gifemund and I have much to discuss about the future of Woodhurst. There is time for that. Today, we celebrate our victory.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Nothmar has been defeated</rgb>","Herubrand is within the door of the mead hall.\
\
Herubrand wishes to give directions on how the group will approach the coming battle.","Enter the mead hall with the others.\
\
The battle for Woodhurst has progressed into the mead hall.","<rgb=#FF0000>Scurfa has been defeated</rgb>","You defeated the enemy around the fountain, and can hear Herubrand and Nothmar approaching...","Defeat the enemy outside the mead hall","Defeat the enemy who hold the fountain area in Woodhurst.","The enemy has heavily guarded the pathway up to the mead hall, and appear to be guarding the front door.","<rgb=#FF0000>Scurfa must survive</rgb>","Follow the others into the mead hall","Defeat the enemy throughout the mead hall and make your way to the throne.","'We have a fight ahead of us. Herubrand and Nothmar said they would meet us at the fountain. We should capture and hold the fountain area while they make their way to us.'","'Thurferth, that vile traitor! He helped them take the city...\
\
'Weapons ready! For glory!'","Herubrand signals to Nothmar and Gifemund to attack"},
[7452]={"'Come, we will reassemble at the Mead Hall.'","'You have fought well, but this plague of Orcs and Uruks seems endless. In a short time, the Orcs will have taken hold of the area again, and we will have to clear them out once more. For now, we must be content with having cleared the road for those seeking refuge.\
\
'You fight with bravery and heroism... I see now why some consider you to be such a gallant ${CLASS}. Let us return to the city.'","Athelward can be found along the road south of Cliving.\
\
Athelward wishes to discuss the results of your encounter with the Orcs and Uruks.","Accompany Reeve Athelward on the field of battle.","You have completed patrolling the southern road","Talk to Reeve Athelward","Talk to Athelward","Reeve Athelward is not content with simply giving orders. He wishes to lead by example. He has taken to the fields alongside you, in order to witness your prowess in battle firsthand.","'Stay with me as I patrol this area. We shall remove from these lands any of the scattered vermin that now infest them.\
\
'Ready your weapon, friend. If your noteworthy reputation is not groundless, these Orcs should prove to be no match for us.'","Instancia: La ira del Reeve"},
[7453]={"Ghân-gharâf se encuentra muy por debajo de las Profundidades Inundadas, más allá de una serie de cavernas parcialmente inundadas.\
\
Bróin desea que seas testigo del regreso de Zigilburk a Ghân-gharâf. En tu camino, hablarás con muchos de los enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro que has ayudado durante tus viajes por Moria.","Habla con Ráthwald","Habla con Rink","Habla con Bróin","'Gracias por venir aquí por nosotros, ${PLAYER}. Bróin está un poco más adelante, con Zigilburk.\
\
'Es lo mejor; el hacha de mithril no debe ser usada a partir de ahora, dejada para todas las edades del mundo en la cámara acuática donde fue encontrada.'","'Volvamos a la Sala Vigesimoprimera. Hemos hecho lo que nos propusimos hacer, ${PLAYER}. Hemos tomado la difícil decisión... la correcta.'","Habla con Wafi","'Mis enanos han sido llamados hoy para colapsar el pasaje que conduce a Ghân-gharâf, una vez que el hacha de mithril haya sido dejada dentro. ¡Me resulta extraño cubrir un pasaje, en lugar de descubrirlo!\
\
'De hecho, ayudaste a mis enanos a desenterrar las Puertas de Durin en la Puerta Oeste, ¿no es así? Hemos tenido muchas dificultades desde entonces, pero mira ahora la gloria de la Guarnición de Hierro. ¡El verdadero trabajo apenas ha comenzado!'","'¡Muy bien, muy bien, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! Me alegra que hayas venido; sé que es importante para Bróin que estés aquí.\
\
'Aún recuerdo cómo te encargaste de matar a los crebains que intentaban espiar a la Guarnición de Hierro en nuestro campamento justo afuera de la Puerta de Acebeda. ¿Quién sabe qué malhechores evitaste ese día, ? Esos sucios pájaros no pudieron reportar nada de lo que hacíamos a su misterioso amo, gracias a ti.\
\
'¡Y gracias al enano que te pidió que lo hicieras también!'","Habla con Bori","Habla con Stóthkell","'Te doy la bienvenida de nuevo a Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Por el gran servicio que has hecho a mi familia y por rescatar a mi hijo de las mazmorras de Dol Guldur, siempre tendrás un hogar aquí, si lo quieres.\
\
'Sé que Brogur no está contento con la idea de dejar Zigilburk en las profundidades de Ghân-gharâf, sin tocar, pero el hacha de mithril nos ha traído poco más que problemas. Estoy de acuerdo con mi hijo y mi sobrino en esto.'","Estás presente para presenciar el sellado de Zigilburk.","'¡Cuidado con tus pasos, ${PLAYER}! El terreno aquí es traicionero.'\
\
Sweina piensa por un momento, y luego se ríe.\
\
'¿Quién soy yo para decirte qué es traicionero? Nos conocimos cuando me lancé audazmente a las profundidades de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata para desafiar a un nido de trasgos en combate. ¡Podría haberme defendido admirablemente, y estaba a punto de hacerlo, pero tu intervención fue igualmente apreciada!'","Presencia el sellado de Ghân-gharâf","'¡Míranos, ${PLAYER}! ¿Alguna vez pensaste que estaríamos en este lugar, a punto de dejar un arma de tal poder enterrada detrás de grandes muros de piedra, para nunca más ser usada?\
\
'¿Es este el curso correcto de acción? Bueno, eso es algo que Bósi y Brogur, y sus hijos, deben decidir. Hacemos nuestro deber, como se nos asigna, y debemos confiar en que ellos saben lo que hacen.\
\
'¿Me dudaste cuando te envié a recuperar armas utilizables por toda Khazad-dûm? Fue por una buena causa, ¿no es así?'","'¡Sabía que no te perderías este momento, ${PLAYER}, ${RACE} que eres! Parece que la aventura te sigue dondequiera que vayas.\
\
'Las hazañas heroicas que cometimos en las profundidades de Buzun-ghâr y en Rushdurinul todavía son una maravilla para mí... y lo serán hasta el fin de mis días, estoy seguro.\
\
'¡Las historias de las que hemos sido parte resonarán hasta las alturas talladas del más grandioso salón de cerveza de Khazad-dûm!'","Habla con Sigdan","Instancia: El regreso de Zigilburk","Habla con Sweina","Habla con Hundi","Bróin te ha dicho que le digas a Bori que Zigilburk ha sido dejado con Óin en la cámara inundada.","Habla con Stilling","Habla con Brogur.","'Como puedes ver, logramos resistir a los Orcos, ${PLAYER}. Thórgnyr y yo mantuvimos el flujo de suministros hacia cada uno de los puestos avanzados de la Guarnición de Hierro dentro de Khazad-dûm.\
\
'Fuiste una gran parte de nuestro éxito para mantener las líneas de suministro funcionando, ${PLAYER}, y te lo agradecemos.'","'¿Tienes la intención de seguir esta tonta decisión de mi hijo y mi sobrino de dejar Zigilburk aquí, en las profundidades?\
\
'Esto es un error, ${PLAYER}. Estoy seguro de que cualquier desgracia que nos haya traído el hacha de mithril nos habría caído encima incluso sin ella.\
\
'¿Por qué abandonar un arma así? ¡Seguramente la necesitaremos de nuevo! ¿Puedes decir que no?'","'No te he visto desde que pasaste a Moria, ${PLAYER}! ¿Cómo te ha servido el arma legendaria que te di de las reliquias desenterradas en Eregion?'\
\
El ceño de Hundi se frunce con decepción ante tu respuesta.\
\
'¿La has rehecho? Oh, ya veo. Bueno, a veces es así con las armas, ¿no es así?'","Ghân-gharâf se encuentra muy por debajo de las Profundidades Inundadas, más allá de una serie de cavernas parcialmente inundadas.\
\
Bróin desea que seas testigo del regreso de Zigilburk a Ghân-gharâf. En tu camino, hablarás con muchos de los Enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro a los que has ayudado durante tus viajes por Moria.","'Entonces está hecho. Es bueno saber que Zigilburk no molestará más a los enanos.'","Habla con Tulk","'Mira, Wili, si no es nuestro compañero, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Puede que no lo recuerdes, ${PLAYER}, pero Wili y yo lanzamos el ataque de distracción en el Cruce Vigilado mientras tú y Bori se enfrentaban a Ashpar en Stazgnâkh.\
\
'¡No fue nada fácil evitar que los Orcos regresaran mientras aún estabas en su campamento, pero lo logramos!'","Habla con Wárr","'Esta es la última vez que estaré dentro de las paredes de Ghân-gharâf, ${PLAYER}. Recuerdo cuando salí arrastrándome, empapado y asustado, de la piscina, y mis ojos se posaron en esta cámara inundada.\
\
'Si no hubiera sido por Zigilburk, agarrada en la mano del enano Óin, amigo de mi abuelo, no habría podido mantener a raya a la terrible bestia de la piscina.'","'Ah, estos túneles no serán usados por los enanos después de este día. Me pregunto qué historias surgirán entre nuestros jóvenes parientes sobre nuestras acciones aquí.\
\
'Ya le he contado a mi hijo sobre la gran habilidad con la que despachaste a los corredores trasgos en las Profundidades Inundadas por mí, ${PLAYER}. Está asombrado por el número... aunque para ser sincero, he olvidado cuántos fueron. ¿Cincuenta? ¿Cien?'","Habla con Slóthi","'He venido a presenciar el sellado de Zigilburk en persona, ${PLAYER}, y pocos de mis enanos pudieron soportar la idea de venir conmigo. El hacha de mithril fue forjada en el Corazón de Fuego durante un tiempo muy lejano, y que ya no se use me parece una gran vergüenza.\
\
'Entiendo que este hacha ha traído muchos malos recuerdos para los Enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro pero como maestro de las forjas y un enano apasionado por el trabajo artesanal, el momento marca el amanecer de un nuevo día para mí.'","Habla con Orvar","Habla con Thálfi","'Ciertamente hemos recorrido un largo camino desde que solicité tu ayuda para la Guarnición de Hierro, ¿no es así, ${PLAYER}? ¿Quién podría decir que esperaba que fueras de tanta ayuda para nosotros? ¡Debo admitir que yo no lo esperaba!\
\
'Nosotros, los enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro, nos reunimos para presenciar el sellado del hacha de mithril en las profundidades de Ghân-gharâf. Estoy seguro de que todos querrán hablar contigo mientras te diriges a Bróin.'","'Ya casi estás en Ghân-gharâf, ${PLAYER}. No pensé que estaría tan lejos, pero Melmar aquí me asegura que ya estamos cerca.'","Bróin ha decidido que Zigilburk no puede permanecer con los Enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro y ha llamado a su gente a Ghân-gharâf para devolver el hacha al lugar de donde proviene.","'¡Cuidado, ${PLAYER}! ¡El agua aquí es rápida!\
\
'Mi primo Sporr todavía está de servicio, explorando los caminos de la Cámara de la Encrucijada, pero sé que Sporr apreció tu ayuda persiguiendo a los espías orcos antes de la gran batalla.\
\
'¡Fue un trabajo bien hecho, ${PLAYER}, y ha sido un placer trabajar para recuperar los salones de Khazad-dûm con un aliado tan firme como tú!'","Habla con Bósi.","Ghân-gharâf se encuentra muy por debajo de las Profundidades Inundadas, más allá de una serie de cavernas parcialmente inundadas.\
\
Bróin desea que presencies el regreso de Zigilburk a Ghân-gharâf. En tu camino, hablarás con muchos de los enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro que has ayudado durante tus viajes dentro de Moria."},
[7454]={"Recolecta mineral de narfulz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El mineral de narfulz se puede encontrar en el lado oeste del Puente de Khazad-dûm, al sureste de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
El siguiente paso en las instrucciones del mapa para construir la antorcha implica el procesamiento del mineral de narfulz, un metal conocido por prenderse fuego cuando se muele en polvo.","Geirfast se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, al noroeste del Puente de Khazad-dûm.\
\
Geirfast querrá comenzar a procesar el mineral de narfulz en polvo para la antorcha.","'Esto debería funcionar muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Muy bien, de hecho.\
\
'Ahora, examinemos el mapa para conocer el siguiente componente de esta antorcha...\
\
'Las siguientes instrucciones son... algo desagradables. ¿Sabes dónde encontrar gusanos de las profundidades? Necesitamos recolectar su ícor, convertirlo en una pasta y untarla por toda la antorcha. Aparentemente el ícor tiene algún efecto sobre el color o el brillo de la antorcha, no estoy seguro de cuál.\
\
'He visto gusanos al sureste de aquí, más allá del pie de Khadar-zarâm, pero antes del Puente de Khazad-dûm. Búscalos alrededor de las piscinas del este.\
\
'Tráeme todo el ícor que puedas y procederemos al siguiente paso.'","Instrucciones en el mapa","Este mapa es antiguo, desgastado y ha sido manipulado en numerosas ocasiones. Representa una cámara oculta y contiene instrucciones complicadas para la fabricación de una antorcha muy especial.","'Ten cuidado con el mineral de narfulz, ${PLAYER}. Aunque no debería prenderse hasta que esté pulverizado, hace mucho tiempo que ningún enano lo ha trabajado.'","'Tu resplandor casi anuncia tu regreso, mi ${PLAYERNAME:buen -- y ligeramente empapado[m]|buena -- y ligeramente empapada[f]} -- .\
\
'No me llevará más que unos momentos convertir esto en la pasta descrita en las instrucciones que lleva el mapa...\
\
'No estoy completamente seguro de que mi dedo deje de brillar en verde. ¿Qué pedirán a continuación?\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:seguro[m]|segura[f]} de que quieres continuar con esta empresa, mi ${PLAYERNAME:temerario[m]|temeraria[f]} ? No se pone más fácil. Lo siguiente que las instrucciones piden es un mineral muy raro -- los enanos lo llamamos mineral de narfulz, porque cuando se martilla fino, arde con una luz blanca que atraviesa como un rayo de sol en la oscuridad. ¡Sí, metal de fuego! He oído que se usa como luz, pero rara vez, ya que es difícil de encontrar y refinar.\
\
'Encontrarás mineral de narfulz al este. Dirígete a Nud-melek, hasta el borde del Puente de Khazad-dûm, y busca en esa área. Las rocas con el mineral presentan una veta verde.'","Recolección de ícor de gusanos de las profundidades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Páshnar se encuentra más allá de Khadar-zarâm.'","Geirfast se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, al noroeste de Khadar-zarâm.\
\
Geirfast estará ansioso por comenzar a convertir el ícor en una pasta para la antorcha.","Has encontrado un mapa antiguo entre los restos del Campamento de Balin. Contiene instrucciones para fabricar una antorcha muy extraña y especial.","Habla con los enanos de la Sala Vigesimoprimera sobre el mapa","Mineral de narfulz recolectado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Maravilloso! Temía que no pudieras encontrar ninguno. ¡Excelente trabajo!\
\
'Me llevará un tiempo convertir esto de forma segura en el polvo que la mapa pide...'","Ícor de gusano de las profundidades recogido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva la antorcha endeble a Geirfast en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","El ícor se puede encontrar en los gusanos de las profundidades entre Khadar-zarâm y el Puente de Khazad-dûm, al sureste de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Para continuar con el siguiente paso de la fabricación de la antorcha, Geirfast te ha dicho que necesita ícor de los gusanos de las profundidades de Nud-melek.","Puedes encontrar enanos en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, al oeste del Campamento de Balin.\
\
Quizás desees consultar con los enanos de la Sala Vigesimoprimera sobre el mapa que encontraste. Tal vez uno de ellos pueda ayudarte a descifrarlo.","Has recogido una antorcha endeble de Páshnar","'¿Qué tienes ahí? Muéstrame, vamos a extenderlo por el suelo para echarle un buen vistazo.\
\
'Esta mapa es antiguo, pero no es de la Khazad-dûm de la época de Durin. Estoy seguro de eso: mira lo rectas que son las líneas de estas runas. Son de un estilo popular hace algunos siglos en Ered Luin. Da instrucciones para fabricar una antorcha de un tipo del que nunca he oído hablar. Por la barba de Durin, mira lo que se necesita... esta base recubierta de aceite va a ser difícil de encontrar.\
\
'Un momento. ¡Ya lo tengo! Los jinetes de huargos a veces llevan antorchas similares, sumergidas en aceite de roca: toma una de ellos y estarás un paso más cerca de fabricar esta antorcha. Dirígete al este por Khadar-zarâm, luego mira hacia el sur.'","'Reconozco que el ícor de los gusanos de las profundidades no es exactamente lo más atractivo para recolectar. Te sugeriría que intentes evitar que se te manche la ropa.'","Lleva el mineral de narfulz a Geirfast en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Lleva el ícor de los gusanos de las profundidades a Geirfast en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Recoge una antorcha endeble de Páshnar","Geirfast se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, al oeste de Khadar-zarâm.\
\
Geirfast podrá ayudarte a aprender qué hacer a continuación para revelar el tesoro del mapa.","Páshnar se encuentra al norte de Khadar-zarâm, al este de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Geirfast cree que podrías obtener una antorcha de Páshnar, un goblin jinete de huargo. Esta antorcha te permitirá comenzar a seguir las instrucciones encontradas en el antiguo mapa."},
[7455]={"Has recogido lanzas de los orcos de la Mano Blanca en Skrithûrz-ulíma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Instrumentos del enemigo","Los orcos que empuñan lanzas pueden encontrarse en Skrithûrz-ulíma, al noroeste de la Guardia Orca.\
\
Los orcos están utilizando lanzas robadas de los antiguos arsenales de armas de Moria.","Moria está llena de antiguas reservas de armas de los antepasados de los enanos. La mayoría de las mejores piezas desaparecieron hace tiempo, pero los orcos de Skrithûrz-ulíma han encontrado un gran suministro de lanzas.\
\
Las lanzas son armas peligrosas en manos de un oponente experimentado.","Los orcos de Moria llevan mucho tiempo saqueando los arsenales de antiguas armas enanas almacenadas en las viejas salas, pero las lanzas que utilizan ahora son especialmente crueles y mortales.","Completado","Recoge lanzas de los orcos de la Mano Blanca en Skrithûrz-ulíma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se reconoce la obra de un verdadero artesano cuando resiste el paso del tiempo.\
\
Has recuperado valiosas armas de manos equivocadas y probablemente has salvado la vida de muchos enanos inocentes que habrían sufrido el filo de esas lanzas.","Has recuperado muchas lanzas antiguas de los orcos de Skrithûrz-ulíma.","Recoge lanzas de los orcos en Skrithûrz-ulíma"},
[7457]={"Defeat the Kala-gijak messenger","'I spotted a group of Uruk-hai travelling between Kala-gijak and what we suspect may be the direction of Seregost. If the Uruks are getting their orders from that forsaken place, perhaps we can intercept the messages to find out more. See if you can find them.'","Collect orders from Seregost","Faeron has spotted an important-looking Uruk travelling between Kala-gijak and Seregost. You should intercept whatever information this messenger carries.","Faeron can be found outside the mountain pass in Agarnaith.\
\
You should talk to Faeron.","Collected orders from Seregost","Talk to Faeron","'Ah, the orders! Let me see. Hmm, so I was correct. Seregost has control of the Uruk-hai in Kala-gijak. And they're aware that we're in Mordor! Interesting. It sounds like they are expecting an invasion force and not the small group of explorers that were actually sent, however. We can possibly use that to our advantage.'","Intercept the Messenger","The Kala-gijak messenger can be found travelling on the path east of Kala-gijak.\
\
You should defeat him and intercept any orders he carries.","Defeated the Kala-gijak messenger"},
[7459]={"Frodo is gone, like all the rest. All of your friends have gone away","Frodo stares at you silently. It has been so long since you have seen him.\
\
You beg him to speak, but you find that you no longer remember the sound of his voice.","There's no sign of Pippin, but you have found... Sam Gamgee?","Save Éowyn","You remember these Orcs. But where is Pip?","Run with the Orcs","Loneliness grips your heart","Nothing moves in the camp of Rohan","Sam looks at you sadly, and then he too is gone","Find a living man among the Rohirrim","Look for Pippin to the south-east, among the barrows","Is that Pippin? You see someone back to the west, among the barrows!","You are surprised to see Sam here among the barrows, and you tell him so. He frowns, and his face is full of sorrow.\
\
'Have you seen Frodo?' he asks. 'I cannot find him anywhere! He was here, and now he is gone!'\
\
You tell him that Pippin has gone away, but you will look for both of them. They cannot be gone forever, can they?","Pippin was here, but now he is gone. Look for him to the south-east, somewhere among the barrows.","Is that Pippin? What is he doing in the Barrow-downs?","This man sleeps the unending sleep of death, and gains no rest from it. His sightless eyes stare at you accusingly.","Éowyn does not respond.\
\
You cannot tell if the warrior lives. Would remaining behind have been a crueler fate?","Talk to Pippin among the barrows","Do any of the Rohirrim still live?","Éowyn is in danger! She needs help!","The man stares past you with sightless eyes. He died on the Pelennor, and will never return home to his family.","Death hangs above all.","Pippin seems as if he wants to say more, but then he is gone","Merry's body is held in the grip of the Black Shadow, but his dreaming mind works to free him of the malady's nightmare.","Talk to Sam among the barrows","What is Sam Gamgee doing here in among the barrows? Where is Frodo?","Your friends have all gone.","Talk to Éowyn","Talk to Dernhelm","Interludio: Un sueño de frío y silencio","Isengard?","Death hangs above all","Find your friend to the north, among the barrows","'Merry! Thank goodness I have found you!'\
\
Your mind is full of confusion. The last thing you remember is the great beast descending on Théoden and Snowmane, and then... and then...\
\
Pippin's face is a mask of concern.\
\
'Théoden? Éowyn? They have been brought up to the Citadel, I think. Gandalf sent me to look for you. Are you wounded? Here, come with me. I'm supposed to bring you back...'","Who has come to this camp among all the dead?","Talk to Uglúk","You remember these Orcs... but where is Pippin?","Find Pippin","'You'll run now, if you know what's good for you! There's a lot of Horse-country to cover, but we'll outpace our pursuers, even in the sunlight!\
\
'Now run, maggot! You'll taste the whip if you do not, and I'll have your hide!'","Dernhelm does not respond.\
\
You cannot tell if the warrior lives, if ever he did."},
[7460]={"Examine Merry and complete 'Interlude: A Dream of Cold and Silence'","The battle may be over, but many of those wounded during the fighting still fight for their lives.","'Look at him, ${PLAYER}. He is so pale! What will I do if he dies?'","Interludio: Un sueño de frío y silencio","Pippin is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.","'A messenger from the Houses of Healing was seeking you on behalf of Peregrin the Halfling. You should go to him in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing and learn why he summons you thither.'","'I am so glad you are here, ${PLAYER}, but I am afraid that not even you can help now! They tell me that the leechcraft of Gondor is the finest in Middle-earth, but no one seems to be able to do anything for Merry. He is caught in the throes of some terrible malady. They call it the Black Shadow, and many of the soldiers that came near to the terrible Riders suffer from it too.\
\
'Merry is so pale! He seems caught in a dream, but sometimes he cries out in his sleep. I wish there was something we could do for him!'","Merry suffers from a malady the Gondorians call the Black Shadow. He is on a bed in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, still caught in the throes of a terrible dream from which he cannot wake.","'Peregrin the Halfling desired to see you. He is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing.'","Pippin is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.","Talk to Pippin in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing","'I was hoping to find you, ${PLAYER}. A messenger from the Houses of Healing was seeking you on behalf of Peregrin the Halfling. You should go to him in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing and learn why he summons you thither.\
\
'Doubtless you would have seen him sometime today, in any event, for I know you have been doing much throughout the city to help in the aftermath of the battle.'","'There you are, ${PLAYER}! Your feet carry you throughout the city with so much haste that I despaired of finding you! Indeed, I had nearly resolved to sit here and wait until your errands brought you once more to this Circle of the city.\
\
'Peregrin the Halfling desired to see you. He is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing.'","'I wish there was something we could do for Merry. I will stay here by his side until I think of something!\
\
'You should keep helping out in the city. I will let you know if I think of anything that might help cure him and these other wounded soldiers of the Black Shadow once and for all!'","Merry has grown very pale, and cannot wake. The Black Shadow comes from the Nazgûl, and he was very near indeed to their leader. Will it now cost him his life?"},
[7461]={"Examine Merry in the Houses of Healing","Examine Faramir in the Houses of Healing","Éowyn is held in the grip of a troubled sleep, but a grey shadow has crept over her features and she is very pale. You have heard whispers of the Black Shadow that comes from the Nazgûl, and it seems to have settled very heavily upon her.\
\
Her shield-arm is broken, but the healers have tended to it with all their skill, and it seems to your eyes that it will heal in time. The state of her sword-arm is more troubling, for it seems that there is no life in it, though the bones are not broken.","Ioreth has never heard of athelas. Could it be she would know it by another name?","Talk to Mithrandir in the Houses of Healing","Mithrandir has come down out of the city to speak with you.","Enter the Houses of Healing with Imrahil and Mithrandir","'If she finds any athelas in the city, she will bring it back here with haste. And if there is none to be found, I will ride to the woods near Lossarnach and bring back the plant myself!\
\
'It is good that you came here, Aragorn. May it not be too late for our friends, and for the others who suffer in the grip of the Black Shadow. If Ioreth runs as quickly as her tongue, she will be back with athelas before the sun moves another step in the sky!'","You ask Ioreth if there might be some athelas to be had in the storerooms.\
\
'We have healing herbs of many varieties, but of course never as many as we might wish, especially not with so many needing our help! It has been some time since a carrier from Lossarnach has come, and our stock of cemenduril liquor is very low. But I am afraid I do not know of any herb by the name of athelas. I can ask the herb-master. He knows the old names.'","You arrive in the Sixth Circle without incident","Examine Éowyn in the Houses of Healing","Ioreth has never heard of athelas. Perhaps she knows it by another name?","Talk to Mithrandir outside the city","Aragorn did not make it to the Houses of Healing in time","You have entered the Houses of Healing at the behest of Mithrandir.","Sneak through the city to the Houses of Healing","Interludio: Un regreso secreto","You greet Mithrandir warmly and ask him how the folk of the city fare in the aftermath of the battle.\
\
'The uninjured are slowly waking from the horrors of the siege, and before long they will return to their daily lives. But many soldiers and townsfolk lie in the Houses of Healing, suffering from the wounds of battle and the greater hurts inflicted by the Nazgûl. Some of the healers remark that if there were a king in Gondor, as of old, these wounds might be healed through his skill.'\
\
You tell Mithrandir that you did not wish to upset the delicate situation in Minas Tirith by entering the city without the invitation of its Steward.\
\
'If you do not go to the Houses of Healing, there might be no Steward by nightfall that could offer you such an invitation, Aragorn! Faramir needs your healing-arts, as do many others. You might save them still if you enter the city in disguise. Avoid Knowing Scholars who might see you for who you are, and the political situation should be unharmed. I cannot command you to do this, but I do request it as your friend, and as a friend of Gondor.'","You tell Ioreth that some folk also know athelas by another name: kingsfoil.\
\
'Kingsfoil? Say you so? My sisters claimed it to be naught but a weed! Now that you mention it, I have noticed that it does give off a sweet smell when its flowers are disturbed. It is somehow a wholesome smell, if you understand what I mean. I did wonder why any king would wish such a plant to be named so, and not one more brightly-coloured or eye-catching.'","Ask Ioreth for kingsfoil","Talk to Imrahil outside the Houses of Healing","Pass through the gates and make your way up through Minas Tirith to the Houses of Healing without being seen by Knowing Scholars who might see through your disguise.","Ioreth might know where you can find some athelas.","You were seen by a Knowing Scholar, upsetting the delicate political situation!","Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth is outside the Houses of Healing.","Ask Ioreth for athelas","You have made it through the city without being identified","You study Faramir's face closely, and note that he is covered in sweat. His forehead glistens, and he burns feverishly. He breathes shallowly, and the rise and fall of his chest is very difficult to detect without close scrutiny.\
\
The son of Denethor seems close to death. If nothing changes, and soon, he will join his father by nightfall.","'Aragorn! I was told you did not wish to enter the city. I am glad you have done so, for Mithrandir claims that in you alone may rest the only hope for recovery of the sick that lie within.\
\
'Let us attend to them at once, and may he prove correct in this belief!'","Mithrandir is in the Houses of Healing.","Athelas might help to heal them, but is there any to be had?","The words of Ioreth compelled Mithrandir to seek for one who might be able to heal those suffering from the Black Shadow.","Éowyn is lying in a bed two rooms to the north of Faramir's room in the Houses of Healing.","Merry is in the north-western room of the Houses of Healing.","Merry suffers troubled dreams. Like Éowyn, he pierced the Lord of the Nazgûl with his weapon and the encounter worked a grievous harm upon him. A grey pall has settled upon his face, and the Black Shadow stifles his breath.","Faramir lies in a bed against the right wall. He does not look well","Avoid Knowing Scholars","You decide to make your way up through the city in secret","Faramir is in the south-eastern sick-room of the Houses of Healing."},
[7462]={"Talk to Gandalf and complete 'Interlude: A Secret Return'","Ioreth is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.","'I bear a message from the healers, seeking any who might be able to provide assistance within the Houses of Healing! Go at once to Ioreth in the High Hall and she will find a use for you. I saw her last by Faramir's bedside.\
\
'If you can help the healers to make Faramir well, you should do what you can! I have heard troubling whispers about Steward Denethor, but I will not repeat them here. At the very least I will tell you that Faramir must recover, or Minas Tirith will be at risk of further grief!'","'We are pulled in so many directions, ${PLAYER}! How can we hope to address the needs of so many wounded? So many suffer in the aftermath of the battle, Faramir not least of all!\
\
'There he lies, and he burns with a fire that consumes him from within! What will we do if he should die? If only Gondor still had a king. Minstrels used to sing of the Kings of Gondor, saying of them that their hands were the hands of healers, and by that trait would they be known. But there has not been a King in Gondor for many years.'","Interludio: Un regreso secreto","'Did you hear the words of Ioreth? She speaks of songs only half-remembered in these modern days, and I do not doubt that she often refers to such tales, but her words on this day have stirred me as if from a stupor!\
\
'The hands of the King are the hands of a healer? Gondor has not had a King for many years, but these are times of change and it could be that one such worthy is indeed close at hand! Ioreth, men may well remember your own words in the days to come!\
\
'You know who I mean, ${PLAYER}! Speak to me with haste and we will fetch him!'","'Faramir burns with a fire that consumes him from within! What will we do if he should die? If only Gondor still had a king. Minstrels used to sing of the Kings of Gondor, saying of them that their hands were the hands of healers, and by that trait would they be known. But there has not been a King in Gondor for many years.'","Talk to Gandalf in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing","Talk to Ioreth in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing","'We must trust in Aragorn now, for time is growing short. If there is any kingsfoil to be found within this city, may it be found while it might still be used to good effect!\
\
'I know that Aragorn did not wish to enter the city before the right time, but without his healer's skill I fear that these wounded might never recover. Now there is some hope, though it be slight.\
\
'Now go and find kingsfoil, wherever it might be found!'","'The healers have sent messages throughout the city, calling for any who might be able to aid the sick and wounded quartered in the Houses of Healing. Go to the ward where Faramir lies, in the High Hall, and Ioreth will set you upon some useful task.'","'The recollections of Ioreth may prove a boon for our suffering friends, ${PLAYER}. I must go at once in search of he who may prove to have the healer's touch!'","The Houses of Healing are full, and the healers are having a difficult time seeing to the needs of the wounded.","Gandalf is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith."},
[7463]={"<rgb=#00FF00>It is recommended, but not required, that you complete The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves, Chapters 1-4 before playing 'Blood of Azog.'</rgb>\
\
'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. This is not the manner of reunion I would have preferred, but I'm afraid it could not be helped.\
\
'Though I have tried to convince him otherwise, Prince Durin blames himself for the setback at the gates of Mount Gundabad. He considers it a defeat, a failure, and perhaps most of all, a rebuke to his worthiness of the name Durin. Even though that is not so, I fear he believes that vengeance might be his only path to redemption in the eyes of the Longbeards.\
\
'Prince Durin has heard many tales of the deeds of his grandfather, but neither he nor even King Thorin know them as I do. In my youth, I learned the cost of vengeance first-hand. I was at Azanulbizar! I know well the price that was paid to see Azog's head set upon a pike!\
\
'It is true that Gorgar and Hrímil await us beyond the gates of Mount Gundabad, but within the Mountain-home, the advantage belongs to them. If we are to win this war and reclaim the sacred mountain, our soldiers must be given the time to tend their wounds and prepare for the battles ahead.\
\
'Let us help Prince Durin to lead the Gabil'akkâ to victory, my friend. That is all I ask.'","Aid Prince Durin with 'Blood of Azog: Fathers and Sons'","Interlude: Blood of Azog","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Vosh Torú, in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.","Glóin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.","King Thorin can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.","Prince Durin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.","Hersegg can be found in Akrâz-zahar at Erebor.","After the escape of Gorgar, son of Bolg, and the sealing of the gates of Mount Gundabad by Hrímil Frost-heart, Prince Durin faces his first true test. As Durin weighs whether it will be vengeance or wisdom that guides his hand, Lord Glóin's thoughts turn to conflicts of old. All too familiar with the triumphs and sorrows of Durin's Folk, Glóin hopes that a lesson in history might temper Prince Durin's desire to bring the War of Three Peaks to an end at all cost.","Aid Hersegg with 'Blood of Azog: The Sixth War'","Aid Hermáth Stormhammer with 'Blood of Azog: At Seventh Light'","Aid King Thorin with 'Blood of Azog: Muster to the Mountain-home'","Aid King Thorin with 'Blood of Azog: Brethren of Past and Present'","Aid Glóin with 'Blood of Azog: A Lesson Hard-learned'","Durin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
After speaking with Hermáth Stormhammer, Durin has decided that the Gabil'akkâ will march on Mount Gundabad in seven days. You should talk to Durin.","Aid King Thorin with 'Blood of Azog: Will of the Stormhammer'","Talk to Durin at Annâk-khurfu","'I can hardly believe how much has changed since you departed Elderlsade. I am told you studied Hermáth's account of the Sixth War, and perhaps I should as well when at last I return to the Lonely Mountain. In the meantime, I am fortunate enough to have the Stormhammer at my side!\
\
'The last blood of Azog still dwells within Mount Gundabad, but when the final test comes in those hallowed halls, we shall be victorious! Neither Gorgar nor Hrímil shall keep us from our prize!\
\
'Were it not for you and Glóin, I... thank you, my friend.'"},
[7464]={"Helchon is somewhere in the Hall of the Huntsman.","Talk to Helchon","You speak, slowly and haltingly at first, but gradually with greater confidence and urgency. You tell the mighty figure of the Huntsman of your concern that the Falcon Clan has wrought some great evil in the caves of Tâl Methedras, and that the shaking in the earth may spell the doom of your friends.\
\
The Huntsman is silent for a long while before speaking.","'You say you have a feeling about this place, Calenglad, but I cannot sense anything! You say you feel a mysterious presence? I feel the chill shadows of the trees and smell old growth, but nothing else.\
\
'Are you sure this is the place of which Daervunn spoke? There is nothing here but trees, corrupted beasts, and we two. I say we leave the trees to the miserable bears, and be done with it!'","Follow the stag deeper into the forest","A majestic stag has appeared in the forest of the Mournshaws.","You and Helchon have come to the Mournshaws in search of answers, but the journey is wearing on the young Ranger.","'I... I do not know what to say, Calenglad. I have never seen such wonders. I do not want to leave, but I know we must. We do not belong in this place, with so much beauty around us.\
\
'Did you learn anything of use from the Huntsman? He seems unreal to me, as if he is only partway in this world of ours... I never would have believed any of this, to hear you tell it, Calenglad, but I have seen it with my own eyes. You must forgive me my doubts.\
\
'This journey has not reassured me, Calenglad. Now I am more worried than ever! If such a mighty figure as the Huntsman can really exist, who knows what terror the Falcon Clan could have unleashed in the caves beneath Tâl Methedras?'","Helchon is exhausted. The frequent attacks by corrupted creatures have drained his desire to proceed.","You have travelled to the Mournshaws following the rumour of a great spirit that might know what shakes the earth in Dunland.","Talk to Helchon in the Hall of the Huntsman","Talk to the mighty figure of the Huntsman","'Calenglad, we have been journeying for hours, fighting the corrupted denizens of this forest, and we are no closer to learning anything! I know Daervunn spoke of seeing a great spirit in these woods, but we have seen no sign of such a lord.\
\
'Whatever beast or magic shakes the stones of Tâl Methedras, we will learn nothing of it in these woods.'","The Huntsman awaits your request, Calenglad.","Slowly approach the majestic stag","The majestic stag is leading you deeper into the forest.","Interludio: El llamado de Calenglad"},
[7465]={"Prestadír has woken you for your turn at watch.","Habla con Halbarad","Halbarad is waiting to speak with you following the attack by the Falcon Clan.","Wake up your brethren before the Falcon Clan attacks!","Habla con Prestadír","'I thought this would happen one of these nights. We may not have much time before the Falcon Clan strikes!\
\
'You three slip down the hill to the side and see if you can approach our attackers from behind.\
\
'Halros! Prestadír! Come with me, and we will see if they can listen to reason.'","'I am sorry to wake you, Halros, but it is time for your watch to begin. These last few hours have been quiet, and it was a struggle at times to keep my eyes open. I will be glad of the sleep.\
\
'There is a good place to watch among the trees just to the west. I will show you.'","'There is no honour to be had by attacking a sleeping foe, Halros, but we should have expected nothing else from the Falcon Clan. Mair learned that tonight, to her sorrow.\
\
'We have not repaid Lheu Brenin and the Falcon Clan for our losses, not by a wide throw, but we have shown them our claws. We are all fortunate you have such alert senses, Halros!\
\
'I am glad you journeyed south with us, for this reason and many others. Look! Dawn breaks. Your vigil for the night is ended! Let us break our fast and see to the coming of the day.'","Interludio: La Guardia de Halros","Did you see something move in the darkness?","Investigate your uneasy feeling","Talk to Halbarad and prepare for the Falcon Clan attack","It is now your turn to keep watch while the rest of the Grey Company sleeps. You will waken Halbarad at the dawn.","Halbarad has instructions for you, and you should receive them quickly! The Falcon Clan attack is imminent!","You need to wake up your comrades before the attack!","That was a Falcon Clan scout! The camp is about to be attacked!","Prestadír has woken you for your turn at the watch. You have five hours to spend until the dawn.","Stand watch until dawn"},
[7466]={"Habla con el Frontero Primstone","Bounder Primstone is in the Greenfields, waiting for you to walk with him to Oatbarton.","Bounder Primstone is outside Oatbarton.","Talk to Bill Ferny outside Oatbarton","'Oh my, where has the time gone? Already the sun is beginning to set. Let us take a short rest and then we will walk the rest of the way to Oatbarton. What do you say, Halros?'","Interludio: La Guardia de Halros","You have agreed to walk with Bounder Primstone on his rounds to Oatbarton today.","Bill Ferny is on the outskirts of Oatbarton, and if you know him, the Man is up to no good.","'You have my thanks for sending him away, Halros. I'm glad you were here. He was up to no good, you mark my words.\
\
'We fought some wolves tonight, but I think maybe not every wolf we encountered wore fur. That one's teeth might prove sharpest yet.\
\
'We should see about finding a place to stay for tonight, before we head back to the Greenfields on the morrow. Let us find an accomodating burrow, with a laden table full of supper, if we can!'","It is getting late, and you are not yet at Oatbarton. Bounder Primstone wants to take a short rest.","You have arrived at the outskirts of Oatbarton with Bounder Primstone.","'You don't scare me, Ranger. I've seen plenty of your type 'round Bree-way, and it seems to me you bleed just like everybody else. Maybe easier.'\
\
Ferny laughs an unpleasant laugh.\
\
'I'm meeting a friend here, but I can see you're just dying to stick your nose into my business, so I'll move along. I'll be sure to tell my friend who it was what caused this inconvenience. You can count on that, Ranger.'","'Good afternoon to you, Halros! It is good to see you again. I do enjoy the company. The walk to Oatbarton is quite a long one, but it goes more quickly with company.\
\
'I am always pleased when you join me for walking my rounds. I have not met very many of the Big Folk, but of those few you are as pleasant and kind a fellow as I could hope to meet. You are quite all right in my book, Halros.\
\
'You will forgive me, as you usually do, if I share some of the news of the day? That is a relief. There is so much going on in the Shire, and keeping it all straight helps to clean the cobwebs out of my head. Relaying some of it to you serves as mental exercise of the highest order!'","'Is that the sound of wolves? Sometimes they come down into the Shire, but it does not happen very often. If they do come upon us, you can stand behind me, Halros. Wolves can be frightening, but I am a Bounder and have been trained to deal with the creatures.\
\
'I am sorry, but the sandwiches will have to wait.'","Talk to Bounder Primstone outside Oatbarton","Talk to Bounder Primstone in the Greenfields","'Look up ahead. Is that one of the Big Folk? You are an exception, Halros. Usually they do not trouble to come into the Shire, and we are pleased to not be troubled by them!\
\
'I suppose we should see what he wants, Halros.'","You have walked with Bounder Primstone about halfway to Oatbarton, but you have heard the sound of wolves on the wind."},
[7467]={"The Ents have smashed open the gate to Isengard, and now you should proceed into the ring.","'What has happened here? You... you have worked some mischief...'\
\
The little man's eyes dart left and right, taking in as much of the devastation as he can.\
\
'What has happened to Saruman? I... bore messages for him from the King, but it seems they are no longer necessary...'\
\
He turns to go, but you stop him. It is plain he served the Wizard and was complicit in his designs. They deserve each other's company.","Interludio: Última Marcha de los Ents","Saruman's servant has gone to join his master in the tower.","Saruman's servant has gone to join his master in the tower","Talk to Quickbeam in front of the gate to Isengard","Pass through the ruined gate of Isengard and defeat Saruman's forces","The Ents have diverted the river and flooded the Ring of Isengard. Their purpose: to wash it clean of Saruman's filth.","'That was a rousing march, Treebeard! We have come to the ring of Isengard sooner than I thought we would, and our business with the Wizard waits before us!'\
\
Quickbeam peers at the hobbits clinging to your upper branches.\
\
'Hold on, little ones! Keep a good grip, and do not fall!'","Quickbeam must not be defeated","You have come to the ring of Isengard with as many of the Ents that responded to your call. The time has come to remind Saruman of what he has forgotten!","Talk to Quickbeam outside the ring of Isengard","Survey your handiwork and greet the newcomer","The Ents have been driven mad by the fires of Saruman! His evil must be washed away!","The Ents have torn down the gate that gives entrance to the Ring of Isengard.","Saruman has fought back with flame and smoke!","The Ents have come to Isengard to remind Saruman of the danger he has risked with his plans.","'I will gather the rest of our people, Fangorn, while you press forward through the main gate into Isengard! I will meet up with you beyond the gate!'","Quickbeam has fallen!"},
[7468]={"Treebeard is near the base of Orthanc, and has agreed to finish the story begun by Merry.","Treebeard is by the base of Orthanc.","Treebeard has agreed to finish the story begun by Merry, telling you of the last march of the Ents.","Talk to Treebeard and listen to his tale","Interludio: Última Marcha de los Ents","'Are you ready to hear the tale, little one? Hoom, boom, hrum.'","Talk to Treebeard by the base of Orthanc","'The young hobbits told you of the moot, but did not tell you of our arrival here? You wish to hear that tale?'\
\
Treebeard seems to give it some thought... and some thought... and some more thought. Eventually his eyes focus on you again.\
\
'Ents do not often get asked to tell stories, little one. But I will see what I can do... hoom, hrum, hoom. I hope you have enough time to listen.'","'That is the tale, little one. I have not seen Saruman since Gríma Wormtongue came to the tower. His schemes may be at an end; the water seems to have dampened his spirits.\
\
'Oh! Oh, that is very good! Hoom, hrum, boom! Dampened his spirits!\
\
'I have enjoyed telling you the tale, little ${RACE}. I hope you will remember the Ents. It seems to me that Saruman wishes he remembered us sooner. I am glad he did not.'"},
[7469]={"Elrohir is waiting to speak with you on the road up the hill in Tûr Morva.","Radanir is among the buildings atop the hill in Tûr Morva.\
\
Radanir has returned from his expedition in the mountains.","Talk to Elrohir on the road through Tûr Morva","Talk to Calenglad by the entrance to the ruins atop the hill","Await the gathering of the Dúnedain atop the hill in Tûr Morva","Interludio: Muchas preocupaciones","'This is the situation in which we find ourselves, Halbarad? The Falcon Clan harries us from the mountains and caves into which they fled. The earth shakes and rumbles more and more with each passing day. Our numbers diminish the further south we travel, brothers and friends lost to death or to urgent need in distant lands.\
\
'You are our leader. What road or roads do we take from here? How then does the Grey Company proceed?'\
\
Prestadír looks at you expectantly, and you know that you must dispatch some members of your group to deal with each of these situations. For now, you must think upon how best to deal with the various roads ahead.","Talk to Golodir up the hill in Tûr Morva","'My brother returned from his sojourn in the mountains, and he says a small group of warriors makes their way hither. \\qMore of the Falcon Clan?\\q I asked him, but he was not certain. He has gone back with Radanir to cut them off before they arrive.'\
\
Elrohir pauses, and you can tell he is struggling to find the right words. Soon he continues.\
\
'We have been through much, my friend, and will certainly see more danger before we find Aragorn. But I feel I must ask: why do we linger in Tâl Methedras? I understand that much hurt was done to us here, and the desire to avenge our fallen is great, but delay may prove as deadly.'","'You have stumbled into the middle of a surprise attack, Halbarad! Are you willing to fight alongside me?'\
\
Radanir laughs.\
\
'Oh, you are on the right side of the ambush, this time. We are doing the ambushing! Elladan and I have lured a small group of the Falcon Clan back here. They think they have us on the run, but they are about to be surprised! Are you ready?'","Talk to Radanir in Tûr Morva, south of Calenglad","Saeradan is north-east of Elrohir, in Tûr Morva. Golodir is up the hill in Tûr Morva. Calenglad is by the entrance to the ruins.\
\
Elrohir is pleased that you have decided to leave Tâl Methedras at last and thinks the others will be similarly pleased.","The Rangers have gathered atop the hill in Tûr Morva.\
\
You have helped Radanir fight off a small group of the Falcon Clan, and should now give the Grey Company some of the direction they seek by speaking with Prestadír.","The time has come to decide what each member of the Grey Company should do in the coming days.","'The rumbling in the earth is getting worse, Halbarad. I do not like it.'\
\
Saeradan listens as you explain that it is time for the Grey Company to leave Tâl Methedras.\
\
'That is wise. I have already decided it was time to leave, and I wanted to see if you agreed with me. I wish to leave Tâl Methedras, but I wish to travel north... not south.'\
\
Saeradan sees your puzzled expression and hurries to explain.\
\
'Many of our brothers have fallen on this road, and it grieves me to think they must be laid to rest in these hostile southern lands. They are Dúnedain! They should be brought back to the northern lands they held dear. I propose to bring their bodies by waggon back to their homes.'","Talk to Saeradan in Tûr Morva","Talk to Prestadír atop the hill in Tûr Morva","Halbarad has led the Grey Company through many dangers already on its journey to aid Aragorn, but many treacherous miles still lie ahead.","'Corunir and I have been collecting the weapons the Falcon Clan left behind when we drove them into the caves. This accursed shaking in the earth is making it more difficult than it need be.'\
\
Golodir listens as you explain your decision for the Grey Company to continue on its road, and his face becomes a thundercloud.\
\
'That is an impossibility, Halbarad! We cannot leave yet! Lheu Brenin still lives, and his cronies! You cannot have forgotten the wounds he gave us, and the lives his treachery cost. We must have our vengeance upon him before we go!'","'Did you feel those rumblings in the earth, Halbarad? They are getting worse. It almost sounds as if, well...'\
\
Calenglad trails off, embarrassed. You prompt him to continue, but his tone remains sheepish.\
\
'Well, it sounds as if a great beast was running beneath the earth, shaking the ground with the fury of its passage. Could such a creature be?\
\
'You may think such musings are the province of children's tales, but I have seen many strange and wondrous things in my life, Halbarad, and learning of these wonders keeps me putting one foot before the other. If there is such a beast, we must know if it poses a threat to our people and the good people of Dunland. Mustn't we?'"},
[7470]={"That should be enough. Yes, precious, time to slip away...","'No, precious, don't go this way! We mustn't hurt the nice Master!\
\
'We swore, precious! We swore to serve the nice Master! Do not try to hurt him! Must not, gollum! Gollum!'","Sméagol is back, the coward","Climb the final stair with the hobbitses","We have to find Her, and tell her what we have brought with us!","Sneak to the east, towards the tower, precious","'Sam and I need to rest from the climb before we move on to this tunnel you mentioned, Sméagol. I am exhausted, and I do not want us to pass beneath that tower without recovering whatever strength we may.\
\
'You should <rgb=#00FF00>lie down</rgb> and get some sleep as well, Sméagol. We will all need our rest for what lies ahead, I imagine.'","'We shouldn't leave the hobbitses, gollum, gollum! They trusts us, they do, and we swore on the Precious! Nice master trusts Sméagol, yes, he's a friend to us, a good friend!\
\
'We swore to serve the Master of the Precious!'","She will help us get the Precious, yes she will, gollum, gollum!","The nice Master and the other hobbit need to rest.","Wait until the hobbitses are deep in conversation","The nice master is near the top of the Winding Stair, looking out upon the dead city below.","You have business ahead. Leave the hobbitses behind and go to the east, beneath the tower.","Talk to Sméagol and tell him this will retrieve the Precious","Leave us alone, Sméagol! This is the only way, gollum!","The nice master has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>lie down</rgb>, at least for a little while.","Sleep, precious... yes, for a little while","Find Her, precious, and tell Her what we have brought!","Talk to nice Master","We have to tell Her what we have brought. She will be so pleased, gollum, gollum!","Wait for the hobbitses to become absorbed in their conversation.","She won't want the Precious, though, no indeed, gollum!","Enter the tunnel, gollum, gollum!","Interludio: Ningún otro camino","Weak! Do not listen to him, gollum, gollum!","Sméagol is back, and he wants to keep us from the Precious! Only we know what we must do, gollum!","What do you want, precious? Leave me alone!","There is one more stair to climb before the hobbitses can put the Winding Stair behind them.\
\
And then?","Once we have the Precious, we will be the Master!","The tunnel lies ahead. You need to go there, precious, and make certain all is ready!","'Please don't go inside the tunnel, gollum, gollum! We can't bring the hobbitses to Her! She'll eat them, yes, not just the fat one but the Master too, and Sméagol can't do that to them! No, precious, no! Don't go to Her!'","'Thank you for bringing us this far, Sméagol. I know it cannot have been easy for you to come this way again, or to creep so near to the city below, but you have done right by your promise.\
\
'Just a little further, you said? I am ready to put these stairs behind us, and then we will need to rest, if we can. I am so very tired, and Sam may not say it but he must be as well.'","Talk to Sméagol outside the tunnel","Sméagol is here. What does he want? Why is he in my way, gollum, gollum?","You have led the good master and his protector into the mountains, as you were asked. The Straight Stair and the Winding Stair are behind, and the Tunnel lies ahead.","Sneak east to the tunnel, precious","Talk to Sméagol, precious","Sneak to the east, towards the tunnel, gollum","<rgb=#00FF00>Lie down</rgb> and get some sleep, as the nice Master requested","Now what was the right way, gollum, gollum?","Sméagol is back. He doesn't have the nerve to get the Precious!"},
[7471]={"Britou stands before you, a figure of malice that has caused you grief in the recent past. You cannot forgive him, but he appears to offer you no immediate threat.","Talk to Britou","Candaith was dear to you, and you still keenly feel the pain of his loss. He often came to visit your cabin on the Bree-fields, and many were the nights the two of you spent in quiet conversation about the events of the day. The conversations became more serious and more grim as the shadows deepened in Middle-earth, but your favourites will always be those that were full of smiles and laughter.\
\
'We came back for you, my brother. We should not have left you here for even one day. Forgive me, Candaith.'\
\
Your words hang in the still air.","Pay your respects to your kinsmen who fell along the Forsaken Road (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Shades of the oath-breakers you encountered on the Forsaken Road have appeared all around you! What evil do they pose to you now?","You gaze upon the fallen form of Hodhon, and think of the delight upon his face each time he recovered a curious artifact from the ruins of Annúminas. Many were the nights you spent warming yourself by the fire while Calenglad explained to Hodhon the historical significance of the artifact he had found, and the memory brings a smile to your face even now.\
\
This grim road should not be his tomb. You and Radanir will see to it that he rests at last along the shores of Nenuial that he so loved.","The oathbreakers fade from your sight, returning to the Mountain from which they fled.","Talk to Radanir along the Forsaken Road, where Candaith fell","Radanir has sensed something is wrong, and he is standing by the stopped waggon.","You and Radanir have arranged the use of a waggon to bring your fallen brothers back to their homes in the north.","'I am ready for us to carry our fallen brothers outside, Saeradan. Let us not delay. They have remained in this terrible place for too long already.'","Linnor lived in service to the Grey Company and fell upon the Forsaken Road","'I offer you no words of contrition, Dúnadan. If you seek out Men such as we are, you deserve any ill that befalls you. Learn from the lesson, and put your trust in those who deserve it.\
\
'We abandoned the Mountain, thinking to escape the chain of our suffering, but there was no escape from it. There was no end to our days, no relief from the night. Only fools stumbled upon us, and those paid with their lives. If you seek the Dead, only death awaits you.\
\
'But my people learned from yours that our curse may yet be lifted. If an heir of Isildur's lives still, as your kin pretended, the glimmer of that hope may be rekindled. We love you not, but we will not slay you this night. We return to the Mountain. We will not come this way again.'","'This place holds mainly painful memories, Saeradan. Let us find the bodies of our fallen kinsmen and leave as quickly as we are able.'","You should find the bodies of your fallen friends and pay your respects, and Radanir will begin carrying them out of the Forsaken Road.","You have honoured your kinsmen, and should now speak with Radanir along the Forsaken Road.","'I did not think to encounter those dead men again, Saeradan. Many of our friends and brothers were slain at their hands. How many went beneath the earth along the Forsaken Road, and did not return into the daylight? Good men, all.'\
\
Radanir pauses, and you can read his thoughts on his face, as plain as day even in the gloom of night.\
\
'The oath-breakers have abandoned the Forsaken Road, Saeradan. Now is the time for us to return there and rescue the bodies we were forced to leave behind. We must bring them back above-ground and to the waggon of our fallen. We must do this at once! Let us go, and quickly!'","Allow the oathbreakers to pass","Calithil lived in service to the Grey Company and fell upon the Forsaken Road","'I am sorry I have made us stop, Saeradan, but something is not right. Do you feel it? I feel a chill in my very bones. I have not felt such a dread since... I do not wish to say.'\
\
Radanir shudders.\
\
'We have driven this waggon with our fallen brothers this far already, and we have much farther to go yet... but I want to set my mind at ease before we proceed. Do you agree, Saeradan? Then walk with me for a short way. We will not go far.'","Talk to Radanir along the Forsaken Road","Candaith lived in service to the Grey Company and fell upon the Forsaken Road","Linnor was well-known to you, for he lived on the Bree-fields and often visited your cabin to share a meal and the news. He was generally well-regarded by Man and Bree-hobbit alike, and it was Linnor who helped Burle Pierson construct the frame for his farm-house south of Bree-town.\
\
Linnor did not range as far afield as many of your kin, and his decision to join the Grey Company was not an easy one. You hope he knows, somehow, that his service was not for nothing. You and Radanir will make sure he is laid to rest among the comfortable hills of his home.","Survive your second encounter with the oath-breakers","Radanir has had an idea, and wants to tell it to you.","Talk to Radanir","Interludio: Un viaje más","Hodhon lived in service to the Grey Company and fell upon the Forsaken Road","Radanir is beneath the earth along the Forsaken Road.","Calithil kept to himself, and in that way he was much like Aragorn your chieftain. He strode often in the Trollshaws 'neath the moon, and it was he who introduced Radanir to Elweleth at Thorenhad. He used to jest that he did it only to make things difficult for Radanir.\
\
He will rest more easily beneath the trees, perhaps a stone's throw from the sound of Loudwater.","Himeldir lived in service to the Grey Company and fell upon the Forsaken Road","You gaze upon Himeldir's face with deep sorrow, for you remember how much he argued against coming to the Forsaken Road. He believed the words of Ergothorn should not be trusted, and thought seeking beneath the earth for the honourless ones to be a foolish journey.\
\
He spoke of it to you in private, and shared his concerns with Candaith, but in the end he agreed to walk the Forsaken Road. From that point onward you heard no complaint from him, and he descended bravely.\
\
'I am sorry, Himeldir,' you whisper to his fallen form. 'Be at peace, my kinsman. We will not leave you here.'","Talk to Radanir by the stopped waggon"},
[7473]={"Talk to Corunir outside the prison-caves... again","You have dropped into the pit at the bottom of the prison-caves, where members of the Falcon Clan who displeased Lheu Brenin have been abandoned.","The entrance to the prison-caves of Tûr Morva is to the north-east.","Drop into the pit at the bottom of the prison-caves","You have survived your encounter with the Beast in the Pit, and should see how Corunir is doing.","For the first time in a long time, your vengeance is forgotten","Corunir is waiting before the entrance to the prison-caves. He must know your mind.","Golodir can no longer resist the lure of vengeance, and has decided to return to the prison-caves of Tûr Morva in search of Lheu Brenin, chieftain of the Falcon Clan.","Talk to Wenda","'I know you are angry, my friend, but returning to the prison-caves by yourself is simply throwing away your life!\
\
'I am angry too, Golodir! Lheu Brenin cost us much, and I have not forgotten his treachery. Many good men lost their lives when he sided with the Wizard, friends of us both, and if the leader of the Falcon Clan had his way none of us would have survived.'\
\
Corunir sighs.","'Age has not slowed you down at all, Golodir! I am lucky you were here to take the brunt of the creature's attacks!\
\
'Do not laugh at me for this, friend, but I feel some remorse for slaying such a mighty creature. I know it sought to devour us, but I cannot help think it was a captive here as well. Lheu Brenin kept it in this pit, and he made use of its appetite. Mayhap we did it a courtesy by freeing it of its confines?\
\
'If you will comfort Wenda and ease her fright, I will call up to Maelona. She will find us a rope and we can climb out of this pit.'","Return to the entrance of the prison-caves","Talk to Corunir inside the prison-caves","Wenda is frightened, but it has been a long time since you were adept with comforting words.","Corunir refuses to let you enter the prison-caves in search of Lheu Brenin.","Corunir is waiting by the entrance to the prison-caves","Something lives in the bottom of the pit where Lheu Brenin throws his captives.","'You have to believe me, Ranger! Many of us spoke against Lheu Brenin, and he repaid us for our dissent with death and violence! He cast those who still remained into this pit before he left.\
\
'You must save them!'","Interludio: Foso del Halcón","Maelona has requested your help deep within the prison-caves.","A terrible smell of rot fills the pit","'You have to believe me, Ranger. I spoke against Lheu Brenin's decision, and many good folk did the same. Your people were betrayed by Lheu Brenin, but so were many of my own! He believed the Wizard's lies, and thought to raise the Falcon to heights undreamed-of... but in so doing he gave the Falcon a death-blow. The symbol of my clan is now little better than that of the Orcs.'\
\
Maelona spits.\
\
'But there is no time! Lheu Brenin has taken those loyal to him and crossed over the mountains. If you are seeking to have vengeance upon him, you are too late. He will be in the land of the horse-lords by now.'","You try to ease Wenda's fears with comforting words, but it has been a long time since such words came easy to you, and your face reddens with each stumbling syllable.\
\
'You are kind... Ranger.... Thank you...'\
\
Wenda tests her leg, and winces gingerly.\
\
'My arms... are fine. But I will need... some help with the rope...'\
\
While Corunir and Maelona arrange for getting everyone out of the pit, you listen as Wenda haltingly tells you how she learned the craft of tree-climbing when she was young.\
\
'My father will be shamed in the world of spirits if I fall from the rope... and I will blame you, Ranger!'\
\
You swear that she will not fall, and that her father will be proud of her ascent... but if she does fall, she should make sure to fall on Corunir, who is relatively plump, for a Ranger.\
\
She laughs at that, and you laugh with her.","Lheu Brenin has left Dunland and passed into Rohan with those loyal to him, but before he left he cast dissenting members of the Falcon Clan into the Pit of the Falcon at the bottom of the prison-caves.","Talk to Maelona in the prison-caves","Talk to Corunir outside the prison-caves","'I thought you might come here sooner or later, Golodir. I know what you want to do, and I am here to keep you from doing something rash!'\
\
Corunir shrugs his shoulders, and looks up at you with a stern expression on his face.\
\
'Lheu Brenin has so many at his command. It would be foolish for you to return to the caves in search of him. We should do as Halbarad wishes, and leave the leader of the Falcon Clan be. He wronged us, but we cannot do anything about that now.'","'Are you... here to help us? I hurt... my leg in the fall...'\
\
The girl winces with pain, and you are stricken suddenly by the memory of Lorniel lying before the gates of Carn Dûm.\
\
'My name... Wenda... we have to...'\
\
Wenda falls silent, exhausted by the effort, but her darting eyes flicker to the tunnel leaving the chamber and you can see the fear in them.","'I think she is telling the truth, Golodir. If Lheu Brenin cast some of his own people into this pit, and left them to die, I think they must surely help us. We cannot leave them there!'","Corunir has decided to accompany you into the prison-caves in search of Lheu Brenin.","'Someone is just ahead, Golodir! A woman, from the sound, and she may be in trouble. She is the first living creature we have seen in all these caves today.\
\
'We should be cautious.'","Defeat the Beast in the Pit","Talk to Corunir in the pit"},
[7474]={"Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","'Tell me your name, stranger. There is much I do not know, and I hope you will have the answers I seek.\
\
'Shreds of fog cling still to my waking mind. The sleep I endured has not yet freed me from its grasp. The song of the Maiden was a balm for my restless thoughts, a soothing lullaby borne out of love, but that sleep seems now to me a prison, and I want it not! What I desire is recompense for my hurts, but I cannot tell where to aim any such vengeance!\
\
'I remember little from the life I had. Fragments of memory drift like wisps of cloud before my eyes, and are gone. I swore an oath, ${PLAYER}, I remember that. I bore a token, a great weapon of the Enemy, and I vowed to bring it to Rivendell, where it could be protected by the Elves of that hidden haven. I failed in that task, to my shame, for we were set upon by Orcs, and...'\
\
The shade pauses. He lifts his head and looks at you with haunted eyes.\
\
'I was betrayed, ${PLAYER}. The ambush was carried out by Orcs, but they were given succor by one of my own! I cannot see the face of my betrayer, but I feel it with certainty that my company was not waylaid by mistake or misfortune. We were betrayed!\
\
'As the Maiden's enchanted slumber fades, perhaps my memories will return to me. That is my fervent hope. I must know what happened, ${PLAYER}. I must know who caused my downfall and the deaths of my men and my sons. You must help me discover the truth, where it lies and wherever it leads!'","Help Gandalf with 'Shades in the Swamp: The Wanderer Sought'","Talk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús","Help Grimbeorn with 'Shades in the Swamp: Ghostly Figures'","Talk to the Shade of Isildur","'This adventure has given me much to ponder, ${PLAYER}! It is a wonder to me that Elendil's son remains bound to the Gladden Fields where he fell, though he had been hidden from our sight for so long by the arts of Gultháva, Maid of the Gladden. Let it not be forgotten that he was hidden too from the searching of our enemies. She may not deserve our thanks, but not all that she worked here can be called evil.\
\
'I believe it was the shade of Isildur that Marhairu Winter-hair followed so long ago; I think too that the song of Gultháva is responsible for the Northman's year-long disappearance. Isildur intended to do no harm; it is only my conjecture, but perhaps Isildur convinced the Maiden to release Marhairu? I cannot say with certainty, but it possesses the ring of truth.\
\
'The shade of Isildur spoke of an oath he swore? It must be that vow that keeps him bound here beyond the span of his life, and I would learn more of it. It seems clear to me that there are two shades at work in the Gladden Fields, and unless I miss my mark I deem they are related. Can it be that this second shade, called by the Woodmen Vagári the Wanderer, might have sworn an oath of similar power? My heart tells me that Vagári has some connexion to the betrayal of Isildur, but what it might be I cannot say. \
\
'There are so many questions, ${PLAYER}. As the Maiden's sorcery fades and his memory returns to him, the shade of Isildur may have much to tell us. Once I told you of the Disaster that befell Isildur and his men, as it was understood by the Wise. But now it seems there is more to the tale than we knew! Remain at the ready, my friend. I feel we are nearer than ever to knowing what befell the High King of Gondor following the defeat of Sauron.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>This story concludes in future chapters of The Black Book of Mordor!</rgb>","Help Gultháva with 'Shades in the Swamp: The Maiden of Gladden'","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús.","'Gandalf speaks of a darkness that has settled upon the Vales of Anduin? I have felt it too, but the lands of my people will not be threatened as soon as will others. My scouts report seeing strange lights among the foetid pools of the Gladden Fields, and some have heard a woman's song keening on the still air. It has always been a strange place, home to shades and spirits, but of late these reports have become more frequent.\
\
'Has something changed? I cannot say, and will not. But I will face it with tooth and claw, if I must. That has always been my way!'","'As the Maiden's enchanted slumber fades, perhaps my memories will return to me. That is my fervent hope. I must know what happened, ${PLAYER}. I must know who caused my downfall and the deaths of my men. You must help me discover the truth, where it lies and wherever it leads!'","Help Gultháva with 'Shades in the Swamp: Only Half-Remembered'","Gultháva, the Maid of the Gladden, is by the rocky path that leads into the Gladdenmere.","Gultháva, the Maid of the Gladden, is by the ruins of Kidzul-kâlah along the path that runs through Gladdenmere.","Grimbeorn is outside the Beorninghús.","Eurik's son Badwila is in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields.","'Speak with Grimbeorn and learn if there is aught he requires, ${PLAYER}. I feel a darkness settling upon the vales, and the master of the Beorninghús may know more of it. At any rate he will welcome any attempt to combat it and make safe his land and that of his neighbours.'","Interlude: Shades in the Swamp","<rgb=#00FF00>It is recommended, but not required, that you complete The Black Book of Mordor, Chapters 1-10 before playing 'Shades in the Swamp.'</rgb>\
\
'A darkness has settled upon the Vales of Anduin, ${PLAYER}. Can you not feel it? The Beornings and the Woodmen have made homes for themselves among the hills and the trees; they are not strangers to the press of the shadow, but of late it has become deeper.\
\
'Elrond's household will stay for a time at the Beorninghús before continuing on to Gondor for the wedding of his daughter Arwen. While they remain in the Vales of Anduin they will rely upon the hospitality of Grimbeorn, Lord of the Beornings. Speak with Grimbeorn and learn if he has noticed anything untoward among the vales. I doubt not that he will welcome any attempt to make safe his land and that of his neighbours.'","The shade of Isildur waits on Tol Send, lost within his memories.","Darkness has fallen upon the Gladden Fields, disturbing the sleep of the shades that have long haunted the area. Gandalf has given you two purposes: to investigate the cause of this disorder, and to preserve the safety of the Woodmen who live nearby.","Help Badwila with 'Shades in the Swamp: Vagári the Wanderer'"},
[7475]={"Tip over the slop bucket","Survive the consequences of your defiance","'You're mine again today, little Ranger. And this time you will do as I say, won't you? You remember what happened the last time you refused to do your chores, don't you? Spent some time in the dungeons learning the meaning of pain, you did.\
\
'So this time will be different! Scoop some slop from that bucket and serve it to the boys!'","Gun Ain has come to the kitchens underneath Isengard to bring you before Saruman.","Talk to Gun Ain in the kitchens below Isengard","Tip over the other slop bucket","Lothrandir of the Dúnedain still stands strong in the dungeons beneath Isengard, resisting the torments of his captors.","Keep Saruman from dominating your mind","'Gun Ain, stop him!' the Wizard screams!","Barkh is not pleased with you","You have showed your defiance yet again, and the Uruks are not pleased!","Barkh wants you to scoop some slop, but you have a better idea","You have come with Gun Ain to the tower of Orthanc, there to speak with Saruman.","Barkh is not pleased with your defiance.","Interludio: Fuerza de voluntad","'The Wizard wants to see you, Ranger. This could be your last day of life, and my last day without a name!\
\
'What a fortunate day this is, if that be so! Your freedom from this life would be my release from shame. Both of us would rejoice, would we not?'","Barkh wants you to serve some slop to the hungry uruks, but you have a better idea.","Barkh has asked you one more time to comply with his orders.","Talk to Barkh and receive your orders","Talk to Gun Ain atop Orthanc","'We are here. Will the Wizard share his mind with his poor servant and his unworthy captive?'","You have been told to report to Barkh in the kitchens for the day's orders.","You have been brought before the Wizard Saruman."},
[7476]={"Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Gléowine has offered to tell you the tale of Háma's heroic last stand before the gates of the Hornburg.","'Do not forget Háma. I know that Théoden King will not. He served the King faithfully for many years, even with his death.'","'Listen well to the tale of Háma, who fell before the Hornburg, and gave Théoden a chance to attain his victory.'","'I know what this victory cost us, ${PLAYER}: many good men, children of Rohan all. They fought to defend their people, and I will remember their valiant deeds.\
\
'But one loss will loom more large in my mind than the rest, for Háma, son of Léoferth, was more than the doorward of my hall. He served me faithfully for many years, but he did not do so blindly. When I succumbed to the whisperings of Gríma Wormtongue, and only Gandalf could restore me to my senses, it was Háma that weighed the Wizard's wish against my own command. And though he was sworn to uphold my word, Háma was a true man of Rohan and made the judgement he deemed necessary. It was disobedience, but in service of the kingdom, and I both forgive and am proud of him.\
\
'He gave his life before the Hornburg, and without his sacrifice we could not have had victory this day. I will see to it that Háma will not be forgotten.'","Interludio: El Portero","Talk to Gléowine on the field of victory","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Théoden is on the field of victory, before the walls at Helm's Deep.","'This day brings a new dawn for Rohan, but not without cost, ${PLAYER}. Many friends and kinsmen came to their ends during the long night on the wall, and it is the minstrel's sad duty to remember their names and their tales.\
\
'Háma, the doorward of Théoden, fell before the Hornburg. Without his valiant efforts, the gate would surely have been breached, and the King slain before he could ride to victory. I will tell you the tale of Háma's heroic stand, if you will hear it.'","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
You have heard his tale of Háma, and should speak now to Gléowine.","'And so passed Háma, the doorward of Théoden. Without him the gate, and perhaps the kingdom itself, would now be broken. Do not forget him. I know that Théoden King will not. He served the King faithfully for many years, even with his death.'","Gléowine is preparing a song mourning Háma, the doorward of Théoden, who fell before the Hornburg.","Talk to Gléowine on the field of victory, and complete 'Interlude: The Doorward'","Talk to Théoden on the field of victory"},
[7478]={"'Gracias, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}.'","Talk to Corudan at the Harbour Warden's tower","Interlude: The Ghost Returns","Corudan has returned after months away, and he desires to catch up with lost friends.","Talk to Corudan and go with him on one more journey","Corudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.","'In the space before your adventures continue, my friend, I would ask to take one more journey with you.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'Your mission has concluded, ${PLAYER}, and I am pleased it has ended happily! Now that it has, I can confess to you something.\
\
'The physical hurt of the wound I suffered outside Helm's Deep pained me greatly, even as it would in time be healed by Leafshade's ministrations. But one pain remained even afterward: the pain of loss, of not knowing what befell my friends. As my body recovered, my heart dwelled on the uncertainty of what might be happening even then to you, and to Gléowine, and to Horn, and to Nona.\
\
'Now that Thorongil of Pinnath Gelin has been rescued from the Kindred of the Coins... will you take one last journey with me, ${PLAYER}?'"},
[7479]={"'Gracias, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}.'","Talk to Corudan at the Harbour Warden's tower","Interlude: The Ghost Returns","Corudan has returned after months away, and he desires to catch up with lost friends.","Corudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.","Talk to Corudan and go with him to see a lost friend","'Your mission has concluded, ${PLAYER}, and I am pleased it has ended happily! Now that it has, I can confess to you something.\
\
'The physical hurt of the wound I suffered outside Helm's Deep pained me greatly, even as it would in time be healed by Leafshade's ministrations. But one pain remained even afterward: the pain of loss, of not knowing what befell my friends. As my body recovered, my heart dwelled on the uncertainty of what might be happening even then to you, and to Gléowine, and to Horn, and to Nona. I sorrow now to know that Horn perished on the Pelennor Fields... but other of our friends survive, and my heart goes out to them.\
\
'Now that Thorongil of Pinnath Gelin has been rescued from the Kindred of the Coins... will you take one last journey with me, ${PLAYER}?'","'In the space before your adventures continue, my friend, I would ask to take one more journey with you.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>"},
[7480]={"'Pip and I went to Quickbeam's house after that, but my hunger has quite gotten the best of me and I have lost the mood for story-telling. Perhaps I will tell you of the last march of the Ents after I have eaten. But that is enough for now, I think. Quite a tale, was it not?'","Pippin looks at you amiably, but says nothing.","Merry's stomach grumbles, and he smiles at you apologetically","Merry is outside the gate of Isengard.","'It is quite a long story, but I will tell it to you if you will listen! These are not the most comfortable surroundings for a bit of story-telling, but I will do the very best I can.'","Talk to Merry outside the gate of Isengard","Merry is outside the gate of Isengard.\
\
Merry has agreed to tell you the story of how he and Pippin met Treebeard the Ent.","Talk to Merry and hear the story of how he met Treebeard","Pippin smokes contentedly, and says nothing.","'Pip and I met Treebeard after we escaped from the Orcs. He is an Ent, you know, a shepherd of the forests. I can tell you how we met him, if you like.'","Merry has agreed to tell you the story of how he and Pippin met Treebeard.","Interludio: La Asamblea"},
[7481]={"Talk to Pippin on the way to Derndingle","Talk to Pippin and tell him your house is near","Wait for your new hobbit-friends to finish drinking the Ent-draught","You should pick up two bowls for your hobbit friends and one for yourself.","One of your new hobbit friends, Pippin, wants to speak with you.","You have called a moot of your people to decide what is to be done concerning Saruman.","Merry wishes to speak with you about something.","Baldbark needs to be convinced.","Talk to Merry in Wellinghall","Interludio: La Asamblea","'Are you certain this is the right place, Treebeard? I don't see a house anywhere.'","One of the curious creatures wishes to speak with you. How peculiar.","Show your new hobbit friends the way to your home","'Greetings to you, my friend from long ago, when the forest was young and we were not full-grown. Many seasons have turned since last we spoke together in the light of either sun or moon. It is many Ent-strides from my home. Why have you called me to this place?'\
\
You greet Baldbark and reminisce about conversations shared and absent friends. Eventually you speak of Saruman.\
\
'I have been made aware of the Wizard's crimes. He worked great evil in the reaches of the forest near my own home. I agree that something must be done. What will the others say of this?'\
\
You thank Baldbark for his supportive words, and wish him well in the debate to come.","'You Ents certainly do take a long time to make up your minds, Treebeard! I feel certain we could have decided this matter six or seven times over if we were still in the Shire!'\
\
Merry and Pippin listen as you explain that Quickbeam will watch over them. You feel certain they will like the young Ent, for he is quite hasty in many respects.\
\
'Well, if you say so, Treebeard! I think you might consider the slow drip of honey in the comb quite hasty in comparison to yourself, so Pip and I will be the judge of that, if you don't mind!'","You have decided to show the hobbits to your home.","You greet Beechbone, a handsome Ent. His path has crossed with yours several times recently, and the memory of those pleasant conversations is still somewhat fresh. After a polite amount of time, your words turn to the matter of Saruman.\
\
'You speak of our neighbour as if he is an enemy, and indeed, he does not seem to be the friend he was once. Fumes rise from his home and the smell gives my nose offence, but that is not a crime. Orcs, too, could come from any number of holes. What evidence marks Saruman as their master?'\
\
Beechbone politely declines to discuss the matter with you further, but he agrees to listen to the debate and may in time come around to your point of view.","Pick up the container of Ent-draught","Merry has agreed to fill you in on how he and Pippin met the Ent named Treebeard, and what happened afterwards.","You should tell the hobbits that Quickbeam will go with them while the moot continues.","Talk to one of the curious creatures","Follow the hobbits to Derndingle","Pick up three bowls with which to serve your friends and yourself","The other hobbit wishes to speak with you.","'I do not know what to expect, Treebeard... are all of the Ents like you?'","Convince Quickbeam that something must be done","'That was delicious, Treebeard! I feel refreshed and invigorated, as if I had bountiful reserves of energy and could use them for anything at all!\
\
'But we were going to tell you how we came to be in your forest, weren't we? I hope I have energy enough for tale-telling!'","You have decided to show these curious little creatures, these hobbits, to your home.","Viaja al Valle Emboscado con los hobbits","Your hobbit friends could use a sip of Ent-draught. You should bring them the bowls you picked up.","Convince Beechbone that something must be done","Learn the nature of the curious little creatures","Beechbone needs to be convinced.","The hobbits seem to be enjoying the Ent-draught.","Bring your new hobbit friends to Wellinghall","Many of your people have come to Derndingle to discuss the matter of Saruman.","You have heard the sound of two curious creatures speaking to one another, and should investigate.","You exchange pleasantries with Quickbeam, one of the younger Ents. His home is not far from Derndingle, and sometimes you have seen him walking in the sunlight among the trees. Before much time has passed, the conversation turns to Saruman. Quickbeam seems to have some idea of the Wizard's crimes already.\
\
'Saruman has much for which to answer. He is a tree-killer, and we have been quiet neighbours for too long already. You find me over-hasty, I know, but in this there seems to be little need for discussion, Fangorn. I have quite made up my mind.'\
\
You tell Quickbeam of the two young hobbits you met, and ask if he will watch them while you speak to the rest of the Ents at the moot. He readily agrees.","You have brought the hobbits to Derndingle, where the Ents will discuss the matter of Saruman. You should tell the young one what to expect.","Quickbeam needs to be convinced.","'Well, it is nice to meet you, Treebeard. I have never met an Ent before! My name is Peregrin Took, but my friends call me Pippin, or Pip. I am a hobbit.'","Your new hobbit friends may enjoy a sip of Ent-draught.","'It is a pleasure to meet you, Treebeard. My name is Meriadoc Brandybuck, but most people call me Merry. We have become separated from our friends, and it seems that Saruman's Orcs would very much like to find us again and bring us to their master.'","Capítulo 5: La reunión de la Compañía Gris","Talk to the other hobbit","The creatures seem to offer no threat, but you have not seen their like before.","Convince Baldbark that something must be done","Bring the bowls of Ent-draught to your new hobbit friends"},
[7482]={"Talk to Glynn Brenin atop the village","Defeated a worm loose in Lhanuch (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'The Dragon Clan is not alone, Radanir! They brought the worms they worship down from the mountains with them, and they are loose in the village! Help my people drive them away, Ranger!'","The worm hisses at its trapped victims, and lumbers in for its meal. You have to get its attention!\
\
'Over here, worm! Over here! Let me get a look at that ugly visage of yours, and see if I can work any improvements!'\
\
As the worm closes for battle, you wonder if you could have fashioned a better battle-cry.","This worm has not noticed your approach, and though it pains you to attack unaccompanied by a shout borne of your sharp wit, you do so anyway. There will be time enough, and worms enough in Lhanuch, for you to think of something clever in the meantime.","Anirin can be found down the hill in Lhanuch.\
\
Anirin, the messenger of the Falcon Clan who has been recovering in Lhanuch from a leg injury, should be told what has happened in Tûr Morva.","You have travelled with Saeradan into Enedwaith and have stopped for the night at Lhanuch on your way north with the waggon containing your fallen comrades.","Talk to Anirin down the hill in Lhanuch","Interludio: El buey y el dragón","'This man says the Falcon Clan and the Dragon Clan are now allies. If this is true, then my decision is made easy.'","'Another day of our journey nears its end, Radanir. Let us see if the Uch-lûth, the Ox Clan, will consent to stabling us for the night.\
\
'We have tidings from the south to give to Glynn Brenin, as well. Do you remember how highly he spoke of Lheu Brenin and the Falcon Clan? The news that his southern neighbours have thrown in with Saruman will not please him.'","Find and defeat the worms loose in Lhanuch (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Glynn Brenin's open face grows cloudy and troubled as you speak of the Grey Company's betrayal by Lheu Brenin and the Falcon Clan.\
\
'Alas for your fallen, and for the hopes of my people, Radanir. If Lheu Brenin has succumbed to the whispered promises of Saruman, how can we hope to persevere 'gainst him?'\
\
Glynn Brenin snorts. 'Lheu was not as strong as I believed, Radanir. That must now be the truth. His weakness, buried deeply, has emerged and betrayed us all.'","'Not now, Ranger. There are rude ones outside this gate that need a lesson in manners!'","Talk to Anirin","'I think that is all of them, Radanir. Did I hear you shouting something about the worms smelling foul? It sounded like you, friend.'\
\
He grimaces.\
\
'When the fighting started, the horses bolted and the waggon rolled down the hill. You should help me find the horses and tether one of them to the waggon, and then... I think you should take the other horse and return to Halbarad.'\
\
He raises a hand to still your protest.\
\
'I can drive the waggon north by myself. You are of more use in a fight than I am, and if the Falcon Clan and the Dragon Clan have joined together, as it seems they have, Halbarad will have need of strong fighters. You may continue north with me if you desire, but I think you should return to Halbarad and tell him what happened here.\
\
'This should be good-bye, my friend. For now.'","Glynn Brenin can be found near the top of the village, in front of his dwelling.","Talk to Suvulch at the west-gate of Lhanuch","Talk to Saeradan outside the gates of Lhanuch","The Dragon Clan has released worms throughout Lhanuch, and Glynn Brenin wants you to defeat them!","Saeradan is outside the gates of Lhanuch.\
\
Now that the Dragon Clan has been driven away from Lhanuch, you should speak with Saeradan.","Glynn Brenin is near the top of Lhanuch, fighting off warriors of the Dragon Clan.","The worm snaps its fangs together as it menaces its prey.\
\
'Oh, what is that horrible stench? Is that you, worm? It is! It is a wonder you creatures are even able to breed!'","Talk to Glynn Brenin at the top of the village","'The Rangers have returned! What can you tell me of my home? Did you not travel to Tûr Morva in Tâl Methedras?'\
\
Anirin's face falls as you describe the Falcon Clan's betrayal of the Grey Company, and despite your natural skepticism, Anirin's reaction seems genuine.\
\
'What of my family? Do you have any news of them? My beloved is named Wenda, and she is no warrior. Is she in danger? And my mother Seren is aged and would not know to still her tongue, if she were put in a precarious position! What can you tell me of my family, Ranger? Speak!'","Suvulch of the Uch-lûth is by the gate, confronting a large and hostile force of Dunlendings.","The Dragon Clan has offered Anirin a chance to share in the treasure taken from Lhanuch. Talk to him at the West gate of the village.","Saeradan is standing outside the gates of Lhanuch and wishes to speak with you."},
[7484]={"'I am unsure what this meeting means for Gondor, but I know it will be significant. Let our own meeting be as timely, but let it signify only good fortune for the kingdom I serve!'","'You may keep your secrets, my interesting friend. I do not wish to pry. Only the Dead know what drove them to the Hill of Erech to meet with this grim man, but I do believe you know more of this matter than you let on.'","Interludio: Aquellos que Están Muertos","Rovalang beheld a frightening meeting atop the Hill of Erech, and does not know what it signifies, but you know part of its significance, at the least: Aragorn spoke with the oath-breakers in the dead of night.","Rovalang stands on the slope of the Hill of Erech.\
\
Rovalang wishes to learn more of the meeting between the Dead and Aragorn, if you are willing to speak to him.","Rovalang is on the slope of the Hill of Erech.","'I know little of the Dead, and count myself lucky. Who can say what drove them to meet with that curious company and its grim-faced leader?\
\
'You know of this man. I can see it in your face. Are you willing to speak of him?'","Talk to Rovalang and experience 'Interlude: Those Who Are Dead'","Talk to Rovalang"},
[7485]={"Each of the suspects may be found within the city of Cliving: Swithorne at the Rohirrim tents by the Mead Hall, Eldora at her home by the west gate, and Wigfugol at his estate in the north-west part of the city.\
\
Walnoth would like you to interrogate the people he believes to be the main suspects in the crimes that have occurred.","'Captain Théodmar told me of the circumstances involving Malbéort and my dagger. I understand your reason to suspect me, but I can assure you that I had nothing to do with his murder. My weapon was likely taken from me in order to draw suspicion towards me and away from the real killer.\
\
'On the night that Malbéort's life was taken, I was patrolling the city perimeter with other guards. Had I left to visit his home, my absence would have been very strongly noticed.\
\
'I have been grieving the loss of my brother, yet as I have explained to Théodmar, I do not blame the Reeve for his death. I respect Athelward greatly, and I understand his decision must have been a difficult one. I am an honourable man, and these despicable crimes are below me.'","Wigfugol has established that he had no possible access to the kitchen","Talk to Eldora at her home near the west entrance to Cliving","Walnoth believes that he has narrowed the list of suspects down to three individuals. The soldier Swithorne, the cook's assistant Eldora, and an elderly man -- Wigfugol -- all must be interrogated.","'I know that you are investigating the poison found in the kitchen, and the murder of Malbéort. Yes, I have heard the rumours. I must explain my actions so that you understand why I am innocent in these matters.\
\
'I have been taking care of the injured man you see before us, Fréastan. He was wounded in battle, and is greatly impaired. I care greatly for Fréastan, though he knows it not, and I have been overseeing his aid through medicinal herbs that Malbéort has provided for us. I have been here frequently tending to him, thus my absence from the kitchen.\
\
'It is true that no one can account for my whereabouts when the crimes were commited, but know that I have no more reason to harm Athelward than anyone else in town. Furthermore, Malbéort was helping me to treat Fréastan, and I would never have wished harm to come upon him!'","Return to Walnoth and discuss each suspect's testimony","'Speak with each suspect alone and listen carefully to their words. Consider each person's motive, access to the places of the crimes, and any witnesses of their whereabouts.\
\
'Swithorne may be found among the soldiers stationed around the Mead Hall. Eldora is said to live in a small home just inside the western entrance to the city. Wigfugol lives alone at his estate, north of the western gate.'","Eldora has established that she had no motive to harm either victim","Talk to Wigfugol at his estate in the north-west part of Cliving","'I believe we are getting ever closer to solving this mystery, ${PLAYER}. There are three primary suspects that we must consider: the soldier, Swithorne; the cook's assistant, Eldora; and the old man, Wigfugol. Each was seen visiting Malbéort and may have killed him to cover their attempted poisoning against Reeve Athelward.\
\
'You have been paramount to our progress in this investigation thus far. Interrogating these individuals will prove to be crucial to discovering the truth, so I must leave this task to you.\
\
'Swithorne should be among the Rohirrim near the Mead Hall, Wigfugol resides at an estate to the north-west, and Eldora's home can be found near the west entrance to Cliving. Question each of them carefully and return to me with their responses.'","Walnoth may be found near the fountain at the centre of Cliving.\
\
Walnoth awaits the results of your interrogations.","Swithorne has established that his witness should absolve him of the crimes","'You suspect me of these rumoured crimes? How shameful! Know that I am a respected elder in this community.\
\
'I was visiting Malbéort for treatment to the terrible nightmares I began having, shortly after my son and his family lost their lives. His croft was raided and burned in the first Orc-assaults, and still Athelward has refused to defend those helpless families outside the city walls.\
\
'It is true, I harbour no love for the Reeve after such a heartless decision, yet I would not resort to poisoning him. Consider for a moment, how a citizen such as myself would have access to the Reeve's kitchen? Surely someone would have noticed my unexpected presence there.'","'Each suspect has given a different reason why he or she should be absolved. Swithorne claims to have witnesses for when Malbéort was slain, Eldora seems to be lacking a motive to harm either victim, and Wigfugol would like us to consider his lack of access to the restricted kitchen.\
\
'The time draws near... consider each testimony and all of the evidence discovered. Action must be taken before others come to harm. We must apprehend a guilty party.'","Talk to Swithorne at his tent near the Mead Hall","Interrogating the Suspects"},
[7486]={"Lolo Wendingway mencionó que Bree está lleno de rumores sobre sombras que crecen y refugiados que llegan del sur. Te dijo que buscaras al segundo vigilante Heathstraw si querías continuar ayudando en las Tierras de Bree.","'¿Lolo? Solía venir aquí a menudo. Buen tipo robusto, buen pregonero y buen vendedor. Extraño para un hobbit, es cierto, pero dicen que la mayoría de los hobbits que viven por aquí son raros.\
\
'Su información es correcta, sin embargo, Bree ha visto su parte de sangre nueva últimamente, y no todos han sido de tu calidad.\
\
'Si necesitas trabajo, estoy seguro de que puedo encontrarte algo.'","El segundo vigilante Heathstraw se encuentra cerca de la Fuente del Jabalí en el centro de la Plaza del Mercado en Bree.\
\
Lolo Wendingway mencionó que el segundo vigilante Heathstraw podría tener información sobre personas que necesitan cosas hechas en Bree.","Hacia Bree","'Has sido de gran ayuda para mí, ${PLAYER}. Algo en ti me dice que podrías ser de gran ayuda para muchos. Si buscas seguir con tu naturaleza caritativa, quizá quieras hablar con el segundo vigilante Heathstraw en Bree.\
\
'Heathstraw está muy al tanto de los problemas que enfrenta Bree. Con los refugiados que vienen del sur y todos los rumores sobre la oscuridad creciente, creo que tiene bastantes detalles que seguir, pobre hombre.\
\
'Puedes encontrarlo pasando la puerta de Entibo de Bree, junto a la Fuente del Jabalí en la Plaza del Mercado.'"},
[7487]={"Return to Shukûri in the Gorge of Woe to inform her you have reduced the number of Orcs in the camps near Utug-bûr.","Into Enemy Territory","Return to Shukûri","'I am glad to see you have returned safely.'\
\
You inform Shukûri of what you have seen at the camps near Utug-bûr.\
\
'That confirms my fears. The threat here is overwhelming and may even threaten Gondor if we cannot halt or even slow their advance.\
\
'I thank you for your help. We now know more about our foes.'","Defeated Orcs in Ab-dâna (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Shukûri has asked that you go to Sar-kidul and Ab-dâna to the north near Utug-bûr to see what you find and defeat any Orcs you encounter there.","'${CLASS}, I need your help dealing with the dangers emerging from the demon-pit.\
\
'Their numbers are many and we must put a stop to their advances. To the north of here, near Utug-bûr, you will find two of their camps by the entrance. Sar-kidul to the north-west and Ab-dâna to the south-east of it.\
\
'If you are willing, I ask that you travel there and see what you can discover. Defeating any Orcs you see would be welcomed as well.'","Shukûri in the Gorge of Woe has asked you to scout out the camps to the north near Utug-bûr and defeat any Orcs you find there.","Derrota a los Orcos en Sar-kidul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los Orcos en Ab-dâna (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Orcs in Sar-kidul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7488]={"Find the source of the voices in Falch Gurth","Taurdir can be found at Torgris.\
\
You have discovered a small encampment of Rangers within a cleft of Falch Gurth. You should talk to Taurdir.","Talk to Taurdir","'Have you heard all the talk of Thuringwath, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Prince Faramir told us to hold our post, but after one of ours found the way into Falch Gurth, it wasn't long before Nidhlas took his men into the pass.\
\
'It's been days and I've heard no word from him or his men. To be honest, I don't care if the rumours are true or not.\
\
'All I ask is that you go into Falch Gurth to find Nidhlas and his men. Will you aid me?'","Search for Nidhlas and his men in Falch Gurth","Falch Gurth can be found to the south of Taen Orwath.\
\
You have entered Falch Gurth in search of Nidhlas and his men. You should continue searching for signs of them.","Shadows loom ahead of you, but you hear hushed voices up the path to the east","A small company of Rangers entered Falch Gurth in an attempt to explore Thuringwath, the Valley of Secret Shadow.","The source of the voices seems to be coming from a raised cleft within Falch Gurth.\
\
While exploring Falch Gurth, you overheard hushed voices from the east. You should investigate the source of the voices.","Falch Gurth can be found to the south of Taen Orwath.\
\
Cuilion has asked you to enter Falch Gurth and learn what has become of Nidhlas and his men.","A foreboding pass has been carved through the black slopes of Ephel Dúath","Find the entrance of Falch Gurth","It seems a few Rangers have made camp in a small cleft within Falch Gurth","'I did not expect help to come so soon, but... we are in dire need of it.\
\
'Nidhlas... is gone.'","Into Falch Gurth"},
[7490]={"'So, Cerdic would have you enter the forest? There are strange happenings afoot within the Balewood, ${PLAYER}... it is as if the forest itself has come alive with a rage.\
\
'The few times that I have ventured within to observe the Orcs, I have felt... eyes... on my every move. I know not if it was merely my fear of being seen by Orcs, or that something unnatural dwells within. Take heed if you travel into the forest, for more than Orcs may rally against you.'","Cerdic has asked that you speak to his men to learn more of the Balewood before venturing into the forest.","Talk to Athelman","You hear the snarls of Wargs in the distance. Look to the road!","Stand at the nearby bunker and watch the road","Talk to Frethi","'Be wary, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs have cut a swath through the forest in Núrzum's wake, and they patrol the path constantly. Their numbers are great, and their armour far thicker than most.\
\
'I cannot promise your safety if you stick to the wilds, but I assure you, the Orcs will find you, and quickly, if you do not.'","'The forest is no place for my people, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs spill forth from the wood each day, and while my men and I have been able to slay a few stragglers, their force is simply too large for us to engage. If you seek to enter Fangorn in search of my people, you must be mindful of their patrols and know that still even more lurk upon that frozen trail into the forest.\
\
'Confer with my men. Perhaps they can explain what dangers you face... and once you have done that, look to the road. If the Orcs pass on their foul mounts, you may have a chance to sneak into Balewood.'","Into Harm's Way","Cerdic is concerned with the increased patrols of Orcs through the part of Fangorn known as the Balewood.","The bunker can be found in Cerdic's camp overlooking the roadway to the east.\
\
You have spoken to Cerdic's men. You should now take up a post at the nearby bunker and watch the road for signs of Warg-riders.","The Orc raiding party has passed along the road.\
\
You should speak to Cerdic before venturing into the Balewood.","Talk to Cerdic","'The Orcs have passed! You would be wise to stay clear of the road that they have cut through the Balewood, lest you be caught by their raiding parties.\
\
'The time is now or never... you must venture into the Balewood before another wave advances!'"},
[7491]={"Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should search Naerband for information about Thraknûl.","Into Naerband","Complete The Key to Chaos","Find the lever that opens the torture chamber","Retrieve the guard's key","It sounds like Akhrûn has been recaptured!","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should retrieve the key from the corpse of the guard.","With Akhrûn returning to Nurn, you decide to infiltrate Naerband to learn more of the terrible Thraknûl.","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should retrieve and read the guard's register.","The register contains text about the coming and goings of prisoners, jailers, and torturers","Retrieve and read the guard's register","Search Naerband for information about Thraknûl","You hear a noise echoing through the prison halls","<rgb=#FF0000>Listen</rgb> more closely to the noise","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should enter Naerband.","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should find the lever that opens the torture chamber.","'Quickly, help me ${PLAYER}! We were ambushed at the mountain's base on our way to Nurn!'","Listen","It looks as if the former guard had been recently tortured","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should listen more closely.","The guard abandoned the post.\
\
You should search Naerband's dungeons for the guard.","You hear the door to the torture chamber unlock","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should listen.","Complete Servants of Urudanî","Akhrûn is in Naerband.\
\
You should find and speak with Akhrûn quickly.","Enter Naerband","You find some sort of register inside a locked guard room","'Before we part ways, there is something that I think you should know about Naerband.\
\
'When flames poured from the mountain and created the lake of fire, the heat reached all the way underneath the prison fortress and burned alive those within. I overheard the story from Orcs while I was imprisoned.\
\
'The prison is still run by a Black Uruk known far and wide as Thraknûl. He was known as the Dark Lord's chief torturer. It seems Thraknûl is still running Naerband as a prison even after the tower fell. Does the Uruk serve a new master? I know not.'\
\
You decide it would be worthwhile to investigate further the matter of Thraknûl.\
\
'I wish you luck. Be careful, ${PLAYER}. If Thraknûl catches you, you may never see the outside of Naerband again!'","The smell of burnt flesh permeates the air around you","Now you should be able to find out what is in the guard's register","Find Akhrûn","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
Now with the knowledge you have acquired through the guard's register, you should complete additional tasks within Naerband.","Complete The Madness of Thraknûl","Search Naerband for the guard"},
[7492]={"'You have defeated Hontimûrz? You have earned my praise, ${PLAYER}! That is one less trouble I need worry about in these dark days.'","Naerost lies to the east of Weathertop in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree.\
\
Nidgyl has asked you to assault the ruins of Naerost and defeat the villianous half-orc Hontimûrz. He suggested that you take allies with you.","'${PLAYER}, should you find yourself in the hills east of Weathertop, there is a particular half-orc by the name of Hontimûrz who has been making quite a nuisance of himself in that region. It has even reached my ears that he may be in the service of some ally of the Enemy.\
\
'In any case, I -- and many others  would like to see his evil put to an end. Perhaps you would go against him? He has set up a camp in the ruins of Naerost.\
\
'I should warn you however, he is said to be an accomplished warrior, and he is often surrounded by fellow brigands who will defend him... you would do well to take allies with you.'","Derrota a Hontimûrz","Nidgyl is in Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the west of Naerost.\
\
You should return to Nidgyl and tell him of Hontimûrz' defeat.","Into Naerost","Nidgyl in Bree-town told you of a ruthless band of half-orcs that has inhabited the ruins of Naerost in the Lone-lands.","Talk to Nidgyl","Hontimûrz ha sido derrotado"},
[7494]={"Oganuin ha sido derrotada","Derrota a Cráthair","Sant Lhoer, conocido como los Jardines Emponzoñados de Carn Dûm, es un lugar húmedo repleto de plantas, árboles y flores mortales, como pocas o ninguna se han visto antes en la Tierra Media. Más allá de las aguas fétidas de color verde berilo que fluyen por Sant Lhoer, se alzan inmensas estructuras de cristal, incluyendo Bâr Heledh, la Casa de Cristal. Es aquí donde la hechicera Oganuin practica su arte, experimentando con criaturas, plantas y personas por igual. ¿Con qué fin y para qué propósito? Solo se pueden suponer los más oscuros designios.","Mientras explorabas Sant Lhoer, has encontrado un pabellón de cristal. Deberías buscar dentro por señales de Málruv.","Encontraste una llave de hierro","¿Quién eres? No te conozco. ¿Rhúnelleth te envió? La elfa se mete y no ha dejado de molestarme desde que llegué aquí.'\
\
Ella suspira y se recompone.\
\
'En justicia, he apreciado su preocupación, y ella me ha mantenido alejada de lanzarme a esa maldita lugar sin un plan. He explorado en las puertas de los Jardines Emponzoñados, y veo mucho movimiento más allá de sus rejas metálicas. Dudo que pueda proceder contra tan grandes número de enemigos, pero tú pareces lo suficientemente formidable como para darme algo de esperanza.\
\
'Si tú lideras el camino, yo te seguiré de cerca. ¡Quizás Málruv pueda ser encontrado dentro! Encontremos entonces, en Sant Lhoer.'","Entra en Sant Lhoer y busca alguna señal de Málruv","Has descubierto una llave de hierro en el cuerpo de Cráthair. Dolág piensa que podría abrir una puerta que vio en el extremo norte de los Jardines Emponzoñados.\
\
Deberías buscar y abrir la puerta del norte.","'¿Qué le ha pasado a este gigante? No se parece en nada al Jorthkyn que he visto antes. Hay algo extraño con las criaturas de este jardín. Los orcos y los trolls, y ahora el Jorthkyn, parecen mutaciones grotescas y retorcidas. Esto es obra de Oganuin, si se cree a Rhúnelleth. El Elfo estará encantado de saber que has puesto fin a esta abominación de la naturaleza.'\
\
Le muestras la llave de hierro que encontraste.\
\
'¡Una llave! Debe ser para la puerta al norte que vi más allá de las aguas venenosas. Dirijámonos hacia allí.'","Busca la puerta norte","Dolág te ha encontrado dentro de la puerta de los Jardines Emponzoñados y te está esperando para continuar. Deberías buscar a su hermano desaparecido.","Has encontrado a Málruv y lo has rescatado de las maquinaciones de la maga angmarim, Oganuin. Deberías hablar con Málruv.","Espera a Dolág y luego habla con ella","Dejas los Jardines Emponzoñados atrás y te diriges hacia enormes estructuras de hierro y vidrio. Deberías continuar buscando a Málruv.","'¿No me ayudarás a liberar a mi hermano de la Corona de Hierro?'","Encontraste una enorme casa de cristal","Dentro de Sant Lhoer has encontrado a un mago angmarim, Cráthair, y su compañero, el Jorthkyn Tarkka-oka. El último es como nada que hayas visto antes. ¡Esto debe ser uno de los horribles experimentos de Oganuin! Deberías derrotar a ambos.","Habla con Dolág","Continúa buscando a Málruv","Derrota a la Alta Cultivadora Oganuin","Has descubierto enormes invernaderos de vidrio y hierro dentro de Sant Lhoer. Espera a que Dolág te alcance y luego habla con ella.","El gran Jorthkyn se estrella en el suelo","Habla con Dolág dentro de Sant Lhoer, los Jardines Emponzoñados","Después de derrotar a la hechicera Oganuin, rescataste a Málruv y te ocupaste de su bienestar. Su preocupada hermana ahora está esperando para hablar contigo.\
\
Deberías hablar con Dolág","Rhúnelleth te ha sugerido que hables con Dolág, cuyo hermano desapareció mientras exploraba los Jardines Emponzoñados de Carn Dûm.\
\
Dolág está en Bail Avarc, cerca de Carn Dûm.","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]} de nuevo, mi ${PLAYERNAME:nuevo amigo[m]|nueva amiga[f]}. Málruv está a salvo ahora, gracias a ti. Aunque está bien de cuerpo, los horrores que vio dentro de Bâr Heledh se quedarán con él para siempre, me temo.\
\
'Sin embargo, ahora tengo la esperanza de que personas como tú ayudarán a crear un nuevo mundo donde la gente buena esté segura una vez más.'","Entra en Sant Lhoer, los Jardines Emponzoñados","Habla con Málruv","Te paras ante Bâr Heledh, la Casa de Vidrio de Carn Dûm. Dentro de sus muros de metal y vidrio, la hechicera Oganuin practica sus artes oscuras, creando abominaciones y retorciendo seres vivos hacia fines inhumanos. Debes derrotarla y buscar señales de Málruv.","'Más allá de las puertas de hierro de Sant Lhoer se encuentran jardines mortales y casas de cristal llenas de hongos que expulsan esporas nocivas. ¡Algunas de las plantas dentro de los Jardines Emponzoñados pueden matar a una persona en un instante! Más allá de los jardines, a través de los ríos abarrotados de líquido verde, se encuentra Bâr Heledh, donde se dice que una hechicera angmarim está experimentando con plantas, criaturas y gente libre por igual. Hay cosas que nunca deberían ser intentadas, y temo que ella haya ido muy lejos de ese límite. Os ruego que pongáis fin a sus esfuerzos.\
\
'Antes de aventuraros a Sant Lhoer, deberíais hablar con Dolág. Su hermano Málruv fue atacado y ella rastreó a sus secuestradores hasta aquí. Está casi tan afligida como para ir tras él por sí misma, pero si lo hiciera, temo que no regresaría.\
\
'Por favor, ofrezca su ayuda si es posible.'","Determinada a rescatar a su hermano desaparecido, Dolág te ha pedido que la encuentres en la entrada de Sant Lhoer, los Jardines Emponzoñados.\
\
Los Jardines Emponzoñados están ubicados en Carn Dûm.","Has descubierto a Cráthair y Tarkka-oka","Dolág te espera para hablar contigo en Bail Avarc, cerca de Carn Dûm.","La llave se desliza en la cerradura y la puerta se abre","'Las palabras por sí solas no pueden expresar mi alivio. Vamos, salgamos de este lugar infame. Encuéntrame de nuevo en Bail Avarc. Quiero llevar a mi hermano a un lugar seguro.'","Dentro de un pabellón de hierro y vidrio en Sant Lhoer, Tarkka-oka y su guardián Cráthair te tendieron una emboscada. Tras derrotarlos, encontraste una llave de hierro.\
\
Dolág se ha unido a ti en el pabellón y está esperando para hablar contigo.","Busca en el pabellón","Habla con Dolág en Bail Avarc","'¡Mira allí, más allá de las paredes de cristal! Hay una extraña luz parpadeando dentro. Hemos encontrado Bâr Heledh, donde Rhúnelleth dice que Oganuin está creando las criaturas con las que has estado luchando. ¿Podría estar mi hermano dentro también?\
\
'Recobra el ánimo, porque no dudo que ella tendrá más sorpresas aterradoras esperándote.'","'¿Qué clase de mundo tan vil es este en el que vivimos?'","'Yo... te saludo con alegría, ${PLAYERNAME:sureño[m]|sureña[f]}. Las cosas que planeaba para mí...'\
\
Él se estremece.\
\
'¡Llegaste justo a tiempo!'","¡Viniste! Yo... admito que no esperaba que vinieras.'\
\
Ella permanece en silencio un momento, y cuando vuelve a hablar, sus hombros están más firmemente decididos.\
\
'Mi gratitud es profunda. Vamos entonces, pero ten cuidado. Las aguas aquí son repugnantes y tienen un aspecto amenazante. Te seguiré detrás.'","Derrota a Tarkka-oka","Encontraste un pabellón de cristal"},
[7495]={"Into the Abyss","'So Váskmun has led them into the Mordath... and into a trap laid by Sauron himself?\
\
'The Order of the Eye has sent many of its number into the Black Pits in search of the hidden vault, and now, Váskmun and the Firehorns have travelled there.\
\
'Is this the making of a new war for Mordor? Or had Sauron worked to ensure that he did not fall alone? Perhaps it is neither....\
\
'Whether it is this day or another, Váskmun and the Firehorns must be freed from their delusions! He leads them down a treacherous path, and I do not think whatever is in that vault shall set all to rights.\
\
'But in the meantime, my folk will keep a close watch on the abyss. When the time comes, we hope that you and Gimli will stand with us against whatever evils lurk in the Mordath!'","You have come to the abyss of Mordath...","'This is a mighty big chasm, ${PLAYER}! Sauron's sorcery must have been holding more than his tower together!\
\
'So they have not come this way then? Good! After studying more of Zôreth's notes, Spakorth has learned of a new passage into the dungeons of Barad-dûr. And even better, it is not one of much use to those cultists in the tower!'\
\
Gimli draws a coil of rope from his belt.\
\
'Aye, that's right. We're going down right here!\
\
'If Zôreth's notes were correct, there should be a rocky landing about twenty yards down. If they weren't, well... at least we'll find out just how deep this abyss is!'\
\
Gimli ties the rope around a nearby boulder and tests its strength.\
\
'Well, are you coming, ${PLAYER}? I would hate to go on such an adventure by myself!'","'We have done a good thing for these dwarves, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'If they had rescued Váskmun themselves as Zôreth had hoped, I do not believe it would be any different. Perhaps worse, but certainly not better!\
\
'It is a sorry fate that Sauron devised for Váskmun, and I refuse to abandon hope that he still might be freed from the Ring's influence. If that day should come, we must honour the dwarves who fell in service of their King. We must honour those whose blood was spilled to ensure the freedom of the Dwarves of Mordor!\
\
'Spakorth and those who still call themselves Stout-axes have sworn oaths to keep watch on the lands of Dor Amarth while our friends and allies remain here, and once that is done, I shall escort them to Erebor myself!'\
\
Gimli bows deeply before you.\
\
'You have done me and the Dwarves of Mordor a great honour!'","Travel to the mouth of the abyss of Mordath in Dor Amarth","'I brought enough rope for the both of us, ${PLAYER}. Let's get down there!'","Talk to Spakorth at the ruins of Díngarth","Gimli is standing near the mouth of the abyss of Mordath.\
\
You have learned that King Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into the Abyss of Mordath. You should speak to Gimli and pursue them.","'Have you read what I have, ${PLAYER}?!\
\
\\qDevoured\\q? What sort of creatures could have devoured four of the Dwarf-rings? Surely Sauron would have slain them at once for such an offence!'\
\
Spakorth reads over Zôreth's notes again.\
\
'Ah, yes, the key around the King's neck.... Sauron gave King Váskmun the key, and deceived him into believing that the mithril lockbox was all that stood between him and reclaiming Manthríf for his folk. It was likely never within... and who can say where it might be now?\
\
'As Zôreth has written, the Order of the Eye has learned much of the Mordath through their expeditions in the deep dungeons of Barad-dûr. I thought they toiled for the return of the Dark Lord, but this vault she has written of... this is what must have drawn them into Barad-dûr! None but the Gúrzyul—the Deathless—may have ever known of such a vault, and what would be kept guarded and hidden so far beneath the earth?\
\
'A great abyss has sunken into the Mordath to the north of Barad-dûr and the Order thinks it an omen that Sauron's secrets are to be laid bare for the most loyal of his servants. If there remains any chance of finding Manthríf, King Váskmun shall lead the Firehorns into the abyss of Mordath.\
\
'Patrol the mouth of the abyss and see if King Váskmun and the Firehorns have left any sign of their descent. For my part, I shall study more of Zôreth's research—with Gimli's protection, of course!\
\
'Once I have finished, I will send him to meet you at the abyss—and I shall travel far away from this place!'","The abyss of Mordath can be found to the south-east of the Oath-taker's Horn in Dor Amarth.\
\
Spakorth has asked you to patrol the mouth of the abyss amidst the ruins of Barad-dûr, and search for any sign of King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns.","Deep in the depths of Barad-dûr, there lies a passage into the Mordath, the Black Pits of Mordor, through which Váskmun Greytooth intends to lead the Firehorns in his quest to reclaim the Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.","Gimli is standing near the mouth of the abyss of Mordath.\
\
You searched the mouth of the abyss, finding no sign of King Váskmun Greytooth or the Firehorns, but Gimli has now arrived at the Mordath. You should speak to him, and learn what he and Spakorth discovered.","Talk to Gimli at the abyss of Mordath","You find no evidence that the Firehorns travelled this way, but you suddenly hear a familiar voice nearby...","Gimli can be found at the ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You have returned to the ruins of Díngarth from the dungeons of Barad-dûr after learning that King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into the Mordath. Spakorth and his folk are free at long last, but the fate of Firehorns is still unwritten. You should speak to Gimli.","<RGB=#FF00FF>Look</rgb> for any sign of the Firehorns at the abyss of Mordath","Spakorth can be found at the ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth.\
\
You and Gimli have escaped the ruins of Barad-dûr after confronting a glamour, and have returned to the ruins of Díngarth to tell Spakorth of what you discovered. You should speak to Spakorth.","Talk to Gimli at the ruins of Díngarth"},
[7496]={"Ídolo de Bail Grundail destruido","Ídolo de Bail Cátharnakh destruido","Hacia los Bails","Areneth está en Gath Forthnír, al oeste de Himbar.\
\
Tras destruir los ídolos de Himbar, debes volver a Gath Forthnír y contarle a Areneth lo que has conseguido.","Ídolo de Bail Dílas destruido","Destruye el ídolo de Bail Cátharnakh","'Tu fuerza de convicción no deja de impresionarnos, ${PLAYER}. Hay una última tarea que querría encomendarte, si aceptas hacerte cargo de ella.'","'¡Se retiran! Ahora debemos asegurarnos de que no vuelvan nunca. Ve a cada Bail y destruye sus ídolos. Es la única manera de impedir que nos amenacen de nuevo.\
\
'Encontrarás los tres Bails al oeste de Gath Forthnír, repartidos por Himbar.\
\
'Esta no es una tarea sencilla, ${PLAYER}. Debes reunir a un par de amigos en quienes más confíes para lograr completarla. ¡Te deseo buena suerte!'","Destruye el ídolo de Bail Dílas","Destruye el ídolo de Bail Grundail","Los ídolosde los Angmarim se encuentran en los tres bails al sur de Himbar, al oeste de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Areneth te ha pedido que te dirijas a los tres Bails al sur de Himbar. En el centro de cada uno de ellos hay un ídolo que debe ser destruido para impedir que los Angmarim ataquen de nuevo.","Los Angmarim, siervos del Señor Oscuro, amenazan a los Montaraces de Gath Forthnír.\
\
A los Montaraces les gustaría que los rechazaras de una vez por todas destruyendo los ídolos en el centro de cada Bail.","'Debes dirigirte a cada uno de los tres Bails al sur de Himbar: Bail Dílas, Bail Cátharnakh y Bail Grundail.\
\
'Debemos expulsar a los Angmarim de una vez por todas si queremos que la paz llegue a esta región.'"},
[7498]={"Debes explorar el interior de la cueva y averiguar cuántos trolls hay.","La entrada a la cueva de los trolls está al noreste del campamento de Arrod.\
\
Deberías explorar el interior de la cueva, ya que hay pocos trolls afuera durante la luz del día.","Dentro de la Cueva","La entrada a la cueva de los trolls está al noreste del campamento de Arrod.\
\
Deberías explorar el interior de la cueva, ya que no parece haber muchos trolls afuera.","Arrod está en su campamento sobre el acantilado al suroeste de la cueva de los trolls.\
\
Debes regresar con Arrod y contarle lo que descubriste en la cueva.","Has derrotado al hendroval, pero viste pocos trolls; quizá estén refugiados en lo profundo de su cueva.","'¿Trolls de caverna? No había oído que se aventuraran tan lejos de Moria...\
\
'Sin duda, es una noticia terrible.'","Estos trolls de caverna son mucho más resistentes que los trolls de piedra que encontraste en otras partes del Bosque de los Trolls.","Explora el interior de la cueva de los trolls","Habla con Arrod"},
[7499]={"There appears to be no visible means of entering this tower","The Rangers of Ithilien have decided that now is the time to enter Minas Morgul and begin to cleanse the Dead City, if such a thing might be possible.","'Faramir has commanded me to lead a group of Rangers into the Dead City. I would like you to assist us, ${PLAYER}. There are many challenges that await us within its walls, but the very first awaits us without! We must find a safe way into the city.\
\
'I fear the most direct route, by way of the main gate, may not be the best choice. Our numbers are few and the foes arrayed against us are many. I would like you to patrol the outer wall and search for weaknesses; perhaps there may be some secret entrance, heretofore undetected. There may be some way for us to enter the city while remaining beneath the notice of those who dwell there.'","Talk to Damrod in Barad Angarth","Talk to Damrod","Complete 'Instance: Into the Circle of Wrath'","Enter Barad Angarth, the Gate-wardens' Keep","Minas Morgul nestles among the mountains in Imlad Morgul.\
\
You should patrol the outer wall of the Dead City.","This narrow path leaves you too open for an ambush","A small hatchway juts from the base of this tower","The wall here is smooth and impossible to climb","'I thank you, ${PLAYER}, for leading the charge. We have successfully secured the tower of Barad Angarth. This will be our first base of operations in Minas Morgul, but likely not the last! From here we will work towards retaking the Dead City.'","Damrod can be found at Barad Angarth.\
\
You should talk to Damrod.","The entrance to Barad Angarth can be found at the base of the outer wall of Minas Morgul.\
\
You should enter the tower of Barad Angarth.","Patrol the outer wall of Minas Morgul (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The main entrance to Minas Morgul is too heavily guarded for a direct assault","Into the Dead City","'You have returned from patrolling the outer wall of Minas Morgul? What have you found?'\
\
You tell Damrod of the small hatch you discovered at the base of one of the towers.\
\
'I believe this may be our best option for entering the city. That tower is called Barad Angarth. Our scouts have spied Orcs patrolling the very top of the tower, and when night blankets the Vale they have seen the flicker of firelight in the windows. We should expect some resistance inside, but I think they will be unprepared for our attack. Quickly let us gather what is needed and prepare to take hold of Barad Angarth!'","Damrod can be found at Echad Uial.\
\
You should talk to Damrod.","The walls here appear too steep for you to scale"},
}
